7,25,16813,5,'EVS Part 2','en',40,'','Activity','activity','What revolution was brought about by Homo sapiens in the tool‑making technique?',16,1,'25/039.jpg',NULL,NULL,1,'25/039_1.jpg',NULL),(5058,25,16814,5,'EVS Part 2','en',43,'','Answer the following','one_sentence','What is the characteristic of the New Stone Age that allowed people to stay in one place over longer periods of time?',1,0,NULL,NULL,'The development of agriculture allowed people to grow food and store it, so they could stay in one place for long periods.',1,NULL,NULL),(5059,25,16814,5,'EVS Part 2','en',44,'','Answer the following','fill_blank','The materials used to construct houses in your locality include ______, ______, and ______.',2,1,'25/043.jpg',NULL,'wood, stone, mud',1,NULL,NULL),(5060,25,16814,5,'EVS Part 2','en',44,'','Answer the following','short_answer','Write about the effects on your life of observing seasonal changes in weather on the continents shown on a world map.',3,1,'25/043.jpg',NULL,'(Student answer may vary, e.g., \"Seasonal changes affect agriculture, clothing, and daily activities.\" )',1,NULL,NULL),(5061,25,16814,5,'EVS Part 2','en',44,'','Answer the following','short_answer','Compare the New Stone Age village map with a modern village and write short notes about them.',4,1,'25/043.jpg',NULL,'(Student answer may vary, e.g., \"New Stone Age villages were small and close to water; modern villages have roads and electricity.\" )',1,NULL,NULL),(5062,25,16814,5,'EVS Part 2','en',44,'','Answer the following','solve','Construct models of different types of houses. Do you know this? The earth is subject to cycles of glacial and interglacial periods. In the glacial period most of the earth’s surface is covered with ice sheets and the climate is extremely cold and dry. The level of water in the sea falls because a lot of it is converted into ice. An interglacial period is the period between two glacial periods. During the interglacial, the ice melts, sea levels rise, and the clima