owing','descriptive','What did Gopal Bhand want to tell the husband and wife?',2,0,NULL,NULL,'He wanted to warn them that the cows had ruined his field of beans and cucumbers.',1,NULL,NULL),(5150,27,16828,5,'English','en',13,'','Answer the following','difference','What is the difference between a ‘dream’ and a ‘daydream’?',3,0,NULL,NULL,'A dream happens while sleeping; a daydream happens while awake and thinking about something pleasant.',1,NULL,NULL),(5151,27,16828,5,'English','en',13,'','Read the following words aloud and copy them in your notebook','vocabulary','idle, enough, exclaimed, commotion, astounded, antics, wander, wielding',4,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(5152,27,16828,5,'English','en',13,'','Answer the following','descriptive','What did the husband want to buy?',5,0,NULL,NULL,'He wanted to buy more cows.',1,NULL,NULL),(5153,27,16828,5,'English','en',13,'','Answer the following','descriptive','What plans did the wife make?',6,0,NULL,NULL,'She planned to use the extra milk to make dahi, butter, ghee and to send some to her sister.',1,NULL,NULL),(5154,27,16828,5,'English','en',13,'','Answer the following','descriptive','What did the husband want to do with the extra milk?',7,0,NULL,NULL,'He wanted to use it for making dairy products and to give some to his sister.',1,NULL,NULL),(5155,27,16828,5,'English','en',13,'','Answer the following','descriptive','What did Gopal Bhand say he was doing?',8,0,NULL,NULL,'He said he was driving away the greedy cows that had ruined his field.',1,NULL,NULL),(5156,27,16828,5,'English','en',13,'','Answer the following','true_false','Did Gopal Bhand have a field?',9,0,NULL,'[\"True\",\"False\"]','1',1,NULL,NULL),(5157,27,16828,5,'English','en',14,'','Discuss in groups','activity','That’s true! + Wouldn’t it be lovely! + Just try stopping me!',10,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(5160,27,16828,5,'English','en',14,'','Choose ‘a’ or ‘an’ correctly and fill in the blanks','fill_blank','Choose ‘a’ or ‘an’ correctly and fill in the blanks: earthen pot, cow, jar, sister, stout stick, lovely field, eyebrow ______.',11,0,NULL,NULL,'a earthen pot, a cow, a jar, a sister, a stout stick, a lovely field, an eyebrow',1,NULL,NULL),(5161,27,16828,5,'English','en',14,'','Write the plural forms of the following','vocabulary','COW, pot, jar, sister, market, drop, stick, corner, field, cucumber',12,0,NULL,NULL,'COWS, pots, jars, sisters, markets, drops, sticks, corners, fields, cucumbers',1,NULL,NULL),(5178,27,16829,5,'English','en',17,'','Answer the following','one_sentence','Which are the two different places where strawberries grow?',1,0,NULL,NULL,'In gardens and in the woodland vine',1,NULL,NULL),(5179,27,16829,5,'English','en',17,'','Answer the following','one_sentence','What are the two different ways of eating strawberries?',2,0,NULL,NULL,'Eating them fresh or adding them to dishes',1,NULL,NULL),(5180,27,16829,5,'English','en',17,'','Answer the following','one_sentence','Which strawberries are plump and juicy?',3,0,NULL,NULL,'The ones that grow in gardens',1,NULL,NULL),(5181,27,16829,5,'English','en',17,'','Answer the following','one_sentence','Which strawberries are sweeter?',4,0,NULL,NULL,'The ones that grow in the woodland vine',1,NULL,NULL),(5182,27,16829,5,'English','en',17,'','Answer the following','one_sentence','How would you like to eat your strawberries?',5,0,NULL,NULL,'I would like to eat them fresh or in a salad',1,NULL,NULL),(5184,27,16829,5,'English','en',17,'','Solve','solve','Find out when and where we get strawberries in Maharashtra',6,0,NULL,NULL,'In Maharashtra, strawberries are usually available from March to May in the western districts and from September to November in the eastern districts',1,NULL,NULL),(5185,27,16829,5,'English','en',17,'','Explain','explain','Make a list of your favourite fruits and vegetables and note down the time of the year when they are available in plenty',7,1,'27/016.jpg',NULL,'Students should list fruits like mangoes, bananas, guavas and vegetables like spinach, carrots, and note that mangoes are plentiful in summer, bananas year‑round, guavas in monsoon, spinach in winter, carrots in spring',1,NULL,NULL),(5186,27,16829,5,'English','en',17,'','Answer the following','short_answer','Have you ever eaten any fruit/vegetable picking it straight from the tree or field? Write about that experience in 3-5 lines.',8,1,'27/016.jpg',NULL,'Yes, I once picked ripe mangoes from a mango tree in my village and ate them fresh. The mangoes were sweet and juicy, and I felt proud to have harvested them myself.',1,NULL,NULL),(5199,27,16829,5,'English','en',23,'','Solve','solve','Find at least two fairy tales/folk tales each and share them with other members in your group. Make a collection of 10 different stories in each group',9,0,NULL,NULL,'Students should research and list stories such as \'The Tortoise and the Hare\', \'The Boy Who Cried Wolf\', \'Raja Harishchandra\', \'Sita and the Monkey King\', etc., ensuring a total of 10 distinct tales per group',1,NULL,NULL),(5200,27,16829,5,'English','en',23,'','Explain','explain','Language Study (See pages 84-88.) Note the words that are highlighted. The highlighted words are all nouns. Find 5 other nouns from the story',10,0,NULL,NULL,'Other nouns include \'fire\', \'mountain\', \'snow\', \'tree\', \'apple\'',1,NULL,NULL),(5223,27,16830,5,'English','en',32,'','Read the poem aloud using proper intonation','descriptive','Read the poem aloud using proper intonation',1,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(5224,27,16830,5,'English','en',32,'','Note that we say ‘its appetite’, ‘its manners’ and not ‘it’s appetite’ or ‘it’s manners’','explain','Explain the difference between ‘its’ and ‘it’s’.',2,0,NULL,'[\"‘Its’ means it is, ‘it’s’ means belonging to it\",\"‘Its’ means belonging to it, ‘it’s’ means it is\",\"Both mean the same\",\"None of the above\"]','1',1,NULL,NULL),(5225,27,16830,5,'English','en',32,'','Activities','activity','Think of other funny names for imaginary creatures. Write any 3 of them.',3,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(5226,27,16830,5,'English','en',32,'','Is the insect described in the poem a real insect?','explain','Is the insect described in the poem a real insect? Think about an imaginary creature. Describe it in your own words. You may draw its picture and label it.',4,1,'27/031.jpg',NULL,NULL,1,'27/031_3.jpg',NULL),(5227,27,16830,5,'English','en',34,'','Answer the following questions','short_answer','What common qualities did the three brothers have?',5,0,NULL,NULL,'They were honest, kind and hardworking.',1,NULL,NULL),(5228,27,16830,5,'English','en',34,'','Answer the following questions','reason','What was the businessman looking for? Why?',6,0,NULL,NULL,'He was looking for a suitable son‑in‑law to manage his business and care for his daughter.',1,NULL,NULL),(5229,27,16830,5,'English','en',34,'','Answer the following questions','short_answer','How did the middle brother use the rice?',7,0,NULL,NULL,'He used the rice to feed the poor and to help the land grow.',1,NULL,NULL),(5230,27,16830,5,'English','en',34,'','Answer the following questions','reason','Was it right for the youngest brother to ask for a share in the money? Why?',8,0,NULL,NULL,'No, because he had already given the money to the poor and did not owe the youngest brother any share.',1,NULL,NULL),(5231,27,16830,5,'English','en',35,'','Find any other story of three brothers or three sisters','descriptive','Find any other story of three brothers or three sisters.',9,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(5232,27,16830,5,'English','en',35,'','Find out how rice is cultivated. Describe the process with the help of pictures or diagrams','explain','Describe how rice is cultivated, using pictures or diagrams.',10,1,'27/034.jpg',NULL,NULL,1,'27/034_1.jpg',NULL),(5233,27,16830,5,'English','en',35,'','Group Work Form a group of 4 or 5. Make a ‘storyboard’ for the story ‘Three Sacks of Rice’','activity','Create a storyboard for the story ‘Three Sacks of Rice’, arranging the story in a sequence o