ees in that garden, then how many eucalyptus trees are there?',12,0,NULL,NULL,'150-36=114',1,NULL,NULL),(7669,34,16965,6,'Maths','en',87,'','Find the total number of quintals of food grains','solve','The government made some quintals of food grains available for distribution to the earthquake-affected families in Patan taluka. Out of this, 34 quintals of food grains were distributed to the families in Adul village, leaving 48 quintals of food grains remaining. So how many quintals of food grains were available in total from the government?',13,0,NULL,NULL,'34+48=82',1,NULL,NULL),(7680,34,16965,6,'Maths','en',88,'','Find the ages of Deepali and Asma','solve','Deepali\'s age is 5 years less than Asma\'s age. If the sum of their ages is 27 years, what are their ages?',14,0,NULL,NULL,'Let Asma = a, Deepali = a-5. a+(a-5)=27 → 2a-5=27 → 2a=32 → a=16. Deepali=11',1,NULL,NULL),(7681,34,16965,6,'Maths','en',88,'','Find the total number of students','solve','Students of a school collected some funds to help the flood victims. The amount of the collected funds is four times the number of students. When teachers added Rs. 1500 to it, the total amount became Rs. 5140. Then what is the total number of students of that school?',15,0,NULL,NULL,'Let students = s. 4s +1500 =5140 → 4s=3640 → s=910',1,NULL,NULL),(7682,34,16965,6,'Maths','en',88,'','Find the number of neem trees','solve','The number of Neem trees planted near a milk collection centre is 52 more than the number of Peepal trees. If the total number of trees of both types is 170, how many neem trees were planted?',16,0,NULL,NULL,'Let Peepal = p. Neem = p+52. p+(p+52)=170 → 2p+52=170 → 2p=118 → p=59 → Neem=111',1,NULL,NULL),(7683,34,16966,6,'Maths','en',90,'','Answer the following','fill_blank','If the star has six points, what difference will there be in the measures of the angles? ______',1,1,NULL,NULL,'The angles will be larger by 36° each compared to a five‑pointed star',1,NULL,NULL),(7684,34,16966,6,'Maths','en',91,''