 Exercise','Arrange the following events in the correct chronological order','descriptive','1. Gautam Buddha travelled and preached to the people 2. The one who teaches and spreads religious knowledge in Jainism 3. The principal holy text of the Jewish people 4. The prayer house of Islam is known',13,0,NULL,NULL,'1,2,3,4',1,NULL,NULL),(9143,39,17036,6,'History & Civics','en',55,'& Exercise','Arrange the following events in the correct chronological order','descriptive','1. Gautam Buddha travelled and preached to the people 2. The one who teaches and spreads religious knowledge in Jainism 3. The principal holy text of the Jewish people 4. The prayer house of Islam is known',14,0,NULL,NULL,'1,2,3,4',1,NULL,NULL),(9144,39,17036,6,'History & Civics','en',55,'& Exercise','Write short notes on','short_answer','The Four Noble Truths (Aryasatya)',15,0,NULL,NULL,'1. Dukkha (suffering) 2. Cause of Dukkha 3. Cessation of Dukkha 4. Path to cessation (Eightfold Path)',1,NULL,NULL),(9145,39,17036,6,'History & Civics','en',55,'& Exercise','Write short notes on','short_answer','The prayer house of Islam is known',16,0,NULL,NULL,'Mosque',1,NULL,NULL),(9150,39,17037,6,'History & Civics','en',59,'','Answer the following','short_answer','Avanti — Ujjayini and Mahishmati coexisted.',1,0,NULL,NULL,'They were two separate kingdoms that existed at the same time.',1,NULL,NULL),(9151,39,17037,6,'History & Civics','en',59,'','Answer the following','short_answer','Gandhara — Takshashila.',2,0,NULL,NULL,'Gandhara was a region and Takshashila was its famous university.',1,NULL,NULL),(9152,39,17037,6,'History & Civics','en',59,'','Answer the following','short_answer','The development of the voting procedure in Gana Parishad Mahajanapadas was an important stage. In the Gana Parishad, decisions were made by majority. Various methods were adopted to decide the majority, such as open vote, voice vote, or secret vote. A member’s vote was counted only if the member was physically present.',3,0,NULL,NULL,'The Gana Parishad used majority voting with methods like open, voice, or secret vote, counting only present members.',1,NULL,NULL),(9153,39,17037,6,'History & Civics','en',59,'','Answer the following','short_answer','In some Mahajanapadas, participation of the common people was an integral part of administration. These Mahajanapadas were known as ‘Ganarajya’ (Republic). In these republics, the king was not the absolute authority. The king was assisted in decision‑making by an advisory council consisting of elders, warriors or elected representatives of the people.',4,0,NULL,NULL,'Ganarajya were republics where kings were assisted by councils of elders, warriors or elected representatives.',1,NULL,NULL),(9154,39,17037,6,'History & Civics','en',60,'','Answer the following','short_answer','Administrative reforms led to a more organised state structure.',5,0,NULL,NULL,'Reforms made the state structure more organised.',1,NULL,NULL),(9155,39,17038,6,'History & Civics','en',62,'','Mark the correct option with MW.','mcq','What are the groups of village settlements in ancient India called?',1,0,NULL,'[\"Janapada\",\"Mahajanapada\",\"Kingdom\",\"Village\"]','0',1,NULL,NULL),(9156,39,17038,6,'History & Civics','en',62,'','Answer the following.','mcq','Explain the term ‘Janapada’?',2,0,NULL,'[\"A group of villages\",\"A king\",\"A city\",\"A river\"]','0',1,NULL,NULL),(9157,39,17038,6,'History & Civics','en',62,'','Answer the following.','mcq','What led to the formation of the Mahajanapadas?',3,0,NULL,'[\"Political unity\",\"Economic growth\",\"Military conquest\",\"Social reforms\"]','0',1,NULL,NULL),(9158,39,17038,6,'History & Civics','en',62,'','Answer the following.','short_answer','Describe the development of the Mahajanapadas.',4,0,NULL,NULL,'The Mahajanapadas were large, powerful kingdoms that emerged after the decline of the smaller Janapadas, expanding through trade, warfare, and alliances.',1,NULL,NULL),(9159,39,17038,6,'History & Civics','en',62,'','Answer the following.','short_answer','Who laid the foundation of the Magadha Empire and what reforms did Ajatshatru introduce to make it more powerful?',5,0,NULL,NULL,'Chandragupta Maurya founded Magadha; Ajatshatru introduced administrative reforms, a standing army, and improved irrigation.',1,NULL,NULL),(9160,39,17038,6,'History & Civics','en',62,'','Answer the following.','difference','Compare the voting method used in the Ganaparishad (Assembly) with the voting method used in present time.',6,0,NULL,NULL,'Ganaparishad used a council of elders voting, while modern elections use universal suffrage and secret ballots.',1,NULL,NULL),(9161,39,17038,6,'History & Civics','en',62,'','Answer the following.','difference','Which dynasty’s rule did Chandragupta’s voting method resemble in present time?',7,1,'39/061.jpg',NULL,'It resembles the democratic system where representatives are elected.',1,'39/061_3.jpg',NULL),(9162,39,17038,6,'History & Civics','en',62,'','Answer the following.','short_answer','Name the Mahajanapadas that are located outside India’s current international boundary.',8,0,NULL,NULL,'Kalinga (Odisha), Gandhara (Afghanistan), and others in present-day Pakistan.',1,NULL,NULL),(9163,39,17038,6,'History & Civics','en',62,'','Match the following.','match','Match the terms with their meanings.',9,0,NULL,'[\"A: Voting Officer | B: Adoption of\",\"A: Adoption of | B: Voting Officer\"]','A: Voting Officer | B: Adoption of',1,NULL,NULL),(9164,39,17038,6,'History & Civics','en',62,'','Answer the following.','short_answer','In which river basin are the majority of the Mahajanapadas situated?',10,0,NULL,'[\"A: Ganges | B: Indus\",\"A: Indus | B: Ganges\"]','A: Ganges | B: Indus',1,NULL,NULL),(9165,39,17038,6,'History & Civics','en',62,'','Match the following.','match','Match the terms with their meanings.',11,0,NULL,'[\"Vrijji | Shalaka grahaka\",\"Ajatashatru | Mahajanapada\",\"Voting Officer | Adoption of Buddhism\"]','Vrijji – Shalaka grahaka; Ajatashatru – Mahajanapada; Vot