hy is Cuscuta found in the sea?',1,0,NULL,NULL,'Cuscuta is a parasitic plant that attaches to host plants; it is not found in the sea because it requires a terrestrial host for survival.',1,NULL,NULL),(10905,46,17146,7,'Science','en',43,'','Answer the following','reason','Why do living organisms need animals?',2,0,NULL,NULL,'Animals provide essential nutrients, proteins, and other compounds that are not available in plant food alone, and they play roles in ecosystems such as pollination, decomposition, and nutrient cycling.',1,NULL,NULL),(10906,46,17146,7,'Science','en',43,'','Answer the following','reason','Why is plant food not produced in the sea?',3,0,NULL,NULL,'Plants produce food through photosynthesis, which requires sunlight and chlorophyll; marine environments lack sufficient light penetration and chlorophyll-bearing plants are scarce, so most sea organisms rely on other food sources.',1,NULL,NULL),(10907,46,17146,7,'Science','en',43,'','Answer the following','explain','Explain the process of production of any other parts of the plant except food in plants. The green ones?',4,0,NULL,NULL,'Plant parts such as leaves, stems, and roots are formed through cell division and differentiation, driven by hormones and light signals; chlorophyll gives leaves their green color, while stems and roots develop specialized tissues for support and nutrient transport.',1,NULL,NULL),(10908,46,17146,7,'Science','en',43,'','Answer the following','one_word','What is meant by parasitic plants? Name their different types with examples of each.',5,0,NULL,NULL,'Parasitic plants are those that derive nutrients from other living plants. Types include hemiparasites (e.g., mistletoe) and holoparasites (e.g., Cuscuta).',1,NULL,NULL),(10909,46,17146,7,'Science','en',43,'','Answer the following','explain','Name some unicellular organisms in which all life‑processes take place within their unicellular body.',6,0,NULL,NULL,'Examples are Amoeba, Paramecium, and Euglena, which perform ingestion, digestion, and excretion within a single cell.',1,NULL,NULL),(10910,46,17146,7,'Science','en',43,'','Answer the following','reason','Insectivorous plants are attractively?',7,0,NULL,NULL,'Insectivorous plants have evolved sticky glands or pitfall traps to attract, capture, and digest insects, providing essential nutrients like nitrogen.',1,NULL,NULL),(10911,46,17146,7,'Science','en',43,'','Prepare a PowerPoint presentation coloured on the topic ‘Nutrition in Living Organisms’.','activity','Prepare a PowerPoint presentation coloured on the topic ‘Nutrition in Living Organisms’.',8,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(10912,46,17146,7,'Science','en',43,'','Answer the following','reason','Butterflies have a long tube‑like organ called proboscis.',9,0,NULL,NULL,'The proboscis is a specialized feeding tube that butterflies use to suck nectar from flowers.',1,NULL,NULL),(10913,46,17146,7,'Science','en',43,'','Complete the flowchart according to type of nutrition','mcq','Nutrition Plants Animals Autotrophic [_] [_] [J] [) Parasitic on anee Insectivorous [_] Ectoparasitic [_]',10,1,'46/042.jpg','[\"A: Autotrophic\",\"B: Heterotrophic\",\"C: Parasitic\",\"D: Insectivorous\",\"E: Ectoparasitic\"]','A: Autotrophic, C: Parasitic, D: Insectivorous, E: Ectoparasitic',1,'46/042_2.jpg',NULL),(10914,46,17147,7,'Science','en',46,'','Serve yourself only as much as you can eat','short_answer','Serve yourself only as much as you can eat.',1,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(10915,46,17147,7,'Science','en',46,'','Avoid over-cooking food. What can we do to avoid use of','short_answer','Avoid over-cooking food. What can we do to avoid use of?',2,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(10916,46,17147,7,'Science','en',46,'','Avoid throwing away left-over rice grains as ‘akshata’ and to prevent food wastage during wedding feasts?','short_answer','Avoid throwing away left-over rice grains as ‘akshata’ and to prevent food wastage during wedding feasts?',3,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(10917,46,17147,7,'Scien