 precautions will you take to make accurate measurements in day-to-day affairs?',4,0,NULL,NULL,'Use appropriate calibrated instruments, follow standard procedures, and check against known standards.',1,NULL,NULL),(10943,46,17148,7,'Science','en',55,'','Match the following','match','Match the items in Group A with the correct unit in Group B.',5,0,NULL,'[\"Velocity | metre\\/second\",\"Area | square metre\",\"Volume | cubic metre\",\"Mass | kilogram\",\"Density | kilogram\\/cubic metre\"]','Velocity – metre/second; Area – square metre; Volume – cubic metre; Mass – kilogram; Density – kilogram/cubic metre',1,NULL,'[[\"Velocity\",\"metre\\/second\"],[\"Area\",\"square metre\"],[\"Volume\",\"cubic metre\"],[\"Mass\",\"kilogram\"],[\"Density\",\"kilogram\\/cubic metre\"]]'),(10949,46,17148,7,'Science','en',55,'','Answer the following','define','Define scalar quantity.',6,0,NULL,NULL,'A quantity that has only magnitude, no direction.',1,NULL,NULL),(10950,46,17148,7,'Science','en',55,'','Answer the following','define','Define vector quantity.',7,0,NULL,NULL,'A quantity that has magnitude and direction.',1,NULL,NULL),(10951,46,17150,7,'Science','en',61,'','Describe the effect of rubbing a plastic comb or ruler on dry hair.','short_answer','A plastic comb or ruler rubbed on dry hair attracts pieces of paper.',1,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(10952,46,17150,7,'Science','en',61,'','Describe the effect of repeatedly passing near a polyester curtain.','short_answer','If we pass near a polyester curtain again and again, it gets attracted towards us.',2,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(10953,46,17150,7,'Science','en',61,'','Fill in the blank.','fill_blank','If we rub a blanket with our hands and take it near a metal object, a spark is seen in the dark ______.',3,0,NULL,NULL,'spark',1,NULL,NULL),(10954,46,17150,7,'Science','en',61,'','Explain the concept of repulsion and attraction.','explain','Repulsion and attraction are the forces between two charged objects. Objects with like charges repel each other, while objects with opposite charges attract each other.',4,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(10955,46,17150,7,'Science','en',67,'','Answer the following question.','reason','Why is the upper end of the lightning conductor pointed?',5,0,NULL,NULL,'To concentrate the electric field and provide a path for the lightning to strike the conductor.',1,NULL,NULL),(10956,46,17150,7,'Science','en',67,'','Answer the following question.','reason','Why are coal and salt added to the pit in the ground?',6,0,NULL,NULL,'They increase the conductivity of the earth, allowing the electric charge to disperse quickly.',1,NULL,NULL),(10957,46,17150,7,'Science','en',67,'','Fill in the blanks and answer in your own words.','fill_blank','There is ______ between like charges. (always repulsion)',7,0,NULL,NULL,'repulsion',1,NULL,NULL),(10958,46,17150,7,'Science','en',67,'','Choose the correct option and fill in the blank.','mcq','There is ______ between like charges.',8,0,NULL,'[\"attraction\",\"repulsion\",\"neutrality\",\"induction\"]','1',1,NULL,NULL),(10959,46,17150,7,'Science','en',67,'','Answer the following question.','reason','Why is lightning not seen everyday?',9,0,NULL,NULL,'Lightning occurs when there is a large separation of charge in clouds, which does not happen in all weather conditions.',1,NULL,NULL),(10960,46,17150,7,'Science','en',67,'','Answer the following question.','reason','What are the characteristics of a static electric charge?',10,0,NULL,NULL,'Static electric charge is a stationary charge that does not flow, is produced by friction or induction, and can be transferred by contact.',1,NULL,NULL),(10961,46,17150,7,'Science','en',67,'','Fill in the blank.','vocabulary','There is ______ when opposite charges are brought together.',11,0,NULL,'[\"attraction\",\"repulsion\",\"neutrality\",\"induction\"]','0',1,NULL,NULL),(10962,46,17150,7,'Science','en',67,'','Describe the function of an electroscope.','activity','An electroscope can be detected with an electroscope. Project: Make an electroscope yourself by using a copper rod, a metal disc, and two thin gold leaves.',12,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(10963,46,17150,7,'Science','en',67,'','Answer the following question.','reason','Explain why it is not safe to go out with a thin aluminium foil and an umbrella when there is heavy rain, and check which substances become ______ —?',13,0,NULL,NULL,'electrically charged',1,NULL,NULL),(10964,46,17151,7,'Science','en',73,'','Fill in the blanks','fill_blank','Maximum heat is absorbed by a ______ object.',1,0,NULL,NULL,'black',1,NULL,NULL),(10965,46,17151,7,'Science','en',73,'','Fill in the blanks','fill_blank','Conduction of heat takes place through a ______ substance.',2,0,NULL,NULL,'solid',1,NULL,NULL),(10966,46,17151,7,'Science','en',73,'','Fill in the blanks','fill_blank','The shining surface in a thermos flask decreases the outgoing heat by ______ when boiling water is poured into it, but a borosil glass bottle does not.',3,0,NULL,NULL,'reflection',1,NULL,NULL),(10967,46,17151,7,'Science','en',73,'','Fill in the blanks','fill_blank','The telephone wires which sag in summer become ______ in winter.',4,0,NULL,NULL,'straight',1,NULL,NULL),(10968,46,17151,7,'Science','en',73,'','Fill in the blanks','fill_blank','Cooking utensils are made from metals due to their property of ______.',5,0,NULL,NULL,'conductivity',1,NULL,NULL),(10969,46,17151,7,'Science','en',73,'','Fill in the blanks','fill_blank','The earth receives heat from the sun by ______.',6,0,NULL,NULL,'radiation',1,NULL,NULL),(10970,46,17151,7,'Science','en',73,'','Fill in the blanks','fill_blank','What will absorb heat? ______',7,1,'46/072.jpg',NULL,'steel spoon, wooden board, glass vessel, plastic plate, soil, water, wax',1,'46/072_4.jpg',NULL),(10971,46,17151,7,'Science','en',73,'','Answer the following','short_answer','How does a fever get lowered by putting a cold compress on the forehead of a patient?',9,0,NULL,NULL,'The cold compress cools the blood vessels in the forehead, reducing blood flow and lowering body temperature.',1,NULL,NULL),(10972,46,17152,7,'Science','en',77,'','रिकाम्या जागा भरा','fill_blank','Do not stand on open ground or below a tree. Do not go to a high location or climb a ______.',1,0,NULL,NULL,'tree',1,NULL,NULL),(10973,46,17152,7,'Science','en',77,'','रिकाम्या जागा भरा','fill_blank','Do not stand near an electric pole, a telephone pole, a tower, or ______.',2,0,NULL,NULL,'etc.',1,NULL,NULL),(10974,46,17152,7,'Science','en',77,'','रिकाम्या जागा भरा','fill_blank','Do not lean on wired fences around a farm, a compound, a garden or a ______.',3,0,NULL,NULL,'house',1,NULL,NULL),(10975,46,17152,7,'Science','en',77,'','रिकाम्या जागा भरा','fill_blank','If you are on a two‑wheeler, a bicycle, a tractor or a boat, get off immediately and go to a ______ place.',4,0,NULL,NULL,'safe',1,NULL,NULL),(10976,46,17152,7,'Science','en',77,'','रिकाम्या जागा भरा','fill_blank','Do not gather all together in one ______.',5,0,NULL,NULL,'place',1,NULL,NULL),(10977,46,17152,7,'Science','en',77,'','रिकाम्या जागा भरा','fill_blank','Take care to keep a distance of 15 feet between any two ______.',6,0,NULL,NULL,'persons',1,NULL,NULL),(10978,46,17152,7,'Science','en',77,'','रिकाम्या जागा भरा','fill_blank','Do not use plugged in electrical appliances. Do not use a mobile or ______.',7,0,NULL,NULL,'telephone',1,NULL,NULL),(10979,46,17152,7,'Science','en',77,'','रिकाम्या जागा भरा','fill_blank','Stand on dry wood, a plastic sheet, sack or jute cloth or dry ______.',8,0,NULL,NULL,'leaves',1,NULL,NULL),(10980,46,17152,7,'Science','en',77,'','रिकाम्या जागा भरा','fill_blank','Keeping your feet together support yourself on the soles of your feet, placing your hands on your knees and ______ low.',9,0,NULL,NULL,'crouch',1,NULL,NULL),(10981,46,17152,7,'Science','en',77,'','रिकाम्या जागा भरा','fill_blank','Swimmers or fishermen should immediately come out of the ______.',10,0,NULL,NULL,'water',1,NULL,NULL),(10982,46,17152,7,'Science','en',7