wer the following','fill_blank','Observe and note the spread of water seen ______ Keep a small stone or a chalk piece on your notebook and move the notebook from left to right with some force.',1,0,NULL,NULL,'in both the photographs',1,NULL,NULL),(11512,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',19,'','Answer the following','one_word','What is this natural event called?',2,0,NULL,NULL,'tide',1,NULL,NULL),(11513,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',20,'','Answer the following','one_sentence','What effect did the movement have on the water in the glass?',3,0,NULL,NULL,'It caused the water to move in a circular motion due to centrifugal force.',1,NULL,NULL),(11514,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',20,'','Answer the following','one_sentence','What happened to the water in the container and the mixer?',4,0,NULL,NULL,'The water in the container moved in a circle, while the mixer’s water remained still.',1,NULL,NULL),(11515,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',23,'','Answer the following','fill_blank','In what different ways can you generate waves in the dish ______.',5,0,NULL,NULL,'by blowing air over the surface, by moving the dish up and down, or by shaking it.',1,NULL,NULL),(11516,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',25,'','Answer the following','one_sentence','Tides are influenced more by the moon than the sun.',6,1,'48/024.jpg',NULL,'True',1,'48/024_1.jpg',NULL),(11517,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',25,'','Answer the following','one_sentence','What are the relative positions of the moon, the sun and the earth?',7,0,NULL,NULL,'The moon, sun and Earth are aligned during spring tide and at right angles during neap tide.',1,NULL,NULL),(11518,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',25,'','Answer the following','one_sentence','What effect will it have on the tides?',8,0,NULL,NULL,'It determines whether the tidal range is high (spring tide) or low (neap tide).',1,NULL,NULL),(11519,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',25,'','Answer the following','one_sentence','At some places along the coast, the low lying areas turn into lagoons or marshy lands.',9,0,NULL,NULL,'True',1,NULL,NULL),(11520,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',25,'','Answer the following','one_word','Place located on the opposite meridian of a point experiencing high tide will also experience high tide.',10,0,NULL,NULL,'True',1,NULL,NULL),(11521,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',25,'','Answer the following','difference','Differentiate between high tide and low tide, and between spring tide and neap tide.',11,0,NULL,NULL,'High tide is the maximum sea level; low tide is the minimum. Spring tide has the greatest tidal range; neap tide has the smallest.',1,NULL,NULL),(11522,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',25,'','Answer the following','explain','Explain the causes of tides.',12,0,NULL,NULL,'Tides are caused by the gravitational pull of the moon and the sun and the centrifugal force due to Earth’s rotation.',1,NULL,NULL),(11523,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',25,'','Answer the following','short_answer','If there is high tide at 7 am, find the time of the next high tide.',13,0,NULL,NULL,'Approximately 7 pm (12 h 25 min later).',1,NULL,NULL),(11524,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',25,'','Answer the following','short_answer','If at Mumbai (73° E) the high tide is at 1 pm, on which other meridian will there also be high tide?',14,0,NULL,NULL,'At the meridian 53° W (180° opposite).',1,NULL,NULL),(11525,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',25,'','Answer the following','short_answer','Explain the reasons for the generation of tides.',15,0,NULL,NULL,'Because of the moon’s stronger gravity and Earth’s rotation creating centrifugal force.',1,NULL,NULL),(11526,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',25,'','Answer the following','short_answer','Collect information from the internet about how electricity is generated from waves.',16,0,NULL,NULL,'Wave‑power devices convert the kinetic energy of waves into electricity using buoys or submerged turbines.',1,NULL,NULL),(11527,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',25,'','Answer the following','vocabulary','Swimming',17,0,NULL,NULL,'Activity',1,NULL,NULL),(11528,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',25,'','Answer the following','vocabulary','Steering a ship',18,0,NULL,NULL,'Activity',1,NULL,NULL),(11529,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',25,'','Answer the following','vocabulary','Fishing',19,0,NULL,NULL,'Activity',1,NULL,NULL),(11530,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',25,'','Answer the following','vocabulary','Salt pans',20,0,NULL,NULL,'Activity',1,NULL,NULL),(11531,48,17183,7,'Geography','en',25,'','Answer the following','vocabulary','Going to coastal areas for trips',21,0,NULL,NULL,'Activity',1,NULL,NULL),(11533,48,17184,7,'Geography','en',26,'','Tie an approximately 5m long thread to','one_sentence','Tie an approximately 5m long thread to the flying lantern so that you can bring the lantern down whenever required.',1,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(11534,48,17184,7,'Geography','en',26,'','After carefully reading the','one_sentence','After carefully reading the instructions given on the package of the lantern, open it and light the candle placed in it.',2,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(11535,48,17184,7,'Geography','en',27,'','What would have happened to the flying','short_answer','What would have happened to the flying lantern after the candle was lit?',3,0,NULL,NULL,'It would rise because the hot air inside expands and becomes lighter.',1,NULL,NULL),(11536,48,17184,7,'Geography','en',27,'','What could be the reason behind a low','short_answer','What could be the reason behind a low pressure belt in the Tropics?',4,0,NULL,NULL,'Warm air rises, creating a low pressure area.',1,NULL,NULL),(11537,48,17184,7,'Geography','en',27,'','Write the latitudinal extent of the low','short_answer','Write the latitudinal extent of the low pressure belt.',5,0,NULL,NULL,'Between 5° N and 5° S.',1,NULL,NULL),(11538,48,17184,7,'Geography','en',30,'','Air pressure decreases with increasing','fill_blank','Air pressure decreases with increasing ______.',6,0,NULL,'[\"millibars\",\"millimetres\",\"millilitres\",\"altitude\"]','altitude',1,NULL,NULL),(11539,48,17184,7,'Geography','en',30,'','Pressure belts oscillate','short_answer','Explain why pressure belts oscillate.',7,0,NULL,NULL,'They shift due to seasonal changes in temperature and solar heating.',1,NULL,NULL),(11540,48,17184,7,'Geography','en',30,'','On the earth, air pressure is','fill_blank','On the earth, air pressure is ______.',8,0,NULL,'[\"constant\",\"variable\",\"uniform\",\"maximum\"]','variable',1,NULL,NULL),(11541,48,17184,7,'Geography','en',30,'','What effect does temperature have on','short_answer','What effect does temperature have on air pressure?',9,0,NULL,NULL,'Higher temperature lowers pressure; lower temperature raises pressure.',1,NULL,NULL),(11542,48,17184,7,'Geography','en',30,'','The ______+ pressure belt spreads air pressure? between 5° North and 5°South parallel','fill_blank','The ______+ pressure belt spreads air pressure between 5° N and 5° S.',10,0,NULL,'[\"equatorial low\",\"polar high\",\"subpolar low\",\"mid‑latitude high\"]','equatorial low',1,NULL,NULL),(11543,48,17184,7,'Geography','en',30,'','Why ene subpolar low pressure belt (Equatorial low, Polar high, Subpolar formed? low, Mid-latitudinal high)','short_answer','Why is a subpolar low pressure belt formed?',11,0,NULL,NULL,'It forms where warm air rises near the poles, creating a low pressure area.',1,NULL,NULL),(11544,48,17184,7,'Geography','en',30,'','Mid-latitudinal high pressure belts','explain','Explain the formation of mid‑latitude high pressure belts.',12,0,NULL,NULL,'Cold air sinks at mid‑latitudes, creating high pressure.',1,NULL,NULL),(11545,48,17184,7,'Geography','en',30,'','How does a high pressure belt get formed','explain','How does a high pressure belt get formed near 30° parallel?',13,0,NULL,NULL,'Cold air sinks at this latitude, raising pressure.',1,NULL,NULL),(11546,48,17184,7,'Geography','en',30,'','Horizontal distribution of air pressure have hot deserts?','short_answer','Why are there hot deserts in the horizontal distribution of air pressure?',14,0,NULL,NULL,'Deserts lie in low‑pressure zones where dry, warm air rises.',1,NULL,NULL),(11547,48,17184,7,'Geography','en',30,'','At higher altitudes air becomes','fill_blank','At higher altitudes air becomes ______.',15,0,NULL,'[\"thicker\",\"thinner\",\"hotter\",\"more humid\"]','thinner',1,NULL,NULL),(11548,48,17184,7,'Geography','en',30,'','Draw aneat diagram showing pressure seeeeeerieeees belts. Label the diagram','draw','Draw a neat diagram showing pressure belts and label the diagram.',16,1,'48/029.jpg',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(11549,48,17185,7,'Geography','en',31,'','Answer the following','descriptive','What can we do to move the rolls to the other end of the table with a greater speed?',1,0,NULL,NULL,'Use the same method that moved the paper rolls, such as creating a pressure difference by blowing air across the rolls.',1,NULL,NULL),(11550,48,17185,7,'Geography','en',32,'','Answer the following','reason','What is the direction of the Westerlies in the high pressure area between 25° and 35° parallels?',2,0,NULL,NULL,'They blow from the west towards the east.',1,NULL,NULL),(11551,48,17185,7,'Geography','en',32,'','Answer the following','reason','Why is the direction of polar winds not the same in both the hemispheres?',3,0,NULL,NULL,'Because the Coriolis effect deflects winds to the right in the Northern Hemisphere and to the left in the Southern Hemisphere.',1,NULL,NULL),(11552,48,17185,7,'Geography','en',35,'','Answer the following','reason','Why do the breezes blow from the sea to the land during the day?',4,0,NULL,NULL,'Because land heats faster than sea, creating lower pressure over land that draws sea air inland.',1,NULL,NULL),(11553,48,17185,7,'Geography','en',35,'','Answer the following','explain','Describe the winds shown in fig. 5.5 a. In the coastal areas, land gets heated during the day and the air pressure on land decreases.',5,1,'48/034.jpg',NULL,'The sea breeze is shown: warm air rises over the sea, creating low pressure that pulls cooler sea air toward the land.',1,NULL,NULL),(11554,48,17185,7,'Geography','en',35,'','Answer the following','descriptive','Compare fig. 5.5a and 5.5b with reference to daytime and nighttime conditions.',6,0,NULL,NULL,'During the day, sea breeze dominates; at night, land breeze dominates as land cools faster than sea.',1,NULL,NULL),(11555,48,17185,7,'Geography','en',38,'','Answer the following','mcq','When the air expands, it ______ : winter is from the ______',7,0,NULL,'[\"becomes solid (south‑east to north‑west)\",\"becomes thinner (south‑west to north‑east)\",\"gets lost (north‑east to south‑west)\",\"becomes humid (north‑west to south‑east)\"]','1',1,NULL,NULL),(11560,48,17185,7,'Geography','en',38,'','Answer the following','mcq','From high air pressure regions, winds ______',8,0,NULL,'[\"blow to regions of still higher pressure\",\"blow towards regions of cooler air\",\"blow towards regions of low air pressure\",\"remain still\"]','2',1,NULL,NULL),(11561,48,17185,7,'Geography','en',38,'','Answer the following','mcq','The Roaring Forties in the southern hemisphere ______',9,0,NULL,'[\"blow towards the equator\",\"blow in the areas around 40° S\",\"blow from the subpolar region of low pressure\",\"blow from the subpolar region of low pressure\"]','1',1,NULL,NULL),(11566,48,17185,7,'Geography','en',38,'','Answer the following','descriptive','In the northern hemisphere, winds blow around 40° N parallel.',10,0,NULL,NULL,'They blow from the west to the east, forming the Westerlies.',1,NULL,NULL),(11567,48,17185,7,'Geography','en',38,'','Answer the following','descriptive','These winds turn to the south.',11,1,'48/037.jpg',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(11568,48,17185,7,'Geography','en',38,'','Answer the following','descriptive','These winds from the south‑west bring rains to the Indian subcontinent during June to September.',12,1,'48/037.jpg',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(11569,48,17185,7,'Geography','en',38,'','Answer the following','descriptive','These winds turn to the east during the monsoon season.',13,1,'48/037.jpg',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(11570,48,17185,7,'Geography','en',38,'','Answer the following','descriptive','These winds turn to the west during the retreating monsoon.',14,1,'48/037.jpg',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(11571,48,17185,7,'Geography','en',38,'','Answer the following','descriptive','During June to September, India gets rains; after this period these winds retreat.',15,1,'48/037.jpg',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(11572,48,17185,7,'Geography','en',39,'Activity','Answer the following','reason','A belt of calm exists near the equator. Why do the winds and pressure areas behave this way?',16,0,NULL,NULL,'The equatorial region has very small pressure gradients, leading to weak winds.',1,NULL,NULL),(11573,48,17185,7,'Geography','en',39,'Activity','Answer the following','reason','The winds coming from the north‑west in the southern hemisphere have greater velocities than the winds coming from the south‑west in the northern hemisphere. Why?',17,0,NULL,NULL,'Because the Coriolis effect is stronger at higher latitudes, increasing wind speed.',1,NULL,NULL),(11574,48,17185,7,'Geography','en',39,'Activity','Answer the following','reason','The monsoon winds in the summer come from the sea but the retreating monsoon winds in winter come from land. Why?',18,1,'48/038.jpg',NULL,'Seasonal heating of land and sea creates pressure differences that reverse the wind direction.',1,NULL,NULL),(11575,48,17186,7,'Geography','en',40,'','Answer the following','reason','Why are all the house types shown in the pictures found in our surroundings? If not, where do you think they can be found?',1,1,'48/039.jpg',NULL,'Because the houses are adapted to local climate and resources; similar houses are found in regions with similar conditions.',1,NULL,NULL),(11576,48,17186,7,'Geography','en',40,'','Answer the following','solve','Can the animals from polar regions like polar bears and penguins find the reasons behind all this?',2,0,NULL,NULL,'Polar bears live in cold, snowy regions with abundant seals; penguins live in cold, but not snowy, coastal areas with fish.',1,NULL,NULL),(11577,48,17186,7,'Geography','en',46,'','Answer the following','short_answer','Which natural region consists of short‑lived vegetation?',3,0,NULL,NULL,'Tundra',1,NULL,NULL),(11578,48,17186,7,'Geography','en',46,'','Answer the following','reason','In which natural region will you find the kraals? Why do people in hot deserts live a nomadic life?',5,0,NULL,NULL,'Kraals are found in hot desert regions; nomadic life is due to scarce water and grazing land.',1,NULL,NULL),(11579,48,17186,7,'Geography','en',46,'','Answer the following','reason','Which region has winter rains? Why are carnivorous animals found in the grasslands?',6,0,NULL,NULL,'Mediterranean region has winter rains; carnivores in grasslands hunt large herbivores.',1,NULL,NULL),(11580,48,17186,7,'Geography','en',46,'','Answer the following','descriptive','Which regions favour dairy farming?',7,0,NULL,NULL,'Grasslands and some parts of the temperate zones.',1,NULL,NULL),(11581,48,17186,7,'Geography','en',47,'','Answer the following','descriptive','Due to its mild and warm climate',8,1,'48/046.jpg',NULL,'This statement refers to the Monsoon region.',1,'48/046_3.jpg',NULL),(11582,48,17186,7,'Geography','en',47,'','Answer the following','short_answer','Trees in equatorial forests grow tall. People from the West European region are not energetic. Vegetation is short‑lived in the Tundra.',9,1,'48/046.jpg',NULL,'The statement is incorrect; equatorial trees are tall, West European people are energetic, and tundra vegetation is short‑lived.',1,'48/046_1.jpg',NULL),(11586,48,17186,7,'Geography','en',47,'','Answer the following','short_answer','What is the latitudinal extent of the Taiga region?',10,1,'48/046.jpg',NULL,'Approximately 55° to 70° latitude.',1,'48/046_3.jpg',NULL),(11587,48,17186,7,'Geography','en',47,'','Answer the following','short_answer','The trees in the Mediterranean region have thick leaves and the juice is useful for...',11,1,'48/046.jpg',NULL,'The statement is incomplete; Mediterranean trees have thick leaves but the juice is not a common use.',1,'48/046_1.jpg',NULL),(11588,48,17186,7,'Geography','en',47,'','Answer the following','short_answer','Name any three herbivorous animals from the Sudan region.',12,1,'48/046.jpg',NULL,'Zebras, antelopes, and giraffes.',1,NULL,NULL),(11589,48,17186,7,'Geography','en',47,'','Answer the following','short_answer','The camel is an important animal of the hot desert region as it can survive without water and is useful for transport.',13,1,'48/046.jpg',NULL,'True',1,'48/046_4.jpg',NULL),(11590,48,17186,7,'Geography','en',47,'','Answer the following','short_answer','What are the characteristics of the hot desert region?',14,1,'48/046.jpg',NULL,'Very hot summers, very low rainfall, sparse vegetation, animals adapted to water scarcity.',1,NULL,NULL),(11591,48,17186,7,'Geography','en',47,'','Answer the following','short_answer','Carnivorous animals like tigers and lions are found in large numbers in the equatorial regions.',15,1,'48/046.jpg',NULL,'False – they are found in grasslands and savannas, not equatorial forests.',1,NULL,NULL),(11592,48,17187,7,'Geography','en',49,'','Answer the following','descriptive','What are the different constituents of soil?',1,0,NULL,NULL,'Soil consists of weathered rock particles, organic matter (humus), water, air, and living organisms such as bacteria, fungi, earthworms and other soil fauna.',1,NULL,NULL),(11593,48,17187,7,'Geography','en',50,'','Answer the following','descriptive','What do you learn from this?',2,0,NULL,NULL,'The experiment shows that seeds need soil and water for growth; soil provides nutrients and support.',1,NULL,NULL),(11594,48,17187,7,'Geography','en',50,'','Answer the following','descriptive','What happened to the seeds put in the pot filled with soil and the optimum availability of water?',3,0,NULL,NULL,'The seeds germinated and grew into healthy plants, showing that soil and adequate water are essential for plant growth.',1,NULL,NULL),(11596,48,17187,7,'Geography','en',52,'','Answer the following','descriptive','In which region is alluvial soil found?',4,0,NULL,NULL,'Alluvial soil is found in the river valleys and plains of Maharashtra, especially along the coast and in the Deccan Plateau.',1,NULL,NULL),(11597,48,17187,7,'Geography','en',55,'','Answer the following','reason','To the west of Sahyadris, laterite soils are formed from basalt rock.',5,0,NULL,NULL,'Laterite soils form because basalt weathers and iron oxides leach out, giving a reddish colour.',1,NULL,NULL),(11598,48,17187,7,'Geography','en',55,'','Answer the following','reason','Humus content in the soil increases.',6,0,NULL,NULL,'Humus increases when organic matter decomposes with the help of microorganisms and plant residues.',1,NULL,NULL),(11599,48,17187,7,'Geography','en',55,'','Answer the following','reason','Soil formation process is faster in the equatorial climate.',7,0,NULL,NULL,'High rainfall and warm temperatures accelerate weathering and decomposition, speeding up soil formation.',1,NULL,NULL),(11600,48,17187,7,'Geography','en',55,'','Answer the following','reason','The salinity of the soil increases.',8,0,NULL,NULL,'Excessive irrigation draws salts upward, accumulating them in the soil and raising salinity.',1,NULL,NULL),(11601,48,17187,7,'Geography','en',55,'','Answer the following','reason','Rice is the staple diet of the people in the Konkan region.',9,0,NULL,NULL,'The fertile alluvial soils and abundant water supply in Konkan support rice cultivation, making it a staple.',1,NULL,NULL),(11602,48,17187,7,'Geography','en',55,'','Answer the following','reason','Soil erosion occurs due to wind and water.',10,0,NULL,NULL,'Wind and water remove the topsoil, especially on slopes and bare surfaces, leading to erosion.',1,NULL,NULL),(11603,48,17187,7,'Geography','en',55,'','Answer the following','reason','Soil degradation is caused by excessive use of chemicals and lack of organic matter.',11,0,NULL,NULL,'Chemical residues and low humus content weaken soil structure and reduce fertility, causing degradation.',1,NULL,NULL),(11604,48,17187,7,'Geography','en',55,'','Answer the following','reason','Measures of soil conservation include planting trees, building embankments and contour trenches.',12,0,NULL,NULL,'These practices reduce erosion, retain water and improve soil health.',1,NULL,NULL),(11605,48,17187,7,'Geography','en',55,'','Answer the following','reason','Organic manures and chemical fertilizers are used to improve soil fertility.',13,0,NULL,NULL,'Organic manures add humus and nutrients; chemical fertilizers supply specific nutrients quickly.',1,NULL,NULL),(11606,48,17187,7,'Geography','en',55,'','Answer the following','reason','Place where you will get the fertilizers used in agriculture.',14,0,NULL,NULL,'Fertilizers are sourced from agricultural chemical factories, organic farms and local markets.',1,NULL,NULL),(11607,48,17187,7,'Geography','en',55,'','Answer the following','reason','Importance of soils for plant growth.',15,0,NULL,NULL,'Soils provide nutrients, water, support, and a habitat for microorganisms essential for plant growth.',1,NULL,NULL),(11608,48,17187,7,'Geography','en',55,'','Answer the following','reason','Visit a soil testing centre/laboratory and note the work that is carried out in the centre.',16,0,NULL,NULL,'Soil testing involves sampling, pH measurement, nutrient analysis, and recommendations for fertiliser application.',1,NULL,NULL),(11609,48,17187,7,'Geography','en',55,'','Answer the following','reason','Prepare compost at home or in your housing society.',17,0,NULL,NULL,'Compost is made by mixing kitchen waste, garden litter and water, allowing microbes to decompose it into nutrient‑rich material.',1,NULL,NULL),(11610,48,17187,7,'Geography','en',55,'','Answer the following','reason','Visit a place where ‘Arrest water, let it percolate’ is being implemented and collect information about it.',18,0,NULL,NULL,'Such proj