ctations, and involving parents in a supportive plan.',1,NULL,NULL),(12601,52,17237,8,'English','en',54,'','Convert the following sentences into indirect speech','short_answer','1. Ritesh: May I come in, Madam?\n2. Mrs Sen: Ritesh, you are too early for the second period.\n3. Ritesh: I had left my bag at the shop.\n4. Ritesh: I am sorry, Ma’am!\n5. Mrs Sen: There’s a story‑writing competition.',7,0,NULL,NULL,'1. Ritesh asked if he could come in.\n2. Mrs Sen told Ritesh that he was too early for the second period.\n3. Ritesh said that he had left his bag at the shop.\n4. Ritesh apologized to the teacher.\n5. Mrs Sen mentioned that there was a story‑writing competition.',1,NULL,NULL),(12602,52,17237,8,'English','en',54,'','Convert to indirect speech','short_answer','Ritesh: May I come in, Madam?',8,0,NULL,NULL,'Ritesh asked if he could come in, Madam.',1,NULL,NULL),(12603,52,17237,8,'English','en',54,'','Convert to indirect speech','short_answer','Mrs Sen: Ritesh, you are too early for the second period.',9,0,NULL,NULL,'Mrs Sen told Ritesh that he was too early for the second period.',1,NULL,NULL),(12604,52,17237,8,'English','en',54,'','Convert to indirect speech','short_answer','Ritesh: I had left my bag at the shop.',10,0,NULL,NULL,'Ritesh said that he had left his bag at the shop.',1,NULL,NULL),(12605,52,17237,8,'English','en',54,'','Convert to indirect speech','short_answer','Ritesh: I am sorry, Ma’am!',11,0,NULL,NULL,'Ritesh apologized to the teacher.',1,NULL,NULL),(12606,52,17237,8,'English','en',54,'','Convert to indirect speech','short_answer','Mrs Sen: There’s a story‑writing competition.',12,0,NULL,NULL,'Mrs Sen mentioned that there was a story‑writing competition.',1,NULL,NULL),(12623,52,17238,8,'English','en',59,'','Answer the following','short_answer','She stayed back home, with her parents ______?',1,0,NULL,NULL,'who?',1,NULL,NULL),(12624,52,17238,8,'English','en',59,'','Answer the following','short_answer','A ship was wrecked that night. ______?',2,0,NU