em is addressed to the reader',1,NULL,NULL),(12727,52,17241,8,'English','en',78,'','Answer the following','short_answer','Identify the main points in every stanza',3,0,NULL,NULL,'Stanza 1: words hurt like stones; Stanza 2: words leave scars on mind and heart; Stanza 3: words can heal; Stanza 4: reflection on kindness',1,NULL,NULL),(12728,52,17241,8,'English','en',78,'','Answer the following','short_answer','Explain implied meaning',4,0,NULL,NULL,'The poem implies that words, though invisible, can cause lasting emotional damage and healing.',1,NULL,NULL),(12729,52,17241,8,'English','en',78,'','Answer the following','short_answer','Write down the points making short paragraph for each stanza',5,1,'52/077.jpg',NULL,'Stanza 1: Words can hurt like stones. Stanza 2: Words leave emotional scars. Stanza 3: Kind words can heal. Stanza 4: Reflect on using kind words.',1,'52/077_1.jpg',NULL),(12738,52,17242,8,'English','en',81,'','Complete the following:','fill_blank','Cronin’s story focuses on ________ .',1,0,NULL,NULL,'self‑less help and dedication',1,NULL,NULL),(12739,52,17242,8,'English','en',81,'','Complete the following:','fill_blank','The narrator ________ to encourage the two brothers.',2,0,NULL,NULL,'offers help and support',1,NULL,NULL),(12740,52,17242,8,'English','en',81,'','Complete the following:','fill_blank','The narrator develops a liking for the two brothers because they are ________ .',3,0,NULL,NULL,'innocent, serious, pleasant and earnest',1,NULL,NULL),(12741,52,17242,8,'English','en',81,'','Complete the following:','fill_blank','The boys wish to visit the village Poleta to ________ .',4,0,NULL,NULL,'get a lift for their sister’s treatment',1,NULL,NULL),(12742,52,17242,8,'English','en',81,'','Complete the following:','fill_blank','So, one can conclude from the story that ‘______’ which means ‘______’.',5,0,NULL,NULL,'Where there is a will there’s a way – It means that determination leads to success',1,NULL,NULL),(12755,52,17242,8,'English','en',82,'','Answer