ans fail in the struggle of 1857?',2,0,NULL,NULL,'Because there was no central leadership, the rebellion was fragmented, and the British used divide‑and‑rule tactics, leading to a lack of unified strategy and resources.',1,NULL,NULL),(16132,61,17377,8,'History & Civics','en',30,'','Answer the following in brief','descriptive','After the struggle of 1857 the post of ______ was created to look after the affairs of India.',3,0,NULL,NULL,'Secretary of State for India',1,NULL,NULL),(16133,61,17377,8,'History & Civics','en',30,'','Answer the following in brief','descriptive','______ was the Governor General who annexed the princely states.',4,0,NULL,NULL,'Lord Dalhousie',1,NULL,NULL),(16134,61,17377,8,'History & Civics','en',30,'','Explain the following statements','explain','The Paikas made an armed rebellion against the British.',5,1,'61/029.jpg',NULL,'The Paikas were local militia in Odisha who, inspired by earlier revolts, rose against British rule in 1817, demonstrating early resistance to colonial authority.',1,'61/029_1.jpg',NULL),(16135,61,17377,8,'History & Civics','en',30,'','Explain the following statements','explain','There was discontent among the regions where the freedom struggle of 1857 took place.',6,0,NULL,NULL,'Regions such as North India (Delhi, Lucknow), Bengal, Bihar, and parts of the princely states felt economic hardship, political annexation, and religious interference, fueling widespread discontent.',1,NULL,NULL),(16136,61,17377,8,'History & Civics','en',30,'','Explain the following statements','explain','The Indian sepoys could not keep standing in front of the British army.',7,0,NULL,NULL,'Indian soldiers lacked adequate training, equipment, and strategic coordination, and were often outnumbered and outmaneuvered by the better-equipped British forces.',1,NULL,NULL),(16137,61,17378,8,'History & Civics','en',33,'','Answer the following','short_answer','At present, what kind of transformation has occurred in the life of women due to education?',1,