 Stafford Cripps to India?',1,0,NULL,NULL,'Vinoba Bhave was the first individual satyagrahi to be sent by Sir Stafford Cripps to India.',1,NULL,NULL),(16182,61,17382,8,'History & Civics','en',54,'','Answer the following','explain','The nation wide movement of 1942 during the spread of news of arrest is! ASO. CAILER :______csesessssarse of main leaders of the Indian',2,0,NULL,NULL,'The nationwide movement of 1942 during the spread of news of arrest was a mass protest against the arrest of main leaders of the Indian National Congress.',1,NULL,NULL),(16183,61,17382,8,'History & Civics','en',54,'','Answer the following','explain','In November 1943, Japan conquered National Congress ? cesses iSlands and handed them over to Azad Hind Government.',3,0,NULL,NULL,'In November 1943, Japan conquered the Andaman and Nicobar Islands and handed them over to the Azad Hind Government.',1,NULL,NULL),(16184,61,17382,8,'History & Civics','en',54,'','Answer the following','explain','Prepare a timeline of the events of the struggle of Indian National Army',4,0,NULL,NULL,'- 1942: INA formed under Subhash Chandra Bose.\n- 1943: INA captures some territories and establishes Azad Hind Government in Singapore.\n- 1944: Bose dies in a plane crash.\n- 1945: INA soldiers surrender and are tried by the British.',1,NULL,NULL),(16185,61,17382,8,'History & Civics','en',54,'','Answer the following','activity','With the help of internet collect the pictures of Quit India Movement of 1942 and organise an exhibition on occasion of a national day',5,1,'61/053.jpg',NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(16186,61,17382,8,'History & Civics','en',54,'','Answer the following','explain','In November 1939, _ provincial ministers of Indian National Congress gave their resignations',6,0,NULL,NULL,'In November 1939, the provincial ministers of the Indian National Congress gave their resignations.',1,NULL,NULL),(16187,61,17382,8,'History & Civics','en',54,'','Answer the following','explain','The Indian National Army had to lay down their arms',7,0,NULL,NULL,'The Indian National Army had to lay down their arms after the defeat of the Japanese forces and the end of World War II.',1,NULL,NULL),(16188,61,17382,8,'History & Civics','en',54,'','Answer the following','explain','The Parallel Government became a source of inspiration to the people',8,0,NULL,NULL,'The Parallel Government became a source of inspiration to the people by providing local administration and encouraging resistance against the British.',1,NULL,NULL),(16189,61,17382,8,'History & Civics','en',54,'','Answer the following','explain','Complete the following table\n\nForward Bloc\n\nIndian Independence League\n\nToofan Sena\n\nMadaasaneneeseee aaasaaaseseanene',9,1,'61/053.jpg',NULL,'Forward Bloc – founded by Subhash Chandra Bose\nIndian Independence League – an organization supporting the Indian National Army\nToofan Sena – a local revolutionary group in Maharashtra\nMadaasaneneeseee aaasaaaseseanene – (no clear meaning; likely a corrupted text)',1,NULL,NULL),(16190,61,17383,8,'History & Civics','en',59,'','Write a detail description of the attack on Chittagong Armoury named ______ : is oa','short_answer','Write a detail description of the attack on Chittagong Armoury named ______ : is oa',1,0,NULL,NULL,'The Chittagong Armoury Raid was carried out by Surya Sen and his comrades on 18 April 1930 to seize arms from two police armories in Chittagong, Bengal. They broke telephone lines, destroyed communication, and fought bravely against the British forces, but the raid was ultimately unsuccessful and many revolutionaries were arrested or killed.',1,NULL,NULL),(16191,61,17383,8,'History & Civics','en',59,'','In Punjab, ou______ «organised an','short_answer','In Punjab, ______ organised an uprising against the Government',2,0,NULL,NULL,'Swatantryaveer Savarkar organised an uprising against the Government in Punjab',1,NULL,NULL),(16192,61,17383,8,'History & Civics','en',59,'','Explain the contribution of uprising against the Government Swatantryaveer Savarkar in the armed','short_answer','Explain the contribution of uprising against the Government Swatantryaveer Savarkar in the armed',3,0,NULL,NULL,'Savarkar’s uprising in Punjab inspired many to join the armed struggle, spreading revolutionary ideas and encouraging the use of weapons against the British.',1,NULL,NULL),(16193,61,17383,8,'History & Civics','en',59,'','______ founded the India House. revolutionary movement','short_answer','______ founded the India House revolutionary movement',4,0,NULL,NULL,'Pandit Shyamji Krishna Varma founded the India House revolutionary movement',1,NULL,NULL),(16195,61,17383,8,'History & Civics','en',59,'','Chafekar brothers killed Rand','explain','Chafekar brothers killed Rand',5,0,NULL,NULL,'The Chafekar brothers, Damodar, Balkrishna, and Vasudev, were executed by the British for their involvement in the 1897 rebellion against the colonial government.',1,NULL,NULL),(16196,61,17383,8,'History & Civics','en',59,'','Khudiram Bose was hanged to death','explain','Khudiram Bose was hanged to death',6,0,NULL,NULL,'Khudiram Bose was hanged to death in 1908 after he attempted to bomb a train to kill a British judge.',1,NULL,NULL),(16197,61,17384,8,'History & Civics','en',65,'','Answer the following questions in brief.','short_answer','Social work of Vitthal Ramji Shinde DW',1,0,NULL,NULL,'He worked to abolish the Balutedari system, promoted education and self‑respect among Dalits.',1,NULL,NULL),(16198,61,17384,8,'History & Civics','en',65,'','Answer the following questions in brief.','short_answer','Reforms of Rajarshi Shahu Maharaj',2,0,NULL,NULL,'He introduced free compulsory primary education, abolished the Balutedari system and allowed Dalits to practice any occupation.',1,NULL,NULL),(16199,61,17384,8,'History & Civics','en',65,'','Answer the following questions in brief.','short_answer','Read the biography of Dr. Anandibai Joshi in the state of Kolhapur. Joshi',3,1,'61/064.jpg',NULL,'Dr. Anandibai Joshi was the first Indian female doctor, studied in the US and returned to India to practice medicine.',1,'61/064_3.jpg',NULL),(16200,61,17384,8,'History & Civics','en',65,'','Answer the following questions in brief.','short_answer','Read the biography of Rajarshi Shahu Maharaj',4,1,'61/064.jpg',NULL,'Rajarshi Shahu Maharaj was a king of Kolhapur who championed social reforms for Dalits and introduced education and land reforms.',1,'61/064_3.jpg',NULL),(16201,61,17384,8,'History & Civics','en',65,'','Explain the following statements with reasons.','explain','The Government decided to crush down the communist movement.',5,0,NULL,NULL,'The British feared that communists would incite rebellion and threaten colonial rule, so they arrested leaders and tried them in the Meerut Conspiracy Case.',1,NULL,NULL),(16202,61,17384,8,'History & Civics','en',65,'','Explain the following statements with reasons.','explain','Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar - started newspapers like “Muknayak’ Bahishkrut Bharat etc.',6,0,NULL,NULL,'Ambedkar used newspapers to spread his ideas on social justice, equality and to mobilise Dalits.',1,NULL,NULL),(16203,61,17384,8,'History & Civics','en',65,'','Explain the following statements with reasons.','explain','There aroused a need of nation wide workers union',7,0,NULL,NULL,'Workers faced exploitation and lack of rights; a national union was needed to coordinate strikes, demand wages and protect labour rights.',1,NULL,NULL),(16204,61,17385,8,'History & Civics','en',68,'','Answer the following questions in brief','short_answer','The plan of creation of two independent nations, India and Pakistan, was made granting freedom to India.',1,0,NULL,NULL,'The Cabinet Mission of 1946 proposed the creation of two independent nations, India and Pakistan, as part of the plan to grant India freedom.',1,NULL,NULL),(16205,61,17385,8,'History & Civics','en',68,'','Answer the following questions in brief','short_answer','Why did the British take steps towards granting freedom to India?',2,0,NULL,NULL,'After World‑II, the British realized they could not maintain control over India and decided to grant independence to end colonial rule.',1,NULL,NULL),(16206,61,17385,8,'History & Civics','en',68,'','Answer the following questions in brief','short_answer','Identify the person who proposed the Wavell Plan.',3,0,NULL,NULL,'Lord Wavell, the Viceroy of India, proposed the Wavell Plan in 1945.',1,NULL,NULL),(16207,61,17385,8,'History & Civics','en',68,'','Answer the following questions in brief','short_answer','Why did the Muslim League observe 16 August as Direct Action Day?',4,0,NULL,NULL,'The Muslim League observed 16 August as Direct Action Day to demand the creation of Pakistan and to pressure the British and Congress.',1,NULL,NULL),(16208,61,17385,8,'History & Civics','en',68,'','Answer the following questions in brief','short_answer','What were the effects of Direct Action Day?',5,0,NULL,NULL,'Direct Action Day led to widespread communal riots, violence, and loss of life across India.',1,NULL,NULL),(16209,61,17385,8,'History & Civics','en',68,'','Answer the following questions in brief','short_answer','Which demand was advocated by the Muslim League after gaining independence?',6,0,NULL,NULL,'The Muslim League advocated the demand for a separate Muslim state, Pakistan, after independence.',1,NULL,NULL),(16210,61,17385,8,'History & Civics','en',68,'','Answer the following questions in brief','short_answer','Write the name of the ministers who participated in the Cabinet Mission.',7,0,NULL,NULL,'The Cabinet Mission included Lord Mountbatten, Lord Cripps, and Pethick Lawrence, among others.',1,NULL,NULL),(16211,61,17385,8,'History & Civics','en',68,'','Explain the following statements','explain','The Indian National Congress approved the partition.',8,0,NULL,NULL,'The Indian National Congress opposed the partition; it did not approve it.',1,NULL,NULL),(16212,61,17385,8,'History & Civics','en',68,'','Explain the following statements','explain','The workin