lk\",\"All of them\"]','1',1,NULL,NULL),(201682,57,17322,8,'Science','en',57,'','Count phases in each beaker after stirring','fill_blank','After stirring, the number of phases in beaker 1 (sand+water) is ______, in beaker 2 (blue vitriol+water) is ______, in beaker 3 (blue vitriol+sand) is ______.',8,0,NULL,NULL,'2, 1, 2',1,NULL,NULL),(201683,57,17322,8,'Science','en',57,'','Explain difference between homogeneous and heterogeneous mixtures','short_answer','What is the difference between a homogeneous mixture and a heterogeneous mixture?',9,0,NULL,NULL,'In a homogeneous mixture, components are uniformly distributed forming one phase; in a heterogeneous mixture, components are distributed in two or more phases.',1,NULL,NULL),(201684,57,17322,8,'Science','en',57,'','Identify solvent and solute in a salt solution','one_word','In a salt solution, which is the solvent and which is the solute?',10,0,NULL,NULL,'Solvent: water; Solute: salt.',1,NULL,NULL),(201685,57,17322,8,'Science','en',57,'','Identify colloid in water and milk mixture','one_word','In the mixture of water and milk, which component is the colloid?',11,0,NULL,NULL,'Milk is the colloid.',1,NULL,NULL),(201686,57,17322,8,'Science','en',57,'','Explain difference between solution and suspension','short_answer','What is the difference between a solution and a suspension?',12,0,NULL,NULL,'In a solution, solute particles are dissolved and not visible; in a suspension, solid particles are dispersed and may settle.',1,NULL,NULL),(201687,57,17322,8,'Science','en',57,'','Explain difference between solution and colloid','short_answer','What is the difference between a solution and a colloid?',13,0,NULL,NULL,'In a solution, particles are at molecular level; in a colloid, particles are larger (nano) and may scatter light.',1,NULL,NULL),(201688,57,17322,8,'Science','en',57,'','List the various states of matter','short_answer','What are the various states of matter?',14,0,NULL,NULL,'Solid, liquid, gas.',1,NULL,NULL),(201689,