 is 90⁰ and other is 45⁰ 		iii) Remaining two angles are complementary\na) (i) only 		b) (ii) only 		c) (iii) only 		d) (i) and (ii)\n','','','c) (iii) only ','',0,0,0,NULL),(9240,110,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following statement is incorrect?\na) The sum of any two sides of a triangle is greater than the third side.	b) A triangle can have all its angle acute	\nc) A right-angled triangle cannot be equilateral	                     d) difference of any two sides of a triangle is greater than the third side.\n','','','d) difference of any two sides of a triangle is greater than the third side.','',0,0,0,NULL),(9241,110,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In a right isosceles triangle the measure of one of the angles other than the right angle is -----\na) 90⁰		b) 60⁰ 		c) 45⁰ 		d) can’t be determined\n','','','c) 45⁰','',0,0,0,NULL),(9242,110,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following set of angles cannot be the angles of a triangle\na) 67⁰, 51⁰, 62⁰		b) 70⁰, 83⁰, 27⁰		c) 90⁰, 70⁰, 20⁰		d) 40⁰, 132⁰, 18⁰\n','','','d) 40⁰, 132⁰, 18⁰','',0,0,0,NULL),(9243,110,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following is not a set of length of the sides of a triangle?\na) 8, 4, 20 		b) 9, 17, 25 		c) 11, 16, 26 	d) None of these\n','','','a) 8, 4, 20 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(9244,110,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','If two angles of a triangle measure 63⁰ and 27⁰, then it is a /an \na) Acute angle triangle 		b) Obtuse angle triangle 	c) Right angled triangle 		d) None of these\n','','','c) Right angled triangle ','',0,0,0,NULL),(9245,110,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In a triangle, there are 3 different angles. Which of the following statements is /are definitely true about the angles?\ni) Sum of all the angles is 100⁰ 		ii) One angles is obtuse and other two are acute and right angle respectively. 	iii) Sum of any two angles is always less than 180⁰\na) (i) only 		b) (ii) and (iii) both         	c) (iii) only 		d) (i) and (iii) both\n','','','c) (iii) only ','',0,0,0,NULL),(9246,110,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','If the measures of the angles of ΔABC are in ratio 1 : 2 : 3, then the measure of the smallest angle is \na) 30⁰ 		b) 60⁰	c) 90⁰	d) 120⁰\n','','','a) 30⁰','',0,0,0,NULL),(9247,110,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','A triangle can be constructed by taking its sides as ------ cm.\na) 1.8, 2.6, 4.4  	  b) 2, 3, 4 		c) 2.4, 2.4, 6.4 	        d) 3.2, 2.3, 5.5\n','','','b) 2, 3, 4 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(9248,110,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the measure of the largest angle of a triangle, if one angle is 70⁰ and the other two angles are in the ratio 7 : 15.\na) 70⁰	b) 75⁰	c) 80⁰	d) 90⁰\n','','','b) 75⁰','',0,0,0,NULL),(9249,110,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is the measure of each angle of an equilateral triangle?\n','','','In equilateral triangle each angle is 60⁰','',0,0,0,NULL),(9250,110,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Is it possible to draw a triangle whose sides are 5 cm, 8 cm, 9 cm?\n','','','The sum of lengths of any two sides must be greater than third side.\n∴ Taking lengths 5 cm, 8 cm, 9 cm are possible to draw triangle.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9251,110,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','How many lines of symmetry are there in an equilateral triangle?\n','','','Equilateral triangle having three lines of symmetry.','',0,0,0,NULL),(9252,110,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the angles of a ΔABC which are in the ratio 11 : 13 : 12.\n','','','11x + 13x + 12x = 180⁰\n∴ 36x = 180       ⟹ x = 5\n∴ Angles of triangle are 11x = 11 × 5 = 55⁰, 13x = 13 × 5 = 65⁰, 12x = 12 × 5 = 60⁰\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9253,110,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Two angles of a triangle are equal and the third angle measure 80⁰. Find the measure of each of the unknown angles.\n','','','Let unknown angle be x⁰\n∴ x + x + 80 = 180⁰ ---- [sum of angles of triangle]\n∴ 2x = 180 – 80 = 100    ⟹ x = 50⁰\n∴ Unknown angles are 50⁰, 50⁰ respectively.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9254,110,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The angles of a triangle are in the ratio 3 : 5 : 10. Find the measure of each angle.\n','','','3x + 5x + 10x = 180⁰ ----- [sum of angles of triangle]\n∴ 18x = 180⁰     ⟹ x = 10\n∴ Angles of triangle are 3x = 3 × 10 = 30⁰, 5x = 5 × 10 = 50⁰, 10x = 10 × 10 = 100⁰\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9255,110,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The angles of a triangle are in the ratio 6 : 5 : 4. Find the unit digit of the largest angle.\n','','','6x + 5x + 4x = 180⁰  ----- [sum of angles of triangle]\n∴ 15x = 180⁰       ⟹   x = 12⁰\n∴ Angles of triangles are 6x = 6 × 12 = 72⁰, 5x = 5 × 12 = 60⁰, 4x = 4 × 12 = 48⁰ \n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9256,110,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Draw the perpendicular bisector of the given line segments of length 5.3 cm\n','','','Student can draw the figure by given information.','',0,0,0,NULL),(9257,110,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Draw the perpendicular bisector of the given line segments of length 6.7 cm\n','','','Student can draw the figure by given information.','',0,0,0,NULL),(9258,110,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Draw the perpendicular bisector of the given line segments of length 3.8 cm\n','','','Student can draw the figure by given information.','',0,0,0,NULL),(9259,110,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Draw angles of the measures given below and draw their bisectors: 105⁰\n','','','Student can draw the figure by given information.','',0,0,0,NULL),(9260,110,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Draw angles of the measures given below and draw their bisectors : 55⁰\n','','','Student can draw the figure by given information.','',0,0,0,NULL),(9261,110,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Draw angles of the measures given below and draw their bisectors: 90⁰\n','','','Student can draw the figure by given information.','',0,0,0,NULL),(9262,110,'descriptive','1b',1,2