ow many were sold on the third day?','','','Total sold tickets = 36563\nTicket sold on first day + Tickets sold on second day\n= 13608 + 8955 = 22563\nTickets sold on third day = 36563 – 22563 = 14000\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9795,115,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','A city has a population of 4898197. If this includes 18245 men and 14324 women, what is the number of children in the city?','','','Total population of city = 4898197 \nTotal number of men and women = 18245 + 14324 = 32569\nTotal number of children = 4898197 – 32569 = 4865628\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9796,115,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','The management of a certain factory had 5060700 rupees in the labour welfare fund from this fund 2438824 rupees were used for medical expenses, 982324 rupees were spent on the construction of houses and the remaining was put a side for a planting trees. How many was put aside for planting trees?','','','Total fund = Rs. 5060700\nManagement used fund for medical and construction of houses\n= 2438824 + 982324 = 3421148\nPlanting trees aside fund = 5060700 – 3421148 = Rs. 1639552\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9797,115,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve: i) 84924 + 32892 – 43296 		ii) 32848 + 22348 – 24346 ','','','i) 74520		ii) 30850','',0,0,0,NULL),(9798,115,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve: i) 89248 – 28974 + 32894 		ii) 48329 – 28300 + 42432 ','','','i) 93168		ii) 62461','',0,0,0,NULL),(9799,115,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Use the numbers 89348 and 98005 to make a subtraction problem. Solve the problem.','','','Prathmesh wants to buy a laptop worth 98005 rupees. He has 89348 rupees. What is the amount he still needs to be able to buy the laptop?\nAmount need to Prathmesh = 98005 – 89348 = Rs. 8657\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9800,115,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','If the total members are 49000 out of which 27500 are men how many women in this members? ','','','Total number of women member = 49000 – 27500 = 21