 books she packed into each cartoon.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9881,116,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','If 48 sheets are required for making one notebook how many notebooks at the most will 5880 sheets make and how many sheets will be left over?','','','If we divide 5880 ÷ 48, quotient is 122 and remainder = 24\n∴ 24 sheets will be left over.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9882,116,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','What will the quotient be when the smallest five-digit number is divided by the smallest four-digit number?','','','The smallest five-digit number is 10000\nThe smallest four-digit number is 1000\n10000 ÷ 1000 = 10\n∴ The quotient will be 10.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9883,116,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','The 45 persons requires 9000 plants for cultivation. How much plant can be need by one person?','','','Number of plant need by one person = 9000 ÷ 45 = 200','',0,0,0,NULL),(9884,116,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which number, on being multiplied by 29, gives a product 2581?','','','Let the number multiplied by x\n∴ x × 29 = 2581        ⟹ x = 2581/29 = 89\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9885,116,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','The 30 students takes the equipment’s of a cricket game for rupees 1350. What is the cost requires for each students.','','','Cost required for each students = 1350/30 = Rs. 45','',0,0,0,NULL),(9886,116,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','One chair cost Rs. 450 what is the cost of such 87 chairs?','','','Cost of 87 chairs = 87 × 450 = Rs. 39150','',0,0,0,NULL),(9887,116,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','One person requires 8250 rupees for a journey. How many rupees required by such 18 person.','','','Money required to 18 person = 8250 × 18 = 148500','',0,0,0,NULL),(9888,116,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply: i) 4894 × 12 		ii) 43232 × 18 ','','','i) 58728		ii) 778176','',0,0,0,NULL),(9889,116,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply: i) 5483 × 48 		ii) 6832 × 56','','','i) 263184		ii) 382592','',0,0,0,NULL),(9890,116,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply: i) 38943 × 85 		ii) 98754 × 89','','','i) 3310155		ii) 8789106','',0,0,0,NULL),(9891,116,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply: i) 32432 × 38 		ii) 34832 × 75','','','i) 1232416 		ii) 2612400','',0,0,0,NULL),(9892,116,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply: i) 75698 × 68 		ii) 4324 × 895','','','i) 5147464		ii) 3869980','',0,0,0,NULL),(9893,116,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','The contribution for a picnic was 65 rupees each. Altogether, 2925 rupees were collected. How many had paid for the picnic?','','','2925 ÷ 65 = 45\nThe 45 paid for the picnic.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9894,116,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which number, on being multiplied by 56, gives a product of 9688?','','','Let the number multiplied by x\n∴ x × 56 = 9688        ⟹ x = 9688/56 = 173\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9895,116,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','From a total of 10000 rupees, Anna donated 7000 rupees to a school. The remaining amount was to be divided equally among students as the ‘all- round student’ prize. What was the amount of each prize?','','','The total rupees = 10000, donated rupees = 7000\nRemaining rupees = 3000\nThe remaining amount was to be divided equally among six students\n∴ The prize for each student = Rs. 500\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9896,116,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','An amount of 260 rupees each was collected from 50 students for a picnic. If 11450 rupees were spent for the picnic, what is the amount left over?','','','The total amount collected from 50 students = 260 × 50 = Rs. 13000\nThe rupees spent for the picnic = Rs. 11450\nThe amount left over = 13000 – 11450 = 1550\n∴ The amount left over = Rs. 1550\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9897,116,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','A shopkeeper bought a sack of 50 kg of sugar for 1750 rupees. As the price of sugar tell, he had to sell it at the rate of 32 rupees per kilo. How much less money did he get than he had spent?','','','The cost of 50 kg sugar was sold at rate 32 rupees = 50 × 32 = Rs. 1600\n∴ The less amount got by him = 1750 – 1600 = Rs. 150\n∴ The less amount got by a shopkeeper = Rs. 150\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9898,116,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','A shopkeeper bought 7 pressure cookers at the rate of 1870 rupees per cooker. He sold them all for a total of 14230 rupees. Did he get less or more money than he had spent?','','','The cost of 7 cookers = 7 × 1870 = 13090\nHe sold all for a total of 14230 rupees. He got more money than he had spent\n= 14230 – 13090 = Rs. 1140\n∴ He got rupees 1140 more than he had spent.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9899,116,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Fourteen families in a society together bought 8 sacks of wheat, each weighing 98 kilos. If they shared all the wheat equally, what was the share of each family?','','','The weight of 8 sacks = 98 × 8 = 784 kilo\nShare of each family = 784 ÷ 14 = 56\n∴ Each family share = 56 kilo.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9900,116,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','The capacity of an overhead water tank is 3000 liters. There are 16 families living in this building. If each family uses 225 liters every day, will the water be enough for all the families? If not, what will be the daily shortfall be?','','','Total water used = 225 × 16 = 3600\n3600 liters water used by the families. \nTotal capacity = 3000 liter\nThe water is not enough for all the families = 3600 – 3000 = 600 liter\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9901,116,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','An amount of 250 rupees each was collected from 75 students for a picnic 15750 rupees were spent for the picnic, what is the amount left over.','','','Total amount collected = 250 × 75 = 18750\nAmount left over = 18750 – 15750 = Rs. 3000\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9902,116,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','If the cost of 27 chairs is 17550 rupees what is the cost of one chair. If the person gives 20000 rupees to the shopkeeper how much will remains left behind?','','','Cost of one chair = 17550 ÷ 27 = Rs. 650\nAmount left behind = 20000 – 17550 = Rs. 2450\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(9904,114,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) How are the number 10000010 written in words?\na) Ten ten thousand and ten 	  b) One crore and ten 	  c) Ten lakh and one 	d) Ten lakh and ten \n','','','b) One crore and ten','',0,0,0,NULL),(9905,114,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','How is the number six lakh sixty thousand sixty written in figures?\na) 660660 		b) 606606 		c) 660060 		d) 606060 \n','','','c) 660060 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(9906,114,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write the number ninety lakh and nine in figures.\na) 900009 		b) 9000009 		c) 90000009 	d) 90009\n','','','b) 9000009 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(9907,114,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write seven lakh twenty-seven thousand in figures.\na) 72070 		b) 702700		c) 72700 		d) 727000\n','','','d) 727000','',0,0,0,NULL),(9908,114,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write eight lakh in figures.\na) 80000 		b) 800000 		c) 800008 		d) 8000000\n','','','b) 800000 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(9909,114,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','How is ninety-nine lakh nine hundred and nine written in figures?\na) 990909		b) 9900990		c) 9900909		d) 9900099\n','','','c) 9900909','',0,0,0,NULL),(9910,114,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write five forty-three thousand four hundred and forty-six in numerals. \na) 543464		b) 543644		c) 543046		d) 543446\n','','','d) 543446','',0,0,0,NULL),(9911,114,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write the number 4685270 in words.\na) Forty-six lakh eighty-five thousand two hundred and seventy.\nb) Forty-six lakh eighty-five thousands thousand and seventy\nc) Four lakh sixty-eight thousand two hundred two hundred and seventy.\nd) Forty-six lakh fifty-eight thousand two hundred and seventy\n','','','a) Forty-six lakh eighty-five thousand two hundred a