ptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the square root of 1369','','','√1369 = √37 × 37 = 37','',0,0,0,NULL),(18794,155,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write the following sentences with the help of indices of 10.          a) The diameter of sun is 1400000000 m          b) The velocity of light is 300000000 m/sec\n','','','a) 1400000000 = 1.4 × 10⁹ m\nb) 300000000 = 3 × 10⁸ m/sec\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18795,155,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Compare the following : i) 2.7 × 10¹² ; 1.5 × 10⁸ 		ii) 4 × 10¹⁴ ; 3 × 10¹⁷','','','i) 2.7 × 10¹² ; 1.5 × 10⁸\n2.7 × 10¹² = 27 × 10¹¹ = 27000 × 10⁸ and 1.5 × 10⁸\n27000 > 1.5\n∴ 2.7 × 10¹² > 1.5 × 10⁸\nii) 4 × 10¹⁴ ; 3 × 10¹⁷\n3 × 10¹⁷ = 3000 × 10¹⁴\n∴ 4 × 10¹⁴ < 3 × 10¹⁷\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18796,155,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','If [5⁹ × 5³] ÷ [5¹⁵ ÷ 5³] = 5ᵐ then find the value of m.','','','[5⁹ × 5³] ÷ [5¹⁵ ÷ 5³] = 5ᵐ\n5¹² ÷ 5¹² = 5ᵐ\n5⁰ = 5ᵐ\n∴ m = 0\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18797,155,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Express the following as power of rational number : i) 16/81 		ii) -32/3125','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(18798,155,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Simplify : i) (-3)² × (-5)² 	ii) (-2)³ × (-10)³','','','i) (-3)² × (-5)² = 9 × 25 = 225\nii) (-2)³ × (-10)³ = -8 × (-1000) = 8000\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18799,156,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The point of intersection of X and Y axis called as -----\na) X- axis 		b) Y – axis 		c) Origin 		d) can’t say\n','','','c) Origin','',0,0,0,NULL),(18800,156,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In a graph, vertical line is called as ------\na) X- axis 		b) Y – axis 		c) Origin 		d) can’t say\n','','','b) Y – axis ','',0,0,0,NULL),(18801,156,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In a graph, horizontal line is called as -----\na) X- axis 		b) Y – axis 		c) Origin 		d) can’t say\n','','','a) X- axis ','',0,0,0,NULL),(18802,156,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In a graph, X- axis and Y-axis intersect at ------\na)