xt Book','','The bar graph given below shows the interest of boys and girls in different activities. Answer the following questions : a) In which two activities, 55 girls are interested together? 		b) How many less boys are interested in yoga, dance and art altogether than girls?','','','a) Dance = 35 and Yoga = 20\nDance + Yoga = 35 + 20 = 55\nb) Number of boys in Yoga, dance and art = 20 + 25 + 10 = 55\nNumber of girls in Yoga, dance and art = 20 + 35 + 15 = 70\nNumber of girls more than boys = 70 – 55 = 15\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(18810,156,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','The given bar graph shows the buyers of DVDs and CDs. Study the graph and answer the following questions : a) In which music category the differences between DVD buyers and CD buyers is minimum? 		b) What is the ratio of Pop music CD buyers to Jazz music DVD buyers?','','','a) Pop\nb) 55 : 80 = 11/16 \n','',1,0,0,NULL),(18811,156,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','The means of transportation used by children in a school is given below. Draw a joint bar graph.','','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(18812,156,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Marks obtained by a student in both terms for different subjects is given below. draw a joint bar graph.','','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(18813,156,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','The number of trees planted by students of different division of seventh standard is given below. Draw a joint bar graph.','','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(18814,156,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','Read the graph and answer the question below : a) What data is shown on X – axis?          b) What data is shown on Y – axis?       c) On which day had the highest temperature?        d) On which day is the minimum temperature the highest?        e) On Thursday, what is the difference between the minimum and maximum temperature?       f) On which day is the difference between the minimum and maximum temperature the greatest? \n','','','a) Days are shown on the X-axis\nb) Temperature is shown on the Y-axis\nc) The highest temperature was Monday.\nd) The minimum temperature was highest on Wednesday.\ne) The difference between the minimum and maximum temperature on Thursday is (29.5 – 15) = 14.5⁰C\nf) The difference between the minimum and maximum temperature is greatest on Thursday.\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(18815,156,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','The number of boys and girls in a school is given. Draw a joint bar graph to show this information.','','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(18816,156,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','The number of sapling planted by schools on WORLD Tree Day is given in the table below. Draw a joint bar graph to show these figures.','','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(18817,156,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','The percentage of literate people in the states of Maharashtra and Gujrat are given below. Draw a joint bar graph for this data.','','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(18818,156,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','The number of Men and Women participated in Swatch Bharat Abhiyan in different districts given below. Draw a joint bar graph.','','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(18819,156,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','The table below shows the number of people who had the different juices at a juice bar on a Saturday and a Sunday. Draw a joint bar graph for this data.','','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(18820,156,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','The following numbers of votes were cast at 5 polling booths during the Gram Panchayat elections. Draw a joint bar graph for this data.','','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(18821,156,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','The maximum and minimum temperatures of five Indian cities are given in ⁰C. Draw a joint bar graph for this data.','','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(18822,156,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','The numbers of children vaccinated in one day at the government hospitals in Solapur and Pune are given in the table. Draw a joint bar graph for this data.','','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(18823,156,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','There are four pooling booths for a certain election. The numbers of men and women who cast their votes at each booth is given in the table below. Draw a joint bar graph.','','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(18824,157,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Simplify (3x – 11y) – (17x + 13y) and choose the right answer.\na) 7x – 12y 		b) -14x – 54y 	        c) -3 (5x + 4y)           	d) -2 (7x + 12y)\n','','','d) -2 (7x + 12y)','',0,0,0,NULL),(18825,157,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The product of (23x²y³z) and (-15x³yz²) is ------\na) -345x⁵y⁴z³      	b) 345x²y³z⁵ 		c) 145x³y²z 		d) 170x³y²z³\n','','','a) -345x⁵y⁴z³  ','',0,0,0,NULL),(18826,157,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','An algebraic expression having two terms is called as ------\na) Monomial         	b) binomial 		c) Trinomial 		d) Polynomial\n','','','b) binomial ','',0,0,0,NULL),(18827,157,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The solution of the equation 3x – 1/2 = 5/2 + x\na) 5/3 		b) 7/2 		c) 4 		d) 3/2\n','','','d) 3/2','',0,0,0,NULL),(18828,157,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The value of 1/2 mn + 4/3 mn is -----\na) 11/6 mn 		b) 4/6 mn 		c) 5/6 mn 		d) -11/6 mn\n','','','a) 11/6 mn','',0,0,0,NULL),(18829,157,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The