20x + 2y 		d) 10x + y\n','','','c) 20x + 2y ','',0,0,0,NULL),(18840,157,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The HCF of 14x³y² and 21y³z² is -----\na) 7xyz 		b) 7x²y 		c) 7y² 		d) xyz\n','','','c) 7y² 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(18841,157,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','If 7x + 3 = 17, then what is the value of 7x – 3?\na) 14 		b) 11 		c) 0 		d) -3\n','','','b) 11','',0,0,0,NULL),(18842,157,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','If 5x – 3/4 = 2x – 2/3, then the value of x is ------\na) 1/12 		b) 1/4 		c) 1/36 		d) 36\n','','','c) 1/36 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(18843,157,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','If (2n + 5) = 3(3n – 10), then the value of n is ------\na) 5 			b) 3 			c) 2/5 		d) 2/3\n','','','a) 5 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(18844,157,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve for x : 18 – (2x – 12) = 8x \na) 15 			b) 26 		c) 3 			d) 13/5\n','','','c) 3 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(18845,157,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve for m : 3m + 2(m + 2) = 20 – (2m – 5) \na) 2 			b) 3 		c) 5 			d) 6\n','','','b) 3 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(18846,157,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The statement “Thrice a number x decreased by 5 is equal to 27” is expressed in equation as ----\na) 5 – 3x = 27 		b) 3x – 5 = 27 	         c) x/3 – 5 = 27 	d) 3x – 27 + 5 = 0  \n','','','b) 3x – 5 = 27','',0,0,0,NULL),(18847,157,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Add : -3x – 8x + 5x ','','','-6x','',0,0,0,NULL),(18848,157,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Add : 2/3 ab – 5/7 ab','','','-1/21 ab','',0,0,0,NULL),(18849,157,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Add : -2p² + 7p² ','','','5p²','',0,0,0,NULL),(18850,157,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Add : 9p + 16q ; 13p + 2q','','','9p + 16q + 13p + 2q = 22p + 18q','',0,0,0,NULL),(18851,157,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Add : 2a + 6b + 8c ; 16a + 13c + 18b','','','2a + 6b + 8c + 16a + 13c + 18b = 18a + 24b + 21c','',0,0,0,NULL),(18853,157,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Subtract the second expression from the first : (4xy – 9z) ; (3xy – 16z)','','','(4xy – 9z) - (3xy – 16z) = 4xy – 9z – 3xy + 16z = xy + 7z','',0,0,0,NULL),(18854,157,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply : 3x × 12y ','','','36xy','',0,0,0,NULL),(18855,157,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply : (-12x) × (3y²)','','','-36xy²','',0,0,0,NULL),(18856,157,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply : 2a² × 3ab²','','','6a³b²','',0,0,0,NULL),(18857,157,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply : (-3x²) × (-4xy)','','','12x³y','',0,0,0,NULL),(18858,157,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply : x (x + y)','','','x² + xy','',0,0,0,NULL),(18859,157,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply : (7x – 6y) × 3z','','','21xz – 18yz','',0,0,0,NULL),(18860,157,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve : x + 7 = 4','','','x = 4 – 7 = -3 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(18861,157,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve : 4p = 12','','','p = 3','',0,0,0,NULL),(18862,157,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve : m – 5 = 4','','','m = 4 + 5 = 9','',0,0,0,NULL),(18863,157,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve : t/3 = 6','','','t = 6 × 3 = 18','',0,0,0,NULL),(18864,157,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve : 10 = 2y + 5','','','2y = 10 – 5 = 5     ∴ y = 5/2 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(18865,157,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve : (6a – 5b – 8c) + (15b + 2a – 5c)','','','8a + 10b – 13c','',0,0,0,NULL),(18866,157,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve :  4(x + 12) = 8','','','x + 12 = 2     ∴ x = 2 – 12 = -10','',0,0,0,NULL),(18867,157,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Add : 13x² - 12y² ; 6x² - 8y²','','','13x² - 12y² + 6x² - 8y² = 19x² - 20y²','',0,0,0,NULL),(18868,157,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Add : 17a²b² + 16c ; 28c – 28a²b²','','','17a²b² + 16c + 28c – 28a²b² = -11a²b² + 44c','',0,0,0,NULL),(18869,157,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Add : 3y² - 10y + 16 ; 2y – 7 ','','','3y² - 10y + 16 + 2y – 7 = 3y² - 8y + 9','',0,0,0,NULL),(18870,157,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Add : -3y² + 10y – 16 ; 7y² + 8','','','-3y² + 10y – 16 + 7y² + 8 = 4y² + 10y – 8 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(18871,157,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Subtract the second expression from the first : 16x + 23y + 12z ; 9x – 27 y + 14z','','','16x + 23y + 12z – (9x – 27 y + 14z)\n= 16x + 23y + 12z – 9x + 27y – 14z = 7x + 50y – 2z \n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18872,157,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Subtract the second expression from the first : (5xy + 4y + 7z) ; (x + 2y + 3z)','','','(5xy + 4y + 7z) - (x + 2y + 3z)\n= 5xy + 4y + 7z – x – 2y – 3z = 5xy + 2y + 4z\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18873,157,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Subtract the second expression from the first : (14x² + 8xy + 3y²) ; (26x² - 8xy – 17y²)','','','(14x² + 8xy + 3y²) - (26x² - 8xy – 17y²)\n= 14x² + 8xy + 3y² - 26x² + 8xy + 17y²\n= -12x² + 16xy + 20y²\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18874,157,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply : (3x + 4y) × (5x + 7y)','','','(3x + 4y) × (5x + 7y) = 3x(5x + 7y) + 4y(3x + 5y)\n= 15x² + 21xy + 12xy + 20y²\n= 15x² + 33xy + 20y²\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18875,157,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the area of a rectangular field whose length is (2x + 7) m and breadth is (x + 2) m.','','','Area of rectangle = length × breadth\n∴ Area of rectangle = (2x + 7)(x + 2) \n= 2x(x + 2) + 7(x + 2) = 2x² + 4x + 7x + 14\n= 2x² + 11x + 14\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18876,157,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply : i) 16xy × 18xy 		ii) 23xy² × 4yz²','','','i) 16xy × 18xy = 288x²y²\nii) 23xy² × 4yz² = 92xy³z²\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18877,157,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve : i) 2x + 2 = 8 		ii) 3x – 5 = x – 17 ','','','i) 2x + 2 = 8      ⟹ 2x = 8 – 2 = 6    ⟹ x = 3\nii) 3x – 5 = x – 17   ⟹ 3x – x = -17 + 5   ⟹ 2x = -12\n∴ x = -6\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18878,157,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','The length of a rectangle is 1 cm more than twice its breadth. If the perimeter of the rectangle is 50 cm, find its length.','','','Let breadth of rectangle be x cm then length = 2x + 1\nPerimeter of rectangle = 2[l + b]\n∴ 50 = 2[(2x + 1) + x]    ⟹ 3x + 1 = 25     ⟹ 3x = 24\n∴ x = 8\n∴ length = 2x + 1 = 2(8) + 1 = 17 cm and breadth = x = 8 cm\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18879,157,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve : i) 4x + 1/2 = 9/2 		ii) 5m – 4 = 1','','','i) 4x = 9/2 – 1/2  = 8/2 = 4\n∴ x = 1\nii) 5m = 1 + 4 = 5      ∴ m = 1\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18880,157,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve : i) 6x – 1 = 3x + 8 		ii) 2(x – 4) = 4x + 2','','','i) 6x – 3x = 8 + 1    ∴ 3x = 9     ∴   x = 3\nii) 2(x – 4) = 4x + 2      ⟹ 2x – 8 = 4x + 2 \n∴ 2x – 4x = 2 + 8     ⟹ -2x = 10     ⟹ x = -5\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18881,157,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve : (3x + 2y) (7x – 8y)','','','3x(7x – 8y) + 2y(7x – 8y)\n= 21x² - 24xy + 14xy – 16y² \n= 21x² - 10xy – 16y²\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18882,157,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve : (7m – 5n) – (-4n – 11m)','','','7m – 5n + 4n + 11m = 18m – n ','',0,0,0,NULL),(18883,157,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve : (11m – 12n + 3p) – (9m + 7n – 8p)','','','11m – 12n + 3p – 9m – 7n + 8p \n= 2m – 19n + 11p\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18884,157,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve : 4(x + 12) = 8','','','x + 12 = 2       ∴   x = 2 – 12 = -10','',0,0,0,NULL),(18885,157,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve : 3y + 4 = 5y – 6 ','','','3y – 5y = -6 – 4 \n-2y = -10       ∴ y = 5\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18886,157,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Subtract the second expression from the first : (6x² + 7xy + 16y²) ; (16x² - 17xy)','','','(6x² + 7xy + 16y²) - (16x² - 17xy) \n= 6x² + 7xy + 16y² - 16x² + 17xy = -10x² + 24xy +16y²\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18887,157,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Subtract the second expression from the first : (4x + 16z) – (19y – 14z + 16x)','','','(4x + 16z) – (19y – 14z + 16x)\n= 4x + 16z – 19y + 14z – 16x = -12x + 30z – 19y \n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18888,157,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply : i) (12a + 17b) × 4c 		ii) (4x + 5y) × (9x + 7y)','','','i) (12a + 17b) × 4c = 48ac + 68bc\nii) 4x(9x + 7y) + 5y(9x + 7y)\n= 36x² + 28xy + 45xy + 35y² = 36x² + 73xy + 35y²\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18889,157,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','A rectangle is (8x + 5) cm long and (5x + 3) cm broad. Find its area.','','','Area of rectangle = l × b = (8x + 5) × (5x + 3)\n= 8x(5x + 3) + 5(5x + 3) = 40x² + 24x + 25x + 15\n= 40x² + 49x + 15\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18890,157,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','The sum of two consecutive natural numbers is 69. Find the numbers.','','','Let two consecutive natural number be x and x+ 1\n∴ x + x + 1 = 69      ⟹  2x = 69 – 1 = 68\n∴ x = 34\n∴ The numbers are x = 34 and x + 1 = 34 + 1 = 35\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18891,157,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve : i) 5(x + 1) = 74 		ii) 3 (2m – 1) = 12','','','i) 5x + 5 = 74      ⟹  5x = 74 – 5 = 69\n∴ x = 69/5\nii) 2m – 1 = 4     ⟹  2m = 4 + 1 = 5\n∴ m = 5/2 \n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18892,157,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Classify the following algebraic expressions as monomials, binomials, trinomials or polynomials : x²y - y², -x³, 3x² - 3y² + 2xy, 8y, x² - y², m² - mn + n² - m²n²','','','Monomial : -x³, 8y\nBinomial : x²y – y², x² - y²\nTrinomial : 3x² - 3y² + 2xy\nPolynomial : m² - mn + n² - m²n²\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18893,157,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Simplify : (5p² + 3q² - pq) – (4pq – 5q² - 3p²) + (p² + 3q²)','','','(5p² + 3q² - pq) – (4pq – 5q² - 3p²) + (p² + 3q²)\n= 5p² + 3q² - pq – 4pq + 5q² + 3p² + p² + 3q²\n= 9p² + 11q² - 5pq \n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18894,157,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','What should be added to (x² + xy + y²) to get (2x² + 3xy)','','','Let p(x) be added, we get, \np(x) = 2x² + 3xy – (x² + xy + y²) = 2x² + 3xy - x² - xy - y²\n= x² + 2xy - y²\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18895,157,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve : i) (21b – 32) + (7b – 20) 		ii) (4m² - 3mn + 8) - (-m² + 5mn) ','','','i) 21b – 32 + 7b – 20 = 20b – 52 \nii) 4m² - 3mn + 8 + m² - 5mn = 5m² - 8mn + 8\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18896,157,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Classify the following algebraic expressions as monomials, binomials, trinomials or polynomials : 7x, 5y – 7z, 3x³ - 5x² - 11, 1 – 8a – 7a² - 7a³, 5m – 3, a, 4, 3y² - 7y + 5.','','','Monomials : 7x, a, 4\nBinomial : 5y – 7z, 5m – 3\nTrinomial : 3x³ - 5x² - 11, 3y² - 7y + 5\nPolynomial : 1 – 8a – 7a² - 7a³\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18897,157,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Rakesh’s age is less than Sanika’s age by 5 years. The sum of their ages is 27 years. How old are they?','','','Let Sanika age be x years then Rakesh age be x – 5 years\nAccording to given condition, x + x – 5 = 27\n∴ 2x = 32      ⟹ x = 16\n∴ Sanika’s age be 16 years and Rakesh age be x – 5 = 16 – 5 = 11 years\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18898,157,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','When planting a forest, the number of jambhul trees planted was greater than the number of Ashoka trees by 60. If there are altogether 200 trees of these two types, how many jambhul trees were planted?','','','Let number of Ashoka trees planted be x, then number of Jambhul trees be (x + 60)\nAccording to their condition, x + x + 60 = 200\n∴ 2x = 200 – 60 = 140         ⟹ x = 70\n∴ Number of Ashoka tree planted 70 and Jambhul tree plated x + 60 = 70 + 60 = 130.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18899,157,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Shubhangi has twice as many 20 rupees notes as she has 50 rupees notes. Altogether, she has 2700 rupees. How many notes does she have?','','','Let Shubhangi have Rs. 50 notes be x, then Rs. 20 notes be 2x\nAccording to given condition, 50x + 20(2x) = 2700\n∴ 50x + 40x = 2700      ⟹ 90x = 2700\n∴ x = 30\n∴ Rs. 50 notes be 30 and Rs. 20 notes be 2x = 2 × 30 = 60\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18900,157,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Virat made twice as many runs as Rohit. The total of their scores is 2 less than a double century. How many runs did each of them make?','','','Let Rohit made by run be x, then Virat made runs be 2x\nTotal score = 2(100) – 2 = 198\nAccording to the given condition, x + 2x = 198\n∴ 3x = 198       ⟹ x = 66\n∴ Rohit make runs be 66 and Virat makes runs be 2x = 2 × 66 = 132\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18901,157,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','A natural number is 4 more than twice the other number. If their sum is 31, find the numbers.','','','Let 1st natural number be x then other natural number be 2x + 4\n∴ x + 2x + 4 = 31      ⟹ 3x = 31 – 4 = 27   \n∴ x = 9\n∴ Natural numbers be x = 9 and 2x + 4 = 2(9) + 4 = 22\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18902,157,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','The base of a triangle is (2x + 4) cm and its height is (3y + 5) cm, find its area.','','','Area of triangles = 1/2 × base × height\n= 1/2 × (2x + 4) (3y + 5) = 1/2 × [6xy + 10x + 12y + 20]\n= 1/2 × 2[3xy + 5x + 6y + 10] \n= 3xy + 5x + 6y + 10\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18903,157,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','If side of a square is of (x + 4) cm, find its perimeter and area.','','','Perimeter of square = 4 × side \n= 4 × (x + 4) = 4x + 16\nArea of square = (side)² = (x + 4)(x + 4)\n= x² + 8x + 16\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(18904,157,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve : i) (3m + 5) × (2m – 8) 			ii) 5(8 + y) = 3y + 13','','','i) 3m(2m – 8) + 5(2m – 8)\n= 6m² - 24m + 10m – 40 \n= 6m² - 14m – 40 \nii) 40 + 5y = 3y + 13\n∴ 5y – 3y = 13 – 40 \n∴ 2y = -27\n∴ y = -27/2\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(19221,163,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','If 17/21 < */21, then * = ?\na) 18 		b) 15 		c) 17 		d) 16\n','','','a) 18','',0,0,0,NULL),(19222,163,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the fractions 1/3, 1/9, 1/5, 1/6 is the smallest?\na) 1/3		b) 1/9 		c) 1/5 	