the empty space.','',1,0,0,NULL),(31402,309,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','Divide the given figure into four parts in such a way that the area and shape of each part is the same. Colour the parts with different colours.','','','The given figure is divided into four similar parts by different shades as shown below.','',1,0,1,NULL),(31403,309,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Three rounds of wire fence have to be put around a field. If a field is 50 m long and 30 m wide, how much wire will be needed?','','','Length = 50 m, breadth = 30 m\nPerimeter of rectangle = 2 × [length + breadth]\n               = 2 × [50 + 30] = 2 × 80 = 160 m\n∴ 160 m wire will be needed.','',0,0,0,NULL),(31404,309,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','How much wire will be needed to put a triple fence around a square plot with side 30 m? What will be the total cost of the wire at ` 70 per metre?','','','Side of square = 30 m\nPerimeter of square = 4 × side = 4 × 30 = 120 m\nA square plot having triple fence = 3 × 120 = 360 m\nCost of wire per meter is Rs. 70\n∴ Total cost of fencing = 70 × 360 = ₹ 25200.','',0,0,0,NULL),(31405,309,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','A wall that is 4 m long and 3 m wide has to be painted. If the labour charges are ` 25 per sq m, what is the cost of labour for painting this wall?','','','Length = 4 m, breadth = 3 m\nArea of rectangle (wall) = length × breadth = 4 × 3 = 12 m²\nLabour charges = ₹ 25 per square meter\n∴ Cost of painting a wall = 25 × 12 = ₹ 300','',0,0,0,NULL),(31406,309,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','One side of a square room is 4 m. If the cost of labour for laying 1 sq m of the floor is 35 rupees, what will be the total cost of labour?','','','Side of square = 4 m\nArea of square shaped wall = side × side = 4 × 4 = 16 m²\nArea of floor = 4 × 16 = 64 m²\nCost of labour per sq m is ₹ 35\n∴ Cost of floor = 35 × 64 = ₹ 2240.','',0,0,0,NULL),(31407,376,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','त्रिकोणाच्या