ause malnutrition.   ','',0,0,0,NULL),(31839,120,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which are the ways to prevent malnutrition?','','','Taking wholesome food and balanced diet is the way to prevent malnutrition. Similarly as per our age and type of work, we have to manage our diet to prevent malnutrition. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(31840,166,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','How and where is food wasted?','','','i) Food gets wasted during the transportation from farm to market.\nii) Improper handling, unsuitable transport options and wrong kind of transportation results in a lot of food wastage.\niii) If food storage is not done properly, the grains will get infested with insects, rats, micro-organisms etc.\niv) At home too, if proper care is not taken, the food is wasted\nv)  Many people waste food while making different preparations. The prepared food too is wasted due to carelessness. \n','',0,0,0,NULL),(31841,167,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Why is the weight of the same object different on different planets?','','',') The gravitational force is act on the mass of an object is called weight.\nii) The gravitational force exerted by the earth is not constant at everywhere.\niii) It is different at different places on the earth\niv) Weight of an object is depends upon the distance of the planets\nv) Hence, the weight of the same object is a different on the different planets.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(31842,167,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','What precautions will you take make accurate measurement in day-to-day affairs?','','','The following precautions need to be taken for accurate measurement.\ni) While buying grocery or any other food stuffs balance and weight should be checked.\nii) While, filling petrol that the digital display that indicates litres of petrol should be seen carefully.\niii) Check the balance while buying vegetables that is stable with its pointer upright, if weights are made up of metals and pans of the balance are proper.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(31843,169,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Explain in brief lighting strike.','','','i) When electrically charged clouds comes over the tall building or tree electricity is attracted towards a tall building or tree if lightning strike there.\nii) An opposite electric charge is generated due to induction.\niii) due to the attraction between the opposite charges on the cloud and the building, the charge on the cloud flows towards the building. This is called a lightning strike.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(31844,171,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is an earthquake?','','','The vibrations and the cracking up of the earth’s crust is called an earthquake.','',0,0,0,NULL),(31845,171,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What will happen if an earthquake and volcanic eruption occur at the bottom of the sea?','','','Tremendous energy comes out of the earth’s crust at the time of earthquake. If such movements occur at the bottom of the sea, the huge waves are formed.','',0,0,0,NULL),(31846,171,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','What gives rise to a storm? What are their effects?','','','i) There is formation of high and low air pressure belts in the atmosphere.\nii) This causes strong winds to blow.\niii) The weather suddenly changes due to this resulting into storms.\nEffects of storm :\ni) there is a large scale damage to the property and life.\nii) The storm affected are greatly damaged.\niii) The electric supply and transportation is disrupted.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(31848,129,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','What is the point of difference between the place of electron in the atomic models of Thomson and Rutherford?','','','In Thomson\'s atomic model, electrons are embedded in the positive charge distributed throughout the atom, whereas in Rutherford’s atomic model electrons revolve around the nucleus.','',0,0,0,NULL),(31849,129,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','Diagrammatic sketch and electronic configuration of Magnesium (Atomic number 12)\n','','','Diagram : ','',0,0,1,NULL),(31850,129,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','Diagrammatic sketch and electronic configuration of Argon (Atomic number 18)\n','','','Diagram : ','',0,0,1,NULL),(32154,33,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Convert the given rational number into decimal form : 7/9\n','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(32155,33,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Convert the given rational number into decimal form : 8/13\n','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(32156,33,'descriptive','3',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Convert the given rational number into decimal form : 5/16\n','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(32157,33,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Convert the given rational number into decimal form : 11/7\n','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(32158,79,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','A shopkeeper decides to sell a certain item at a certain price. he marks the price of the item, by increasing the decided price by 30%. While selling the item, he offers 20% discount. Find how many percent he gets more on the decided price.','','','Solution : The percentage increase in price and profit depends upon the decided price of the item. By assuming decided price to be Rs. 100 the solution of the problem will be easy.\n∴ Let the decided price be Rs. 100\n∴ he marks the price as Rs. 130\n∴ MP = Rs. 130\nDiscount = (20/100) × 130 = Rs. 26\n∴ SP = 130 – 26 = Rs. 104\n∴ If the decided price is Rs. 100, he get Rs. 104\nHence, he gets 4% more than his decided price.','',0,0,0,NULL),(32267,261,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','19 ही संख्या रोमन अंकामध्ये खालीलपैकी कोणती येईल?\n   a) XVIIII			b) IXX 		c) XIX 			d) XXI\n\nउकल : ----------------------','','','c) XIX','',0,0,0,NULL),(32268,261,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','XVII ही रोमन संख्या आंतरराष्ट्रीय संख्या मध्ये खालीलपैकी कोणती येईल?\n         a) 12 			b) 17 			c) 12 		d) 21\n\nउकल : ----------------------','','','b) 17 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(32269,261,'mcq','1