 See the picture and write down a dialogue to describe it. (Picture 2) ------------- 3M\n\nA : -------------------------------------------------------------- \n\nB : ----------------------------------- ---------------------------\n\nA : -----------------------------------------------------------------\n\nB : ------------------------------------------------------------------------','',' A : may I come in please, Teacher? \n B : Yes. Please come in.\n2) A : Where are you going? \n    B : We are going to the playground. \n   A : Would you like to come with us? \n   B : Yes. Please wait for me.','',1,0,0,NULL),(36503,389,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read The passage carefully and answer the following questions \nThe Golden Feather\nOne day, the Queen was taking a walk in her garden, when she found a big, beautiful golden feather.\nThen she met a little man. He said, \"If you give me that feather, I will give you three big diamonds.\" \"Sorry!\" said the Queen.\nThen she met an old woman. The old woman said, \"If you give me that feather, I will give you a necklace of twenty-one pearls\"\n\"Sorry!\" said the Queen.\nThen she met the King. The King said, \"If you give me that feather. I will give you ninety-nine gold coins. \"Sorry!\" said the Queen.\nThen she met the little prince. He said,\n\"Oh, Mamma What a bright beautiful feather!\" \"Take it, my dear,\" said the Queen \"Keep it safe\"\n1) Who as taking a walk? -------------------------- 1M\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------\n2) Where was the queen taking a walk? ---------------- 1M\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------- \n3) Write and complete the table -------------------------- 3M\n    What did the following (persons) people offer the queen?\n People They offered\n i) Little man                              ------------------------- \nii) ---------------                            a necklace of twenty-one pearls. \niii) The king                                    ------------------------- \n','','','1) The queen was taking a walk \n2) The queen was taking a walk in the garden.\n3) i) three big diamond           ii) Old woman            \n             iii) ninety nine gold coins','',0,0,0,NULL),(36504,389,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read The passage carefully and answer the following questions \nThe Golden Feather\nOne day, the Queen was taking a walk in her garden, when she found a big, beautiful golden feather.\nThen she met a little man. He said, \"If you give me that feather, I will give you three big diamonds.\" \"Sorry!\" said the Queen.\nThen she met an old woman. The old woman said, \"If you give me that feather, I will give you a necklace of twenty-one pearls\"\n\"Sorry!\" said the Queen.\nThen she met the King. The King said, \"If you give me that feather. I will give you ninety-nine gold coins. \"Sorry!\" said the Queen.\nThen she met the little prince. He said,\n\"Oh, Mamma What a bright beautiful feather!\" \"Take it, my dear,\" said the Queen \"Keep it safe\"\n1) What did the queen find? ---------------------------- 1M\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) Complete the following sentences -------------------------- 2M\n     a) The queen found -----------------------------------------------\n     \n      b) The queen gave the golden feather to --------------------\n3) Read the story and find the numbers from it ----------------- 2M\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------','','','1) The queen found a big, beautiful golden feather.\n2) a) The queen found a big, beautiful golden feather.\n     b) the princes  \n3) one, three, twenty-one, ninety-nine\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(36505,389,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Read the following sentences and underline the numbers : ------------ 3M\n i) They had two daughters\n ii) January has thirty-one days \niii) There are seven days in