,'',1,0,0,NULL),(36555,393,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Look at the pictures and frame the sentences for each of the following words ------------------------------ 5M\n[in, on, under, near, infront of, behind]\n','\nAns. : 1) --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           2) -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           3) ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          4) --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          5) ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           6) -------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','1) There is a boy in the house.\n2) The girl is playing on the slide.\n3) The cow is sitting under the tree.\n4) The house is near the tree.\n5) The slide is near the house.\n6) There is a car infront of the house.\n7) There are hills behind the house.\n8) There is the sun behind the hills.\n9) There are clouds in the sky.','',1,0,0,NULL),(36557,393,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Look at the pictures and frame the sentences for each of the following words ------------------------------ 5M\n[in, on, under, near, infront of, behind]\n','\nAns. : 1) --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           2) -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           3) ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          4) --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          5) ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','1) There are fish in the tank.\n2) The doll is on the fish tank.\n3) There is a plant near the stone in the fish tank.\n4) There is a cat infront of the fish tank.\n5) The fish are swimming in the tank.','',1,0,0,NULL),(36558,394,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write down meaningful commands from ‘A’ and ‘B’ : ---------------- 5M\n','\n1) Sit : --------------------------------------\n\n2) Stand : -------------------------------------\n\n3) Walk : -----------------------------------------\n\n4) Run : ------------------------------------------------\n\n5) Turn : --------------------------------------------------','','1) down             2) up quickly                3) fast/slowly/ quickly	4) fast		5) left/right','',1,0,0,NULL),(36559,394,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write down meaningful commands from ‘A’ and ‘B’ : ---------------- 5M\n','\n1) Bend : --------------------------------------\n\n2) Sing : -------------------------------------\n\n3) Smile : -----------------------------------------\n\n4) Laugh : ------------------------------------------------\n\n5) Speak : --------------------------------------------------','','1) down/slowly/quickly		2) slowly/loudly/softly		3) softly          	4) loudly/softly		5) fast/slowly/loudly/quickly\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(36561,394,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the object in the picture and write what you can do with it. ------------ 5M\n','\n1) It’s an -------. We can -------------\n\n2) It’s a ----------. We can -------------\n\n3) It’s a --------. We can ---------------','','1) apple. We can eat it/wash it/ peel it/ cut it/ throw it/ buy it/ sell it/ taste it\n2) bottle. We can wash it/fill it/buy it/open it/ close it/ hold it/ lift it/ clean it.\n3) cloth. We can cut it/ wash it/ sew it/ stitch it/ tear it/ use it/ choose it/ colour it','',1,0,0,NULL),(36562,394,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the object in the picture and write what you can do with it. ------------ 5M\n','\n1) It’s an -------.           We can -------------\n\n2) These are ----------. We can -------------','','1) It’s a sheet of paper. We can buy it/ sell it/ fold it/ shape it/ tear it/ throw it/ use it/ colour it\n2) flowers. We can smell them/buy them/sell them/pick them/touch them/pluck them\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(36563,395,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write all the words in the table in alphabetical order ------------ 5M\n','\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','a, all, and, any, but, by, every, her, here, him, his, how, if, may, me, my, no, now, of, one, only, our, some, that, the, their, them, then, this, to, us, what, when, where, who, with, without, your','',1,0,0,NULL),(36564,395,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find and write rhyming words from the chart --------------- 5M\n','\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','1) Their – there, where           2) then – when            3) who – to, \n4) any – many             5) your – our \n','',1,0,0,NULL),(36565,395,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Solve the following questions ----------------------- 5M\n','\n1) Find and write the words that begin with ‘t’ and ‘w’ --------------- 2M\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) Find and write the words that end with ‘o’ and ‘y’ ------------- 2M\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n 							  \n3) Find the shortest and the longest word --------------- 1M\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','1) i) ‘t’ – the, their, them, to, this, their, that, then\n               ii) ‘w’ – who, where, what, with, without, when\n2) i) ‘o’ – who, no, to\n    ii) ‘y’ – any, my, every, by, many, only\n3) i) The shortest word – a\n    ii) The longest word – without ','',1,0,0,NULL),(36566,386,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Put the letters in alphabetical order.\n     a, z ,m, t\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(36567,386,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Put the following words in alphabetical order.\ncamel, bag, unit, tree\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(36568,386,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find out missing letter.\n  a....c.....e....g\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(36569,386,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Copy the following sentences into English.\n  I saw an aeroplane.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(36570,386,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write down plural forms of the following words.\n     a) bag               b) paper \n\nAns. : a) ------------------    b) --------------------------------','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(36571,386,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write down rhyming words for.\n   a) pen               b) mat\n\nAns. : a) ------------------    b) --------------------------------','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(36572,386,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write down small 