all world after all\nThere is just one moon \nAnd one golden sun \nAnd a smile means\n Friendship to every one. \nThough the mountains divide\nAnd the oceans are wide\nIt\'s a small world after all ------\n1) Complete the following web \n\nIt\'s a world of ------ i) -------- ii) ---------- iii) ---------- iv) --------------- \n\nAns. : i) ------------ ii) -------------- iii) ---------- iv) --------------\n2) i) Complete the following sentence.\n       Smile means ----------------------------------------------------\n    ii) Write the correct word in the blanks \n        a) The world is ------------                    b) The sun is ---------------\n        c) The ocean is ------------------ \n3) Write two pairs of rhyming words from the poem.\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','','1) i) laughter ii) tears iii) hopes iv) fears\n2) i) Smile means friendship to every one.\n    ii) a) small             b) golden             c) wide\n3) a) tears – fears          b) share – aware           c) divide – wide ','',0,0,0,NULL),(36722,180,'descriptive','2',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the following extract and do the activities.\nIt\'s a world of laughter, \nA world of tears.\nIt\'s a world of hopes, \nAnd a world of fears. \nThere\'s so much that we share \nThat it\'s time we\'re aware\n It\'s a small world after all\nThere is just one moon \nAnd one golden sun \nAnd a smile means\n Friendship to every one. \nThough the mountains divide\nAnd the oceans are wide\nIt\'s a small world after all ------\n1) Find the lines from the poem having the meaning given below\n    a) This world is full of expectations, desires and terror also.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   b) Now this is the perfect time for us to become alert and conscious.\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) List the words from the poem which are repeated frequently.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) a) What is there just one in this world?\n\n    Ans. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    b) What is a ‘smile’?\n \n        Ans. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) a) Find the describing words (adjectives) from the poem.\n      \n       Ans. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n      b) Write the opposites (Antonyms) \n           i) Smile × ---------------             ii) Friend × -----------------------\n\n           iii) Small × --------------------      iv) Wide × ----------------------------\n','','','1) a) It’s a world of hopes\n         And a world of tears\n     b) That it’s time we’re aware\n2) world, It’s, small, after, all, of\n3) a) There is just one moon and one sun in this world.\n     b) A smile means friendship to everyone.\n4) a) i) golden             ii) wide\n     b) i) Cry             ii) Enemy               iii) Big                iv) Narrow','',0,0,0,NULL),(36725,181,'descriptive','2',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','a) Write one meaningful question each beginning with the following with the following words : ---------------------- 5M\ni) Who ----------?                                             ii) What -------------? \nii) Where -------?                                            iv) When ----------? \nv) Why ---------?                                               vi) How ------------?\nb) Write one meaningful question each beginning with the following with the following words : ----------------------- 5M\n i) Are ----------?                                       ii) Is -------------?\n ii) Have -------?                                        iv) Has ----------? \nv) Do ---------?                                            v) Does ------------?','','','a) i) Who is that boy?                     ii) What are you doing? \n          iii) Where do you live?               iv) When is English period? \n          v) Why are you laughing?           vi) How do you go to school? \nb) i) Are you ready?                              ii) Is she is good girl?\n     iii) Have you finished your work?     iv) Has she finished her lunch? \n      v) Do you like cold drink?                  vi) Does she know everything? ','',0,0,0,NULL),(36726,181,'descriptive','2',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','a) Write one meaningful question each beginning with the following with the following words : ------------------------------ 5M\n i) Aren\'t they ----------?                             ii) Isn\'t he -------------? \nii) Don\'t you -------?                                    iv) Doesn\'t she ----------? \nv) Can\'t we ---------?                                    vi) Won\'t you ------------?\nb) Write one meaningful question each beginning with the following with the following words : ------------------------------ 5M\n i) Can ----------?                                 ii) Will ---------------?\n iii) May ---------?                                iv) Could --------------?\n  v) Did ----------?','','','a) i) Aren\'t they coming?                        ii) Isn\'t he precious?\n         iii) Don\'t you have any money?         iv) Doesn\'t she like to play? \n         v) Can\'t we swim today?                      vi) Won\'t you play? \n     b) i) Can you sing?                ii) Will you stand up, please?\n          iii) May I come in?       iv) Could you please send me your mobile number?  \n          v) Did they go home?','',0,0,0,NULL),(36727,181,'descriptive','3a',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','a) Complete the following sentences using the \'to be\', \'to have\' : ----------- 5M\ni) I am ------                         ii) I have ----------- \niii) You have ---------           iv) They have ---------- \nv) She has ---------              vi) He is ----------\nb) Complete the following sentence using the \'to be\', \'to have\' : ------------- 5M\ni) It is ----------                         ii) We have ------\n iii) They are ---------               iv) He has ---------- \nv) You has ---------- ','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(36728,181,'descriptive','2',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write the following conversation using this titles (any two) : ---------- 10M\n i) Asking a friend to lend you her notebook.\n ii) Inviting a friend to your birthday party.\n iii) Saying sorry to someone for trodding on his/her foot. \niv) Offering a glass of water to a guest.','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(36729,181,'descriptive','3a',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write the following conversation using this titles (Any 2) ---------- 10M\ni) Asking a friend for his postal address \nii) Asking a friend for his telephone number\niii) Asking your teacher to explain something to you again.\niv) Asking your teacher’s permission to enter/leave the class.\nv) Answering the phone.','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(36730,181,'descriptive','2',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','a) Adding \'s\' to verbs. -------------- 5M\ni) I like -----------                    ii) We like ---------- \niii) You like -------                 iv) He likes ---------- \nv) She likes ----------\nb) Use of \'do\' : ---------------- 5M\ni) I do/don’t ---------                     ii) You do/don’t ------------\niii) We do/don’t ----------            iv) We did/didn’t ------------\nv) You did/didn’t ------------        vi) They did/didn’t ----------------','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(36731,181,'descriptive','3a',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','Answer the following questions : ----------------------- 10M\n1) Why is Tara excited?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) Why did Bittu become nervous?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Why is Kuku happy?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) Why did Cat think that they are lucky?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) What did Parrot say to the Cat?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','','1) Tara is excited about starting studies again.\n2) Bittu became nervous because holidays were over.\n3) Kuku is happy because now she can play more on the school ground.\n4) The cat thought that they were lucky because they didn\'t have school.\n5) Parrot said to the Cat that it would never learn.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(36732,181,'descriptive','2',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','Observe the following table and answer the questions: ------------ 10M\n1) Write down three letter words from the given table.\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) Write down the words which begin with ‘a’\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Write down the words which end with ‘t’.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) Write down four letter words.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','','1) the, and, for, not, you, but, his, her, she, one, all, out, who, can\n2) and, as, at, an, all, about\n3) that, it, not, at, but, what, out, about\n4) that, have, with, this, from, they, will, what, when','',1,0,0,NULL),(36737,181,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Observe the following table and answer the questions : \n\n','\n1) Write down three letter words from the given table.\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) Write down the words which begin with ‘a’\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Write down the words which end with ‘t’.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) Write down four letter words.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','1) the, and, for, not, you, but, his, her, she, one, all, out, who, can\n2) and, as, at, an, all, about\n3) that, it, not, at, but, what, out, about\n4) that, have, with, this, from, they, will, what, when','',1,0,0,NULL),(36740,181,'descriptive','2b',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','Answer the following questions : \n1) Why is Tara excited?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) Why did Bittu become nervous?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Why is Kuku happy?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) Why did Cat think that they are lucky?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) What did Parrot say to the Cat?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','','Answer\n1) Tara is excited about starting studies again.\n2) Bittu became nervous because holidays were over.\n3) Kuku is happy because now she can play more on the school ground.\n4) The cat thought that they were lucky because they didn\'t have school.\n5) Parrot said to the Cat that it would never learn.','',0,0,0,NULL),(36742,182,'descriptive','2',10,2,'Out of Text Book','It was an early Easter. In the yards lay snow, and rills ran down the village. A large puddle had run down from a manure pile into a lane between two farms. And at this puddle two girls, one older than the other, had met. Both of them had been dressed by their mothers in new clothes. The little girl had a blue dress, and the elder a yellow one with a design. Both had their heads wrapped in red kerchiefs.\nAfter prayers in the Church, the two girls went to the puddle, where they showed their new garments to each other, and began to play. They wanted to plash in the water. The little girl started to go into the puddle with her shoes on, but the older girl said to her: \n\"Don\'t go, Malasha, your mother will scold you. I will take off my shoes, and you do the same.”','Read the following passage and complete the activities : \n1) i) Name the following :   \na) Name of the festival : -------\nAns. : ------------------\n b) Place of worship for the christians : ------------ \nAns. : ----------------\nii) Complete the following sentences :\na) The two girls went to the puddle (time) ----------\nAns. : ----------------------------\nb) The large puddle ran into (place) --------\nAns. : --------------------\n\n','2) Complete the following : Two girls  ----------- 1M\nAge : \nDress : \nAns. :  ----------------------------------------------------------\n          ------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Write the following words in appropriate Coloumn : Snow, village, water, farms \ni) Countable noun : ----------------------------------------------------\nii) Uncountable noun : -------------------------------------------------\n4) Write the past tense of given verbs :\ni) grasp - --------------------------                ii) pick - -----------------------\n\niii) gather - ---------------------                  iv) laugh -----------------------','','1) i) a) Easter     b) Church\n               ii) a) After prayers in the church\n                    b) a lane between two farms\n        2) Age : elder, younger\n            Dress : yellow, blue\n3) i) Countable Noun : Village, farms\n    ii) Uncountable noun : Snow, water \n4) i) grasped                 ii) picked                 iii) gathered              iv) laughed ','',0,0,0,NULL),(36744,182,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','After prayers in the Church, the two girls went to the puddle, where they showed their new garments to each other, and began to play. They wanted to plash in the water. The little girl started to go into the puddle with her shoes on, but the older girl said to her:\n\"Don\'t go, Malasha, your mother will scold you. I will take off my shoes, and you do the same.\"\nThe girls took off their shoes, raised their skirts, and walked through the puddle toward each other. Malasha stepped in up to her ankles, and said:\n\"It is deep, Akulka, I am afraid.\"\n\"Never mind,\" she replied, \"it will not be any deeper. Come straight toward me!\"\nThey came closer to each other. Akulka said: \"Malasha, look out, and do not splash it up, but walk softly.\"\nShe had barely said that when Malasha plumped her foot into the water and bespattered Akulka\'s new dress, and not only her dress, but also her nose and eyes. When Akulka saw the spots on her dress, she grew angry at Malasha, and scolded her, and ran after her, and wanted to strike her. Malasha was frightened and, seeing what trouble she had caused, jumped out of the puddle and ran home.\nAkulka\'s mother passed by; she saw her daughter\'s dress bespattered and soiled.\n\"Where, accursed one, did you get yourself so dirty?\"\n\"Malasha has purposely splashed it on me.\"\nAkulka\'s mother grasped Malasha and gave her a knock on the nape of her neck. Malasha began to howl, and her mother ran out of the house.','Read the following passage and do the activities :\n','Q.1) a) Where did the two girls go after prayers in the church?\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nb) Which mistakes did Malasha commit?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) a) Why did Akulka want to strike Malasha?\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nb) Why did Malasha run home?\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) What did Akulka tell her mother?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) How did-Akulka\'s mother react at that time?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) Spot the names of body parts from the story. Add three other names of your own.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','1) a) After prayers in the church, the two girls went to the puddle.\nb) Malasha plumped her foot into the water and bespattered Akulka’s new dress.\n2) a) Malasha bespattered Akulka\'s new dress, her nose and eyes. That\'s why Akulka grew angry with Malasha and wanted to strike her.\nb) Akulka grew angry with Malasha after seeing the spots on her new dress. She scolded Malasha and ran after her. Malasha was frightened by this and ran home.\n3) Akulka told her mother that Malasha had purposely splashed the spots on her dress.\n4) Akulka\'s mother grasped Malasha and gave her a knock on the nape of her neck.\n5) head, foot, eyes, nose, neck, back, legs, hands, ears, shoulders, mouth.','',0,0,0,NULL),(36745,182,'descriptive','3a',10,2,'Out of Text Book','After prayers in the Church, the two girls went to the puddle, where they showed their new garments to each other, and began to play. They wanted to plash in the water. The little girl started to go into the puddle with her shoes on, but the older girl said to her:\n\"Don\'t go, Malasha, your mother will scold you. I will take off my shoes, and you do the same.\"\nThe girls took off their shoes, raised their skirts, and walked through the puddle toward each other. Malasha stepped in up to her ankles, and said:\n\"It is deep, Akulka, I am afraid.\"\n\"Never mind,\" she replied, \"it will not be any deeper. Come straight toward me!\"\nThey came closer to each other. Akulka said: \"Malasha, look out, and do not splash it up, but walk softly.\"\nShe had barely said that when Malasha plumped her foot into the water and bespattered Akulka\'s new dress, and not only her dress, but also her nose and eyes. When Akulka saw the spots on her dress, she grew angry at Malasha, and scolded her, and ran after her, and wanted to strike her. Malasha was frightened and, seeing what trouble she had caused, jumped out of the puddle and ran home.\nAkulka\'s mother passed by; she saw her daughter\'s dress bespattered and soiled.\n\"Where, accursed one, did you get yourself so dirty?\"\n\"Malasha has purposely splashed it on me.\"\nAkulka\'s mother grasped Malasha and gave her a knock on the nape of her neck. Malasha began to howl, and her mother ran out of the house.','Read the following passage and do the activities :','Q.1) a) Where did the two girls go after prayers in the church?\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nb) Which mistakes did Malasha commit?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) a) Why did Akulka want to strike Malasha?\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nb) Why did Malasha run home?\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) What did Akulka tell her mother?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) How did-Akulka\'s mother react at that time?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) Spot the names of body parts from the story. Add three other names of your own.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','1) a) After prayers in the church, the two girls went to the puddle.\nb) Malasha plumped her foot into the water and bespattered Akulka’s new dress.\n2) a) Malasha bespattered Akulka\'s new dress, her nose and eyes. That\'s why Akulka grew angry with Malasha and wanted to strike her.\nb) Akulka grew angry with Malasha after seeing the spots on her new dress. She scolded Malasha and ran after her. Malasha was frightened by this and ran home.\n3) Akulka told her mother that Malasha had purposely splashed the spots on her dress.\n4) Akulka\'s mother grasped Malasha and gave her a knock on the nape of her neck.\n5) head, foot, eyes, nose, neck, back, legs, hands, ears, shoulders, mouth.','',0,0,0,NULL),(36746,182,'descriptive','2',10,2,'Out of Text Book','One word brought back another, and the women began to quarrel. The men, too, ran out, and a big crowd gathered in the street. All were crying, and nobody could hear his neighbour. They scolded and cursed each other; one man gave another man a push, and a fight had begun, when Akulka\'s grandmother came out. She stepped in the midst of the peasants, and began to talk to them:\n\"What are you doing, dear ones? Consider the holiday. This is a time for rejoicing. And see what sin you are doing!\"\nThey paid no attention to the old woman, and almost knocked her off her feet. She would never have stopped them, if it had not been for Akulka and Malasha.\nWhile the women exchanged words, Akulka wiped off her dress, and went back to the puddle in the lane. She picked up a pebble and began to scratch the ground so as to let the water off into the street. While she was scratching, Malasha came up and began to help her. She picked up a chip and widened the rill.','Read the following passage and do the activities : \n\n','1) How did the quarrel start?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------\n          --------------------------------------------------------\n           -----------------------------------------------------\n2) Did the people stop fighting?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------\n           --------------------------------------------------------     \n3) What did Akulka do?\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------\n          ------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) What did Malasha do?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) Change the words in the boxes to make other meaningful sentences :\n     i) I’ll take off may shoes and you do the same.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------\n     ii) This is a time for rejoicing.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------\n','','1) Malasha bespattered Alkuka’s new dress, her nose and eyes. Akulka told her mother that Malasha had purposely did it. So Akulka’s mother grasped Malasha and gave her a knock. Malasha began to howl and her mother ran out of the house. When Malasha’s mother saw that she began to scold her neighbor and the quarrel began.\n2) People didn\'t stop their fighting eventhough the old woman was telling them to stop.\n3) Akulka wiped off her dress and went back to the puddle in the lane. She picked up a pebble and began to scratch the ground to let the water off into the street.\n4) While Akulka was scratching, Malasha came up and began to help her. She picked up a chip and widened the rill.\n5) i) I’ll put on my new dress and you do the same.\nii) This is a time for studying.','',0,0,0,NULL),(36747,182,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','One word brought back another, and the women began to quarrel. The men, too, ran out, and a big crowd gathered in the street. All were crying, and nobody could hear his neighbour. They scolded and cursed each other; one man gave another man a push, and a fight had begun, when Akulka\'s grandmother came out. She stepped in the midst of the peasants, and began to talk to them:\n\"What are you doing, dear ones? Consider the holiday. This is a time for rejoicing. And see what sin you are doing!\"\nThey paid no attention to the old woman, and almost knocked her off her feet. She would never have stopped them, if it had not been for Akulka and Malasha.\nWhile the women exchanged words, Akulka wiped off her dress, and went back to the puddle in the lane. She picked up a pebble and began to scratch the ground so as to let the water off into the street. While she was scratching, Malasha came up and began to help her. She picked up a chip and widened the rill.','Read the following passage and do the activities : ','1) How did the quarrel start?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------\n         \n --------------------------------------------------------\n         \n -----------------------------------------------------\n2) Did the people stop fighting?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------\n          \n --------------------------------------------------------     \n3) What did Akulka do?\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------\n         \n ------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) What did Malasha do?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n         \n  ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) Change the words in the boxes to make other meaningful sentences :\n     i) I’ll take off may shoes and you do the same.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------\n     ii) This is a time for rejoicing.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------','','1) Malasha bespattered Alkuka’s new dress, her nose and eyes. Akulka told her mother that Malasha had purposely did it. So Akulka’s mother grasped Malasha and gave her a knock. Malasha began to howl and her mother ran out of the house. When Malasha’s mother saw that she began to scold her neighbor and the quarrel began.\n2) People didn\'t stop their fighting eventhough the old woman was telling them to stop.\n3) Akulka wiped off her dress and went back to the puddle in the lane. She picked up a pebble and began to scratch the ground to let the water off into the street.\n4) While Akulka was scratching, Malasha came up and began to help her. She picked up a chip and widened the rill.\n5) i) I’ll put on my new dress and you do the same.\nii) This is a time for studying.','',0,0,0,NULL);
INSERT INTO `ep_questions` VALUES (36748,182,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','The peasants had begun to fight, just as the water went down the rill toward the place where the old woman was trying to separate the men. The girls ran, one from one side of the rill, the other from the other side.\n\"Look out, Malasha, look out!\" shouted Akulka.\nMalasha wanted to say something herself, but could not speak for laughter. The girls were running and laughing at a chip which was bobbing up and down the rill. They ran straight into the crowd of the peasants. The old woman saw them and said to the peasants:\n\"Shame on you before God, men! You have started fighting on account of these two girls, and they have long ago forgotten it: the dear children have been playing nicely together. They are wiser than you.\"\nThe men looked at the girls, and they felt ashamed. Then they laughed at themselves, and scattered to their farms.','Read the following passage and do the activities ','1) What was the old woman trying to do?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) Did the girls forget their quarrel?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) How can we say that?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) Why did the men feel ashamed?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) List the characters in the story and write their approximate ages.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         --------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','1) The old woman was trying to stop the fighting among the peasants. She was trying to tell them that it was Easter, time for rejoicing and not for making sin.\n2) Yes, the girls forgot their quarrel after some time.\n3) After sometime when the men were fighting, Akulka and Malasha began to talk and play with each other.\n4) When the old woman told peasants that they had started fighting on account of those two girls and they had long ago forgotton it and they had started playing nicely together. At that time the men looked at the girls and they felt ashamed.\n5) i) Akulka – 10, Malasha – 8, Akulaka’s Mother – 35, Malasha’s Mother – 32, Akulaka’s Grand-mother – 60','',0,0,0,NULL),(36749,182,'descriptive','3a',10,2,'Out of Text Book','The peasants had begun to fight, just as the water went down the rill toward the place where the old woman was trying to separate the men. The girls ran, one from one side of the rill, the other from the other side.\n\"Look out, Malasha, look out!\" shouted Akulka.\nMalasha wanted to say something herself, but could not speak for laughter. The girls were running and laughing at a chip which was bobbing up and down the rill. They ran straight into the crowd of the peasants. The old woman saw them and said to the peasants:\n\"Shame on you before God, men! You have started fighting on account of these two girls, and they have long ago forgotten it: the dear children have been playing nicely together. They are wiser than you.\"\nThe men looked at the girls, and they felt ashamed. Then they laughed at themselves, and scattered to their farms.','Read the following passage and do the activities \n\n\n','1) What was the old woman trying to do?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n           -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) Did the girls forget their quarrel?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n           ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) How can we say that?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n          ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) Why did the men feel ashamed?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) List the characters in the story and write their approximate ages.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n          ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n         --------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','1) The old woman was trying to stop the fighting among the peasants. She was trying to tell them that it was Easter, time for rejoicing and not for making sin.\n2) Yes, the girls forgot their quarrel after some time.\n3) After sometime when the men were fighting, Akulka and Malasha began to talk and play with each other.\n4) When the old woman told peasants that they had started fighting on account of those two girls and they had long ago forgotton it and they had started playing nicely together. At that time the men looked at the girls and they felt ashamed.\n5) i) Akulka – 10, Malasha – 8, Akulaka’s Mother – 35, Malasha’s Mother – 32, Akulaka’s Grand-mother – 60','',0,0,0,NULL),(36750,183,'descriptive','2',10,2,'Out of Text Book','This particular journey that we are going to read about was actually a journey from China to our own country! It was made by the famous seventh century travellers Yuan Chwang.\nIn those days, travelling from China to India was not an easy rask – one had to travel thousands of miles on foot or horseback, crossing deserts, crossing snow-clad mountains, crossing strange, unfamiliar regions, using roads where bandits and robbers roamed – who would do it? But Yuan Chwang had a dream. He wanted to take Buddhist scriptures from India to his homeland in China. It was like a pilgrimage to him.','Read the following passage and complete the activity :\n\n','1) Complete the following sentences\n\ni) Yuan Chwang was ----------------------\n\nii) Yuan Chwang travelled from ------------- to --------\n\niii) Yoan Chewang’s dream was to ------------ to --------\n\n2) i) What was Yuan Chwang\'s dream?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------\nii) What is the novel about?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------\n3) Complete the following web : \nTravelling from China to India was difficult because \n      ↓                                 ↓                                 ↓\n\n----------              -------------------               -------------------\n4) i) From the passage find the opposite of : \n\na) difficult × --------------            b) familiar × -------------\nii) Find out the words that mean.\na) really             b) thieves \n\nAns. : a) -------------                b) -----------------','','1) i) The famous seventh century traveller.\nii) China to India.\niii) To take Buddhist scriptures from India to China.\n2) i) Yuan Chwang wanted to take Buddhist Scriptures from India to his homeland in China.\n ii) The novel is about the famous pilgrimage undertaken by Yuan Chwang.\n3) i) One had to travel thousands of miles on foot or horseback.\nii) One had to cross deserts, snow-clad mountains and unfamiliar regions.\niii) One had to use roads where robbers roamed.\n4) i) a) easy        b) unfamiliar\nii) a) actually           b) robbers ','',0,0,0,NULL),(36753,183,'descriptive','3a',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the following passage and complete the activity : \nQ.1) Say whether the following sentences are true or false.\ni) Sun Wukong was most powerful.\n\nAns. : ---------------------\nii) Sun Wukong was born on the Flower Fruit Mountain.\nAns. : -------------------------\nThe most powerful among the three disciples is Sun Wukong. Everything about him is extra- ordinary. He was born when winds blew over a huge stone egg on the Flower Fruit Mountain. He is able to transform himself in 72 different ways. Not only that but he can also transform each of his hair strands into any living or non-living thing of his choice. His \'As-you-wish-gold-banded cudgel\' is also magical. It can grow as big as a pillar supporting the sky, but at other times, it becomes as tiny as a needle. Then the Monkey King just tucks it away behind his ear. Sun Wukong can travel thousands of kilometres in just one somersault. He can walk through fire, travel under water and fly to any place at will. His body is as hard as a diamond. So no one and nothing can injure him. His \'golden-gaze-fiery eyes\' have x-ray vision. No one can deceive him.\nQ.2) i) Who’s the most powerful among the three disciples?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nii) Write any five features of Sun Wukong’s character that you like best.\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Complete the following web :\n\nAns. : i) --------------------                  ii) --------------------\n          iii) ------------------                   iv) ------------------------\n','','','1) i) True           ii) False\n2) i) The most powerful among the three disciples was Sun Wukong.\nii) can walk through fire, can travel under water, can fly to any place at will, can grow as big as a pillar, can become as tiny as needle. \n3) i) Sun Wukong can transform himself in 72 different ways.\nii) He can walk through fire\niii)  He can travel under water \niv) His body was as hard as a diamond\n4) i) blew         ii) grew          iii) chose          iv) flew ','',1,0,0,NULL),(36754,183,'descriptive','2',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','Answer the following questions : \nA] Say whether the following sentences are right or wrong : \n1) The novel \'Journey to the West\' is about a journey to western countries like England and America.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------\n2) In the days of Yuan Chwang travelling from China to India was not an easy task.\nAns. : -------------------------------------\n3) Yuan Chwang travelled to many parts of India.\nAns. : -------------------------------------\n4) Yuan Chwang\'s way back home was relatively easy\nAns. : -------------------------------------\n5) Gods and supernatural powers had helped Yuan Chwang in his quest.\nAns. : -------------------------------------\n6) The three disciples were three saints.\nAns. : -------------------------------------\n7) The three disciples have supernatural powers.\nAns. : -------------------------------------\nB] List all the persons and characters mentioned in the story. Which of them are real? Which are imaginary?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','','A] 1) wrong           2) right             3) right             4) wrong            5) right       6) wrong             7) right\nB] Characters in the story : i) Yuan Chwan	 ii) Guanyin deity       iii) Monkey King         iv) Zu Bajji          v) Sha Wujing\nAmong these characters only Yuan Chwang is real character and remaining all are imaginary.','',0,0,0,NULL),(36757,183,'descriptive','3a',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','Answer the following questions : \nA] Read the statements on the chit and think on it. Say whether each one is historical or fictional :\n1) Indian merchants used to travel across the seas many centuries ago.\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------\n2) Sindbad, the sailor completed seven voyages.\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------\n3) Neil Armstrong landed on the moon in the 20th century.\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------\n4) Alladdin could fly on his magic carpet.\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------\n5) Alexander the great conquered a number of counties before he came to India.\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------\n6) Gulliver met very tiny people in Lilliput and giants in the country of Brobdingnag.\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------\n7) There\'s a man in the moon who watches what\'s going on the earth.\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------\n8) Emperor Ashoka\'s Empire stretched from the modern day Afghanistan to Bangladesh.\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------\nB] i) Can you think of other words starting with \'folk\'?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------\nii) Write the opposites of the following :\n\na) Unsafe × --------                     b) Unimportant × --------------\n\n','','','Answer\ni) Fictional               ii) Historical    \nAns. : A] 1) Historical         2) Fictional               3) Historical             4) Fictional      5) Historical             6) Fictional             7) Fictional               8) Historical    \nB] i) folksong, folkdance, folklore, folkliterature.\n     ii) a) safe              b) important','',0,0,0,NULL),(36758,184,'descriptive','2',10,2,'Out of Text Book','The Sun, after hos morning dip in the river\nDressed up in his golden muslin turban\nWaits and smiles on one side of the road,\nFor children are going to school.\nThrough the green-topped branches,\nBreezes sing their songs of blessings.\nFragrant Flowers awaken the sleepy roads\nWith their melodies.\nAt the corner of the lane,\nThe Peepal in his lush deep foliage \nWaves his hands','A] Read the following extract and complete the activity : -------------- 5M\n1) Complete the following sentences.\ni) The sun is dressed up in ----------------\nii) The children are -------------------\niii) The trees have ---------------\niv) The peepal tree is at --------------\n\n','2) Match the following parts to make meaningful sentences\n              A                                                B\ni) The Sun                                 a) waits and smiles \nii) The breezes                        b) sing their songs\niii) Fragrant flowers               c) waves his hands\niv) The Peepal                         d) awaken the sleepy roads\n3) From the extract find the words that rhyme with.\ni) code             ii) pool             iii) power               iv) cart\n\nAns. : i) -----------------                       ii) ---------------------\n\niii) ----------------------                          iv) ------------------------\nB] Answer the following questions : ------------------ 5M\n1) Find at least two phrases from the poem that indicate the following : \ni) It is an early morning \nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nii) The atmosphere is pleasant.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','A] 1) i) ---------- his golden muslin turban.\nii) ------------- going to school\niii) ------------ green topped branches\niv) ------------ at the corner of the lane.\n2) i – a, ii – b, iii – d, iv – c \n3) i) road           ii) school            iii) hour            iv) heart \nB] i) a) Morning light spreads over the earth.\nb) The sun, after his morning dip in the river dressed up in his golden muslin turban.\n ii) a) Breezes sing their songs of blessings.\n      b) Fragrant flowers awaken the sleepy roads with their melodies.','',0,0,0,NULL),(36860,180,'descriptive','1a',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the word by using correct letters :  \ni) appe_r              ii) che_k             iii) d_nce            iv) fa_al\n\n\nAns. : a) -------------------   b) ------------------------\n\n         c) -------------------    d) ------------------------','','','i) appear                 ii) check                   iii) dance              iv) fatal','',0,0,0,NULL),(36861,180,'descriptive','1a',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the word by using correct letters :  \n i) ang_r           ii) bri_k                iii) cy_le              iv) f_rget\n\nAns. : a) -------------------   b) ------------------------\n\n         c) -------------------    d) ------------------------\n','','','i) anger             ii) brick               iii) cycle               iv) forget','',0,0,0,NULL),(36862,180,'descriptive','1a',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the word by using correct letters :  \ni) ass_t            ii) care_r               iii) de_th            iv) f_ther\n','','','i) asset            ii) career             iii) death              iv) father','',0,0,0,NULL),(36863,181,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the word by using correct letters :  \ni) lit_le           ii) p_int            iii) sh_ky            iv) t_lent\n\nAns. : i) -------------------         ii) ---------------------------\n\n      iii) -------------------         iv) ----------------------------\n','','','i) little          ii) point            iii) shaky             iv) talent','',0,0,0,NULL),(36864,181,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete th