se: Duck can live on land as well as in water.\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------','','','True','',0,0,0,NULL),(37601,481,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statements are true or false: The forelegs of birds are modified into wings.\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------','','','True','',0,0,0,NULL),(37602,481,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Who is lying? : Cockroach – I have five legs\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Cockroach is lying. Cockroach has six legs.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37603,481,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Who is lying? : Hen – My toes are webbed\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Hen is lying. Its toes are not webbed.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37604,481,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Who is lying? : Cactus – My fleshy, green part is a leaf\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Cactus is lying. Its fleshly and green part is stem.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37605,481,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the odd man out: Neem, banyan, water hyacinth, fungi\n\nAns. : --------------------------------','','','fungi','',0,0,0,NULL),(37606,481,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the odd man out : carrot, grape wine, beet, raddish\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------','','','grape wine','',0,0,0,NULL),(37607,481,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the odd man out : frog, duck, fish, tortoise\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------','','','frog','',0,0,0,NULL),(37608,481,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the odd man out : Deer, fox, tiger, lion\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------','','','Deer','',0,0,0,NULL),(37609,481,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the odd man out: House lizards, garden lizard, yak, crocodile\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------','','','yak','',0,0,0,NULL),(37610,481,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write scientific names of : Dog\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------','','','Canis lupus familiars','',0,0,0,NULL),(37611,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the desert animals.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Camel, Rats, snakes, spiders, lizards in deserts','',0,0,0,NULL),(37612,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the theories given by Charles Darwin.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Survival of the fittest		ii) Theory of Natural Selection','',0,0,0,NULL),(37613,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Tell the hierarchy of the classification.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Classification starts with Kingdom Animalia or Kingdom Plantae. Then depending upon basic similarities and differences their further groups and sub-groups are formed.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37614,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Distinguish between : Aquatic plants and Desert plants\n\nAns. : \n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','Answer :','',0,0,1,NULL),(37615,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Distinguish between: Carnivores and Herbivores\nAns. :\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n ','','','Answer :','',0,0,1,NULL),(37616,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Distinguish between : Adaptation in birds and Adaptations in fish\nAns. : \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','Answer','',0,0,1,NULL),(37617,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reason: The petiole and stem of aquatic plants have air spaces.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Air spaces in the petiole and stem helps the plants to float flat on the water. Therefore, as an adaptation to survive in water, the aquatic plants have such structure.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37618,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reason: Trees and creepers in the jungle grow tall.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The plants in jungle are many in number. They compete with each other to get enough sunlight. To achieve these trees and creepers in jungle grow tall.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37619,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reason: There are Haustorial roots in Cuscuta.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Cuscuta is a parasitic plant. It does not have leaves and thus is unable to perform photosynthesis. It sucks the nutrition from the host plant with the help of Haustorial roots.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37620,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reason: Fungus cannot perform photosynthesis.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Fungus lacks chlorophyll and thus is unable to perform photosynthesis.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37621,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reason: The fishes have gills instead of nose.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Fishes are aquatic animals. They can breathe oxygen only that is dissolved in water. The gills help in absorbing oxygen from water. The nose cannot be of any function for aquatic fish and hence the fishes have gills instead of nose.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37622,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reason: The prey is unaware about tiger approaching.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','There are soft pads under the paw of tiger. It walks with caution and stalks the prey and captures easily.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37623,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is the main function of canine teeth in carnivorous animals?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The carnivores animals use the canine teeth to prerace and hold the prey caught by them.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37624,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is the main difference between vehicles on the road and aeroplanes?\n\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The vehicles are designed to run on the road, and Aeroplanes have wings to fly in the sky.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37625,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Why does water trickle of lotus leaves. \n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Lotus is an aquatic plant that has a coating of waxy layer on its stems and leaves. If water falls on the leaves, it is not absorbed but gets trickled down.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37626,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Why don’t the leaves of aquatic plant rooted in water?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The leaves of aquatic plants have waxy coating on them. There are no stomata on the leaves and thus water cannot enter the leaves. Therefore, the leaves do not rot in water.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37627,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Define adaptation \n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Adaptation are the modifications seen due to gradual changes in the body parts and in the behaviour of plants and animals. These long-term changes help them to adjust to their surroundings.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37628,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Draw neat and labelled diagram of ‘fish’.\n\nDiagram : \n\n\n\n\n\n','','','Diagram :','',0,0,1,NULL),(37629,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Draw neat and labelled diagram of ‘Cuscuta’.\nDiagram :\n\n\n\n\n','','','Diagram :','',0,0,1,NULL),(37630,481,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write scientific names of: i) Cow 		ii) Hibiscus \n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Bos taurus	ii) Hibiscus rosa-sinensis','',0,0,0,NULL),(37631,481,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','In what different ways is the diversity in living things seen?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) We seen differences in the plants and animals based on their habitat. \nii) Some plants and animals can survive in desert while some in water.\niii) Different living things have different body structure.\niv) Movement in different organisms are seen different.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37632,481,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','In what ways are sloping branches useful to plants in a snowy regions?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) The plants like deodar and pine are conical in shape. Which are found in snowy region.\nii) The conical shape prevent the snow from accumulating on these elements.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37633,481,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Why is the camel called the ‘ship of the desert’.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) The skin of a camel is thick \nii) The legs are long with cushioned soles. \niii) There is a fold of skin for protection of nostrils.\niv) The eyelashes are long and thick and thus they protect the eyes.\nv) Fat is stored in its hump, due to which it can survive for a long time without water.\nvi) Due to all of such adaptations, camel becomes most suitable to walk in the desert. Thus, it is used as a means of transport and is called ‘ship of the desert’.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37634,481,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','How can the plants like cactus and acacia found in desert? With scarce of water?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Cactus and Acacia are plants that grow in deserts. They show adaptations to survive in the scarcity of water. \nii) Cactus does not have use leaves. Leaves are modified into thrones. Therefore water is not lost by evaporation through leaves.\niii) The stem takes up the function of photosynthesis and hence turns fleshly and green\niv) There is thick layer of waxy substances on the stems\nv) Roots of these plans penetrate deep down into the soil in search of water\nvi) All such adaptations help the cactus and acacia to survive in deserts with scarce water.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37635,481,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is the inter-relationship between adaptation of organism and their surrounding?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) All the organisms are adapted in their surrounding.\nii) Adaptation are take place in the body parts.\niii) Some life process help the organism to feed, to reproduce new generation as well as survive.\niv) This protect to the organism from their enemies in species and in specific surrounding upon the habitat and its geographical condition.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37636,481,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','How are organisms classified? \n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Organisms are classified according to their characteristics.\nii) different criteria’s are used to classify plants and animals based on similarities and differences.\niii) A hierarchy is formed in the classification plants and animals with Kingdom plantae and kingdom animalia.\niv) In this way organisms are placed in group and subgroups.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37637,481,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','What adaptation do you see in the plants of forest regions?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) A variety of plants like trees, shrubs and herbs are found in forest.\nii) Trees grow tall to get sunlight.\niii) Spring like tendrils on the stem of climbers in an examples of adaptation. \niv) Herbs grow with the help of water, sunlight in the forest regions.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37638,481,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','How does adaptation take place in aerial animals?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Aerial consisting birds and insects.\nii) The spindle shaped body of birds minimizes the resistance of air while flying.\niii) They have hollow bones and forelegs are modified into wings.\niv) Body if aerial animals are light weight and tapers at both end.\nv) This adapted for flying them.\nvi)  They fly with the help of wings.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37639,481,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','How is frog adapted to amphibious habitat? Why is it called an amphibian? \n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Animals that live in water and on land they are called amphibious.\nii) The webbed toes and triangular head for swimming in water.\niii) The colour on the back help to hide in grasses.\niv) Frog can catch insect with his long tongue.\nv) It breathes through skin in water.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37640,481,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Who gave the system of binomial nomenclature? Explain the method in brief. \n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Carl Linnaeus discovered to the system of binomial nomenclature. \nii) According to this method every living organisms is given a same uniform scientific name throughout the world.\niii) There are two terms in this name. The first term denote genus and second term denotes species.\niv) Every identified organisms receives a binomial name as for the standard guidelines of International Code of Nomenclature.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37641,481,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which type of plants grow in the soil that is deficient in nitrogen? Why? \n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Insectivorous plants inhabit the soil that is deficient in nitrogen.\nii) Plants need nitrogen, Phosphorus and potassium for proper growth.\niii) In order to obtain the nutrition, they consume insects.\niv) Hence, plants like Drosera (Sundew), Venus fly trap, pitcher plants, etc. grow in the soil that is deficient in nitrogen.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37642,481,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','What are adaptations do you see in the plants of snowy regions?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) There are coniferous trees like deodar and pine in the snowy regions. \nii) These trees are conical in shape with sloping branches so that the snow does not remain accumulated on the tree top.\niii) The bark of the tree is thick which helps the tree to withstand the cold.\niv) All these adaptations help the trees to survive in snowy regions.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37643,481,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write scientific names of: i) Jowhar 	ii) Human 		iii) Mango \n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Sorghum bicolor            	ii) Homo sapiens		iii) Mangifera indica','',0,0,0,NULL),(37644,481,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Observe the bodies of frog, duck and tortoise: a) Of what use are their legs to these animals? 		b) What helps frog to breadth under water?		c) Of what use are the long hind legs of a frog? 	d) Why doesn’t duck get wet in water?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','a) Legs help these animals for locomotion.\nb) A frog helps its skin to breath underwater.\nc) Long hind legs helps to jump for a frog.\nd) i) There is waxy layer on the feather of a duck\nii) This prevent accumulating water hence a duck doesn’t get wet in water.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37645,481,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the given statement. Write the paragraph about adaptation with reference to each statement: There is extreme heat in desert.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','There is a scarcity of water in the desert. Animals is like rats, snakes, spider, lizards in desert live in a deep burrows during daytime and activate night. Camel shows adaptation like modified legs, eyes, nose and hump on the back. The plants are also modified in desert. They show different adaptation, too.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37646,481,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the given statement. Write the paragraph about adaptation with reference to each statement: Grasslands are lush green.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','In grassland different types of bushes and grasses are appear. There is availability of water extremely high. Roots of these grasses hold the soil and prevent the erosion of soil. Due to the water and sunlight the grassland always appear lush green.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37647,481,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the given statement. Write the paragraph about adaptation with reference to each statement: Insects are found in large numbers.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','We found insects in any type of habitat. The body of insects is light in weight and tapers at both ends. They can fly with two pairs of wings and walks with six stick- like legs. They reproduce in large number in any habitat.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37648,481,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the given statement. Write the paragraph about adaptation with reference to each statement: We hide\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Some animals hide to take protection from their enemies. Colours of some animals merge with their surroundings. Thus enemies do not see easily them. Colour of deep and black- have mixes with their surrounding.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37649,481,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the given statement. Write the paragraph about adaptation with reference to each statement: We have long ears.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Mainly we found long ears in herbivorous these long ears alerts them from their receive sounds from long distances and different direction. This type of adaptation to escape from enemies.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37650,481,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the paragraph and answer the following question?\nI am a penguin. I live in polar region covered by snow. My abdomen is white. My skin is thick with a layer of fat underneath. My body is spindle-shaped. My wings are small. My toes are webbed. We live in flocks.\na) Why is my skin white and thick and why is there a thick layer of fat underneath?\nb) Why do we live in flocks sticking close to each other.\nc) Which geographical region do I inhabitat? Why? \nd) Which adaptations should you have to enable you to live permanently in the polar region? Why? \n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','a) i) White colour of penguin match with its surrounding hence it cannot easily located.\nii) This protect against predators.\niii) A thick layer of fat underneath because it does not allow the body heat to escape out.\n b) i) They live for protection from predators.\nii) Due to sticking close, they do not lose the heat surrounding.\niii) To caring of parental as well as themselves.\nc) i) Generally, penguin stays in polar region as well as in Antarctic region.\nii) There is available enough for feeding, therefore, they are inhabited here.\nd) i) For permanent in habited, the body should be adapted to cold temperature.\nii) There should be thick layer of fat and thick skin to protect the body.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37651,481,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','How is frog adapted to amphibious habitat? Why is it called an amphibian?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Animals that live in water and on land they are called amphibious.\nii) The webbed toes and triangular head for swimming in water.\niii) The colour on the back help to hide in grasses.\niv) Frog can catch insect with his long tongue.\nv) It breathes through skin in water.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37652,481,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which animals other than birds can fly? Why are the adaptations in their body?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Other than birds, some insects and bats can fly.\nii) The shape of the body of insects is tapering and like a spindle.\niii) The body weight is less and thus they can easily fly.\niv) They have two pairs of wings. They also have six stick like legs by which they can walk when on land.\nv) Bats have patagium which is a thin fold of skin between the forelegs and hind legs.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37653,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The capacity of air to hold moisture depends upon the ---- of the air.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','Temperature','',0,0,0,NULL),(37654,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Water does not have a ---- but has definite ----- and ------.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','Shape, Volume, mass','',0,0,0,NULL),(37655,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','While freezing the -------- of water is lowered.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','density','',0,0,0,NULL),(37656,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','-------- Soil has PH 7.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','Natural','',0,0,0,NULL),(37657,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','------ Pressure is the same in all the directions.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','atmospheric','',0,0,0,NULL),(37658,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The proportion of water vapour in the air is high during the -------\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','monsoon','',0,0,0,NULL),(37659,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The substances in which the solute dissolved is called -------\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','Solvent','',0,0,0,NULL),(37660,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','------ Soil has a high water holding capacity.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','Clay','',0,0,0,NULL),(37661,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','------ soil contains a large proportion of organic materials. \n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','Silt','',0,0,0,NULL),(37662,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Crops should be rotated in order to maintain the ------ of the land.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','Fertility','',0,0,0,NULL),(37663,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','----- are an effect of the difference in air pressure.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','Winds','',0,0,0,NULL),(37664,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Air is a ----- of various gases.\na) mixture 		b) compound 		c) element 		d) all above\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','a) mixture ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37665,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Aquatic animals use dissolved ------- in water for respiration.\na) carbon dioxide 		b) oxygen 		c) Salt 		d) none of these\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','b) oxygen ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37666,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The ---- of the gases in the air are in constant motion.\na) element 		b) compound 		c) molecules 	         d) atom\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','c) molecules','',0,0,0,NULL),(37667,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following is not a constituent of air?\na) nitrogen 		b) carbon dioxide 		c) water vapour 	d) salt\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','d) salt','',0,0,0,NULL),(37668,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following is not constituent of air?\na) Water 		b) Soil 		c) salt 		d) all above\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','d) all above','',0,0,0,NULL),(37669,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Water is found in ------ \na) Solid form    	b) liquid form 	        c) gaseous form 		d) all above\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','b) liquid form','',0,0,0,NULL),(37670,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is the unit of measuring mass?\na) centimeters 	b) gram 		c) second 		d) g/cc\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','b) gram','',0,0,0,NULL),(37671,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The proportion of sand, silt and clay in a soil sample determines ------\na) structure 		b) texture 		c) nutrient 		d) fertility level\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','b) texture','',0,0,0,NULL),(37672,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following soil is used in cosmetics? \na) Shadu soil 	    b) China soil 		c) Multani Soil 		d) Terracotta soil \n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','c) Multani Soil ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37673,488,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which day is celebrated as a world soil day?\na) 22nd March 		b) 29th April 		c) 20 August	 	d) 5th December\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','d) 5th December','',0,0,0,NULL),(37674,488,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Match the columns : ','','','(1 – b), (2 – a), (3 – c)','',1,0,0,NULL),(37675,488,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Match the columns :','','','(1 – b), (2 – c), (3 – a)','',1,0,0,NULL),(37676,488,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Match the columns :','','','(1 – d), (2 – c), (3 – b), (4 – a)','',1,0,0,NULL),(37677,488,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false : Sandy soil has low capacity for holding water.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','True','',0,0,0,NULL),(37678,488,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false : Sea water is bad conductor of electricity. \n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','False','',0,0,0,NULL),(37679,488,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false: The substance in which a solute dissolve is called a solvent.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','True','',0,0,0,NULL),(37680,488,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false: The pressure exerted by air is called atmospheric pressure.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','True','',0,0,0,NULL),(37681,488,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false: Air is mixture of various gases.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','True','',0,0,0,NULL),(37682,488,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false: The level of humidity is same in different places.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','False','',0,0,0,NULL),(37683,488,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false : Water is an excellent coolant.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','True','',0,0,0,NULL),(37684,488,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false : The colour of soil is not depend upon its texture.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','False','',0,0,0,NULL),(37685,488,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false: The fertility of soil depends upon soil structure.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','True','',0,0,0,NULL),(37686,488,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false: Repeated cultivation of the same crop increase the fertility of the soil.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','','False','',0,0,0,NULL),(37687,488,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What will happen if : The amount of water vapours in the air increases.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','When the amount of water vapour increases in the air, the humidity rises. The air becomes humid.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37688,488,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What will happen if: Only one crop is grown repeatedly in the soil.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','If same crop is grown again and again, its texture disturbs and the fertility is lowered. The soil does not support the cultivation and the crops will not give proper yield.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37689,488,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What will happen if: An uncorked inverted empty bottle is dipped in a slanting position into the wide container containing water.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The air in the bottle comes out in the form of bubbles.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37690,488,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name some of the substances that dissolve completely in water.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Salt, sugar, powder of sharbat, fruit salts etc. dissolved in water.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37691,488,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','What will happen if: If there will no air on the earth\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) The average temperature of the earths will be very low.\nii) The biotic and abiotic factor will be disturbed.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(37692,488,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','What will happen if: The proportion of water vapour in the air become high.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','If the water vapour in the air is high the dampness and humidity will be increased.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37693,488,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','What will happen if: When rays of light fall on minute particles in the air.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The light shows scattering effect. The minute particles present in the air spread the light in all the directions.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37694,488,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reason: Air is a homogeneous mixture of various gases.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','There are many constituent gases in the air. they are in the form of mixture. The separate existence of each gas is not felt. The individual gases cannot be separated easily. Therefore, the air is said to be the homogeneous mixture. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37695,488,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reason: Water is a universal solvent.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Many substances easily dissolve in water. Therefore, water is said to be the universal solvent.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37696,488,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reason: There is no alternative to water for cleaning purposes.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Many substances can dissolve in water. Therefore, for bathing, cleaning utensils and washing clothes water becomes very useful solvent. It is cheap, easily available remedy for cleaning purpose. Therefore, it is said that there is no alternative to water for cleaning purpose.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37697,488,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reason: The pulled-out piston of a syringe if released, gets immediately pushed inside again.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) When we close the inlet hole of a syringe and pull the piston out, there is more space for the air inside the syringe.\nii) The air inside thus become rarefied. The air pressure inside the syringe thus becomes less.\niii) Comparatively the pressure of the outside air is quite heigh. That is why, when the pulled out piston is released, it is immediately pushed in.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37698,488,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reason: The earth’s surface remains warm.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) The energy from the sun is received by the Earth.\nii) This energy is reflected by the earth in the form of heat.\niii) However, some constituents of air such as water vapour, carbon dioxide, absorb a part of this heat.\niv) Since, air surrounds the earth this heat keeps earth’s surface warm.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37699,488,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reason: We can hear the whistle of a distant train clearly early in the morning winter.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) The sounds travel through the medium of air.\nii) What we hear reach us through the surrounding air.\niii) In winter, the density of air is increased due to change in its temperature. \niv) Therefore, we can hear the whistle of a distant train clearly early in the morning in winter.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37700,488,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Why is the density of seawater more than that of rain water?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) The proportion of salt is greater in the seawater than the rainwater.\nii) This amount of salt increase the density of that water.\niii) This amount of salt mixed into the sea water from the different sources of water through which inlet the sea.\niv) Therefore, the density of seawater is greater than that of rainwater.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37701,488,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is the importance of good soil structure? \n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) The fertility of soil is depending upon its structure.\nii) Roots get sufficient supply of oxygen.\niii) It has sufficient nutrients which help in the growth of plants\niv) good soil structure is useful for planting the trees.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37702,488,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is the effect of increased temperature on the pressure of air?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) The pressure of air increases if that air is inside a closed space and the temperature there in is increased. \nii) When the temperature increases the molecules of air start vibrating with speed. \niii) This results into increasing air pressure.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37703,488,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','In summer, wet clothes dry quickly, but in the rains, they do not. Why this so?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) The air during rainy season is humid. The air contains much moisture during the period.\nii) The wet clothes dry only when the moisture in this clothes evaporates into the atmosphere.\niii) But due to excessive moisture in the air, during rainy season, moisture from wet clothes is not lost.\niv) Therefore, the clothes do not dry up soon. On the other hand during summer season, the temperatures are high and humidity is less. The clothes therefore dry quickly in summer.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37704,488,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Why is it difficult to plough clay soil?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) In clay soil the proportion of small particles of soil is more.\nii) The soil is too soft.\niii) The water logging occurs in the soil very easily. \niv) Therefore, it becomes difficult to plough clay soil.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37705,488,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Why is it easy to plough sandy soil?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) In sandy soil, the proportion of large particles is very high.\nii) Due to this water drains rapidly through sandy soil.\niii)  These particles do not dissolve in water and can be easily shuffled through ploughing.\niv) Therefore, the sandy soil is easier for ploughing.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37706,488,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is the water holding capacity of silt soil?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) The particle size of silt is medium.\nii) It has good water holding capacity.\niii) It is also called sedimentary soil as it has reach content of sediments and organic material.\niv) All these factors helps silt soil to hold water.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37707,488,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','How is light scattered by the air?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Air consists of a mixture of very fine particles of some gases ,dust, smoke and moisture.\nii) When the light falls on the minute particles present in the air, these particles spread the light in all the directions.\niii) This is called scattering of the light.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37708,488,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Why do we see ice floating on water?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) When the water freezes into ice, it changes its state from liquid to solid.\nii) At that time, the volume of the water increase and the density becomes less. iii) When solid ice is formed it is lighter than the original water.\niv) Therefore, the ice floats on water.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37709,488,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is the need and importance of soil testing from the point of view of farmers?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) The farmers wants to good produce from his crops.\nii) By testing the soil he understands the constituents of soil in his farm.\niii) Colour, texture and the proportion of organic matter in the soil is tested by various testing procedures.\niv) If there is any deficiency in the soil that in also found out Measures to be taken to remove deficiency are also suggested.\nv) The pH and the electrical conductivity tests are particularly useful in understanding the characteristics of soil.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37710,488,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','What are causes of diminished soil fertility?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Causes of diminished soil fertility :\ni) The pH of soil is either less than 6 or more than 8. That means if the soil is acidic or alkaline it reduces the fertility of soil.\nii) If there is no proportion of organic matter in the soil.\niii) There is not sufficient drainage of water.\niv) If the same crop is repeated again and again.\nv) When the saline water is continuously used it reduced fertility.\nvi) Excessive use of pesticides and chemical fertilizers also reduce fertility.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37711,488,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','On pouring water in an oil-cladded dish, water does not spread but forms small round drops. Why does this happen?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) The water drop fallen on the oily plate is spherical in shape.\nii) The water molecules attract each other. But they do not have affinity for oil droplets.\niii) Therefore, oil and water do not mix with each other.\niv) Due to their immiscibility, on pouring water in an oil- cladded dish, water does not spread but from small round drops.  ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37712,488,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','What would happen if all the air surrounding us is removed?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Life will not be possible if there is no air in the surrounding.\nii) The processes of respiration and combustion will come to an end.\niii) Phenomena like transmission of sound, heat, humidity etc. will not be possible.\niv) The seasons will not be formed neither there would be a rainfall.\nv) Everything will come to an end if all the air surrounding us is removed.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37713,488,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Will sound be heard in space?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','',') We can able to hear the sounds due to medium of sir.\nii) If this medium of transmission is lacking then we are unable to hear.\niii) In the space there is no air and hence we will not able to hear anything.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37714,488,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','In cold countries, how do aquatic animals remain alive even after the rivers or lakes freeze in winter?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Due to anomalous expansion of water, the lakes, rivers or any water body freezes only on the upper layers.\nii) In cold countries the temperature is very low. Sometimes, it may even reach below zero.\niii) In such times, the temperature of the upper layers of water decreases and becomes lesser than 4⁰C.\niv) At 4⁰C water has maximum density. These dense waters start moving to deeper layers. The deeper waters come to the top to replace these cold waters. The upper layers reach 0⁰C and start freezing.\nv) The lower layers however, remain at 4⁰C and is in liquid state. The aquatic animals remain safe in these waters. Due to ice cover on the top, the external lesser temperatures do not reach lower layers. \nvi) Therefore, aquatic animals remain alive even after the rivers or lakes freeze in winter.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37715,488,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which soil is suitable for cultivation? Why?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) The mixture of clay soil, little sandy soil and same silt soil is suitable for cultivation.\nii) Clay soil has high water holding capacity.\niii) Silt soil is rich in organic matter.\niv) Sandy soil helps in ploughing. If to this mixture organic fertilizers are added then the soil provides water and minerals to the growing crop.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37716,488,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which was the principle put forth by Daniel Bernoulli in 1726?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The principle put forth by Daneil Bernoulli in 1726 :\ni) The pressure of air increases when its velocity decreases.\nii) The pressure of air decreases when its velocity increases.\niii) If a body is moving through air, the air pressure decreases perpendicular to the direction of the motion.\niv) Because of this the air in its surroundings flows rapidly from higher pressure to the lower pressure.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37717,488,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is importance of air in transmission of sound?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Air is the medium for the transmission of the sound.\nii) We are able to perceive the sound due to the air around us.\niii) The sound waves travel through the medium of air and reach us.\niv) In absence of sound we cannot hear the sound. Hence air is most important for the transmission of the sound.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37718,488,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Why should glass bottle completely filled with water never be kept in a freezer?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Due to anomalous expansion of water, it expands while getting frozen.\nii) When the temperature goes below 4⁰C, the density of water start decreasing and at the same time the volume increases.\niii) Temperature in freezer is always less than 4⁰C. This causes expansion of the water. Due to expansion the bottle may burst.\niv) Bottle is made up of glass. The broken glass pieces may cause harm. Therefore, the glass bottles should not be kept in freezer after completely filling them. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37719,488,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Explain the various properties of water.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Water has following properties :\ni) Fluidity : Water has the property of fluidity, due to which it can flow. Water is therefore used for transport and get generation of electricity.\nii) Coolant : It can cool the heated equipment.\niii) Universal solvent : Almost all the things dissolve in water and hence it is called universal solvent.\niv) Ability to perform body functions : Water takes part in the different biochemical reactions taking place in the body.\nv) Cleaning Abilities : Water can clean almost everything. Thus is used in our day-to- day life.  ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37720,488,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is the various uses of soil?\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Plant conservation : Soil helps plants to grow.\nii) Water conservation : Soil has water holding capacity. Therefore, water is available to us, throughout the year.\niii) Plasticity : Plasticity is the property due to which soil can be given any required shape. Therefore, various articles are made from soil. They are baked and made hard for longer use. e.g. storage earthen pots, earthen lamps, idols, bricks, etc.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37721,488,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Explain the picture in your own words:\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) In figure ‘a’ water is seen in the crevice over a land surface. this water is in liquid form.\nii) In figure ‘b’ the same water is converting into solid ice.\niii) As the temperature is decreasing, the water is freezing.\niv) Since there is formation of ice, that means the temperature is less than 4⁰C.\nv) The water whose temperature is less than 4⁰C becomes less dense, but its volume increases.\nvi) The water starts expanding which is shown by arrows in figure ‘b’.\nvii) Due to anomalous expansion of water the crevice in figure ‘b’ now looks bigger than the crevice in figure ‘a’.','',1,0,0,NULL),(37723,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','During photosynthesis plants convert ----- energy into ------ energy.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','Light, chemical','',0,0,0,NULL),(37724,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The leaves have microscopic opening called ------\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','Stomata','',0,0,0,NULL),(37725,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The chloroplast present in the leaves contain -------\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','Chlorophyll','',0,0,0,NULL),(37726,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The transport system of the plant consist of the ------ and the -------\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','Xylem, phloem','',0,0,0,NULL),(37727,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','------- plant do not contain chlorophyll.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','Parasitic','',0,0,0,NULL),(37728,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The process of eliminating waste products and undigested food from the body is called --------\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','Excretion','',0,0,0,NULL),(37729,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Animals that obtain their food from both plants and animals are called -----\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','Omnivores','',0,0,0,NULL),(37730,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Amoeba moves with the help of -------\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','Pseudopodia','',0,0,0,NULL),(37731,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Nutrients can be classified into two types, namely, ------ and ------.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','macronutrients, micronutrients','',0,0,0,NULL),(37732,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Plants make their food in their leaves. This process is called ------\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','photosynthesis','',0,0,0,NULL),(37733,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','---- absorb atmospheric nitrogen and convert it into its compound.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','Rhizobium','',0,0,0,NULL),(37734,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following is a nutrient?\na) Protein 		b) Fat 		c) Vitamin 		d) All of these\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','d) All of these','',0,0,0,NULL),(37735,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which one of the following is a symbiotic?\na) Lichen 		b) Pitcher plant 		c) Loranthus 		d) Cuscuta\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','a) Lichen 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(37736,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Plants that grow on the body of other plants to obtain food are called as -----\na) Insectivorous plants 	b) Saprophytic plant 	c) Parasitic plants 	d) Symbiotic plants \n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','c) Parasitic plants ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37737,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Insectivore plant among the following is ------\na) Lichen 		b) Cuscuta 		c) Algae  		d) Pitcher plant \n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','d) Pitcher plant ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37738,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In the process of photosynthesis plants ------\na) Take CO₂ and release CO₂	b) Take CO₂ and release O₂	c) Take CO₂ and release water 	d) Take and release O₂\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','b) Take CO₂ and release O₂','',0,0,0,NULL),(37739,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The process of taking food into the body is called ------\na) Absorption 		b) Egestion 		c) Ingestion 		d) Digestion\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','c) Ingestion ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37740,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','------ use plants directly as their food.\na) Omnivores 		b) herbivores         	c) carnivores 	          d) Decomposers \n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','b) herbivores ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37741,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following is a scavenger animal?\na) Lion 		b) Monkey 		c) Hyena 		d) sparrow \n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','c) Hyena','',0,0,0,NULL),(37742,489,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In which of the following organism is obtained saprozoic nutrition?\na) chimpanzee 	b) Louse  	c) Round worm 	d) House flies \n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','d) House flies ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37743,489,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Match the columns :','','','(1 – d), (2 – c), (3 – a), (4 – b)','',1,0,0,NULL),(37744,489,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Match the columns :','','','(1 – c), (2 – d), (3 – b), (4 – a)','',1,0,0,NULL),(37745,489,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Match the following :','','','(1 – e), (2 – d), (3 – c), (4 – b), (5 – a)','',1,0,0,NULL),(37746,489,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Match the columns :','','','(1 – e), (2 – d), (3 – b), (4 – c), (5 – a)','',1,0,0,NULL),(37747,489,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false: Photosynthesis takes only in the green plants.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','True','',0,0,0,NULL),(37748,489,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false: The phloem transport minerals and water.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','False','',0,0,0,NULL),(37749,489,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false: Fixation of nitrogen occurs by biological and atmospheric methods.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','True','',0,0,0,NULL),(37750,489,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false: Yeast suck the food with the help of proboscis.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','True','',0,0,0,NULL),(37751,489,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false: All the animals are autotrophic. \n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','False','',0,0,0,NULL),(37752,489,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false: Carbon dioxide is released into the atmospheric in the process of photosynthesis.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','False','',0,0,0,NULL),(37753,489,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false: The xylem transports the food from the leaves to other parts of the plant where  it is either consumed or stored.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','False','',0,0,0,NULL),(37754,489,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false: Root-nodules of leguminous plants contain Azotobacter micro-organisms.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','False','',0,0,0,NULL),(37755,489,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false:  During atmospheric fixation of nitrogen, nitric acid is produced. \n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------','','','False','',0,0,0,NULL),(37756,489,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give four names of scavenger animals.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Crow, vulture, Hyaena, Ants','',0,0,0,NULL),(37757,489,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the organisms that show symbiotic nutrition.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Lichen and fungus growing near the roots of the tree.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37758,489,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','How do plants produce their own food?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Plants prepare their own food by the process of photosynthesis.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37759,489,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reason: Insectivorous plants are attractively coloured.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Insectivores plants feed on insects. They need to capture the insects. In order to attracts these insects towards the plant, they are attractively coloured.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37760,489,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reason: Butterflies have a long tube-like proboscis.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Ever insect is provided with mouth parts for ingestion. It feeds on nectar and pollen from the flowers. It thus has a tube like proboscis to suck this food from flower.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37761,489,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which part of the Loranthus plant carries out photosynthesis? \n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Leaves of Loranthus carries out photosynthesis.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37762,489,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','From where do they obtain minerals and water?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Loranthus obtains the necessary minerals and water from the host plant. For absorption of these nutrients there are specialized roots which are inserted into xylem of the host plants.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37763,489,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Why is Loranthus known as a partially parasitic plant?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Loranthus takes shelter on the host tree. It sucks the water and minerals from the host. But it can photosynthesize and prepare its own food. Therefore, it is called a partial parasite.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37764,489,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Why does the pitcher plant feed on insects even though it produces food by photosynthesis?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Pitcher plant grows in the soil that is deficient on nitrogen. Plant requires nitrogen for building up proteins. To overcome this problem, pitcher plant feed on insects. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37765,489,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name some unicellular organism in which all life-processes take place within their unicellular body.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Amoeba, Euglena and Paramecium are the unicellular organisms in which all the life processes take place within a single cell. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37766,489,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Draw neat and labelled diagrams of the Feeding in Amoeba.\nDiagram : \n\n\n\n\n\n','','','Diagram : ','',0,0,1,NULL),(37767,489,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is malnutrition?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Malnutrition is the state when the required nutrients for proper functioning of the body are not obtained through the diet. Imbalanced diet or over nutrition can cause malnutrition.   ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37768,489,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which are the ways to prevent malnutrition?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Taking wholesome food and balanced diet is the way to prevent malnutrition. Similarly as per our age and type of work, we have to manage our diet to prevent malnutrition. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37769,489,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the micro-organisms that help in biological fixation of nitrogen.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) When nitrogen fixation is done by the microbes present in the soil, then it is known as biological nitrogen fixation.\nii) There are two species of microbes performing nitrogen fixation viz. Rhizobium and Azotobacter.\niii) Rhizobium microbes are seen in the root-nodules of leguminous plants. they absorb atmospheric nitrogen and convert it into its compound called nitrates.\niv) Azotobacter microbes are present in soil. They also convert atmospheric nitrogen into nitrates.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37770,489,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Classify according to food type: Tiger, cow, vulture, bacteria, deer, goat, human, fungus, lion, sparrow, buffalo, frog, cockroach, tick\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Herbivores : Cow, deer, Goat, Buffalo\nii) Carnivores : Tiger, lion, frog\niii) Omnivores : Sparrow, human, Cockroach\niv) Scavengers : vulture\nv) Decomposers : Bacteria, fungus\nvi) Parasitic : Tick','',0,0,0,NULL),(37771,489,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is chemosynthesis? Which plants produce their food by chemo-synthesis?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Using carbon dioxide, methane, hydrogen, hydrogen sulphide, etc. as the sources of energy and producing food in this process is called chemosynthesis.\nii) No autotrophic green plant performance chemosynthesis. Only bacteria (microbes) residing in the areas where sunlight does not reach, perform chemosynthesis. However, chemosynthesis microbes are not plants. They are placed in another Kingdom. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37772,489,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','How does ingestion occur in unicellular animals like Amoeba? \n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) In unicellular amoeba there are no special organs for feeding.\nii) It takes the food through any part of its surface.\niii) When a food particle is located, Amoeba, encircles its totally with the help of Pseudopodia.\niv) The food particle is taken inside the body.\nv) the enzymes are secreted over it by which it digest the food.\nvi) When undigested food is to be thrown out, amoeba leaves it behind and moves further.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37773,489,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which are the different substances excreted by the plants? Why?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Plants excrete substances like resins, gums, rubber, oil, etc. which are not of any use to the plants.\nii) However, for human beings there are important commercial products.\niii) Plants do not have excretory system so such substances are given out by the process of diffusion.\niv) Some substances are stored in the bark of the stem, while some are deposited in the old xylem vessel.\nv) Since, these products are useless for plants their excreted by the plants.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37774,489,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','We prepare a variety of foodstuffs and dishes at home. Are we then autotrophic organisms?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) We prepare variety of foodstuffs by using grains, pulses, vegetables, etc.\nii) These provisions are given to us by plants. We may also prepare food from flesh and eggs of other animals.\niii) We cannot perform photosynthesis wherein we can actually synthesize the food matter.\niv) Hence, we are not autotrophs, we are heterotrophs.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37775,489,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which organisms are greater in number-autotrophs or heterotrophs? Why?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) The number of autotrophs is certainly more. The number of plants should be more so that they can be enough for the herbivorous.\nii) Herbivorous are dependent upon autotrophs.\niii) The autotrophs decrease in numbers; the heterotrophs too will starve and die.\niv) Therefore, in nature the autotrophs are always more than the heterotrophs to balance the food chain.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37776,489,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','The number of heterotrophs found in desert regions is smaller. However, they are found in greater numbers in the sea. Why is this so?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) In desert region, the autotrophs are lesser in number as well as heterotrophs dependent on them are also less.\nii) The food is scarce, therefore, the number of heterotrophs also reduces.\niii) In oceans and seas are multitude of zooplankton and phytoplankton. Phytoplankton are very small, microscopic floating plants which we may not see.\niv) The food chain in the seas is dependent on these planktonic species. Therefore, the number of heterotrophs found in desert regions is smaller but they are found in greater numbers in the sea.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37777,489,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Why is plant food not produced in any other parts of the plant except the green ones?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) The chlorophyll is present in the green parts of the plants.\nii) In these parts photosynthesis takes place.\niii) This produces food.\niv) The non-green parts do not produce food due to lack of chlorophyll.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37778,489,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Draw neat and labelled diagrams of transport system in plants.\nDiagram : \n\n\n\n\n','','','Diagram :','',0,0,1,NULL),(37779,489,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','What factors are necessary for the plants to making their food? \n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Following factors are necessary for plants to make their own food :\ni) Sunlight, carbon dioxide, water and chlorophyll are necessary for the plant to make their food.\nii) Plants need some nutrients for their growth.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37780,489,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Why do living organisms need nutrition?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) To supply the energy required for doing work.\nii) For growth and development of body.\niii) To repair to tissues and for replacing the damaged cells.\niv) To fight diseases.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37781,489,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Explain the process of production of food in plants.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Plants can produced their own food with the help of sunlight, carbon dioxide, water and chlorophyll.\nii) They make their food in the leaves using water and nutrients.\niii) Plants converts light energy into chemical energy and store it in the form of food,','',0,0,1,NULL),(37782,489,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is meant by parasitic plants? name their different types with examples of each.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) The plant that grow on the body of other plants to obtain food are called parasitic plants.\nii) Parasitic plants are heterotrophic.\niii) Cuscuta or dodder do not have chlorophyll.\niv) Hence is complete depends on the host plants.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37783,489,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a short note on Drosera.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Drosera burmanii is an insectivorous plant.\nii) It is seen in the soil which is deficient in nitrogen. To satisfy this need Drosera resorts to feeding on insects.\niii) The plant body looks like a flower. It grows close to the ground. The leaves are pinkish red and they attract the insect. There are hair like structures at the end of the leaves. Droplets of sticky substance are found at the tips of these hairs.\niv) Scientist Johannes Burman studied and identified this plant. The species name of this plant has been named after him.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37784,489,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is the peculiarity of Lichen?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Lichen is the symbiotic association between alga and fungi.\nii) Algae prepare the food through photosynthesis while fungi supply minerals and water to the algae.\niii) Fungi also provide shelter to alga.\niv) The alga and fungus cannot live independently from each other. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37785,489,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Explain the various steps of nutrition in animals.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Ingestion : Process in which food is taken into the body.\nii) Digestion : Conversion of food into the simple soluble form.\niii) Absorption : Soluble substance is transferred into the blood.\niv)  Assimilation : Utilization of absorbed food by cell and tissue for energy production growth and repair.\nv) Egestion : Eliminating waste material and untested food from the body.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37786,489,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','What damage or harm do ectoparasitic and Endo parasitic animals cause?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Parasitic animals are depends on other animals for its nutrition.\nii) These organism sucks the blood with the help of specialized part. E.g. Mosquito and bed bugs.\niii) Mosquito spread some disease like malaria, dengue and elephantiasis.\niv) Endo parasitic are live in the body of animals. e.g. Round worm, hook worm, pinworm, etc.\nv) Endo parasitic absorbs host’s nutrition and cause malnourishment to the host, therefore, ectoparasitic and endo parasitic both are harmful causes damage to our health.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37787,489,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','How does photosynthesis occur in dark red or purple coloured leaves?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) In coloured plants, there are carotenoids, xanthophyll and anthocyanins.  ii) These are plant pigments other than chlorophyll. Carotenoids absorb greenish- blue colour from the sunlight.\niii) The light reflected by this pigment appears Orange to us. xanthophyll imparts yellow coloration. Anthocyanins make the plant part violet and reddish. \niv) These plants also have chlorophyll besides these coloured pigments. However, duo to extra coloured pigments these plants appear to be of that colour and not green.\nv) Photosynthesis in such plants also occur due to chlorophyll. The other pigments absorb some radiation and pass it on to the chlorophyll molecule.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37788,489,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','What are saprophytic plants? \n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Plants which obtain the food from dead animals and decaying bodies of other animals are called saprophytic plants. e.g. mushrooms and yeast.\nii) Fungi secrete digestive enzymes on the dead remains to digest or breakdown the carbon compounds they obtain.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(37789,489,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare and complete the flowchart according to type of nutrition:','','','Tree diagram :','',1,0,1,NULL),(37790,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Draying the food grains from farms under the hot sun is called -----\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','dehydration','',0,0,0,NULL),(37791,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Materials like milk are instantly cooled after heating up to a certain high temperature. This method of food preservation is called -------\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','pasteurization','',0,0,0,NULL),(37792,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Salt is a ----- type of food preservative.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','natural','',0,0,0,NULL),(37793,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Vinegar is a ----- type of food preservative.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','chemical','',0,0,0,NULL),(37794,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','----- is the main energy source.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','Carbohydrates','',0,0,0,NULL),(37795,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','----- is sprayed on the gunny bags containing food grains.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','malathion','',0,0,0,NULL),(37796,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','There is a loss of its nutrient content when the food is -------\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','Spoiled','',0,0,0,NULL),(37797,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Foodstuffs may be spoiled due to by ------\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','micro-organism','',0,0,0,NULL),(37798,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Excessive use of ------ is a qualitative wastage of the food.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','preservatives','',0,0,0,NULL),(37799,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','------ and some other chemicals are used to make bananas look more bright yellow.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','Calcium carbide','',0,0,0,NULL),(37800,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following is a source of carbohydrates?\na) Oil 		b) Papaya 		c) Rice 		d) Pulses\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','c) Rice ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37801,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following is not constituent of food?\na) Carbohydrates 		b) Protein 		c) Vitamin 		d) Sodium benzoate \n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','d) Sodium benzoate','',0,0,0,NULL),(37802,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which method would you use for preserving milk?\na) Pasteurization	b) Irradiation   	c) Smoking 		d) Settling \n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','a) Pasteurization','',0,0,0,NULL),(37803,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','----- is sprayed on the gunny bags containing food grains.\na) Nitrate 	b) Malathion   	c) Vinegar 		d) Citric acid\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','c) Vinegar ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37804,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Who was developed the technique of preserving the quality of food by raising its temperature to prevent microbial growth in the food?\na) Louis Pasteur 	b) Sir Issac Newton 	c) James Watt           	d) Thomas Browne\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','a) Louis Pasteur ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37805,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following is not a chemical preservative?\na) Acetic acid 		b) Citric acid 		c) Sodium benzoate 	d) Salt\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','d) Salt','',0,0,0,NULL),(37806,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','----- is a natural preservative.\na) Sodium benzoate 	b) Nitrite 		c) Sugar 		d) Vinegar\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','b) Nitrite','',0,0,0,NULL),(37807,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','',' ------ are used to prevent the sprouting of potatoes and onion.\na) gamma-rays 		b) sun rays 		c) Light rays 		d) None\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','a) gamma-rays ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37808,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following is a adulterants?\na) Milk 		b) Turmeric powder 	c) Rava 	d) Fine iron fillings\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','d) Fine iron fillings','',0,0,0,NULL),(37809,490,'fillinblanks','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','----- is used to make fruits look more attractive.\na) Methyl yellow  	 	b) calcium carbide 		c) Calcium oxide 		d) Sodium phosphate\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','c) Calcium oxide','',0,0,0,NULL),(37810,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false : The foodstuffs we get from the plant only.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','False','',0,0,0,NULL),(37811,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false : Food get spoil due to growth of microorganisms in it.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','True','',0,0,0,NULL),(37812,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false : Gamma-rays are used to prevent the sprouting of potatoes and onions.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','True','',0,0,0,NULL),(37813,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false : The growth of microorganisms depends upon the temperature.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','True','',0,0,0,NULL),(37814,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false : Proteins protect our body from diseases.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','False','',0,0,0,NULL),(37815,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false : Milk and egg are not good source of proteins.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','False','',0,0,0,NULL),(37816,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false : Leafy vegetables are the source of vitamins.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','True','',0,0,0,NULL),(37817,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false : Rice alone is sufficient to provide all nutrients of the body.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','False','',0,0,0,NULL),(37818,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false : Adulterants decreases the quality of food.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','True','',0,0,0,NULL),(37819,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','State whether the given statement is true or false : Calcium carbide is used to make fruits look more attractive.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','True','',0,0,0,NULL),(37820,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the odd-man out : Salt, vinegar, Citric acid, sodium benzoate.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','Salt','',0,0,0,NULL),(37821,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the odd-man out : Lakhi dal, brick dust, Methyl yellow, turmeric powder.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','turmeric powder','',0,0,0,NULL),(37822,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the odd-man out : Banana, apple, guava, almond\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','almond','',0,0,0,NULL),(37823,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the odd-man out :  Storing, Freezing, settling, drying\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','Storing','',0,0,0,NULL),(37824,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the odd-man out : Milk, rice, wheat, maize\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','Milk','',0,0,0,NULL),(37825,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the odd-man out :  Oil, ghee, butter, vegetables\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------','','','vegetables','',0,0,0,NULL),(37826,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give four examples of : Carbohydrates \n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Cereal, sugar, potatoes, rice','',0,0,0,NULL),(37827,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give four examples of : Proteins\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Pulses, milk, egg, meat','',0,0,0,NULL),(37828,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give four examples of : Vitamins\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Green leafy vegetables, fruits, milk, early morning sunlight','',0,0,0,NULL),(37829,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give four examples of : Fats\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Oily seeds, ghee, butter, paneer','',0,0,0,NULL),(37830,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give four examples of : Minerals\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Milk, raisins, sea food, vegetables','',0,0,0,NULL),(37831,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the methods of food protection.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Freezing, use of insecticides, irradiation pasteurization are the methods of food protection.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37832,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is the common adulterant use in milk?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Urea, formalin, detergents, ammonium sulphate, boric acid, caustic soda etc.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37833,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','How is milk pasteurized?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The milk is heated to a certain temperature for a fixed period of time and then is quickly cooled.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37834,490,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the food constituents that you know?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins, minerals, fiber and water.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37835,490,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the chart given below : ','','','Table :','',1,0,1,NULL),(37836,490,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write the source of carbohydrates.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Jowar, wheat, rice, potatoes are some sources of carbohydrates.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37837,490,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name any four method of food protection.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Freezing, use of insecticides, irradiation pasteurization are the methods of food protection.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37838,490,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Who was developed the technique of preserving the quality of food?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The microbiologist, Louis Pasteur was developed the technique of preserving the quality of food.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37839,490,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name any two food adulterant that you know.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Brick dust, fine iron fillings are the two food adulterant.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37840,490,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','What kind of chemical is used to make fruits look more attractive?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Chemical like calcium carbide is used to make fruits look more attractive.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37841,490,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','For what purpose the chemical preservatives are used?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Chemical preservatives are used for preserving of food.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37842,490,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reason : Food remains safe at 5⁰C.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) In cold temperature of 5⁰C, the reactions caused by micro-organisms do not take place.\nii) At low temperature in refrigerator prevents the growth of micro-organisms in fruits, vegetables as well as in foodstuffs.\niii) Microbes like bacteria, fungi which spoil the food does not grow in the food.\niv) Hence, food remains safe at 5⁰C temperature.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37843,490,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reason : Nowadays, food is served buffet style during large gathering.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Buffet style is used to prevent the wastage of food.\nii) But people take the amount of food in plate that they consume.\niii) The traditional custom of serving too much food to the guest at traditional feasts caused a lot of food wastage.\niv) The guests are free to decide the quantity of food they can eat and serve themselves only that much. Therefore, food is served buffet style during large gatherings.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37844,490,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a short note on : Irradiation\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The process in which food is exposed to ionizing radiations such as high energy electrons emitted by accelerators, X-rays, gamma rays by radioactive isotopes to destroy the microbes and insects this is known as irradiation.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37845,490,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a short note on : Pasteurization\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The technique in which milk is heated up to 80⁰C for 15 minutes to destroy the microbes present in the milk and cooled quickly. This is called pasteurization.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37846,490,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which are the chemical preservatives?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Sodium benzoate, benzoic acid, nitrites, sulfites, sodium sorbate and potassium sorbate. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37847,490,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','What shall we do? : There are vendors selling uncovered sweet meals in open places in the market.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) We should avoid to eat such uncovered food.\nii) The uncovered food may contain the microorganisms causes the food becomes spoil.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(37848,490,'descriptive','3',3,3,'Out of Text Book','','What shall we do? : A ‘Pani – Puriwala’ is serving the pani with dirty hands.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) We should suggest to pani puriwalla to clean his hands.\nii) We should avoid the pani puri which are served with dirty hands.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(37849,490,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','What shall we do? : We have purchased a large quantity of fruits and vegetables. \n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','All fruits and vegetable that we purchased should be washed with clean water.\nii) After washing them, they should be stored in refrigerator in a proper way.\niii) This prevent the growth of microorganisms in them and it remain safe for longer period.\niv) We should purchases only that is needed us.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37850,490,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Explain why this happens and suggest possible remedies : Qualitative wastage of food.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Qualitative wastage of food may happens because of the following reasons : i) Wrong methods of protecting food		ii) Over cooking	iii) Mis- handling the fruits and vegetables	iv) Washing the vegetables after the cutting	v) Mis-calculation of the time required to transport food from producer to consumer.\nRemedies : i) Proper method should be used for protection of food	ii) Some delicate fruits should be handled properly	iii) Avoid the overcooking	  	iv) vegetables should be washed before cutting them.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37851,490,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Explain why this happens and suggest possible remedies : The cooked rice is underdone.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) The cooked rice remains underdone due to lack of water.\n Remedies : i) Add the sufficient water		ii) The rice should be steamed again.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(37852,490,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Explain why this happens and suggest possible remedies : The wheat that was bought in a bit moist.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','If the wheat is not stored properly in a dry place, the moisture from the surrounding make it moist.\nRemedies : i) The wheat should not be touched by wet hand	ii) It should be dried in the hot sun	\n                  iii) Wheat should be stored in a dry place	          iv) The dried wheat should be stored in airtight containers.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37853,490,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Explain why this happens and suggest possible remedies : The test of yoghurt is too sour/slightly bitter.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','','i) If the yoghurt is not stored at low temperature at the right time causes the taste of yoghurt may turn sour.\nRemedies : i) This happens because the process of microbial growth in the yoghurt continues, if it remains at higher temperature\nii) Possible remedies : Store at low temperature.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37854,490,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Explain why this happens and suggest possible remedies : Cut fruits have turned black.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The chemical reaction takes place between the air and fruits. Due to this fruits become turned black.\nRemedies : i) These cut fruits should be consumed immediately		ii) Don\'t keep exposed for longer time         	iii) Cut fruits should be stored at low temperature.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(37855,490,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the chart given below : ','','','Table :','',1,0,1,NULL),(37856,490,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is the exact difference between food protection and food preservation?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The main difference between food protection and food preservation is as follows :\ni) In food protection the food is, protected against spoilage, Care is taken for the prevention of spoilage by microbial growth and infestation by pests.\nii) In food preservation various preservatives are used to prevent food spoilage due to internal factors. Food is kept safe for a longer duration by different food preservation methods.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37857,490,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is meant by quantitative wastage of food? How does quantitative wastage of food take place?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Wastage of food in numbers or quantities is called quantitative wastage. ii) Wrong methods of farming operations such as like hand sowing of seeds, inadequate, threshing, improper storage and wrong methods of distribution results into quantitative loss.\niii) Much food is wasted due to custom of offering and serving in excess to guest at traditional feast or banquets. Similarly in buffet system too, many people fill the plates unnecessary and then they throw the food stuffs uneaten.  ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37858,490,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','How is milk pasteurized?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) In this technique milk is heated up to 80⁰C for 15 minutes and cooled quickly.\nii) Pasteurization kills the microorganisms present in the milk.\niii) After pasteurization milk can be remain safe for longer time.	','',0,0,0,NULL),(37859,490,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Why should we not consume adulterated food materials?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Consuming adulterated food may lead a person to fall ill.\nii) In the process of adulteration people can be added low quality of food, cheapest and sometimes harmful substances to get profit.\niii) However, adding adulterants food becomes poisonous.\niv) When we eat such adulterants food we can fall ill or may death.\nv) Therefore, we should not consume adulterated food materials. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37860,490,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','What precautions do your parents take to keep foodstuffs safe?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) They stored food like milk, vegetables, cooked food and curry in the refrigerator.\nii) Foods like milk and curry are boiled.\niii) Air tight container are used.\niv) Foods like James, murabba, pickles are preserved by adding natural preservatives like salt, sugar, etc.\nv) Some foodstuffs are kept in dry place to avoid the fungus attack thus, my parents take precautions to keep foodstuffs safe.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37861,490,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','How does food spoilage occur? Which are the various factors spoilage the food?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Food spoilage occurs due to improper handling, storage and transportation.\nii) If the micro-organisms from the surrounding entered the food causes food get spoil.\niii) Improper storage of food lead to spoilage of food.\niv) Due to the chemical reaction with a metal pot food get spoiled.\nv) From the surrounding air, water and  land, the micro-organisms enter the food and causes their deterioration.\nvi) Some insects are harmful for the health.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37862,490,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which methods of food preservation would you use?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The following methods I would use for the preservation of food :\ni) Freezing : I would store the perishable foods like cooked food, dairy and poultry products etc. at low temperature. The growth of micro-organisms get slow down.\nii) Boiling : I would boil the foodstuffs like curry, milk to destroy the micro-organisms in it.\niii) Drying : The water content from the grains, some food items prevents them from getting spoiled.\niv) By adding preservatives : a) Natural preservatives like sugar, salt are used for preserving the foodstuffs.	b) I would make pickles from raw mango, chilies and lemons by adding preservation which is prevent the microbial growth.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37863,490,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','What measures you will take for preventing food wastage?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Measures to prevent food wastage :\ni) Not to take extra food into the plate\nii) Finishing all the food that is being served in a plate\niii) Not to overcook the food\niv) The leftover food should not be thrown, it should be properly stored in air tight covered containers.\nv) Buying only required foodstuffs like grains, pulses, vegetables, fruits, etc. Avoid consumerism\nvi) Storing the food materials brought from the market in the appropriate way vii) Checking the expiry date before the purchase. The foodstuffs consumed after expiry date are harmful.  ','',0,0,0,NULL),(37864,490,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is FDA? What is the function of FDA? \n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','FDA stands for Food and Drug Administration. It is a government organization that controls production and distribution of food and drugs by their standardization.','',0,0,0,NULL),(37865,490,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','How and where is food wasted?\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Food gets wasted during the transportation from farm to market.\nii) Improper handling, unsuitable transport options and wrong kind of transportation results in a lot of food wastage.\niii) If food storage is not done properly, the grains will get infested with insects, rats, micro-organisms etc.\niv) At home too, if proper care is not taken, the food is wasted\nv)  Many people waste food while making different preparations. The prepared food too is wasted due to carelessness. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(38020,28,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Which constituents present in an atom?','','','An atom has positively charged protons and negatively charged electrons.','',0,0,0,NULL),(38021,28,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','How can we measure water flow emerging from a pipe? We can find it from the amount of water (litres) coming out in a specific time period? How then is the electric current measured? ','','','i) Electric current is measured by the number of charged particles flowing through a wire in 1 second.\nii) Electric current has its S.I. unit Ampere or Coulomb per second and the instrument to measure electric current is Ammeter.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(38022,493,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Put the following letters in alphabetical order.\n     a, l, d, f','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(38023,493,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find out missing letters.\n s.....u......w......y','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(38024,493,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the series of the months.\nJune........august...... October ','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(38025,493,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write down opposite words for :.\n a) tiny                                 b) safe','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(38026,493,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write down plural forms of the following.\na) boat                           b) root','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(38027,493,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Copy the following sentence :\n Students dance in a hall.','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(38028,493,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write down two words in which \'C\' sound as \'K\'','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(38029,493,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Put the following letters in alphabetical order.\n      r, a, n, h','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(38030,493,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find out missing letters in\n  g.....i....