osite words for.\n            a)  difficult                b)  cold\n      3) Complete the following sentences using correct preposition.\n          I am going ....... station (in/ to/ on)\n\nB) Translation into Marathi ------------- 2M\n    1) Meena is playing football.\n    2) Meera is studying science.\n\nAns. : A] 1) -------------------------------------------------------------\n\n              2) ------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             3) --------------------------------------------------------------\n\nB]        1) --------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           2) --------------------------------------------------------------    ','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(38080,395,'descriptive','3',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Do as directed ----------------- 3M\n      1) Fill in the blanks with appropriate article.\n           I like to eat ..... icecream.\n       2) Fill in the blanks using on or in.\n           Gopal is ........the room.\n      3) Write down past participle form of \'write\'\n\nB) Translation in to Marathi ---------------- 2M \n       1) The dog is faithful animal.\n        2) The sun is behind the hills.\n\nAns. : A] 1) -------------------------------------------------------------\n\n              2) ------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             3) --------------------------------------------------------------\n\nB]        1) --------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           2) --------------------------------------------------------------    ','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(38081,395,'descriptive','3',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Do as directed -------------- 3M\n      1) Write down past tense form of.\n            a) read    b) hit\n       2) Write down past participle form of \n            a) Walk      b) eat\n      3) Write down \'ing\' form of the verb \n         a) take               b) make\n\nB) Translate in to Marathi ----------------- 2M\n      1) The car is in front of house.\n      2) Raju and Kedar are friends.\n\nAns. : A] 1) -------------------------------------------------------------\n\n              2) ------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             3) --------------------------------------------------------------\n\nB]        1) --------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           2) --------------------------------------------------------------    ','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(38082,493,'descriptive','3',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Do as directed ------------------ 3M\n       1) Fill in the blanks using correct preposition from those given in the brackets.\n            Our bags are ..... the carpet. (On/over/in)\n      2) Use proper article.\n           She is...... American writer.\n     3) Write down past tense form of.\n         Give\n\nB) Translation  ---------------------- 2M\n     1) Mohan is reading newspapers.\n     2) Reema saw a big dish.','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(38083,493,'descriptive','3',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Do as directed -------------- 3M\n     1) Fill in the blanks with correct preposition.\n            The dog is sitting......the boy (on/under/near)\n        2) Use proper article.\n           Meena is ...clever student.\n       3) Write past tense form of \'take\'\n\nB) Translation  -------------------------- 2M\n      1) The basket is full.\n      2) I kept money in pocket.','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(38084,494,'descriptive','3',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Do as directed ----------------- 3M\n     1) Fill in the blanks using correct preposition from those given in the brackets.\n          There is a playground ....our school (under, in front of , in)\n      2) Use proper article.\n          This is ....kind of happiness.\n      3) Write down past tense form of.\n          Make\n\nB) Translation ------------------------------ 2M\n     1) Mohini closed the door.\n     2) Rohan opens the window.','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(38085,494,'descriptive','3',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Do as directed ------------------- 3M\n      1) Fill in the blanks with correct preposition.\n          Meena is standing ...Seema and Monica. ( over, between, in)\n      2) Write down \'ing\' form of \n          Keep\n      3) Write past tense form of. \n         Take \n\nB) Translation ------------------------ 2M\n     1) Teacher is teaching English.\n     2) We are studying mathematics.','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(38335,248,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','सोपे रूप द्या : (x – 2y + 3)² + (x + 2y – 3)²','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(38402,547,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The point of concurrence of angle bisectors of a triangle is called as its -----\na) Circumcenter 		b) Incenter 		c) Orthocenter 	d) Centroid\n\nAns. : ------------------------------','','','b) Incenter ','',0,0,0,NULL),(38403,547,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The point of concurrence of the perpendicular bisectors of all sides of a triangle is called as its -----\na) Circumcenter 		b) Incenter 		c) Orthocenter 	d) Centroid\n\nAns. : ------------------------------','','','a) Circumcenter ','',0,0,0,NULL),(38404,547,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The point of concurrence of perpendicular bisectors of sides of which triangle lies outside the triangle?\na) Obtuse angled triangle 	b) Acute angled triangle 		c) Right angled triangle 	d) equilateral triangle\n\nAns. : ------------------------------','','','a) Obtuse angled triangle ','',0,0,0,NULL),(38405,547,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In ΔABC, if ∠A = 30⁰ and ∠B = 60⁰ then ΔABC is of the type -----\na) equilateral triangle 		b) obtuse angled triangle 		c) isosceles triangle 		d) Right angled triangle\n\nAns. : ------------------------------','','','d) Right angled triangle','',0,0,0,NULL),(38406,547,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','A triangle can be constructed by taking two of its angles as.\na) 90⁰, 90⁰ 		b) 80⁰, 105⁰ 		c) 110⁰, 40⁰       	d) 125⁰, 55⁰\n\nAns. : ------------------------------','','','c) 110⁰, 40⁰ ','',0,0,0,NULL),(38407,547,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In a ΔABC, ∠A = 65⁰, ∠B = 35⁰, find the measure of ∠C.\na) 100⁰ 		b) 80⁰ 		c) 60⁰             	d) 90⁰\n\nAns. : ------------------------------','','','b) 80⁰ 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(38408,547,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In a ΔABC, if ∠A = ∠B + ∠C, then find ∠A.\na) 60⁰ 		b) 45⁰ 		c) 90⁰ 	       d) 120⁰\n\nAns. : ------------------------------','','','c) 90⁰ ','',0,0,0,NULL),(38409,547,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In an isosceles triangle one of its equal angle is 25⁰, then the greatest angle is \na) 60⁰ 		b) 95⁰ 		c) 130⁰ 		d) 67.5⁰\n\nAns. : ------------------------------','','','c) 130⁰ ','',0,0,0,NULL),(38410,547,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In a triangle, one angle is of 90⁰. Then in the given statements which is true?\ni) The other two angles are of 45⁰ each 	ii) In remaining two angles, one angle is 90⁰ and other is 45⁰ 		iii) Remaining two angles are complementary\na) (i) only 		b) (ii) only 		c) (iii) only 		d) (i) and (ii)\n\nAns. : ------------------------------','','','c) (iii) only ','',0,0,0,NULL),(38411,547,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following statement is incorrect?\na) The sum of any two sides of a triangle is greater than the third side.	\nb) A triangle can have all its angle acute	\nc) A right-angled triangle cannot be equilateral	\nd) difference of any two sides of a triangle is greater than the third side.\n\nAns. : ------------------------------','','','d) difference of any two sides of a triangle is greater than the third side.','',0,0,0,NULL),(38412,547,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In a right isosceles triangle the measure of one of the angles other than the right angle is -----\na) 90⁰		b) 60⁰ 		c) 45⁰ 		d) can’t be determined\n\nAns. : ------------------------------','','','c) 45⁰ ','',0,0,0,NULL),(38413,547,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following set of angles cannot be the angles of a triangle\na) 67⁰, 51⁰, 62⁰		b) 70⁰, 83⁰, 27⁰		c) 90⁰, 70⁰, 20⁰		d) 40⁰, 132⁰, 18⁰\n\nAns. : ------------------------------','','','d) 40⁰, 132⁰, 18⁰','',0,0,0,NULL),(38414,547,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following is not a set of length of the sides of a triangle?\na) 8, 4, 20 		b) 9, 17, 25 		c) 11, 16, 26            	d) None of these\n\nAns. : ------------------------------','','','a) 8, 4, 20 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(38415,547,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','If two angles of a triangle measure 63⁰ and 27⁰, then it is a /an \na) Acute angle triangle 		b) Obtuse angle triangle 	c) Right angled triangle 		d) None of these\n\nAns. : ------------------------------','','','c) Right angled triangle','',0,0,0,NULL),(38416,547,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In a triangle, there are 3 different angles. Which of the following statements is /are definitely true about the angles?\ni) Sum of all the angles is 100⁰ 		ii) One angles is obtuse and other two are acute and right angle respectively. 	iii) Sum of any two angles is always less than 180⁰\na) (i) only 		b) (ii) and (iii) both    	c) (iii) only 		d) (i) and (iii) both\n\nAns. : ------------------------------','','','c) (iii) only ','',0,0,0,NULL),(38417,547,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','If the measures of the angles of ΔABC are in ratio 1 : 2 : 3, then the measure of the smallest angle is \na) 30⁰ 	b) 60⁰	               c) 90⁰	          d) 120⁰\n\nAns. : ------------------------------','','','a) 30⁰ ','',0,0,0,NULL),(38418,547,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','A triangle can be constructed by taking its sides as ------ cm.\na) 1.8, 2.6, 4.4 	           b) 2, 3, 4 		c) 2.4, 2.4, 6.4 	                   d) 3.2, 2.3, 5.5\n\nAns. : ------------------------------','','','b) 2, 3, 4 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(38419,547,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the measure of the largest angle of a triangle, if one angle is 70⁰ and the other two angles are in the ratio 7 : 15.\na) 70⁰	              b) 75⁰	c) 80⁰	                    d) 90⁰\n\nAns. : ------------------------------','','','b) 75⁰','',0,0,0,NULL),(38420,547,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is the measure of each angle of an equilateral triangle?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','In equilateral triangle each angle is 60⁰','',0,0,0,NULL),(38421,547,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Is it possible to draw a triangle whose sides are 5 cm, 8 cm, 9 cm?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The sum of lengths of any two sides must be greater than third side.\n∴ Taking lengths 5 cm, 8 cm, 9 cm are possible to draw triangle.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(38422,547,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','How many lines of symmetry are there in an equilateral triangle?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Equilateral triangle having three lines of symmetry.','',0,0,0,NULL),(38423,547,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the angles of a ΔABC which are in the ratio 11 : 13 : 12.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','11x + 13x + 12x = 180⁰\n∴ 36x = 180       ⟹ x = 5\n∴ Angles of triangle are 11x = 11 × 5 = 55⁰, 13x = 13 × 5 = 65⁰, 12x = 12 × 5 = 60⁰','',0,0,0,NULL),(38424,547,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Two angles of a triangle are equal and the third angle measure 80⁰. Find the measure of each of the unknown angles.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Let unknown angle be x⁰\n∴ x + x + 80 = 180⁰ ---- [sum of angles of triangle]\n∴ 2x = 180 – 80 = 100    ⟹ x = 50⁰\n∴ Unknown angles are 50⁰, 50⁰ respectively.','',0,0,0,NULL),(38425,547,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The angles of a triangle are in the ratio 3 : 5 : 10. Find the measure of each angle.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','3x + 5x + 10x = 180⁰ ----- [sum of angles of triangle]\n∴ 18x = 180⁰     ⟹ x = 10\n∴ Angles of triangle are 3x = 3 × 10 = 30⁰, 5x = 5 × 10 = 50⁰, 10x = 10 × 10 = 100⁰','',0,0,0,NULL),(38426,547,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The angles of a triangle are in the ratio 6 : 5 : 4. Find the unit digit of the largest angle.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','6x + 5x + 4x = 180⁰  ----- [sum of angles of triangle]\n∴ 15x = 180⁰       ⟹   x = 12⁰\n∴ Angles of triangles are 6x = 6 × 12 = 72⁰, 5x = 5 × 12 = 60⁰, 4x = 4 × 12 = 48⁰ ','',0,0,0,NULL),(38427,547,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Draw the perpendicular bisector of the given line segments of length 5.3 cm\nAns. : \n\n\n\n\n','','','Student can draw the figure by given information.','',0,0,0,NULL),(38428,547,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Draw the perpendicular bisector of the given line segments of length 6.7 cm\nAns. : \n\n\n\n\n','','','Student can draw the figure by given information.','',0,0,0,NULL),(38429,547,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Draw the perpendicular bisector of the given line segments of length 3.8 cm\nAns. :\n\n\n\n\n','','','Student can draw the figure by given information.','',0,0,0,NULL),(38430,547,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Draw angles of the measures give