 woman had been to sleep a teeny-tiny time, she was awakened by a teeny-tiny voice from the teeny-tiny cupboard, which said:\n\'Give me my bone!\'\nAnd this teeny-tiny woman was a teeny-tiny bit frightened, so she hid her teeny-tiny head under the teeny-tiny clothes and went to sleep again. And when she had been to sleep again a teeny-tiny time, the teeny-tiny voice again cried out from the teeny- tiny cupboard a teeny-tiny louder,\n\'Give me my bone!\'\n2) Give reasons.\n     i) The teeny-tiny woman went up to her bed.\n     ii) The teeny-tiny woman hid her head under clothes.\n3) Put the following words in alphabetical order. \n      teeny, tiny, Tony, Tanny.','','1) Woman, house, stairs, bed, bone\n2) i) because she was tired.\n   ii) because she was frightened.\n3) Tanny Teeny tiny tony','',1,0,0,NULL),(39322,571,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Arrange the following sentences in proper order.\n     i. She was frightened.\n     ii. She was awakened by the voice.\n     iii. She put the teeny-tiny bone in the cupboard.\n     iv. The teeny tiny woman went up to her bed.\nNow, when the teeny-tiny woman got home to her teeny-tiny house, she was a teeny-tiny bit tired; so she went up her teeny-tiny stairs to her teeny-tiny bed, and put the teeny-tiny bone into a teeny-tiny cupboard. And when this teeny-tiny woman had been to sleep a teeny-tiny time, she was awakened by a teeny-tiny voice from the teeny-tiny cupboard, which said:\n\'Give me my bone!\'\nAnd this teeny-tiny woman was a teeny-tiny bit frightened, so she hid her teeny-tiny head under the teeny-tiny clothes and went to sleep again. And when she had been to sleep again a teeny-tiny time, the teeny-tiny voice again cried out from the teeny- tiny cupboard a teeny-tiny louder,\n\'Give me my bone!\'\n2) Write the following words in appropriate column :\n      (sleep, woman, bone)\n    i. Concrete Nouns  : -------------------------\n    ii. Abstract Nouns : ------------------------\n3) What should we do when we find something in the street?','','','1) iv, iii, ii, i\n2) i) Concrete Noun : Woman, bone \n    ii) Abstract Noun : Sleep\n3) If we find something in the street we should give it to him who owes it. We should tell others about it.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(39323,571,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Once upon a time there was a teeny-tiny woman who lived in a teeny-tiny house in a teeny-tiny village. Now, one day this teeny-tiny woman tied her teeny-tiny scarf, and went out of her teeny-tiny house to take a teeny-tiny walk. And when this teeny-tiny woman had gone a teeny-tiny way, she came to a teeny-tiny gate; so the teeny-tiny woman opened the teeny-tiny gate, and went into a teeny-tiny churchyard.\nAnd when this teeny-tiny woman had got into the teeny-tiny churchyard, she saw a teeny-tiny bone on a teeny-tiny grave, and the teeny-tiny woman said to her teeny-tiny self:\n\'This teeny-tiny bone will make me some teeny-tiny soup for my teeny-tiny supper.\'\nSo the teeny-tiny woman put the teeny-tiny bone into her teeny-tiny pocket, and went home to her teeny-tiny house.\n1) Read the following sentences and fill in the blanks. ----------- 3M\n     i. The teeny - tiny woman lived in a teeny – tiny -----------\n     ii. The teeny - tiny woman went out to take a -----------------\n     iii. The teeny - tiny woman went into a teeny-tiny ----------------\n     iv. The teeny-tiny woman found a teeny - tiny  ------ on a teeny - tiny --------\n      v. The teeny - tiny woman put the teeny - tiny ------- in to her teeny tiny ------\n2) The word teeny-tiny is a compound word that is a word made of two words. Words like teeny tiny are mostly used in informal language, children\'s stories and songs, folk tales etc. Write other words like teeny - tiny.  -------- 2M','','','1) i) house,       ii) Teeny - tiny walk,         iii) churchyard, \n    iv) bone, grave,                 v) bone, pocket,\n2) incy – wincy, tic – tac, hickary – dickary, chit – chat','',0,0,0,NULL),(39324,571,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Now, when the teeny-tiny woman got home to her teeny-tiny house, she was a teeny-tiny bit tired; so she went up her teeny-tiny stairs to her teeny-tiny bed, and put the teeny-tiny bone into a teeny-tiny cupboard. And when this teeny-tiny woman had been to sleep a teeny-tiny time, she was awakened by a teeny-tiny voice from the teeny-tiny cupboard, which said:\n\'Give me my bone!\'\nAnd this teeny-tiny woman was a teeny-tiny bit frightened, so she hid her teeny-tiny head under the teeny-tiny clothes and went to sleep again. And when she had been to sleep again a teeny-tiny time, the teeny-tiny voice again cried out from the teeny- tiny cupboard a teeny-tiny louder,\n\'Give me my bone!\'\nThis made the teeny-tiny woman a teeny - tiny more frightened, so she hid her teeny-tiny head a teeny-tiny further under the teeny-tiny clothes. And when the teeny - tiny woman had been to sleep again a teeny-tiny time, the teeny-tiny voice from the teeny-tiny cupboard said again a teeny-tiny louder,\n\'Give me my bone!\'\nAnd this teeny-tiny woman was a teeny-tiny bit more frightened, but she put her teeny-tiny head out of the teeny tiny clothes, and said in her loudest teeny-tiny voice,\n\'TAKE IT.\n1) Read the following sentences and fill in the blanks : ------------ 3M\n     i. The teeny-tiny woman went home and put the teeny- tiny ------- into a teeny tiny ---------------\n     ii. The teeny-tiny woman was awakened by a teeny- tiny ---------- from the teeny – tiny ----------------\n    iii. The teeny-tiny woman was ----------------\n    iv. The teeny – tiny woman said in her --------- teeny-tiny voice.\n2) The word teeny-tiny is a compound word that is a word made of two words. Words like teeny tiny are mostly used in informal language, children\'s stories and songs, folk tales etc. Write other words like teeny - tiny. ---------- 2M','','','1) i) bone, cupboard,         ii) voice, cupboard,          iii) teeny-ti