','',1,0,0,NULL),(39362,572,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Look at the picture given below. Write the instructions for making this pretty paper  bird using the clues given in the picture.','','','1) take a square paper             2) Draw a circle on it.          3) Cut the circle\n4) Fold the paper in middle        5) cut along the middle      6) take one part\n7) fold it in the direction of the arrow         8) fold again      9) cut it as shown          10) fold upwards         11) now make beck         12) Pretty paper bird is ready','',1,0,0,NULL),(39363,572,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Tara and friends are busy producing their ‘Class Magazine’. Many children have sent their contributions to the magazine. But sadly, the pieces have all got mixed up. Can you help Tara to sort out the pieces?\nSorting out : Fruit Chat','','','i) Ingredients: 1 big guava, 1 big piece of papaya, 1 big apple, 1 big slice of pineapple, sweet lemon segments, lemon juice-1 teaspoon, 1 tablespoon of pomegranate seeds, chat masala, salt to taste\nii) Method:\n    1. Wash the guave and cut it into big pieces.\n    2. Put all the ingredients in a glass bowl.\n    3. Sprinkle chat masala and mix the ingredients well.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39365,572,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Tara and friends are busy producing their ‘Class Magazine’. Many children have sent their contributions to the magazine. But sadly, the pieces have all got mixed up. Can you help Tara to sort out the pieces?\nSorting out : Green Chutney ','','','i) Ingredients: A medium piece of coconut, 2 green chillies, coriander leaves, salt to taste and a 1/2 spoonful of sugar.\n    1. Wash the chillies and coriander leaves.\n    2. Cut the coconut into pieces.\n    3. Add salt and sugar.\nii) Put all the ingredients together and grind them in a mixer or on the grinding stone.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39366,189,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Tara and friends are busy producing their ‘Class Magazine’. Many children have sent their contributions to the magazine. But sadly, the pieces have all got mixed up. Can you help Tara to sort out the pieces?\nSorting out : Paper Penguin ','\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','i) Cut out a head and body shape and two wings from black craft paper \nii) Cut out a beak a hat a bow tie and feet from different coloured craft paper\niii) Paste the different part together on card paper\niv) Draw a proper background to show the sky and the ice.\nv) Decorate it with coloured paper markers and stickers ','',1,0,0,NULL),(39367,189,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Look at the picture given below. Write the instructions for making this pretty paper  bird using the clues given in the picture.','\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','1) take a square paper             2) Draw a circle on it.          3) Cut the circle\n4) Fold the paper in middle        5) cut along the middle      6) take one part\n7) fold it in the direction of the arrow         8) fold again      9) cut it as shown          10) fold upwards         11) now make beck         12) Pretty paper bird is ready','',1,0,0,NULL),(39368,189,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Tara and friends are busy producing their ‘Class Magazine’. Many children have sent their contributions to the magazine. But sadly, the pieces have all got mixed up. Can you help Tara to sort out the pieces?\nSorting out : Fruit Chat','\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','i) Ingredients: 1 big guava, 1 big piece of papaya, 1 big apple, 1 big slice of pineapple, sweet lemon segments, lemon juice-1 teaspoon, 1 tablespoon of pomegranate seeds, chat masala, salt to taste\nii) Method:\n    1. Wash the guave and cut it into big pieces.\n    2. Put all the ingredients in a glass bowl.\n    3. Sprinkle chat masala and mix the ingredients well.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39369,189,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Tara and friends are busy producing their ‘Class Magazine’. Many children have sent their contributions to the magazine. But sadly, the pieces have all got mixed up. Can you help Tara to sort out the pieces?\nSorting out : Green Chutney ','\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -----------------------