e following sentence : \nShe goes to school everyday. \n','','','Subject : She\nPredicate : goes to school everyday','',0,0,0,NULL),(39457,574,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find out subject and predicate in the following sentence : \nThe sky is blue \n','','','Subject : The sky\nPredicate : is blue','',0,0,0,NULL),(39458,574,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write the related words for – classroom','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(39459,574,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Make meaningful sentence by using phrase ‘to be over’ \n                              OR \nAdd a clause to the following sentence to expand it meaningfully. \n                           This is the answer','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(39460,574,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Make meaningful sentence by using phrase ‘to be settled down’ \n                                     OR \nAdd a clause to the following sentence to expand it meaningfully. \n                          I meet a newspaper boy','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(39461,574,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Make meaningful sentence by using phrase ‘to be confined up’ \n                                          OR \nAdd a clause to the following sentence to expand it meaningfully. \n                                     Swami is a kid','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(39462,574,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Add a prefix or suffix to make new words. \n          (i) Discuss                    (ii) Ignore \n                                  OR \nMake a meaningful sentence using any one of the following words. \n              (i) Discuss                                     (ii) Ignore','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(39463,574,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Add a prefix or suffix to make new words. \n     (i) Loyal                             (ii) Local \n                              OR \nMake a meaningful sentence using any one of the following words. \n          (i) Loyal                              (ii) Local','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(39464,574,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Name the following :\n    i. Great scientists               ii. His birth year\n    iii. His birth place               iv. Musical instruments\nBorn in Tiruchirapalli in southern India, in the year 1888, Raman grew up to be one of the greatest scientists in India. He was a bright student right from the start and was deeply interested in optical science and acoustics. This is what perhaps led him to discover that the mridangam and the tabla produced more melodious sounds than any other percussion instrument. He was fascinated by colourful things, be it a flower, butterfly or gem. He kept seeking knowledge about everything around him.\n2) Find out the words from the passage that mean :\n     i. related to eye                 ii. sweet\n     iii. related to sound          iv. stroke\n3) Find out subject and predicate \n    He was a bright student.','','','1) i) C. V. Raman         ii) 1988         \n    iii) Tiruchirapalli        iv) mridangam and tabla\n2) i) optical             ii) melodious         iii) acoustics       iv) percussion \n3) subject = He            Predicate =  was a bright future.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39465,574,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following sentences \n     i. Raman was deeply interested in --------------\n    ii. Raman was fascinated by ------------------\nBorn in Tiruchirapalli in southern India, in the year 1888, Raman grew up to be one of the greatest scientists in India. He was a bright student right from the start and was deeply interested in optical science and acoustics. This is what perhaps led him to discover that the mridangam and the tabla produced more melodious sounds than any other percussion instrument. He was fascinated by colourful things, be it a flower, butterfly or gem. He kept seeking knowledge about everything around him. He became a scholar in sound and sound related physics. \n2) Which subject scholar in Raman?\n3) Write 3 – 4 sentences on any scientist. ','','','1) i) Optical science and acoustics           ii) colourful things\n2) sound and sound related physics.\n3)  Luther barbank was a great scientist. He is called as agricultural wizard. He grew 120 types of mangoes on only one tree.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39466,574,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following web :\n','When the ship anchored at Calcutta, the young man immediately went on to conduct experiments to prove his theory. His research in optics, the science of light, resulted in the discovery of the Raman Effect. He announced it to the scientific world in March 1928. The discovery won him the Nobel Prize for Physics in 1930. It was the first time this prize was awarded to an Asian! The day he discovered the Raman Effect, 28 February, was later declared as National Science Day.\nEven before this, his contribution to the science of optics had been acknowledged and he was elected Fellow of the Royal Society in 1924. \n2) Find out the past tense of : \n     a) go                  b) win\n3) Write the following in the correct column :\n     (young, man, immediately, went)\n     i. Noun : -------------------                     ii. Verb : ----------------------\n     iii. Adjectives : ----------------------       iv. Adverb : -----------------','','1) Raman Effect is a theory in optics, the science of light. The great Indian scientist C.V. Raman discovered it in 1930 Raman won the Nobel Prize for physics for this discovery.\n2) a) went               b) won\n3) i) Noun : Man                         ii) verb : went          \n    iii) Adjective : young              iv) Adverb : immediately ','',1,0,0,NULL),(39467,574,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following web :','When the ship anchored at Calcutta, the young man immediately went on to conduct experiments to prove his theory. His research in optics, the science of light, resulted in the discovery of the Raman Effect. He announced it to the scientific world in March 1928. The discovery won him the Nobel Prize for Physics in 1930. It was the first time this prize was awarded to an Asian! The day he discovered the Raman Effect, 28 February, was later declared as National Science Day.\nEven before this, his contribution to the science of optics had been acknowledged and he was elected Fellow of the Royal Society in 1924. \n2) Find out the opposites of :\n     a) lost                 b) former \n3) Why was 28 February declared as National science Day?','','1) Raman\'s contribution to the science of optics were acknowledged by the world and he was elected fellow of the Royal Society. In 1930, Raman won the Nobel prize for Physics. The day of his discovery was later declared as National Science Day.\n2) a) won              b) later\n3) C.V. Raman was the first Indian who won the Nobel prize for physics for his Raman Effect. He discovered it on 28th February. So the Government of India declared the day as National Science Day in his honour.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39468,191,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Name the following :\n    i. Great scientists               ii. His birth year\n    iii. His birth place               iv. Musical instruments\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBorn in Tiruchirapalli in southern India, in the year 1888, Raman grew up to be one of the greatest scientists in India. He was a bright student right from the start and was deeply interested in optical science and acoustics. This is what perhaps led him to discover that the mridangam and the tabla produced more melodious sounds than any other percussion instrument. He was fascinated by colourful things, be it a flower, butterfly or gem. He kept seeking knowledge about everything around him.\n2) Find out the words from the passage that mean :\n     i. related to eye                 ii. sweet\n     iii. related to sound          iv. stroke\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Find out subject and predicate \n    He was a bright student.\n\n    ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','1) i) C. V. Raman         ii) 1988         \n    iii) Tiruchirapalli        iv) mridangam and tabla\n2) i) optical             ii) melodious         iii) acoustics       iv) percussion \n3) subject = He            Predicate =  was a bright future.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39469,191,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following sentences \n\n     i. Raman was deeply interested in ---------------------------\n\n    ii. Raman was fascinated by -------------------------------------\nBorn in Tiruchirapalli in southern India, in the year 1888, Raman grew up to be one of the greatest scientists in India. He was a bright student right from the start and was deeply interested in optical science and acoustics. This is what perhaps led him to discover that the mridangam and the tabla produced more melodious sounds than any other percussion instrument. He was fascinated by colourful things, be it a flower, butterfly or gem. He kept seeking knowledge about everything around him. He became a scholar in sound and sound related physics. \n2) Which subject scholar in Raman?\n\n      ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Write 3 – 4 sentences on any scientist. \n\n      ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','1) i) Optical science and acoustics           ii) colourful things\n2) sound and sound related physics.\n3)  Luther barbank was a great scientist. He is called as agricultural wizard. He grew 120 types of mangoes on only one tree.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39470,191,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following web :','\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWhen the ship anchored at Calcutta, the young man immediately went on to conduct experiments to prove his theory. His research in optics, the science of light, resulted in the discovery of the Raman Effect. He announced it to the scientific world in March 1928. The discovery won him the Nobel Prize for Physics in 1930. It was the first time this prize was awarded to an Asian! The day he discovered the Raman Effect, 28 February, was later declared as National Science Day.\nEven before this, his contribution to the science of optics had been acknowledged and he was elected Fellow of the Royal Society in 1924. \n2) Find out the past tense of :\n\n     a) go = -----------                b) win = ------------------------------\n\n3) Write the following in the correct column :\n     (young, man, immediately, went)\n\n     i. Noun : -------------------                     ii. Verb : ----------------------\n\n     iii. Adjectives : ----------------------       iv. Adverb : -----------------','','1) Raman Effect is a theory in optics, the science of light. The great Indian scientist C.V. Raman discovered it in 1930 Raman won the Nobel Prize for physics for this discovery.\n2) a) went               b) won\n3) i) Noun : Man                         ii) verb : went          \n    iii) Adjective : young              iv) Adverb : immediately ','',1,0,0,NULL),(39471,191,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following web :','\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nWhen the ship anchored at Calcutta, the young man immediately went on to conduct experiments to prove his theory. His research in optics, the science of light, resulted in the discovery of the Raman Effect. He announced it to the scientific world in March 1928. The discovery won him the Nobel Prize for Physics in 1930. It was the first time this prize was awarded to an Asian! The day he discovered the Raman Effect, 28 February, was later declared as National Science Day.\nEven before this, his contribution to the science of optics had been acknowledged and he was elected Fellow of the Royal Society in 1924. \n2) Find out the opposites of :\n\n     a) lost × ----------                b) former × ----------------------\n3) Why was 28 February declared as National science Day?\n\n      ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','1) Raman\'s contribution to the science of optics were acknowledged by the world and he was elected fellow of the Royal Society. In 1930, Raman won the Nobel prize for Physics. The day of his discovery was later declared as National Science Day.\n2) a) won              b) later\n3) C.V. Raman was the first Indian who won the Nobel prize for physics for his Raman Effect. He discovered it on 28th February. So the Government of India declared the day as National Science Day in his honour.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39475,575,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) A) Complete the sentences. ------------ 1M\n     i. If the baby doesn’t sleep -----------\n   B] Have you noticed the changed mood of the mother in the stanza? \nSleep, baby, sleep! \nAnd bleat not like a sheep, \nOr else the shepherd\'s angry dog\nWill come and bite my naughty rogue; \nSleep, baby, sleep!\nSleep, baby, sleep ! \nGo out and herd, the sheep,\nGo out, you barking black dog, go\nAnd waken not my baby so;\nSleep, baby, sleep!\n2) Complete the following table.','3) Write down to pairs of rhyming words.','','1) A] the shepherds angry dog will bite it.\n     B] Yes, the mother’s changed mood is clearly visible. Earlier the mother warns the baby that the dog will bite it. But here she orders the dog to go out and let the baby sleep quietly.\n2) i) Mother asks the baby to go out and herd the sheep.\n    ii) She asks the dog not to waken her baby.\n3) i) sleep – sheep          ii) go – so ','',1,0,0,NULL),(39476,446,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following sentences.\n     i. Mother asks her baby to ----------------------------\n\n     ii. Pretty dreams fall from --------------------------------\n\n     iii. The stars are ---------------------------------------------\n\n     iv. The moon is ---------------------------------------------\nSleep, baby, sleep ! \nYour father herds his sheep: \nYour mother shakes the little tree \nFrom which fall pretty dreams on thee; \nSleep, baby, sleep !\nSleep, baby, sleep ! \nThe heavens are white with sheep : \nFor they are lambs- those stars so bright: \nAnd the moon\'s shepherd of the night\n2) Complete the following table :','\ni) --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ii) ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Find out four adjectives from the extract.\n\n    --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','1) i) sleep           ii) the little tree         iii) very bright         iv) the shepherd of the night\n2) i) Father : herds his sleep\n     ii) Mother – shakes the little tree\n3) little, pretty, white, bright','',1,0,0,NULL),(39477,446,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) A) Complete the sentences. ------------ 1M\n\n     i. If the baby doesn’t sleep --------------------------------------------\n   B] Have you noticed the changed mood of the mother in the stanza?\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- \nSleep, baby, sleep! \nAnd bleat not like a sheep, \nOr else the shepherd\'s angry dog\nWill come and bite my naughty rogue; \nSleep, baby, sleep!\nSleep, baby, sleep ! \nGo out and herd, the sheep,\nGo out, you barking black dog, go\nAnd waken not my baby so;\nSleep, baby, sleep!\n2) Complete the following table.','\ni) -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nii) --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Write down to pairs of rhyming words.\n \n     -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','1) A] the shepherds angry dog will bite it.\n     B] Yes, the mother’s changed mood is clearly visible. Earlier the mother warns the baby that the dog will bite it. But here she orders the dog to go out and let the baby sleep quietly.\n2) i) Mother asks the baby to go out and herd the sheep.\n    ii) She asks the dog not to waken her baby.\n3) i) sleep – sheep          ii) go – so ','',1,0,0,NULL),(39478,576,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','(A village road. Chaturbhuj Babu has come back to the village after passing his MA examinations, hoping that everyone will make a great fuss over him. There is a plump Afghan cat with him. Enter Nilratan.) \nNilratan : : Hello there, Chatur Babu. When did you arrive?\nChaturbhuj : Directly after the MA exams were over. I - \nNilratan : Ah, you\'ve got a fine cat there! \nChaturbhuj : This year the exams were very – \nNilratan : Tell me, where did you find that cat?\nChaturbhuj : Bought it. The subjects I\'d offered \nNilratan : How much did you pay for it?\nChaturbhuj : I don\'t remember. Nilratan Babu, has anybody passed any exams in our village?\nNilratan : Oh, lots of them. But you won\'t see a cat like that in these parts.  \nChaturbhuj : (to himself) Confound him, he can\'t talk about anything but the cat! It doesn\'t seem to matter that I\'ve just passed my MA!','<b>1) Complete the following sentences.</b>\n i. Chaturbhuj is talking about -----------\n ii. Nilratan is talking about --------------\n','<b>2) Find out the words that mean </b>\n     a) come                b) many\n<b>3) Do as directed</b>\n    i. I don\'t remember. (Make it Affirmative)\n    ii. He can\'t talk about anything but the cat (Make Affirmative)','','1) his M.A. examination          ii) the car\n2) a) arrive                b) lots of\n3) i) I forget\n    ii) He can talk only about the cat','',0,0,0,NULL),(39479,576,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','(A village road. Chaturbhuj Babu has come back to the village after passing his MA examinations, hoping that everyone will make a great fuss over him. There is a plump Afghan cat with him. Enter Nilratan.) \nNilratan : : Hello there, Chatur Babu. When did you arrive?\nChaturbhuj : Directly after the MA exams were over. I - \nNilratan : Ah, you\'ve got a fine cat there! \nChaturbhuj : This year the exams were very – \nNilratan : Tell me, where did you find that cat?\nChaturbhuj : Bought it. The subjects I\'d offered \nNilratan : How much did you pay for it?\nChaturbhuj : I don\'t remember. Nilratan Babu, has anybody passed any exams in our village?\nNilratan : Oh, lots of them. But you won\'t see a cat like that in these parts.  \nChaturbhuj : (to himself) Confound him, he can\'t talk about anything but the cat! It doesn\'t seem to matter that I\'ve just passed my MA!','<b>1) Why is Chaturbhuj angry with Nilratan?</b>\n','<b>2) Find out opposite of </b>\n    a) forget               b) failed \n<b>3) Write 3-4-sentences about what you think about the temper of Nilratan - the villager?</b>','','1) Chatubhuj is angry with Nilratan because he doesn\'t talk about anything but the cat. He doesn\'t seem to matter that Chatubhuj have passed his M.A. examination.\n2) a) remember             b) passed\n3) I think that Nilratan is illiterate. He is not interested in the exam that Chaturbhuj has passed. On the contrary he is interested in the fine cat that Chaturbhuj has.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39480,576,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Say whether the following sentences are true or false\n     i. Chaturbhuj was angry with all.\n     ii. Chaturbhuj decided to leave at once.\n     iii. Mother cared more for the cat than for Chaturbhuj:\n      iv. Mother asked Chaturbhuj to bathe first.\n(Inside Chaturbhuj\'s house.)\nMaid : Mother, Dada Babu has come home in a blazing temper.\nMother : Why, what\'s the Why, what\'s the matter \nMaid : I don\'t know (Enter Chaturbhuj.)\nLittle Boy : Dada, can I have this cat?\nChaturbhuj : (slaps him hard.) Cat, cat, cat the whole day long, is it?\nMother : No wonder the poor boy\'s angry! He comes home after such a long time and these brats start annoying him at once. (To Chaturbhuj) Let me have the cat, son. I\'ll give it some rice and milk that I\'ve put by.\nChaturbhuj  : (furiously) Here, mother, you can have the cat and feed it all\nyou want. I shan\'t stop to eat - I\'m leaving at once.\nMother : (plaintively) What makes you say such a thing? - Your meal\'s ready and waiting, dear. You can sit down to it as soon as you\'ve had your bath!\n2) Find out the words that mean\n    i. naughty kids               ii. making angry.\n    iii. angrily                        iv. in a sad way. \n3) Punctuate the following.\n     mother said what makes you say such a thing.','','','1)  i) True         ii) Ture            iii) False          iv) True\n2) i) brats         ii) annoying        iii) furiously        iv) plaintively\n3) Mother said, \" What makes you say such a thing?\"','',0,0,0,NULL),(39481,576,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Was Chaturbhuj was angry with mother too why?\n(Inside Chaturbhuj\'s house.)\nMaid : Mother, Dada Babu has come home in a blazing temper.\nMother : Why, what\'s the Why, what\'s the matter \nMaid : I don\'t know (Enter Chaturbhuj.)\nLittle Boy : Dada, can I have this cat?\nChaturbhuj : (slaps him hard.) Cat, cat, cat the whole day long, is it?\nMother : No wonder the poor boy\'s angry! He comes home after such a long time and these brats start annoying him at once. (To Chaturbhuj) Let me have the cat, son. I\'ll give it some rice and milk that I\'ve put by.\nChaturbhuj  : (furiously) Here, mother, you can have the cat and feed it all\nyou want. I shan\'t stop to eat - I\'m leaving at once.\nMother : (plaintively) What makes you say such a thing? - Your meal\'s ready and waiting, dear. You can sit down to it as soon as you\'ve had your bath!\n2) Name the tense of the following sentences \n    i. We had completed the work\n    ii. She has written a story.\n3) Do you think that Chaturbhuj\'s mother cared more for the cat than for her son?','','','1) Yes, Chaturbhuj was angry with mother too. Because she cared more for the cat and not for Chaturbhuj. She offered some rice and milk to cat. But she did not ask Chaturbhuj about his meal.\n2) i) Perfect Past tense           ii) Perfect Present Tense\n3) No, I don\'t think so. Mother cared for the cat as well as for Chaturbhuj. She offered some rice and milk to the cat. But before that she had made Chaturbhuj\'s meal ready. And she was waiting for Chaturbhuj to have bath and take his meal. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(39482,447,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following sentences.\n\n i. Chaturbhuj is talking about --------------------------\n\n ii. Nilratan is talking about ----------------------------------\n(A village road. Chaturbhuj Babu has come back to the village after passing his MA examinations, hoping that everyone will make a great fuss over him. There is a plump Afghan cat with him. Enter Nilratan.) \nNilratan : : Hello there, Chatur Babu. When did you arrive?\nChaturbhuj : Directly after the MA exams were over. I - \nNilratan : Ah, you\'ve got a fine cat there! \nChaturbhuj : This year the exams were very – \nNilratan : Tell me, where did you find that cat?\nChaturbhuj : Bought it. The subjects I\'d offered \nNilratan : How much did you pay for it?\nChaturbhuj : I don\'t remember. Nilratan Babu, has anybody passed any exams in our village?\nNilratan : Oh, lots of them. But you won\'t see a cat like that in these parts.  \nChaturbhuj : (to himself) Confound him, he can\'t talk about anything but the cat! It doesn\'t seem to matter that I\'ve just passed my MA!\n2) Find out the words that mean :\n\n     a) come = ---------------------------                \n     \n    b) many = -----------------------------------------\n3) Do as directed\n    i. I don\'t remember. (Make it Affirmative)\n\n        -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    ii. He can\'t talk about anything but the cat (Make Affirmative)\n\n         -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','1) his M.A. examination          ii) the car\n2) a) arrive                b) lots of\n3) i) I forget\n    ii) He can talk only about the cat','',0,0,0,NULL),(39483,447,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Why is Chaturbhuj angry with Nilratan?\n\n     ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(A village road. Chaturbhuj Babu has come back to the village after passing his MA examinations, hoping that everyone will make a great fuss over him. There is a plump Afghan cat with him. Enter Nilratan.) \nNilratan : : Hello there, Chatur Babu. When did you arrive?\nChaturbhuj : Directly after the MA exams were over. I - \nNilratan : Ah, you\'ve got a fine cat there! \nChaturbhuj : This year the exams were very – \nNilratan : Tell me, where did you find that cat?\nChaturbhuj : Bought it. The subjects I\'d offered \nNilratan : How much did you pay for it?\nChaturbhuj : I don\'t remember. Nilratan Babu, has anybody passed any exams in our village?\nNilratan : Oh, lots of them. But you won\'t see a cat like that in these parts.  \nChaturbhuj : (to himself) Confound him, he can\'t talk about anything but the cat! It doesn\'t seem to matter that I\'ve just passed my MA!\n2) Find out opposite of :\n\n    a) forget  × -------------             b) failed × --------------------------\n3) Write 3-4-sentences about what you think about the temper of Nilratan - the villager?\n\n        -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','1) Chatubhuj is angry with Nilratan because he doesn\'t talk about anything but the cat. He doesn\'t seem to matter that Chatubhuj have passed his M.A. examination.\n2) a) remember             b) passed\n3) I think that Nilratan is illiterate. He is not interested in the exam that Chaturbhuj has passed. On the contrary he is interested in the fine cat that Chaturbhuj has.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39484,447,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Say whether the following sentences are true or false\n     i. Chaturbhuj was angry with all.\n     ii. Chaturbhuj decided to leave at once.\n     iii. Mother cared more for the cat than for Chaturbhuj:\n      iv. Mother asked Chaturbhuj to bathe first.\n\n        ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(Inside Chaturbhuj\'s house.)\nMaid : Mother, Dada Babu has come home in a blazing temper.\nMother : Why, what\'s the Why, what\'s the matter \nMaid : I don\'t know (Enter Chaturbhuj.)\nLittle Boy : Dada, can I have this cat?\nChaturbhuj : (slaps him hard.) Cat, cat, cat the whole day long, is it?\nMother : No wonder the poor boy\'s angry! He comes home after such a long time and these brats start annoying him at once. (To Chaturbhuj) Let me have the cat, son. I\'ll give it some rice and milk that I\'ve put by.\nChaturbhuj  : (furiously) Here, mother, you can have the cat and feed it all\nyou want. I shan\'t stop to eat - I\'m leaving at once.\nMother : (plaintively) What makes you say such a thing? - Your meal\'s ready and waiting, dear. You can sit down to it as soon as you\'ve had your bath!\n2) Find out the words that mean\n    i. naughty kids               ii. making angry.\n    iii. angrily                        iv. in a sad way. \n\n    ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Punctuate the following.\n     mother said what makes you say such a thing.\n\n      -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','1)  i) True         ii) Ture            iii) False          iv) True\n2) i) brats         ii) annoying        iii) furiously        iv) plaintively\n3) Mother said, \" What makes you say such a thing?\"','',0,0,0,NULL),(39485,447,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Was Chaturbhuj was angry with mother too why?\n\n      ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(Inside Chaturbhuj\'s house.)\nMaid : Mother, Dada Babu has come home in a blazing temper.\nMother : Why, what\'s the Why, what\'s the matter \nMaid : I don\'t know (Enter Chaturbhuj.)\nLittle Boy : Dada, can I have this cat?\nChaturbhuj : (slaps him hard.) Cat, cat, cat the whole day long, is it?\nMother : No wonder the poor boy\'s angry! He comes home after such a long time and these brats start annoying him at once. (To Chaturbhuj) Let me have the cat, son. I\'ll give it some rice and milk that I\'ve put by.\nChaturbhuj  : (furiously) Here, mother, you can have the cat and feed it all\nyou want. I shan\'t stop to eat - I\'m leaving at once.\nMother : (plaintively) What makes you say such a thing? - Your meal\'s ready and waiting, dear. You can sit down to it as soon as you\'ve had your bath!\n2) Name the tense of the following sentences \n    i. We had completed the work\n    ii. She has written a story.\n\n      i)  ------------------------------------        ii) ----------------------------------------------\n3) Do you think that Chaturbhuj\'s mother cared more for the cat than for her son?\n\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','1) Yes, Chaturbhuj was angry with mother too. Because she cared more for the cat and not for Chaturbhuj. She offered some rice and milk to cat. But she did not ask Chaturbhuj about his meal.\n2) i) Perfect Past tense           ii) Perfect Present Tense\n3) No, I don\'t think so. Mother cared for the cat as well as for Chaturbhuj. She offered some rice and milk to the cat. But before that she had made Chaturbhuj\'s meal ready. And she was waiting for Chaturbhuj to have bath and take his meal. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(39486,448,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following web :','\n -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe famous physics professor Stephen Hawking has warned that mankind is facing the most dangerous time in its history today. He said that the world today is facing huge challenges like climate change, overpopulation, epidemic diseases. \'We have the technology to destroy the planet on which we live and have not yet developed the ability to escape it. Perhaps in a few hundred years from now, we will have built colonies amid the stars, but right now, we have only one planet and we need to work together to protect it.\' Hawking wrote recently in the Guardian newspaper.\n2) From the passage find out the words that are related to astronomy.\n\n    ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Find out the adjective forms of :\n\n     a) danger = -------------          b) fame = ----------------------','','1) i) Climate change           ii) overpopulation       iii) epidemic diseases \n2) i) world         ii) climate         iii) planet          iv) stars\n3) a) dangerous          b) famous','',1,0,0,NULL),(39487,448,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following web.','\n\n -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe famous physics professor Stephen Hawking has warned that mankind is facing the most dangerous time in its history today. He said that the world today is facing huge challenges like climate change, overpopulation, epidemic diseases. \'We have the technology to destroy the planet on which we live and have not yet developed the ability to escape it. Perhaps in a few hundred years from now, we will have built colonies amid the stars, but right now, we have only one planet and we need to work together to protect it.\' Hawking wrote recently in the Guardian newspaper.\n2) Find out the past tense of:\n\n      a) write - ----------              b) build - ----------------------\n3) What should we do to save our planet?\n\n     ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n     ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n     ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','1) Stephen Hawking has warned us that we are e facing the most dangerous time today. Our technology will destroy our earth And we have not the ability to escape it.\n2) a) wrote           b) built\n3) To save our planet we should :\n     i) plant more and more trees.\n     ii) avoid excessive use of natural resources.\n     iii) ban plastic','',1,0,0,NULL),(39488,448,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Name the following\n     i. A tiny settlement                   ii. A quack\n     iii. Mountain                              iv. Hospital\n\nAns. : i) --------------------------   ii) -----------------------------\n\n         iii) --------------------------  iv) ------------------------------\nHundreds of people flock every hour to Ralewadi, a tiny settlement near Ambegaon. They wait in long winding queues in the hot sun to get a \'special\' powder from Miribaba who claims that it cures all sorts of diseases. According to him, he has developed this powder from a special herb in the Himalayas. \nUnwilling to give the exact name and source of the herb, he only says that it was revealed to him. He offers it at Rs 25 a packet. Each packet is specially \'blessed\' by him. Some of his followers claim that they have seen him euring thousands of people with his powder. However, Dr Karnik of Ambegaon Civil Hospital says that the number of patients in their hospital has in fact increased in the last few weeks.\n2) From the passage find out the opposites of:\n\n     i. cold x  ---------                         ii. decreased x ----------------\n\n     iii. huge x  ---------                     iv. cursed x ----------------\n3) Frame \'wh questions\' to get ‘Ralewadi’ words by answers.\n     Hundered of people flock every hour to Ralewadi\n\n     ----------------------------------------------------------------------','','','1) i) Ralewadi              ii) Miribaba\n     iii) Himalaya            iv) Ambegaon Civil Hospital\n2) i) hot                       ii) increased\n     iii) tiny                     iv) blessed\n3) Where do hunderds of people flock every hour?','',0,0,0,NULL),(39489,448,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following web :','\n  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHundreds of people flock every hour to Ralewadi, a tiny settlement near Ambegaon. They wait in long winding queues in the hot sun to get a \'special\' powder from Miribaba who claims that it cures all sorts of diseases. According to him, he has developed this powder from a special herb in the Himalayas. \nUnwilling to give the exact name and source of the herb, he only says that it was revealed to him. He offers it at Rs 25 a packet. Each packet is specially \'blessed\' by him. Some of his followers claim that they have seen him euring thousands of people with his powder. However, Dr Karnik of Ambegaon Civil Hospital says that the number of patients in their hospital has in fact increased in the last few weeks.\n2) Frame \'wh questions\' to get ‘sorts of diseases’ words by answers.\n     It cures all sorts of diseases.\n\n     ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) What shows that Miribaba\'s claim is unreliable?\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','1) Special powder: Miribaba claims that his special powder cures all sort of diseases. He has developed it from a special herb in the Himalayas. He offers it at Rs. 25 a packet.\n2) What does it cure?\n3) Miribaba claims that his special powder cures all sorts of diseases. As a result of his claim, the number of patients should have decreased. But Dr. Karnik points out the that number of patients has increased. It shows that Miribaba\'s claim is unreliable.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39492,577,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Name the following\n     i. A tiny settlement                   ii. A quack\n     iii. Mountain                              iv. Hospital\nHundreds of people flock every hour to Ralewadi, a tiny settlement near Ambegaon. They wait in long winding queues in the hot sun to get a \'special\' powder from Miribaba who claims that it cures all sorts of diseases. According to him, he has developed this powder from a special herb in the Himalayas. \nUnwilling to give the exact name and source of the herb, he only says that it was revealed to him. He offers it at Rs 25 a packet. Each packet is specially \'blessed\' by him. Some of his followers claim that they have seen him euring thousands of people with his powder. However, Dr Karnik of Ambegaon Civil Hospital says that the number of patients in their hospital has in fact increased in the last few weeks.\n2) From the passage find out the opposites of:\n     i. cold x                          ii. decreased x\n     iii. huge x                       iv. cursed x\n3) Frame \'wh questions\' to get ‘Ralewadi’ words by answers.\n     Hundered of people flock every hour to Ralewadi','','','1) i) Ralewadi              ii) Miribaba\n     iii) Himalaya            iv) Ambegaon Civil Hospital\n2) i) hot                       ii) increased\n     iii) tiny                     iv) blessed\n3) Where do hunderds of people flock every hour?','',0,0,0,NULL),(39493,577,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following web :','Hundreds of people flock every hour to Ralewadi, a tiny settlement near Ambegaon. They wait in long winding queues in the hot sun to get a \'special\' powder from Miribaba who claims that it cures all sorts of diseases. According to him, he has developed this powder from a special herb in the Himalayas. \nUnwilling to give the exact name and source of the herb, he only says that it was revealed to him. He offers it at Rs 25 a packet. Each packet is specially \'blessed\' by him. Some of his followers claim that they have seen him euring thousands of people with his powder. However, Dr Karnik of Ambegaon Civil Hospital says that the number of patients in their hospital has in fact increased in the last few weeks.\n2) Frame \'wh questions\' to get ‘sorts of diseases’ words by answers.\n     It cures all sorts of diseases.\n3) What shows that Miribaba\'s claim is unreliable?','','1) Special powder: Miribaba claims that his special powder cures all sort of diseases. He has developed it from a special herb in the Himalayas. He offers it at Rs. 25 a packet.\n2) What does it cure?\n3) Miribaba claims that his special powder cures all sorts of diseases. As a result of his claim, the number of patients should have decreased. But Dr. Karnik points out the that number of patients has increased. It shows that Miribaba\'s claim is unreliable.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39494,578,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','<div style=\"column-count:2;\">You\'re not allowed to read this. \nYou really have to stop. \nIf you don\'t quit this instant, \nI swear I\'ll call a cop.\nHe\'ll drag you off in handcuffs. \nHe\'ll lock you up in jail, \nand leave you there forever \nuntil you\'re old and frail.<div style=\"column-count:2;\">','<b>1) Complete the following sentences</b>\n     i. You really have to stop to read this because -----------\n     ii. If you don\'t stop reading this poem ------------------\n','<b>2) What will cop do the reader?</b>\n<b>3) From the extract, find out two pairs of rhyming words.</b>','','1) i) you are not allowed to do so.\n     ii) I will call a cop.\n2) If the reader doesn\'t stop reading the poem, the cop will drag him off in handcuffs, He will lock the reader -up in jail.\n3) i) stop = cop\n    ii) jail = frail','',0,0,0,NULL),(39495,578,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Your friends will all forget you. \nYou won\'t be even missed. \nYour family, too, will likely \nforget that you exist.\nAnd all because you read this \ninstead of having fun. \nIt\'s too late now, amigo;\nthe poem\'s nearly done.\nThere\'s only one solution.\nHere\'s what you\'ll have to do : \nTell all your friends and family \nthey shouldn\'t read it too.\nAnswer the following questions :\n1) The poet is telling someone not to read the poem. Who is that someone?\n2) Does the poet really want you to stop reading the poem? \n3) What does the poet mean when he says, \"Tell all your friends & family they should not read it too\".\n4) Find all contracted forms used in the poem. \n5) Find the pairs of rhyming words used in each stanza. ','','','1) It must be the poet\'s friend.\n2) No, he does not want so.\n3) He means that all friends & family should read it.\n4) don\'t, it\'s, that\'s, there\'s, isn\'t, won\'t, Here\'s, shouldn\'t.\n5) fun – done, do – too, family – likely ','',0,0,0,NULL),(39496,578,'descriptive','3a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','<div style=\"column-count:2;\">You\'re not allowed to read this. \nYou really have to stop. \nIf you don\'t quit this instant, \nI swear I\'ll call a cop.\nHe\'ll drag you off in handcuffs. \nHe\'ll lock you up in jail, \nand leave you there forever \nuntil you\'re old and frail.<div style=\"column-count:2;\">','<b>1) Complete the following sentences</b>\n     i. You really have to stop to read this because -----------\n     ii. If you don\'t stop reading this poem ------------------\n','<b>2) What will cop do the reader?</b>\n<b>3) From the extract, find out two pairs of rhyming words.</b>','','1) i) you are not allowed to do so.\n     ii) I will call a cop.\n2) If the reader doesn\'t stop reading the poem, the cop will drag him off in handcuffs, He will lock the reader -up in jail.\n3) i) stop = cop\n    ii) jail = frail','',0,0,0,NULL),(39497,578,'descriptive','3b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','<div style=\"column-count:2;\">Your friends will all forget you. \nYou won\'t be even missed. \nYour family, too, will likely \nforget that you exist.\nAnd all because you read this \ninstead of having fun. \nIt\'s too late now, amigo;\nthe poem\'s nearly done.\nThere\'s only one solution.\nHere\'s what you\'ll have to do : \nTell all your friends and family \nthey shouldn\'t read it too.<div style=\"column-count:2;\">','<b>Answer the following questions </b>\n1) The poet is telling someone not to read the poem. Who is that someone?\n2) Does the poet really want you to stop reading the poem? \n3) What does the poet mean when he says, \"Tell all your friends & family they should not read it too\".\n4) Find all contracted forms used in the poem. \n5) Find the pairs of rhyming words used in each stanza. ','','','1) It must be the poet\'s friend.\n2) No, he does not want so.\n3) He means that all friends & family should read it.\n4) don\'t, it\'s, that\'s, there\'s, isn\'t, won\'t, Here\'s, shouldn\'t.\n5) fun – done, do – too, family – likely ','',0,0,0,NULL),(39498,449,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following sentences\n     i. You really have to stop to read this because -----------\n\n     ii. If you don\'t stop reading this poem ------------------\nYou\'re not allowed to read this. \nYou really have to stop. \nIf you don\'t quit this instant, \nI swear I\'ll call a cop.\nHe\'ll drag you off in handcuffs. \nHe\'ll lock you up in jail, \nand leave you there forever \nuntil you\'re old and frail.\n2) What will cop do the reader?\n\n    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) From the extract, find out two pairs of rhyming words.\n\n     -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','1) i) you are not allowed to do so.\n     ii) I will call a cop.\n2) If the reader doesn\'t stop reading the poem, the cop will drag him off in handcuffs, He will lock the reader -up in jail.\n3) i) stop = cop\n    ii) jail = frail','',0,0,0,NULL),(39499,449,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Your friends will all forget you. \nYou won\'t be even missed. \nYour family, too, will likely \nforget that you exist.\nAnd all because you read this \ninstead of having fun. \nIt\'s too late now, amigo;\nthe poem\'s nearly done.\nThere\'s only one solution.\nHere\'s what you\'ll have to do : \nTell all your friends and family \nthey shouldn\'t read it too.\nAnswer the following questions :\n1) The poet is telling someone not to read the poem. Who is that someone?\n\n      --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) Does the poet really want you to stop reading the poem? \n\n     --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) What does the poet mean when he says, \"Tell all your friends & family they should not read it too\".\n\n    --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) Find all contracted forms used in the poem. \n\n      --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) Find the pairs of rhyming words used in each stanza. \n\n     --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','1) It must be the poet\'s friend.\n2) No, he does not want so.\n3) He means that all friends & family should read it.\n4) don\'t, it\'s, that\'s, there\'s, isn\'t, won\'t, Here\'s, shouldn\'t.\n5) fun – done, do – too, family – likely ','',0,0,0,NULL),(39500,449,'descriptive','3a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following sentences\n     i. You really have to stop to read this because -----------\n\n     ii. If you don\'t stop reading this poem ------------------\nYou\'re not allowed to read this. \nYou really have to stop. \nIf you don\'t quit this instant, \nI swear I\'ll call a cop.\nHe\'ll drag you off in handcuffs. \nHe\'ll lock you up in jail, \nand leave you there forever \nuntil you\'re old and frail.\n2) What will cop do the reader?\n\n    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) From the extract, find out two pairs of rhyming words.\n\n     -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','1) i) you are not allowed to do so.\n     ii) I will call a cop.\n2) If the reader doesn\'t stop reading the poem, the cop will drag him off in handcuffs, He will lock the reader -up in jail.\n3) i) stop = cop\n    ii) jail = frail','',0,0,0,NULL),(39501,449,'descriptive','3b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Your friends will all forget you. \nYou won\'t be even missed. \nYour family, too, will likely \nforget that you exist.\nAnd all because you read this \ninstead of having fun. \nIt\'s too late now, amigo;\nthe poem\'s nearly done.\nThere\'s only one solution.\nHere\'s what you\'ll have to do : \nTell all your friends and family \nthey shouldn\'t read it too.\nAnswer the following questions :\n1) The poet is telling someone not to read the poem. Who is that someone?\n\n      --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) Does the poet really want you to stop reading the poem? \n\n     --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) What does the poet mean when he says, \"Tell all your friends & family they should not read it too\".\n\n    --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) Find all contracted forms used in the poem. \n\n      --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) Find the pairs of rhyming words used in each stanza. \n\n     --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','1) It must be the poet\'s friend.\n2) No, he does not want so.\n3) He means that all friends & family should read it.\n4) don\'t, it\'s, that\'s, there\'s, isn\'t, won\'t, Here\'s, shouldn\'t.\n5) fun – done, do – too, family – likely ','',0,0,0,NULL),(39504,579,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following sentences.\n     i. The revolver fell down on the floor because --------------\n     ii. The man\'s companion had --------------------\nWe waited silently for more than an hour. It was pitch dark in the cellar. Then suddenly, a point of bright light appeared in the floor of the cellar, then a line, and a gash seemed to open, and a hand appeared. A broad stone turned over upon its side, and left a square hele. A boyish face emerged. \nThe man looked about and came out of the hole. He had a companion with him, a man with very red hair. The pair was none other than Spaulding the assistant alias the criminal Clay and the red-headed Mr Duncan Ross! As soon as they climbed out of the hole, Sherlock Holmes sprang out and seized Clay by the collar. \nThe other dived down the hole and disappeared. Clay took out a revolver. But Holmes hit him on his wrist, and the revolver fell on the floor.\n2) From the passage find out two adjectives and two adverbs.\n3) Change the following sentence into a question and negative sentence.\n      There was pitch dark in the cellar.','','','1) i) Holmes hit him on his wrist.           ii) very red hair.\n2) i) Adjectives = dark, bright         ii) Adverbs = silently, suddenly\n3) i) Question - Was there pitch dark in the cellar?\n    ii) Negative - There was not pitch dark in the cellar.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39505,579,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Arrange the following sentences in chronological order.\n     i. Holmess seized him by the collar\n     ii. A broad stone turned over upon its side.\n     iii. A point of bright light appeared in the floor.\n      iv. A man came out of the hole.\nWe waited silently for more than an hour. It was pitch dark in the cellar. Then suddenly, a point of bright light appeared in the floor of the cellar, then a line, and a gash seemed to open, and a hand appeared. A broad stone turned over upon its side, and left a square hele. A boyish face emerged. \nThe man looked about and came out of the hole. He had a companion with him, a man with very red hair. The pair was none other than Spaulding the assistant alias the criminal Clay and the red-headed Mr Duncan Ross! As soon as they climbed out of the hole, Sherlock Holmes sprang out and seized Clay by the collar. \nThe other dived down the hole and disappeared. Clay took out a revolver. But Holmes hit him on his wrist, and the revolver fell on the floor.\n2) Who were the two criminals?\n3) Find out the sentences from the passage that show that Holmes was a very brave man.','','','1) iii, ii, iv, i\n2) Spaulding the assistant alias Clay and red-headed Mr. Duncan Ross.\n3) Sherlock Holmes sprang out and seized Clay by the collar. Holmes hit him on his wrist and the revolver fell on the floor.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39506,450,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Say whether the following sentences are true or false.\n\n     i. Sherlock Holmes is narrating the story - ------------------\n\n     ii. Mr. Jabez Wilson was a pawn-broker. - ------------------\n\n     iii. The office of the Red -headed League is on Fleet street. ---------------\n\n     iv. Mr. Wilson liked his assistant. ---------------------\nWhen I called upon my friend, Mr Sherlock Holmes, he was conversing with a visitor, who was an elderly man with fiery red hair.\nHolmes introduced me to the visitor, Mr Jabez Wilson. He was a pawn-broker. Holmes asked him to repeat his story for me. He began by showing us an advertisement in a newspaper. It read as follows-\nTO THE RED-HEADED LEAGUE\nThere is a vacancy for a member of the League, and the salary is four pounds a week for nominal services. Red-headed men may apply in person on Monday, at eleven o\'clock. to Duncan Ross, at the office of the League, 7 Fleet Street.\nThe advertisement had appeared in newspaper two months ago. Mr Wilson\'s assistant, Vincent Spaulding, had shown it to him. Mr Wilson liked his assistant Spaulding. He was smart, efficient and worked for only half the normal wages! But, the assistant also had his faults. Every now and then, he left work and went down into the cellar to develop photographs. Photography was his hobby.\n2) Match the following words with their meanings','\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Identify the tense of the following sentences,\n     i. He was conversing with a visitor.\n   \n         --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n     ii. Vincent Spaulding had shown it to him.\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n','','1)  i) False           ii) True            iii) True            iv) True\n2) (1 – b), (2 – c), (3 – d), (4 – a)\n3) i) Continuous present tense           ii) perfect past tense','',1,0,0,NULL),(39507,450,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following web.','\n    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWhen I called upon my friend, Mr Sherlock Holmes, he was conversing with a visitor, who was an elderly man with fiery red hair.\nHolmes introduced me to the visitor, Mr Jabez Wilson. He was a pawn-broker. Holmes asked him to repeat his story for me. He began by showing us an advertisement in a newspaper. It read as follows-\nTO THE RED-HEADED LEAGUE\nThere is a vacancy for a member of the League, and the salary is four pounds a week for nominal services. Red-headed men may apply in person on Monday, at eleven o\'clock. to Duncan Ross, at the office of the League, 7 Fleet Street.\nThe advertisement had appeared in newspaper two months ago. Mr Wilson\'s assistant, Vincent Spaulding, had shown it to him. Mr Wilson liked his assistant Spaulding. He was smart, efficient and worked for only half the normal wages! But, the assistant also had his faults. Every now and then, he left work and went down into the cellar to develop photographs. Photography was his hobby.\n2) Why was Fleet street full of red – headed people?\n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) There is a vacancy for a teacher in your school Make an advertisement for it.\n \n       ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','1) Vincent Spaulding was Mr. Wilson\'s assistant. He was smart, efficient. He worked for only half the normal wages. Photography was his hobby.\n2) Fleet street was full of red-headed people because there was vacancy for a red handed person.\n3) New English school, Pune \n     Wanted Teacher\n      Sub - English\n      Interested candidates may apply to \n       Headmaster, New English School, Pune.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39508,450,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following sentences.\n     i. The revolver fell down on the floor because -----------------------------\n\n     ii. The man\'s companion had ---------------------------------------------\nWe waited silently for more than an hour. It was pitch dark in the cellar. Then suddenly, a point of bright light appeared in the floor of the cellar, then a line, and a gash seemed to open, and a hand appeared. A broad stone turned over upon its side, and left a square hele. A boyish face emerged. \nThe man looked about and came out of the hole. He had a companion with him, a man with very red hair. The pair was none other than Spaulding the assistant alias the criminal Clay and the red-headed Mr Duncan Ross! As soon as they climbed out of the hole, Sherlock Holmes sprang out and seized Clay by the collar. \nThe other dived down the hole and disappeared. Clay took out a revolver. But Holmes hit him on his wrist, and the revolver fell on the floor.\n2) From the passage find out two adjectives and two adverbs.\n\n       ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Change the following sentence into a question and negative sentence.\n      There was pitch dark in the cellar.\n\n       -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','1) i) Holmes hit him on his wrist.           ii) very red hair.\n2) i) Adjectives = dark, bright         ii) Adverbs = silently, suddenly\n3) i) Question - Was there pitch dark in the cellar?\n    ii) Negative - There was not pitch dark in the cellar.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39509,450,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Arrange the following sentences in chronological order.\n     i. Holmess seized him by the collar\n     ii. A broad stone turned over upon its side.\n     iii. A point of bright light appeared in the floor.\n      iv. A man came out of the hole.\n\n      -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWe waited silently for more than an hour. It was pitch dark in the cellar. Then suddenly, a point of bright light appeared in the floor of the cellar, then a line, and a gash seemed to open, and a hand appeared. A broad stone turned over upon its side, and left a square hele. A boyish face emerged. \nThe man looked about and came out of the hole. He had a companion with him, a man with very red hair. The pair was none other than Spaulding the assistant alias the criminal Clay and the red-headed Mr Duncan Ross! As soon as they climbed out of the hole, Sherlock Holmes sprang out and seized Clay by the collar. \nThe other dived down the hole and disappeared. Clay took out a revolver. But Holmes hit him on his wrist, and the revolver fell on the floor.\n2) Who were the two criminals?\n\n       ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Find out the sentences from the passage that show that Holmes was a very brave man.\n\n       ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','1) iii, ii, iv, i\n2) Spaulding the assistant alias Clay and red-headed Mr. Duncan Ross.\n3) Sherlock Holmes sprang out and seized Clay by the collar. Holmes hit him on his wrist and the revolver fell on the floor.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39510,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','Social networking implies the use of internet programs to make connections with friends, family, classmates, customers and clients. Social networking can occur for social or business purposes through sites such as Facebook, Instagram, Twitter, LinkedIn, etc. The biggest advantage of using social networks is that you can stay in touch with your friends and family from all around the world. These social networks can be used to improve our social awareness. Students can explore topics that they are interested in by using online social networking. This can be done by interacting with people from different parts of the world. Teachers, students and professionals can also create discussion forums, or write blogs and posts to explore different and wide-ranging topics. It is online platform where people meet and share ideas and experiences. This can create opportunities for relationship-building, brand-building, publicity and promotions. As people spend more time on social networking sites, they experience less face-to-face interaction which also makes them more dependent on devices. Fifty per cent of people between the age of 25 and 35 years admitted that they are so attached to social networks that they even use them during working hours.','1) Complete the following web :','2) Advantages of Social Networking Sites :\n3) Find out similar words from the passage for the following:\n     a) benefit                             b) enhance \n     c) chance                             d) communication \n4) Do as directed:\n    i) They use them during working hours. (Name the Tense)\n    ii) It is online platform where people share their ideas and experiences.\n            (Use not only ... but also ...)\n5) Do you really think using social media is a waste of time?','','1) Facebook, Instagram, Linkedin, Twitter\n2) a) We can stay in touch with our friends and family from all around the world.\n     b) It improves our social awareness.\n     c) We can find out information on different topics.\n     d) We can meet different people and share our ideas and experiences with them. \n3) a) advantage                             b) improve\n     c) opportunity                          d) interaction\n4) i) Simple Present Tense\n    ii) It is online platform where people not only share their ideas but also experiences.\n5) I don\'t think using social media is a waste of time because it totally depends on us whether to use it for our benefit or just to waste time. If we use it to surf information we need, communicate people to know something, it is going to be more beneficial. But if we use it for playing games and doing a mere timepass for hours and hours, it is going to waste lot of our time. So it totally depends on us how to use it.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39511,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','Global warming is the term used to describe a gradual increase in the average temperature of the Earth\'s atmosphere and its oceans. This causes a change in the Earth\'s climate. Global warming occurs when carbon dioxide (CO2) and other air pollutants and greenhouse gasses collect in the atmosphere and absorb sunlight and solar radiation that have bounced off the Earth\'s surface. Normally, this radiation would escape into space. But these pollutants, which can last for years even up to centuries in the atmosphere, trap the heat and make the planet warmer. This is known as the greenhouse effect. Climatologists agree that the average temperature of the earth has risen between 0.4 and 0.8°C over the past 100 years. They feel that in the past 50 years, the average global temperature has increased at the fastest rate in recorded history. This is chiefly because the increased volumes of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases released by the burning of fossil fuels, land clearing, agriculture and other human activities have been the chief causes of the global warming that has occurred over the decade. Global warming has many environmental, economic, and health consequences. It will be manifested in the melting of the polar ice caps, as well as an increase in the occurrence of storms.','1) State whether you Agree or Disagree with the following statements :\n    a) The average temperature of the earth has risen between 0.4 and 0.8°C over the past 100 years.\n    b) In the last 50 years the average global temperature has increased at the fastest rate.\n    c) Global warming is good for human being.\n   d) Solar radiations last for 5-10 years in the atmosphere.\n','2) Describe Global Warming.\n3) Give one word for the following description from the passage:\n    a) The thin layer of air that surrounds the earth.\n    b) Substance released into the environment due to natural or human activity which adversely affects the environment.\n4) Do as directed:\n    a) It will be manifested in the melting of the polar ice caps, as well as an increase in the occurrence of storms. \n            (Use not only... but also ...)\n     b) Rising sea level could lead to coastal flooding. \n           (Frame a wh-question to get the underlined part as an answer)\n5) What will you do to protect our environment?','','1) a) agree           b) agree           c) disagree          d) disagree\n2) A gradual increase in the average temperature of the Earth\'s atmosphere due to a change in the Earth\'s Climate is known as Global Warming. It occurs when carbon dioxide and other air pollutants and other greenhouse gases collect in the atmosphere and absorb sunlight. It takes place because of the increased volumes of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases released by the burning of fossil fuels, land clearing, agriculture and other human activities.\n3) a) atmosphere            b) pollutants\n4) a) It will be manifested not only in the melting of the polar ice caps but also an increase in the occurrence variety of storms.\n     b) What could lead to coastal flooding?\n5) I will do the following things to protect our environment,\n     a) I will try to plant more and more trees in our surroundings and at my village with the help of my friends and parents.\n     b) I will try my level best to convey the people to avoid use of plastic, throwing garbage anywhere and manage dry and wet garbage properly.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39512,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','Most of us nowadays carry the world in our pocket! It is amazing but true. It is a mobile phone that connects us to the rest of the world within a second. Apart from making calls and sending SMS, the mobile phone is used as a multipurpose gadget. It is a calculator, timepiece, calendar, voice recorder, media player, camera, gaming device, net browser and what not. Its development brought convenience and advantages to the world.\nCommunication between people has become quite easy and very fast. We can keep in contact with others from any place on the bus, in a street or in a meeting by sending a message for less than the price of a call. The radiations of mobile may be dangerous to health and may cause a headache, earache and blurring vision. These invisible radiations destroy the cells located in ear and head which cause damage to the brain and neurons in the head region. It\'s use in certain places causes disturbance sometimes. Mobile phones with camera are causing privacy problems such as using it as a hidden camera to take pictures and making videos.','1) Fill in the blanks and complete the following sentences:\n    a) ----------- in mobile phones causes privacy problem.\n   b) ------------- of mobile may be dangerous to health.\n','2) Write two advantages of using mobiles.\n3) Write two present participles and two past participles from the passage.\n4) Do as directed\n    a) It\'s development brought convenience and advantages to the world. \n           (Use \'As well as\')\n   b) It is amazing. (Make it exclamatory)\n5) Write two disadvantages of using mobile.','','1) a) Camera in mobile phones causes privacy problem.\n     b) The radiations of mobile may be dangerous to health.\n2) Advantages of using mobiles:\n    i) It is used to make calls and send messages.\n    ii) It is used as a calculator, calendar, voice recorder, media player, camera and a gaming device.\n3) i) Present Participles - Amazing, making, sending, gaming, blurring, meeting.\n    ii) Past Participle Connected, brought.\n4) a) It\'s development brought convenience as well as advantages to the world.\n    b) How amazing it is!\n5) Disadvantages of using mobiles:\n     i) It takes away our valuable time if it is not used properly.\n    ii) It affects our eyes, ears and neck.\n    iii) It disturbs our daily routine.\n     iv) It makes the people addict.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39513,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','Agriculture is one of the major sectors of the Indian economy. It is present in the country for thousands of years. Over the years it has developed and the use of new technologies and equipment replaced almost all the traditional methods of farming. India largely depends on the agriculture sector. Agriculture is not just a means of livelihood but a way of living life in India. Moreover, the government is continuously making efforts to develop this sector as the whole nation depends on it for food.\nAfter independence, we used to import food grains from other countries to fulfill our demand. But, after the green revolution, we became self-sufficient and started exporting our surplus to other countries. In addition, the agricultural sector is one of the major contributors to Gross Domestic Product (GDP) and national income of the country. Also, it requires a large labour force and employees around 80% of the total employed people. The agriculture sector not only employees directly but also indirectly. Moreover, agriculture forms around 70% of our total exports. The main export items are tea, cotton, textiles, tobacco, sugar, jute products, spices, rice and many other items.','1) Answer in one word:\n    a) One of the major sectors of the Indian economy -\n    b) The sector which is continuously making efforts to develop the agricultural sector\n','2) Complete the following:\n    a) The main export items from the agricultural sector -------------\n   b) Agriculture is the only sector that contributed ---------------\n3) Arrange the following words alphabetically. \n      sector, country, method, export\n4) Name the Tense:\n     i) It requires a large labour force.\n    ii) The government is continuously making efforts to develop this sector.\n5) Do you think agriculture is important for the people who live in a city like Mumbai or Pune? Why?','','1) a) Agriculture          b) Government\n2) a) The main export items from the agricultural sector are tea, cotton, textiles, tobacco, sugar, jute products, spices, rice and many other items.\n    b) Agriculture is the only sector that contributed to the growth of not only itself but also of the other sectors of the country.\n3) country, export, method, sector\n4) i) Simple Present Tense             ii) Present Continuous Tense\n5) I think agriculture is not only important to the people living in cities like Mumbai, Pune but also at the villages. It is the main source of fulfilling our three basic needs, food, clothing and shelter. Without it no one can survive. So it is very important everywhere.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39514,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','All plants and animals need water to survive. There can be no life on earth without water. Why is water so important? Because 60 per cent of our body weight is made up of water. Our bodies use water in all the cells, organs, and tissues, to help regulate body temperature and maintain other bodily functions. Because our bodies lose water through breathing, sweating, and digestion, it\'s crucial to rehydrate and replace water by drinking fluids and eating foods that contain water. Staying hydrated is critical for maintaining a normal body temperature. \nOur bodies lose water when we sweat and in hot environments. Sweat keeps our bodies cool, but our body temperature will go up if we don\'t replenish the water we lose. Water helps to lubricate and cushion our joints, spinal cord and tissues. It helps us to be more physically active, and reduces the discomfort caused by conditions such as arthritis.','1) State whether the following statements are True or False:\n     i) Water helps us to be more physically inactive.\n    ii) We need water to survive.\n    iii) Without water there would be life on the earth.\n    iv) By drinking fluids and eating foods we can avoid dehydration.\n','2) State the uses of Water. \n3) Find out opposite words from the passage for the following:\n     i. inactive                 ii. abnormal \n     iii. irregular              iv. disuse \n4) a) There can be no life on earth without water. (Make it affirmative)\n    b) Water helps to lubricate and cushion our joints. (Identify the tense)\n5) Why should we use water carefully?','','1) i) False           ii) True            iii) False            iv) True\n2) Uses of Water:\n     i) All plants and animals need water to survive.\n     ii) We need water to regulate all the cells, organs and tissues in our body.\n     iii) Water maintains a normal body temperature.\n     iv) Water helps to lubricate and cushion our joints, spinal cord and tissues.\n3) i) active          ii) normal          iii) regular           iv) use\n4) a) Earth can be lifeless without water.\n    b) Simple Present Tense\n5) We require water for different purposes. Without it we cannot survive. Conservation of water minimizes the effects of drought and water shortages. It helps with reducing greenhouse gas emissions. So it is our duty to use water carefully and save water for future.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39515,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Describe your own world in 10 sentences in front of the whole class. ------- 5M\n   I am a girl/boy. My name is ----------. I am ----------- years old. I am in standard VII. My father’s name is -------------. He is a ------------ by occupation. My mother’s name is ----------. She is a housewife. I have ---------- sisters. I have a brother. I love my family. My mother makes very tasty food for me. my mother and father take care of me. They love me very much.\n      My school name is ----------. My favourite subject is ----------. I have many friends. My best friend is --------. I like to play with my friends. I like my school and teachers also.\nB] Add an appropriate word or suffix to the following words. --------- 3M\n     i. sun            ii. moon           iii. friend          iv. hope\nC] Copy the sentences : ------------- 2M\n     a) They paid no attention to the old woman.\n     b) They come closer to each other.','','','A] I am a girl/boy. My name is Tushar. I am 14 years old. I am in standard VII. My father’s name is Vitthal. He is a teacher by occupation. My mother’s name is Radhika. She is a housewife. I have one sisters. I have a brother. I love my family. My mother makes very tasty food for me. my mother and father take care of me. They love me very much.\n      My school name is New English School. My favourite subject is English. I have many friends. My best friend is Amol. I like to play with my friends. I like my school and teachers also.\nB] i) sunset, sunbeam            ii) moonlight, moonbeam\n       iii) friendship              iv) hopeful, hopeless\nC] a) They paid no attention to the old woman.\n     b) They come closer to each other.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39516,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Fill in the blanks : ---------------- 5M','B] Classify the following words into parts of speech. ------------ 5M\n     [under, beautiful, river, Alas!, play, and, fast, day, of, or, he, slowly, nice, they, oh!, eat]\n     a) Noun : -----------------             b) Pronoun : ---------------------------\n    c)  Adjective : --------------           d) verb : ----------------------------\n    e) Adverb : ---------------              f) Preposition : -------------------\n    g) Conjunction : ---------------     h) Interjection : --------------------','','A] i) I am watching my face in my mirror.\n    ii) We are watching our faces in our mirror.\n    iii) You are watching your face in your mirror.\n    iv) He is watching his face in his mirror.\n    v) She is watching her face in her mirror.\n    vi) It is watching its face in its mirror.\n     vii) They are watching their faces in their mirror.\nB] a) Noun : river, day                          b) Pronoun : he, they\n    c)  Adjective : beautiful, nice           d) verb : play, eat\n    e) Adverb : fast, slowly                      f) Preposition : under, of\n    g) Conjunction : and, or                    h) Interjection : Alas!, oh!','',1,0,0,NULL),(39517,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Correct the following sentences ----------------- 3M\n     i. I is a parrot                            ii. My teacher are very nice.\n     iii. I like milks                            iv. you doesn’t study hard\n     v. They red apple eat              vi. You is a boy.\nB] Write any four words that end with (s/es). ------------- 2M\nC] Write any four words that end with ‘-ing’. --------------- 2M\nD] Write any four words that end with ‘-ed’. ------------------2M','','','A] i) I am a parrot                   ii) My teacher is very nice\n    iii) I like milk                        iv) You don’t study hard.\n    v) They ate a red apple      vi) You are a boy.\nB] notebooks, trees, boys, houses, shoes\nC] beginning, caring, loving, joking, riding\nD] walked, stopped, talked, offered, helped','',0,0,0,NULL),(39518,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Frame meaningful sentences using the following adverbs ----------- 4M\n     i. always                ii. regularly              iii. sometimes           iv. never\nB] Answer the following questions ------------ 4M\n     i. List uncountable nouns\n     ii. List the units that we use to measure the following.\n         a) water              b) milk            c) distance           d) weight\nC] Write the past Tense of given verbs. ------------ 2M\n      a) dress               b) start          c) want           d) walk','','','A] i) he is always with me             ii) I regularly go to bed at ten.\n    iii) I sometimes watch television\n    iv) I never tell lies.\nB] i) hair, water, sky, fun, fire\n    ii) a) liter           b) liter         c) kilometer        d) kilogram\nC] a) dressed         b) started        c) wanted       d) walked','',0,0,0,NULL),(39519,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Identify the Tense of the following examples ----------- 4M\n     i. We didn’t mind it              ii. we are all friends\n    iii. This will not do                 iv. We liked our class.\nB] Add more words like given example ------------ 2M\n    Example : sudden – suddenly, real – really \nC] Tell the names of our sensory organs. discuss about their work. -------- 2M\nD] Write the past Tense of given verbs ------------- 2M\n     i. jump             ii. pass            iii. grasp            iv. pick','','','A] i) Past Tense                 ii) Present Tense           \n     iii) Future Tense          iv) Past tense\nB] slow – slowly, quiet – quietly, happy – happily, tender – tenderly, active – actively, honest – honestly\nC] Nose – smell, Eyes – see, Ears – hear, Tongue – taste, Skin – touch \nD] i) jumped           ii) passed          iii) grasped          iv) picked','',0,0,0,NULL),(39520,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Write the names of your classmates and add any one adjectives before the name. ------------------ 3M\n      Example : Radha – Smart Radha ; Vijay – Clever Vijay \nB] Which materials are included in the magazines? ------------ 3M\n      Examples : stories, recipes, ……\nC] Turn the following commands/orders into negative ---------- 2M\n      i. Mix the ingredients            ii. Grind them in a mixer.\nD] Change the following sentences into positive ones ----------- 2M\n      i. I do not like that music at my dinner.\n      ii. The other did not know what to do.','','','A] i) Deepak – Naughty Deepak      ii) Pinky – Sensitive Pinky \n     iii) Meera – Sincere Meera         iv) Raju – Honest Raju \n     v) Geeta – Beautiful Geeta          vi) Chintu – Intelligent Chintu \nB] poems, interviews, word puzzles, picture puzzles, riddles, news items, plays, craft ideas, jokes, picture stories, photographs, board games, quizzes, tips on how to study\nC] i) Don’t mix the ingredients.            ii) Don’t grind them in a mixer.\nD] i) I like that music at my dinner.\n     ii) The other knew what to do.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39521,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Read the word picture of a bicycle carefully. List the words from the diagram. -------------- 5M','B] Divide the sentence into subject and predicate --------------- 2M\n     i. Great scientific minds are restless with questions.\n     ii. They go home in the evening.\nC] Find out the subjects and objects in the following sentences ----------- 3M\n     i. The hare ran fast           ii. We speak English.\n     iii. Please help me.','','A] 1) Top tube           2) Down tube           3) Hand tube         4) Stem Handlebars\n     5) Seat post         6) Saddle                    7) Chainstay           8) Chain ring\n     9) Spoke              10) Pedal                    11) Derailleur         12) Brake\n    13) Tyre                14) Brake lever          15) Shifter               16) Free wheel\nB] i) Subject - Great scientific minds ; Predicate – are restless with questions.\n     ii) Subject – They ; Predicate – go home in the evening.\nC] i) Subject – The hare\n     ii) Subject – We ; Object – English \n     iii) Object – me ','',1,0,0,NULL),(39522,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Spot the subjects and objects in the following sentences ----------- 4M\n     i. They search for our holes.\n     ii. They will spend huge amount.\n     iii. They kill us.\n     iv. They hold meetings.\nB] Find the words ending with the suffix ‘-less’. ------------- 2M\nC] Find out the verbs from the following sentences and decide whether they are transitive or intransitive ---------------- 2M  \n     i. He ran a race                ii. He ran fast.\nD] Add prefixes or suffixes and make new words -------------- 2M\n     i. arrange           ii. write            iii. beauty            iv. enjoy','','','A] i) Subject – They, Object – our holes \n     ii) Subject – They, Object – huge amount\n     iii) Subject – They, Object – us\n      iv) Subject – They, Object – meetings\nB] frictionless, emotionless, weariness, motionless, careless\nC] i) Transitive verb – ran      ii) Intransitive verb – ran \nD] i) rearrange             ii) rewrite          iii) beautiful          iv) enjoyment ','',0,0,0,NULL),(39523,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Read the information carefully and complete the application form for Library Membership with the help of it : --------------- 5M\nVidyut Vaibhav Vaidya who is staying at A/2 Sai Sadan, M. G. Road, Shivaji Nagar, Pune - 411 003. He is studying in Std. VII B - Roll No. 48 in Sun Grace High School. He wants to fill up the application form for Library Membership. He was born on 26-02-2012. His contact number is 759484XXXX and mail ID is vidyutv26@gmail.com.','B] Write five examples for each of the following : ----------------- 5M\n    i. vegetables          ii. animals            iii. body parts        iv. birds       v. clothes ','','A]                          Sun Grace High School\n                       Application for Library Membership\n     Full Name : Vidyut Vaibhav Vaidya   \n     Std. : VII        Div. : B                             Roll No. : 48\n     Date of Birth : 26 /02 /2012               Gender : Male\n     Address : A/2, Sai Sadan, M. G. Road, Shivaji Nagar, Pune – 411 003.\n     Phone No. 759484xxxxx           E-mail Id : vidyutv26@gmail.com\n     I have read the rules and regulations carefully and I will follow them.\n      Date :  20 /06/2024                                        Signature : -----------------\nB] i) brinjal, cabbage, cauliflower, onion, potato\n     ii) cat, dog, goat, horse, lion\n     iii) brain, heart, stomach, hand, leg\n     iv) crow, duck, eagle, hen, pigeon\n      v) shirt, pants, frock, sari, trousers ','',1,0,0,NULL),(39524,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Read the menu card and complete the following sentences : ----------- 5M','1) A tool which contains information about a list of food is called ----------\n     2) It is the Menu Card of -------- Restaurant.\n     3) It includes only ----------, ------------, --------------, -------------, ------------, and ---------.\n     4) The cost of Veg Biryani is ₹ ---------.\n     5) The Menu Card contains veg and ---------- food items.\n     6) Beverages are sold as per ------------ .\nB] Underline the material nouns : ----------------- 3M\n     Man, hen, plastic, gold, son, oil, Manini, hand, milk, spoon, liquid\nC] Spot the error and rewrite the corrected sentences --------- 2M\n      The more powerful among the three disciples in Sun Wukong.','','A] 1) A tool which contains information about a list of food is called Menu Card.\n     2) It is the Menu Card of Paradise Restaurant.\n     3) It includes only Biryanis, Starters, Kebabs, Indian Breads, Desserts and Beverages.\n     4) The cost of Veg Biryani is ₹ 154/-.\n     5) The Menu Card contains veg and non-veg food items.\n     6) Beverages are sold as per MRP.\nB] plastic, gold, oil, milk, liquid\nC] The most powerful among the three disciples is Sun Wukong.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39525,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Read the following information and complete the Bio-data. ---------- 5M\n     Imagine you are Miss Sayli Anil Sarnobat, born on 5th December 2003.\n     You have completed your B.Com from Mumbai University and also completed Diploma in Taxation. You are staying at A/2, Samarth Niwas, P. J. N. Road, Mulund (West), Mumbai - 400 080. You are a fresher and want to apply for the post of Assistant Accountant. Your contact number is 9876XXXX55.','B] Pick out the adverbs from the following ----------- 3M\n     i. They were not attending school regularly.\n     ii. Suddenly, her eyes filled with tears.\n     iii. She was really impressed.\nC] Spot the error and rewrite the corrected sentences --------- 2M\n     Sun Wukong’s body is as stronger as diamond.','','A] Post : Assistant Account \nDate : 26/10/2024\nFull Name : Sayali Anil Sarnobat\nDate of Birth 05/12/2003\nAddress for correspondence : A/2, Samarth Niwas, P. J. N. Road, Mulund (W), Mumbai – 400 080\nEducational Qualification : i) B. Com – Mumbai University\n                                                ii) Diploma in Taxation\nContact No. : 9876XXXX55\n\nB] i) regularly            ii) Suddenly           iii) really \nC] Sun Wukong’s body is as strong as diamond.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39526,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Observe the following picture carefully. Complete its description by filling in the blanks. Use the correct words from the brackets. Give a suitable title to your write up : --------------------------- 5M\n[school, spacious, premises, Vikas Vidyalaya, indicates, entering, parents, buses, playing]\n','                       --------------------------------------\n     1) It is the picture of a -----------.\n     2) The name of the school is ------------------.\n     3) The scene ----------  that the school is not yet started.\n     4) Some children are ---------- on the grass.\n     5) Some children are getting down from the -------------.\n     6) Some ---------- are there to drop the children in the school.\n     7) Some children are ---------- the school.\n     8) The ---------- of the school is very clean and beautiful.\n     9) It is big and ------------ too.\nB] Pick out the adverbs from the following sentences : ----------- 3M\n     i. Every one of us began to try hard, honestly.\n     ii. She congratulated each one of us, personally. \n     iii. You must always maintain unity.\nC] Spot the error and rewrite the corrected sentences --------- 2M\n     These children are wise than you.','','A]  IN THE SCHOOL COMPOUND\n     1) It is the picture of a school.\n     2) The name of the school is Vikas Vidyalaya.\n     3) The scene indicates that the school is not yet started.\n     4) Some children are playing on the grass.\n     5) Some children are getting down from the buses.\n     6) Some parents are there to drop the children in the school.\n     7) Some children are entering the school.\n     8) The premises of the school is very clean and beautiful.\n     9) It is big and spacious too.\nB] i) hard, honestly           ii) personally          iii) always \nC] These children are wiser than you.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39527,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Observe the following picture carefully. Complete its description by filling in the blanks. Use the correct words from the brackets. Give a suitable title to your write up : --------------------------- 5M\n[celebrate, Holi, festival, very much, praying, evil, bonfire, coconuts]\n','                       ----------------------------------------------\nThe picture shows the scene of --------. It is a popular Hindu ---------. People are gathered around a huge ---------. This ritual is symbolic of victory of good over -------. People --------- this festival with joy and enthusiasm. Some women and children are ----------. Some men are offering -------- to the bonfire (Holi). I like this festival --------------.\nB] Underline the pronouns in the following sentences ---------- 3M\n     i. So they have thrown them out of heaven.\n     ii. We were used to teachers shouting at us for our poor marks.\n     iii. They are wiser than you. \nC] Spot the error and rewrite the corrected sentences --------- 2M\n     It can grow more big than a pillar supporting the sky.','','A] HOLI - THE FESTIVAL OF COLOURS\nThe picture shows the scene of Holi. It is a popular Hindu festival. People are gathered around a huge bonfire. This ritual is symbolic of victory of good over evil. People celebrate the festival with joy and enthusiasm. Some women and children are praying. Some men are offering coconuts to the bonfire (Holi). I like this festival very much. \nB] i) they, them           ii) it            iii) They\nC] It can grow bigger than a pillar supporting the sky.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39528,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Observe the following picture carefully. Complete its description by filling in the blanks. Use the correct words from the brackets. Give a suitable title to your write up : --------------------------- 5M\n[paper lantern, Diwali, Lights, wearing, lighting, mother, festival, family]','------------------------------------\nA happy ------- is seen in this picture. They are celebrating the festival of -------- together. It is called the festival of ---------. The -------- is carrying diyas. She is -------- diyas outside their home. The family members are ---------- new clothes. A beautiful ----------- is hanged out of their house. I like this ------- very much.\nB] Write opposite words of : --------------------- 3M\n     i. condemn             ii. humble            iii. just\nC] Spot the error and rewrite the corrected sentences --------- 2M\n     She is the more intelligent girl in the whole class.','','A] DIWALI - FESTIVAL OF LIGHTS\nA happy family is seen in this picture. They are celebrating the festival of Diwali together. It is called the festival of Lights. The mother is carrying diyas. She is lighting diyas outside their home. The family members are wearing new clothes. A beautiful paper lantern is hanged out of their house. I like this festival very much.\nB] i) praise            ii) proud           iii) unjust\nC] She is the most intelligent girl in the whole class.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39529,586,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Observe the following picture carefully. Complete its description by filling in the blanks. Use the correct words from the brackets. Give a suitable title to your write up : --------------------------- 5M\n[silence, observing, Microscope, chemicals, reactions, heating, experiments, laboratory, equipment’s]\n','-------------------------------------------\nIt is the picture of a school ---------. Students are conducting --------- in the laboratory. There are a number of -------- on the table. The girl is --------- something on the burning candle. The boy is watching chemical -------- in the beaker. There are some --------- in the beakers, flask and test tubes. The --------- is lying on the table. They are --------- reactions very carefully. There is a pin drop ------------ in the laboratory.\nB] Write the opposite words of : ------------------- 3M\n     i. dry                ii. kind                iii. large\nC] Spot the error and rewrite the corrected sentences --------- 2M\n     Better beans and bread in peace as cakes and jellies in fear.','','A] IN THE LABORATORY\nIt is the picture of a school laboratory. Students are conducting experiments in the laboratory. There are a number of equipments on the table. The girl is heating something on the burning candle. The boy is watching chemical reactions in the beaker. There are some chemicals in the beakers, flask and test tubes. The microscope is lying on the table. They are observing reactions very carefully. There is a pin drop silence in the laboratory.\nB] i) wet          ii) unkind/cruel           iii) small\nC] Better beans and bread in peace than cakes and jellies.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39530,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the following passage and do the activities :\n      Social networking implies the use of internet programs to make connections with friends, family, classmates, customers and clients. Social networking can occur for social or business purposes through sites such as Facebook, Instagram, Twitter, LinkedIn, etc. The biggest advantage of using social networks is that you can stay in touch with your friends and family from all around the world. These social networks can be used to improve our social awareness. Students can explore topics that they are interested in by using online social networking. This can be done by interacting with people from different parts of the world. Teachers, students and professionals can also create discussion forums, or write blogs and posts to explore different and wide-ranging topics. It is online platform where people meet and share ideas and experiences. This can create opportunities for relationship-building, brand-building, publicity and promotions. As people spend more time on social networking sites, they experience less face-to-face interaction which also makes them more dependent on devices. Fifty per cent of people between the age of 25 and 35 years admitted that they are so attached to social networks that they even use them during working hours.\n1) Complete the following web :','\n    --------------------------  -------------------------------------\n\n    ---------------------------   -------------------------------------\n2) Advantages of Social Networking Sites :\n    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Find out similar words from the passage for the following:\n\n     a) benefit  = ----------                            b) enhance  = ----------------\n\n     c) chance = -----------                           d) communication = ---------------\n4) Do as directed:\n    i) They use them during working hours. (Name the Tense)\n    \n        --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    ii) It is online platform where people share their ideas and experiences.\n            (Use not only ... but also ...)\n\n           -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) Do you really think using social media is a waste of time?\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','1) Facebook, Instagram, Linkedin, Twitter\n2) a) We can stay in touch with our friends and family from all around the world.\n     b) It improves our social awareness.\n     c) We can find out information on different topics.\n     d) We can meet different people and share our ideas and experiences with them. \n3) a) advantage                             b) improve\n     c) opportunity                          d) interaction\n4) i) Simple Present Tense\n    ii) It is online platform where people not only share their ideas but also experiences.\n5) I don\'t think using social media is a waste of time because it totally depends on us whether to use it for our benefit or just to waste time. If we use it to surf information we need, communicate people to know something, it is going to be more beneficial. But if we use it for playing games and doing a mere timepass for hours and hours, it is going to waste lot of our time. So it totally depends on us how to use it.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39531,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the following passage and do the activities.\nGlobal warming is the term used to describe a gradual increase in the average temperature of the Earth\'s atmosphere and its oceans. This causes a change in the Earth\'s climate. Global warming occurs when carbon dioxide (CO2) and other air pollutants and greenhouse gasses collect in the atmosphere and absorb sunlight and solar radiation that have bounced off the Earth\'s surface. Normally, this radiation would escape into space. But these pollutants, which can last for years even up to centuries in the atmosphere, trap the heat and make the planet warmer. This is known as the greenhouse effect. Climatologists agree that the average temperature of the earth has risen between 0.4 and 0.8°C over the past 100 years. They feel that in the past 50 years, the average global temperature has increased at the fastest rate in recorded history. This is chiefly because the increased volumes of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases released by the burning of fossil fuels, land clearing, agriculture and other human activities have been the chief causes of the global warming that has occurred over the decade. Global warming has many environmental, economic, and health consequences. It will be manifested in the melting of the polar ice caps, as well as an increase in the occurrence of storms.\n1) State whether you Agree or Disagree with the following statements :\n    a) The average temperature of the earth has risen between 0.4 and 0.8°C over the past 100 years. -----------\n\n    b) In the last 50 years the average global temperature has increased at the fastest rate. ---------------\n\n    c) Global warming is good for human being. -----------\n\n   d) Solar radiations last for 5-10 years in the atmosphere. --------------\n2) Describe Global Warming.\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n3) Give one word for the following description from the passage:\n    a) The thin layer of air that surrounds the earth.\n  \n         -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    b) Substance released into the environment due to natural or human activity which adversely affects the environment.\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) Do as directed:\n    a) It will be manifested in the melting of the polar ice caps, as well as an increase in the occurrence of storms. \n            (Use not only... but also ...)\n       \n         -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n     b) Rising sea level could lead to coastal flooding. \n           (Frame a wh-question to get the underlined part as an answer)\n\n           -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) What will you do to protect our environment?\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','1) a) agree           b) agree           c) disagree          d) disagree\n2) A gradual increase in the average temperature of the Earth\'s atmosphere due to a change in the Earth\'s Climate is known as Global Warming. It occurs when carbon dioxide and other air pollutants and other greenhouse gases collect in the atmosphere and absorb sunlight. It takes place because of the increased volumes of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases released by the burning of fossil fuels, land clearing, agriculture and other human activities.\n3) a) atmosphere            b) pollutants\n4) a) It will be manifested not only in the melting of the polar ice caps but also an increase in the occurrence variety of storms.\n     b) What could lead to coastal flooding?\n5) I will do the following things to protect our environment,\n     a) I will try to plant more and more trees in our surroundings and at my village with the help of my friends and parents.\n     b) I will try my level best to convey the people to avoid use of plastic, throwing garbage anywhere and manage dry and wet garbage properly.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39532,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the following passage and do the activities :\nMost of us nowadays carry the world in our pocket! It is amazing but true. It is a mobile phone that connects us to the rest of the world within a second. Apart from making calls and sending SMS, the mobile phone is used as a multipurpose gadget. It is a calculator, timepiece, calendar, voice recorder, media player, camera, gaming device, net browser and what not. Its development brought convenience and advantages to the world.\nCommunication between people has become quite easy and very fast. We can keep in contact with others from any place on the bus, in a street or in a meeting by sending a message for less than the price of a call. The radiations of mobile may be dangerous to health and may cause a headache, earache and blurring vision. These invisible radiations destroy the cells located in ear and head which cause damage to the brain and neurons in the head region. It\'s use in certain places causes disturbance sometimes. Mobile phones with camera are causing privacy problems such as using it as a hidden camera to take pictures and making videos.\n1) Fill in the blanks and complete the following sentences:\n\n    a) ----------- in mobile phones causes privacy problem.\n\n   b) ------------- of mobile may be dangerous to health.\n2) Write two advantages of using mobiles.\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Write two present participles and two past participles from the passage.\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) Do as directed\n    a) It\'s development brought convenience and advantages to the world. \n           (Use \'As well as\')\n\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   b) It is amazing. (Make it exclamatory)\n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) Write two disadvantages of using mobile.\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','1) a) Camera in mobile phones causes privacy problem.\n     b) The radiations of mobile may be dangerous to health.\n2) Advantages of using mobiles:\n    i) It is used to make calls and send messages.\n    ii) It is used as a calculator, calendar, voice recorder, media player, camera and a gaming device.\n3) i) Present Participles - Amazing, making, sending, gaming, blurring, meeting.\n    ii) Past Participle Connected, brought.\n4) a) It\'s development brought convenience as well as advantages to the world.\n    b) How amazing it is!\n5) Disadvantages of using mobiles:\n     i) It takes away our valuable time if it is not used properly.\n    ii) It affects our eyes, ears and neck.\n    iii) It disturbs our daily routine.\n     iv) It makes the people addict.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39533,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the following passage and do the activities : \nAgriculture is one of the major sectors of the Indian economy. It is present in the country for thousands of years. Over the years it has developed and the use of new technologies and equipment replaced almost all the traditional methods of farming. India largely depends on the agriculture sector. Agriculture is not just a means of livelihood but a way of living life in India. Moreover, the government is continuously making efforts to develop this sector as the whole nation depends on it for food.\nAfter independence, we used to import food grains from other countries to fulfill our demand. But, after the green revolution, we became self-sufficient and started exporting our surplus to other countries. In addition, the agricultural sector is one of the major contributors to Gross Domestic Product (GDP) and national income of the country. Also, it requires a large labour force and employees around 80% of the total employed people. The agriculture sector not only employees directly but also indirectly. Moreover, agriculture forms around 70% of our total exports. The main export items are tea, cotton, textiles, tobacco, sugar, jute products, spices, rice and many other items.\n1) Answer in one word:\n    a) One of the major sectors of the Indian economy –\n\n         -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    b) The sector which is continuously making efforts to develop the agricultural sector\n\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) Complete the following:\n    a) The main export items from the agricultural sector -------------\n\n   b) Agriculture is the only sector that contributed ---------------\n3) Arrange the following words alphabetically. \n      sector, country, method, export\n \n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) Name the Tense:\n     i) It requires a large labour force.\n\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    ii) The government is continuously making efforts to develop this sector.\n\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) Do you think agriculture is important for the people who live in a city like Mumbai or Pune? Why?\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','1) a) Agriculture          b) Government\n2) a) The main export items from the agricultural sector are tea, cotton, textiles, tobacco, sugar, jute products, spices, rice and many other items.\n    b) Agriculture is the only sector that contributed to the growth of not only itself but also of the other sectors of the country.\n3) country, export, method, sector\n4) i) Simple Present Tense             ii) Present Continuous Tense\n5) I think agriculture is not only important to the people living in cities like Mumbai, Pune but also at the villages. It is the main source of fulfilling our three basic needs, food, clothing and shelter. Without it no one can survive. So it is very important everywhere.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39534,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the following passage and do the activities :\nAll plants and animals need water to survive. There can be no life on earth without water. Why is water so important? Because 60 per cent of our body weight is made up of water. Our bodies use water in all the cells, organs, and tissues, to help regulate body temperature and maintain other bodily functions. Because our bodies lose water through breathing, sweating, and digestion, it\'s crucial to rehydrate and replace water by drinking fluids and eating foods that contain water. Staying hydrated is critical for maintaining a normal body temperature. \nOur bodies lose water when we sweat and in hot environments. Sweat keeps our bodies cool, but our body temperature will go up if we don\'t replenish the water we lose. Water helps to lubricate and cushion our joints, spinal cord and tissues. It helps us to be more physically active, and reduces the discomfort caused by conditions such as arthritis.\n1) State whether the following statements are True or False:\n     i) Water helps us to be more physically inactive. ----------\n\n    ii) We need water to survive. -------------------------\n\n    iii) Without water there would be life on the earth. ----------------\n\n    iv) By drinking fluids and eating foods we can avoid dehydration. -------------\n2) State the uses of Water. \n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Find out opposite words from the passage for the following:\n     i. inactive × --------                ii. abnormal × -------------\n     iii. irregular × -------              iv. disuse × --------------\n4) a) There can be no life on earth without water. (Make it affirmative)\n\n         -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    b) Water helps to lubricate and cushion our joints. (Identify the tense)\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) Why should we use water carefully?\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','1) i) False           ii) True            iii) False            iv) True\n2) Uses of Water:\n     i) All plants and animals need water to survive.\n     ii) We need water to regulate all the cells, organs and tissues in our body.\n     iii) Water maintains a normal body temperature.\n     iv) Water helps to lubricate and cushion our joints, spinal cord and tissues.\n3) i) active          ii) normal          iii) regular           iv) use\n4) a) Earth can be lifeless without water.\n    b) Simple Present Tense\n5) We require water for different purposes. Without it we cannot survive. Conservation of water minimizes the effects of drought and water shortages. It helps with reducing greenhouse gas emissions. So it is our duty to use water carefully and save water for future.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39535,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Describe your own world in 10 sentences in front of the whole class. ------- 5M\n    \n     I am a girl/boy. My name is ----------. I am ----------- years old. I am in standard VII. My father’s name is -------------. He is a ------------ by occupation. My mother’s name is ----------. She is a housewife. I have ---------- sisters. I have a brother. I love my family. My mother makes very tasty food for me. my mother and father take care of me. They love me very much.\n      My school name is ----------. My favourite subject is ----------. I have many friends. My best friend is --------. I like to play with my friends. I like my school and teachers also.\nB] Add an appropriate word or suffix to the following words. --------- 3M\n     i. sun            ii. moon           iii. friend          iv. hope\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nC] Copy the sentences : ------------- 2M\n     a) They paid no attention to the old woman.\n  \n         -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n     b) They come closer to each other.\n\n         -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','A] I am a girl/boy. My name is Tushar. I am 14 years old. I am in standard VII. My father’s name is Vitthal. He is a teacher by occupation. My mother’s name is Radhika. She is a housewife. I have one sisters. I have a brother. I love my family. My mother makes very tasty food for me. my mother and father take care of me. They love me very much.\n      My school name is New English School. My favourite subject is English. I have many friends. My best friend is Amol. I like to play with my friends. I like my school and teachers also.\nB] i) sunset, sunbeam            ii) moonlight, moonbeam\n       iii) friendship              iv) hopeful, hopeless\nC] a) They paid no attention to the old woman.\n     b) They come closer to each other.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39536,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Fill in the blanks : ---------------- 5M','B] Classify the following words into parts of speech. ------------ 5M\n     [under, beautiful, river, Alas!, play, and, fast, day, of, or, he, slowly, nice, they, oh!, eat]\n     a) Noun : -----------------             b) Pronoun : ---------------------------\n\n    c)  Adjective : --------------           d) verb : ----------------------------\n\n    e) Adverb : ---------------              f) Preposition : -------------------\n\n    g) Conjunction : ---------------     h) Interjection : --------------------','','A] i) I am watching my face in my mirror.\n    ii) We are watching our faces in our mirror.\n    iii) You are watching your face in your mirror.\n    iv) He is watching his face in his mirror.\n    v) She is watching her face in her mirror.\n    vi) It is watching its face in its mirror.\n     vii) They are watching their faces in their mirror.\nB] a) Noun : river, day                          b) Pronoun : he, they\n    c)  Adjective : beautiful, nice           d) verb : play, eat\n    e) Adverb : fast, slowly                      f) Preposition : under, of\n    g) Conjunction : and, or                    h) Interjection : Alas!, oh!','',1,0,0,NULL),(39537,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Correct the following sentences ----------------- 3M\n     i. I is a parrot                            ii. My teacher are very nice.\n     iii. I like milks                            iv. you doesn’t study hard\n     v. They red apple eat              vi. You is a boy.\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nB] Write any four words that end with (s/es). ------------- 2M\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nC] Write any four words that end with ‘-ing’. --------------- 2M\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nD] Write any four words that end with ‘-ed’. ------------------2M\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','A] i) I am a parrot                   ii) My teacher is very nice\n    iii) I like milk                        iv) You don’t study hard.\n    v) They ate a red apple      vi) You are a boy.\nB] notebooks, trees, boys, houses, shoes\nC] beginning, caring, loving, joking, riding\nD] walked, stopped, talked, offered, helped','',0,0,0,NULL),(39538,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Frame meaningful sentences using the following adverbs ----------- 4M\n     i. always                ii. regularly              iii. sometimes           iv. never\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nB] Answer the following questions ------------ 4M\n     i. List uncountable nouns\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n     ii. List the units that we use to measure the following.\n         a) water              b) milk            c) distance           d) weight\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nC] Write the past Tense of given verbs. ------------ 2M\n      a) dress               b) start          c) want           d) walk\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','A] i) he is always with me             ii) I regularly go to bed at ten.\n    iii) I sometimes watch television\n    iv) I never tell lies.\nB] i) hair, water, sky, fun, fire\n    ii) a) liter           b) liter         c) kilometer        d) kilogram\nC] a) dressed         b) started        c) wanted       d) walked','',0,0,0,NULL),(39539,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Identify the Tense of the following examples ----------- 4M\n     i. We didn’t mind it              ii. we are all friends\n    iii. This will not do                 iv. We liked our class.\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nB] Add more words like given example ------------ 2M\n    Example : sudden – suddenly, real – really \n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nC] Tell the names of our sensory organs. discuss about their work. -------- 2M\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nD] Write the past Tense of given verbs ------------- 2M\n     i. jump             ii. pass            iii. grasp            iv. pick\n\n     ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- \n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','A] i) Past Tense                 ii) Present Tense           \n     iii) Future Tense          iv) Past tense\nB] slow – slowly, quiet – quietly, happy – happily, tender – tenderly, active – actively, honest – honestly\nC] Nose – smell, Eyes – see, Ears – hear, Tongue – taste, Skin – touch \nD] i) jumped           ii) passed          iii) grasped          iv) picked','',0,0,0,NULL),(39540,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Write the names of your classmates and add any one adjectives before the name. ------------------ 3M\n      Example : Radha – Smart Radha ; Vijay – Clever Vijay \n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nB] Which materials are included in the magazines? ------------ 3M\n      Examples : stories, recipes, ……\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nC] Turn the following commands/orders into negative ---------- 2M\n      i. Mix the ingredients            ii. Grind them in a mixer.\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nD] Change the following sentences into positive ones ----------- 2M\n      i. I do not like that music at my dinner.\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n      ii. The other did not know what to do.\n\n           -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','A] i) Deepak – Naughty Deepak      ii) Pinky – Sensitive Pinky \n     iii) Meera – Sincere Meera         iv) Raju – Honest Raju \n     v) Geeta – Beautiful Geeta          vi) Chintu – Intelligent Chintu \nB] poems, interviews, word puzzles, picture puzzles, riddles, news items, plays, craft ideas, jokes, picture stories, photographs, board games, quizzes, tips on how to study\nC] i) Don’t mix the ingredients.            ii) Don’t grind them in a mixer.\nD] i) I like that music at my dinner.\n     ii) The other knew what to do.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39541,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Read the word picture of a bicycle carefully. List the words from the diagram. -------------- 5M\n','\n      -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nB] Divide the sentence into subject and predicate --------------- 2M\n     i. Great scientific minds are restless with questions.\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n     ii. They go home in the evening.\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nC] Find out the subjects and objects in the following sentences ----------- 3M\n     i. The hare ran fast           ii. We speak English.\n     iii. Please help me.\n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  \n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','A] 1) Top tube           2) Down tube           3) Hand tube         4) Stem Handlebars\n     5) Seat post         6) Saddle                    7) Chainstay           8) Chain ring\n     9) Spoke              10) Pedal                    11) Derailleur         12) Brake\n    13) Tyre                14) Brake lever          15) Shifter               16) Free wheel\nB] i) Subject - Great scientific minds ; Predicate – are restless with questions.\n     ii) Subject – They ; Predicate – go home in the evening.\nC] i) Subject – The hare\n     ii) Subject – We ; Object – English \n     iii) Object – me ','',1,0,0,NULL),(39542,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Spot the subjects and objects in the following sentences ----------- 4M\n     i. They search for our holes.\n     ii. They will spend huge amount.\n     iii. They kill us.\n     iv. They hold meetings.\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nB] Find the words ending with the suffix ‘-less’. ------------- 2M\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nC] Find out the verbs from the following sentences and decide whether they are transitive or intransitive ---------------- 2M  \n     i. He ran a race                ii. He ran fast.\n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nD] Add prefixes or suffixes and make new words -------------- 2M\n     i. arrange           ii. write            iii. beauty            iv. enjoy\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','A] i) Subject – They, Object – our holes \n     ii) Subject – They, Object – huge amount\n     iii) Subject – They, Object – us\n      iv) Subject – They, Object – meetings\nB] frictionless, emotionless, weariness, motionless, careless\nC] i) Transitive verb – ran      ii) Intransitive verb – ran \nD] i) rearrange             ii) rewrite          iii) beautiful          iv) enjoyment ','',0,0,0,NULL),(39543,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Read the information carefully and complete the application form for Library Membership with the help of it : --------------- 5M\nVidyut Vaibhav Vaidya who is staying at A/2 Sai Sadan, M. G. Road, Shivaji Nagar, Pune - 411 003. He is studying in Std. VII B - Roll No. 48 in Sun Grace High School. He wants to fill up the application form for Library Membership. He was born on 26-02-2012. His contact number is 759484XXXX and mail ID is vidyutv26@gmail.com.','B] Write five examples for each of the following : ----------------- 5M\n    i. vegetables          ii. animals            iii. body parts        iv. birds       v. clothes \n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','A]                          Sun Grace High School\n                       Application for Library Membership\n     Full Name : Vidyut Vaibhav Vaidya   \n     Std. : VII        Div. : B                             Roll No. : 48\n     Date of Birth : 26 /02 /2012               Gender : Male\n     Address : A/2, Sai Sadan, M. G. Road, Shivaji Nagar, Pune – 411 003.\n     Phone No. 759484xxxxx           E-mail Id : vidyutv26@gmail.com\n     I have read the rules and regulations carefully and I will follow them.\n      Date :  20 /06/2024                                        Signature : -----------------\nB] i) brinjal, cabbage, cauliflower, onion, potato\n     ii) cat, dog, goat, horse, lion\n     iii) brain, heart, stomach, hand, leg\n     iv) crow, duck, eagle, hen, pigeon\n      v) shirt, pants, frock, sari, trousers ','',1,0,0,NULL),(39544,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Read the menu card and complete the following sentences : ----------- 5M','\n1) A tool which contains information about a list of food is called ----------\n     2) It is the Menu Card of -------- Restaurant.\n     3) It includes only ----------, ------------, --------------, -------------, ------------, and ---------.\n     4) The cost of Veg Biryani is ₹ ---------.\n     5) The Menu Card contains veg and ---------- food items.\n     6) Beverages are sold as per ------------ .\nB] Underline the material nouns : ----------------- 3M\n     Man, hen, plastic, gold, son, oil, Manini, hand, milk, spoon, liquid\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nC] Spot the error and rewrite the corrected sentences --------- 2M\n      The more powerful among the three disciples in Sun Wukong.\n\n         -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','A] 1) A tool which contains information about a list of food is called Menu Card.\n     2) It is the Menu Card of Paradise Restaurant.\n     3) It includes only Biryanis, Starters, Kebabs, Indian Breads, Desserts and Beverages.\n     4) The cost of Veg Biryani is ₹ 154/-.\n     5) The Menu Card contains veg and non-veg food items.\n     6) Beverages are sold as per MRP.\nB] plastic, gold, oil, milk, liquid\nC] The most powerful among the three disciples is Sun Wukong.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39545,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Read the following information and complete the Bio-data. ---------- 5M\n     Imagine you are Miss Sayli Anil Sarnobat, born on 5th December 2003.\n     You have completed your B.Com from Mumbai University and also completed Diploma in Taxation. You are staying at A/2, Samarth Niwas, P. J. N. Road, Mulund (West), Mumbai - 400 080. You are a fresher and want to apply for the post of Assistant Accountant. Your contact number is 9876XXXX55.','B] Pick out the adverbs from the following ----------- 3M\n     i. They were not attending school regularly.\n     ii. Suddenly, her eyes filled with tears.\n     iii. She was really impressed.\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nC] Spot the error and rewrite the corrected sentences --------- 2M\n     Sun Wukong’s body is as stronger as diamond.\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','A] Post : Assistant Account \nDate : 26/10/2024\nFull Name : Sayali Anil Sarnobat\nDate of Birth 05/12/2003\nAddress for correspondence : A/2, Samarth Niwas, P. J. N. Road, Mulund (W), Mumbai – 400 080\nEducational Qualification : i) B. Com – Mumbai University\n                                                ii) Diploma in Taxation\nContact No. : 9876XXXX55\n\nB] i) regularly            ii) Suddenly           iii) really \nC] Sun Wukong’s body is as strong as diamond.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39546,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Observe the following picture carefully. Complete its description by filling in the blanks. Use the correct words from the brackets. Give a suitable title to your write up : --------------------------- 5M\n[school, spacious, premises, Vikas Vidyalaya, indicates, entering, parents, buses, playing]','\n--------------------------------------\n     1) It is the picture of a -----------.\n     2) The name of the school is ------------------.\n     3) The scene ----------  that the school is not yet started.\n     4) Some children are ---------- on the grass.\n     5) Some children are getting down from the -------------.\n     6) Some ---------- are there to drop the children in the school.\n     7) Some children are ---------- the school.\n     8) The ---------- of the school is very clean and beautiful.\n     9) It is big and ------------ too.\nB] Pick out the adverbs from the following sentences : ----------- 3M\n     i. Every one of us began to try hard, honestly.\n     ii. She congratulated each one of us, personally. \n     iii. You must always maintain unity.\n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nC] Spot the error and rewrite the corrected sentences --------- 2M\n     These children are wise than you.\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','A]  IN THE SCHOOL COMPOUND\n     1) It is the picture of a school.\n     2) The name of the school is Vikas Vidyalaya.\n     3) The scene indicates that the school is not yet started.\n     4) Some children are playing on the grass.\n     5) Some children are getting down from the buses.\n     6) Some parents are there to drop the children in the school.\n     7) Some children are entering the school.\n     8) The premises of the school is very clean and beautiful.\n     9) It is big and spacious too.\nB] i) hard, honestly           ii) personally          iii) always \nC] These children are wiser than you.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39547,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Observe the following picture carefully. Complete its description by filling in the blanks. Use the correct words from the brackets. Give a suitable title to your write up : --------------------------- 5M\n[celebrate, Holi, festival, very much, praying, evil, bonfire, coconuts]','\n----------------------------------------------\nThe picture shows the scene of --------. It is a popular Hindu ---------. People are gathered around a huge ---------. This ritual is symbolic of victory of good over -------. People --------- this festival with joy and enthusiasm. Some women and children are ----------. Some men are offering -------- to the bonfire (Holi). I like this festival --------------.\nB] Underline the pronouns in the following sentences ---------- 3M\n     i. So they have thrown them out of heaven.\n     ii. We were used to teachers shouting at us for our poor marks.\n     iii. They are wiser than you. \n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nC] Spot the error and rewrite the corrected sentences --------- 2M\n     It can grow more big than a pillar supporting the sky.\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','A] HOLI - THE FESTIVAL OF COLOURS\nThe picture shows the scene of Holi. It is a popular Hindu festival. People are gathered around a huge bonfire. This ritual is symbolic of victory of good over evil. People celebrate the festival with joy and enthusiasm. Some women and children are praying. Some men are offering coconuts to the bonfire (Holi). I like this festival very much. \nB] i) they, them           ii) it            iii) They\nC] It can grow bigger than a pillar supporting the sky.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39548,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Observe the following picture carefully. Complete its description by filling in the blanks. Use the correct words from the brackets. Give a suitable title to your write up : --------------------------- 5M\n[paper lantern, Diwali, Lights, wearing, lighting, mother, festival, family]\n','\n------------------------------------\nA happy ------- is seen in this picture. They are celebrating the festival of -------- together. It is called the festival of ---------. The -------- is carrying diyas. She is -------- diyas outside their home. The family members are ---------- new clothes. A beautiful ----------- is hanged out of their house. I like this ------- very much.\nB] Write opposite words of : --------------------- 3M\n\n     i. condemn  × -------            ii. humble × --------            iii. just × -----------\nC] Spot the error and rewrite the corrected sentences --------- 2M\n     She is the more intelligent girl in the whole class.\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','A] DIWALI - FESTIVAL OF LIGHTS\nA happy family is seen in this picture. They are celebrating the festival of Diwali together. It is called the festival of Lights. The mother is carrying diyas. She is lighting diyas outside their home. The family members are wearing new clothes. A beautiful paper lantern is hanged out of their house. I like this festival very much.\nB] i) praise            ii) proud           iii) unjust\nC] She is the most intelligent girl in the whole class.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39549,587,'descriptive','4',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Observe the following picture carefully. Complete its description by filling in the blanks. Use the correct words from the brackets. Give a suitable title to your write up : --------------------------- 5M\n[silence, observing, Microscope, chemicals, reactions, heating, experiments, laboratory, equipment’s]\n','\n                             -------------------------------------------\nIt is the picture of a school ---------. Students are conducting --------- in the laboratory. There are a number of -------- on the table. The girl is --------- something on the burning candle. The boy is watching chemical -------- in the beaker. There are some --------- in the beakers, flask and test tubes. The --------- is lying on the table. They are --------- reactions very carefully. There is a pin drop ------------ in the laboratory.\nB] Write the opposite words of : ------------------- 3M\n\n     i. dry × -----------   ii. kind × --------------    iii. large × ------------\nC] Spot the error and rewrite the corrected sentences --------- 2M\n     Better beans and bread in peace as cakes and jellies in fear.\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','A] IN THE LABORATORY\nIt is the picture of a school laboratory. Students are conducting experiments in the laboratory. There are a number of equipments on the table. The girl is heating something on the burning candle. The boy is watching chemical reactions in the beaker. There are some chemicals in the beakers, flask and test tubes. The microscope is lying on the table. They are observing reactions very carefully. There is a pin drop silence in the laboratory.\nB] i) wet          ii) unkind/cruel           iii) small\nC] Better beans and bread in peace than cakes and jellies.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39550,588,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a note to your friend and invite him/her on your birthday. Write the note with the help of the following words:\n[friends, birthday, little, to invite, to come, little, evening, sending, small, invited)\nDate : --------------------,\nDear ----------------------,\nI cannot come ---------- you personally. So, I am --------- this note with Raghukaka. My -------- is on 10th October. We have a -------- birthday party in the ------------- at about 7 p.m. at my home. I have ------------ only my close ---------------. I want you ----------. Please do come.\nPlease bring ------------ Pinki with you.\nYours,\nReshma.','','','Date : ---------------\nDear Sakshi,\nI cannot come to invite you personally. So, I am sending this note with Raghukaka. My birthday is on 10th October. We have a small birthday party in the evening at about 7 p.m. at my home. I have invited only my close friends. I want you to come. Please do come.\nPlease bring little Pinki with you.\nYours,\nReshma.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39551,588,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Mohan\'s mother has gone to visit his sick aunty. Mohan comes from school. He gets his mother\'s note. Write the mother\'s note with the help of the following words:\n[home, little, kitchen, return, Mohan, forget, mummy, going]\nDate : -------------------------\nDear --------------,\nI am to ---------- Radhakaku. There is upma for you in the ----------. There are bananas, too. Look after --------- Sonu. Don’t ----------- to give her milk. Stay at --------- till your father comes. I shall return at night.\nYours,\n--------------','','','Dear Mohan,\nI am going to Radhakaku. There is upma for you in the kitchen. There are bananas, too. Look after little Sonu. Don\'t forget to give her milk. Stay at home till your father comes. I shall return at night.\nYours,\nMummy.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39552,588,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','You have recently celebrated your birthday. Your uncle couldn\'t attend it. However, he sent you a nice wrist watch. Write a letter to him using the words given below:\n[Thank, nephew, birthday, useful, studies, wrist watch, come, preparing, disappointed, a lot, friends, great, over, beautiful]\nJeevandhara,\n3/304, Mangal Road,\nLatur-413 512.\n11th January, 2025.\n\nDear ----------,\nI was ---------- that you couldn’t be present here for my birthday. I missed you -----------. However, when I received the ----------, you sent with Kaki, I was thrilled. -------------- you very much. Kaka. I’ve always wanted one. Most of my --------- have watches, and now I, too, have one. Thanks to you! It will be very --------- to me.\nMy --------- went very well. All my friends had -----------. We had a --------- time. Our Unit Tests are ---------- and I am now ------------- for the annual examination. My ----------- are going on very well.\nThank you again for your ----------- gift.\nLove to all.\nYour loving, \nSumit.','','','Jeevandhara,\n3/304, Mangal Road,\nLatur-413 512.\n11th January, 2025.\nDear Suresh Kaka,\nI was disappointed that you couldn\'t be present here for my birthday. I missed you a lot. However, when I received the wrist watch, you sent with Kaki, I was thrilled. Thank you very much. Kaka. I\'ve always wanted one.\nMost of my friends have watches, and now I, too, have one. Thanks to you! It will be very useful to me.\nMy birthday went of very well. All my friends had come. We had a great time. Our Unit Tests are over and I am now preparing for the annual examination. My studies are going on very well.\nThank you again for your beautiful gift.\nLove to all.\nYour loving nephew,\nSumit.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39553,588,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','You need a mobile to attend online lectures. Write a letter to your father and ask him to buy a new mobile for the same. Promise him that you would use it very carefully. Use the following words and complete the letter:\n[mother, agreed, to conduct, use, renovation, assure, completing, Android, attend, Waiting, health, fine, lectures, everything]\nRadha Sheth,\n10, Dnyandeep,\nM. G. Road,\nJalgaon - 412 005\n15th August, 2024.\nDear ------------,\n\nOur school is undergoing some ---------- work. So, they have decided ------ classes online through Google Meet for this full month. Parents have ------- it in the parents meeting. The mobile which --------- has been using is not an android mobile so I can’t ----------- it for the same.\nSo requesting you to buy and send a new ----------- mobile so that I can attend the online lectures. I ------------------ you that I won’t misuse it at any cost and hand it over to mother after ---------- my lectures.\nHope ---------- is fine there. ----------- for the mobile before 1st of September so that I would be able to attend online ----------- from the first day. Everything is -------- here. Take care of your -------------.\nYours lovingly,\nRadha Sheth','','','Radha Sheth, \n10, Dnyandeep, \nM. G. Road, Jalgaon 412 005 \n15th August, 2024.\nDear father,\nOur school is undergoing some renovation work. So, they have decided to conduct classes online through Google Meet for this full month. Parents have agreed for it in the parents meeting. The mobile which mother has been using is not an android mobile so I can\'t use it for the same.\nSo, requesting you to buy and send a new Android mobile so that I can attend the online lectures. I assure you that I won\'t misuse it at any cost and hand it over to mother after completing my lectures.\nHope everything is fine there. Waiting for the mobile before 1st of September so that I would be able to attend online lectures from the first day. Everything is fine here. Take care of your health.\nYours lovingly,\nRadha Sheth.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39554,588,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','You have been suffering from Typhoid for the last two days and doctor has advised you to take bed rest for 4 days. You are unable to attend the school for 4-5 days. Write a letter to the class teacher by using the following words:\n[school, leave, advised, recovery, infection, obedient, assure, Thanking, Typhoid, studying, illness, needful]\nAnish Shirke, \nShivneri, A2/69, \nTulja Bhavani Nagar, \nKharadi, \nPune-411 014. \n6th July, 2024.\nTo\nThe Class teacher, \nMahatma Gandhi High School, \nKharadi,\nPune - 411 014.\nSub. : About 5 days leave.\nRespected Madam,\nI am the student of your class --------- in Standard VII A. I have been suffering from ----------- from ----------- for the last two days. Our family doctor has --------- me to take complete bed rest. It is good for speedy -----------. So I am not able to attend the ---------- from 7th July to 11Th July.\nIt will also avoid the --------- to spread to the other students in my class. So, kindly sanction me 5 days -------- so that I can take complete bed rest. I ---------- that I will complete my studies once I recover from this -----------.\nKindly do the --------------. ------------------- you in anticipation. \nYours ---------- student,\nAnish Shirke.','','','Anish Shirke, \nShivneri, A2/69, \nTulja Bhavani Nagar, \nKharadi, \nPune - 411 014. \n6th July, 2024.\nTo\nThe Class teacher, \nMahatma Gandhi High School, \nKharadi, \nPune - 411 014.\nSub. : About 5 days leave\nRespected madam,\nI am the student of your class studying in Standard VII A. I have been suffering from Typhoid for the last two days. Our family doctor has advised me to take complete bed rest. It is good for speedy recovery. So I am not able to attend the class from 7th July to 11th July.\nIt will also avoid the infection to spread to the other students in my class. So kindly sanction me 5 days leave so that I can take complete bed rest. I assure you that I will complete my studies once I recover from this illness. Kindly do the needful. Thanking you in anticipation.\nYours obedient student,\nAnish Shirke.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39555,588,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Your school library has got good number of books from one of the NGOs. The Librarian has taken a lot of efforts for it. Write a letter to him/her by using the words given in the brackets:\n[books, reader, library, student, faithfully, efforts, Recently, Librarian, guide, teachers)\n\n-----------------------,\nA/24, Swapnapurti, \nV. P. Road, \nSawantwadi, \nSindhudurg - 416 510. \n26th August 2024.\nTo\nThe ----------, \nNew English High School, \nSawantwadi, \nSindhudurg - 416 510. \nSub. Thanks for the books in the -----------\nRespected Sir,\nI am a ----------- of New English High School, studying in Standard VII (A). I am a regular ----------- of different books. You always ----------- me to read different books. ---------------- our school library has got a good store of books from one of the NGOs from Mumbai. I know you have a lion’s share to get these ----------- for the library.\nNow students and ------------ will be able to read different books on different subjects. Thanks a lot for your ---------- to get these books.\nThank you.\nYours\nPratik Dalvi.','','','Pratik Dalvi, \nA/24, Swapnapurti,\nV. P. Road, \nSawantwadi, \nSindhudurg - 416 510. \n26th August, 2024.\nTo \nThe Librarian, \nNew English High School, \nSawantwadi, \nSindhudurg - 416 510.\nSub. : Thanks for the books in the Library.\nRespected Sir,\nI am the student of New English High School, studying in Standard VII (A). I am a regular reader of different books. You always guide me to read different books. Recently our library has got a good store of books from one of the NGOs from Mumbai. I know you have a lion\'s share to get these books for the library.\nNow students and teachers will be able to read different books on different subjects. Thanks a lot for your efforts to get these books for the students. Thank you.\nYours faithfully, \nPratik Dalvi.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39556,588,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Your Friend is weak in health. Write a letter to him / her with the help of the following points.\ni. Tell him / her the importance of good health.\nii. Suggest him/her some suitable excercises.\niii. Ask him / her to have a good and balanced diet.\niv. Request him / her to consult a doctor. A','','','Shlok Kuldeep Kakade\nBhagwant Krupa, \nKrantisinhanagar, \nUplai Road, Barsi.\nMarch 02, 2021\nDear Aryan,\nI have received your letter. I am glad to read it. One thing makes me sad is that you are weak in health. That is not good.\nRemember that \'Health is Wealth\'. I suggest some rules to keep fit. Please follow them. First thing is that you don\'t eat any type of junk food. Have a good\nand balanced diet. You should go for a morning walk regularly. And if necessary you should consult a doctor and ask for tonic.\nI am happy here. Don\'t worry. Take care of your health. Convey my regards to your Pappa and Mummy. With love to all.\nYours lovingly, \nShlok.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39558,589,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a note to your friend and invite him/her on your birthday. Write the note with the help of the following words:\n[friends, birthday, little, to invite, to come, little, evening, sending, small, invited)\nDate : --------------------,\nDear ----------------------,\nI cannot come ---------- you personally. So, I am --------- this note with Raghukaka. My -------- is on 10th October. We have a -------- birthday party in the ------------- at about 7 p.m. at my home. I have ------------ only my close ---------------. I want you ----------. Please do come.\nPlease bring ------------ Pinki with you.\nYours,\nReshma.','','','Date : ---------------\nDear Sakshi,\nI cannot come to invite you personally. So, I am sending this note with Raghukaka. My birthday is on 10th October. We have a small birthday party in the evening at about 7 p.m. at my home. I have invited only my close friends. I want you to come. Please do come.\nPlease bring little Pinki with you.\nYours,\nReshma.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39559,589,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Mohan\'s mother has gone to visit his sick aunty. Mohan comes from school. He gets his mother\'s note. Write the mother\'s note with the help of the following words:\n[home, little, kitchen, return, Mohan, forget, mummy, going]\nDate : -------------------------\nDear --------------,\nI am to ---------- Radhakaku. There is upma for you in the ----------. There are bananas, too. Look after --------- Sonu. Don’t ----------- to give her milk. Stay at --------- till your father comes. I shall return at night.\nYours,\n--------------','','','Dear Mohan,\nI am going to Radhakaku. There is upma for you in the kitchen. There are bananas, too. Look after little Sonu. Don\'t forget to give her milk. Stay at home till your father comes. I shall return at night.\nYours,\nMummy.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39560,589,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','You have recently celebrated your birthday. Your uncle couldn\'t attend it. However, he sent you a nice wrist watch. Write a letter to him using the words given below:\n[Thank, nephew, birthday, useful, studies, wrist watch, come, preparing, disappointed, a lot, friends, great, over, beautiful]\nJeevandhara,\n3/304, Mangal Road,\nLatur-413 512.\n11th January, 2025.\nDear ----------,\nI was ---------- that you couldn’t be present here for my birthday. I missed you -----------. However, when I received the ----------, you sent with Kaki, I was thrilled. -------------- you very much. Kaka. I’ve always wanted one. Most of my --------- have watches, and now I, too, have one. Thanks to you! It will be very --------- to me.\nMy --------- went very well. All my friends had -----------. We had a --------- time. Our Unit Tests are ---------- and I am now ------------- for the annual examination. My ----------- are going on very well.\nThank you again for your ----------- gift.\nLove to all.\nYour loving, \nSumit.','','','Jeevandhara,\n3/304, Mangal Road,\nLatur-413 512.\n11th January, 2025.\nDear Suresh Kaka,\nI was disappointed that you couldn\'t be present here for my birthday. I missed you a lot. However, when I received the wrist watch, you sent with Kaki, I was thrilled. Thank you very much. Kaka. I\'ve always wanted one.\nMost of my friends have watches, and now I, too, have one. Thanks to you! It will be very useful to me.\nMy birthday went of very well. All my friends had come. We had a great time. Our Unit Tests are over and I am now preparing for the annual examination. My studies are going on very well.\nThank you again for your beautiful gift.\nLove to all.\nYour loving nephew,\nSumit.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39561,589,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','You need a mobile to attend online lectures. Write a letter to your father and ask him to buy a new mobile for the same. Promise him that you would use it very carefully. Use the following words and complete the letter:\n[mother, agreed, to conduct, use, renovation, assure, completing, Android, attend, Waiting, health, fine, lectures, everything]\nRadha Sheth,\n10, Dnyandeep,\nM. G. Road,\nJalgaon - 412 005\n15th August, 2024.\nDear ------------,\nOur school is undergoing some ---------- 