-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Shlok Kuldeep Kakade\nBhagwant Krupa, \nKrantisinhanagar, \nUplai Road, Barsi.\nMarch 02, 2021\nDear Aryan,\nI have received your letter. I am glad to read it. One thing makes me sad is that you are weak in health. That is not good.\nRemember that \'Health is Wealth\'. I suggest some rules to keep fit. Please follow them. First thing is that you don\'t eat any type of junk food. Have a good\nand balanced diet. You should go for a morning walk regularly. And if necessary you should consult a doctor and ask for tonic.\nI am happy here. Don\'t worry. Take care of your health. Convey my regards to your Pappa and Mummy. With love to all.\nYours lovingly, \nShlok.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39565,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the following dialogue :\nA : What is your father?\nB : -------------------------------\nA : And your mother?\nB : ----------------------------','','','A : What is your father?\nB : My father is a teacher.\nA : And your mother?\nB : She is also  a teacher.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39566,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the following dialogue :\nKuldeep : What is your hobby?\nSumit : --------------------------------\nKuldeep : What kind of books do you like read?\nSumit : ------------------------------------','','','Kuldeep : What is your hobby?\nSumit : Reading is my hobby.\nKuldeep : What kind of books do you like read?\nSumit : I like adventures stories to read.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39567,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the following dialogue :\nShlok : What is social distancing, mamma?\nAishwarya : ------------------------------------------\nShlok : But why should we keep social distance?\nAishwarya : -----------------------------------------------','','','Shlok : What is social distancing, mamma?\nAishwarya : Keeping safe distance between two.\nShlok : But why should we keep social distance?\nAishwarya : Because Covid – 19 is a highly infectious disease.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39568,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the following dialogue :\nTeacher : Rahul, how many days are there in a week?\nRahul : ----------------------------------------------------------\nTeacher : On which day our school is having a holiday every week?\nRahul : -----------------------------------------------------------','','','Teacher : Rahul, how many days are there in a week?\nRahul : There are seven days in a week.\nTeacher : On which day our school is having a holiday every week?\nRahul : On Sunday our school is having holiday every week.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39569,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the following dialogue :\nMummy : Rahul, why are you not eating the salad?\nRahul : -----------------------------------------------------------\nMummy : Raw vegetables are good for health. Besides, you must eat whatever is made in the house.\nRahul : --------------------------------------------------------------','','','Mummy : Rahul, why are you not eating the salad?\nRahul : I don’t like raw vegetables, Mummy.\nMummy : Raw vegetables are good for health. Besides, you must eat whatever is made in the house.\nRahul : Alright, Mummy. I’ll try.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39570,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the following dialogue :\nBrijesh : Can I get two tickets of Mahalaxmi express from Pune to Kolhapur?\nClerk : --------------------------------------------------------------\nClerk : When do you want to go?\nBrijesh : --------------------------------------------------------','','','Brijesh : Can I get two tickets of Mahalaxmi express from Pune to Kolhapur?\nClerk : Yes, sure. Trains are running empty nowadays.\nClerk : When do you want to go?\nBrijesh : We want to go by tomorrow. Please give me two tickets.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39571,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare the meaningful dialogue from jumbled sentences :\n     * I like to drink milk.\n     * No, I don\'t.\n    * Do you like to drink tea?\n    * What do you like to drink then?','','','* Do you like to drink tea?\n* No, I don\'t.\n* What do you like to drink then.\n* I like to drink milk.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39572,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare the meaningful dialogue from jumbled sentences :\n* We should wear mask and keep social distancing.\n* It is the result of our negligence.\n* How\'s that?\n* Corona is again spreading rapidly.','','','* Corona is again spreading rapidly.\n* It is the result of our negligence.\n* How is that?\n* We should wear masks and keep social distancing.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39573,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare the meaningful dialogue from jumbled sentences :\n* Don\'t mention it.\n* Thanks a lot.\n* With great pleasure. Please take it.\n* Will you please give me your pencil?','','','* Will you please give me your pencil?,\n* With great pleasure. Please take it.\n* Thanks a lot.\n* Don\'t mention it.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39574,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Rearrange the sentences in each set to complete a meaningful dialogue :\nAmit : Yes. Yesterday itself. It was the last date. What about you? \nSumit : Not yet. Because of my sickness.\nAmit : Oh! Better you meet the teacher and tell the reason.\nSumit : Did you submit your English assignments?','','','Sumit : Did you submit your English assignments?\nAmit : Yes. Yesterday itself. It was the last date. What about you?\nSumit : Not yet. Because of my sickness.\nAmit : Oh! Better you meet the teacher and tell the reason.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39575,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Rearrange the sentences in each set to complete a meaningful dialogue :\nPriya : I am going. Please do come. I need your company.\nRiya : Ok. I will ask my father today. If he says \'yes\', I will come.\nPriya : Are you going for school picnic?\nRiya : Not yet decided. What about you?','','','Priya : Are you going to school picnic?\nRiya : Not yet decided. What about you?\nPriya : I am going. Please do come. I need your company.\nRiya : Ok. I will ask my father today. If he says \'yes\', I will come.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39576,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Rearrange the sentences in each set to complete a meaningful dialogue :\nLibrarian : Did you submit the book you have taken last time?\nSamir : No, Madam. I will submit both the books together.\nLibrarian : No. First submit the book you have taken. Then you will get another book.\nSamir : May I get a new book Madam?','','','Samir : May I get a new book Madam?\nLibrarian : Did you submit the book you have taken last time?\nSamir : No, Madam. I will submit both the books together.\nLibrarian : No. First submit the book you have taken. Then you will get another.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39577,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Rearrange the sentences in each set to complete a meaningful dialogue :\nPassenger : Thanks a lot, my dear boy.\nRishi : Mention not Madam. I am getting down at next stop.\nPassenger : It\'s a ladies seat. Can you get up please?\nRishi : Sure Madam. You can sit here.','','','Passenger : It\'s a ladies seat. Can you get up please?\nRishi : Sure Madam. You can sit here.\nPassenger: Thanks a lot my dear boy.\nRishi : Mention not madam. I am getting down at next stop.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39578,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Rearrange the sentences in each set to complete a meaningful dialogue :\nStranger: Yes. You will be in front of Z.P. office.\nYou : Is it nearby once I take the first right?\nStranger : Yes, it\'s quiet easy. Just go straight and take first right.\nYou : Excuse me, may I know how to reach Z.P office?','','','You : Excuse me! May I know how to reach Z.P office?\nStranger : Yes, it\'s quiet easy. Just go straight and take first right.\nYou : Is it nearby once I take the first right?\nStranger : Yes. You will be in front of Z.P. office.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39579,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare a dialogue each from the jumbled sentences :\nAsking for postal address :\n: Is it so? Then please give your new postal address.\n: Thank you!\n: Sure! Here it is.\n: Do you know, I have changed my residence.','','','A : Do you know. I have changed my residence.\nB : Is it so? Then please give your new postal address.\nA : Sure! Here it is.\nB : Thank you!','',0,0,0,NULL),(39580,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare a dialogue each from the jumbled sentences :\nInviting a friend to your birthday party:\n: Aren\'t you going to celebrate it?\n: Yes. sure. Do come to attend my birthday party.\n: My birthday falls on this Sunday.\n: It\'s in the evening!\n: At what time?','','','A : My birthday falls on this Sunday.\nB : Aren\'t you going to celebrate it?\nA : Yes, sure. Do come to attend my birthday party.\nB : At what time?\nA : It\'s in the evening.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39581,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare a dialogue each from the jumbled sentences :\nAsking a friend to lend you her notebook:\n: Yes, sure. What are friends for!\n: I was absent yesterday.\n: Will you please lend me your notebook? I\'ll know what was taught yesterday.\n: How can I help you?','','','A : I was absent yesterday.\nB : How can I help you?\nA : Will you please lend me your notebook?\n       I\'ll know what was taught yesterday.\nB : Yes, sure. What are friends for!','',0,0,0,NULL),(39582,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare a dialogue each from the jumbled sentences :\nSaying sorry to someone for trodding on his/her feet:\n: Not much. It\'s all right.\n: Can\'t you see properly? You have trodden on my feet.\n: Oh! I\'m extremely sorry! Are you hurt?\n: I hope you will forgive me.','','','A : Can\'t you see properly? You have trodden on my feet.\nB : Oh! I\'m extremely sorry! Are you hurt?\nA : Not much. It\'s all right.\nB : I hope you will forgive me. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(39583,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare a dialogue each from the jumbled sentences :\nOffering a glass of water to a guest:\n: (Bell rings) Who\'s there?\n: Please, come in. I have heard your name.\n: Have a seat, Uncle, I\'ll bring a glass of water.\n: I\'m your father\'s friend, Mr. Shyamlal. \n: Thank you!','','','(Bell rings)\nA : Who\'s there?\nB : I\'m your father\'s friend. My Shyamlal.\nA : Please come in. I have heard your name. Have a seat, uncle. I\'ll bring a glass  \n       of water.\nB : Thank you!','',0,0,0,NULL),(39584,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Information Transfer\nRead the points given in the following web chart and brackets and complete a paragraph based on it. Give a suitable title to your write up :\n[relationship, support system, lucky, views, younger]','----------------------------------\nSibling relationship is the most crucial --------------- in the world. From a young age they listen to each other, argue with each other, and speak to each other so one can learn --------------- from sibling. Younger sibling is always lucky to --------- a lot of things from elder one. They are always ---------- to each other in sorrow or in any difficult times in life. So they are good ----------- for each other. a child learns a lot of social values like ------------ support, bonding from it’s early age from sibling. They are always there to share their opinions, ------------- and emotions, so they are good source of ---------------. They are also a good source of ------------- for each other as they provide a lot of knowledge to each other. the person who is having elder or ----------- sibling is considered to be -------- in life.','','Importance of siblings in our life\nSibling relationship is the most crucial relationship in the world. From a young age they listen each other, argue with each other, and speak to each other so one can learn important communication skills from siblings. Younger sibling is always lucky to learn to express a lot of things from elder one. They are always an emotional support to each other in sorrow or in any difficult times in life. So they are good support system for each other. A child learns a lot of social values like love, co-operation, support, bonding from it\'s early age from sibling. They are always there to share their opinions, views and emotions, so they are good source of sharing and caring. They are also a good source of information\nand knowledge for each other as they provide a lot of things to each other. The person who is having elder or younger sibling is considered to be lucky in life.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39585,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the points given in the following picture and complete a paragraph based on it. give a suitable title to your write up :','----------------------------------\nA ------------------ is a useful two-wheeler vehicle and ------------- is a fun activity enjoyed by people of all ages. It is one of the easiest ways to give ---------- to our whole body. It strengthens our --------------, reduces high blood pressure and ----------------. It helps us lose fat and -------------------. It improves ------------- Cycling burns our ------------ not fuel. It strengthens our ----------- and boosts our -------------. It reduces risk ------------ and relives our ---------------. So, cycling is good for our health and to protect nature also.','','Cycling - The best way for full body exercise\nA cycle is a useful two-wheeler vehicle and cycling is a fun activity enjoyed by people of all ages. It is one of the easiest ways to give exercise to our whole body. It strengthens our immune system, reduces high blood pressure and risk of diabetes. It helps us lose fat and build muscles. It improves co-ordination. Cycling burns our calories not fuel. It strengthens our legs, boosts our metabolism. It reduces risk of heart disease and relieves our stress. So cycling is good for our health and to protect nature also.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39586,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the points given in the following tree diagram and complete the paragraph based on it. give a suitable title to your write up :','------------------------------------\n------------- is a substance that is burnt to provide energy, heat or power. There are --------- types of fuel. Solid fuel, ----------- and ---------------. We get solid fuel in the form of coal, liquid fuel in the form of ------------- and --------- in the form of natural gas. Peat, -------------, -------------- and ------------ are the examples of solid fuel (Coal). --------------, -------------------. Diesel and ---------- are the examples of liquid fuel (Mineral Oil). LNG and ------------ are the examples of ----------- (Natural gas). Fuels are very important in our life. We cannot make progress without fuels.','','Different Types of Fuels - Real source of our development\nFuel is a substance that is burnt to provide energy, heat or power. There are three types of fuel. Solid fuels, liquid fuels and gaseous fuels. We get solid fuels in the form of Coal, liquid fuel in the form of mineral oil and gaseous fuels in the form of natural gas. Peat, Lignite, Bituminous and coal are the examples of Solid fuel (Coal). Kerosene, Naphtha, Diesel and Gasoline are the examples of Liquid fuel (Mineral Oil). LNG and CNG are the examples of gaseous fuels (Natural gas). Fuels are very important in our life. We cannot make progress without fuels.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39587,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the points given in the following Web – chart and complete the paragraph based on it. Giva a suitable title to your write up :','                                 ---------------------------------\nA -------------- who possesses different good qualities and is a center of attraction of the classroom is called a good student. Everyone likes to be a ---------- but those who possesses some important qualities can become a good student. The important qualities are – to come ------------, respect ------------, complete his --------------. He should be friendly ----------- and actively participates --------------. He follows --------------- in the classroom, at home and in the society wherever he goes. He stays ------------ and motivates others. He always keeps ------------ and remains ----------- every time as a student. . It is possible for every student from his/her bottom of heart.','','A Good Student: A Future of India\nA student who possesses different good qualities and is a centre of attraction of the classroom is called a good student. Everyone likes to be a good student but those who possesses some important qualities can become a good student. The important qualities are to come to school on time, respect parents, teachers and elders, complete his homework on time. He should be friendly with everyone and actively participates in classroom activities. He follows discipline in the classroom, at home and in the society wherever he goes. He stays motivated and motivates others. He always keeps positive attitude and remains confident every time as a student. It is possible for every student to become a good student, if he or she follows these important qualities from his/her bottom of heart.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39588,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the points given in the following table and complete the paragraph based on it. Give a suitable title to your write up :','                       ----------------------------------------\nThere are different types of --------------. The stories mentioned in this table are Adventure, -----------------, --------------------, Historical fiction and ------------. A story in which the characters go somewhere exciting and dangerous are called ---------- is the best example of it. Akbar and Birbal is the collection of --------------- stories in which readers enjoy laughter and fun. The stories which involve magical events and imaginary creatures are called -----------, ------------- and ---------- ----------------- are the examples of fairy tales. Historical fictions are based on -----------. Salman Rushdie’s  ------------ is one of the good examples of it. in horror, writer addresses ---------------- and the readers enjoy it. A face in the Dark written by --------- is the best example of it.','','Different types of stories\nThere are different types of stories. The stories mentioned in this table are Adventure, Humorous, Fairy tales, Historical fiction and Horror. A story in which the characters go somewhere exciting and dangerous are called adventure story. The Jungle Book is the best example of it. Akbar and Birbal is the collection of Humorous stories in which readers enjoy laughter and fun. The stories in it involves magical events and imaginary creatures are called Fairy Tales. Beauty and the Beast and Cinderella are the examples of fairy tales. Historical fictions are based on particular historical events. Salman Rushdie\'s Midnight\'s Children is one of the best examples of it. In horror, writer addresses realistic psychological fear and the readers enjoy it. A Face in the Dark written by Ruskin Bond is the best example of it.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39589,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Observe the following picture carefully and complete the dialogues with the help of the words given in the brackets :\n[today, enjoy, played, play, many, cricket]\n','Children : We are here after so ----------- days?\nRaju : What game shall we ----------- today?\nChildren : Let’s play ---------- today.\nRaju : But last time we ----------- cricket. Shall we play football --------------?\nChildren : Why not? Let’s --------- football.','','Children : We are here after so many days.\nRaju : What game shall we play today?\nChildren : Let\'s play cricket today.\nRaju : But last time we played cricket. Shall we play football today?\nChildren : Why not? Let\'s enjoy football.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39590,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Observe the following picture carefully and complete the dialogue with the help of the words given in the brackets :\n  [uncle, think, father, passing, mother, family, come, urgent, home]\n','Guest : Rahul, is your father at ---------?\nRahul : No, -----------, he gas gone out for a wedding.\nGuest : What about your ---------? Is she at home?\nRahul : She also went with ------------.\nGuest : Okay! What time will they --------- back?\nRahul : I --------, they will be back by 6 O’clock. Any thing ----------?\nGuest : No dear. I was just --------- by this side, so thought of visiting your --------.','','Guest : Rahul, is your father at home?\nRahul: No, uncle, he has gone out for a wedding.\nGuest : What about your mother? Is she at home?\nRahul : She also went with father.\nGuest : Okay! What time will they come back?\nRahul : I think, they will be back by 6 O\' clock. Any thing urgent?\nGuest : No dear. I was just passing by this side, so thought of visiting your family.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39591,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Observe the following picture carefully and complete the dialogue with the help of the words given in the brackets :\n[cough, feel, feeling, medicines, worry, thank, again, matter, how]\n','Doctor : So, ---------- are you, Sameer?\nSameer : I’m not ------------ very well, sir.\nDoctor : What is the ------------?\nSameer : I have a bad cold and --------------\nDoctor : Ok, don’t ----------. I will give you some ----------.\nSameer : Shall I meet you --------?\nDoctor : Meet me after two days. If you do not -------- well.\nSameer : ---------- you doctor.','','Doctor : So, How are you, Sameer?\nSameer : I\'m not feeling very well, sir.\nDoctor : What is the matter?\nSameer : I have a bad cold and cough.\nDoctor: Ok. Don\'t worry. I will give you some medicines.\nSameer : Shall I meet you again?\nDoctor : Meet me after two days if you do not feel well.\nSameer : Thank you doctor.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39592,590,'descriptive','5b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Observe the following picture carefully and complete the dialogue with the help of the words given in the brackets :\n[congrats, match, cricket, wish, tournaments, a lot, happy]\n','Rahul : You are looking very ----- today, Sahil.\nSahil : Yes, I’m very happy. I got the first prize in our school badminton --------.\nRahul : ---------! Keep it up.\nSahil : Thanks a lot. I think you are also taking part in ----- tournaments.\nRahul : Yes. Our cricket ---------- will be there tomorrow.\nSahil : Ohh! --------- you all the best!\nRahul : Thanks --------- for your wishes.','','Rahul : You are looking very happy today, Sahil.\nSahil : Yes, I\'m very happy. I got the first prize in our school badminton tournaments.\nRahul : Congrats! Keep it up!\nSahil : Thanks a lot. I think you are also taking part in cricket tournaments.\nRahul : Yes. Our cricket match will be there tomorrow.\nSahil : Ohh! Wish you all the best!\nRahul : Thanks a lot for your wishes.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39593,590,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Observe the following picture carefully and complete the dialogue with the help of the words given in the brackets :\n[forgotten, completely, ready, to visit, getting, fast, wake, holiday]\n','Mummy : ---------- up, Tejas. It’s 6.30.\nTejas : Today is Sunday, Mummy. We have a ------------\nMummy : Have you -------- that we are going ---------- a fort today?\nTejas : The fort! Oh, I --------- forgot. I’ll get up now!\nMother : That’s good. Get up --------- and get ready.\nTejas : What about papa and Trisha? Are they -------------?\nMother : they are ---------- ready.','','Mummy : Wake up, Tejas. It\'s 6.30.\nTejas : Today is Sunday, Mummy. We have a holiday.\nMummy : Have you forgotten that we are going to visit a fort today?\nTejas : The fort! Oh, I completely forgot! I\'ll get up now!\nMother : That\'s good. Get up fast and get ready.\nTejas : What about papa and Trisha? Are they ready?\nMother : They are getting ready.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39594,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the following dialogue :\nA : What is your father?\n\nB : -------------------------------\nA : And your mother?\n\nB : ----------------------------','','','A : What is your father?\nB : My father is a teacher.\nA : And your mother?\nB : She is also  a teacher.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39595,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the following dialogue :\nKuldeep : What is your hobby?\n\nSumit : --------------------------------\nKuldeep : What kind of books do you like read?\n\nSumit : ------------------------------------','','','Kuldeep : What is your hobby?\nSumit : Reading is my hobby.\nKuldeep : What kind of books do you like read?\nSumit : I like adventures stories to read.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39596,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the following dialogue :\nShlok : What is social distancing, mamma?\n\nAishwarya : ------------------------------------------\nShlok : But why should we keep social distance?\n\nAishwarya : ----------------------------------------------','','','Shlok : What is social distancing, mamma?\nAishwarya : Keeping safe distance between two.\nShlok : But why should we keep social distance?\nAishwarya : Because Covid – 19 is a highly infectious disease.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39597,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the following dialogue :\nTeacher : Rahul, how many days are there in a week?\n\nRahul : ----------------------------------------------------------\nTeacher : On which day our school is having a holiday every week?\n\nRahul : -----------------------------------------------------------','','','Teacher : Rahul, how many days are there in a week?\nRahul : There are seven days in a week.\nTeacher : On which day our school is having a holiday every week?\nRahul : On Sunday our school is having holiday every week.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39598,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the following dialogue :\nMummy : Rahul, why are you not eating the salad?\n\nRahul : -----------------------------------------------------------\nMummy : Raw vegetables are good for health. Besides, you must eat whatever is made in the house.\n\nRahul : --------------------------------------------------------------','','','Mummy : Rahul, why are you not eating the salad?\nRahul : I don’t like raw vegetables, Mummy.\nMummy : Raw vegetables are good for health. Besides, you must eat whatever is made in the house.\nRahul : Alright, Mummy. I’ll try.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39599,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the following dialogue :\nBrijesh : Can I get two tickets of Mahalaxmi express from Pune to Kolhapur?\n\nClerk : --------------------------------------------------------------\nClerk : When do you want to go?\n\nBrijesh : --------------------------------------------------------','','','Brijesh : Can I get two tickets of Mahalaxmi express from Pune to Kolhapur?\nClerk : Yes, sure. Trains are running empty nowadays.\nClerk : When do you want to go?\nBrijesh : We want to go by tomorrow. Please give me two tickets.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39600,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare the meaningful dialogue from jumbled sentences :\n     * I like to drink milk.\n     * No, I don\'t.\n    * Do you like to drink tea?\n    * What do you like to drink then?\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','* Do you like to drink tea?\n* No, I don\'t.\n* What do you like to drink then.\n* I like to drink milk.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39601,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare the meaningful dialogue from jumbled sentences :\n* We should wear mask and keep social distancing.\n* It is the result of our negligence.\n* How\'s that?\n* Corona is again spreading rapidly.\n      \n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','* Corona is again spreading rapidly.\n* It is the result of our negligence.\n* How is that?\n* We should wear masks and keep social distancing.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39602,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare the meaningful dialogue from jumbled sentences :\n* Don\'t mention it.\n* Thanks a lot.\n* With great pleasure. Please take it.\n* Will you please give me your pencil?\n\n           -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','* Will you please give me your pencil?,\n* With great pleasure. Please take it.\n* Thanks a lot.\n* Don\'t mention it.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39603,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Rearrange the sentences in each set to complete a meaningful dialogue :\nAmit : Yes. Yesterday itself. It was the last date. What about you? \nSumit : Not yet. Because of my sickness.\nAmit : Oh! Better you meet the teacher and tell the reason.\nSumit : Did you submit your English assignments?\n\n         -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Sumit : Did you submit your English assignments?\nAmit : Yes. Yesterday itself. It was the last date. What about you?\nSumit : Not yet. Because of my sickness.\nAmit : Oh! Better you meet the teacher and tell the reason.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39604,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Rearrange the sentences in each set to complete a meaningful dialogue :\nPriya : I am going. Please do come. I need your company.\nRiya : Ok. I will ask my father today. If he says \'yes\', I will come.\nPriya : Are you going for school picnic?\nRiya : Not yet decided. What about you?\n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Priya : Are you going to school picnic?\nRiya : Not yet decided. What about you?\nPriya : I am going. Please do come. I need your company.\nRiya : Ok. I will ask my father today. If he says \'yes\', I will come.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39605,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Rearrange the sentences in each set to complete a meaningful dialogue :\nLibrarian : Did you submit the book you have taken last time?\nSamir : No, Madam. I will submit both the books together.\nLibrarian : No. First submit the book you have taken. Then you will get another book.\nSamir : May I get a new book Madam?\n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Samir : May I get a new book Madam?\nLibrarian : Did you submit the book you have taken last time?\nSamir : No, Madam. I will submit both the books together.\nLibrarian : No. First submit the book you have taken. Then you will get another.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39606,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Rearrange the sentences in each set to complete a meaningful dialogue :\nPassenger : Thanks a lot, my dear boy.\nRishi : Mention not Madam. I am getting down at next stop.\nPassenger : It\'s a ladies seat. Can you get up please?\nRishi : Sure Madam. You can sit here.\n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Passenger : It\'s a ladies seat. Can you get up please?\nRishi : Sure Madam. You can sit here.\nPassenger: Thanks a lot my dear boy.\nRishi : Mention not madam. I am getting down at next stop.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39607,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Rearrange the sentences in each set to complete a meaningful dialogue :\nStranger: Yes. You will be in front of Z.P. office.\nYou : Is it nearby once I take the first right?\nStranger : Yes, it\'s quiet easy. Just go straight and take first right.\nYou : Excuse me, may I know how to reach Z.P office?\n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','You : Excuse me! May I know how to reach Z.P office?\nStranger : Yes, it\'s quiet easy. Just go straight and take first right.\nYou : Is it nearby once I take the first right?\nStranger : Yes. You will be in front of Z.P. office.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39608,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare a dialogue each from the jumbled sentences :\nAsking for postal address :\n: Is it so? Then please give your new postal address.\n: Thank you!\n: Sure! Here it is.\n: Do you know, I have changed my residence.\n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n       --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','A : Do you know. I have changed my residence.\nB : Is it so? Then please give your new postal address.\nA : Sure! Here it is.\nB : Thank you!','',0,0,0,NULL),(39609,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare a dialogue each from the jumbled 