A ------------------ is a useful two-wheeler vehicle and ------------- is a fun activity enjoyed by people of all ages. It is one of the easiest ways to give ---------- to our whole body. It strengthens our ----\n\n----------, reduces high blood pressure and ----------------. It helps us lose fat and -------------------. It improves ------------- Cycling burns our ------------ not fuel. It strengthens our ----------- and \n\nboosts our -------------. It reduces risk ------------ and relives our ---------------. So, cycling is good for our health and to protect nature also.','','                          Cycling - The best way for full body exercise\nA cycle is a useful two-wheeler vehicle and cycling is a fun activity enjoyed by people of all ages. It is one of the easiest ways to give exercise to our whole body. It strengthens our immune system, reduces high blood pressure and risk of diabetes. It helps us lose fat and build muscles. It improves co-ordination. Cycling burns our calories not fuel. It strengthens our legs, boosts our metabolism. It reduces risk of heart disease and relieves our stress. So cycling is good for our health and to protect nature also.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39615,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the points given in the following tree diagram and complete the paragraph based on it. give a suitable title to your write up :','\n                                                                                             ------------------------------------\n------------- is a substance that is burnt to provide energy, heat or power. There are --------- types of fuel. Solid fuel, ----------- and ---------------. We get solid fuel in the form of coal, liquid fuel in the \n\nform of ------------- and --------- in the form of natural gas. Peat, -------------, -------------- and ------------ are the examples of solid fuel (Coal). --------------, -------------------. Diesel and ---------- \n\nare the examples of liquid fuel (Mineral Oil). LNG and ------------ are the examples of ----------- (Natural gas). Fuels are very important in our life. We cannot make progress without fuels.','','Different Types of Fuels - Real source of our development\nFuel is a substance that is burnt to provide energy, heat or power. There are three types of fuel. Solid fuels, liquid fuels and gaseous fuels. We get solid fuels in the form of Coal, liquid fuel in the form of mineral oil and gaseous fuels in the form of natural gas. Peat, Lignite, Bituminous and coal are the examples of Solid fuel (Coal). Kerosene, Naphtha, Diesel and Gasoline are the examples of Liquid fuel (Mineral Oil). LNG and CNG are the examples of gaseous fuels (Natural gas). Fuels are very important in our life. We cannot make progress without fuels.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39616,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the points given in the following Web – chart and complete the paragraph based on it. Giva a suitable title to your write up :','\n                                                             ---------------------------------\n\nA -------------- who possesses different good qualities and is a center of attraction of the classroom is called a good student. Everyone likes to be a ---------- but those who possesses some important \n\nqualities can become a good student. The important qualities are – to come ------------, respect ------------, complete his --------------. He should be friendly ----------- and actively participates --------\n\n------. He follows --------------- in the classroom, at home and in the society wherever he goes. He stays ------------ and motivates others. He always keeps ------------ and remains ----------- every \ntime as a student. It is possible for every student from his/her bottom of heart.','','A Good Student: A Future of India\nA student who possesses different good qualities and is a centre of attraction of the classroom is called a good student. Everyone likes to be a good student but those who possesses some important qualities can become a good student. The important qualities are to come to school on time, respect parents, teachers and elders, complete his homework on time. He should be friendly with everyone and actively participates in classroom activities. He follows discipline in the classroom, at home and in the society wherever he goes. He stays motivated and motivates others. He always keeps positive attitude and remains confident every time as a student. It is possible for every student to become a good student, if he or she follows these important qualities from his/her bottom of heart.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39617,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the points given in the following table and complete the paragraph based on it. Give a suitable title to your write up :','\n                                                                           ----------------------------------------\nThere are different types of --------------. The stories mentioned in this table are Adventure, -----------------, --------------------, Historical fiction and ------------. A story in which the characters go \n\nsomewhere exciting and dangerous are called ---------- is the best example of it. Akbar and Birbal is the collection of --------------- stories in which readers enjoy laughter and fun. The stories which \n\ninvolve magical events and imaginary creatures are called -----------, ------------- and ---------- ----------------- are the examples of fairy tales. Historical fictions are based on -----------. Salman \n\nRushdie’s  ------------ is one of the good examples of it. in horror, writer addresses ---------------- and the readers enjoy it. A face in the Dark written by --------- is the best example of it.','','Different types of stories\nThere are different types of stories. The stories mentioned in this table are Adventure, Humorous, Fairy tales, Historical fiction and Horror. A story in which the characters go somewhere exciting and dangerous are called adventure story. The Jungle Book is the best example of it. Akbar and Birbal is the collection of Humorous stories in which readers enjoy laughter and fun. The stories in it involves magical events and imaginary creatures are called Fairy Tales. Beauty and the Beast and Cinderella are the examples of fairy tales. Historical fictions are based on particular historical events. Salman Rushdie\'s Midnight\'s Children is one of the best examples of it. In horror, writer addresses realistic psychological fear and the readers enjoy it. A Face in the Dark written by Ruskin Bond is the best example of it.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39618,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Observe the following picture carefully and complete the dialogues with the help of the words given in the brackets :\n[today, enjoy, played, play, many, cricket]\n','\nChildren : We are here after so ----------- days?\n\nRaju : What game shall we ----------- today?\n\nChildren : Let’s play ---------- today.\n\nRaju : But last time we ----------- cricket. Shall we play football --------------?\n\nChildren : Why not? Let’s --------- football.','','Children : We are here after so many days.\nRaju : What game shall we play today?\nChildren : Let\'s play cricket today.\nRaju : But last time we played cricket. Shall we play football today?\nChildren : Why not? Let\'s enjoy football.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39619,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Observe the following picture carefully and complete the dialogue with the help of the words given in the brackets :\n  [uncle, think, father, passing, mother, family, come, urgent, home]\n','\nGuest : Rahul, is your father at ---------?\n\nRahul : No, -----------, he gas gone out for a wedding.\n\nGuest : What about your ---------? Is she at home?\n\nRahul : She also went with ------------.\n\nGuest : Okay! What time will they --------- back?\n\nRahul : I --------, they will be back by 6 O’clock. Any thing ----------?\n\nGuest : No dear. I was just --------- by this side, so thought of visiting your --------.','','Guest : Rahul, is your father at home?\nRahul: No, uncle, he has gone out for a wedding.\nGuest : What about your mother? Is she at home?\nRahul : She also went with father.\nGuest : Okay! What time will they come back?\nRahul : I think, they will be back by 6 O\' clock. Any thing urgent?\nGuest : No dear. I was just passing by this side, so thought of visiting your family.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39620,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Observe the following picture carefully and complete the dialogue with the help of the words given in the brackets :\n[cough, feel, feeling, medicines, worry, thank, again, matter, how]\n','\nDoctor : So, ---------- are you, Sameer?\n\nSameer : I’m not ------------ very well, sir.\n\nDoctor : What is the ------------?\n\nSameer : I have a bad cold and --------------\n\nDoctor : Ok, don’t ----------. I will give you some ----------.\n\nSameer : Shall I meet you --------?\n\nDoctor : Meet me after two days. If you do not -------- well.\n\nSameer : ---------- you doctor.','','Doctor : So, How are you, Sameer?\nSameer : I\'m not feeling very well, sir.\nDoctor : What is the matter?\nSameer : I have a bad cold and cough.\nDoctor: Ok. Don\'t worry. I will give you some medicines.\nSameer : Shall I meet you again?\nDoctor : Meet me after two days if you do not feel well.\nSameer : Thank you doctor.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39621,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Observe the following picture carefully and complete the dialogue with the help of the words given in the brackets :\n[congrats, match, cricket, wish, tournaments, a lot, happy]\n','\nRahul : You are looking very ----- today, Sahil.\n\nSahil : Yes, I’m very happy. I got the first prize in our school badminton --------.\n\nRahul : ---------! Keep it up.\n\nSahil : Thanks a lot. I think you are also taking part in ----- tournaments.\n\nRahul : Yes. Our cricket ---------- will be there tomorrow.\n\nSahil : Ohh! --------- you all the best!\n\nRahul : Thanks --------- for your wishes.','','Rahul : You are looking very happy today, Sahil.\nSahil : Yes, I\'m very happy. I got the first prize in our school badminton tournaments.\nRahul : Congrats! Keep it up!\nSahil : Thanks a lot. I think you are also taking part in cricket tournaments.\nRahul : Yes. Our cricket match will be there tomorrow.\nSahil : Ohh! Wish you all the best!\nRahul : Thanks a lot for your wishes.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39622,591,'descriptive','5b',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Observe the following picture carefully and complete the dialogue with the help of the words given in the brackets :\n[forgotten, completely, ready, to visit, getting, fast, wake, holiday]\n','\nMummy : ---------- up, Tejas. It’s 6.30.\n\nTejas : Today is Sunday, Mummy. We have a ------------\n\nMummy : Have you -------- that we are going ---------- a fort today?\n\nTejas : The fort! Oh, I --------- forgot. I’ll get up now!\n\nMother : That’s good. Get up --------- and get ready.\n\nTejas : What about papa and Trisha? Are they -------------?\n\nMother : they are ---------- ready.','','Mummy : Wake up, Tejas. It\'s 6.30.\nTejas : Today is Sunday, Mummy. We have a holiday.\nMummy : Have you forgotten that we are going to visit a fort today?\nTejas : The fort! Oh, I completely forgot! I\'ll get up now!\nMother : That\'s good. Get up fast and get ready.\nTejas : What about papa and Trisha? Are they ready?\nMother : They are getting ready.','',1,0,0,NULL),(39623,592,'descriptive','6',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','A) Translate the following words in Marathi ---------- 1M\n      i. ocean            ii. holiday\nB) Translate the following sentences in Marathi --------- 2M\n      i. All Indians are my brothers and sisters.\n      ii. It’s nice to be back in school.','','','A] i) महासागर           ii) सुट्टी\nB] i) सर्व भारतीय माझे बंधू आणि भगिनी आहेत\n    ii) पुन्हा शाळेत यायला फारच छान वाटते.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39624,592,'descriptive','6',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','A) Translate the following words in Marathi ---------- 1M\n      i. permission             ii. adjective\nB) Translate the following sentences in Marathi --------- 2M\n      i. We spent our holidays at Ratnagiri.\n      ii. Please do not bring any gifts or presents.','','','A] i) परवानगी         ii) विशेषण\nB] i) आम्ही आमची सुट्टी रत्नागिरी येथे घालवली\n    ii) कृपया कोणतीही भेटवस्तू अथवा आहेर आणू नये ','',0,0,0,NULL),(39625,592,'descriptive','6',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','A) Translate the following words in Marathi ---------- 1M\n      i. serious           ii. puddle\nB) Translate the following sentences in Marathi --------- 2M\n      i. The girls took of their shoes.\n      ii. It was really unbelievable.','','','A] i) गंभीर           ii) डबके \nB] i) मुलींनी त्यांचे शूज काढले \n    ii) ते खरोखरच अविश्वसनीय होते','',0,0,0,NULL),(39626,592,'descriptive','6',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','A) Translate the following words in Marathi ---------- 1M\n      i. purposely           ii. peasants \nB) Translate the following sentences in Marathi --------- 2M\n      i. Our day starts with a prayer.\n      ii. We all liked her very much.','','','A] i) मुद्दामहून                ii) शेतकरी\nB] i) आमचा दिवस प्रार्थनेने सुरू होतो\n    ii) आम्हा सर्वांना ती फारच आवडते','',0,0,0,NULL),(39627,592,'descriptive','6',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','A) Translate the following words in Marathi ---------- 1M\n      i. laughter              ii. scatter\nB) Translate the following sentences in Marathi --------- 2M\n      i. Keep pin drop silence in the classroom.\n      ii. I am not good at climbing trees.','','','A] i) हशा             ii) पसरणे\nB] i) कृपया वर्गाने पूर्ण शांतता ठेवा\n    ii) मला झाडांवर चढायला जमत नाही','',0,0,0,NULL),(39628,592,'descriptive','6',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','A) Translate the following words in Marathi ---------- 1M\n      i. traveller                   ii. regions\nB) Translate the following sentences in Marathi --------- 2M\n      i. He welcomed his friend heartly.\n      ii. They are not serious about their studies.','','','A] i) प्रवासी              ii) विभाग \nB] i) त्याने त्याच्या मित्राचे अंत:करणापासून स्वागत केले\n    ii) ते त्यांच्या अभ्यासाबाबत गंभीर नाही आहेत','',0,0,0,NULL),(39629,592,'descriptive','6',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','A) Translate the following words in Marathi ---------- 1M\n      i. eager           ii. powerful\nB) Translate the following sentences in Marathi --------- 2M\n      i. Cut the cloth into pieces.\n      ii. Follow the discipline in the school.','','','A] i) उत्सुक               ii)  शक्तीशाली\nB] i) कापडाचे तुकडे कर\n    ii) शाळेत शिस्तीचे पालन करा','',0,0,0,NULL),(39630,592,'descriptive','6',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','A) Translate the following words in Marathi ---------- 1M\n      i. imagine            ii. companions\nB) Translate the following sentences in Marathi --------- 2M\n      i. Soldiers guard our borders day and night.\n      ii. Raman was really a great scientists.','','','A] i) कल्पना करणे           ii)  सोबती\nB] i) सैनिक आपल्या सीमांचे दिवस रात्र रक्षण करतात\n    ii) रामन एक थोर शास्त्रज्ञ होते','',0,0,0,NULL),(39631,592,'descriptive','6',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','A) Translate the following words in Marathi ---------- 1M\n      i. breeze                ii. discussion\nB) Translate the following sentences in Marathi --------- 2M\n      i. We like to listen to patriotic songs.\n      ii. How much did you pay for it?','','','A] i) वाऱ्याची              ii) झुळूक चर्चा \nB] i) आम्हाला देशभक्तीपर गीते ऐकायला आवडतात\n    ii) तू यासाठी किती पैसे दिलेस?','',0,0,0,NULL),(39632,592,'descriptive','6',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','A) Translate the following words in Marathi ---------- 1M\n      i. probably            ii. scold\nB) Translate the following sentences in Marathi --------- 2M\n      i. Is it your final decision?\n      ii. He was graduated in 2010.','','','A] i) बहुदा                ii) खरडपट्टी काढणे\nB] i) हा तुझा अंतिम निर्णय आहे का?\n    ii) त