descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','It\'s a world of laughter, \nA world of tears. \nIt\'s a world of hopes, \nAnd a world of fears. \nThere\'s so much that we share \nThat it\'s time we\'re aware \nIt\'s a small world after all ...\nIt\'s a small world after all \nIt\'s a small world after all \nIt\'s a small world after all \nIt\'s a small, small world.\nThere is just one moon \nAnd one golden sun \nAnd a smile means \nFriendship to every one. \nThough the mountains divide\nAnd the oceans are wide \nIt\'s a small world after all','1) Answer the following questions :\n    a) How is a world after all according to the poet?\n\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    b) How are oceans?\n\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','2) Which things other than laughter are mentioned in this poem?\n\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) write two rhyming words from the poem.\n\n     -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','1) a) According to the poet, it’s a small world after all\n    b) Oceans are wide\n2) Tears, fears and hopes are things mentioned in this poem other than laughter.\n3) tears – fears, share – aware, divide – wide ','',0,0,0,NULL),(39671,562,'descriptive','1a',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Copy the sentences \na) Be a bush, if you can’t be a tree \nb) Be the best of whatever you are ','','','a) Be a bush, if you can’t be a tree \nb) Be the best of whatever you are \n','',0,0,0,NULL),(39672,562,'descriptive','1a',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Put the following words in alphabetical order. \ni) valley, pine, crew, captains \nii) hill, here, highway, heroic ','','','i) captains, crew, pine, valley \nii) here, heroic, highway, hill \n','',0,0,0,NULL),(39673,562,'descriptive','1a',2,2,'Out of Text Book