 up]\n\n       1) Come --------------                   2) Go --------------\n\n       3) Sit ---------------                        4) Stand -----------\nB] What will you say if someone says to you – \n        1) Congratulations!               2) Thank you!\n        3) Sorry!\n \n---------------------------------------------      ---------------------------------------------\n\n---------------------------------------------      ---------------------------------------------','','','A] 1) Come here ; Come fast                2) Go there\n     3) Sit down                                          4) Stand up \nB] 1) Thank you                         2) Welcome/No mention\n     3) It’s ok.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39931,499,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Instead of let’s, use ‘Let me’ at the beginning and make meaningful sentence.\n1) Let’s work hard.                              2) Let’s work well.\n3) Let’s drink quickly.                          4) Let’s play cricket.\n5) Let’s eat biscuits.\n\n---------------------------------------------      ---------------------------------------------\n\n---------------------------------------------      ---------------------------------------------\n\n--------------------------------------------       ','','','1) Let me work hard.            2) Let me work well.\n3) Let me drink quickly.        4) Let me play cricket.\n5) Let me eat biscuits.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39932,618,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Choose the words, sentences and complete the following dialogues.\n[eat, pani-puri, well, Thank you, stomach]\nA : Aren’t you feeling ------------?\nB : Yes, I have ----------------- ache.\nA : What did you ---------- yesterday?\nB : I ate ------------. Please tell our teacher.\nA : Sure\nB : ------------------ very much.','','','well, stomach, eat, pani-puri, Thank you','',0,0,0,NULL),(39933,618,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Choose the words, sentences and complete the following dialogues.\n[do