 rivers\n2) a) without            b) go                  c) pass          d) night\n3) a) trains                  b) fail','',1,0,0,NULL),(39937,621,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following web :','Over the mountains, \nOver the plains \nOver the rivers \nHere come the trains.\nCarrying passengers, \nCarrying mail, \nBringing their precious loads \nIn without fail\nThousands of freight cars \nAll rushing on \nThrough day and darkness, \nThrough dusk and dawn\n2) Write the opposite words of :\n     a) small                   b) profit\n     c) dusk                      d) load\n3) Write the rhyming words of\n    a) on                     b) rushing','','1) a) passengers              b) mail           c) precious load \n2) a) big          b) loss           c) dawn          d) unload\n3) a) dawn                 b) gushing  ','',1,0,0,NULL),(39938,501,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following web :','\n--------------------------------------        -----------------------------------\n\n----------------------------------------\nOver the mountains, \nOver the plains \nOver the rivers \nHere come the trains.\nCarrying passengers, \nCarrying mail, \nBringing their precious loads \nIn without fail\nThousands of freight cars \nAll rushing on \nThrough day and darkness, \nThrough dusk and dawn\n2) Write the opposite words of :\n\n     a) with × ---------                  b) come × --------------\n\n     c) fail × -----------                     d) day × -------------\n3) Write the rhyming words of\n\n    a) plains = ----------                     b) mail = ----------------','','1) a) mountains        b) plains            c) rivers\n2) a) without            b) go                  c) pass          d) night\n3) a) trains                  b) fail','',1,0,0,NULL),(39939,501,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','1) Complete the following web :','\n------------------------------------           -------------------------------------\n\n---------------------------------\nOver the mountains, \nOver the plains \nOver the rivers \nHere come the trains.\nCarrying passengers, \nCarrying mail, \nBringing their precious loads \nIn without fail\nThousands of freight cars \nAll rushing on \nThrough day and darkness, \nThrough dusk and dawn\n2) Write the opposite words of :\n\n     a) small × -----------                  b) profit × --------------\n\n     c) dusk × ---------                     d) load × ------------------\n3) Write the rhyming words of\n\n    a) on = -----------                     b) rushing = ------------------','','1) a) passengers              b) mail           c) precious load \n2) a) big          b) loss           c) dawn          d) unload\n3) a) dawn                 b) gushing  ','',1,0,0,NULL),(39940,622,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the passage and do the activities :\n1) Complete the following web :\n','In a grove of mango trees, there was one little babul tree.\nThe little tree was pretty, but it was\nnot happy. One day it said,\n\"I do wish I had big leaves!\nAll the other trees have big leaves.\nMy thorns are sharp and stiff.\nChildren do not like me.\"\nNext day, when the little tree woke up, it had big leaves. It was just like the mango trees.\n\"Now I am happy,\" it said.\nBut a goat came along and ate up all the big leaves.\n\"Oh, dear!\" said the babul tree.\n\"I wish I had gold leaves.\nGoats do not eat gold leaves.\"\nNext day, when the little tree woke up, it had gold leaves.\n\"How happy-I am!\" it said.\nBut a thief came along and stole all the gold leaves.\n\"Oh dear!\" said the babul tree.\n\"I wish I had glass leaves.\nThieves do not steal glass leaves.\"\n2) Complete the following sentences.\n     i. The babul tree wished to have big leaves because ------------\n     ii. The babul tree wished to have golden leaves because --------\n3) From the passage find the opposites of :\n     i. small × ----------          ii) ugly × --------------','','1) i) It did not have big leaves       ii) Its thorns were sharp and stiff\n    iii) Children did not like it.\n2) i) other trees have big leaves.\n     ii) goats do not eat gold leaves\n3) i) big            ii) beautiful ','',1,0,0,NULL),(39941,622,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the passage and do the activities :\n1) The babul tree wished to have its thorns and small leaves again because ------\nIn a grove of mango trees, there was one little babul tree.\nThe little tree was pretty, but it was\nnot happy. One day it said,\n\"I do wish I had big leaves!\nAll the other trees have big leaves.\nMy thorns are sharp and stiff.\nChildren do not like me.\"\nNext day, when the little tree woke up, it had big leaves. It was just like the mango trees.\n\"Now I am happy,\" it said.\nBut a goat came along and ate up all the big leaves.\n\"Oh, dear!\" said the babul tree.\n\"I wish I had gold leaves.\nGoats do not eat gold leaves.\"\nNext day, when the little tree woke up, it had gold leaves.\n\"How happy-I am!\" it said.\nBut a thief came along and stole all the gold leaves.\n\"Oh dear!\" said the babul tree.\n\"I wish I had glass leaves.\nThieves do not steal glass leaves.\"\n2) Make negatives\n     i. Now I am happy.\n     ii. Goat ate up all the leaves.\n3) From the passage find the opposites of :\n     a) unhappy × --------       b) blunt × ------------','','','1) i) Goats do not eat them all up\n    ii) Thieves do not steal them.\n    iii) The wind will do them no harm.\n2) i) Now I am not happy.\n     ii) Goat did not eat up all the leaves\n3) a) happy           b) sharp','',0,0,0,NULL),(39942,622,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Drop \'do not\' / does not and frame meaningful sentences. \n1) Goats do not eat gold leaves.\n2) Thieves do not steal glass leaves.\n3) He does not play cricket.\n4) She does not like grapes.\n5) A lion does not eat grass. ','','','1) Goats eat green leaves.\n2) Thieves steal gold leaves.\n3) He plays badminton.\n4) She likes apples.\n5) A lion eats animals.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39943,622,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Use \'do not\' / \'does not appropriately the following and frame meaningful sentences\n1) I like mangoes.\n2) You travel by bus.\n3) He gets up at 7 : 30.\n4) A rabbit has a short tail.\n5) She uses a black pen.','','','1) I do not like figs.\n2) You do not travel by train.\n3) He does not get up at 6 : 30.\n4) A rabbit does not have a long tail.\n5) She does not use a blue pen.','',0,0,0,NULL),(39944,502,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the passage and do the activities :\n1) Complete the following web :\n','\n-------------------------------------        ------------------------------------------------\n\n---------------------------------------\nIn a grove of mango trees, there was one little babul tree.\nThe little tree was pretty, but it was\nnot happy. One day it said,\n\"I do wish I had big leaves!\nAll the other trees have big leaves.\nMy thorns are sharp and stiff.\nChildren do not like me.\"\nNext day, when the little tree woke up, it had big leaves. It was just like the mango trees.\n\"Now I am happy,\" it said.\nBut a goat came along and ate up all the big leaves.\n\"Oh, dear!\" said the babul tree.\n\"I wish I had gold leaves.\nGoats do not eat gold leaves.\"\nNext day, when the little tree woke up, it had gold leaves.\n\"How happy-I am!\" it said.\nBut a thief came along and stole all the gold leaves.\n\"Oh dear!\" said the babul tree.\n\"I wish I had glass leaves.\nThieves do not steal glass leaves.\"\n2) Complete the following sentences.\n\n     i. The babul tree wished to have big leaves because -----------------------\n\n     ii. The babul tree wished to have golden leaves because -------------------\n3) From the passage find the opposites of :\n\n     i. small × ------------------          ii) ugly × --------------','','1) i) It did not have big leaves       ii) Its thorns were sharp and stiff\n    iii) Children did not like it.\n2) i) other trees have big leaves.\n     ii) goats do not eat gold leaves\n3) i) big            ii) beautiful ','',1,0,0,NULL),(39945,502,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the passage and do the activities :\n1) The babul tree wished to have its thorns and small leaves again because ------\n\n----------------------------------------                   --------------------------------------------\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------\nIn a grove of mango trees, there was one little babul tree.\nThe little tree was pretty, but it was\nnot happy. One day it said,\n\"I do wish I had big leaves!\nAll the other trees have big leaves.\nMy thorns are sharp and stiff.\nChildren do not like me.\"\nNext day, when the little tree woke up, it had big leaves. It was just like the mango trees.\n\"Now I am happy,\" it said.\nBut a goat came along and ate up all the big leaves.\n\"Oh, dear!\" said the babul tree.\n\"I wish I had gold leaves.\nGoats do not eat gold leaves.\"\nNext day, when the little tree woke up, it had gold leaves.\n\"How happy-I am!\" it said.\nBut a thief came along and stole all the gold leaves.\n\"Oh dear!\" said the babul tree.\n\"I wish I had glass leaves.\nThieves do not steal glass leaves.\"\n2) Make negatives\n     i. Now I am happy.\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------\n     ii. Goat ate up all the leaves.\n\n      ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) From the passage find the opposites of :\n\n     a) unhappy × ------------------       b) blunt × ------------','','','1) i) Goats do not eat them all up\n    ii) Thieves do not steal them.\n    iii) The wind will do them no harm.\n2) i) Now I am not happy.\n     ii) Goat did not eat up all the leaves\n3) a) happy           b) sharp','',0,0,0,NULL),(39946,502,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Drop \'do not\' / does not and frame meaningfu