s first,” said the apple tree.\n4) Write suitable things/objects for given numbers and complete the web','5) Write the related words of the word (at least 2) : classroom\n6) Make/complete the word chain of describing words\nGreat → ------ → -----\n','','i) holiday            ii) picture\n2) boy, brother, ellipse, escape \n3) “eat one of my wild apples first,” said the apple tree.\n4) caps, bags, coins\n5) board, chalk, benches, light, fan \n6) tall, long, good','',1,0,0,NULL),(40016,654,'descriptive','1a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the words :\n       i. dr_ve                     ii. re_ly\n2) Arrange the words in alphabetical order :\n      rich, rather, symbol, elect \n3) Copy the sentences : \n      The warm he wiggles all around.\n4) Name picture and use the given describing words to make meaningful phrases for each thing','5) Write the related words of the word (at least 2) : market\n6) Make/complete the word chain of describing words\n       New → ------ → -------','','i) drive            ii) reply\n2) elect, rather, rich, symbol\n3) The warm he wiggles all around.\n4) Apple – a big, red, sweet apple\n5) stalls, peoples, shopkeepers, boards, toys, cars, policemen, clothes, dogs, flowers, vegetables\n6) white, easy, yellow','',1,0,0,NULL),(40017,654,'descriptive','1a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the words :\n      i. bo_rd            ii. fr_me\n2) Arrange the words in alphabetical order :\n     poor, pure, simple, busy\n3) Copy the sentences : \n     “I must do something about this!” he thought.\n4) Name picture and use the given describing words to make meaningful phrases for each thing','5) Write the related words of the word (at least four) : jungle\n6) Find and write the words that end with ‘y’\n','','i) board            ii) frame\n2) busy, poor, pure, simple\n3) “I must do something about this!” he thought.\n4) an elephant – a big, black, fat\n5) trees, animals, birds, fruits, flowers, monkeys, tigers, foxes\n6) any, my, every, by, many, only','',1,0,0,NULL),(40018,655,'descriptive','1a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the words :\n       i. ba_ket                 ii. sc_ool\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) Arrange the words in alphabetical order :\n     pen, tree, basket, apple, sky\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Copy the sentences : \n      Give me that feather.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) Name picture and use the given describing words to make meaningful phrases for each thing','\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) Complete the word chain of given action words\n\n         Give → -------------- → ----------\n6) Read the following sentence and underline the number.\n     i. They had two daughters.\n     ii. January had thirty – one days.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','i) basket                   ii) school\n2) Apple, basket, pen, tree\n3) Give me that feather.\n4) a parrot – a green, beautiful, soft, small parrot\n5) eat, take, enter\n6) i) two                ii) Thirty – one   ','',1,0,0,NULL),(40019,655,'descriptive','1a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the words :\n       i. colo_r                ii. ho_se       \n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) Arrange the words in alphabetical order :\n       sow, thresh, cut, bake, eat\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Copy the sentences :\n      One day, the Queen was taking a walk in her garden.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) Name picture and use the given describing words to make meaningful phrases for each thing','\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) Complete the word chain of given action words\n\n         knock → --------------- → ----------------\n6) Read the following sentence and underline the number.\n    i. A spider has eight legs.\n    ii. I have twenty pencils. \n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','i) colour              ii) house\n2) bake, cut, eat, sow, thresh\n3) One day, the Queen was taking a walk in her garden.\n4) house – a small, yellow, new house\n5) kick, keep, put\n6) i) eight             ii) twenty   ','',1,0,0,NULL),(40020,655,'descriptive','1a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the words :\n       i. tomorr_w              ii. s_op  \n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------           \n2) Arrange the words in alphabetical order :\n      Amit, Sumit, Anuja, Sadhana, Bhavana\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Copy the sentences :\n      There are eighty-eight pages in this book.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) Name picture and use the given describing words to make meaningful phrases for each thing','\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) Complete the word chain of given action words\n\n         fly → ----------------- → ---------- \n6) Read the following sentence and underline the number.\n     i. Sachin Tendulkar scored 250 runs yesterday.\n     ii. There are seven days in a week.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','i) tomorrow                ii) shop\n2) Amit, Anuja, Bhavana, Sadhana, Sumit\n3) There are eighty-eight pages in this book.\n4) oranges – tasty, juicy, ripe, big oranges\n5) yawn, nod, draw\n6) i) 250                  ii) seven  ','',1,0,0,NULL),(40021,655,'descriptive','1a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the words :\n        i. Hap_y               ii. b_tter\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) 