\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) Write the things related with given actions','\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) Make a new word of given word ‘are’\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n6) Find the words staring with ‘g’\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','i) admit               ii) actor \n2) carrier, mouse, must, Sunday\n3) The lion walks on padded paws.\n4) bag, umbrella, paper, cloth\n5) ear\n6) goat, give, glass, grass    ','',1,0,0,NULL),(40032,655,'descriptive','1a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the words :\n       i. ph_ne            ii. ca_le        \n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------   \n2) Arrange the words in alphabetical order :\n       mobile, phone, murder, active\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Copy the sentence :\n      On the left, there lived a carpenter.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) Complete the web','\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) Write words that begin with letter ‘k’\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n6) Make a new word by using word ‘dog’ \n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','i) phone                 ii) cable\n2) active, mobile, murder, phone\n3) On the left, there lived a carpenter.\n4) butter milk, curd, butter, sweets, paneer, khava\n5) kite, kind, kitten, keep, king\n6) god  ','',1,0,0,NULL),(40033,655,'descriptive','1a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the words :\n       i. gar_en           ii. f_the\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) Arrange the words in alphabetical order :\n      blue, green, violet, black, white\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Copy the sentences : \n      “Oh, Mamma! What a bright beautiful feather!”\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) Look at the picture and write the names.','\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) Make the list of following : Birds\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n6) Write the related words of the word (at least 2) : Railway station \n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','i) garden          ii) father\n2) black, blue, green, violet, white\n3)  “Oh, Mamma! What a bright beautiful feather!”\n4) i) ball             ii)  tree\n5) parrot, crow, sparrow, owl, duck, crane\n6) Railway, stalls, fruits, platforms, ticket checker, windows, enquiry','',1,0,0,NULL),(40034,655,'descriptive','1a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the words :\n      i. t_ble        ii. M_ther\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) Arrange the words in alphabetical order :\n      rain, cloud, sky, soil, land\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Copy the sentences :\n      They had two daughters.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) Look at the picture and write the names.','\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) Make the list of following : Animals\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n6) Find and write the words that end with ‘o’\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','i) table       ii) Mother\n2) cloud, land, rain, sky, soil\n3) They had two daughters.\n4) i) cat             ii) girl\n5) squirrel, mouse, elephant, lion, tiger\n6) who, no, to