             ii) वाफ\nB] i) कष्टाशिवाय फळ नाही              ii) सार्वजनिक वाहनांचा वापर करा.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(40749,714,'descriptive','6',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Translate the following words into Marathi ------------ 1M\n      i. skin                 ii. ghost \nB] Translate the following Proverbs into Marathi ---------- 2M\n     i. Service to man is service to God.\n     ii. Where there is will, there is a way.','','','A] i) कातडी                  ii) भूत\nB] i) जनसेवा हीच खरी ईश्वरसेवा           ii) इच्छा असेल तर मार्ग दिसेल.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(40750,714,'descriptive','6',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Translate the following words into Marathi ------------ 1M\n      i. pain               ii. remember\nB] Translate the following Proverbs into Marathi ---------- 2M\n     i. A friend is need is a friend indeed.\n     ii. Necessity is the mother of invention.','','','A] i) वेदना                    ii) कधीही न विसरणे\nB] i) संकट समयी मदत करतो तोच खरा मित्र \n     ii) गरज ही शोधाची जननी आहे.','',0,0,0,NULL),(40751,714,'descriptive','6',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Translate the following words into Marathi ------------ 1M\n      i. patient               ii. refuse\nB] Translate the following Proverbs into Marathi ---------- 2M\n     i. Practice makes man perfect.\n     ii. Laughter is the best medicine. ','','','A] i) रुग्ण                  ii) नकार देणे\nB] i) सरावाने मनुष्य परिपूर्ण होतो.\n     ii) हास्य हे सर्वोत्तम औषध आहे.      ','',0,0,0,NULL),(40752,186,'descriptive','3a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Say whether the following sentences are Ture or false.\n\n     i. We shall walk hand in hand. ---------------\n\n     ii. We shall live peacefully. -----------------------\nWe shall overcome, we shall overcome, \nwe shall overcome some day; \nOh! Deep in my heart I do believe, \nwe shall overcome some day.\nWe\'ll walk hand in hand, we\'ll walk hand in hand, \nWe\'ll walk hand in hand some day; \nOh! Deep in my heart I do believe, \nwe shall overcome some day.\nWe are not afraid, We are not afraid, \nWe are not afraid today. \nOh! Deep in my heart I do believe, \nwe shall overcome some day.\nThe truth shall make us free, the truth shall make us free, \nThe truth shall make us free someday; Oh! Deep in my heart I do believe, we shall overcome some day.\nWe shall live in peace, we shall live in peace, \nWe shall live in peace some day; \nOh! Deep in my heart I do believe, \nwe shall overcome some day.\n2) Complete the following sentences.\n\n    i. I do believe that ------------ ----------------\n\n    ii. ------- ------------ shall make us free.\n3) Write the rhyming words for the following words.\n\n     i. hand = ----------           ii. Peace = ----------------','','','i) True           ii) True\n2) i) we shall overcome someday.\n     ii) The truth\n3) i) land, band           ii) niece, fleece','',0,0,0,NULL),(40753,186,'descriptive','3b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','We shall overcome, we shall overcome, \nwe shall overcome some day; \nOh! Deep in my heart I do believe, \nwe shall overcome some day.\nWe\'ll walk hand in hand, we\'ll walk hand in hand, \nWe\'ll walk hand in hand some day; \nOh! Deep in my heart I do believe, \nwe shall overcome some day.\nWe are not afraid, We are not afraid, \nWe are not afraid today. \nOh! Deep in my heart I do believe, \nwe shall overcome some day.\nThe truth shall make us free, the truth shall make us free, \nThe truth shall make us free someday; Oh! Deep in my heart I do believe, we shall overcome some day.\nWe shall live in peace, we shall live in peace, \nWe shall live in peace some day; \nOh! Deep in my heart I do believe, \nwe shall overcome some day.\n1) Which is the main thing we believe the most?\n\n     ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2) How will we walk some day?\n\n    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) How are we today?\n\n    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4) What will the truth do?\n\n    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5) How will we live some day?\n\n    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The main thing we believe the most is that we shall overcome some day.\n2) We will walk hand in hand some day.\n3) We are not afraid today.\n4) The truth shall make us free.\n5) We will live in peace some day.','',0,0,0,NULL),(40754,190,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the following lines :\n\n     i. The child asks -----------------------\n\n    ii. The wind if -----------------------------\n\n   iii. It is -------------------------------\nO you that are so strong and cold, \nO blower, are you young or old? \nAre you a beast of field and tree, \nOr just a stronger child than me?\nO wind, a-blowing all day long, \nO wind, that sings so loud a song!\n2) Complete the following web : ','3) Find out two pairs of rhyming words from the extract.\n \n    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','i) Young or old               ii) a beast of field and tree            iii) a stronger child than it.\n2) i) blowing all day long           ii) Sings a very loud song\n3) i) cold - old                ii) long -  song','',1,0,0,NULL),(40755,190,'descriptive','2b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Match the following :','Rise, brothers, rise; the wakening skies \npray to the morning light, \nThe wind lies asleep in the arms of the dawn \nlike a child that has cried all night.\n2) Find out lines from the extract that indicate sunrise.\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Find out the words that are related to time.\n\n   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','(i – b), (ii – c)\n2) The wakening skies pray to the morning light.\n3) morning, dawn, night','',1,0,0,NULL),(40756,190,'descriptive','3a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the following lines :\n\n     i. The child asks -----------------------\n\n    ii. The wind if -----------------------------\n\n   iii. It is -------------------------------\nO you that are so strong and cold, \nO blower, are you young or old? \nAre you a beast of field and tree, \nOr just a stronger child than me?\nO wind, a-blowing all day long, \nO wind, that sings so loud a song!\n2) Complete the following web : ','3) Find out two pairs of rhyming words from the extract.\n\n    --------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','i) Young or old               ii) a beast of field and tree            iii) a stronger child than it.\n2) i) blowing all day long           ii) Sings a very loud song\n3) i) cold - old                ii) long -  song','',1,0,0,NULL),(40757,190,'descriptive','3b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Match the following :','Rise, brothers, rise; the wakening skies \npray to the morning light, \nThe wind lies asleep in the arms of the dawn \nlike a child that has cried all night.\n2) Find out lines from the extract that indicate sunrise.\n\n    --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3) Find out the words that are related to time.\n\n    ------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','(i – b), (ii – c)\n2) The wakening skies pray to the morning light.\n3) morning, dawn, night','',1,0,0,NULL),(40758,710,'descriptive','3',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Do as directed ------------------------ 3 M\n     1) It is your pen. (Identify tense)\n     2) Fill in the blanks with the correct simple present tense form of the verbs given in the brackets :\n          The earth ------------- around the sun. (revolve) \n    3) He was not a coward (Add Question tag)\nB] Translate the following sentences into Marathi : ---------------------- 2M\n     1) All Indians are my brothers and sisters.\n    