 3462950 + 326578 = Rs. 3789528','',0,0,0,NULL),(40976,717,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','The forest Department planted 23078 trees of Khair, 19476 of behada besides trees of several other kinds. If the Department planted 50000 trees altogether, how many trees were neither of Khair nor of behada?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Total trees of Khair + Trees of behada = 23078 + 19476 = 42554\nOut of 50000 trees other trees are = 50000 – 42554 = 7446.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(40977,717,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','A city has a population of 3704926. If this includes 1124069 men and 1096478 women, what is the number of children in the city?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Total number of Men and Women = 1124069 + 1096478 = 2220547\nNumber of children = 3704926 – 2220547 = 1484379\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(40978,717,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','The management of a certain factory had 2540600 rupees in the labour welfare fund from this fund, 1237865 rupees were used for medical expenses, 842317 rupees were spent on the education of the worker’s children and the remaining was put a side for a canteen. How much money was put a side for the canteen?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Total money spent = 1237865 + 842317 = 2080182\nThe money was put aside for the canteen = 2540600 – 2080182 = 460418\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(40979,717,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','For a three-day cricket match 13608 tickets were sold on the first day and 8955 on the second day. If altogether, 36563 tickets were sold in three days, how many were sold on the third day?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Total sold tickets = 36563\nTicket sold on first day + Tickets sold on second day\n= 13608 + 8955 = 22563\nTickets sold on third day = 36563 – 22563 = 14000','',0,0,0,NULL),(40980,717,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','A city has a population of 4898197. If this includes 18245 men and 14324 women, what is the number of children in the city?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Total population of city = 4898197 \nTotal number of men and women = 18245 + 14324 = 32569\nTotal number of children = 4898197 – 32569 = 4865628','',0,0,0,NULL),(40981,717,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','The management of a certain factory had 5060700 rupees in the labour welfare fund from this fund 2438824 rupees were used for medical expenses, 982324 rupees were spent on the construction of houses and the remaining was put a side for a planting trees. How many was put aside for planting trees?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            ------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Total fund = Rs. 5060700\nManagement used fund f