e computer costs 27540 rupees. How much will 18 such computers cost?\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Cost of 18 computers = 27540 × 18 = Rs. 495720','',0,0,0,NULL),(41045,718,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','If a certain two-wheeler costs 53670 rupees. How much will 35 such two wheelers?\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The cost of 35 two wheelers = 53670 × 35 = 1878450','',0,0,0,NULL),(41046,718,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','One traveler incurs a cost of 7650 rupees for a certain journey. What will be the cost for 26 such traveler? \n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The cost of 26 traveler  = 7650 × 26 = 198900','',0,0,0,NULL),(41047,718,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Divide: 56741 ÷ 26\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','2182.34','',0,0,0,NULL),(41048,718,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','How many hours will it take travel 336 km at a speed of 48 km per hour?\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Total time taken = 336/48 = 7 hours','',0,0,0,NULL),(41049,718,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','The cost of one bag is 1750 rupees, what is the cost of such 56 bags?\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Total cost of 56 bags = 1750 × 56 = Rs. 98000','',0,0,0,NULL),(41050,718,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','The cost of one bicycle is 4500 rupees, what is the cost of such 16 bicycles?\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Total cost of 16 bicycles = 4500 × 16 = Rs. 72000','',0,0,0,NULL),(41051,718,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write multiplication for the 8985 and 324 numbers.\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             ----------------------------------------------------------------------','','','8985 × 324 = 2911140','',0,0,0,NULL),(41052,718,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Divide: 8546 ÷ 13\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','657.38','',0,0,0,NULL),(41053,718,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Divide: 3269 ÷ 35\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','93.4','',0,0,0,NULL),(41054,718,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Divide: 4326 ÷ 95\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','45.53','',0,0,0,NULL),(41055,718,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Divide: 8732 ÷ 85\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','102.729','',0,0,0,NULL),(41056,718,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply: 326 × 225\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             ----------------------------------------------------------------------','','','73350','',0,0,0,NULL),(41057,718,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply: 826 × 143\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             ----------------------------------------------------------------------','','','118118','',0,0,0,NULL),(41058,718,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply: 789 × 432\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             ----------------------------------------------------------------------','','','340848','',0,0,0,NULL),(41059,718,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply: i) 8975 × 8 		ii) 6985 × 3\n\nAns. : -------------------------------                -------------------------------------\n\n           -------------------------------               ------------------------------------\n\n             ------------------------------                ----------------------------------------','','','i) 71800		ii) 20955','',0,0,0,NULL),(41060,718,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply: i) 7324 × 8 		ii) 4323 × 8\n\nAns. : -------------------------------                -------------------------------------\n\n           -------------------------------               ------------------------------------\n\n             ------------------------------                ----------------------------------------','','','i) 58592		ii) 34584','',0,0,0,NULL),(41061,718,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Under the ‘Inspire Awards = Rs. 5000 rupees per students were granted for the purchase of science project materials. If 154 students in a certain taluka were covered under the scheme, find the total amount granted to that taluka.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             ----------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Total amount granted to that taluka = 5000 × 154 = Rs. 770000 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(41062,718,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','One hour has 3600 seconds. How many seconds do 365 hours have?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Number of seconds in 365 hours = 1314000','',0,0,0,NULL),(41063,718,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Frame a multiplication word problem with the numbers 5473 and 627 and solve it.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n              ------------------------------------------------------------------','','','5473 × 627 = 3431571','',0,0,0,NULL),(41064,718,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the product of the biggest three digit number and the biggest four-digit number.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n              ------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Three digit biggest number = 999, four digit biggest number = 9999\nThe product of 999 × 9999 = 9989001\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(41065,718,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Girija needed 35 cartoons a pack 1400 books. There are an equal number of books in every carton. How many books did she pack into each carton?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n              ------------------------------------------------------------------','','','1400 ÷ 35 = 40\n40 books she packed into each cartoon.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(41066,718,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','If 48 sheets are required for making one notebook how many notebooks at the most will 5880 sheets make and how many sheets will be left over?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n              ------------------------------------------------------------------','','','If we divide 5880 ÷ 48, quotient is 122 and remainder = 24\n∴ 24 sheets will be left over.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(41067,718,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','What will the quotient be when the smallest five-digit number is divided by the smallest four-digit number?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n              ------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The smallest five-digit number is 10000\nThe smallest four-digit number is 1000\n10000 ÷ 1000 = 10\n∴ The quotient will be 10.','',0,0,0,NULL),(41068,718,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','The 45 persons requires 9000 plants for cultivation. How much plant can be need by one person?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n              ------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Number of plant need by one person = 9000 ÷ 45 = 200','',0,0,0,NULL),(41069,718,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which number, on being multiplied by 29, gives a product 2581?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n              ------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Let the number multiplied by x\n∴ x × 29 = 2581        ⟹ x = 2581/29 = 89\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(41070,718,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','The 30 students takes the equipment’s of a cricket game for rupees 1350. What is the cost requires for each students.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n              ------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Cost required for each students = 1350/30 = Rs. 45','',0,0,0,NULL),(41071,718,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','One chair cost Rs. 450 what is the cost of such 87 chairs?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n              ------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Cost of 87 chairs = 87 × 450 = Rs. 39150','',0,0,0,NULL),(41072,718,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','One person requires 8250 rupees for a journey. How many rupees required by such 18 person.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n              ------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Money required to 18 person = 8250 × 18 = 148500','',0,0,0,NULL),(41073,718,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply: i) 4894 × 12 		ii) 43232 × 18 \n\nAns. : -----------------------------              --------------------------------------\n\n           -----------------------------              -------------------------------------\n\n              -----------------------------            -------------------------------------','','','i) 58728		ii) 778176','',0,0,0,NULL),(41074,718,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply: i) 5483 × 48 		ii) 6832 × 56\n\nAns. : -----------------------------              --------------------------------------\n\n           -----------------------------              -------------------------------------\n\n              -----------------------------            -------------------------------------','','','i) 263184		ii) 382592','',0,0,0,NULL),(41075,718,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply: i) 38943 × 85 		ii) 98754 × 89\n\nAns. : -----------------------------              --------------------------------------\n\n           -----------------------------              -------------------------------------\n\n              -----------------------------            -------------------------------------','','','i) 3310155		ii) 8789106','',0,0,0,NULL),(41076,718,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply: i) 32432 × 38 		ii) 34832 × 75\n\nAns. : -----------------------------              --------------------------------------\n\n           -----------------------------              -------------------------------------\n\n              -----------------------------            -------------------------------------','','','i) 1232416 		ii) 2612400','',0,0,0,NULL),(41077,718,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Multiply: i) 75698 × 68 		ii) 4324 × 895\n\nAns. : -----------------------------              --------------------------------------\n\n           -----------------------------              -------------------------------------\n\n              -----------------------------            -------------------------------------','','','i) 5147464		ii) 3869980','',0,0,0,NULL),(41078,718,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','The contribution for a picnic was 65 rupees each. Altogether, 2925 rupees were collected. How many had paid for the picnic?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             ----------------------------------------------------------------------','','','2925 ÷ 65 = 45\nThe 45 paid for the picnic.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(41079,718,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which number, on being multiplied by 56, gives a product of 9688?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             ----------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Let the number multiplied by x\n∴ x × 56 = 9688        ⟹ x = 9688/56 = 173\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(41080,718,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','From a total of 10000 rupees, Anna donated 7000 rupees to a school. The remaining amount was to be divided equally among students as the ‘all- round student’ prize. What was the amount of each prize?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             ----------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The total rupees = 10000, donated rupees = 7000\nRemaining rupees = 3000\nThe remaining amount was to be divided equally among six students\n∴ The prize for each student = Rs. 500','',0,0,0,NULL),(41081,718,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','An amount of 260 rupees each was collected from 50 students for a picnic. If 11450 rupees were spent for the picnic, what is the amount left over?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             ----------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The total amount collected from 50 students = 260 × 50 = Rs. 13000\nThe rupees spent for the picnic = Rs. 11450\nThe amount left over = 13000 – 11450 = 1550\n∴ The amount left over = Rs. 1550','',0,0,0,NULL),(41082,718,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','A shopkeeper bought a sack of 50 kg of sugar for 1750 rupees. As the price of sugar tell, he had to sell it at the rate of 32 rupees per kilo. How much less money did he get than he had spent?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             ----------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The cost of 50 kg sugar was sold at rate 32 rupees = 50 × 32 = Rs. 1600\n∴ The less amount got by him = 1750 – 1600 = Rs. 150\n∴ The less amount got by a shopkeeper = Rs. 150','',0,0,0,NULL),(41083,718,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','A shopkeeper bought 7 pressure cookers at the rate of 1870 rupees per cooker. He sold them all for a total of 14230 rupees. Did he get less or more money than he had spent?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             ----------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The cost of 7 cookers = 7 × 1870 = 13090\nHe sold all for a total of 14230 rupees. He got more money than he had spent\n= 14230 – 13090 = Rs. 1140\n∴ He got rupees 1140 more than he had spent.','',0,0,0,NULL),(41084,718,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Fourteen families in a society together bought 8 sacks of wheat, each weighing 98 kilos. If they shared all the wheat equally, what was the share of each family?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             ----------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The weight of 8 sacks = 98 × 8 = 784 kilo\nShare of each family = 784 ÷ 14 = 56\n∴ Each family share = 56 kilo.','',0,0,0,NULL),(41085,718,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','The capacity of an overhead water tank is 3000 liters. There are 16 families living in this building. If each family uses 225 liters every day, will the water be enough for all the families? If not, what will be the daily shortfall be?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             ----------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Total water used = 225 × 16 = 3600\n3600 liters water used by the families. \nTotal capacity = 3000 liter\nThe water is not enough for all the families = 3600 – 3000 = 600 liter','',0,0,0,NULL),(41086,718,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','An amount of 250 rupees each was collected from 75 students for a picnic 15750 rupees were spent for the picnic, what is the amount left over.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             ----------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Total amount collected = 250 × 75 = 18750\nAmount left over = 18750 – 15750 = Rs. 3000\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(41087,718,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','If the cost of 27 chairs is 17550 rupees what is the cost of one chair. If the person gives 20000 rupees to the shopkeeper how much will remains left behind?\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n             ----------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Cost of one chair = 17550 ÷ 27 = Rs. 650\nAmount left behind = 20000 – 17550 = Rs. 2450\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(41088,719,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','If 17/21 < */21, then * = ?\na) 18 		b) 15 		c) 17 		d) 16\n\nAns. : ----------------------------','','','a) 18 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(41089,719,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the fractions 1/3, 1/9, 1/5, 1/6 is the smallest?\na) 1/3		b) 1/9 		c) 1/5 		d) 1/6\n\nAns. : ----------------------------','','','b) 1/9 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(41090,719,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','If a = b = c = d, then which of the following fractions is the greatest?\na) a/7 		b) b/5 		c) c/9 		d) d/11\n\nAns. : ----------------------------','','','b) b/5 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(41091,719,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Put the appropriate sign in the box : 17/8 □ 23/6 \na) > 		b) < 		c) = 		d) 