nii) (6⁵)⁴ = 6²⁰\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(41733,729,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Simplify :   ','\nAns. : -----------------------------------              ------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------             ------------------------------------------------','','Answer :','',1,0,1,NULL),(41734,729,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Simplify :  ','\nAns. : -----------------------------------              ------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------             ------------------------------------------------','','Answer :','',1,0,1,NULL),(41735,729,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write in positive indices : i) (2/7)¯² 		ii) (11/3)¯⁵\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------              ------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------             ------------------------------------------------','','','i) (2/7)¯² = (7/2)²	\nii) (11/3)¯⁵ = (3/11)⁵\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(41736,729,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write in positive indices: i) (1/6)¯³ 		ii) (y)¯⁴\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------              ------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------             ------------------------------------------------','','','i) (1/6)¯³ = 6³\nii) (y)¯⁴ = 1/y⁴\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(41737,729,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the square root of 625\n\n\n\n','','','√625 = √25 × 25 = 25','',0,0,0,NULL),(41738,729,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the square root of 1225\n\n\n\n\n','','','√1225 = √35 × 35 = 35','',0,0,0,NULL),(41739,729,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the square root of 1089\n\n\n\n\n','','','√1089 = √33 × 33 = 33','',0,0,0,NULL),(41740,729,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the square root : 3025\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','√3025 = √55 × 55 = 55','',0,0,0,NULL),(41741,729,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Simplify :         ','\nAns. : -----------------------------------              ------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------             ------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------                -------------------------------------------------','','Answer :','',1,0,1,NULL),(41742,729,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the square root of 4096\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','√4096 = 64 × 64 = 64','',0,0,0,NULL),(41743,729,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the square root of 1681\n\n\n\n\n','','','√1681 = √41 × 41 = 41','',0,0,0,NULL),(41744,729,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the square root of 9801\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','√9801 = √99 × 99 = 99','',0,0,0,NULL),(41745,729,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Simplify : i)  2 × 10³ 		ii) 7² × 2²\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------              ------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------             ------------------------------------------------','','','i) 2 × 10³ = 2 × 1000 = 2000\nii) 7² × 2² = 49 × 4 = 196\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(41746,729,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Simplify : i) 2³ × 5 		ii) 3 × 4⁴\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------              ------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------             ------------------------------------------------','','','i) 2³ × 5 = 8 × 5 = 40\nii) 3 × 4⁴ = 3 × 256 = 768\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(41747,729,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Express each of the following numbers in exponential notation: i) 512 	ii) 343\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------              ------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------             ------------------------------------------------','','','i) 512 = 8 × 8 × 8 = 8³\nii) 343 = 7 × 7 × 7 = 7³\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(41748,729,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Express each of the following numbers in exponential notation: i) 729 	ii) 3125\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------              ------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------             ------------------------------------------------','','','i) 729 = 9 × 9 × 9 = 9³\nii) 3125 = 5 × 5 × 5 × 5 × 5 = 5⁵\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(41749,729,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Identify greater number : i) 4³ or 3⁴ 	ii) 5³ or 3⁵\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------              ------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------             ------------------------------------------------','','','i) 4³ = 64 and 3⁴ = 81\n∴ 4³ < 3⁴\nii) 5³ = 125  and 3⁵ = 243\n∴ 5³ < 3⁵','',0,0,0,NULL),(41750,729,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Using laws of exponents, simplify and write answer in exponential form: i) 3² × 3⁴ × 3⁸ 		ii) (2²⁰ ÷ 2¹⁵) × 2³\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------              ------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------             ------------------------------------------------','','','i)  3² × 3⁴ × 3⁸ = 3¹⁴\nii) (2²⁰ ÷ 2¹⁵) × 2³ = 2⁵ × 2³ = 2⁸\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(41751,729,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the square root of 19321\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','√19321 = √139 × 139 = 139','',0,0,0,NULL),(41752,729,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the square root of 141.61\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','√141.61 = √11.9 × 11.9 = 11.9','',0,0,0,NULL),(41753,729,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the square root of 4225\n\n\n\n\n','','','√4225 = √65 × 65 = 65','',0,0,0,NULL),(41754,729,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find the square root of 1369\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','√1369 = √37 × 37 = 37','',0,0,0,NULL),(41755,729,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write the following sentences with the help of indices of 10.\na) The diameter of sun is 1400000000 m\nb) The velocity of light is 300000000 m/sec\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------ ------------------------------------------------','','','a) 1400000000 = 1.4 × 10⁹ m\nb) 300000000 = 3 × 10⁸ m/sec\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(41756,729,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Compare the following : i) 2.7 × 10¹² ; 1.5 × 10⁸ 		ii) 4 × 10¹⁴ ; 3 × 10¹⁷\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------              ------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------             ------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------             -------------------------------------------------','','','i) 2.7 × 10¹² ; 1.5 × 10⁸\n2.7 × 10¹² = 27 × 10¹¹ = 27000 × 10⁸ and 1.5 × 10⁸\n27000 > 1.5\n∴ 2.7 × 10¹² > 1.5 × 10⁸\nii) 4 × 10¹⁴ ; 3 × 10¹⁷\n3 × 10¹⁷ = 3000 × 10¹⁴\n∴ 4 × 10¹⁴ < 3 × 10¹⁷','',0,0,0,NULL),(41757,729,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','If [5⁹ × 5³] ÷ [5¹⁵ ÷ 5³] = 5ᵐ then find the value of m.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------ ------------------------------------------------','','','[5⁹ × 5³] ÷ [5¹⁵ ÷ 5³] = 5ᵐ\n5¹² ÷ 5¹² = 5ᵐ\n5⁰ = 5ᵐ\n∴ m = 0','',0,0,0,NULL),(41758,729,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Express the following as power of rational number : i) 16/81 		ii) -32/3125','\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------ ------------------------------------------------\n\n            -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','Answer :','',0,0,1,NULL),(41759,729,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Simplify : i) (-3)² × (-5)² 	ii) (-2)³ × (-10)³\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ------------------------------------ ------------------------------------------------','','','i) (-3)² × (-5)² = 9 × 25 = 225\nii) (-2)³ × (-10)³ = -8 × (-1000) = 8000\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(41760,730,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The point of intersection of X and Y axis called as -----\na) X- axis 		b) Y – axis 		c) Origin 		d) can’t say\n\nAns. : --------------------------------','','','c) Origin 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(41761,730,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In a graph, vertical line is called as ------\na) X- axis 		b) Y – axis 		c) Origin 		d) can’t say\n\nAns. : --------------------------------','','','b) Y – axis ','',0,0,0,NULL),(41762,730,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In a graph, horizontal line is called as -----\na) X- axis 		b) Y – axis 		c) Origin 		d) can’t say\n\nAns. : --------------------------------','','','a) X- axis ','',0,0,0,NULL),(41763,730,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In a graph, X- axis and Y-axis intersect at ------\na) right angle 	      b) acute angle 	         c) obtuse angle 	d) none of these\n\nAns. : --------------------------------','','','a) right angle 	 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(41764,730,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The given graph shows the number of pupils who participated in the fitness test on different days of the week. What percentage of the total number of pupils has their fitness test on Wednesday? ','\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','Total number of students = 40 + 90 + 120 + 80 + 150 = 480\nPercentage of pupils has their fitness test on Wednesday\n= (120/480) × 100 = 25%','',1,0,0,NULL),(41765,730,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Define joint bar graph\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','In a joint bar graph, the bars representing the given information are joined together.','',0,0,0,NULL),(41766,730,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','How many more boys like Cricket and Hockey together than girls?','\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','Number of boys like Cricket and Hockey = 20 + 14 = 34\nNumber of girls like Cricket and Hockey = 14 + 10 = 24\n10 boys more than girls like Cricket and Hockey together.','',1,0,0,NULL),(41767,730,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write proper word : In a joint bar graph, the width of all columns should be equal/unequal.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------','','','equal','',0,0,0,NULL),(41768,730,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write proper word :  The distance between any two consecutive sets of joint bars should be equal/unequal.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------','','','equal','',0,0,0,NULL),(41769,730,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Observe the graphs alongside and answer the following questions: ','a) In which year did they both produce equal quantities of wheat?\n\n     -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nb) In year 2014, who produced more wheat?\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nc) In year 2013, how much wheat did Ajay and  Vijay each produce?\n\n    -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','a) They both produced equal quantities of wheat in the year 2011\nb) Ajay produced more wheat in the year 2014\nc) In the year 2013, Ajay produced 40 quintals of wheat and Vijay produced 30 quintal of wheat.  ','',1,0,0,NULL),(41770,730,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','The bar graph given below shows the interest of boys and girls in different activities. Answer the following questions: a) In which two activities, 55 girls are interested together? 		b) How many less boys are interested in yoga, dance and art altogether than girls?','\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -------------------------------------------------------------------------','','a) Dance = 35 and Yoga = 20\nDance + Yoga = 35 + 20 = 55\nb) Number of boys in Yoga, dance and art = 20 + 25 + 10 = 55\nNumber of girls in Yoga, dance and art = 20 + 35 + 15 = 70\nNumber of girls more than boys = 70 – 55 = 15','',1,0,0,NULL),(41771,730,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','The given bar graph shows the buyers of DVDs and CDs. Study the graph and answer the following questions : \na) In which music category the differences between DVD buyers and CD buyers is minimum? 		\nb) What is the ratio of Pop music CD buyers to Jazz music DVD buyers?','\nAns. : -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------','','a) Pop\nb) 55 : 80 = 11/16 \n','',1,0,0,NULL),(41772,730,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','The means of transportation used by children in a school is given below. Draw a joint bar graph.','\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(41773,730,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Marks obtained by a student in both terms for different subjects is given below. draw a joint bar graph.','\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(41774,730,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','The number of trees planted by students of different division of seventh standard is given below. Draw a joint bar graph.','\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(41775,730,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the graph and answer the question below:','a) What data is shown on X – axis? \n\n      ------------------------------------------------------------------\nb) What data is shown on Y – axis?\n\n       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nc) On which day had the highest temperature?\n\n     ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nd) On which day is the minimum temperature the highest?\n\n     ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\ne) On Thursday, what is the difference between the minimum and maximum temperature?\n\n     ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nf) On which day is the difference between the minimum and maximum temperature the greatest? \n\n    --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','a) Days are shown on the X-axis\nb) Temperature is shown on the Y-axis\nc) The highest temperature was Monday.\nd) The minimum temperature was highest on Wednesday.\ne) The difference between the minimum and maximum temperature on Thursday is (29.5 – 15) = 14.5⁰C\nf) The difference between the minimum and maximum temperature is greatest on Thursday.','',1,0,0,NULL),(41776,730,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','The number of boys and girls in a school is given. Draw a joint bar graph to show this information.','\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(41777,730,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','The number of sapling planted by schools on WORLD Tree Day is given in the table below. Draw a joint bar graph to show these figures.\n','\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(41778,730,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','The percentage of literate people in the states of Maharashtra and Gujrat are given below. Draw a joint bar graph for this data.','\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(41779,730,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','The number of Men and Women participated in Swatch Bharat Abhiyan in different districts given below. Draw a joint bar graph.','\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(41780,730,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','The table below shows the number of people who had the different juices at a juice bar on a Saturday and a Sunday. Draw a joint bar graph for this data.','\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(41781,730,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','The following numbers of votes were cast at 5 polling booths during the Gram Panchayat elections. Draw a joint bar graph for this data.','\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(41782,730,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','The maximum and minimum temperatures of five Indian cities are given in ⁰C. Draw a joint bar graph for this data.','\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(41783,730,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','The numbers of children vaccinated in one day at the government hospitals in Solapur and Pune are given in the table. Draw a joint bar graph for this data.','\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Student can draw joint bar graph from given information.','',1,0,0,NULL),(41784