25 min – 1 hour 55 min\n\n\n\n\n','','','     Hrs            Min\n      3                60 + 25\n -   1                55\n----------------------\n        2             30\ni. e.  2 hrs 30 minutes ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49237,822,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Subtract : 6 hours 15 min – 2 hours 45 min\n\n\n\n\n','','','    Hrs            Min\n      5                60 + 15\n -   2                45\n----------------------\n        3             30\ni. e.  3 hrs 30 minutes ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49238,822,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Add : 2 hours 15 min + 6 hours 50 min\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','      Hrs            Min\n      2                15\n +   6                50\n----------------------\n        8             65\ni. e.  9             05\n9 hrs 05 minutes ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49239,822,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Subtract : 6 hours 20 min – 4 hours 45 min\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','     Hrs            Min\n      5                60 + 20\n -   4                45\n----------------------\n        1             35\ni. e.  1 hrs 35 minutes ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49240,822,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','If a bus that leaves Nashik at 5 o’clock in the morning reaches Pune that same day at ten thirty in the morning, how long does the journey take?\n\n\n\n\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------','','','The bus leaves at 5 o’clock in the morning. The bus reaches at 10.30 in the morning.\n    10.30\n-  05.00\n-------------\n    05.30\nIt takes 5.30 time to reach the Pune.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49241,822,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','A play, that was to start at nine fifteen at night, was delayed by half an hour because of a power failure. What time did the play start?\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------','','','9.15 PM a play start but by problem a power outage it starts by half an hour. i.e. 30 min late\n     9.15\n +  0.30\n------------\n    9.45\nThe play starts at 9.45 PM.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49242,822,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','A government office opens at 7 in the morning and closes at 3 in the afternoon. how long is this office open?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','Opens at 7 Am\nCloses at 3 PM\n     15.00\n  -  07.00\n  ------------\n     8.00\nThe office opens for 8 hours.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49243,822,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','A movie starts at 45 minutes past 3 in the afternoon and finishes two and a half hour later. At what time does the movie end?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','Movie starts at 3 : 45 in the afternoon ends at 2 : 50 hour later.\n      Hrs            Min\n      3                45\n +   2                30\n----------------------\n        5             75\ni. e.  6 hrs 15 minutes \nThe movie ends at 6 : 15 hours','',0,0,0,NULL),(49244,822,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','Sakharam ploughed the field from 8 in the morning till 12 : 30 in the afternoon. he stopped and started for home. He reached home at 1 : 30 for lunch. How long did he plough the field? How long did it take him to reach home from the field?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','The ploughing started at 8 in the morning stopped at 12 : 30 in the afternoon\nReached at 1 : 30 = 13 : 30\n     12 : 30\n-    08 : 00\n-------------------\n     4 : 30\nHe ploughed for 4 hours and 30 minutes\n      13 : 30\n   -  12 : 30\n   ---------------\n       01 : 00\nIt takes one hour to reach home from the field. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49245,822,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','Rambhau started the water pump at ten thirty at night and put it off the same night at a quarter to twelve. How long did he keep the water pump on?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','Started the water pump at 10 : 30 at night 22 : 30 at a quarter twelve\n        = 11.45 = 23.45\n       Hrs            Min\n       23                45\n -    22                30\n----------------------\n        1             15\ni. e.  1 hrs 15 minutes \nThe water give for 1 : 15 hours ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49246,822,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','If Abdul started working on the computer at 11 in the morning and finished his work at 3:30 in the afternoon, how long did he work?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','Started working 11 in the morning = 11 : 00\nFinished 3 : 30 in the afternoon = 15 : 30\n         Hrs            Min\n           15             30\n -         11              00\n----------------------\n             4             30\ni. e.  4 hrs 30 minutes  ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49247,822,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Amruta travelled by bus for 3 hours 40 minutes and by motorcycle for 1 hour 45 minutes. How long did she spend travelling?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','Amruta total travelled by bus and by motorcycle is\n       Hrs            Min\n         3                40\n +     1                45\n----------------------\n        4             85\ni. e.  5 hrs 25 minutes ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49248,822,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','',' If a train leaves Mumbai at ten fifteen at night and reaches Nagpur at one forty the next afternoon, how long does the journey take?\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------','','','The time from ten fifteen at night to ten fifteen in the morning next day = 12 hours\nThe time from ten fifteen in the morning to one fifteen in the afternoon = 3 hours\nThe time from one fifteen to one forty = (40 – 15) min = 25 min\nThe total time = 12 hours + 3 hours + 25 minutes\n               = 15 hours 25 minutes\nThe journey takes 15 hours 25 minutes.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49249,822,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','Match the following :','','','(i – d), (ii – c), (iii – e), (iv – a), (v – b)','',1,0,0,NULL),(49250,822,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','Geeta taught in the classroom for 2 hours and 25 minutes in the morning and 1 hour and 45 minutes in the afternoon. How long did she teach in all?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','Add to find the total time\n      Hrs            Min\n      2                25\n +   1                45\n----------------------\n        3             70\ni. e.  4 hrs 10 minutes\nGeeta taught for 4 hours 10 minutes. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49251,822,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','If a bank is open for business from 10 in the morning till 4 : 30 in the evening, how long is it open?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','According to 24-hour clock, 4 : 30 in the evening means 16 : 30\nHere, subtract 10 : 00 from 16 : 30.\n     Hrs            Min\n      16              30\n -    10               00\n----------------------\n        6             30\ni. e.  6 hrs 30 minutes  \nThe bank remains open for 6 hours 30 minutes.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49252,822,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','If a shop is open from 9 : 30 am to 10 pm, how long is it open?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','According to 24-hour clock, 10 pm means 22 : 00\nHere, we subtract 9 : 30 from 22 : 00\n         Hrs            Min\n          21               60\n -        9                30\n----------------------\n        12             30\ni. e.  12 hrs 30 minutes \nthe shop is open for 12 hours 30 minutes.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49253,822,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','If the Maharashtra Express leaving Kolhapur at 15 : 30 arrives at Gondiya the next day at 20 : 15, how long is the journey from Kolhapur to Gondiya?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','If leaves Kolhapur at 15 : 30 arrives at Gondia at 20 : 15 the next day\n        Hrs      Min               Hrs          Min           Hrs           Min\n         24        00                 8              30              20             15\n   -     15        30            +  20             15          -   00            00\n    -----------------               ------------------           ------------------\n          8         30                   28          45                 20           15\nIt requires 35 hours 45 min to reach from Kolhapur to Gondia.     ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49254,822,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Geeta travelled by train for 2 hours 20 minutes and by rickshaw for 4 hours 40 minutes. How long did she spend travelling?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','Total time spend to Geeta by train and by rikshaw is \n          Hrs            Min\n           2               20\n +       4                40 \n----------------------\n          6               60\ni. e.  7 hrs 00 minutes   	','',0,0,0,NULL),(49255,823,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','How will you write, 12 m 3 mm in decimal form?\na) 12.03 m		b) 12.003 m		c) 12.3 m 		d) 12.0003 m\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------','','','b) 12.003 m	','',0,0,0,NULL),(49256,823,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','A rikshaw covers 30 km in 1 hour. How far will it travel in three-quarters of an hour at the same speed?\na) 1500 m 		b) 15000 m 		c) 22500 m 		d) 2500 m\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------','','','c) 22500 m 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(49257,823,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','If there are in all 1002 trees on both the sides of a road at a distance of 12 m each, what is the length of the road?\na) 500 m 		b) 6 km 		c) 60 m 		d) 12 km \n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------','','','b) 6 km ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49258,823,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Sam travelled 25 km on bicycle, 220 km by train and 175 km by bus. How many more km did he travel by train than on bicycle and bus together?\na) 20 km 		b) 70 km 		c) 25 km 		d) 45 km\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------','','','a) 20 km 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(49259,823,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','42000 millimeters long wire is cut equally at 6 places. Find the length of each piece of wire.\na) 700 mm 		b) 600 mm 		c) 7 m 		d) 6 m\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------','','','d) 6 m','',0,0,0,NULL),(49260,823,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','30 m long rope cut at 5 places. What will be the length of 2 pieces?\na) 6 m 		b) 10 m 		c) 5 m 		d) 18 m\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------','','','b) 10 m','',0,0,0,NULL),(49261,823,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','24 cm 2 mm – 8 cm 8 mm = ?\na) 16 cm 		b) 164 mm 		c) 15 cm 		d) 154 mm\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------','','','d) 154 mm','',0,0,0,NULL),(49262,823,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Sayali covered a distance of 4 km in 10 minutes. How much distance will she cover in one minute?\na) 4/10 m 		b) 800 m 		c) 400 m 		d) 40 m\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------','','','c) 400 m 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(49263,823,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','10 kg 10 g = how many kg?\na) 10.10 		b) 10.01 		c) 10.001 		d) 10.100\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------','','','b) 10.01 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(49264,823,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Out of 17 kg of sugar, 50 persons each were given 300 g of sugar. How much sugar remained?\na) 300 g 		b) 100 g 		c) 2 kg 		d) 2.3 kg\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------','','','c) 2 kg ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49265,823,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','40 kg – 750 g = how many kg?\na) 390250 		b) 39.250 		c) 39.50 		d) 40.75\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------','','','b) 39.250 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(49266,823,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','360 grams make how many kilograms?\na) 360 		b) 36 		c) 0.360 		d) 0.036\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------','','','c) 0.360 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(49267,823,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','A sack contains 48 kg of rice. How many such sacks are required to fill 11040 kg of rice?\na) 230 			b) 460 		c) 320 		d) 640\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------','','','a) 230 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(49268,823,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','0.09 kg + 0.5 g – 120 mg = ?\na) 93.38 mg 			b) 93.38 g 		c) 90.38 mg 		d) 90.38 g\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------','','','d) 90.38 g','',0,0,0,NULL),(49269,823,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','One marble weigh 75 grams. What is the total weight of 600 such marbles?\na) 4.5 kg 		b) 45 kg 		c) 0.45 kg 		d) 48 kg\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------','','','b) 45 kg 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(49270,823,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Add : 13 km 590 m + 28 km 725 m\n\n\n\n\n','','','        Km             m\n        13              590\n   +   28              725\n  ----------------------------\n       41                1315\n    i.e. 42 km 315 m  [1000 m = 1 km]','',0,0,0,NULL),(49271,823,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Subtract : 37 liter 500 ml – 15 liter 750 ml\n\n\n\n\n','','','        lit                ml\n        36              1000 + 500\n   -   15                750\n     --------------------------\n      21              750\ni.e. 21 lit 750 ml','',0,0,0,NULL),(49272,823,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Add : Rs. 9 p 50 + Rs. 14 p 60\n\n\n\n\n','','','        Rs           P\n         9            50\n    +  14           60\n   -------------------\n       23           110\n  i.e. Rs. 24 paise 10  [100 paise = 1 Rs.]','',0,0,0,NULL),(49273,823,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Add : 6 cm 5 mm + 7 cm 9 mm\n\n\n\n\n','','','       Cm            mm\n        6                 5\n  +   7             9\n  ---------------------\n      13          14\ni.e. 14 cm 4 mm     [10 mm = 1 cm]','',0,0,0,NULL),(49274,823,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Subtract : Rs. 19 p 50 – Rs. 12 p 60\n\n\n\n\n','','','         Rs              P\n        18               100 + 50\n    -    12                 60\n    ----------------------------\n         6                  90\ni.e. Rs. 6 P 90','',0,0,0,NULL),(49275,823,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Subtract : 24 cm 2 mm – 3 cm 8 mm\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','          Cm             mm\n          23             10 + 2\n      -   3                8\n -------------------------------\n        20                4\ni.e. 20 cm 4 mm','',0,0,0,NULL),(49276,823,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Subtract : 20 m 30 cm – 17 m 60 cm\n\n\n\n\n','','','        M               cm\n        19               100 + 30\n   -    17                60\n    ------------------------------\n        2                  70\ni.e. 2 m 70 cm','',0,0,0,NULL),(49277,823,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The rate of toor dal is Rs. 90 per kg. What is the cost of 3 kg of toor dal?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------','','','Rate of 1 kg toor dal is ₹ 90\n∴ Cost of 3 kg toor dal = 3 × 90 = ₹ 270\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49278,823,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','How many rupees in all are Rs. 11 p 50 and Rs. 8 p 50?\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','       Rs             P\n       11           50\n   +   8             50\n  ------------------------\n       19            100\ni.e. 20 Rupees     [100 paise = 1 Rs.]','',0,0,0,NULL),(49279,823,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','3 m 25 cm of cloth is needed to make 1 dress. How much cloth is needed for 3 such dresses?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------','','','3 m 25 cm of cloth is needed to make 1 dress.\n∴ Cloth need to 3 such dresses = 3 × 3.25 = 9.75 = 9 m 75 cm\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49280,823,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Add : 22 m 50 cm + 25 m 75 cm\n\n\n\n\n','','','       M             cm\n       22             50\n  +   25             75\n  ------------------------\n      47             125\ni.e. 48 m 25 cm','',0,0,0,NULL),(49281,823,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Add : 15 km 740 m + 13 km 950 m\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','        Km           m\n        15           740\n   +   13            950\n   -------------------------\n       28           1690\ni.e. 29 Km 690 m','',0,0,0,NULL),(49282,823,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Add : 25 kg 650 g + 29 kg 770 g\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','        Kg               g\n       25             650\n   +  29             770\n  -------------------------\n       54             1420\ni.e. 55 kg 420 g','',0,0,0,NULL),(49283,823,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Add : 19 liter 840 ml + 25 liter 250 ml\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','        lit           ml\n       19           840\n   +  25           250\n   -----------------------\n       44           1090\ni.e. 45 lit 90 ml','',0,0,0,NULL),(49284,823,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Subtract : 40 km 255 m – 17 km 960 m\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','        Km           m\n       39           1000 + 255\n  -    17            960\n    ------------------------\n       22           265\ni.e. 22 km 265 m','',0,0,0,NULL),(49285,823,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Subtract : 35 kg 150 g – 26 kg 470 g\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','        Kg            g\n       34          1000 + 150\n  -    26        470\n----------------------\n      8          680\ni.e. 8 kg 680 g','',0,0,0,NULL),(49286,823,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Subtract : 46 liter 200 ml – 38 liter 750 ml\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','       lit          ml\n       45         1000 + 200\n   -   38          750\n    --------------------------\n       7            450\ni.e. 7 lit 450 ml','',0,0,0,NULL),(49287,823,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','If half a liter of milk costs Rs. 22, how much will 7 liters cost?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------','','','Half a liter of milk costs Rs. 22\n∴ 1 liter milk cost = ₹ 44\n∴ 7 liters milk costs = 7 × 44 = ₹ 308','',0,0,0,NULL),(49288,823,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','How much distance does a bus cover in 4 hours at the speed of 50 km/h?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------','','','Speed of bus is 50 km/hr\n∴ Distance covered by bus in 4 hours = 4 × 50 = 200 km/hrs\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49289,823,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','If the cost of half a liter of milk is Rs. 25, what will 1 liter of milk cost?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------','','','Cost of half liter milk = ₹ 25\n∴ Cost of 1 liter milk = 2 × 25 = ₹ 50\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49290,823,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','If a shopkeeper has 150 kg 500 g of rice and sells 75 kg 750 g, how much rice will be left?\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','Rice will be left :\n          Kg          g\n         149        1000 + 500\n   -      75          750\n       ---------------------------\n          74       750\ni.e. 74 kg 750 gm rice will be left.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49291,823,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','A can of milk has 20 l 450ml of milk. Another can has 18 l 800ml. How much milk is there in the two cans altogether?\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','         lit            ml\n         20          450\n    +   18           800\n        -------------------\n           38         1250\ni.e. 39 lit 250 ml milk in the two can altogether. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49292,823,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','At a speed of 90 km per hour, what distance will a train cover in two and a half hours?  \n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------','','','Speed of train in 1 hour = 90 km\n∴ Distance covered by train in 2.5 hours = 2.5 × 90 = 225 km \n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49293,823,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','If one dress requires 3 m 25 cm of cloth, how much do 4 dresses need?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------','','','One dress requires 3 m 25 cm of cloth\n∴ 4 dresses requires cloth = 4 × 3.25 = 13 m cloth\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49294,823,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','If a wire that is 9 m 50 cm long is cut into pieces of 5 cm each, how many pieces will be made?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------','','','Length of wire = 9 m 50 cm \n∴ Length of wire = 900 + 50 = 950 cm   [100 cm = 1 m]\n∴ No. of pieces having length 5 cm each = 950/5 = 190','',0,0,0,NULL),(49295,823,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','On his birthday, Ajay gave 20 liter 450 ml of milk to the children in an Ashramshala and 28 liter 800 ml of milk to the children in an orphanage. How much milk did Ajay distribute?\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','     lit    ml\n     20   450\n +  28    800\n  --------------\n     48      1250\ni.e. 19 lit 250 ml\nAjay donated 49 lit 250 ml milk to Ashramshala.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49296,823,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','Under the Rural Cleanliness Mission, college students cleaned 1 km 750 m of village road that is 2 km 575 m long. How much road remained to be cleaned?\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','        Km          m\n         1            1000 + 575\n    -    1              750\n      ------------------------\n           0            825\ni.e. 0 km 825 m','',0,0,0,NULL),(49297,823,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','Babulgaon used 21250 liters of treated waste water in the fields. Samvatsar village used 31350 liters of similar water. How much treated waste water was used in all in the fields?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------','','','Babhulgaon used waste water = 21,250 lit\nSamvatsar used waste water = 31,350 lit\nTotal water used = 21250 + 31350 = 52,600 lit\n∴ Total waste water used = 52,600 lit','',0,0,0,NULL),(49298,823,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','If the speed of a motorcycle is 40 km per hour, how far will it travel in an hour and a quarter?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------','','','An hour and a quarter = 1 + 1/4 hrs\nFor one hour 40 km and 1/4 h = 10 Km\n∴ Total travel = 40 + 10 = 50 Km\nThe motorcycle travels 46 km in an hour and a quarter. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49299,823,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','If a man walks at a speed of 4 km/h, how long will it take him to walk 3 km?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------','','','The speed is 4 km/h\n∴ It takes 1 hour to walk 4 Km\n∴ To walk 3 Km, it takes = 3/4 hours = 45 min\n∴ The man takes 45 min.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49300,823,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','If a rickshaw travels at a speed of 30 kmph, how far will it travel in three quarters of an hour?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------','','','Three quarter = 3/4 hours\n∴ 30 × 3/4 = 90/4 = 22 Km 500 m\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49301,823,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','If one shirts needs 2 m 50 cm of cloth, how much cloth do 5 shirts need?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------','','','One shirt need 2 m 50 cm of cloth\n∴ 5 shirts needs = 2.50 × 5 = 12.50\n∴ 5 shirts needs 12 m 50 cm cloths. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49302,823,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','If one gold bangle is made from 12 grams 250 milligrams of gold, how much gold will be needed to make 8 such bangles?\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','         Grams     milligrams\n          12              250\n           ×               8\n      -------------------------\n            98           000\nSuch 8 bangles needs 98 gm of gold.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49303,823,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','How many pouches each of 20 gm of cloves can be made from 1 kg 240 g of cloves.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------','','','1 cloves made by 1 kg 240 g = 1240 gm \n∴ 20 cloves made by = 1240/20 = 62 Pouches \n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49304,823,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','Seema’s mother bought 2 m 70 cm of cloth for a kurta and 2 m 40 cm for a shirt. How much cloth did she buy in all?\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','           m       cm\n            2         70\n      +     2        40\n        --------------------\n              5         10\nShe bought 5 m 10 cm cloth.        ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49305,823,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','During a cleanliness week, children cleaned the public park in their town. They collected three-quarter kilogram of plastic bags and five and a half kilograms of other garbage. How much garbage did they collect in all?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------','','','Total garbage collection = 0.750 gm plastic bags + 5 kg 500 gm other garbage \n∴ Total garbage = 6 kg 250 gm\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49306,823,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','If a car travels 60 km in an hour, how far will it travel in (a) 2 hours		(b) 15 minutes 		(c) half an hour 		(d) three and a half hours?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------','','','a) Speed of car is 60 km per hour\n∴ distance covered by car in 2 hours = 2 × 60 = 120 km\nb) 15 min = 1/4 hours \n∴ Distance covered by car in 15 min = 60 × 1/4 = 15 km\nc) half an hour = 30 min\n∴ Distance covered by a car in 30 min = 60/2 = 30 km\nd) three and half hour = 3.50\n∴ Distance covered by a car in 3 hrs 30 min = 60 × 3.50 = 210 km','',0,0,0,NULL),(49307,823,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','A water tank holds 125 liter of water. If 97 liter 500 ml of water is used, how much water remains in the tank?\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','        lit           ml\n       124         1000\n   -    97            500\n    --------------------------\n        27           500\n∴ 27 lit 500 ml water remains in the tank.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49308,823,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','Harminder bought 57 kg 500 g of wheat from one shop and 36 kg 800 g of wheat from another shop. How much wheat did he buy altogether?\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','       Kg             gm\n        57             500\n  +    36              800\n     -------------------------\n        94               300\nHe bought 94 kg 300 g wheat altogether. ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49309,823,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','Renu took part in a 100 m race. She tripped and fell down after running 80 m 50 cm. How much distance did she have left to run?\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','        m          cm\n        99          100\n    -   80           50\n     --------------------\n         19         50\nShe left 19 m 50 cm to run','',0,0,0,NULL),(49310,823,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','A sack had 40 kg 300 grams of vegetables. There were 17 kg 700 gram of potatoes, 13 kg 400 gram of cabbage and the rest were onions. What was the weight of onions?\n\n\n\n\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------','','','Weight of potatoes + cabbage = 17 kg 700 gm + 13 kg 400 gm \n                  = 31 kg 100 gm\nTotal weight of sack = 40 kg 300 gm\n∴ Weight of onion \n           Kg                gm\n           40               300\n      -     31               100\n       ---------------------------\n             9              200\n∴ The weight of the onion is 9 kg 200 gm.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49311,823,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','One day, Gurminder Singh walked 3 km 750 m and Parmindar Singh walked 2 km 825 m. Who walked farther and by how much?\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','        Km           m\n        2              1000 + 750\n    -   2                825\n     --------------------------\n          0              925\nGurminder Singh walked more distance by 925 m','',0,0,0,NULL),(49312,823,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','Suresh bought 3 kg 250 gram of tomatoes, 2 kg 500 gram of peas and 1 kg 750 g of cauliflower. How much was the total weight of the vegetables he bought? \n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','       kg               gm\n         3                250\n   +    2                500\n   +    1                750\n  --------------------------\n       7                500\nHe bought total weight of the vegetables are 7 kg 500 gm.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49313,823,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','The distance of some places from Akola are given below. use them to make word problems and solve the problems : Amravati – 95 km, Bhusawal – 154 km, Nagpur – 249 km, Jalgaon – 181 km.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------','','','1) Which distance is more? Akola to Bhusawal or Akola to Nagpur? How much more?\n2) Which distance is less? Bhusawal to Akola or Amravati to Akola? How much less?\nSolution : 1) Suppose distance from Akola is 0 Km\nThe distance between Akola to Bhusawal = 95 – 0 = 95 km\nThe distance between Akola and Nagpur = 249 – 0 = 249 km\nThe difference between the distance = 249 – 95 = 154 km\n2) The distance between Bhusawal and Akola = 154 – 0 = 154 km\nThe distance between Amravati and Akola = 95 – 0 = 95 \nThe distance between Amravati and Akola is less than the distance between Bhusawal and Akola = 154 – 95 = 59 km','',0,0,0,NULL),(49314,823,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','Complete the following table and prepare the total bill :','','','Answer : ','',1,0,1,NULL),(49315,823,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','A sack has capacity to collect the vegetables is 75 kg 250 g, if it contains 15 kg 500 g potatoes, 10 kg 250 g tomatoes and 20 kg 750 g chillis in it. What quantity of other vegetables if has?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------','','','Total vegetables : 15.50 kg + 10.250 kg + 20.750 kg = 46.500 \n       Total weight of vegetables = 46 kg 500 gm\n      Quantity of other vegetables in the sack = 75.250 – 46.500 = 28.750\n                     = 28 kg 750 gm','',0,0,0,NULL),(49316,823,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','The capacity of one petrol tank is 50 lit 250 ml and other tank is 24 lit 750 ml. What is total capacity of the tank?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','','Total Capacity of tank : \n           Lit          ml\n          50           250\n    +    24          750\n    ---------------------------\n         74           1000\ni.e. 75 lit 00 ml          [1000 ml = 1 lit]','',0,0,0,NULL),(49317,824,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The sides of a triangle are 5 cm, 6 cm and 7 cm. What is its perimeter?\na) 18 cm 		b) 13 cm 		c) 11 cm 		d) 12 cm\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------\n','','','a) 18 cm','',0,0,0,NULL),(49318,824,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is the perimeter of a square having length of the side 6 cm?\na) 6 cm 		b) 12 cm 		c) 24 cm 		d) 30 cm\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------\n','','','c) 24 cm 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(49319,824,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The perimeter of a square and a rectangle are equal. If the perimeter of the rectangle is 80 cm, what is the length of the side of the square?\na) 80 cm 		b) 40 cm 		c) 20 cm 		d) 10 cm\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------','','','c) 20 cm 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(49320,824,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The perimeter of a rectangle is 60 cm. If its breadth is 10 cm, then what will be its length?\na) 10 cm 		b) 20 cm 		c) 30 cm 		d) 50 cm\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------','','','b) 20 cm ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49321,824,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','If two rectangles having length 13 cm and breadth 5 cm are joined at the breadth, what is the perimeter of the new figure formed?\na) 67 cm 		b) 130 cm 		c) 72 cm 		d) 62 cm\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------','','','d) 62 cm','',0,0,0,NULL),(49322,824,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','A rectangle having length 12 cm and breadth 5 cm is joined to a square of sides 5 cm at the breadth. What is the perimeter of the new figure formed?\na) 22 cm 		b) 44 cm 		c) 17 cm 		d) 54 cm\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------','','','b) 44 cm 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(49323,824,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Bhushan runs for practice daily 5 times around a square ground and completes 2 km. What is the length of one side of the ground?\na) 100 m 		b) 10 m 		c) 400 m 		d) 40 m\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------','','','a) 100 m 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(49324,824,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The length of a rectangle is 24 cm and its perimeter is 68 cm. Find its area.\na) 92 cm²		b) 120 cm²		c) 240 cm²		d) 1632 cm²\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------','','','c) 240 cm²	','',0,0,0,NULL),(49326,824,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The area of a rectangle having breadth 20 cm is 1200 cm². What is the perimeter of the rectangle?\na) 160 cm 		b) 120 cm 		c) 100 cm 		d) 80 cm\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------','','','a) 160 cm 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(49327,824,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','A hall with length 48 m and breadth 12 m requires 64 square shaped tiles. What will be the perimeter of each tile?\na) 9 m 		b) 81 m 		c) 8 m 		d) 12 m\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------','','','d) 12 m','',0,0,0,NULL),(49328,824,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The length and breadth of a rectangular room are 4 m and 3 m respectively. If the square tiles of side 40 cm are to be fitted on the floor of the room, how many tiles will be required?\na) 50 		b) 75 		c) 100 		d) 400\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------','','','b) 75 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(49329,824,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Write the perimeter of given figure','\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','Perimeter of given figure = Sum of all sides \n          = 7 + 16 + 20 + 14 = 57 cm\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(49330,824,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Write the perimeter of given figure','\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','Perimeter of given figure = Sum of all sides \n          = 8 + 8 + 10 + 6 + 6 + 10 = 48 cm\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(49331,824,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Write the perimeter of given figure','\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','Perimeter of given figure = Sum of all sides \n          = 8 + 8 + 18 + 12 + 8 = 64 cm\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(49332,824,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Look at the figures on the sheet of a graph paper. Measure their sides with the help of the lines on the graph paper. Write the perimeter of given figure.','\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','The perimeter of rectangle ABCD = (2 × 3.5 + 2 × 2.5)\n            = 7 + 5 = 12\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(49333,824,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Look at the figures on the sheet of a graph paper. Measure their sides with the help of the lines on the graph paper. Write the perimeter of given figure.','\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------','','The perimeter of rectangle PQRS = (4 × 2.4 ) = 9.6 cm','',1,0,0,NULL),(49334,824,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Look at the figures on the sheet of a graph paper. Measure their sides with the help of the lines on the graph paper. Write the perimeter of given figure.','\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','The perimeter of rectangle EFGH = (2 × 3.8 + 2 × 1.3)\n            = 7.6 + 2.6 = 10.2\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(49335,824,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Look at the figures on the sheet of a graph paper. Measure their sides with the help of the lines on the graph paper. Write the perimeter of given figure.','\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','The perimeter of rectangle SVUT = (2 × 3 + 2 × 2)\n            = 6 + 4 = 10\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(49336,824,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write the formula for area of rectangle.\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Area of rectangle = length × breadth','',0,0,0,NULL),(49337,824,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write the formula for area of square.\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Area of square = (side)²','',0,0,0,NULL),(49338,824,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write the formula for perimeter of rectangle.\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Perimeter of rectangle = 2[length + breadth]','',0,0,0,NULL),(49339,824,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write the formula for perimeter of square.\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Perimeter of square = 4 × side','',0,0,0,NULL),(49340,824,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write the perimeter of given figure :','\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','Perimeter of given figure = Sum of all sides \n          = 2 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 3 = 14 cm\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(49341,824,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write the perimeter of given figure :','\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','Perimeter of given figure = Sum of all sides \n          = 3 + 2 + 3 + 2  = 10 cm\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(49342,824,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write the perimeter of given figure :','\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','Perimeter of given figure = Sum of all sides \n          = 5 + 3 + 2 + 5 + 2 + 3 = 20 cm\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(49343,824,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write the perimeter of given figure :','\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','Perimeter of given figure = Sum of all sides \n          = 2 + 8 + 7 + 10  = 27 cm\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(49344,824,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','How much wire will be needed to make a rectangle 7 cm long and 4 cm wide?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Length = 7 cm, breadth = 4 cm\nPerimeter of rectangle = 2[length + breadth]\n                   = 2[7 + 4] = 2 × 11 = 22 cm','',0,0,0,NULL),(49345,824,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','If the length of a rectangle is 20 m and its width is 12 m, what is its perimeter?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Length = 20 m, breadth = 12 m\nPerimeter of rectangle = 2[length + breadth]\n                   = 2[20 + 12] = 2 × 32 = 64 m','',0,0,0,NULL),(49346,824,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Each side of a square is 9 m long. Find its perimeter.\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Side of square = 9 m\nPerimeter of square = 4 × side = 4 × 9 = 36 m\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49347,824,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','If the length of the side of square is 12 m, find its area.\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Side of square = 12 m\nArea of square = (side)² = (12)² = 144 m²\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49348,824,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','If the length of the side of square is 6 cm, find its area.\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Side of square = 6 cm\nArea of square = (side)² = (6)² = 36 cm²\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49349,824,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','If the length of the side of square is 25 m, find its area.\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Side of square = 25 m\nArea of square = (side)² = (25)² = 625 m²\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49350,824,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','If the length of the side of square is 18 cm, find its area.\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Side of square = 18 cm\nArea of square = (side)² = (18)² = 324 cm²\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49351,824,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','The length of the base of a square-shaped box is 5 cm. What is the perimeter of the base?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Side of square based box = 5 cm\nPerimeter of base = 4 × 5 = 20 cm\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49352,824,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is the area of the square with side 5 cm?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Side of square = 5 cm\nArea of square = (side)² = (5)² = 25 cm²\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49353,824,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','How much wire will be needed to make a rectangle 8 cm long and 5 cm wide?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           -------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Here, length = 8 cm, breadth = 5 cm\nPerimeter of rectangle = 2[length + breadth]\n                  = 2 [8 + 5] = 2 × 13 = 26 cm','',0,0,0,NULL),(49354,824,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Each side of a square is 7 cm long, find its perimeter.\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Side of square = 7 cm\nPerimeter of square = 4 × side = 4 × 7 = 28 cm\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49355,824,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','If a square of a side 1 cm is cut off from one corner of a square with side 3 cm. What will be the perimeter of the remaining figure?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The perimeter of 3 cm square = 4 × side = 4 × 3 = 12 cm\nThe perimeter of 1 cm square = 4 × 1 = 4 cm\nThe perimeter of remaining shape = 8 + 4 = 12 cm both have same Perimeter.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49356,824,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','If we take 4 rounds around a field that is 160 m long and 90 m wide, what is the distance we walk in kilometers?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','length = 160 m, breadth = 90 m\nPerimeter of rectangle = 2 × [length + breadth] \n                = 2 × [160 + 90] = 2 × 250 = 500\nThe distance we walk = 500 × 4 = 2000 m or 2 km','',0,0,0,NULL),(49357,824,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','Sanju completes 12 rounds around a square part every day. If the side of the park is 120 m, find out in kilometers and meters the distance that Sanju covers daily.\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','One side of the park = 120 m\nPerimeter of the square = 4 × length of one side\n                = 4 × 120 = 480 m\n12 rounds around a square park = 480 × 12 = 5760 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49358,824,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','Four rounds of wire fence have to be put around a field. If the filed is 60 m long and 40 m wide, how much wire will be needed?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Length = 60 m, breadth = 40 m\nPerimeter of rectangle = 2 × [length + breadth] \n                = 2 × [60 + 40] = 2 × 100 = 200 m\nThe fence have four rounds = 200 × 4 = 800 m','',0,0,0,NULL),(49359,824,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','The sides of a triangle are 24.7 cm, 20.4 cm and 10.5 cm respectively. what is the perimeter of the triangle?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Perimeter of triangle = sum of all sides \n                = 24.7 + 20.4 + 10.5 = 55.6 cm\nThe perimeter of the triangle = 55.6 cm','',0,0,0,NULL),(49360,824,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','If the cost of 1 sq m of a plot of land is Rs. 900, find the cost of a plot of land that is 25 m long and 20 m broad.\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Area of rectangle = length × breadth = 25 × 20 = 500 m²\nThe total cost of a plot = 500 × 900 = 4,50,000 rupees.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49361,824,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','What will be the labour cost of lying the floor of an assembly hall that is 16 m long and 12 m wide, if the cost of lying 1 sq m is Rs. 80?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Length = 16 m, breadth = 12 m\nArea of rectangle = length × breadth = 16 × 12 = 192 m²\n∴ The cost of lying the floor of an assembly hall is 1 sq m is 80 rupees \n         = 192 × 80 = 15,360 rupees \nThe cost is 15,360 rupees.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49362,824,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','A plot which has some part is square in shape. While some part is rectangle shape. If the square has side 6 cm and the rectangle has 14 cm long and 7 cm wide, which perimeter is more?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','a) Perimeter of square : Here, side = 6 cm\nPerimeter of square = 4 × side = 4 × 6 = 24 cm\nb) Perimeter of rectangle : length = 14 cm, breadth = 7 cm\nPerimeter of rectangle = 2 [length + breadth]\n                 = 2 [14 + 7] = 2 × 21 = 42 cm\n∴ Perimeter of rectangle is more than perimeter of square.             ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49363,824,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','The length of a rectangular plot of land is 50 m and its width is 30 m. A triple fence has to be put along its edges. If the wire costs Rs. 60 per meter, what will be the total costs of the wire needed for the fence?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Length = 50 m, breadth = 30 m\nPerimeter of rectangle = 2 × [length + breadth]\n            = 2 × [50 + 30] = 2 × 80 = 160 m\nThe plot has triple fence = 160 × 3 = 480 m\nThe cost of the wire needed for the fence = 480 × 60 = 28800 \n∴ The cost of wire fences 28 rupees 800 paise ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49364,824,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','A game requires its players to run around a square playground. Each side of the playground is 20 m long. One player took 5 rounds around the playground. How many meters did he run altogether? \n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Side of playground = 20 m\nPerimeter of (playground) square = 4 × side\n            = 4 × 20 = 80 m\nOne player took 5 rounds which = 80 × 5 = 400 m\n∴ He ran 400 m altogether.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49365,824,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','The side of a square is 4 cm. The length of a rectangle is 8 cm and its width is 2 cm . Find the perimeter and area of both the figures.\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The area of the square = side × side = 4 × 4 = 16 cm²\nThe area of rectangle = length × breadth = 8 × 2 = 16 cm²\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49366,824,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','The figure given shows some squares. Find out how many squares with the same measures will fit in the empty space in the figure.','\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','The area of the figure = 4 × 3 = 12 sq units\n6 squares are shown in the given figure.\n∴ (12 – 6) = 6 squares will fit in the empty space.','',1,0,0,NULL),(49367,824,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','Divide the given figure into four parts in such a way that the area and shape of each part is the same. Colour the parts with different colours.','\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','The given figure is divided into four similar parts by different shades as shown below.','',1,0,1,NULL),(49368,824,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Three rounds of wire fence have to be put around a field. If a field is 50 m long and 30 m wide, how much wire will be needed?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Length = 50 m, breadth = 30 m\nPerimeter of rectangle = 2 × [length + breadth]\n               = 2 × [50 + 30] = 2 × 80 = 160 m\n∴ 160 m wire will be needed.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49369,824,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','How much wire will be needed to put a triple fence around a square plot with side 30 m? What will be the total cost of the wire at ` 70 per metre?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Side of square = 30 m\nPerimeter of square = 4 × side = 4 × 30 = 120 m\nA square plot having triple fence = 3 × 120 = 360 m\nCost of wire per meter is Rs. 70\n∴ Total cost of fencing = 70 × 360 = ₹ 25200.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49370,824,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','A wall that is 4 m long and 3 m wide has to be painted. If the labour charges are ` 25 per sq m, what is the cost of labour for painting this wall?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Length = 4 m, breadth = 3 m\nArea of rectangle (wall) = length × breadth = 4 × 3 = 12 m²\nLabour charges = ₹ 25 per square meter\n∴ Cost of painting a wall = 25 × 12 = ₹ 300','',0,0,0,NULL),(49371,824,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','One side of a square room is 4 m. If the cost of labour for laying 1 sq m of the floor is 35 rupees, what will be the total cost of labour?\n\nAns. : ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Side of square = 4 m\nArea of square shaped wall = side × side = 4 × 4 = 16 m²\nArea of floor = 4 × 16 = 64 m²\nCost of labour per sq m is ₹ 35\n∴ Cost of floor = 35 × 64 = ₹ 2240.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49372,825,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','If a cube is made by folding the given net, which number will not be adjacent to the number 2?','a) 3 		b) 6 		c) 4 		d) 5\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','d) 5','',1,0,0,NULL),(49373,825,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following nets will fold into a cube?','\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','1) ','',1,0,0,NULL),(49374,825,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following nets fold into a cuboid?','\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','3) ','',1,0,0,NULL),(49375,825,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following figures is not a net pentomino (five square net)?','\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','4) ','',1,0,0,NULL),(49376,825,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','How will the three-dimensional figure given alongside appear as viewed from above?','\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','2) ','',1,0,0,NULL),(49377,825,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','From which of the nets given below can an open box be formed?','\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','3) ','',1,0,0,NULL),(49378,825,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following objects will appear the same when viewed from the front, from a side or from above?','\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','1) ','',1,0,0,NULL),(49379,825,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','If a cube is formed from the given net which letter will be on the opposite side of the letter A?','1) A		2) C			3) D 			4) E\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','2) C','',1,0,0,NULL),(49380,825,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following figures is of pentomino?','\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','2) ','',1,0,0,NULL),(49381,825,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The net of a cube-shaped number die is given below. which number will not come on the adjacent surface which has number 5 on it?','1) 4 			2) 1 		3) 2 			4) 3\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','2) 1','',1,0,0,NULL),(49382,825,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','A paper is folded according to the figure and a cubical box is made. Which letter will there be opposite to the surface with letter R?','1) L 		2) A 		3) I 		4) U\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------','','1) L','',1,0,0,NULL),(49383,825,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','The given figure shows a structure made of blocks. Say whether each view is from the front, from a side or from above.','\nAns. : ------------------------------------   ---------------------------\n\n         ------------------------------------   --------------------------','','i) front          ii) side          iii) above','',1,0,0,NULL),(49384,825,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','The given figure shows a structure made of blocks. Say whether each view is from the front, from a side or from above.','\nAns. : ------------------------------------   ---------------------------\n\n         ------------------------------------   --------------------------','','i) above             ii) side             iii) front ','',1,0,0,NULL),(49385,825,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','The given figure shows a structure made of blocks. Say whether each view is from the front, from a side or from above.','\nAns. : ------------------------------------   ---------------------------\n\n         ------------------------------------   --------------------------','','i) side            ii) front              iii) above','',1,0,0,NULL),(49386,825,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','All the surfaces are square, then this shape is called as ------\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------','','','Cube','',0,0,0,NULL),(49387,825,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The arrangement of five square net is called a ------.\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------','','','pentomino ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49388,825,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','All the surfaces are in rectangular in shape, then this shape is called as -----\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------','','','cuboid ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49389,825,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Define two dimensional objects.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The objects which have only length and breadth and no thickness or negligible thickness are called two dimensional objects.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49390,825,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Define three dimensional objects.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The objects which have length, breadth (width) and height are called three dimensional objects.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49391,825,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Define net. \n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The two dimensional shape, from which three dimensional object can ne made by folding it, is called a net of that object.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49392,825,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Draw a picture of a table, which is three dimensional objects as viewed from the front, from a side and from above.','\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Answer : ','',1,0,1,NULL),(49393,825,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Draw a picture of a chair, which is three dimensional objects as viewed from the front, from a side and from above.','\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Answer : ','',1,0,1,NULL),(49394,825,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Draw a picture of a water bottle, which is three dimensional objects as viewed from the front, from a side and from above.','\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Answer : ','',1,0,1,NULL),(49395,825,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Stocks of various types of grains in a warehouse are as given below. make a pictographs based on the given information :','\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Here, the given numbers are multiple of 8.\nSo, take the scale as 1 picture = 8 sacks \nFor 40 sacks, 40 ÷ 8 = 5 pictures, for 56 sacks, 56 ÷ 8 = 7 pictures, for 8 sacks, 8 ÷ 8 = 1 picture and for 32 sacks, 32 ÷ 8 = 4 pictures \n(Scale : 1 picture = 8 sack)','',1,0,1,NULL),(49396,825,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the scales is appropriate to represent the following information as a pictograph?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Here, the given numbers are multiple of 25.\nSo, take the scale as 1 picture = 25 tree \nFor 75 tree, 75 ÷ 25 = 3 pictures, for 50 tree, 50 ÷ 25 = 2 pictures, for 100 tree, 100 ÷ 25 = 4 picture and for 125 tree, 125 ÷ 25 = 5 pictures \n(Scale : 1 picture = 25 tree)','',1,0,0,NULL),(49397,825,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','Information about the various types of vehicles in Wadgaon is given below. make a pictograph for this data :','\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Here, the given numbers are divisible by 12.\nSo, take the scale as 1 picture = 12 vehicles \n','',1,0,1,NULL),(49398,825,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','The numbers of the various grains kept in a warehouse are as given below. make a pictograph based on the information given.','\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Here, the given numbers are multiple of 8.\nSo, take the scale as 1 picture = 8 sacks \nFor 16 sacks, 16 ÷ 8 = 2 pictures, for 24 sacks, 24 ÷ 8 = 3 pictures, for 32 sacks, 32 ÷ 8 = 4 picture and for 8 sacks, 8 ÷ 8 = 1 pictures \n(Scale : 1 picture = 8 sack)','',1,0,1,NULL),(49399,825,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Make a pictograph showing the information given :','\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Here, the given numbers are multiple of 25.\nSo, take the scale as 1 picture = 25 tree \nFor 75 tree, 75 ÷ 25 = 3 pictures, for 50 tree, 50 ÷ 25 = 2 pictures, for 100 tree, 100 ÷ 25 = 4 picture and for 125 tree, 125 ÷ 25 = 5 pictures \n(Scale : 1 picture = 25 tree)','',1,0,1,NULL),(49400,825,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Answer the given questions (Scale : 1 Δ = 35 students) : \ni) What is the total number of students?	\nii) By how much is the number of students who like Mathematics more than the number of students who like English? ','\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','i) Total number of students = 175 for maths + 105 for Marathi + 70 for English + 140 for science = 490 students\nii) Number of students in mathematics = 175 \nnumber of students for English = 70\n∴ 175 – 70 = 105 students like mathematics more than English subjects. ','',1,0,0,NULL),(49401,825,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','The number of books on different subjects kept in a cupboard in the school library are given below. Make a pictograph showing the information given : ','\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Here, the given number of books is divisible by 7.\nSo, take the scale as 1 picture = 7 books\n','',1,0,1,NULL),(49402,825,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Stocks of various types of books stored in a bookstall are given below. Make a pictograph based on the information given.','\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','','Here, the given number of books is divisible by 5\nSo, take the scale as 1 picture = 5 books\n','',1,0,1,NULL),(49403,825,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Answer the following questions from the given information (scale : 1 @ = 6 students): \ni) What is the number of students about whom the information is given in pictorial diagram? 	\nii) By how much is the number of students liking Maths is more than that of the number of students liking Science?','\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','i) Total number of students = 24 students for maths + 18 students for Marathi + 12 students for Science + 24 students for drawing \n    = 78 students\nii) Number of students in Maths = 24 and number of students in Science = 12\n∴ 24 – 12 = 12 students like maths more than science subjects.','',1,0,0,NULL),(49404,825,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Answer the following questions from the given information (Scale : 1 Δ = 50 students) : \ni) Information about how many students is given in the pictograph?	\nii) How many students coming by Rikshaw are more than the students coming by cycle?','\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','i) Total number of students = 150 students for walk + 200 students for Cycle + 300 students by rikshaw + 100 students with parents \n= 750 students\nii) Students coming in rikshaw = 300 and students coming in cycle = 200\n∴ (300 – 200) = 100 students coming in rikshaw more than by cycle.','',1,0,0,NULL),(49405,826,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the given alternatives will complete the following pattern? 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, ?\na) 11 			b) 12 			c) 13 		d) 14\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------','','','c) 13 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49406,826,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','How many square numbers are there in the two-digit natural numbers?\na) 10 			b) 8 			c) 7 		d) 6\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------','','','d) 6','',0,0,0,NULL),(49407,826,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','How many triangular numbers are there in the given list?\n6, 9, 10, 12, 15, 18, 21, 24, 36\na) 5 		b) 6 			c) 7 			d) 8\n\nAns. : -----------------------------------','','','a) 5 	','',0,0,0,NULL),(49408,826,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','1   3    6 