-------------------------------------','','','(12 × 2) < (25 + 10)','',0,0,0,NULL),(49435,826,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Find the square numbers from the list given below : 5, 9, 12, 16, 50, 60, 64, 72, 80, 81\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The square numbers are = 9, 16, 64, 81','',0,0,0,NULL),(49436,826,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Which are the triangular numbers in the given list: 3, 6, 8, 9, 12, 15, 16, 20, 21, 42.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','The triangular numbers are = 3, 6, 15, 21','',0,0,0,NULL),(49437,826,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','If 3 is the first triangular number, which is the tenth one?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Yes, ‘66’ is the tenth triangular number.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49438,826,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give any two pairs of numbers whose sum is 20.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) (12 + 8) = (22 – 2)\nii) (7 + 13) = (17 + 3)\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49439,826,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Say whether the equality 25 + 7 = 8 × 4 is right or wrong.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','25 + 7 = 32 and 8 × 4 = 32 \nThe given equality is right.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49440,826,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','9 + 9 = x + 8. For what value of x is the given equality true?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ---------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','9 + 9 = x + 8 \n∴ 18 = x + 8 \n∴ 18 – 8 = x + 8 – 8 ------- (subtract 8 from both sides)\n∴ x = 10','',0,0,0,NULL),(49441,826,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','For which value of x, will the statement x × 3 = 4 × 6 becomes true?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ---------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','x × 3 = 4 × 6 = 24\n∴ (x × 3)/3 = 24/3 ------- (divide 3 both sides)\n∴ x = 8 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49442,826,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Say whether right or wrong : i) (5 × 8) = (8 × 5) 		ii) (16 + 0) = 0\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Right        ii) Wrong ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49443,826,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Say whether right or wrong : i) (16 + 0) = 16 		ii) (9 + 4) = 12\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Right       ii) wrong ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49444,826,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Fill in the blanks : i) (45 ÷ 9) ▯ (9 – 4)  		ii) (6 + 1)  ▯  (3 × 2)\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) (45 ÷ 9) = (9 – 4)\nii) (6 + 1) > (3 × 2) \n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49445,826,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','Using brackets, write three pairs of numbers whose sum is 13. Write three equalities using these numbers.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ------------------------------------------------------