-----------------------------------','','','i) (1 × 7) = (7 × 1)\nii) (5 × 4) > (7 × 2)\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49451,826,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','Fill in the blanks in the expression with the proper numbers : \ni) (48 ÷ 3) < (▯ × 5)		ii) (0 + 1) > (▯ × 5)\n\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) (48 ÷ 3) < (5 × 5)\nii) (0 + 1) > (0 × 5)\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49452,826,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Say whether right or wrong :\n i) 25 – 2 = 3 + 20		ii) 188 < 192		iii) 3 × 6 = 2 × 9\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ---------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Right \nii) Right \niii) Right ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49453,826,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','Find four pairs of numbers, one for each of the operations addition, subtraction, multiplication and division that make the number 18. Write the equality for each of them.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','(9 + 9) = (21 – 3) = (6 × 3) = (36 ÷ 2)','',0,0,0,NULL),(49454,826,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','Use a letter for ‘any number’ and write the following properties in short : \ni) The sum of any number and zero is the number itself 		\nii) The product of any two numbers and the product obtained after changing the order of those numbers is the same.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) (x + 0) = x\nii) (a × b) = (b × a)\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49455,826,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Fill in the blanks in the expression with the proper numbers : \ni) (35 ÷ 7) = (▯ + ▯) 		ii) (6 – ▯) < (2 + 3)\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) (35 ÷ 7) = (3 + 2)\nii) (6 – 3) < (2 + 3)\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49456,826,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Use proper symbol >, < or = in the box : i) 18 ▯ 17 		ii) 9 + 7 ▯ 4 + 12		iii) 27 ÷ 3 ▯ 9 + 4		iv) 5 + 5 ▯ 2 × 7\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        --------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) 18 > 17\nii) 9 + 4 = 13 and 4 + 12 = 16\n      ∴ 13 < 16\niii) 27  ÷ 3 = 9 and 9 + 4 = 13\n      ∴ 9 < 13\niv) 5 + 5 = 10 and 2 × 7 = 14\n     ∴ 10 < 14','',0,0,0,NULL),(49457,826,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Use letter for ‘any number’ and write the following properties in short : \ni) The sum of any number and one		\nii) The product of any number and zero is zero		\niii) The any number is divided by two.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','',' i) a + 1 \nii) a × 0 = 0\niii) a ÷ 2','',0,0,0,NULL),(49458,826,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Say whether right or wrong : \ni) 8 × 0 = 8		ii) 7 × 1 = 71		iii) 3 – 2 = 2 – 1 \n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','','i) Wrong ; 8 × 0 = 0 ≠ 8\nii) Wrong ; 7 × 1 = 7 ≠ 71\niii) Right  ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49459,807,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','If the circumference of a circle is 34.54 cm, find its radius. (π = 3.14)\n\nAns. : ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Circumference of circle = 34.54 cm\n∴ c = 2πr\n∴ 34.54 = 2 × 3.14 × r\n∴ r = 34.54/6.28 = 5.5 cm','',0,0,0,NULL),(49460,722,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','How many factors does 36 have?\na) 6 		b) 8 			c) 9 			d) 10\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------','','','c) 9 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49461,722,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following numbers is not a factor of 32?\na) 64 		b) 32 			c) 16 			d) 8\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------','','','a) 64','',0,0,0,NULL),(49462,722,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is the sum of all divisors of 24?\na) 59 		b) 36 			c) 60 			d) 66\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------','','','c) 60 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49463,722,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following numbers is not divisible by 3?\na) 124 		b) 126 		c) 132 		d) 138\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------','','','a) 124 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49464,722,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','By which of the following digits should * be replaced in the number 5*234, so that the number is divisible by 6?\na) 2 		b) 6 			c) 4 			d) 6\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------','','','c) 4 		','',0,0,0,NULL),(49465,722,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which is the digit at the place * in the number 6*54*, so that it is divisible by 9?\na) 6 		b) 7 			c) 8 			d) 9\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------','','','a) 