ext Book','','Write test of divisibility by 2\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','If there is 0, 2, 4, 6 or 8 in the units place, the number is a multiple of 2, or is exactly divisible by 2.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49483,722,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write test of divisibility by 3\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','If the sum of the digits of a number is divisible by 3 then the number is also divisible by 3.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49484,722,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write test of divisibility by 5\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','If the unit place of a number is 0 or 5 then this number is divisible by 5.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49485,722,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Write five three-digit numbers that are multiples of 2.\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------        -------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------        -------------------------------------------','','','i) 284            ii) 468             iii) 238            iv) 254           v) 548 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49486,722,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Write all the prime numbers between 1 and 20.\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Prime numbers between 1 to 20 are : 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49487,722,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Circle the prime numbers in the list given below : 22, 37, 43, 48, 53, 60, 91, 57, 59, 77, 79, 97, 100.\n\nAns. : --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','Prime numbers in the list : 37, 43, 53, 59, 79, 97','',0,0,0,NULL),(49488,722,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Determine whether the pairs of numbers given below are coprime numbers or not : i) 14, 21		ii) 10, 33\n\nAns. : -------------------------------------          -------------------------------------------\n\n          --------------------------------------         ------------------------------------------','','','i) The number 14 and 21 having more than 1 common factor.\n∴ 14 and 21 are not co-prime number.\nii) The number 10 and 33 having only one 1 common factor.\n∴ 10 and 33 are co-prime number.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49489,722,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Determine whether the pairs of numbers given below are coprime numbers or not : i) 50, 52		ii) 17, 18\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------        ----------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------         -----------------------------------------','','','i) The number 50 and 52 having more than 1 common factor.\n∴ 50 and 52 are not co-prime number.\nii) The number 17 and 18 having only one 1 common factor.\n∴ 17 and 18 are co-prime number.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49490,722,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','Write five three-digit numbers that are multiple of 5\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------          ----------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------          ----------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------          ---------------------------------------------','','','i) 125           ii) 525          iii) 450           iv) 785           v) 990','',0,0,0,NULL),(49491,722,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','Write five three-digit numbers that multiples of 10\n\nns. : ----------------------------------          ----------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------          ----------------------------------------------\n\n          ----------------------------------          ---------------------------------------------','','','i) 100            ii) 150            iii) 570            iv) 650           v) 990','',0,0,0,NULL),(49492,722,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','A ribbon is 3 meters long. Can we cut it into 50 cm piece and have nothing left over? Write the reason why or why not?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','We can cut it into 50 cm pieces and nothing left over. Because 3 m is 300 cm and can be divide easily by 50 cm.\n50 cm is multiple of 300 cm.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49493,722,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','If the number given in the table is divisible by the given divisor, put √ in the box. If it is not divisible by the divisor, put × in the box :','','','Answer :','',1,0,1,NULL),(49494,722,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write all the composite numbers from 21 to 50.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','21, 22, 24, 25, 26, 27, 28, 30, 32, 33, 34, 35, 36, 38, 39, 40, 42, 44, 45, 46, 48 49.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49495,722,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','Determine whether the pairs of numbers given below are coprime numbers or not : i) 11, 30		ii) 5, 7 		iii) 15, 16\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) The number 11 and 30 having only one 1 common factor.\n∴ 11 and 30 are co-prime number.\nii) The number 5 and 7 having only one 1 common factor.\n∴ 5 and 7 are co-prime number.\niii) The number 15 and 16 having only one 1 common factor.\n∴ 15 and 16 are co-prime number.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49496,722,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write five numbers that multiples of 2 as well as 3.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','6, 12, 24, 36, 48','',0,0,0,NULL),(49497,722,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','A ribbon is 3 meters long. I need 8 pieces of ribbon each 40 cm long. How many centimeters shorter is the given ribbon than the length I need?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','3 m = 300 cm\nTotal needed = 8 × 40 = 320 cm\nIt is shorter ribbon = 320 – 300 = 20 cm\nIt is 20 cm shorter than the length they need.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49498,722,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','If the number given in the table is divisible by the given divisor, put √ in the box. If it is not divisible by the divisor, put × in the box :','','','Answer : ','',1,0,1,NULL),(49499,722,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Can a 5 meters long ribbon be cut into 50 cm long pieces? If yes, how many?\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','5m long ribbon mean 5m = 500 cm\n500 is a multiple of 50.\n∴ 50 cm  long pieces cut into 50 cm each.\nTotal number of pieces made = 500/50 = 10 ','',0,0,0,NULL),(49500,722,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write all the twin prime numbers pairs from 1 to 100.\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','(3, 5), (5, 7), (11, 13), (17, 19), (29, 31), (41, 43), (59, 61), (71, 73)','',0,0,0,NULL),(49501,722,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Define : i) Prime numbers 		ii) Composite numbers\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Prime number : A number which has only two factors, 1 and the number itself, is called as prime numbers.\nii) Composite numbers : A number which has more than two factors is called a composite numbers.','',0,0,0,NULL),(49502,722,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Define : i) Twin prime numbers 		ii) Co-prime numbers\n\nAns. : ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          ---------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','i) Twin prime numbers : Prime numbers with a difference of two are called as twin prime numbers.\nii) Co – prime numbers : Numbers which have only 1 as a common factor are called co-prime numbers.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(49976,769,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','एका संख्येची सात पट ही 42 आहे, तर ती संख्या कोणती?\na) 7 		b) 6 		c) 8 		d) 24\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(49977,769,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','35 – x हे समीकरण वाक्यामध्ये कसे लिहाल?\na) x पेक्षा लहान 35 आहे		b) 35 पेक्षा लहान x आहे		c)  35 पेक्षा मोठे x आहे		d)  x भागिले 35\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(49978,769,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','एका संख्येची 1/3 पट 