e word by using correct letters : \ni) par_el 	ii) s_ade	 iii) sm_le 	iv) dra_t \n\n       ------------------------------------         -----------------------------------------\n\n       ------------------------------------        ------------------------------------------\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(55659,1179,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Put the following words in alphabetical order : \ni) decide, regard, account, threat \n\n    --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nii) tonight, totally, tourist, tongue \n\n      -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(55660,1179,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Make four words (minimum 3 letters each) using the letters in the given word : investigation \n\n      --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(55661,1179,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write the related words as shown in the example','   --------------------------------      -----------------------------------\n\n   -------------------------------         ------------------------------------\n','','','',1,0,0,NULL),(55662,1179,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the word chain of ‘nouns’. Add four words, each beginning with last letter of the previous word : cap \n\n     ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(55663,1179,'descriptive','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the word chain of ‘Verbs’. Add four words, each beginning with last letter of the previous word : guess \n\n   --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(55664,1179,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Make meaningful sentence by using phrase ‘to be successful’ \n\n       ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                                OR \nAdd a clause to the following sentence to expand it meaningfully. The history is the subject \n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(55665,1179,'descriptive','1b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Add a prefix or suffix to make new words. \n              (i) Arrive                              (ii) Just   \n\n             ------------------------       -----------------------------\n                                       OR \nMake a meaningful sentence using any one of the following words. \n              (i) Arrive                            (ii) just \n             ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n              ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(55666,1179,'descriptive','2',10,2,'Out of Text Book','P. V. Sindhu or Pusarla Venkata Sindhu is an ace shuttler and silver medalist at 2016 Rio Summer Olympics. This young badminton player from Andhra Pradesh was born to volleyball players P. V. Ramana and P. Vijaya in the year 1995. Her father was honoured with Arjuna Award for having displayed excellence in his sport. One of the youngest and talented badminton players of the contemporary times, Sindhu has featured in top 10 in the world badminton rankings for the most part of 2014.\nP. V. Sindhu started playing badminton from the age of eight, after she drew inspiration from Pullela Gopichand\'s victory in All England Open Badminton Championship in 2001. That\'s the reason why she chose badminton over volleyball although her parents were professional volleyball players. Her initial apprenticeship started with Mehboob Ali at the badminton courts of Indian Railway Institute of Signal Engineering and Telecommunications in Secunderabad. Later, she joined Pullela Gopichand\'s badminton academy to further enhance her sporting skills.\nEarly Success\nSindhu\'s first major recognition came in the form of the 5th Servo All India ranking championship for under-10 category. She also won the singles title at the Ambuja Cement All India ranking.\nIn the under-13 category, Sindhu won doubles titles at the IOC All India Ranking, Krishna Khaitan All India Tournament, the Sub-Junior Nationals and the All India Ranking in Pune.\nAt the 51st National School Games in India, Sindhu won the gold medal in under-14 category.\nSindhu\'s Debut and Performance at International level\nP. V. Sindhu didn\'t take much time to launch and establish herself as a promising player in the global arena. She won a bronze medal at the 2009 Sub-Junior Asian Badminton Championships held in Colombo.\nThe star player bagged silver in the women\'s singles at Iran Fajr International Badminton Challenge in 2010 and found a place in the national team at the 2010 Uber Cup.\n','A1] Simple Factual Question \n       Complete the sentences using the information from the passage:\n\n       i. -----------------  was Sindhu\'s first win at international level.\n\n       ii. Sindhu started her achievements in badminton around to age of ------------- .\n\n       iii. Sindhu won her first International medal in the year ------------------.\n\n       iv. P. V. Sindhu won -------------- at 2016 Summer Olympics.\n','','A2] Complex Factual Question \n        What made Sindhu take up badminton at the age of eight? \n\n            ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n              ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA3] Vocabulary \n        Complete the words by filling in the missing letters:\n       i. e_hance          ii. fe_tures          iii. l_unch         iv. p_ayer.\n\n           -----------------------------        --------------------------------\n\n             ----------------------------          -------------------------------\n\nA4] Grammar\n       i. Sindhu won doubles titles.\n           (Begin with \'Double titles-and change the voice.)\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n      ii. She won a bronze medal.\n     (Add a Question Tag.)\n\n          ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA5] Personal Response\n       Who is your favourite player? Why do you like him/her?\n\n           ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n              ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n              ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------  ','','',0,0,0,NULL),(55667,1179,'descriptive','3a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','I know a curious little boy\nWho is always asking, \"why?\"\nWhy this, why that, why then, why now,\nWhy not, why by-and-by?\nHe wants to know why wood should swim, \nWhy lead and marbles sink; \nWhy stars should shine and winds should blow,\nAnd why we eat and drink.\nHe wants to know what makes the clouds,\nAnd why they cross the sky; \nWhy sinks the sun behind the hills, \nAnd why the flowers die.\n','A1] Simple Factual Question :\n       State whether the following statements are True or False:\n      i. The little boy is curious because he never asks questions --------------\n\n      ii. The sun sinks behind the hills --------------------\n\n      iii. The flowers always remain alive ------------------\n\n      iv. Lead and marbles sink in water ------------------\n','A2] Complex Factual Question\n       Complete the following sentences :\n      i. I know that the little boy is really curious because ------------\n\n      ii. The boy wants to know ----------------------\n\n      iii. The boy wants to know --------------\n\n   iv. The boy always asks Why this, --------------------------\nA3] Poetic Device\n       Complete the following with proper action words from the extract:\n\n      i. wood : ------------                   ii. sun : ---------------------                 \n      iii. marbles : --------- 		iv. flowers : -----------------              \n      v. stars : ------------              	vi. winds : ---------------------\n','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(55668,1179,'descriptive','3b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','The Vet\no be a successful and competent vet, \nNeeds knowledge exceedingly wide, \nFor each of the patients he\'s likely to get \nPossesses a different inside. \nHe must know why the cat is refusing her milk,\nWhy the dog is not eating his bone,\nWhy the coat of the horse is not shining like silk,\nWhy the parrot does nothing but groan;\nWhy the ducks and the chickens are failing to lay,\nWhy so faint the canary bird sings, \nAnd if he is called to the zoo he must say \nAn incredible number of things.\n','Read the poem. Write an appreciation of the poem in about 12 to 15 sentences with the help of the following points :\ni. Title                    ii. Poet                     iii.  Rhyme scheme                   iv.  Figures of Speech                v. Theme/Central Idea (2 to 3 lines)\n','       -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n           --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n            ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(55669,1179,'descriptive','4a',10,2,'Out of Text Book','Pongal is a South Indian festival celebrated in Tamil Nadu. It is really the harvest festival held in the month of January every year. It generally coincides with the festival of Makar Sankranti. The houses are decorated with banana and mango leaves and the floors are embellished with decorative patterns drawn using rice flour. Pongal in Tamil generally refers to festivity; more specifically Pongal means \'boiling over\' or \'overflow\', especially of milk or rice.\nThe first day is Thanksgiving day. On the second day, married women have an early bath and cook newly harvested rice in the open. While the rice is being cooked shouts of \'pongal, pongal\' are heard all over. Rice cooked with milk and jaggery (this is also called Pongal) is prepared. The third and last day is devoted to cattle. They are decorated with garlands and fed with love and affection. They are taken out in processions.\n','A1] Simple Factual Question\n       State whether the following statements are True or False:\n\n      i. Pongal is a harvest festival. --------------\n\n      ii. The second day of Pongal is Thanksgiving day. --------------------\n\n      iii. Pongal is celebrated at the end of the harvest in September/October. -----------------\n\n      iv. Rice cooked with milk and jaggery is called Pongal. -------------------\n','A2] Complex Factual Question\n        How is Pongal celebrated? \n\n            -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n               ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA3] Vocabulary\n        Write down the root words of the following:\n        i. generally           ii. celebrated       iii. decorative          iv. taken\n\n             -------------------------------        -------------------------------\n\n                ----------------------------       ---------------------------------\nA4] Grammar\n        i. The houses are decorated with banana and mango leaves.\n             (Rewrite the sentence by using \'as well as.\')\n\n             --------------------------------------------------------------------\n        ii. Pongal means \'boiling over\'.\n              (Frame a Wh-type question to get the ‘boiling over’ answer)\n\n              ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA5] Personal Response\n        Describe your favourite festival.\n               -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n                ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n                   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(55670,1179,'descriptive','5a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Informal Letter\n     Imagine that you are Randhir/Rutuja Sane from 3/303, Ram Nagar, Khetwadi, 7th Lane, Mumbai - 400 004. You have joined a school in Mumbai. Write a letter to your friend Sadanand/Sadicha in your village, telling him about your new class and your different activities :\nYou can use the following points :\nYou like the new school – learning new and interesting things - missing fun and games of new school - read newspapers, magazines - GK books\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                OR\nChoose the correct word from the brackets and complete the story given below.\nPravin was paid back in his own coin\nPravin was a twelve-year-old boy. He lived on a farm with ------------ (his/her) \n\nparents. ------------------(One/Won) day his mother told him to ---------(fed/ feed) \nthe animals on  the -------------(farm/form). He didn\'t ---------------(like/liked) the work. So, he decided to play some mischief.\nHe gave a bowl of cotton -------------- (seed/sid) to the cow. The cat got -------------- \n(sum/some) grass. The hens ------------- (were/wear) given milk. The dog got grains \nand -------------- (seeds/sides). The goats were given a bunch of bananas. He ------- \n(made/maid) a mess of it all and --------------------- (then/than) ran away to play. \nPravin\'s mother saw this. She wanted to teach him a ---------------- (lesson/lesson). \nWhen Pravin returned home, he was ----------------- (hungry/angry). He asked for his \nlunch. His mother put before him a --------------- (plait/plate) of green and dried ------\n--- (leaves/leafs) of different trees and said nothing. She didn\'t give him any food that day.\nPravin ----------- (knew/new) that he was unkind to the animals. He never\n \nplayed such a mischief ---------------- (against/again). Pravin was paid back in his own coin.\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(55671,1179,'descriptive','5b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the following dialogue : \n    A : Has anyone ever helped you in your need?\n\n    B : ------------------------------------------------------\n    A : How did you feel at that time?\n\n    B : ------------------------------------------------\n                                        OR\nInformation Transfer – None – Verbal to Verbal \nYou have visited a tourist place. you liked it very much. use the points given in the table and write a paragraph.\n','   --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n      ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n        -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','','',1,0,0,NULL),(55672,1179,'descriptive','6',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','A] Translate the following words into Marathi ------------ 1M\n\n      i. traffic  : -----------             ii. size : -------------\nB] Translate the following sentences into Marathi ---------- 2M\n       i. Cover your nose and mouth with mask.\n\n         ------------------------------------------------------\n      ii. He left for Pune yesterday.\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(59416,1546,'descriptive','3b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','<div style= \"column-count:2;\"><b>\'A Time to Believe\'</b>\n‘‘To believe is to know that \neveryday is a new beginning.\nIs to trust that miracles happen, \nand dreams really do come true. \nTo believe is to see angels \ndancing among the clouds. \nTo know the wonder of a stardust sky \nand the wisdom of the man in the moon. \nTo believe is to know the value of a nurturing heart, \nThe innocence of a child’s eyes \nand the beauty of an aging hand, \nfor it is through their teachings, we learn to love. \nTo believe is to find the strength \nand courage that lies within us, \nWhen it is time to pick up \nthe pieces and begin again. \nTo believe is to know\nwe are never alone, \nThat life is a gift \nand this is our time to cherish it. \nTo believe is to know \nthat wonderful surprises are just \nwaiting to happen, \nAnd all our hopes and dreams are within reach. \nIf only we believe.’’ \n                 - B J Morbitzer<div style=\"column-count:2;\">\n','Write an appreciation of the poem \'A Time to Believe\' in a paragraph format in about 12 to 15 sentences. You may use the following points to write the appreciation:\ni. Poem and poet	ii. Theme/Central Idea	iii. Tone\niv. Structure and Stanzas	v. Rhyme and Rhythm		vi. Language and Imagery\nvii. Figures of Speech\n','','','                <b>Appreciation of the poem \'A Time to Believe\'</b>\ni. Poem and poet: The Title of the poem is \'A Time to Believe\' and it is written by BJ Morbitzer.\nii. Theme: The central idea of the poem is that one must believe sincerely, imagine that which has never been imagined before, trust in the Creator\'s plans and realise that one has immense potentials in order to achieve one\'s dreams.\niii. Tone: The poem has an optimistic tone as the poet tries to encourage people to have self-belief.\niv. Structure and Stanza: It consists of six stanzas of four lines each, except for the last stanza. The length of the lines in each stanza is different, which gives the poem a non-uniform structure.\nv. Rhyme and Rhythm: The poem has been written in a free-verse format and therefore does not have a fixed rhyme scheme.\nvi. Language and Imagery: The language used is simple and straight-forward. Examples of imagery used in the poem are \'angels dancing among the clouds\' and \'stardust sky\'.\nvii. Figures of Speech: The figures of speech used in the poem are Alliteration, Consonance, Epigram, Personification, Metaphor and Repetition. The line \"And all our hopes and dreams are within reach\" is an example of Epigram.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59417,1546,'descriptive','3b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','<div style= \"column-count:2;\"><b>\'The Pilgrim\'</b>\nA pilgrim, going a lone high way \nCame at evening, cold and gray \nTo a chasm, deep and vast and wide. \nThe old man crossed in the twilight dim. \nThe chasm held no fear for him. \nBut he paused when he reached the other side \nAnd built a bridge to span the tide. \n“Old man,” said a fellow pilgrim near, \n“Why waste your time in building here? \nYour journey ends with the close of the day \nYou never again will pass this way. \nYou have crossed the chasm deep and wide \nWhy build ye here at even tide ?”\nThe pilgrim raised his old gray head, \n“My friend in the path I’ve come,” he said, \n“There followeth after me today \nA fair haired youth, who must pass this way. \nThe chasm which held no fears for me \nTo the fair haired youth, may a pitfall be. \nHe, too, must cross in the twilight dim. \nMy friend, I am building this bridge for him.” \n                                   - Anonymous<div style=\"column-count:2;\">\n','Write an appreciation of the poem \'The Pilgrim\' in a paragraph format in about 12 to 15 sentences with the help of the following points:\ni. Poem and poet	ii. Theme/Central Idea	iii. Tone\niv. Structure and Stanzas	v. Rhyme and Rhythm		vi. Language and Imagery\nvii. Figures of Speech\n','','','','                              <b>Appreciation of the poem \'The Pilgrim\'</b>\ni. Poem and poet: The title of the poem is \'The Pilgrim\' and the poet is unknown.\nii. Theme / Central Idea: The central theme of the poem is that one must be selfless and share life\'s experiences with the next generation, thus enabling them to travel along the journey of life by avoiding the pitfalls.\niii. Tone: The tone of the poem is serious as it is about the older generation trying to make the path easier for the ones who come after them.\niv. Structure and Stanzas: The structure of the poem is irregular as it is a narrative poem. The poem consists of three stanzas of unequal length.\nv. Rhyme and Rhythm: The first stanza has seven lines and has the rhyme scheme \'aabccbb\'; the second stanza consists of six lines and has the rhyme scheme is \'aabbcc\'; whereas the third stanza has eight lines with the rhyme scheme \'aabbccdd\'. This rhyme scheme makes the poem rhythmic.\nvi. Language and Imagery: The language is direct with the use of archaic words like \'ye\'. The description is imaginative and vivid. An example of Imagery from the poem is \"The old man crossed in the twilight dim\".\nvii. Figures of Speech: The figures of speech used in the poem are Alliteration, Consonance, Inversion, Interrogation, Personification, Repetition, Tautology and Transferred Epithet.\n',0,0,0,NULL),(59422,1546,'descriptive','3b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','<div style= \"column-count:2;\"><b>\'Vocation\'</b>\nWhen the gong sounds ten in the morning and \nI walk to school by our lane,\n Every day I meet the hawker crying, ‘‘Bangles, \ncrystal bangles!’’ \nThere is nothing to hurry him on, there is no \nroad he must take, no place he must go to, no \ntime when he must come home. \nI wish I were a hawker, spending my day in \nthe road, crying, ‘‘Bangles, crystal bangles!’’ \nWhen at four in the afternoon I come back from \nthe school, \nI can see through the gate that house the \ngardener digging the ground. \nHe does what he likes with his spade, he soils \nhis clothes with dust, nobody takes him to \ntask, if he gets baked in the sun or gets wet. \nI wish I were a gardener digging away at the \ngarden with nobody to stop me from digging. \nJust as it gets dark in the evening and my \nmother sends me to bed,\nI can see through my open window the \nwatchman walking up and down \nThe lane is dark and lonely, and the street \nlamp stands like a giant with one red eye \nin its head. \nThe watchman swings his lantern and walks \nwith his shadow at his side, and never once \ngoes to bed in his life. \nI wish I were a watchman walking the street all night, \nchasing the shadows with my lantern.\n                                       - Rabindranath Tagore<div style=\"column-count:2;\">\n\n','Write an Appreciation of the poem \'Vocation\' in a paragraph format in about 12 to 15 sentences with the help of the following points.\ni. Poem and poet	ii. Theme / Central Idea	iii. Tone\niv. Structure and Stanzas	v. Rhyme and Rhythm		vi. Language and Imagery\nvii. Figures of Speech\n','','','                                     <b>Appreciation of the poem \'Vocation\'</b>\ni. Poem and poet: The title of the poem is \'Vocation\' and it is written by the great Rabindranath Tagore.\nii. Theme / Central Idea: The central idea of the poem is the want for freedom. The child\'s wandering mind makes him wish for a different vocation each time he sees a new one, because he desires to have the freedom to do what he wants.\niii. Tone: The tone of the poem is light-hearted and complimentary as the poet lists the advantages of each vocation through his own innocent understanding of the world.\niv. Structure and Stanzas: The poem does not have a fixed number of stanzas, which give it a non-uniform structure.\nv. Rhyme and Rhythm: The poem has been written in a free verse format, so it does not have a fixed rhyme scheme or rhythm.\nvi. Language and Imagery: Language used is simple and straight forward. The poet has made use of imagery to paint a vivid picture in the minds of the reader. Example: \'When the gong sound ten in the morning\'; \'The lone is dark and lonely and the street lamp stands like a giant with one red eye in its head\'.\nvii. Figures of Speech: The poet uses poetic devices like Alliteration, Antithesis, Consonance, Imagery, Onomatopoeia, Repetition, Personification and Simile. An example of Alliteration from the poem is \"I wish I were a gardener digging away ..\" - the sound of the letter \'w\' has been repeated for a poetic effect.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59425,1546,'descriptive','3b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','<div style= \"column-count:2;\"><b>\'The worm\'</b>\nTurn, turn thy hasty foot aside, \nNor crush that helpless worm ! \nThe frame thy scornful looks deride \nRequir’d a God to form. \nThe common Lord of all that move, \nFrom whom thy being flow’d, \nA portion of His boundless love \nOn that poor worm bestow’d. \nThe sun, the moon, the stars He made \nTo all His Creatures free : \nAnd spreads o’er earth the grassy blade, \nFor worms as well as thee. \nLet them enjoy their little day, \nTheir lowly bliss received; \nO do not lightly take away \nThe life thou canst not give ! \n                             - Thomas Gisborne<div style=\"column-count:2;\">\n','Frame a point wise Analysis of the poem \'The worm\'. Use the following points.\ni. Poem and poet	ii. Theme	iii. Tone\niv. Structure and stanzas	v. Rhyme and Rhythm		vi. Language and Imagery\nvii. Figures of Speech\n','','','','                               <b>Analysis (Appreciation) of the poem \"The Worm\'</b>\ni. Poem and poet: The title of the poem is \"The Worm\' and is written by Thomas Gishome.\nii. Theme: The theme of the poem is that we should respect all forms of life as they too have been made by the Creator, with a lot of love. He also gives us a message that since we cann create life, we must refrain from taking it.\niii. Tone: The tone of the poem is serious and reflective as it is based on respect and appreciation for life.\niv. Structure and stanzas: The poem has four stanzas of four lines each.\nv. Rhyme and Rhythm: The rhyme scheme of the poem is \'abab\'.\nvi. Language and Imagery: The language used is full of archaic words. There is no use of imagery in the poem.\nvii. Figures of Speech: The figures of speech used in the poem Alliteration, Apostrophe, Consonance, Epigram, Imagery, Inversion, Repetition and Tautology. An example of Epigram from the poem is \"O do not lightly take away the life thou canst not give!\" as it a brief and witty statement about the topic.\n',0,0,0,NULL),(59430,1546,'descriptive','3b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','<div style= \"column-count:2;\"><b>\'The Plate of Gold\'</b>\nOne day there fell in great Benares’ temple-court \nA wondrous plate of gold, whereon these words were writ; \nTo him who loveth best, a gift from Heaven.’ There at \nThe priests made proclamation: ‘At the midday hour, \nEach day, let those assemble who for virtue deem \ntheir right to Heaven’s gift the best; and we will hear the \ndeeds of mercy done, and so adjudge.’ \nThe news \nran swift as light, and soon from every quarter came \nnobles and munshis, hermits, scholars, holy men, \nand all renowned for gracious or for splendid deeds, \nMeanwhile the priests in solemn council sat and heard \nwhat each had done to merit best the gift of Heaven. \nSo for a year the claimants came and went. \nAt last, \nafter a patient weighing of the worth of all, \nthe priests bestowed the plate of gold on one who seemed, \nthe largest lover of the race - whose whole estate, \nwithin the year had been parted among the poor. \nThis man, all trembling with his joy, advanced to take \nthe golden plate when lo ! at his finger’s first touch \nit changed to basest lead ! All stood aghast; but when \nthe hapless claimant dropt it clanging on the floor, \nHeaven’s guerdon was again transformed to shining \ngold. \nSo far another twelve month sat he priests and judged. \nThrice they awarded - trice did Heaven refuse the gift. \nMeanwhile a host of poor, maimed beggars in the street\n lay all about the temple gate, in hope to move \nthat love whereby each claimant hoped to win the gift\nand well for them it was (if gold be charity), \nFor every pilgrim to the temple gate praised God, \nthat love might thus approve itself before the test, \nand so coins rained freely in the outstretched hands; \nbut none of those who gave, so much as turned to look \ninto the poor sad eyes of them that begged. \nAnd now \nThe second year had almost passed, but still the plate \nof gold , by whomsoever touched was turned to lead. \nAt length there came a simple peasant - not aware \nof that strange contest for the gift of God-to pay \na vow within the temple. As he passed along \nthe line of shrivelled beggars, all his soul was moved \nwithin him to sweet pity, and the tears welled up \nand trembled in his eyes. \nNow by the temple gate \nthere lay a poor, sore creature, blind, and shunned by all; \nbut when the peasant came, and saw the sightless face \nand trembling, maimed hands he could not pass, but knelt, \nand took both palms in his, and softly said: ‘O thou, \nmy brother! bear thy troubles bravely. God is good.’ \nThen he arose and walked straightway across the court, \nand entered where they wrangled of their deeds of love \nbefore the priests.\nA while he listened sadly then \nhad turned away but something moved the priest who held \nthe plate of gold to beckon to the peasant. So \nhe came, not understanding and obeyed, and stretched \nhis hand and took the sacred vessel. Lo! it shone \nwith thrice its former lustre, and amazed them all! \n‘Son’, cried the priest, ‘rejoice, the gift of God is thine. \nThou lovest best!’ And all made answers, ‘It is well.’ \nAnd, one by one, departed. But the peasant knelt \nand prayed, bowing his head above the golden plate; \nwhile o’er his soul, like morning, streamed the love of \nGod.\n                                    - James Henry Leigh Hunt<div style=\"column-count:2;\">\n','Write an appreciation of the poem \'The Plate of Gold\' in a paragraph format in about 12 to 15 sentences with the help of the following points.\ni. Poem and poet	ii. Theme/Central Idea	iii. Tone\niv. Structure and Stanzas	v. Rhyme and Rhythm		vi. Language and Imagery\nvii. Figures of Speech\n','','','                                      <b>Appreciation of the poem \'The Plate of Gold\'</b>\ni. Poem and poet: The title of the poem is \'Plate of Gold\' and the poet is James Henry Leigh Hunt, who is an English poet and writer. His works were famous for their expressive descriptions and soulful qualities.\nii. Theme / Central Idea: The central idea of the poem is \'Service towards mankind is true service towards God\'. Only a man who loves all human beings alike can love God to the fullest.\niii. Tone: The tone of the poem is serious.\niv. Structure and Stanzas: The poem has been written in a free verse format and has no regular stanzas.\nv. Rhyme and Rhythm: As this is a narrative poem, it lacks rhythm and uniformity in its overall structure. There is no fixed rhyme scheme in this poem.\nvi. Language and Imagery: Language used is full of archaic words. Example: thou, thy, thine etc. The poet uses plenty of imagery to create a vivid picture.\nvii. Figures of Speech: The figures of speech used in the poem are Alliteration, Consonance, Imagery, Inversion, Onomatopoeia, Personification, Repetition and Simile. An example of Personification from the poem is \"and the tears welled up and trembled in his eyes.\", where tears have been given the animate quality of trembling.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59440,1546,'descriptive','3b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','<div style= \"column-count:2;\"><b>\'Leisure’</b>\nWhat is this life if, full of care, \nWe have no time to stand and stare? \nNo time to stand beneath the boughs \nAnd stare as long as sheep or cows? \nNo time to see, when woods we pass \nWhere squirrels hide their nuts in grass? \nNo time to see, in broad daylight, \nStreams full of stars, like skies at night? \nNo time to turn at Beauty’s glance, \nAnd watch her feet, how they can dance? \nNo time to wait till her mouth can \nEnrich that smile her eyes began? \nA poor life this if, full of care, \nWe have no time to stand and stare.\n                      - William Henry Davies<div style=\"column-count:2;\">\n','Write an appreciation of the poem \'Leisure’ in a paragraph format in about 12 to 15 sentences with the help of the following points.\ni. Poem and poet ii.	ii. Theme/Central Idea	iii. Tone\niv. Structure and Stanzas	v. Rhyme and Rhythm		vi. Language and Imagery\nvii. Figures of Speech\n','','','','                                          <b>Appreciation of the poem \'Leisure\'</b>\ni. Poem and poet: The title of the poem is \'Leisure\' and the poet is William Henry Davies, a Welsh poet, whose works often included his own observations about life and his experiences of meeting different people.\nii. Theme / Central Idea: The theme of the poem is to make humankind understand the importance of appreciating the small things in life. The poet aims to communicate through the poem, the obsession of humans with material objects, which results in their ignorance and they are unable to see the beauty of nature that surrounds them.\niii. Tone: The tone of the poem is reflective as the poet wants people to think about how they are ignoring the beauty of nature that is all around them.\niv. Structure and Stanzas: The poem consists of seven rhyming couplets in an interrogative form so as to emphasise the poet\'s point that humans are so consumed in their own lives, that they can\'t even spare some time to enjoy nature\'s bounty. The use of these couplets gives the poem a uniform structure.\nv. Rhyme and Rhythm: The rhyme scheme of the poem is aa, bb, cc, dd, ee, ff, gg. The use of couplets gives the poem a steady rhythm.\nvi. Language and Imagery: The language is simple and straight forward. The poem contains imagery. Example: \'Streams full of stars\', \'And watch her feet, how they can dance\'. etc.\nvii. Figures of Speech: The figures of speech used in the poem Alliteration, Consonance, Imagery, Interrogation, Metaphor, Personification, Repetition and Simile. An example of Interrogation is \"No time to see, in broad daylight, Streams full of stars, like skies at night?\" - here, the poet asks a question, not to get an answer, but to lay emphasis on the point that he is trying to make.\n',0,0,0,NULL),(59443,1546,'descriptive','3b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','<div style= \"column-count:2;\"><b>\'The Vet\'</b>\nTo be a successful and competent vet, \nNeeds knowledge exceedingly wide, \nFor each of the patients he’s likely to get \nPossesses a different inside. \nHe must know why the cat is refusing her milk, \nWhy the dog is not eating his bone, \nWhy the coat of the horse is not shining like silk, \nWhy the parrot does nothing but groan; \nWhy the ducks and the chickens are failing to lay, \nWhy so faint the canary bird sings, \nAnd if he is called to the zoo, he must say\n An incredible number of things.\n If the lion’s caught a cold, \nIf the zebra’s getting old, \nIf the centipede has trouble with his feet, \nIf the hippo’s feeling ill, \nIf the bison’s got a chill, \nIf the Arctic fox is suffering from heat, \nIf some virulent disease \nHas attacked the chimpanzees, \nIf the tortoise hasn’t stirred for several years, \nIf the bear’s too full of buns, \nIf the cobra eats her sons, \nIf the panther has a wife who chews his ears; \nIf giraffes have had a tiff \nAnd their necks are feeling stiff\nIf hyenas will not laugh at keepers’ jokes, \nIf the monkey’s pinched his tail, \nIf the rhino’s looking pale, \nIf the elephant eats paper-bags and chokes, \nIf the camel hurts his hump, \nIf the kangaroo won’t jump, \nIf the crocodile turns cannibal and bites, \nThey run away and get That omniscient, the vet \nAnd expect him to put everything to rights. \nProfoundly I pity the vet, who must learn \nSuch a very great deal for his pay; \nMy son, I advise you most strongly to earn \nYour living an easier way. \nDon’t attempt to attend the zoological crowd; \na far more advisable plan \nIs to call yourself ‘Doctor’, and so be allowed \nTo treat the illnesses of man.\n                                             - Guy Boas<div style=\"column-count:2;\">\n','Write an Appreciation of the poem \'The Vet\' in a paragraph format in about 12 to 15 sentences with the help of the following points.\ni. Poem and poet	ii. Theme/Central Idea	iii. Tone\niv. Structure and Stanzas	v. Rhyme and Rhythm		vi. Language and Imagery\nvii. Figures of Speech\n','','','                                       <b>Appreciation of the poem \'The Vet\'</b>\ni. Poem and poet: The title of the poem is \'The Vet\' and it is written by Guy Boas.\nii. Theme / Central Idea: The central idea of the poem is to convey the challenges faced by a vet. The poem is a humorous account of the problems that a vet has to deal with. It aims to caution the youth about the hardships they would have to face if they choose to become a vet.\niii. Tone: The tone of the poem is humorous and light.\niv. Structure and Stanzas: The poem consists of 9 stanzas, where the first three stanzas and the last two stanzas have four lines each; while stanza 4, 5, 6, and 7 have six lines each. Though the stanzas differ in length, they do give the poem a uniform structure.\nv. Rhyme and Rhythm: The rhyme scheme of the poem is - Stanza 1, 2, 3, 8, 9 - abab; Stanza 4, 5, 6, 7 aabccb. The rhyme scheme gives the poem a rhythm.\nvi. Language and Imagery: The language used is simple and humorous. Imagery is used in the poem to paint a vivid image of the different animals and their problems.\nvii. Figures of Speech: The figures of speech used in the poem are Alliteration, Consonance, Hyperbole, Imagery, Inversion, Onomatopoeia, Personification, Repetition and Simile. An example of Alliteration from the poem is \"Profoundly I pity the vet, who must learn\" as the sound of the letter \'p\' is repeated in the line. The line is also an example of Inversion as the words have been rearranged for a poetic effect.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59450,1546,'descriptive','3b',5,2,'Out of Text Book','<div style= \"column-count:2;\"><b>\'The Bees\'</b>\nSo work the honey- bees, creatures that by a rule in \nnature teach \nThe art of order to a peopled kingdom, \nThey have a king and officers of sorts; \nWhere some, like magistrates, correct at home; \nOthers, like merchants, venture trade abroad; \nOthers, like soldiers, armed in their stings; \nMake boot upon the summer’s velvet buds; \nWhich pillage they with merry march bring home \nTo the tent royal of their emperor ; \nWho, busied in his magesty, surveys, \nThe singing masons building roofs of gold, \nThe civil citizens kneading up the honey, \nThe poor mechanic porters crowding in \nTheir heavy burdens at his narrowgate, \nThe sad eyed Justice, with his surly hum, \nDelivering over to executors pale \nThe lazy yawning drone \n                                      - William Shakespeare<div style=\"column-count:2;\">\n','Write an appreciation of the poem \'The Bees\' in the paragraph format in 12 to 15 sentences with the help of the following points.\ni. Poem and poet	ii. Theme/Central Idea	iii. Tone\niv. Structure and Stanzas	v. Rhyme and Rhythm		vi. Language and Imagery\nvii. Figures of Speech\n','','','                                            <b>Appreciation of the poem \'The Bees\'</b>\ni. Poem and poet: The title of the poem is \"The Bees\' and it is written by William Shakespeare, who is a world-renowned poet and playwright. His works have been adapted in many languages across the globe.\nii. Theme / Central Idea: The central idea of the poem is that we should look at the way bees work together for each other\'s benefit. They follow the rules that nature has set for them and perfectly carry out the duty that is assigned to them. They are an example and ideal for humans to run their kingdoms with order and ease.\niii. Tone: The tone of the poem admiring and approving as the poet expresses how bees run their kingdoms efficiently and how humans should learn from them to do the same.\niv. Structure and Stanzas: The poem has no distinct stanzas and the lines are irregular in length. This gives the poem a non-uniform structure.\nv. Rhyme and Rhythm: The poem also does not have a rhyme scheme as it is written in a free verse format.\nvi. Language and Imagery: Language is old English with imagery used to describe the activities of the bees.\nvii. Figures of Speech: The figures of speech used in the poem are Alliteration, Consonance, Hyperbole, Imagery, Inversion, Metaphor, Repetition, Onomatopoeia, Personification, and Simile. An example of Simile from the poem is \"Others like merchants, venture trade abroad;\" -here the bees are directly compared to merchants.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59469,1549,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a Formal letter to the principal of your daughter\'s school to request her to grant her a leave of 4 days.','','','C/505, Shivlik Tower,\nThakur Village,\nKandivali East,\nMumbai.\n15th June, 2018\n\nThe Principal,\nModel High School,\nThakur Village,\nKandivali (East).\nMumbai.\nSubject: Leave Application for 4 days.\nRespected Madam,\nI would like to bring to your kind attention that my daughter, Anushka Dubey is studying in Grade 1 of your esteemed school. Due to some health problems, my father has been hospitalised and is recommended a minor surgery by the doctors.\nWe have been busy in taking care of him and are spending our nights in the hospital. I would be really obliged if you grant her a leave for 4 days so that we can cope with the situation better. She will resume school on 20th June, 2018. Whatever portion will be done in the class in her absence, we shall try to complete it within 2 days.\nI hope you will oblige.\nThanking you in anticipation.\nYours sincerely, \nMrs. Devika Dubey \n(Mother of Anushka Dubey)\nGrade I-Div: Α\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59478,1549,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a Formal letter to the Editor of a newspaper complaining about the bad condition of roads in your locality.','','','Bungalow No. 06, \nSector B; Mahavir Colony, \nAndheri (East). \nMumbai.\n21st June, 2018\n\nThe Editor,\nThe Times of India,\nMalad (East).\nMumbai.\nSubject: Bad condition of roads in our locality.\nDear Sir,\nI am a regular reader of your esteemed newspaper. Through the column, I want to draw the attention of the concerned authorities towards the bad condition of roads in our locality.\nThe main road is in a deplorable condition. During the rainy season, potholes are filled with water which creates immense trouble for the pedestrians. Several serious accidents have already taken place. This road requires urgent repairing, before someone loses ha her life.\nHope this letter finds a suitable column in your daily and prove as an eye opener for the concerned authorities.\nThanking you. \nYours sincerely,\nXYZ\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59487,1549,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a Formal letter to the Police Inspector of your locality, bringing to his notice the burglary that took place last night in your neighbourhood.','','','Mr. R. Saxsena,\nDevgiri Towers,\nSolapur.\n4th Feb., 2010\n\nThe Police Inspector,\nJawahar Police Station,\nSolapur.\nSubject: Theft in Devgiri Nagar.\nSir,\nThis is to inform you that our colony is facing a lot of insecurity at night, since the past fifteen days. Last week, one of our neighbour\'s bike parked outside his house has been stolen.\nTwo days back, Mr. Sawant was out of station when the burglars broke into his locked house and took away possessions worth Rs.50,000/-.\nLast night, my neighbour was returning from duty when three men stopped him and tried to snatch away all his belongings. Luckily for him, our dog began to bark and we all rushed to the rescue of Mr. Shakeel, our neighbour.\nWe request you to keep vigil during the night and keep our area out of bounds from these anti-social elements. On our part, we extend all co-operation to make your work meaningful.\nThanking you,\nYours faithfully,\nR. Saxsena\nResident of Devgiri Towers.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59492,1549,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a Formal letter to the Ward Officer of your area requesting him to get the garbage heap near your house removed. Explain the hardships you are facing.','','','6 Suman Apartments,\nGarodia Nagar,\nGhatkopar,\nMumbai, 400 077.\n22 May, 2021\n\nTo\nThe Ward Officer\n\'N\' Ward\nBrihanmumbai Municipal Corporation\nMumbai, 400 077\nSubject: Complaint about non-removal of garbage\nSir:\nI have to bring to your notice a serious public health problem faced by the people in my area.\nThe garbage heap near my house has not been cleared for the past seven days. It is stinking and the foul smell has made the life of the residents in the area miserable. Besides, mosquitoes, flies and other disease-carriers breed in these garbage dumps and pose a serious health hazard to all of us.\nI, therefore, request you to see to it that the garbage is cleared without further delay. and that, in future, the work of removing the garbage is carried out regularly.\nYours truly,\nXYZ\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59496,1549,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a Formal letter as Rakesh Shukla to a renowned photographer to invite him/her as the chief guest of a photography exhibition that is to be conducted in your school.','','','Vidya Niketan School\nM.G. Road, \nWorli, \nMumbai-400018\n30th January, 2020\n\nMrs. Mohini Naik\n3rd Floor, Poplar House, \nVijay Vihar, \nGoregaon, \nMumbai-400060\nSubject: Invitation to preside as the chief guest at the school\'s photography exhibition\nRespected Sir/Madam,\nAs the student representative, I would like to formally invite you on behalf of everyone at Vidya Niketan School to preside as the Chief Guest at the photography exhibition organised by our school.\nWe have organised a photography exhibition on the 2nd of February, 2020 that will feature pictures clicked by our students. We understand that you must have a full calendar. However, it would be great if you coule spare two hours of your time for us. It would be an honour for us to hear you speak and have you as the Chief Guest for this event.\nAs a leading photographer of the country, your guidance and expertise will be extremely useful to all th participants. We\'d love you to initiate the exhibition with a short talk about photography and the techniques you use in your work. The inauguration ceremony is scheduled for 11:00 a.m. in the school auditorium and the event ends at 1:00 p.m. Kindly let us know about your schedule. We sincerely hope that you can find time to grace this occasion with your presence.\nYours truly, \nRakesh Shukla\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59502,1549,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a Formal letter as Neerja Joshi to your ward officer complaining about the fact that half of streetlights in your neighbourhood have not been functioning properly for the past week.','','','Ganesh Society,\nKarve Lane, Kothrud, \nPune - 411038\n12th August, 2019\n\nThe Ward Officer\nPMC Ward Office, \nRanade Road, \nPune-411048\nSubject: Complaint about non-functional streetlights\nRespected Sir,\nI\'m a resident of Ward \'A\' in Pune. I\'m writing this letter to you regarding the streetlights in our locality on Karve Lane that haven\'t been functioning properly for the past week.\nPreviously, the lights that stopped working would promptly be repaired and we would face no inconvenience at all. However, since the past week, 9 out of the 12 streetlights on our lane have either been flickering or have not been working at all. It has become quite difficult for us to navigate the streets at night. It is also dangerous for the pedestrians, as it impairs the visibility of drivers. With the change in season, the heavy rains have added to our troubles. The lack of streetlights at night time might cause children as well as senior citizens to slip and hurt themselves.\nI request you to personally look into this grievance and ensure that the technicians are sent to fix the lights at the earliest.\nYours faithfully, \nNeerja Joshi\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59505,1549,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','As Abhinaya Yadav, write a Formal letter addressed to the organiser of the cultural festival of your city to become a volunteer.','','','Trinity Complex, \nVeer Savarkar Path, \nThane - 400606\n31st January, 2020\n\nThe Person-in-Charge\nJagruti Arts Festival, \nNaupada Cultural Centre, \nThane - 400602\nSubject: Application for registering as a volunteer\nRespected Sir/Madam,\nI have been attending your prestigious festival for the past 5 years. This year, I would like to witness it as a part of the organising team. I have always wanted to volunteer but I wasn\'t old enough to do so previously. This year, I have turned 14, which is the minimum age requirement for becoming a volunteer.\nI have always been a cultural enthusiast. I have participated in many competitions and won a lot of awards. For the past two years, I have been a part of my school\'s cultural committee and have been involved in the Annual Day planning. I have helped in the organisation part of all the events and have assisted in putting together a play this year. If given a chance, I\'m sure that I can be a valuable member of your volunteer team.\nKindly let me know about the application process so that I can register accordingly. I hope to be a part of this event and make it even more successful in its 10th year.\nYours sincerely, \nAbhinaya Yadav\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59527,1550,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a Informal letter to your brother advising him to take steps to improve his health.','','','101/Ashtavinayak Tower,\nBorivali (East).\nMumbai.\n13th June, 2018\nDear Niraj,\nI hope you find this letter in the best of your spirits. Yesterday, I received your progress report from your Head Master but your attendance was quite unsatisfactory. I was sorry to learn that you fall sick regularly.\nI know that during your exams, you are too engrossed in your studies to pay heed towards your health. Your dedication is appreciated but your studies should not hamper your health. I would like to remind you that \'Health is wealth\' and a balanced approach is the essence of life. Try to go to bed early and get up early in the morning. Exercise is vital for the proper functioning of the mind and body. Regular intake of milk, fruits and vegetables cannot be ignored.\nI hope you will follow my suggestions and keep me informed about the progress in your health.\nLooking forward to meeting you soon.\nYour loving sister,\nKalpana\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59530,1550,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a Informal letter to your friend discussing about features of a summer camp and inviting her to join it.','','','157/ Vishal Nagar,\nAurangabad.\n31st July, 2017\nDear Reema,\nI hope this letter finds you in the best of health. I am pleased to know that your summer vacation begins next week. I am writing this letter especially to invite you for the summer camp organized by our Housing Society. It has many features. It will be full of adventures, and new experiences. We will have a lovely time together.\nIt will certainly be a relief from the boring summer vacations. You will love the place as Q.8. you are a nature lover. Trekking, River Rafting, Rock Climbing, Bird Watching are some of the adventurous features of this Camp. Apart from this, there will be special lectures on \'The Importance of Values in our Life\' and lots of fun.\nLet me know about the date and time of your arrival as soon as you can so that Dad and I can come to pick you up at the airport. I do hope that you will accept my invitation and won\'t disappoint me. Eagerly waiting for your positive reply.\nConvey my regards to uncle and aunty and lots of love to your younger sister, Tanisha.\nYours lovingly,\nSheena\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59533,1550,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a Informal letter to your friend congratulating him on winning a scholarship.','','','56-D/Mehar CHS, \nChembur.\nMumbai.\n5th June, 2017\nDear Amit,\nThanks for giving the happiest news about your having won a scholarship. You rea deserved it and achieved it.\nMy happiness knew no bounds, when I got the news. The joy of your victory was shared by every member of our family, as this happiness and achievement is very rare and not possible for all. You are, indeed, the first one in our friend circle to have won such a well merited distinction. Needless to add, a bright future awaits for you, my friend.\nI congratulate you heartily on your brilliant performance. Now, what about the celebration party? We will troop up by the dozen if you care to invite us. I end by wishing you all the best. With sincere regards.\nYour friend,\nTanya\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59535,1550,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a Informal letter to your uncle thanking him for the birthday gift he has sent you.','','','Jay Niketan, \nMasjid Lane, \nSolapur, 413 001. \n18 April, 2021\nMy dear Mama,\nThank you so much for the fantastic birthday gift. How did you guess that I wanted a guitar so badly?\nI have already joined guitar classes. They are very good indeed! Since we are now having vacations, I can also practise all day at home. Very soon I shall be reaching the second grade. My teacher says I am quite good!\nMy friends often come to hear me play. In fact, Saurabh wants me to play at his birthday party next month! I am practising hard for it as I want to put up a good show.\nThank you once again, Mama. How are Mami and Anu? Please convey my regards to them.\nYours affectionately, \nAnkit\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59537,1550,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a Informal letter as Tanvi to a friend who had a minor injury while playing football, asking her if she\'s well and wishing her a speedy recovery.','','','702, Raunak Complex, \nPratap Nagar, \nNagpur - 440022\n22nd February, 2020\nDear Neha,\nI heard that you sprained your ankle in the district level football match last week. I\'m sorry I couldn\'t connect with you sooner as I was busy with my semester exams. Although it\'s a minor injury, I\'d advise you to rest for a week and allow it to heal.\nI know how hard it is to have to sit at home, especially when all your friends are attending school. However, you can use this time to study everything you need to for your examination. You can also use the extra hours to read books, watch movies and pursue hobbies that you don\'t otherwise get time for. Instead of thinking about what you can\'t do, try focusing on all that you can do. This will help you stay happy and get you back on your feet sooner.\nDo write back to me when you get time and give my best wishes to your family. Wish you a speedy recovery.\nYour loving friend, \nTanvi\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59540,1550,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a Informal letter as Abhishek Chaudhari to your aunt who\'s a famous doctor, asking her advice on pursuing a career in the medical field.','','','Pavan House, \nAir India Colony, \nSantacruz-400029\n6th March, 2020\nDear Aunt Sarita,\nI hope you are doing well. I thought I\'d write a letter rather than wait to talk to you in person. Recently, I have been thinking a lot about choosing a career for my future. I feel a strong pull towards the medical profession and it is due to your influence.\nI have always looked up to you for how many people you help everyday by being a doctor. I know that it may seem like an attractive career option, but there\'s also a lot of hard work that goes into it. I am ready to give it my 100% and I\'m sure my interest in science and biology in particular, will prove to be beneficial. I know that only a few manage to become good doctors. Since you\'ve been a Doctor for the past 25 years, you\'re the best person to advise about this profession. Your suggestions would really help me a lot in choosing the right career path. I would like to discuss this in detail whenever you get time.\nI hope to hear from you soon.\nYour nephew,\nAbhishek\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59544,1550,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','You have just returned after your first experience of the kite - festival in Gujarat /Ahmedabad. You were thrilled with the festivities. You have a friend who lives abroad. Write a Informal letter to your friend describing how you enjoyed the kite-festival.','','','B-6, \"Global Residency\', \n34, Shantidoot Marg, \nOff L.B.S. Marg, \nBhandup, Mumbai. \nJanuary 16, 2018.\nDear Sameer,\nHi, How are you? I could not write to you earlier as I was busy with my tests and project work. I am sure you have had a great celebration of Christmas and New Year as well.\nWe, too, celebrated one of our traditional festivals the kite flying festival-called Makar Sankrant. My friends and I bought several kites of different materials and sizes. Soon after breakfast on the morning of 14th January, we made our way to the terrace of our building from where we flew our kites. We also entered into a competition with the residents of the neighbouring building. Though we lost some kites, we were not disappointed for we knew we still have opportunities throughout the day. And rightly so, just in the afternoon, we began flying our kites once again, but this time from backyard of our building. We used all our skills and were able to cut at least 8 to 10 kites till evening. Later on, my cousins and my uncle joined us in flying the lantern-kites which adorned the night sky making it look beautiful and decorative. How I wished you had been here!\nMy mother also served us specially prepared dishes during the mealtimes and of course traditional sweets which were superbly delectable. It was an enjoyable event for all of us. I do hope you enjoy reading this account much as I did writing it to you.\nMy kind regards to all at home.\nYour loving friend,\nPrasann\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59548,1550,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Imagine that you are Sanjay and write a Informal letter of thanks to your Uncle.','','','701, \"Greenfields Apartments\", \nOpp ICICI Bank, \nLink Road, \nMalad (W),\nMumbai.\nMarch 6, 2018\nDear Uncle Nitin,\nI hope this letter finds you and Aunty in good spirits. All of us including Grandfather an and are enjoy the bright summer with the expectation of a good monsoon.\nI have basically written this letter to express my deep gratitude to you for the special car you took of me while my parents were abroad on an urgent assignment. I remember how day you would sit with me to attend to my studies in the early evening and then take me with Aunty for some recreation - sometimes to the Mall down the road and sometimes beach. The most memorable day was last Saturday when we went shopping and then movie. How I enjoyed myself!\nThank you Uncle for all those wonderful times I shared with you and also for the two gift you gave me.\nMay God bless and keep you in His ever-loving care.\nRegards from Mummy, Daddy and Anjali.\nYour loving nephew,\nSanjay\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59551,1550,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a Informal letter to your aunt requesting her to send your cousin to spend Diwali with you.','','','Lake View,\n79, Ridge Road, \nMumbai - 400102.\n15th July, 2016.\nMy dear aunt,\nHow are you? How are Uncle, Abhay and Simran? I am sure you must be surprised to receive this letter from me.\nOur Diwali vacation will begin in the first week of October. Every year I used to be happy in the company of Manoj, my elder brother. Now Manoj has gone abroad for higher studies. I miss him very much, especially on holidays. Diwali will be miserable without Manoj. I cannot enjoy at all. I would love to have Abhay with me during Diwali holidays, specially during the festival.\nSimran, I am sure, won\'t mind it. There are other cousins to keep her company\nAunty, I hope you understand my situation. Please convince uncle and arrange to send Abhay at least two days before Diwali, so we can do shopping together.\nUncle must be busy as usual. Convey my regards to him. Explain to Abhay how much I nee his company. I am depending fully on you to help me.\nThank you,\nYour loving nephew,\nSuresh\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59574,1554,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','It is unfair to be cruel towards animals as they are helpless, poor creatures. Prepare a speech to be delivered in the morning assembly about the \'Cruelty towards Animals.','','','                                             <b>Cruelty towards Animals</b>\nGood morning! Respected Principal, Teachers and my dear friends.\nToday, I am going to express my views on the topic, \'How Can We Prevent Animal Abuse? It is commonly seen that cats, dogs, horses and livestock animals are subjected to abuse by humans.\nLet\'s try and make a difference to these animals who cannot even share their feelings and agony with anyone. When we feel cold, they are cold too. They too feel hungry, just like us.\nHere is what you and I can do: Whenever you find any wound, patches of missing hair or any kind of infection on the animals\' body, please take them to a vet. Similarly, if you come across any extremely thin, starving or limping animal, take it to a vet too. Avoid keeping your pet chained. Be aware and notice possible indicator for abuse. Any case of abuse should be reported immediately. You and only you can make a difference! I make an appeal to you, to respect animals and treat them with love. Be kind!\nThank you!\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59575,1554,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a speech on World Environment Day.','','','                                           <b>World Environment Day</b>\nA very good morning to Principal Sir, teachers and my dear friends. Today, we are here to celebrate, World Environment Day. A day which is especially celebrated to know and solve all the environmental issues. As we all know, that it is being celebrated for years worldwide with a lot of enthusiasm in order to create awareness and bring positive changes in the environment.\nIt is celebrated every year on 5th of June since 1973. It aims to engage and draw the of millions of people including political and health organisations across the make new plans and implement them accordingly. It is very necessary to add issues like wastage and loss of food, increasing global warming, deforestation, pe industrialisation, etc in order to control the negative environmental changes.\nWe need to do something to reduce the rate of climate change. The 4 R techniques. Reuse, Recycle and Refuse can be very effective in reducing the impact of our in activities over our natural ecosystem. Our positive steps will really help in environmental issues in the near future. Together we can! Together we will! Healthy Environment! Healthy Future! Come on India!\nThank you.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59577,1554,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a speech on the occasion of Independence Day for your school.','','','Respected Guest, Principal, Teachers and friends,\nWith great pride, I speak to you on the 65th Independence Day of Amar Bharat. I want all of you to close your eyes and try to imagine the scene of 73 years ago when the Indian Tri colour was hoisted while the British flag was lowered. Splendid! I must say.\n But really, do we live and respect our Independence? Do we at least introspect and audit the strength and weakness of ourselves and our country? Do we even pledge to march ahead and make India a super power?\nWe are all silent. Yes, as a young boy of 15 years, I\'d like to promise myself that as I live, I will respect my country and value my independence. I breathe fresh air in the independent India. I want to thank all my forefathers and freedom fighters who struggled to give me this beautiful day. It\'s a matter of pride. It\'s not a holiday. It\'s a day to renew our vows, introspect, reflect and at least, vow to move ahead. Yes, I vow to you, my India, my country, that I will always maintain your glory. To you, my country, a very Happy Birthday.\nLet us all salute the Tricolour and promise never to disrespect the flag of our country. Yes, friends, on our shoulders, lies the future of this beautiful nation. Let us always sing the National Anthem and voice the pledge with respect and honour for our motherland.\n\'Hum sab Bharatiya hain\', say it with pride. I love my India.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59578,1554,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare a speech for \'Conservation of Conventional Resources\' which is to be submitted in an interschool competition.','','','                                     <b>Conservation of Conventional Resources</b>\nGood morning, teachers and all my dear friends. I, Arun Mahajan, am here talk about the need for conservation of conventional resources.\nConventional resources fall under non-renewable resources. A few examples are coal, natural gas, petroleum, firewood, oil and so on. They are acquired through mining, cutting down of trees, drilling in the ocean, etc. They form a major part of the resources required by us for infrastructural development.\nWhile these resources can renew themselves, they take almost centuries to replenish. Today, humans are using these resources at a rapid rate, which has resulted in their rapid depletion. Burning of fuel, releasing industrial waste in water and cutting down trees lead to pollution. If this continues, we will soon run out of these resources.\nTherefore, we must conserve conventional resources. For example, one should use public transport, use electricity judiciously, and switch to using renewable energy resources such as solar energy and tidal energy. I would like to urge all of you to conserve the conventional resources to help protect and conserve our environment. Thank you.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59579,1554,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare a speech for the occasion of International Yoga Day to be celebrated in your school.','','','                                                     <b>International Yoga Day</b>\nGood morning, honourable Chief Guest, respected Principal, teachers and my schoolmates. I, Rohan Desai, stand before you to speak on International Yoga Day.\nYoga Day is celebrated worldwide on the 21st of June every year. Prime Minister Narenda Modi has given this day its international acclaim as a part of his UN address in 2015. He suggested 21st June, as it signifies the longest day of the year in the Northern Hemisphere.\nYoga is a 5000 years old Indian form of exercise. It doesn\'t just refer to the physical form of exercise, but also to the spiritual exercise of the mind. It consists of exercises or asanas, which have multiple benefits for the human body like an improved immune system, clarity of mind, a flexible body, better bone health, and increased blood circulation. There are close to 8 lakh different asanas in Yoga. Today, people across the globe have taken to Yoga as a way of life.\nTherefore, I encourage you all to take up Yoga as a way of life on the occasion of International Yoga Day.\nThank you.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59580,1554,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare a speech on the topic \'Animals are our friends\', on the occasion of your school\'s Annual Day.','','','                                                  <b>Animals Are Our Friends</b>\nGood morning, respected principal, teachers, students and parents. I welcome all of you to the annual day celebration. I, Neha Dixit, stand before you to talk about Animals as our friends.\nMahatma Gandhi once said that if one wishes to see how developed and progressed a country is, then one should observe how the animals of the country are treated. Today, we are proud of our country\'s rapid economic growth coupled with great development in the fields of technology, infrastructure, health and education. Yet there remains a field which we need to work upon.\nOur country needs to take significant measures for the welfare of animals. At present, the government is creating animal-friendly laws. The people of the country should join the cause by volunteering at pet shelters, conducting vaccination drives for stray animals, or coming together in the form of cooperative societies that focus on nourishment of animals and birds.\nAnimals have been our friends since the beginning of the human civilization. They help our farmers, reside in our homes as our pets, help in the maintenance of biodiversity and environment and form an intricate part of our ecosystem.\nI would thus like to urge all of you to care towards the animal world and make this world a better place for them.\nThank you.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59581,1554,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare a speech focusing on the topic of Waste Management.','','','                                                   <b>Waste Management</b>\nGood morning respected principal, teachers and all my schoolmates. I, Ryan Fernandes, am here today to speak on a topic of extreme importance: waste management.\nWaste management refers to the process of collection, disposal and recycling of industrial and domestic waste materials. Perhaps the greatest advantage of waste management to a country is in keeping its surroundings clean and disease-free.\nMany western countries have been successful in developing a very good waste management system. Sweden has a state-of-the-art recycling industry in place. It imports waste from other\ncountries to convert it into electricity. It is necessary for us to implement similar policies to manage and recycle the waste in our country.\nA number of NGOs and government agencies are organising workshops and awareness programs. Even corporate organisations are beginning to realise the importance of waste management. They conduct workshops to educate their employees on the importance of segregating garbage into dry and wet waste. Even at the community level, citizens come forward to actively participate in the process of waste management.\nI hereby appeal to everyone to give back to the society by managing waste on an individual level and keep our environment clean and green.\nThank you.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59582,1554,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a speech on the occasion of Independence Day Celebrations in your school.','','','                                                      <b>Independence Day</b>\nRespected Principal, Teachers and my dear friends,\nGood morning, Today is a day of great Importance to all Indians, the day we celebrate the freedom we gained by fighting against a foreign rule. While we remember those stalwarts who made many sacrifices to make this freedom possible for us, we should also pause to reflect on what this freedom means to us and what use we are making of it.\nFreedom does not mean that we can do anything we want without regard for others. Freedom does not mean that we can earn money by hook or by crook, or indulge in corrupt practices. Freedom means using the opportunities that our Constitution provides us so as to do our best in whatever field we choose. If every Indian used his or her freedom to become self-sufficient, to serve the poor and helpless, to spread an awareness of social and economic justice. then that freedom will have been well used.\nI urge all my fellow students not to misuse this freedom. Our forefathers fought bravely to achieve it. Let us make them proud and take this nation forward to the pinnacles of glory and success. Jai Hind!\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59583,1551,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Expand the Idea : Procrastination is the Thief of Time','','','                                           <b>Procrastination is the Thief of Time</b>\nIt has always been said, \"Never put off for tomorrow what you can do today\", Yet, there are many people who enjoy postponing things. Such people do not realise the dangers of delaying. The more we postpone, the more work piles up. Work will never disappear if we postpone it. So finally, we have no choice but to deal with it. We complete the work eventually in a careless manner.\nPrecious time wasted means opportunities lost and lost forever. By the time, we realis how much time we have wasted and how many opportunities we have missed, it ma be too late. Sometimes, a person has to pay a very heavy price for it. The one who delay insuring his house will regret it when the house is gutted by a sudden fire. The student who goes on postponing studies will need to burn the midnight oil for the last minute preparation.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59584,1551,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Expand the Idea : Cut you Coat according to your Cloth','','','                                             <b>Cut you Coat according to your Cloth</b>\nThis proverb advises, to cut and stitch the coat according to the cloth available in harm It also warns that the size of the coat should not exceed the piece of the cloth in hand, else the cloth will be wasted, as it would be impossible to stitch something bigger the what the cloth permits. It is necessary for everyone to make a proper plan before begins to put any task into practice. A person who spends more than his income, will soon fall into trouble. He has to face financial problems and hardships and thereby, will have mental agony. So, this proverb instructs us to live within our means and resources. Those who do not know now to make both ends meet, will suffer a lot and their lives would become miserable. Thus, harmony and proportion is extremely essential for income and expenditure.\nIf one does something, without knowing his limitation, he will soon repent his action. If a person spends more than one\'s income, he will have to fall in some peril or the other. So, the proverb explains that we should spend according to our income and available resources.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59585,1551,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Expand the Idea : No Gains without Pains','','','                                               <b>No Gains without Pains</b>\nThis basically means that man cannot succeed without hard work. When our aspirations are fulfilled at the flick of our fingers, we never value this achievement because it hardly accompanies any labour. A perfect tea prepared on a number of odd combinations tastes wonderful after the content are perfectly blended. A gold medal received for an event stands to its value only after every attempt has been a vigorous performance. Hillary Tenzing made it to the Everest only after being confronted by the number of failures. Our leading actors have made it to the apex not by mere chance but by earnest hard work.\nA person grumbles about his torn shoes until some day he sees a man without feet. Our joys will never be meaningful unless we experience the taste of sorrow. It is our sincere effort that will show us both the sides of the same coin. In this age of quick fix, many people get easily frustrated when their efforts do not meet with instant success. They must be made to realise that each failure, if taken objectively, takes us closer to success. There is no substitute to hard work. Success knows no short cuts. The same could be used to illustrate the idea - \"Sweet are the fruits of adversity\".\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59586,1551,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Expand the Idea : No man is an island','','','                                          <b>\'No man is an island\'</b>\nThe famous words by John Donne \'No man is an island\' convey that no human can be completely independent and self-sufficient.\nHuman beings are \'social animals\', because they love being in the company of other humans, who share similar likes and dislikes. We tend to depend on many people through the course of our lives. As children, we depend on our parents to feed us, bathe us, and nourish us. As teenagers, we need our friends and our teachers for guidance and support. As adults, we depend on the society and as we get old we depend on our family members for our well-being. The interdependence of humans promotes mutual well-being and an overall development of all in the society. Since no individual can be completely independent in its absolute sense, the proverb \'No man is an island\' is quite apt.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59587,1551,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Expand the Idea : \'The early bird catches the worm\'','','','                                  <b>\'The early bird catches the worm\'</b>\nBirds are among the first ones to start their day by searching for food and feeding their hatchlings. If we aren\'t able to begin our task on time, we won\'t be able to complete them. The quote lays great emphasis on the ideal of punctuality. We would reach a place on time, only if we begin early. There is a famous incident of a man who went to visit Mahatma Gandhi but reached 10 minutes late and hence was not allowed to meet him. Had the man reached on time, he would have been able to meet Gandhiji. Most of the successful people in history valued time and punctuality. Cultivating a habit of being present before the specified time has its benefits. Just like the bird, we should cultivate the habit of being prompt if we wish to achieve success.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59588,1551,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Expand the Idea : ‘Practice makes a man perfect\'','','','                                <b>\'Practice makes a man perfect\'</b>\nThe proverb \'Practice makes a man perfect\' means that the road to achieve perfection is through practice.\nThomas Edison is known for his invention of the light bulb. But we should take note of the fact that he had to practise his experiments more than a 1000 times to create the final version of an electric light bulb.\nAll of us actively seek to be perfect in our daily life. Only when a cricketer practises a stroke many times, is he able to achieve the perfect shot. Same is the case with a musician, who rehearses for hours, in order to hit the perfect notes.\nWhen we practise, we also get the opportunity to understand a process in detail; we get a chance to locate the faults and become an expert. Thus, practice forms an essential part of the process when one wants to achieve perfection.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59589,1551,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Expand the Idea : Importance of Women in the Family','','','                                <b>Importance of Women in the Family</b>\nWe should acknowledge the massive roles that the female members in our family play in our overall development. Our mother plays the role of a manager, a health officer, a leader as well as an administrator in the house. A mother is the first person that a child connects with as it enters the world. She not only provides the child with nutrition and care but also actively participates in its growth process, physically as well as intellectually. She takes care of the health of the family members, manages finances and keeps the house in order. The ones blessed with a sister find a life-long friend in her. Our grandmothers enrich us with their invaluable wisdom and experiences. The women in our lives shape us into the person that we become. Their influence and contribution in our lives can never be measures and we should thus never forget the crucial parts that they play in our lives.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59590,1551,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Expand the Idea : Role of Media in our Life','','','                                                      <b>Role of Media in our Life</b>\nMedia is a carrier of information. The concept of media has existed in our society sites a long time. In ancient times, public gatherings sock place in order to set down rules and regulations. This came to be known as direct democracy and was largely practised in the Greek and Roman cities. In today\'s world, media exists in two different forms, digital and print.\nNow, in the modern era, media has come so play the fundamental role of the fourth piller of democracy.\nToday, the media is a vigil-keeper, as information dispenser as well as an institution that reminds those in authority about their accountability towards the citizens of the country.\nThrough various blogs, journals, podcasts, interviews, talk shows as well as newspapers and magazines, media has been influential in limiting the negative activities prevalent in our society such as crimes and corruption\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59591,1551,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Expand the theme : ‘Pride goes on horseback, but returns on foot\'.','','','                                    <b>Pride goes on horseback, but returns on foot</b>\nPride refers to having too high an opinion of oneself, one\'s position and possession. Pride makes a person think that he is superior to others. Our achievements in life are due to our pains and hard work. But we should never be proud of accomplishments in life. Whenever pride begins to\nact, there begins our adversity. A proud man will have little consideration for others and treats others with contempt. He who has pride will finally suffer defeat or mee with a shameful end. When a proud man meets with a bad end, others will have no sympathy for him. History is full of examples of powerful monarchs who came riding the horse of pride and returned in humility. King John of England met with a shameful end due to his proud an overbearing nature. A proud man should be aware of the reality that a day will come when t happiness and comfort given by pride will give way to the pain of humiliation. In short, the tr quality of a man is humility, not pride.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59592,1551,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Expand the Theme : Where there is a will, there is a way.','','','                                   <b>Where there is a will, there is a way.</b>\nWhere there is a will, there is a way is an old proverb in English which teaches us that \'determination\' is necessary to get a task completed or a job done. To learn or achieve something in life, willpower acts as a catalyst and enhances the speed of action. So, it is good to have determination even to the smallest tasks in life and never give up easily. All of us wish to achieve many things in life. But usually many of us do not succeed in achieving anything. And often we tend to curse our fate or misfortune. But the fact is that we have only ourselves to blame for our failures. It is not enough that we wish to achieve something. We should have the proper willpower and the proper drive or determination to carry on with our plans in the face of obstacles. Willpower is the key to the greatest of achievements. The more we are determined to win... the more we are on the road to success.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59593,1551,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Expand the Theme : All That Glitters Is Not Gold','','','                                  <b>All That Glitters Is Not Gold</b>\nThis proverb holds much truth - in that - All that appears to be attractive does not necessarily have to be good. So, judging by appearances can be misleading. A book cannot be judged by its cover. A book with a very attractive cover may not have readable material inside. On the other hand, a book with a very dull cover may be very interesting. This is also applicable to many things in life. A stage show that is well advertised may be dull and monotonous whereas a movie that has received very little publicity may be quite entertaining.\nSo we must draw conclusions about the merits or demerits of anything purely on the basis of the way it is packaged. In this present age, marked by advertisement, manufacturers try to show their products in the best light so that people will buy them. But this does not necessarily mean that the product is well worth the cost. Even when we judge people, we should not do so by their looks. Gandhiji dressed in an ordinary loin cloth around himself, but he is still held in great reverence throughout the world. Abraham Lincoln was not endowed with good looks but he is considered to be one of the greatest American Presidents of all time. Mother Teresa had a very simple appearance. But people all over the world remember and revere her. So it is only right and befitting to say that all that glitters is not gold.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59594,1553,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the following story with the help of the given points:\n                                                 <b>A WITTY BLIND WOMAN</b>\nA woman becomes blind ………………. promises to pay handsome reward when cured…………………. if not nothing……………… Doctor begins treatment……………… slows down procedure…………………. declares treatment complete………………… demands payment……………… woman refuses…………… Dr. goes to court……………. Judge studies case minutely………………… punishes the Dr. for robbing the woman.\n','','','                                     <b>A WITTY BLIND WOMAN</b>\nIn a small village, there lived an old woman who became blind due to some illness. She visited many doctors and tried to get back her vision. Finally, she gave an advertisement in the paper that any doctor who cured her would be handsomely rewarded if she got back her vision.\nA young doctor who came in to see her said, \"I shall try to do my best.\"\nFor the first week, he was prompt with his treatment but gradually he began prolonging the treatment. After about six months, he tested the woman at different tests and declared that she was perfectly fine. The woman agreed that she had got back her vision and thanked the doctor for his efforts. But when the doctor asked, \"Give me my due reward. \"On this, she refused to give him anything saying, \"I\'m not fully cured. \"The furious doctor went to the court for help.\nThe judge asked the woman why she refused to pay the doctor, as earlier promised. She replied, \"It\'s true that I can see but I am not fully cured. \"The Judge wondered what such a statement meant. He asked her to make things very clear. The old woman said, \"Your Majesty, this kind doctor treated me for six months and I can see almost everything but I can also see that my expensive furniture and a few valuables have disappeared from my house. Do you think I should still pay the doctor for this kind deed done to me. \"The Judge realised that it was the doctor who had taken away the woman\'s belongings and hence, punished the doctor for robbing the old woman.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59595,1553,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the lines given below, and complete the story. Give the story a title:\nOne day a farmer was returning from the market in his bullock cart. Suddenly it began raining. The mud on the road became wet and sticky and the wheels of the cart got stuck in the mud. The cart would not move. The farmer did not know what to do.\nThe famer cried loudly, \".........\n','','','                               <b>God helps those who help themselves</b>\nOne day a farmer was returning from the market in his bullock cart. Suddenly it began raining. The mud on the road became wet and sticky and the wheels of the cart got stuck in the mud. The cart would not move. The farmer did not know what to do.\nThe famer cried loudly, \"Oh, God, why have you put me in such a terrible state? Now you have to help me.\" He went to the side of the road and sat down with his head in his hands.\nAfter some time a stranger came by and saw the farmer and the stuck cart. The farmer was still crying softly, \"Oh, God, please help me. Please help me.\"\nThe stranger went up to the farmer. \"Have you tried to move the cart?\" he asked. The farmer shook his head. \"No.\"\n\"Have you tried to do anything?\" asked the stranger.\n\"I have prayed to God,\" said the farmer.\n\"Come, let us try to move it,\" said the stranger. The two of them went behind the cart. Both of them together lifted and pushed the cart. Soon the wheels came out from the wet mud.\nThe farmer was happy. \"Thank you,\" he said to the stranger. \"I can now reach home before it gets dark. You have taught me that God only helps those who help themselves, not those who expect Him to do everything.\"\nThe stranger smiled and went on his way.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59597,1553,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Read the following story and change the ending. Give the story a title.\nA hungry fox passed by a vine of grapes. He stood under the vine. \"What a lovely bunch of grapes!\" he said.\nHe jumped but could not reach the grapes. They were too high for him. He tried again and again. It was of no use.\n\"Let it be. Those grapes are sour. I don\'t want them,\" said the tired fox. Saying this, he walked away.\n','','','                                          <b>The Clever Fox</b>\nA hungry fox passed by a vine of grapes. He stood under the vine. \"What a lovely bunch of grapes!\" he said. He jumped but could not reach the grapes. They were too high for him. He tried again and again. It was of no use.\nHowever, the wily fox did not want to leave without eating the grapes. He waited for some time. Finally, he saw a crow alight on the vine.\n\"Oh, smart crow, what a lovely beak you have!\" he said. \"But is it as sharp as my teeth? Or does it only look lovely but does no work?\"\n\"What do you mean?\" asked the crow angrily. \"Of course my beak is sharp!\"\n\"Prove it!\"\n\"Prove it? How can I?\"\n\"Well,\" said the clever fox, pretending to look around. \"You can.. can you break those bunches of grapes? It will show that your beak is sharp.\"\n\"Hal\" said the silly crow. \"That\'s an easy task! Here take this! Two bunches of grapes so fast! Now do you agree that my beak is sharp?\"\n\"Of course dear crow!\" murmured the fox, pouncing on the grapes. \"Of course your beak is sharp! But is your brain?\"\nBefore the crow could understand what the fox meant, the clever fox had run away with the grapes in his mouth!\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59598,1555,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','Have you ever wondered why soldiers are always clad in green? This is to enable them to camouflage themselves during wartime. Hiding in the jungles, their green attire blends into the surrounding trees and shrubs, making it difficult for the enemies to spot them.\nLong before man made use of camouflaging, insects have already adopted the tactic of disguise to escape from the clutches of their predators. By having body colors close to those of the rocks and dried leaves, they catch less attention from the predators and hence escape from being preyed. However, this kind of disguise works only if the insects remain still in the presence of their predators.\nButterflies and moths have developed a variety of camouflage strategies since they are quite defenseless and their predators - birds are abundant in supply. Many moth caterpillars resemble dead twigs while the young of certain species of butterflies appear like bird droppings. Adult butterflies and moths camouflage themselves too, in attempts to escape from their hunters - birds who are superior gliders. Possessing wings which resemble dried leaves help certain butterflies and moths to hide among heaps of dried leaves when predators are around.\nFortunately, not all insects choose the art of disguise to escape from their predators; otherwise, the world would be so dull and colorless. There are insects which assimilate the bright body colors of bees and wasps to escape from being pursued by their predators. The concept of mimicry was derived, owing to the bees and wasps. Long ago, birds had already learn to avoid brilliantly colored wasps and bees in fear of their painful stings. Hence, over millions of years, many harmless insects have assimilated the bees and wasps by imitating their bright body colors and shapes. In this way, they appear dangerous to their predators and hence, ward them off.\nMimics of the wasps and bees are most commonly found in the gardens. The furry, plump bee-fly not only appears like the bumble bee in terms of body colors, even its hums sound similar too. The only difference is that the bee-fly does not have a sting and is, hence harmless. The hoverfly is another insect which imitates the body colors of the wasps Their bodies are striped yellow and black. The only deviations are that hoverflies do not have stings and they have only one pair of wings each while wasps have two pairs each. These variations are hardly noticed by the predators and hence help them to escape.\n','Summarise in not more than 110 words, how camouflaging and mimicry help insects.','','','                                        <b>Camouflaging and Mimicry</b>\nCamouflaging and mimicry have helped defenceless insects escape from their predators. Camouflaging requires insects to have body colors close to the surroundings so as to appear less eye-catching to predators. The moth caterpillars look like dead twigs while certain butterfly caterpillars resemble bird droppings. Some butterflies and moths have wings that resemble dried leaves. Mimicry requires harmless insects to adopt the body colors and shapes of the wasps and bees so as to fool their predators into thinking that they are dangerous. Predators usually avoid them, thinking they have stings too. The bee-fly and hoverfly assimilate the body colors of the bumble bee and wasps respectively and the bee-fly even hums like the bumble bee.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59599,1555,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','As what geographers have estimated, about twenty percent of the earth\'s surface occupied by deserts. A majority of us view deserts as one unique kind of landscape-are with little or no rainfalls.\nIn actual fact, there are differences between the deserts, though in varying degrees. Whi it is common for laymen like us to see deserts as rocky or covered with gravel or pebble there are some where large sand dunes inhabit. Despite the fact that rainfall is minim temperatures do change in deserts, ranging from seasonal ones to daily changes where extreme heat and cold are experienced in the day and night.\nUnfavourable conditions in the deserts, especially the lack of water, have discouraged many living things from inhabiting these landscapes. Nevertheless, there are exceptionally surviving ones which, through their superb tactics, have managed to live through and still going strong. One such kind is the specialist annual plants which overcome seasonal temperature changes with their extremely short, active life cycles. During sudden rains the plant seeds pullulate and grow very quickly to make full use of the rain water. T flowers bloom and set seeds that ripen quickly in the hot sun too. Once the water dry, the mother plant dies, leaving behind the drought-resistant seeds, waiting patiently for the next rainy season to arrive.\nThe Cacti, a native in American deserts, adapts to the dry surroundings by having unique body structures. The plant has swollen stems to help store water that carries it through months. By having sharp pines instead of leaves, water loss through respiration is minimized. Besides, these pointed pines also help the plant ward off grazing animals, thus, enhancing its survival period.\nBesides plants, there are animals also with distinct surviving tactics in deserts. For instance : Skinks (desert lizards) metabolize stored fats in their bulbous tails, producing water to supplement their needs, just like what camels do with the stored food in their humps during long journeys through deserts. Antelopes like the addax, have very low water needs and hence are able to tolerate the conditions in deserts, extracting moisture from the food they eat.\nFinally, there are the sandgrouses (desert birds) which do not have special features to overcome the drought-like nature in deserts. Hence, to survive in these hot, dry deserts, they need to spend a large part of their time flying in search of waterholes.\n','Summarize in not more than 110 words, describing the life in deserts.','','','                                            <b>Life In Deserts</b>\nDespite the dry conditions in the deserts, some plants and animals still manage to survive there. One of them is the specialist annual plants. Their short life cycles allow them to germinate, grow and produce seeds during short rainy seasons. These seeds are drought-resistant and are able to wait for the next rainy season before starting their life cycles again. The Cacti adapts to the dry weather by having swollen stems for water storage and pine-like leaves to minimize water loss through respiration. Skinks generate water from stored fats in their tails and antelopes which requires very little water, survives in deserts by extracting water from the food they eat. Finally, the sandgrouse with no adaptive features turn to waterholes constantly for help.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59600,1555,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','Mumbai is often regarded as India\'s Capital of Hope. Often wondering why this is so, I made a fruitful trip down to the busy city, solving most of my queries.\nMumbai consists of seven islands, joined by land reclamation. Many Indians, especially those from the rural areas regard Mumbai as their paradise, since they could find work relatively easily here, as compared to their homelands.\nBeing the pillar for revenue collection, Mumbai\'s economic growth has far outperformed the other cities. In fact, its per capita (head) production of goods and services is about three times greater than that of Delhi - India\'s second most prosperous city. Despite the economic boom, Mumbai gave me an astonishing image of deterioration when I first stepped into the city.\nThe ostentatiously dignified imperial buildings, erected by the British, are so overly populated that they look as if they are toppling over any minute. There are the 1950s kind of black and yellow taxis, which appeared as if brutally thrashed, lining up like ants trails, clotting up the small avenues. Amidst the dins of traffic jams, stood the oppressed-looking buildings of Benetton outlets, foreign car dealerships, croissant-serving outlets and so on.\nThough unemployment is not a significant problem in Mumbai, housing is. A visit to Dharavi, a slum area in Mumbai will help clarify our imagination. The Mumbaikars so called \"houses\" are actually movable shacks, built from unwanted bits of tarpaulin, tin and cardboard. There are so many of them that a maze of alleys emerged, passable only when I walked sideways like a crab between them. Curious about the living conditions, I wondered around the maze, meeting groups of scantily clad kids and hungry, stray dogs Popping my inquisitive head into one of the small huts, I was totally amazed by their living conditions. Estimating about twelve or more Mumbaikars living in each hut, these two-storey houses are usually partitioned by rough platforms with ceilings no higher than five feet from the ground. Furthermore, \'these shacks look absolutely bare -- no furniture and I deduced that the inhabitants eat and sleep on the ground. In spite of the poor living conditions, many Indians still hope to migrate to Mumbai Interviewing a few of the newcomers, a majority of them said that they came to Mumbai to find jobs. There are some who regard Mumbai as buoyant floats, saving them from natural disasters and tyrannies in their homelands.\n','Summarize in not more than 110 words, how Mumbai existing situation contradicts its flourishing economic status.','','','                                        <b>Condition of Mumbai</b>\nDespite its economic boom, the conditions in Mumbai are always chaotic. The existing buildings in Mumbai are overly inhabited by the large population. With more immigrants flooding in, the emergence of slums is inevitable. The \"houses\" there, are actually shads made from unwanted materials like tarpaulin and cardboard. These shacks flooded the streets of Dharavi creating a maze, with spaces passable only if one walks sideways. The two storeyed, small huts, divided by rough platforms, often have low ceilings which are no more than five feet from the ground. These shabby huts are also barely furnished. Kids are usually seen running around with minimal clothes on them. Furthermore, traffic jams usually caused by old, shabby taxis are common daily sights there.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59602,1555,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','Valley of Flowers National Park is an Indian national park located in the state of Uttarakhand and is known for its beautiful meadows full of colourful flowers. This richly diverse area is also home to the Asiatic black bear, snow leopard, musk deer, brown bear, red fox, blue sheep, Himalayan monal pheasant and a host of other high altitude birds.\nThis enchanting park was unknown to the outside world due to its inaccessibility. In 1931, Frank Smythe, Eric Shipton and R.L. Holdsworth, all British mountaineers, lost their way while returning from a successful expedition to Mt. Kamet and stumbled across a valley, which was full of flowers. They were attracted to the beauty of the area and named it the \'Valley of Flowers\'. It was Frank Smythe who later authored a book by the same name.\nLocal people have been visiting the valley since ancient times. The yogis would also visit the valley for meditation. The valley was declared a national park in 1982 and now it is a World Heritage Site. The best time to visit the Valley of Flowers is during its blooming season that falls in July and August every year.\n','Go through the passage below and write a short summary on it. Suggest a suitable title.','','','                                    <b>The Valley Of Flowers</b>\nThe Valley of Flowers\' is a National Park located in the state of Uttarakhand. Globally renowned for its rich and colourful flowers, it is home to many endangered species of animals. It was known only to locals, but a team of British mountaineers discovered it in 1931 and named it \'The Valley of Flowers\'. It is recognized as a World Heritage Site and has a book written about it. The valley is in full bloom between July and August, which makes it the best time for a visit.\n','',0,0,0,NULL);
INSERT INTO `ep_questions` VALUES (59603,1555,'descriptive','5',5,0,'Out of Text Book','The Great Horned Owl is a spectacular hunting machine armed with excellent sight and hearing, as well as an ability to fly silently. Its diet comprises of just about anything and everything around its nest; from insects to fish and even owls and other animals up to two or three times its size.\nEvery year, Great Horned Owls are among the earliest nesting birds. They choose mates or strengthen their bonds with existing mates by December, and are often heard singing melodious duets before this time. Females are generally larger than males, but this does not necessarily affect the process of mate selection. An exceptionally large female can dwarf a small mate.\nThe reason for the male\'s smaller size may be to enhance its ability to hunt and provide food for the nest, as well as, its defence. One can also argue that the female\'s size can be highly intimidating to a nest-site invader. During the nesting period, females can lay two to five eggs.\nOnce hatched, the young owls or owlets are taken care of by their parents. This process generally lasts for two and a half months, but sometimes can last for a lesser amount of time. The young owls are so independent that sometimes they try to leave the nest even before they are capable of flight.\nThey feed on the ground or some nearby tree or structure for a while, and once they are able to fly, they follow the parents around. Gradually, the owlets learn to hunt from their parents who encourage them to hunt on their own. By the age of 10 months, the owlets are ready to leave their parents\' nests and live on their own.\n','Go through the passage below and write a short summary on it. Suggest a suitable title. ','','','                                       <b>The Great Horned Owls</b>\nThe Great Homed Owl is an excellent hunter, with fearsome sense of sight and hearing. To catch their prey, they fly silently and their diet consists of any insect, bird or animal that is easily available around them. They are known to find their mates, sing duets and start nesting well before the other birds. The female owls are larger in size while the males are swifter. They lay up to 5 eggs and take care of the babies for up to two and half months. Owlets are quick to learn. The owlets hunt by the age of 10 months as that is when they leave their parents\' nest to live by themselves.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59604,1555,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','The North Pole was discovered in 1909 by a pair of US Navy engineers, Robert E. Peary and Matthew Henson, accompanied by four Eskimos. Ever since its discovery, it has been attracting the attention of numerous scientists, researchers, politicians, tourists and explorers worldwide.\nInterestingly enough, there are two different definitions of the North Pole. The first one refers to the Geomagnetic North Pole that moves around on a daily basis and depends on the Earth\'s magnetic field. The other one relates to the best-known Geographic North Pole often called the \'Top of the World\'.\nThere is no land on the North Pole, just sheets of ice on the incredibly cold yet glass-like water. The area of the North Pole does not belong to any country yet. In spite of this, countries like Denmark (via Greenland), Russia, Norway, Canada, and the U.S. (via Alaska) are known to have laid claim to parts of its area. The reason for these claims is that underneath the North Pole resides approximately 22% of the world\'s natural gas and untapped oil reserves.\nYou won\'t be able to see penguins in the North Pole, as they are known to be found in the South Pole. However, apart from Narwhals, one can expect to see fish like Beluga, Humpback, and Orca (Killer) whales, as well as animals like Svalbard Reindeer and Arctic Fox. There are also plenty of polar bears who can be spotted in the North Pole.\n','Go through the passage below and write a short summary of it. Suggest a suitable title for your summary.','','','                                      <b>The Top of the World</b>\nThe North Pole was discovered in 1909 by a pair of American Navy Engineers along with four Eskimos. Since its discovery, the North Pole has caught the eye of everyone around the globe. The North Pole has two definitions - one being the magnetic North Pole, which depends on the Earth\'s magnetic field and the other being the Geographic North Pole, known as the \'Top of the World\'. The area of the North Pole does not belong to any country, but due to the rich deposits of untapped oil and natural gas under it, many countries have laid a claim to it. There are no penguins here, but Narwhals, polar bears, Arctic fox, orcas and humpbacks, among others, are found in plenty.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59605,1555,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','In most homes today, we can expect to find at least one television set. Some of the more affluent homes have more than one. A television set is no longer considered a luxury, as it has become a part of modern living.\nThe benefits of television are manifold. As a means of communication, there is virtually nothing to match it. We can watch a football match thousands of miles away with a mere flick of a switch, in full colour and with high fidelity sound. News that would have taken months to travel from one place to another now takes just a fraction of a second to reach in its original state, minus the factor of distorting human messengers. The impact of this improved communication on our lives is indeed great. We are not only better informed of current events all over the world but we are also exposed to a multitude of different cultures and ways of life. Never before did we have to face such a huge onslaught of information. In this context, when used with discretion, television can provide us with much knowledge, but when used carelessly, it can reduce us to non-thinking entities.\nTelevision is the cheapest form of leisure and it provides a great variety of entertainment. It brings hours of suspense, laughter and thrills into our living rooms. With the development of video equipment, the range of programs available is indeed wide. It is able to provide fun and entertainment to the young and old alike. On the whole, the usefulness of television as a source of entertainment and recreation is undoubted. The danger lies only in the possibility of addiction to watching too much television. We do have television addicts who do virtually nothing but watch television all day long. The prolonged watching does not do any good to the couch potatoes, as these addicts are called. Their vision can deteriorate and furthermore, it is a sheer waste of time.\nVia television, manufacturers are able to reach out to consumers more effectively. The advertisements on television serve to inform consumers about new products. However, nowadays we are literally overwhelmed by scores of advertisements all pushing to sell their products. A couple of adverts in between programs are welcome breaks, but to watch clip after clip for more than five minutes at a stretch is just too much. Likewise, an advertisement clip coming right in the middle of a program can be very irritating as it interrupts the continuity of the program.\nTelevision is also an invaluable educational tool. It enables education planners to co-ordinate and inform students about the requirements of various subjects.\nFrom a security point of view, the television set can be used as a surveillance tool and an \"eye\" in inaccessible places. Banks and other large commercial centers use close circuit television to maintain security. In deep-sea explorations, television is used to reach places no man can reach.\nThe television is part and parcel of our lives and it is here to stay, whether we like it or not. How we make use of this wonderful invention is entirely up to us. Used with care, it is a boon to humankind. Used carelessly, it can be a curse instead.\n','Read the following passage and summarise the main ideas by reducing it to one-third its length.','','','                                             <b>Television</b>\nTelevision provides knowledge and information. It is the cheapest source of entertainment and recreation, and is able to provide a great variety of programs which can entertain both the old and the young. Advertisements on television inform us about new products. Television is also an educational tool. Television has also been used as a surveillance tool and to reach inaccessible places. However, watching too much television can be addictive, a waste of time and can deteriorate vision. It can also reduce people to non-thinking individuals. Furthermore, advertisements in between television programs can be irritating.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59607,1556,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','Ramtron India Ltd. launches its latest product in the market today. A highly modem device, this touch phone, with features similar to any other i-phone in the market comes in a variety of shades that will be appealing to both, young and old. The unbelievable offer of a down-payment of only INR 999 and the rest in eleven equal installments makes it easy on the pockets as well.','Look at the advertisement below. Write your views and counter-views on The mobile phone - Our True Friend or Foe.','','','                                <b>The Mobile phone - Our True Friend or Foe</b>\n<b>View:</b>\n(i) It is a means of speedy communication. It saves time and money.\n(ii) It is easy to carry and operate.\n(iii) It is one of the cheapest means of entertainment. You can play games, or listen to music\n(iv) You can send and receive messages, record voice, and take, send and receive pictures\n(v) It also acts as a watch and a calculator.\n(vi) It is very useful in case of an emergency. Calling up the family, hospital or police can be done instantly. Thus, it ensures safety and security.\n<b>Counter-view:</b>\n(i) It has become an addiction. People have begun to depend on it psychologically. They feel restless without it.\n(ii) It is a distraction. Students cannot concentrate on their studies. People cannot even concentrate on a movie in a theatre as they keep checking their mobile sets every now and then.\n(iii) It is corroding the intellect. People rely on it more and more, even for tasks like simple calculations.\n(iv) People prefer mobile phones over other activities like face-to-face communication with family members or physical exercise,\n(v) It is affecting linguistic capacity; the short forms of words, and abrupt contracted sentences are becoming the order of the day. They are thus, ruining the English language.\n(vi) The mobile phone is useless for communication if you are out of the coverage area.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59608,1556,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','The summer holidays are approaching and it is a time of the year when most school going children are absolutely free, as they begin a new class following the holidays. With the advent of summer camps that encourage children to participate in extra - curricular activities, basic survival techniques have proliferated through the city of Mumbai and you find at least one such advertisement encouraging parents to enroll their wards in these camps every day. Write your views and counter-views on \'Summer Camps help in Personality Development.\'','','','                        <b>Summer camps help in Personality Development</b>\n<b>View:</b>\n(i) Summer camps are a need for children living in urban societies.\n(ii) They make optimum use of children\'s summer vacations.\n(iii) In today\'s setup of nuclear families, they are a substitute for the skills which in joint families would be imparted by the elders of the families.\n(iv) They are a solution for the boredom experienced by children whose parents are aw from home on account of their jobs or professions.\n(v) They add a lesson in sociability. In nuclear families in cities, children do not learn values of caring and sharing; adjustment and co-operation. Summer camps give that experience.\n(vi) During the academic year, schools have a very rigorous routine. The vast syllabus, orals, practicals, exams and co-curricular activities leave no time for children to des creativity or hobbies.\n<b>Counter-view:</b>\n(i) Summer camps have many restrictions. Campers have to follow strict timings. They to do the assigned activities as per instructions. This takes away the carefree spin vacation.\n(ii) The knowledge imparted in most camps is insufficient.\n(iii) If the child does not feel interested, the money and the effort is wasted.\n(iv) The creative instinct or hobbies that these camps indulge in can be nurtured throughout the year as well. One doesn\'t need special summer camps for it.\n(v) If the subject and the group is not to the child\'s liking, he may form an aversion entire life, and may even shy away from larger groups.\n(vi) Summer camps can be quite expensive, and hence are not within the reach of poor children.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59609,1556,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Even though India is a fast developing nation and has grown in various spheres, keeping up with the modern techniques of the rest of the world, there is no denying that the less developed rural sectors of the country are equally important. They are the ones who provide us with our food-grains, vegetables and fruits. Many large industries prefer to put up a segment in the rural areas because the infrastructure and labour are cheaper than they would be in the cities. Keeping these points in mind, write your views and counter-views on the \'Value of Indian Villages in the Urban Society.\'','','','                        <b>The Value of Indian Villages in the Urban Society</b>\n<b>View:</b>\n(i) 72% of our country comprises of villages.\n(ii) They are the backbone of our country.\n(iii) Most of our grains, vegetables and fruits come from villages.\n(iv) They have a cleaner environment.\n(v) They have better social values.\n(vi) Small-scale industries offer opportunities for local employment.\n(vii) Infrastructure and labour are cheaper in villages.\n<b>Counter-view:</b>\n(i) The villages are neglected and are no longer the focus of development.\n(ii) In fact, they too are fast imitating urban lifestyles.\n(iii) They have poor facilities of education and healthcare.\n(iv) They have less facilities for employment as compared to cities and therefore, villagers prefer to migrate to cities these days.\n(v) In their attempts at preserving tradition, they are easy targets for superstition. (v)\n(vi) Poor infrastructure like electricity, roads and sanitation hampers their progress in a major way.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59610,1556,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare a paragraph with an appropriate title to be used for the counter-view section on the following topic in about 110 words:\nStudy says homework does not help students score better grades. View Section \"Homework Still a Key Part of Education\"\n*It engages the child with his study more effectively.\n*It engages the child with what is going on in the class.\n*Homework inculcates students with life skills.\n','','','<b>Counter-view</b>\n                                            <b>Homework should be abolished</b>\nSchool is stressing out our youngsters, as evidenced in the high number of school students committing suicide.\nWe should, therefore, be committed to removing stress from the school system. A primary contributor to stress is the oppressive burden of daily homework given to the student.\n\nWrestling with piles of homework, parent and kids alike are exhausted. The truth is that much of the take-home assignments are needless.\nAfter long-drawn school hours, kids return home and immediately get down to tackling the day\'s homework.\nWhere is the time to relax and do other extra-curricular activities? The constant pressure of moving from one deadline to another leaves them perpetually harassed. Parents too have a hard time, often doing a major part of the homework to help out the child. Is homework necessary to get good grades? There\'s no foundation for this belief. The fear and pressure of homework exhaust students, killing their curiosity and most importantly their keenness and desire to learn.\nAt home the debate over homework is yet to have an impact. Even though there\'s been discussion around inordinately heavy school bags which burden students, directly linked to the issue of homework.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59611,1556,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare a paragraph with an appropriate title to be used for the counter-view section on the following topic in about 110 words:\nYou can take the help of the following points from the View Section\n\"Ambition Breeds Ruin\"\n(1) Ambition gives rise to jealousy, greed, hatred.\n(2) Ambition overrides humane feelings-success at whatever cost.\n(3) Ambition has no room for family, service for others, charity, love, compassion.\n(4) Ambition brings with it loss of peace, restfulness and contentment.\n','','','<b>Counter-view</b>\n                                       <b>Low Ambition Is A Crime</b>\nAmbition works as a stimuli. It gives direction to work on. Thinking that it spreads jealousy and hatred is just a negative mindset. Ambitious person strives hard to achieve his goal. Failure is a stepping stone not a slippery one. Keeping ambition high is human. It does not override any feeling for cheap goal. The true ambitious person knows his positive approach. Such persons will fulfill ambition with strenuous efforts without hurting others\' rights. It is absurd to think that ambition has no place for family, service, charity, love and compassion. In fact, ambition is perceived because of love, for family and service and charity for nation. An ambitious person finds peace and contentment in striving to achieve his/her goals. So, who says ambition breeds ruin? It brings the crown!\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59650,1557,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a report for your school magazine describing a cultural fest held in your school in which various schools of your city took part.','','','                                                                    \n                                      <b>Cultural Extravaganza</b>\n                                                                      - By a Student Correspondent\nModel High School; Mumbai, 24th October, 2018: A colourful and memorable Cultura Fest was organized in Model High School on Saturday, 24th October. This event was whole day long and was held in the auditorium of the school. In this mega event, many schools from the city took part.\nThe grand show commenced by the arrival of various teams from schools. Then the Chief Guest, the District Collector of our District, arrived with his wife. Lamp lighting ceremony was accompanied by a melodious Saraswati Vandana, hailing the Goddess of Knowledge and Wisdom. It was followed by a welcome speech given by the Principal of the school. It was a truly mesmerizing show as the teams from various schools presented many programmes. There was singing, dancing, poetry recitation, skits, mimicry, mono act shows, classical and modern combination of several foot tapping numbers. Everyone sat glued to the show.\nThe Chief Guest praised the entire event a lot. He guided all with his inspirational words and inspired everyone to do better. His words were followed by the announcement of the winning team, ABC School of our city. The team from Model High school bagged second position and everyone complimented one another. It was followed by a  formal vote of thanks and the event concluded.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59651,1557,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a report for the newspaper describing a traffic jam in which you, along many, were trapped for many hours.','','','                                         <b>Traffic Jam: A Nuisance On Roads</b>                                                                                                                                  \n                                                                                     - By a Staff Reporter\nWestern Express Highway - Mumbai, 24th August, 2018: Yesterday on 23rd August, the main highway connecting the two major suburbs of our city witnessed a real chaos in the form of a traffic jam in which thousands of people were caught for several hours.\nIt was around 5 pm in the evening and the office goers, the school buses of various schools and commuters along with many others were returning from the busy route. The traffic was running smoothly but suddenly, the vehicles came to an abrupt halt. There was utter confusion among all. The traffic was not moving even an inch. Soon, anger erupted among many. Patience slowly melted and there were arguments, heated talks, and even many people came out from their vehicles in anger. Fuming, everyone was vexed to know the cause of that traffic jam. People were in hurry to reach their destination but not even one traffic police officer could be seen in the vicinity. Then, some excited youngsters jumped into the scene and began clearing the scene. They reached at the place where the halt had begun. A badly wounded person was seen unconscious in a damaged car. Situation was understood and immediately an ambulance was called by onlookers. Within no time, the ambulance arrived followed by the police too.\nIt took two hours to clear the traffic. But finally, the injured person was taken in the ambulance, the damaged car was picked by the police and the traffic moved.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59653,1557,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a report for about a truck accident of school children.','','','         <b>20 SCHOOL CHILDREN KILLED IN BUS - TRUCK ACCIDENT</b>                                                                                                                                        \n                                                                                       -By a Staff Reporter\nMumbai, 10th July 2018: Twenty school children were killed when an S.T. Bus was smashed by a truck near Matunga yesterday morning.\nSixty five students and five teachers of General English High School were on their way to Water Kingdom at about 9.40 a.m., when the Municipal Garbage truck smashed the S.T. bus. The truck driver was trying to save a boy who was suddenly crossing the road but unfortunately dashed with the S.T. Bus. The S.T bus was beyond the speed limit of 80kmph. Twenty school students were killed on the spot. Five students and 3 teachers were seriously injured and immediately taken to the nearby Sion Hospital.\nWhen contacted, Mr. Ragavan, Commissioner of Police said that the investigations were going on, and a detailed report will be given only after the proper investigations.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59654,1557,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a report of about 20 lines on a tree plantation programme organized by science club of your school to be published in the science bulletin.','','','                                        <b>EACH ONE... PLANT ONE!</b>                                                                                                                      \n                                                                      - By a Student Correspondent\nNew Era High School; Mumbai, 5th June 2018: The first project of the Abdul Science Club of the esteemed New Era High School this academic year was Plantation Programme along the 90 feet road Thakur Complex, Kandivali.\nThe Mayor was present at the ceremony which was held in a small pandal erect for the purpose. Mr. Gopal Shetty, the well-known political leader donated the sapling and the protective steel cages to be placed around the saplings. The Mayor expressed delight at the enthusiasm of the young scientists working for the environmental cause Our beloved Principal also spoke a few words. Then, the students set about digging p at the interval of 50 feet. 16 saplings were planted in all, on either sides of the road.\nThe President of the Science Club then spoke, solemnly promising to super with his team, the maintenance of the trees as they grew. Since it was a holiday, many students from the neighbouring schools were also present.\nEveryone cheered the President and the Club members. It was a very satisfactory day for all.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59655,1557,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a newspaper report in about 20 lines on a train derailment in your locality.','','','                                          <b>Derailment Near Bandra</b>                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                    - By a Staff Reporter\nBandra; Mumbai, 20th July 2018: A devastating rail mishap took place near Banda signal post yesterday. At about 10 p.m., a local train running at full speed derailed few kilometers ahead of the signal post.\nIt had jolted along some distance before coming to a shuddering stop. The presence of mind and timely action of the motorman Mr. Abhay Chauhan prevented greater loss of lives and property. The chief casualties were those who, in panic, jumped off the running train. The mishap left 80 passengers injured, many of them were seriously hurt. Bystanders and other road travelers rushed to the aid of the injured.\nThe police were informed of the accident almost immediately. People of the locality -joined the relief operations. All the injured were taken to the Railway Hospital nearby in Bandra.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59656,1557,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','You have just returned after your first experience of the kitefestival in Gujarat /Ahmedabad. You were thrilled with the festivities. Write a short report about the kite-festival for your local newspaper. Give an attractive headline, a dateline and an account of the kite- festive. Write the report in third person with more use of Passive voice.','','','                                      <b>FLYING HIGH</b>                                                                                                                              \n                                                                                     -By A Staff Reporter\nAhmedabad, January 16\nThe skies of Ahmedabad wore brilliant colours throughout the 14th day of January, when people from all walks of life were seen flying their kites across the great blue sky. Many groups of flyers engaged in competitions and jubilation was seen on the faces of the victorious. A wide variety of kites in all shapes and sizes bearing rich colours were seen gaily swaying or drifting across.\nEarlier during the week, customers stalked the markets even through the nights to make their purchases, thus keeping their stocks ready. The kite vendors did brisk business towards the festival date with the markets remaining open for all 24 hours of the day during the last week. Sweetmeat shops also reported an increase in the sale of traditional sweets.\nLater, with the onset of nightfall, colourfully lit lanterns were set afloat in the night sky as if they were competing with the radiance of the stars. It was an amazing sight to the eye.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59658,1557,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a short report of about 10 to 12 lines on a book exhibition held in your vicinity.','','','                               <b>BOOKS ARE A MAN\'S BEST FRIEND</b>                                                                                                                                               \n                                                                                             - By A Reporter\nPune, November 22\nA book exhibition was recently held by All Maharashtra Book Dealers Association at President Hall on Jyotirao Road. The exhibition commenced on November 20 and lasted for ten days.\nThe books on display and sale covered all major sections of knowledge and information. Children were found to be well engaged in their section. Some were seen browsing through for story books, others for hobby books while others for art and craft things. The Computer section was found to be the most visited one with people of all ages making large purchases.\nIn the section showcasing books on food, diet, beauty, lifestyle, clothing, etc., the womenfolk, who outnumbered the men, were too engrossed in making their selections and choices.\nDiscounts up to 40% and other attractive offers were made available to the purchasers. Many were reported to have made positive comments on this exhibition. One of the customers, whom this reporter spoke to said, \"Truly, books are a man\'s best friend.\"\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59662,1557,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Draft a report on an anti-pollution drive.','','','                               <b>\"SAVE OUR EARTH\" - DRIVE LAUNCHED</b>                                                                                                                                          \n                                                                                              - By A Reporter\nMumbai, 12 December\nEven as motorcades of the city\'s workforce zoomed past Dadar T.T. on Saturday morning. large gathering of school children, members of non-governmental organizations, and various Dignitaries gathered to launch the \"Save Our Earth\" project organized by an environment organization and Mercantile Bank.\n\"Though there are numerous sources of pollution in the city, we aim to target vehicles, as they are the biggest pollutants,\" said an environmentalist. \"Exhaust fumes form 65 per cent of the total air pollution.\"\nAddressing the gathering, the Minister for State Transport expressed the need to make vehicular pollution laws more stringent, especially in a city like Mumbai.\nAn awareness programme in the form of a skit, and a song-and-dance session was to be conducted at all public places highlighting the need to conserve our resources, particularly the natural ones. Posters were put up in residential complexes on the urgency of planting trees in our surroundings. Various competitions and contests were organized in schools, colleges and educational institutions.\nThe Mayor in her address strongly protested against the use of non-biodegradable material especially plastic for packaging. She also urged the citizens to conserve electricity and limit the use of paper. Incentives were to be provided for recycling of paper.\nAll in all, it was observed that taking into account the efforts and tasks undertaken in this venture, this project would be a runaway success.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59663,1557,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Your school recently conducted an arts and crafts workshop for the classes 8, 9 and 10\". Prepare a report on it with the help of the following points:\ni. Venue and duration of the workshop\nii. Purpose of the workshop\niii. The opening lecture by the host\niv. Various designs and objects made by the students\nv. Conclusion\n','','','                                  <b>Choose to Reduce and Reuse</b>\n                                                               - Sakshi Sharma, Student Reporter\nNavi Mumbai, 24th January, 2020\nThe New Horizons School conducted an arts and crafts workshop on 22nd January, 2020 to celebrate Earth Day. The theme was \'Save Paper, Save Nature\'. The special guest was Ms. Roshni Ran, an independent artist specialising in making unique recycled art. The workshop started at 10 a.m. with Ms. Rao explaining her work and talking about what inspires her. It was followed by a general discussion about the benefits of repurposing paper and how it can reduce global warming.\nThe students first learned how to make beautifully crafted animals and birds using just one sheet of paper. After this, Ms. Rao gave a presentation on making papier-mâché at home using old newspapers and creating sculptures and household objects. The last event of the day was a demonstration on paper quilling,\nwhich can be used to turn even the smallest pieces of paper into great works of art. The workshop educated the students on the environmental effects of wasting paper. The students learnt that the things which appear to be worthless can be used to create fine works of art.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59665,1557,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a report on the tree plantation drive recently organised by your town\'s Rotaract Club using the following points:\ni. Time and venue\nii. Number of participants and trees planted\niii. Information about the trees\niv. Presence of senior volunteers\nv. Conclusion\n','','','                                         <b>For a Greener Tomorrow</b>\n                                                          -Mahesh Jadhav, Student Reporter\nChembur, 13th February, 2020\nThe Rotaract Club of Chembur has been organising a yearly tree plantation drive for the past 25 years. On its 25th anniversary, they resolved to plant 2500 saplings. The drive was scheduled to start at 9:00 am. on 10th February and the volunteers gathered at the Club Office at 8 a.m. This year marked the highest number of participants in the plantation drive with a record turnout of 500 people.\nThe senior members led the groups and each group was given an area of two hundred square metres. A variety of native tree species like, Teak, Neem, and Gulmohar were selected, as they provide shade as well as a habitat for birds. The teams focused on planting trees in empty spaces around the newly constructed buildings.\nThe drive went on till 5 p.m. and all 2500 saplings were successfully planted in different neighbourhoods and localities. The senior members concluded the event by presenting every volunteer with a certificate of participation. The Rotaract Club plans to organise this drive twice in the year 2021.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59670,1557,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Your class went to the National Park for your yearly class trip. Write a report on the experience by including the following points:\ni. Date and location of the trip\nii. Mode of transportation\niii. The animals you saw\niv. The information you gathered\nv. Conclusion\n','','','                              <b>In The Heart of Nature</b>\n                                                                    - Janhvi Shah, Student Reporter\nMumbai, 28th January, 2020\nThe students of St. Joseph\'s Convent School embarked on their annual school trip to the Sahyadri Tiger Reserve in Satara during 21 January to 25th January. A group of 200 students were accompanied by 25 teachers in 5 buses to the destination.\nThe reserve is divided into three sections according to the district that they are located in. The northern part situated in Satara is known as the Koyna Wildlife Sanctuary, the central part in Sangli is the Chandoli National Park and the southern part in Kolhapur is the Radhanagari Wildlife Sanctuary. The class visited the Koyna Sanctuary in Satara which includes the Shivsagar reservoir of the Koyna dam. They were delighted to see a number of wild creatures like sloth bears, Indian bisons, Indian giant squirrel, langurs, barking deer, sambhar and even a tiger. A variety of birds and snakes were also spotted by the students.\nThe four days of the trip passed by sooner than anyone realised and the students as well as the teachers returned happy and content, from a trip in the heart of nature.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59671,1557,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a report on the recent archaeological expedition of an ancient civilization with the following points:\ni. Location\nii. Leader of the expedition\niii. Total team members\niv. Details about their findings\nv. Conclusion\n','','','                                     <b>Uncovering The Past</b>\n                                                                 - Nikhil More, Student Reporter\nNagpur, 20th March, 2020\nThe Archaeological Department of Maharashtra recently announced a new site for the excavation of ancient objects, located in Nagardhan which is 50 kilometers from Nagpur. The department has declared it to be the capital of the Vakataka dynasty. More information about\nthe Vakataka rulers is being discovered using these findings as only their historical record has been found.\nThe expedition team was led by Virag Sontakke and included 2 other experts from the Deccan College in Pune, Shrikant Ganvir and Shantanu Vaidya. The most important discovery was a metal coin with the seal of Queen Prabhavati Gupta. Objects made of wood, terracotta, ivory, metal and baked mud, that were used during that time were found in the excavation. Among the discoveries were houses with modem infrastructure facilities like terracotta pipelines for water and waste management. The prehistoric objects made of metal indicate that the region was populated since the late Iron Age.\nThe department plans to make the area a tourist destination as well as a research center so that they can continue making new discoveries.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59672,1557,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a report for a newspaper based on the following headline: Dengue fever has claimed 8 lives in Pune.','','','                                    <b>Dengue Claims 8 Lives</b>                                                                                                                              \n                                                                                            - A staff reporter\nPune, September 14: \nDengue has re-emerged with a vengeance. Bhosari is in the grip of an epidemic with 40 patients being shifted to Pune for treatment.\n90 cases of dengue have been reported in Bhosari and the death toll has reached eight. The Health Department has issued media releases detailing the symptoms and precautions. The stock of required medicines is being sent to the various hospitals in and around Bhosari. A team of five doctors and other paramedical staff set out this morning to work in Bhosari till the situation gets under control.\n\"The important thing to remember is that self-medication should be avoided at all costs. Consult a doctor as soon as the symptoms appear,\" a health ministry spokesperson said.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59674,1558,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a dialogue conservation between you and your friend regarding your future plan after the declaration of the result.','','','Sujon: Hello, Rajib, how are you?\nRajib: I am fine and what about you?\nSujon: I am fine too. So, Rajib now since you have passed H.S.C. examination with 95% marks, what is your future plan?\nRajib: Well, I want to became a doctor. I am preparing to take admission in a medical college.\nSujon: Good idea! Your plan is absolutely great.\nRajib: Finally, you too have passed out with flying colours. Now, what is your goal?\nSujon: I want to be an English teacher. I am planning to take up Arts and do Masters in English.\nRajib: Your choice is great too. There is a lack of qualified teachers in our country\nSujon: Thanks! I am really passionate about teaching. So, I hope I will do well.\nRajib: Oh sure, you will! All the best! It was pleasure talking to you.\nSujit: Wish you the same. Thanks!\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59675,1558,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare a dialogue conversation between a teacher and a student who always arrives late to class.','','','Student: May I come in, Sir?\nTeacher: Yes, stand here, Why do you always come late?\nStudent: Sir, it is the bus which makes me late.\nTeacher: What time do you leave from home?\nStudent: I always leave home at quarter to eight.\nTeacher: How far is your home from here?\nStudent: It is about three kilometers from here.\nTeacher: That is why, you get late. You leave your home very late.\nStudent: Sir, I have my breakfast at 7.30 a.m.\nTeacher: What time do you get up?\nStudent: I get up at about 7.00 a.m.\nTeacher: Don\'t you offer prayers?\nStudent: Not regularly.\nTeacher: My dear, it is a bad habit, change your routine. Always get up early in the morning, offer your prayers and go for a morning walk\nStudent: Sir, there is no park near our home.\nTeacher: No problem. You can walk along the street in the morning. Take breakfast at the right time and then, leave for school.\nStudent: You are right, sir. From tomorrow, I will never be late.\nTeacher: Good! Keep one thing in mind that regularity and punctuality can conquer the mountains.\nStudent: Thank you very much for your kind advice, Sir.\nTeacher: OK. Now you may sit in your place, student.\nStudent: Thank you, sir.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59677,1558,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write a dialogue conversation between a doctor and a patient.','','','<b>Doctor - Dr. Sharma</b>                     <b>Patient - Mr. Kapoor</b>\nMr. Kapoor: Good morning, Dr. Sharma!\nDr. Sharma: Good morning! What\'s wrong with you?\nMr. Kapoor: I have been suffering from fever since yesterday.\nDr. Sharma: Do you have any other symptoms?\nMr. Kapoor: Well, my head is aching and I am shivering.\nDr. Sharma: Let me check your temperature. At this time, the fever is 102 degrees. Don\'t worry, it is nothing serious. I am giving you the medicine, and you will be all right in a couple of days.\nMr. Kapoor: Thank you, doctor.\nDr. Sharma: But get your blood tested for malaria, and come with the report tomorrow.\nMr. Kapoor: Ok.\nDr. Sharma: I shall recommend at least two days rest for you.\nMr. Kapoor: Would you prepare a medical certificate for me to submit in my office?\nDr. Sharma: Oh sure... This is your medical certificate.\nMr. Kapoor: Thank you very much. Please tell me how I should take this medicine?\nDr. Sharma: This medicine is for one day only. Take this first dose as soon as you reach home, the second at 3 pm and the third at night before sleeping\nMr. Kapoor: What should I eat, doctor?\nDr. Sharma: You should eat only light food. You can take milk and fresh fruits also.\nMr. Kapoor: Where shall I pay the fees?\nDr. Sharma: You can pay it at the reception desk.\nMr. Kapoor: Thank you, doctor.\nDr. Sharma: It\'s all right.\nMr. Kapoor: I will see you tomorrow with my blood report. Good day!\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59678,1558,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Compose an imaginary dialogue between hue and Johney, when they realice about what Behrman had done for Johnsy,','','','An imaginary dialogue between Sue and Johnsy\nSue: Oh, so you know that the last leaf was just a painting.\nJohnsy: Yes, but wasn\'t that a masterpiece by Mr Berman?\nSue: Truly, it was....what artistic skill did he have!\nJohnsy: But why did he paint that picture?\nSue: I told him about you and your illogical connection between the falling of the leaves and getting well.\nJohnsy: So what did he do then?\nSue: He too agreed with me and did not agree with your fancy.\nJohnsy: But how did he know the ivy vine?\nSue: I showed it to him\nJohnsy: And then...?\nSue: He began to paint the last leaf.\nJohnsy: So that last leaf had already fallen?\nSue: Yes, and what you saw was the masterpiece of the last leaf.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59679,1558,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write in your notebook an imaginary telephonie conversation between you and your family doctor\'s secretary, asking for an appointment to consult the doctor for a health problem you are suffering from. Begin with\nSecretary: Good morning! This is XYZ Clinic. How can I help you?\nMyself: Good morning! I am (Now continue……………..)\n','','',' An imaginary telephonic conversation between your family doctor\'s secretary and yourself.\nSecretary: Good morning! This is XYZ Clinic. How can I help you!\nSelf: Good morning! I am Mr Rohit Ferreira. I need an appointment with Doctor.\nSecretary: For when, Sir?\nSelf: Tomorrow, if possible?\nSecretary: Tomorrow is possible but late evening, Will that do?\nSelf: Yes, I think so! What time will that be?\nSecretary: I am fixing your appointment for 8:15 pm.\nSelf: All right. That is fine for me. I will be there.\nSecretary: Sir, what is the nature of your illness?\nSelf: I have been experiencing bouts of pain and discomfort in my right leg.\nSecretary: Is it a very severe pain?\nSelf: No, it\'s not so severe, but it occurs often and lasts about an hour.\nSecretary: All right. I have noted that. The doctor will see you tomorrow.\nSelf: Thank you very much.\nSecretary: You are welcome, Sir!\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59680,1558,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Suresh is invited by his friend Pratik. Write an imaginary conversation that could have developed between them.','','',' [Pratik invites his friend Suresh over to his house]\nPratik: Come in, Suresh. I have been waiting for you.\nSuresh: Well, Sorry, I am a bit late. I could not get the bus.\nPratik: It\'s alright, now I have a surprise for you.\nSuresh: For me? What can that be?\nPratik: Come into the inner room.\n(Pratik takes Suresh to the balcony. Suresh just follows, full of suspense)\nPratik: (point out to a cage) Just look at that fellow! See how he is sitting like a lord!\nSuresh: (looking thoughtfully at the caged parrot) Poor fellow!\nPratik: What makes you say that? He receives so much attention and so much to eat.\nSuresh: The poor creature must be pining for jungle life, the trees, fruits, companions and above all, his freedom!\nPratik: Really! I never thought of that! I shall try to give him some greenery around his cage.\nSuresh: Whatever you do, he will not be happy. His wings are clipped, aren\'t they! This is like prison life for him.\nPratik: If you set him free, he will surely die. Allow his wings to grow. Give him a more spacious cage, so that he has some freedom of movement at least.\nPratik: Thank you, Suresh. These points never struck me at all.\nSuresh: You can talk to him. Teach him a few good phrases. He will keep repeating them.\nPratik: He whistles sometimes when he is happy.\nSuresh: Don\'t worry. He will get used to his prison life. Give him company. Take care that cruel children don\'t trouble him.\nPratik: Thank you, Suresh, for your advice.\nSuresh: Meet you next month, Bye.\nPratik: Thank you once again, Bye\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59681,1559,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Prepare ten questions to interview a social worker.','','','(1) What do you hope to accomplish as a social worker?\n(2) What are some of your biggest achievements in your fieldwork?\n(3) Tell me about a time when you disagreed with someone over a treatment plan. How was it resolved?\n(4) What was the most difficult case you ever worked on?\n(5) How do you balance your work and personal life?\n(6) How do you relocate resources for people living in temporary slums?\n(7) Who has been your source of inspiration?\n(8) What is your dream project?\n(9) How do you see your dream for India, five years from now?\n(10) Which profession you would have selected if you were not a social worker.\n(11) Share a message you would like to give to the existing youth who would like to render their services as a social worker.\nThank you so much!\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59683,1559,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','If you had the chance to interview a celebrity, what would you ask?','','','(1) How do you feel after this recent blockbuster?\n(2) How are you planning to celebrate your success?\n(3) What is your upcoming movie about?\n(4) Who is your favourite co-star?\n(5) Who do you dream of working with?\n(6) What do you do in your spare time?\n(7) How do you tackle failures?\n(8) What is your biggest fear?\n(9) What sports do you enjoy playing?\n(10) What is your one annoying habit?\n(11) What message would you like to give to your fans?\nThank You!\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59684,1559,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','A brilliant student from your school has won a Mathematics Quiz at the National Level. Frame questions to interview him/her when the school felicitates him/her. Follow the steps given below.\n(1) Greeting\n(2) Introduction of the interviewee and achievements.\n(3) 2 or 3 questions about growing years.\n(4) 4 to 6 questions about the achievements.\n(5) 2 or 3 questions about future plans and prospects.\n(6) Expression of thanks and good wishes.\n','','','The following questions will form part of the interview that will be conducted with the student who has won a Mathematics Quiz at the National Level.\nGood evening, Rajesh and a very warm welcome from all of us here.\nRajesh, a student from class 8 participated in the All India Topper Quiz in Mathematics and has won the first place at the national level. He is happy and willing to share with us his ideas and views.\n1. At what age did you discover your liking towards mathematics?\n2. What were your parents reaction to this liking?\n3. Who motivated you during your primary school days?\n4. To whom would you attribute your success?\n5. What kind of study or practice did you put in?\n6. How easy do you find the application of mathematics in daily life?\n7. What other recognition or awards have you received so far?\n8. How difficult is the competition, especially at the National level?\n9. What potential do you find in your peers?\n10. State your plans for the future,\nWe are very grateful to you, Rajesh for sharing your time and space with us. Congratulations and all the very best for all your future endeavours.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59688,1559,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Imagine that you are going to have an interview with an artist, a musician, a painter from your area. Prepare eight to ten questions that you would like to ask him/her.','','','The interviewer will pose the following questions to the artist whom he will interview shortly.\n1. Sir, what is your opinion about art in modern day?\n2. How is art rated today in the commercial world?\n3. Who is your inspiration and role-model?\n4. What preparations do you make before a concert?\n5. Why have you chosen this form of art?\n6. Do you get sufficient support from your family, friends and colleagues? Please give us a brief account.\n7. Who is your \'ideal person\'?\n8. What hardships do you face in this field?\n9. Have you had any memorable experience that you would like to share with us! Please state it.\n10. State what message you would like to give to your fans and other upcoming artistes\nThe artist was delighted to share his views in reply to the above questions during his interview.\n\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59689,1559,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','The captain of the team that won the All India Football Tournament has been invited to your school. Frame about eight to ten questions to interview him.','','','The Captain, Mr Akshay Diwakar, will be privileged to answer the following questions in an interview with him.\n1. How do you feel on your victory?\n2. What or whom do you attribute this success to?\n3. State the kind of practice that is required.\n4. Did you face any hardships? Please enumerate a few of them.\n5. How did you fight these encumbrances?\n6. What challenges were posed to you?\n7. Who were your strongest supporters?\n8. What role did your teammates play in your success story?\n9. Have you already decided your future plan? Pleas give us a gist of it.\n10. Would you like to give the young budding sports people a message from you and your team? Please state it.\nMr Diwakar was pleased to answer the above questions when interviewed recently.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59692,1559,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write 8-10 questions you would ask an SSC topper of your school. Begin with a proper greeting and introduction before the interview questions and a proper conclusion at the end.','','','(1) Hello, Tamanna. Congratulations for being this year\'s SSC topper of our school. We are all very proud of you. I would like to ask you a few questions. May I? Thank you.\n(2) Did you expect to top the school?\n(3) What are your feelings about this great achievement?\n(4) Who motivated and encouraged you in your studies?\n(5) How much hard work did you put in?\n(6) What role did your teachers and parents play in this achievement of yours?\n(7) Did you join any classes for study, revision or practice?\n(8) Which were your weak subjects and how did you tackle them?\n(9) What are your future plans?\n(10) Any message for the other students of this school? \nThank you.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59715,1552,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','There are different kinds of fuels. Broadly, they can be divided as solid, liquid and gaseous fuels. Solid fuels include substances such as wood, coal and coke. Most liquid fuels are obtained from petroleum which is obtained from oil wells sunk deep into the earth. Petrol, kerosene and diesel are all separated from petroleum. The most important gaseous fuels are natural gas, coal and water gas. Natural gas is a fuel that is widely used for cooking and heating.','Read the following paragraph and write in the form of a Tree diagram putting the correct information:','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(59716,1552,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','A computer is an electronic device. It is made up of hardware, software and liveware A the physical and mechanical parts of a computer are known as hardware. The hardware comprises of input devices, output devices and a central processing unit (CPU). A keyboard and a mouse are the input devices whereas the monitor and printer are output devices. The CPU has 3 components viz., Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU), Control Unit (CU) and memory. The computer works on 2 types of memory, i.e., Main memory and Secondary memory. The floppy disk and the hard disk are examples of secondary memory but the main memory comprises of 2 types known as RAM and ROM.','Put the information given in the following paragraph in the form of a tree diagram:','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(59721,1552,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','Butterflies belong to group Insects and lay eggs. They pass through four stages in their life cycle. The female butterfly lays the eggs on the leaves of the plants. These eggs are tiny and have a variety of shapes. After 6-7 days, a worm like creature known as baby caterpillar hatches out of the egg which is light green or yellow in colour. The larva eats leaves and grows fully. This fully grown larva is called a caterpillar. It is the young one of the butterfly and does not resemble its parents. Now, the caterpillar grows into the pupa. It spins a cocoon around its body and fastens itself to a plant with a silk thread. Finally, the baby butterfly emerges from the pupa and soon is transformed into an adult butterfly.','Read the following passage and prepare a flow chart:','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(59723,1552,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write the following idea on the writing process in the form of a flow chart:\nThe Writing Process\n*Think about what you want to say.\n*Talk about your ideas with a friend to find a main idea.\n*Use a list or web to organize your ideas.\n*Write your ideas in order.\n*Read your work out loud and note the places where you stumble.\n*Ask a friend for his or her feedback.\n*Try out different beginnings and endings.\n*Use quotes or add dialogue.\n*Include descriptive words.\n*Add detail to develop important parts.\n*Make sure you have complete sentences, correct spellings and necessary capitalization and punctuation.\n*Reread to see if each sentence makes sense.\n*Ask a friend to do proof reading.\n*Type it out or copy it neatly on a new paper.\n*Think of an interesting title.\n*Share your writing.\n','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(59735,1552,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','We must take proper care of our hair. Healthy hair looks beautiful and makes us look presentable. It is important to keep our hair clean by washing it regularly with soap or shampoo. At the same time, washing our hair too often can spoil our hair, it can make it dry and brittle. To have healthy hair, we must eat a balanced diet, which provides nourishment to our hair and skin. We should eat lots of green leafy vegetables, fresh fruits and cereals Consumption of amla juice, ashgourd juice, pumpkin and coconut water enhances hair growth. We should avoid hard chemicals and dyes. We should also avoid the intake of maida (fine flour) and deep fried dishes, sweets made of white sugar, soft drinks, tea and coffee. We should not expose our hair to the sun during the hottest time of the day. We should cover it up and wear a hat instead. If we follow a healthy regime of yoga and breathing exercises, we can enjoy healthy hair for a long time as it slows down the process of greying and ageing.','Here are some tips about hair care. Read and write in a tabular form as Do\'s and Don\'t.','','','<table border=\"1\" style=\"width:fit-content; border-collapse: collapse\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n  <tr>\n    <th> Do\'s </th>\n    <th> Don\'t </th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td>1) Wash your hair regularly.<br>2) Eat balanced diet.<br>3) Consume lots of green leafy vegetables, fresh fruits and cereals.<br>4) Consume amla juice, ashgourd juice, pumpkin and coconut water.<br>5) Do yoga and breathing exercises regularly.<br>6) Cover your hair or wear a hat during the sunny day.</td>\n<td>1) Wash your hair too often.<br>2) Use harsh chemicals and dyes.<br>3) Drink tea, coffee and soft drinks.<br>4) Eat the dishes made of maida (fine flour) and sweets made of white sugar.<br>5) Expose hair to the sun during the hottest time of the day.\n</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59739,1552,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','It has come to the notice of the Management that a few students of the secondary section have been behaving in an unruly fashion by destroying school property and dirtying the school premises. It needs to be noticed that the below mentioned rules should be strictly maintained, the violation of which is going to lead to severe punishment.\nThe students are hereby requested to keep the place clean and not spit or scratch on the walls. They should not pluck flowers from the flower beds on the campus or draw on the walls or notice boards. They are instructed to move about in an orderly manner in the corridors and make way for the teachers. Foul language should be avoided totally. Students should communicate only in English in the school premises and maintain punctuality at all times.\n','The following information was put up on the school notice board after some unruly behaviour was noticed among the students by the Management. Read the notice about the new rules and discipline. Prepare a chart of Do\'s and Don\'t for the students of your school.','','','<table border=\"1\" style=\"width:fit-content; border-collapse: collapse\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n  <tr>\n    <th> Do\'s </th>\n    <th> Don\'t </th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td>1) Keep the place clean.<br>2) Move about in an orderly manner in the corridors.<br>3) Make way for the teachers.<br>4) Speak only in English in the school premises.<br>5) Always maintain punctuality. .</td>\n<td>1) Spit or scratch on the wall.<br>2)Pluck flowers from the flower beds.<br>3) Draw on the walls or notice boards.<br>4) Use foul language. </td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59742,1552,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write Do\'s and Don\'t to be followed for road safety.','','','<table border=\"1\" style=\"width:fit-content; border-collapse: collapse\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n  <tr>\n    <th> Do\'s </th>\n    <th> Don\'t </th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td>1) Follow traffic signal.<br>2) Use seat belt.<br>3) Use zebra crossing to cross the road.<br>4) Park your vehicles only in an authorised parking. </td>\n<td>1) Cross speed limits.<br>2) Talk on mobile phone while driving.<br>3) Drink and drive.<br>4) Overtake in haste. </td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59743,1552,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','The following Pie - chart shows the mode of transport used by students for coming to school. On the basis of the given Pie - chart, write a brief summary:','','','The given pie chart highlights the modes of transport used by students coming to sched It is observed that maximum students i.e. 50% of them come to school by bus 21% of them are picked and dropped by their parents whereas 17% come to school walking. The percentage of students coming by cycling is very less. Only 8% of them prefer the option of cycling and only 4% use personal motorized vehicles to come to school.','',1,0,0,NULL),(59744,1552,'descriptive','5',5,2,'Out of Text Book','','The following food chain shows the flow of energy from one stage to other. On the basis of the given information write a brief summary:','','','For an ecosystem to work, there has to be a flow of energy within it. The organisms of the ecosystem need energy in the form of food. The ultimate source of this energy is the sun. Producers like green plants trap solar energy and convert it into the chemical energy of food. When a primary consumer (grasshopper) eats the producer, a part of this energy is passed on to it. The primary consumer is then, eaten by a secondary consumer (frog). The secondary consumer is eaten by a tertiary consumer(snake), and the tertiary consumer is eaten by the final consumer(hawk). Final consumer when dies it gets decomposed. In this way, energy gets transferred from one consumer to the next higher level of consumer. A series of organisms through which food energy flows in an ecosystem is called a food chain.','',1,0,0,NULL),(59827,1662,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','तुमच्या शाळेत उन्हाळी सु‌ट्टीत \'हस्ताक्षर सुंदर करूया!\' हे दहा दिवसांचे शिबिर आयोजित केले आहे. त्यात तुम्हाला सहभागी करून घेण्याची विनंती करणारे पत्र तुमच्या वर्गशिक्षकांना लिहा.','','','दिनांक : १ मे, २०१८.\nप्रति,\nमाननीय वर्गशिक्षक (इयत्ता ८वी/अ),\nशारदा विद्यामंदिर,\nडोंबिवली (प.)\n<b>विषय</b> : \'हस्ताक्षर सुंदर करूया!\' शिबिरात सहभागी करून घेण्यासंबंधी.\nआदरणीय गुरुवर्य,\nसप्रेम सादर नमस्कार वि. वि.\nमी अ.ब.क., आपल्या शारदा विद्यामंदिर, इयत्ता आठवी \'अ\'चा विद्यार्थी आहे. सर, आपणास माहित आहेच की आपल्या शाळेत यंदा मे महिन्यात १० मे ते २० मे पर्यंत \'हस्ताक्षर सुंदर करुया!\' या विशेष शिबिराचे आयोजन केले आहे व त्यात मोजक्याच विद्यार्थ्यांना प्रवेश दिला जाणार आहे. माझे हस्ताक्षर चांगले नाही. ते सुधारावेब लागेल असे तुम्हीच मला वारंवार सांगितले आहे. हस्ताक्षर सुधारण्याचे आता मी मनावर घेतले आहे. या शिबिराच्या निमित्ताने मला एक चांगली संधी मिळणार आहे या संधीचा उपयोग करून मला माझे हस्ताक्षर सुधारायचे आहे व आपल्या योग्य सल्ल्याचे पालनही करायचे आहे. प्रवेश मर्यादित असल्याने व मला प्रवेश घ्यावयाचाच असल्याने मी माझ्या प्रवेशासंबंधी हे पत्र लिहित आहे. सर, कृपया माझ्‌या विनंतीचा मान राखून आपण मला या शिबिरात सहभागी करून घ्यावे मला हस्ताक्षर सुधारण्याची एक संधी दयावी\nसर, मी आपल्या होकाराची आतुरतेने वाट पाहत आहे. तसेच प्रवेश निश्चित झाल्याचे कळवल्यास मी आपला ऋणी असेन.\nतसदीबद्दल क्षमस्व\nआपला आज्ञाधारक विद्यार्थी,\nअ.ब.क\nआठवी \'अ\'\n१२०१/सोनलसिद्धी,\nटिळक रोड, डोंबिवली (प).\nई मेल आयडी abc110@gmail.com\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59829,1662,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','अनिकेत / अनिता कबरे, इयत्ता आठवी, संत ज्ञानेश्वर विदधालय, पंढरपूर हा श्री. मुख्याध्यापक संत ज्ञानेश्वर विद्यालय, पंढरपूर यांना पत्र लिहून गरीच विद्यार्थी फंडातून गणवेश व वङ्ख्या-पुस्तके मिळण्यासंबंधी विनंती. पत्र लिहितो / लिहिते.','','','दिनांक: १५ जून, २०१८.\nप्रति,\nआदरणीय मुख्याध्यापक,\nसंत ज्ञानेश्वर विद्यालय,\nपंढरपूर\n<b>विषय</b> : गरीब विद्यार्थी फंडातून गणवेश व वह्या-पुस्तके मिळण्यासंबंधी विनंती-पत्र.\nसादर नमस्कार,\nमी अनिकेत कबरे आपल्या शाळेत इयत्ता आठवी \'ब\' मध्ये शिकत असून हे पत्र आपणास एका खास कारणाने लिहीत आहे माझे वडील ज्या कारखान्यात नोकरी करीत होते तो कारखाना गेल्या सहा महिन्यांपासून बंद आहे. घरात आम्ही चार भावडे आहोत. आई चार घरी काम करून कसा तरी संसार चालवते. आईच्या उत्पन्नात वाढत्या महागाईत माझा शालेय खर्च निभावणे अशक्य झाले आहे.\nतरी माझी आपणास अशी नम्र विनंती आहे की, आपण कृपया गरीब विद्यार्थी फंडातून मला गणवेश व वह्या-पुस्तके दयावीत. आपल्या या मदतीमुळे मला पुढील शिक्षण घेता येईल अन्यथा मध्येच मला शाळा सोडावी लागेल.\nमी आपणास आश्वासन देतो की शाळेची पुस्तके वर्षाच्या शेवटी मी सुस्थितीत परत करीन. तसेच खूप-खूप अभ्यास करीन आपण माझी ही विनंती मान्य कराल अशी आशा आहे. आपल्या होकाराची वाट पाहत आहे.\nकळावे तसदीब‌द्दल क्षमस्व.\nआपला आज्ञाधारक,\nअनिकेत कबरे\n(इयत्ता आठवी \'ब\')\nसत ज्ञानेश्वर विद्यालय,\nपंढरपूर.\nई मेल आयडी: aniketkabare90@gmail.com\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59830,1662,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','सदानंद खरे, लक्ष्मी भुवन, शनिवार पेठ, पुणे वेधून श्री संचालक सोनी-मोनी इलेक्ट्रॉनिक्स, शुक्रवार पेठ, पुणे यांना पत्र लिहून नुकत्वाच खरेदी केलेल्या टी व्ही संचाब‌द्दल तक्रार करणारे पत्र लिहितात.','','','दिनांक ३० मे २०१५\nप्रति,\nश्री संचालक,\nसोनी-मोनी इलेक्ट्रॉनिक्स,\nशुक्रवार पेठ, पुणे.\n<b>विषय </b>  :  नवीन खरेदी केलेल्या टी व्ही. संचाब‌द्दलची तक्रार.\nमहाशय,\nसप्रेम नमस्कार,\nमी आपणांकडून दि. १/३/२०१५ रोजी पॅनोसोनिक कंपनीचा (सपाट) टी. व्ही. संच २४,००० रुपयांना खरेदी केला. त्यावेळी आपल्या विक्रेत्याने हा टी. व्ही. संच घेण्याची शिफारस केली व त्याच्या विश्वासाहार्यतेब‌द्दल आम्हांला पूर्ण खात्री दिली.\nत्याप्रमाणे हा टी. व्ही. संच आम्ही खरेदी केला. परंतु दोनच महिन्यांत आम्हांला असे आढळून आले की या संचाच्या यंत्रात बिघाड आहे. कधी आवाज गायब होतो तर कधी चित्र गायब होऊन फक्त आवाज येतो. काही वेळा तर त्यावर फक्त आडव्या व उभ्या रेषा अथवा मुंग्या दिसू लागतात. आपल्याकडील एक तंत्रज्ञ एकदा येऊन थातूर-मातूर काम करून गेला, पण ही खराबी दूर झाली नाही.\nयामुळे टी. व्ही. बपण्याचा आमचा आनंद नष्ट होऊन मानसिक त्रास होत आहे. म्हणून आमची आपणांस अशी विनंती आहे की, आपण कृपया चांगला तंत्रज्ञ पाठवावा अथवा हा संच खराब असल्यास त्वरित तो बदलून दयावा माझ्या रिसोटचा क्रमांक ४५६४०५ असा असून ती दि. १/३/२०१५ची आहे. म्हणजेच शाश्वती समय (Guarantee Period) सपूर्णपणे आपल्या हातात आहे.\nआम्हांस पूर्ण खात्री आहे की, याबाबतीत आपण वैयक्तिक लक्ष घालून आमच्या तक्रारीची दखल घ्याल \'ग्राहकाचे समाधान हाच आमचा व्यापार\' असे आपले ब्रीद आहे. कृपया सहकार्य करावे.\nकळावे. तसदीब‌द्दल क्षमस्व\nआपला विश्वासू,\nसदानंद खरे\nलक्ष्मी भुवन,\nशनिवार पेठ, पुणे\nई मेल आयडी sadanandkhare20@gmail.com\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59831,1662,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','वर्गाचा क्रीडा प्रतिनिधी म्हणून क्रीडा साहित्य विक्रेत्याकडे आवश्यक क्रीडा साहित्याची मागणी करणारे पत्र लिहा.','','','दिनांक: १५ नोव्हेंबर २०२३\nमाननीय व्यवस्थापक,\nमेट्रो स्पोर्ट्स स्टोअर,\nनागोठणे  _ xxxxxx\n<b>विषय</b> : \'क्रीडा साहित्या\' ची मागणी करण्याबाबत.\nमाननीय महोदय,\nआमच्या शाळेत डिसेंबर महिन्याच्या अखेरीस \'जिल्हास्तरीय आंतरशालेय क्रीडा स्पर्धेचे\' आयोजन करण्यात आले आहे. त्यासाठी आम्हांला काही क्रीडा साहित्याची आवश्यकता आहे. क्रीडा शिक्षकांच्या मार्गदर्शनाखाली आवश्यक क्रीडा साहित्याची यादी तयार करून सोबत देत आहे.\n<table border=\"1\" style=\"width:fit-content; border-collapse: collapse\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n  <tr>\n    <th> क्र. (क्षेत्र)</th>\n    <th> क्रीडासाहित्य </th>\n    <th> नग </th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n     <td>१</td>\n    <td> बुद्धिबळाचे पट </td>\n    <td>८ </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n      <td>२ </td>\n    <td> कॅरम बोर्ड </td>\n    <td>४ </td>\n  </tr>\n<tr>\n      <td> ३</td>\n      <td> बॅडमिंटन रॅकेट </td>\n      <td>१२ </td>\n  </tr>\n<tr>\n      <td>४ </td>\n      <td>शटल कॉक </td>\n      <td>२४ </td>\n  </tr>\n<tr>\n      <td>५</td>\n      <td> हँडबॉल </td>\n      <td>४ </td>\n  </tr>\n<tr>\n      <td>६</td>\n      <td> हॉकीस्टिक </td>\n      <td>२४ </td>\n</tr>\n</table>\nआमची शाळा गेली अनेक वर्षे आपल्याच दुकानातून क्रीडा साहित्याची खरेदी करत आहे. या गोष्टी लक्षात घेऊन आम्हांला सवलतीच्या दरात दर्जेदार असे साहित्य उपलब्ध करून क्यावे, ही नम्र विनंती.\nआपला विश्वासू, अ. ब. क., क्रीडा प्रतिनिधी, शारदा विद्यालय, नागोठणे - xxxxxx इ-मेल - abc@gmail.com\n\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59832,1662,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','गणवेश व वह्या-पुस्तके मिळाल्यानंतर आभार मानणारे पत्र.','','','दिनांक १९ जून, २०१८.\nपति,\nमा. मुख्याध्यापक, पंढरपूर.\nसंत ज्ञानेश्वर विद्यालय,\nविषय: वहह्या-पुस्तके व गणवेश मिळाल्याबद्द‌ल आभार पत्र.\nआदरणीय मुख्याध्यापक,\nस.न.वि.वि.\nमी अ.ब.क.. आपल्या शाळेतील आठवी \'ब\'चा विदयार्थी. सर, आपण माझ्या पत्राचा व विनंतीचा मान राखून त्वरित कार्यवाही करून मला योग्य ती मदत मिळवून दिल्याबद्दल मी आपले कृतज्ञतापूर्वक आभार मानत आहे.\nआपण माझ्‌या परिवारावरचा व माझ्याही मनावरचा भार हलका केला आहे. मी आश्वासन देतो की मन लावून अभ्यास करीन व चांगले गुण मिळवून दाखवेन आपल्या मदतीब‌द्दल पुन्हा एकदा आभार धन्यवाद सर.\nतसदीबद्दल क्षमस्व\nकळावे,\nआपला आज्ञाधारक,\nअबक\n(इयत्ता आठवी \'ब\')\nसंत ज्ञानेश्वर विद्यालय,\nपंढरपूर\nई मेल आयडी abc100@gmail.com\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59833,1662,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','तुमच्या परिसरातील खेळाच्या मैदानावर झालेल्या अतिक्रमणावावत लोकप्रतिनिधीकडे तकार करणारे पत्र लिहा.','','','दिनांक १० जुलै २०२३\nप्रति,\nमा श्री मोहन पाटील,\nलोकप्रतिनिधी, प्रभाग क्र. १०,\nकल्याण डोचिवली महानगरपालिका,\nडोंबिवली XXXXXX\nविषयः खेळाच्या मैदानावर झालेल्या अतिक्रमणावावत\nमाननीय महोदय.\nआपल्या प्रभागातील म्हात्रेनगर भागातील \'कुस्तीगिर खाशाबा जाधव या मैदानावर गेले काही दिवस अतिक्रमण होत असल्याचे दिसून येत आहे बांधकामाचे नको असलेले साहित्य, फेरीवाल्यांची अनधिकृत दुकाने आणि काही भाजी विक्रेते व हॉटेल व्यावसायिक यांच्याकडून फेकला जाणारा कचरा यामुळे खेळासाठी राखीव असलेल्या या मैदानाचा गैरवापर होत आहे हे असेच चालू राहिले. तर आम्हां मुलांच्या खेळण्यासाठी उपलब्ध असलेले एकुलते एक मैदानही नष्ट होईल तरी कृपया आपण या तक्रारीची गांभीर्याने दखल घेऊन आवश्यक ती कारवाई करावी, ही नम्र विनंती\nआपला विश्वासू\nअबक\nप्रतिनिधी, बिजेता कीडा मंडळ\nम्हात्रेनगर\nडोंबिवली (प) XXxxxx\nइ-मेल abc@gmail.com\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59836,1662,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','तुमच्या परिसरातील खेळाच्या मैदानावर झालेल्या अतिक्रमणाबाबत महानगरपालिकेकडे तक्रार करणारे पत्र लिहा.','','','दिनाकः ०८ ऑक्टोबर २०२१\nप्रति,\nमा. महानगरपालिका आयुक्त,\nबृहन्मुंबई महानगरपालिका,\nमुबई\n<b>विषय </b> : खेळाच्या मैदानावर झालेल्या अतिक्रमणाबाबत\nमाननीय महोदय, दादरच्या प्रभादेवी परिसरातील \'प्रबोधनकार ठाकरे क्रीडा मैदान\' या मैदानावर अतिक्रमण झाल्याचे दिसून येत आहे. अनधिकृत दुकाने, तसेच अनधिकृत वस्त्या उभारल्या आहेत. यामुळे, येथे कचऱ्याचे साम्राज्य उभे राहिले आहे. खेळासाठी राखीव असलेल्या मैदानाचा गैरवापर होताना दिसत आहे.\nआधीच मुंबईसारख्या शहरात, मुलांना खेळाच्या मैदानासाठी जागा उपलब्ध नाही. जी आहेत त्यांना या अतिक्रमणापासून वाचवावे ही विनती कृपया या तक्रारीची गांभीयनि दखल घेऊन आपण योग्य ती कार्यवाही कराल, अशी आशा करतो.\nआपला विश्वासू,\nअबक\n८०२ - राधाकृष्ण अपार्टमेंट,\nप्रभादेवी, दादर,\nमुंबई - ××××××\nइ-मेल: abc@gmail.com\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59837,1662,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','आपल्या परिसरात होणाऱ्या अनियमित वीज पुरवठ्याब‌द्दल तक्रार करणारे पत्र महानगरपालिकेला लिहा.','','','दिनाकः ०९ फेब्रुवारी २०२२\nप्रति,\nकार्यकारी अभियंता,\nठाणे महानगरपालिका,\nठाणे (प.) xxxxxx\nविषयः अनियमित वीजपुरवठ्याबाबत तक्रार पत्र.\nमाननीय महोदय,\nमी अ.ब.क., ठाण्याच्या चरई विभागातील रहिवासी आहे. आमच्या विभागात गेले दोन आठवडे दुपारी २ ते सायं. ५ वाजेपर्यंत वीज पुरवठा खंडित होत आहे. उन्हाळ्याचे दिवस, तसेच शाळा बंद असल्याकारणाने मुलांचे ऑनलाईन क्लासेस त्यातच येऊन ठेपलेल्या वार्षिक परीक्षा हे सर्व लक्षात घेता तीन तासांच्या या खंडित वीज पुरवठ्याने आम्ही सर्व नागरिक त्रस्त झालो आहोत.\nआपण ही परिस्थिती लक्षात घेऊन योग्य ती कार्यवाही कराल, अशी आशा बाळगतो.\nआपला विश्वासू,\nअ.ब.क..\n४०२ - पारिजात सोसायटी,\nचरई, ठाणे (प.) xxxxxx\nइ-मेल: abc@gmail.com\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59844,1662,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','<b>\'श्रीराम विद्यामंदिर\' आयोजित</b>\n<b>आंतरशालेय निबंधस्पर्धा</b>\n          २५ मार्च स. १० वाजता\nपरीक्षक - सुजय जवळकर (प्रसिद्ध लेखक)\nश्रीराम विद्यामंदिर, अष्टविनायक चौक, ठाणे (प.) - ४००६०१\n','विद्यार्थी प्रतिनिधी या नात्याने आंतरशालेय निबंधस्पर्धेसाठी परीक्षक म्हणून उपस्थित राहण्याची विनंती करणारे पत्र लिहा.','','','दिनांकः १५ मार्च २०२१\nप्रति,\nमा. सुजय जवळकर,\nसंभाजीनगर चौक,\nठाणे (प.) - xxxxxx\nविषयः आतरशालेय निबंधस्पर्धेसाठी परीक्षक म्हणून उपस्थित राहण्याची विनंती करणारे पत्र\nमाननीय महोदय,\nमी अबक, श्रीराम विदद्यामंदिर, ठाणे या विदधालयातील विदधार्थी प्रतिनिधी या नात्याने आपणास हे पत्र लिहीत आहे आमच्या शाळेत दिनाक २५ मार्च रोजी आंतरशालेय निबंधस्पर्धा आयोजित करण्यात आली आहे. इयत्ता ८ वी. ९ वी व १० वीच्या विदयार्थ्यांसाठी ही स्पर्धा आयोजित करण्यात आली आहे.\nआपण या आंतरशालेय निबंधस्पर्धेत परीक्षक म्हणून उपस्थित राहावे अशी आमची इच्छा आहे आमच्या इच्छेस मान देऊन आपण\nपरीक्षक म्हणून उपस्थित राहावे, ही विनंती\nआपला विश्वासू,\n(विट्यार्थी प्रतिनिधी),\nअ ब क\nश्रीराम विद्यामंदिर,\nअष्टविनरायक चौक,\nठाणे (प.)\nइ-मेल: abc@gmail.com\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59847,1662,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','<b>ज्ञानभारती विद्यालयातर्फे</b>\n<b>आंतरशालेय चित्रकला स्पर्धा</b>\nदि. २८ डिसेंबर\nवयोगट - १२ वर्षे ते १५ वर्षे\n(आपला प्रवेश शाळेमार्फत नोंदवावा.)\n','आंतरशालेय चित्रकला स्पर्धेत सहभागी होण्याकरता विनंती करणारे पत्र माननीय मुख्याध्यापकांना लिहा.','','','दिनांकः १५ डिसेंबर २०२१\nप्रति,\nमा. मुख्याध्यापक,\nसंस्कार विदयालय,\nमातोश्री मार्ग,\nमुलुंड, मुंबई - xxxxxx\nविषयः आंतरशालेय चित्रकला स्पर्धेत सहभागी होण्याबाबत.\nमाननीय महोदय,\nमी कु. अ. ब. क., आपल्या शाळेतील इयत्ता आठवीचा विद्यार्थी आहे. २८ डिसेंबर रोजी ज्ञानभारती विद्यालयातर्फे आयोजित करण्यात आलेल्या आंतरशालेय चित्रकला स्पर्धेत भाग घेण्याची माझी इच्छा आहे. आपण मला या स्पर्धेत सहभागी होण्याची संधी दयावी ही नम्र विनंती.\nमी या अगोदरही अनेक चित्रकला स्पर्धांमध्ये बक्षिसे मिळवली आहेत. तसेच, इयत्ता ७ वी मध्ये एलिमेंटरी परीक्षेत \'अ\' श्रेणीने उत्तीर्ण झालो आहे. आपण मला संधी दिलीत, तर मी या स्पर्धेत यश मिळवण्यासाठी मनःपूर्वक प्रयत्न करेन\nकळावे.\nआपला विश्वासू,\nअ. ब. क.,\nइयत्ता - ८ वी \'अ\',\nसंस्कार विद्यालय,\nमातोश्री मार्ग,\nमुलुंड, मुंबई - xxxxxx\nइ-मेल: abc@gmail.com\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59849,1662,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','<b>आपले ग्रंथ भांडार</b>\nस्वस्त आणि मस्त\nशालेय विद्यार्थ्यांकरता सर्व प्रकारचे \nस्टेशनरी सामान मिळेल.\n[विद्यार्थ्यांकरता विशेष सवलत]\nपाच रस्ता, मुलुंड (प.) - xxxxxx\n','विद्यार्थी प्रतिनिधी या नात्याने शालेय वापरासाठी मागवलेल्या साहित्यावर सवलत देण्याची विनंती करणारे पत्र लिहा.','','','दिनांकः १ फेब्रुवारी २०२१\nप्रति, माननीय व्यवस्थापक, आपले ग्रंथ भांडार,\nपाच रस्ता, मुलुंड (प.) xxxxxx\nविषयः मागवलेल्या साहित्यावर सवलत मिळण्याबाबत.\nमाननीय महोदय,\nमी अ. ब. क. केळकर विदयालयाचा विद्यार्थी प्रतिनिधी या नात्याने आपणांस हे पत्र लिहीत आहे. आम्ही काही दिवसांपूर्वी आपल्या दुकानातून शालेय वापरासाठी काही शालेय वस्तूंची मागणी केली होती.\nकेळकर विद्यालय व आपल्या दुकानाचे अनेक वर्षांचे संबंध लक्षात घेऊन आपण आम्हांला या शालेय साहित्यांवर जास्तीत जास्त सवलत ट्यावी, ही विनंती !\nकळावे.\nआपला विश्वासू,\nअ.ब.क.,\n (विद्यार्थी प्रतिनिधी), केळकर विद्यालय, \nस्टेशन रोड, मुलुंड (प.) - xxxxxx\nइ-मेल: abc@gmail.com\n\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59858,1662,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','खालील विषयावर तक्रार पत्र लिहा.','','','','दिनांक ७ मार्च, २०१७.\nप्रति,\nमाननीय विभागीय अधिकारी,\nमहाराष्ट्र राज्य विद्युत मंडळ,\nचरई, ठाणे\n<b>विषय </b>: अनियमित व वारंवार खंडित होणाऱ्या वीज पुरवठ्याबाबत पत्र.\nमा. महोदय,\nसप्रेम नमस्कार वि. वि.\nमी अ.ब.क., आनंद नगर, कोपरी, ठाणे विभागातील रहिवासी आहे. मी आपणांस विनंतीपूर्वक कळवू इच्छितो की जानेवारी महिन्यापासून आमच्या विभागातील वीजपुरवठा वारंवार खंडित होत असून अनियमितही झाला आहे खंडित होण्याचा अवधीहो तीन-तीन तासांचा असतो. यामुळे या विभागातील सर्व रहिवाश्यांना अतिशय त्रास होत आहे. आजारी लोक, वृद्ध तसेच गृहिणी व विद्यार्थ्यांना गैरसोईचा सामना करावा लागत आहे. वीजपुरवठा खंडित झाल्याने बिल्डिंगमध्ये लिफ्ट बंद पडून तेथे राहणाऱ्या नागरिकांची खूप गैरसोय होत आहे. परीक्षा जवळ आल्याने वि‌द्यार्थ्यांनाही त्रास होत आहे.\nआपण एक कर्तव्यदक्ष व सहकार्यतत्पर अधिकारी आहात असा आपला लौकिक आहे. तरी कृपया समस्येची गंभीरता लक्षात घेऊन स्वतः लक्ष घालून या विभागातील वीजपुरवठा नियमित करण्याची व्यवस्था तातडीने करावी. तसेच याबाबत योग्य ती कारवाई ताबडतोब करावी ही नम्र विनंती.\nतसदीबद्दल क्षमस्व. कळावे.\nआपला कृपाभिलाषी,\nअ.ब.क.\nआनंद नगर, कोपरी,\nभिडेगुरुजी पथ,\nठाणे (प.) ४०००६.\nई मेल आयडी abc200@gmail.com\n',0,1,0,NULL),(59882,1663,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','दिलेल्या विषयावरून जाहिरातलेखन करा.\nआईस्क्रीम पार्लर ','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(59883,1663,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','दिलेल्या विषयावरून जाहिरात लेखन तयार करा .\nगावात सर्कस आली आहे','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(59884,1663,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','दिलेल्या विषयावरून जाहिरात लेखन तयार करा .\nकापडी पिशव्या','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(59886,1663,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','दिलेल्या विषयावरून जाहिरात लेखन तयार करा .\nशालेय गणवेश','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(59887,1663,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','दिलेल्या विषयावरून जाहिरात लेखन तयार करा .\nनॅशनल संगणक प्रशिक्षण केंद्र','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(59889,1663,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','दिलेल्या विषयावरून जाहिरात लेखन तयार करा .\nबालनाट्य','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(59908,1663,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','खालील जाहिरातीचे वाचन व निरीक्षण करून दिलेल्या प्रश्नांची उत्तरे लिहा','अ) उत्तरे लिहा.\n१) जाहिरातीचा विषय –\n२) जाहिरातीतील नवे तंत्रज्ञान -\n३) जाहिरातदाराचे नाव -\n४) जाहिरातदाराचा इ-मेल  -\n\nब) आकृती पूर्ण करा','','१) भाजीपाला पुरवठा\n२) गुगल प्लेवर अॅप उपलब्ध\n३) श्री. सुजय पाटील\n४) tajibhaji@gmail.com\n\nब) १) सेंद्रिय शेती\n२) माफक दर\n३) ऑनलाइन खरेदी\n४) माल शेतातून थेट घरात','',1,1,0,NULL),(59920,1663,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','खालील जाहिरातीचे वाचन व निरीक्षण करून दिलेल्या प्रश्नांची उत्तरे लिहा\n','१) जाहिरातीचा विषय -\n२) जाहिरात देणारे (जाहिरातदार) -\n३) वरील जाहिरातीत सर्वात जास्त आकर्षित करून घेणारा घटक -\n४) जाहिरात कोणासाठी आहे ?\nii. वरील जाहिरात अधिक आकर्षक होण्यासाठी त्यात कोणकोणत्या घटकांचा समावेश असावा, असे तुम्हांला वाटते?\n','','१) डिजिटल शाळेतील प्रवेश\n २) शाळा व्यवस्थापन समिती, मोरगाव\n३) विदयार्थी योजना\n४) इयत्ता पहिली ते आठवीमधील विद्यार्थ्यांसाठी\nii) वरील जाहिरातीमध्ये शाळेची वैशिष्ट्ये व विद्यार्थी योजना टॅबच्या आकारात बसवल्यास ते अधिक आकर्षक वाटेल.\'तंत्रज्ञानाची कास धरत, घडवूया उदयाचा भारत\' असे वाक्य शाळेच्या नावाखाली टाकता येईल. याशिवाय, संपर्क क्रमांक अथवा वेबसाइट नमूद केल्यास संपर्काकरिता योग्य माहिती उपलब्ध होईल.\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(59925,1664,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','जिल्हा परिषद उच्च प्राथमिक शाळा, उत्रौली या शाळेत कला शिबिराचा समारोप संपन्न.\n','','','दिनांक: २० डिसेंबर\nलोकप्रतिभा\nचित्रकला शिबिराचा समारोप\nउत्रौली (ता. भोर): उत्रौली येथील जिल्हा परिषद प्राथमिक शाळेत दहा दिवसांचे चित्रकला शिबिर नुकतेच संपन्न झाले. १९ डिसेंबर रोजी दुपारी ४.०० ते ६.०० या वेळात शिबिराचा समारोप समारंभ साजरा झाला. या शिबिराची सांगता प्रसिद्ध चित्रकार श्री. अविनाश नारायण शिवतरे यांच्या सप्रात्यक्षिक मनोगताने करण्यात आली.\nआपल्या जीवनातील कलेचे महत्त्व सांगताना प्रत्येकाने कोणती ना कोणती कला शिकणे आवश्यक आहे, हा विचार त्यांनी आपल्या मनोगतातून व्यक्त केला. समारंभाचे अध्यक्षस्थान प्राथमिक शाळेचे मुख्याध्यापक श्री. सदाशिव शिंदे यांनी भूषवले. कलाशिक्षिका श्रीमती सुनीता सोमण यांनी प्रमुख पाहुणे व उपस्थितांचे आभार मानले.\nया निमित्ताने सर्व पंचवीस शिबिरार्थीच्या चित्रांचे प्रदर्शन भरवण्यात आले होते. त्याला रसिकांचा उदंड प्रतिसाद मिळाला.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59926,1664,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','सावित्रीबाई कन्या शाळा, भुसावळ या शाळेत शालेय संचयिकेचा वर्धापनदिन सोहळा संपन्न.','','','दिनांकः १७ जुलै २०१८\nसंजीवनी संचयिका\nशालेय संचविकेचा वर्धापनदिन\nभुसावळ (ता भुसावळ): दिनांक १६ जुलै, २०१३ रोजी सावित्रीबाई कन्या शाळा, भुसावळ या शाळेतील विद्यार्थिनींनी संचयिकेचा उपक्रम सुरू केला होता. त्यास यंदा पाच वर्षे पूर्ण झाली. त्यानिमित्ताने दि १६ जुलै रोजी दुपारी १२-३० ते संध्याकाळी ५-०० या वेळेत संचयिकेचा वर्धापनदिन साजरा करण्यात आला. याप्रसंगी गुणवंत विद्यार्थ्यांच्या गुणगौरवार्थ कार्यक्रम आयोजित केला होता.\nया कार्यक्रमाचे प्रमुख पाहुणे श्री. गोविंदराव दांडेकर, महाराष्ट्र बँकेचे शाखा प्रमुख (आठवडे बाजार शाखा, भुसावळ) उपस्थित होते. समारंभाच्या अध्यक्षस्थानी माजी विद्यार्थिनी डॉ. जयश्री उपाध्याय होती. शाळेतील सर्व विद्यार्थिनी या कार्यक्रमास आवर्जून उपस्थित होत्या.\nसंचयिका प्रमुख सौ. वैशाली पाटील यांनी संचयिकेबद्दल माहिती दिली. आज संचयिकेत एकूण ३००० खाती आहेत. सुरुवातीला ११० ने प्रत्येक सदस्याने खाती उघडली होती. खाते उघडण्यासाठी रकमेची मर्यादा नव्हती. म्हणूनच आज संचयिकेत समाधानकारक रक्कम जमा आहे. शाळेतील विद्यार्थिनींना आवश्यक असेल तेव्हा या संचयिकेतून आर्थिक सहकार्य मिळू शकते. संचयिकेचे सर्व व्यवहार विद्यार्थिनीच बघतात, त्यामुळे त्यांना बँकेच्या व्यवहाराचे ज्ञान होते. प्रत्येक वर्षी पदाधिकारी बदलले जातात. अर्थातच इ. ५ वी ते इ. ८ वीच्या वर्गातील मुलींना संधी मिळते. या प्रयोगामुळे मुलींना बचतीची सवय लागते. पैशांची बचत व देवाणघेवाणीचे व्यवहार समजतात. कार्यक्रमाच्या शेवटी मुख्याध्यापिका सौ. रजनी देवरे यांनी उपस्थितांचे आभार मानले. या कार्यक्रमास पालकवर्गही मोठ्या प्रमाणात उपस्थित होता.\nअशा प्रकारे प्रत्येक शाळेने \'संचयिकेचा\' उपक्रम राबवावा.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59935,1664,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','दिनांक: ४ जून\nकोकण किनारपट्टीला चक्रीवादळाचा तडाखा\nअरबी समुद्रात कमी दाबाचा पट्टा तयार झाल्यामुळे हवामान खात्याने वर्तवलेल्या अंदाजानुसार निसर्ग चक्रीवादळाचा फटका रायगड जिल्ह्यातील अनेक गावांना बसला. श्रीवर्धन, मुरुड, रोहा, अलिबाग या तालुक्यातील गावांना याचा मोठा तडाखा बसला आहे. कोकणातील हरिहरेश्वर हे गाव तीर्थक्षेत्र, तसेच पर्यटनस्थळ म्हणून ओळखले जाते; परंतु या चक्रीवादळाने या गावाची अत्यंत बिकट अवस्था झाली आहे.\nया चक्रीवादळात नारळ, आंब्यांच्या बागा पूर्णपणे उद्ध्वस्त झाल्या आहेत. घरांची छपरे उडून गेली आहेत. घरातील सामानाचे मोठ्या प्रमाणात नुकसान झाले आहे. अनेकांचे संसार उघड्यावर आले आहेत. वादळापूर्वी अनेक लोकांनी सुरक्षिततेचा उपाय म्हणून स्थलांतर केले होते; त्यामुळे जीवितहानी झाली नाही.\nसरकारतर्फे वादळग्रस्तांना तातडीची मदत जाहीर करण्यात आली असून पंचनाम्याचे काम युद्धपातळीवर करण्याचे आदेश देण्यात आले आहेत.\n','खालील बातमी वाचून त्याखाली दिलेल्या प्रश्नांची उत्तरे लिहा.\nकोकण किनारपट्टीला चक्रीवादळाचा तडाखा\n','अ) उत्तरे सांगा.\n१) चक्रीवादळाचे नाव -\n२) उताऱ्यात आलेले समुद्राचे नाव -\nब) आकृती पूर्ण करा\n','','१) निसर्ग चक्रीवादळ\n२) हरिहरेश्वर\n','',0,1,1,NULL),(59938,1664,'descriptive','5',4,2,'Out of Text Book','दिनांकः ८ फेब्रुवारी\n\'इग्नू\' चे नवे ऑनलाईन अभ्यासक्रम मराठीत\nनागपूर इग्नू (इंदिरा गांधी नॅशनल ओपन युनिव्हर्सिटी) तर्फे नव्या शिक्षण धोरणानुसार अभ्यासक्रमाची रचना करण्यात आली आहे हा नवीन ऑनलाईन अभ्यासक्रम मराठीतही उपस्थित होणार आहे. \'इग्नू\' चे प्रादेशिक केंद्राचे संचालक डॉ. पी. शिवस्वरूप यांनी ही माहिती दिली आहे.\nया विद्यापीठाच्या वतीने २०२२ च्या सत्रात सुरू होणाऱ्या नव्या ऑनलाईन अभ्यासक्रमांची घोषणा करण्यात आली. हे नवीन अभ्यासक्रम अगोदर इंग्रजी भाषेत उपलब्ध असतील; परंतु त्यानतर ते लवकर मराठी भाषेतदेखील सुरू करण्यात येतील. स्वयंप्रभा आणि ज्ञानप्रदर्शन चॅनलच्या माध्यमातून इग्नूचे अभ्यासक्रम मराठीत उपलब्ध करून दिले जातील.\nया नव्या अभ्यासक्रमांमध्ये एम. एस्सी (फूड सेफ्टी अॅन्ड क्वॉलिटी मॅनेजमेंट), एम. ए. (एनव्हार्यमेंटल अॅन्ड ऑक्युपेशनल हेल्थ), पी. जी. डिप्लोमा इन अॅग्रिबिझनेस, पी. जी. डिप्लोमा इन मायग्रेशन, बीए ऑनर्स (संस्कृत, उर्दू), सर्टिफिकेट इन व्हिज्युअल आर्टस् अॅन्ड अप्लाईड आर्ट यांचा समावेश असेल अशी माहिती डॉ. शिवस्वरूप यांनी दिली. नवीन अभ्यासक्रमाची प्रवेश प्रक्रिया जानेवारी २०२२ पासून सुरू करण्यात आली आहे.\n','खालील बातमी वाचून त्याखाली दिलेल्या प्रश्नांची उत्तरे लिहा.','i) उत्तरे सांगा.\n१ \'इग्नू\' चे पूर्ण रूप -\n२)\'इग्नू\' वे प्रादेशिक संचालक -\n३) \'इग्नू\' चे नवीन अभ्यासक्रम या भाषेत उपलब्ध करून दिले जाणार आहेत.\n४) या नवीन अभ्यासक्रमाची प्रवेश प्रक्रिया कधीपासून सुरू करण्यात आली ?\nii) आकृती पूर्ण करा\n','','१) इंदिरा गांधी नॅशनल ओपन युनिव्हर्सिटी\n२) डॉ. पी. शिवस्वरूप\n३) मराठी\n४) जानेवारी २०२२ पासून\n','',0,1,1,NULL),(59941,1666,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','आपल्यासारख्या सामान्यांना शब्दावाचूनचे संवाद भावणारही नाहीत, की परवडणारही नाहीत. आपल्याला कठीण, साधे, सरळ, वक्र कसे का होईना; पण बोलणे आणि ठणठणीत बोलणेच हवे असते आणि या बोलण्याचे किती अनंत प्रकार असतात. \'व्यक्ती तितक्या प्रकृती\' अशी म्हण आहे. त्या चालीवर \'माणसे तितकी बोलणी\' अशी म्हण बनवायला हरकत नाही. \'मोकळा संवाद\' असे आपण म्हणतो; पण समाजात वावरताना या तथाकथित मोकळ्या संवादावर कशी आणि किती बंधने पडत असतात ते पाहिले म्हणजे गंमत वाटते. मित्रमंडळीशी गप्पा मारताना आपण खूप मुक्त, मोकळे असतो अशी आपली समजूत असते; पण ती खरी असते का? आपणाला एकमेकांचे अनेक गुणदोष, एकमेकांच्या जीवनातले बरेवाईट तपशील ठाऊक असतात; त्यामुळे तिथे कधी मोकळ्या गप्पा होत असल्या, तरी अनेकदा नात्यातल्या जवळीकतेमुळेच कधी कधी एक चमत्कारिक अवघडलेपणही अनुभवाला येते. एकमेकांची मते, आग्रह, दुराग्रह ठाऊक असल्यामुळे मतभेदाचे अवघड विषय बहुधा आपण शिताफीने टाळतो. वृत्तीतल्या हळव्या जागा, स्वाभिमानाची ठिकाणे माहीत असल्यामुले बोलताना त्यांना कुठे धक्का लागणार नाही, समोरच्या व्यक्तीचे मन दुखावले जाणार नाही, याची सतत काळजी घ्यावी लागते.','खालील उतारा वाचा. त्याचा तुम्हांला समजलेला अर्थ सारांश रूपाने पुन्हा लिहा. \n','','','सर्वसामान्य माणसांना शब्दांवाचून संवाद करणे शक्य होत नाही. व्यक्तिपरत्वे बोलण्याचे अनंत प्रकार पडतात. समाजात वावरत असताना आपल्या संवादावर अनेक बंधने येतात. त्यामुळे, खऱ्या अर्थाने मोकळा संवाद होतोच असे नाही. मित्रमंडळींशी गप्पा मारतानादेखील आपण मोकळेपणाने न बोलता शब्दांचा जपून वापर करतो. नात्यातल्या जवळीकतेमुळेच मित्रांचे स्वभाव ठाऊक असल्याने त्यांचे मन जपण्यासाठी त्यांना न रुचणारे विषय टाळून त्यांना भावणाऱ्या विषयांवरच संवाद साधण्याचा प्रयत्न करावा लागतो.','',0,0,0,NULL),(59942,1666,'descriptive','5a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','२०१९ साली संपूर्ण मानवजातीवर मोठे संकट आले, ते म्हणजे जगभर झालेला कोरोना विषाणूचा प्रादुर्भाव. अनेक लोक या विषाणूमुळे मृत्युमुखी पडले. साऱ्या जगात हाहाकार उडाला होता. ज्या माणसाने संपूर्ण निसर्गावर सत्ता स्थापन करून आपण या पृथ्वीचे अनभिषिक्त सम्राट असल्यासारखे वर्तन सुरू केले होते, त्या माणसाला. एका न दिसणाऱ्या विषाणूने दाती तृण धरायला भाग पाडले हे सत्य आहे. कोरोना विषाणूमुळे संपूर्ण जगाचे फार मोठे नुकसान झाले, हे जरी खरे असले तरी माणसाला अनेक गोष्टी नव्याने समजून घेता आल्या. स्वच्छतेचा मंत्र माणसाने जपला. आपल्या माणसांचे महत्त्व त्याला लक्षात आले. लॉकडाऊनच्या काळात प्रचंड वेगाने पळणारा मानवी समाज स्वतः पिंजऱ्यात बंदिस्त असल्यासारखा बसला. पृथ्वीवरचे जीवनचक्र सुरळीत राहण्यासाठी माणसाने आपल्याबरोबरच इतर प्राणी, पक्षी, झाडे, कीटक यांचा विचार करायलाच हवा, हा दृष्टिकोन या माणसामध्ये जर विकसित झाला तरच माणूस खऱ्या अर्थाने पृथ्वीचा रक्षक बनेल.','खालील उतारा वाचा. त्याचा तुम्हांला समजलेला अर्थ सारांश रूपाने पुन्हा लिहा.\n','','','कोरोना काळात संपूर्ण जगात खूप हानी झाली. माणूस निसर्गावर विजय मिळवू शकत नाही, हे एका विषाणूच्या प्रादुर्भावामुळे सिद्ध झाले. या वाईट काळातही माणसाला स्वच्छता व आपल्या माणसांचे महत्त्व नव्याने कळले. माणसाने आपल्या बरोबरच इतर सजीवही तेवढेच महत्त्वाचे आहेत हे लक्षात घेतले, तर पृथ्वीवरील जीवनचक्र टिकून राहील.\n\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59943,1666,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','माणसाच्या जीवनाचा एक अविभाज्य भाग म्हणजे क्रीडा किंवा खेळ होय. लहानथोर सारेच जण कोणता ना कोणत्ता खेळ आवडीने खेळतात किवा पाहतात. पूर्वी विटीदांडू, लगोरी, आटापाट्या, सूरपारंब्या, लपाछपी, आंधळी कोशिबीर असे खेळ लहान मुले खेळताना दिसत. संगणकाचे युग आले आणि त्या मागोमाग मोबाइल. मैदानात खेळणारी मुले घराबाहेर पडेनाशी झाली बैठे खेळ अगोदरही होते. पत्ते, कॅरम, सापशिडी, ल्युडो यांसारखे खेळ घराघरांतून खेळले जात; पण मैदानावर, दिवसभर उन्हातान्हात खेळणारी मुले हे चित्र सर्रास दिसत असे. आता मोबाइलवर वेगवेगळे \'गेम\' उपलब्ध झाले आहेत. यामध्ये तासन्तास एकाच जागी बसून हे खेळ खेळले जातात. लहान मुलांमध्ये या खेळांचे आकर्षण वाढत आहे, त्यामुळे एकेकाळी घराबाहेरून ओढत घरी । आणावी लागणारी मुले घरातून बाहेर मैदानात खेळायला जावी म्हणून प्रयत्न करावे लागत आहेत. सतत घरात बसून मोबाइलवर खेळ खेळल्यामुळे डोळ्यांचे आजार, मधुमेह, लठ्ठपणा, मानसिक असंतुलन यांसारख्या विकारांना लहान मुले बळी पडत आहेत. मुलांनी मैदानी खेळ खेळणे त्यांच्या आरोग्याच्या दृष्टीने अतिशय महत्त्वाचे आहे.','खालील उतारा वाचा. त्याचा तुम्हांला समजलेला अर्थ सारांश रूपाने पुन्हा लिहा.\n\n','','','खेळाला मानवाच्या आयुष्यात अनन्यसाधारण महत्त्व आहे. पूर्वी मैदानी खेळ व बैठे खेळ यांचा योग्य मेळा घातला जाई, पण आता मोबाइलच्या अतिवापरामुळे मैदानी खेळ विसरलेली मुले शारीरिक, मानसिक व्याधींनी गांजलेली दिसतात. बैठे खेळ किंवा मोबाइल गेममुळे मुलांनी घराबाहेर पडणे बंद केले आहे. मुलांनी मैदानी खेळ खेळले, तरच त्यांचा योग्य शारीरिक व मानसिक विकास होऊ शकेल.','',0,0,0,NULL),(59944,1666,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','प्रत्येक विजयामागे एक गोष्ट हमखास असते, ती म्हणजे सततचे प्रयत्न किवा कष्ट. कष्ट म्हणजे केवळ शारीरिक श्रम नव्हेत कष्ट म्हणजे आपले ध्येय पूर्ण करण्यासाठी योग्य ते नियोजन करून त्यासाठी सतत प्रयत्न करणे होय. कोणत्याही क्षेत्रातील यश है। एका दिवसात किंवा नशिबाने मिळत नसते. तसे ते मिळेलही; पण ते टिकवणे खूप कठीण असते. याउलट त्या त्या क्षेत्रात आलेले अपयश आणि त्या अपयशी अनुभवानंतर केलेले प्रयत्न ज्या यशोशिखराकडे घेऊन जातात ते यश अधिक आनंददायी, अधिक समाधान देणारे व टिकणारे असते. कोणाचा तरी वशिला, ओळख, नातेवाईक म्हणून अथवा लाच देऊन मिळालेली संधी प्रत्येकवेळी कामी येतेच असे नाही. हिऱ्याची चमक ही त्याला पैलू पाडल्यानंतर येते, सोन्याला आगीतून गेल्यानंतर झळाळी येते । त्याचप्रमाणे व्यक्ती यशस्वी होण्यामागे वर्षानुवर्षांचे प्रामाणिक प्रयत्न कारणीभूत ठरतात. प्रत्येक यशामागे एक अपयशाचा अनुभव। असतो. त्यावर मात करण्यासाठी जिद्दीने प्रयत्न करावे लागतात.','खालील उतारा वाचा. त्याचा तुम्हांला समजलेला अर्थ सारांश रूपाने पुन्हा लिहा.\n\n','','','कोणतीही गोष्ट मिळवण्यासाठी सतत प्रयत्न करावे लागतात. अपयशानंतर मिळालेले यश हे आनंद देणारे व टिकाऊ असते. कोणत्याही प्रकारे चुकीच्या मार्गाने मिळालेले यश टिकत नाही. यशस्वी होण्यासाठी प्रामाणिक प्रयत्न करावे लागतात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(59945,1666,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','असे म्हटले जाते, की पहिला घास घेण्यापूर्वी त्या शेतकऱ्याचे स्मरण करा, त्याला धन्यवाद दया, ज्याने आपल्या रक्ताचे पाणी। करून, मेहनत करून, दिवसरात्र शेतात राबून तुमच्यासाठी धान्य पिकवले. झोपण्यापूर्वी त्या सैनिकाचे आभार माना, जो आपल्या घरादाराचा त्याग करून, थंडी, ऊन, वारा, पावसात देशाच्या सीमेवर शत्रूपासून आपले रक्षण करण्यासाठी उभा आहे. ज्यामुळे आपण निश्चिंतपणे झोपू शकतो. आपले दैनंदिन जीवन, सणवार, उत्सव सारे काही निर्विघ्नपणे पार पाडू शकतो. भारताचे माजी पंतप्रधान स्वर्गीय लालबहादूर शास्त्री यांनी दिलेली \'जय जवान जय किसान\' ही केवळ घोषणा नाही, तर भारतमातेच्या आधारस्तंभांबद्दलची कृतज्ञता यामध्ये सामावलेली आहे. आपण मात्र या शेतकऱ्यांसाठी अथवा सैनिकांसाठी काय करतो? आपली त्यांच्याप्रति काही कर्तव्ये नाहीत का? शेतकऱ्याच्या मालाला योग्य तो भाव मिळत नाही. निसर्गाचा लहरीपणा, कर्ज या सगळ्यांतून मार्ग काढत शेतकरी शेती करत असतो. सैनिकाचेही तसेच आहे. आपले आईवडील, पत्नी, मुले यांचा त्याग करून देशाचे रक्षण करणारा सैनिक परत येईल, की नाही याची शाश्वती नसते; मात्र तो प्राणपणाने तिरंग्याच्या रक्षणार्थ लढा देतो. या दोघांचेही आपल्यावरील उपकार हे कधीही न फिटणारे आहेत.','खालील उतारा वाचा. त्याचा तुम्हांला समजलेला अर्थ सारांश रूपाने पुन्हा लिहा.\n\n','','','अन्नदाता शेतकरी व देशाचे रक्षण करणारे सैनिक यांचे आपल्यावर अनंत ऋण आहेत. त्यांच्यामुळे आपले जीवन सुरळीत चालते हे प्रत्येकाने लक्षात ठेवले पाहिजे. अनंत अडचणींना सामोरे जाणाऱ्या शेतकरी व सैनिकांबद्दल मनात कृतज्ञता बाळगणे आपले कर्तव्य आहे.','',0,0,0,NULL),(59946,1666,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','\'सारे जहाँ से अच्छा हिंदोस्तां हमारा\' असे ज्याचे वर्णन केलेले आहे तो हिंदुस्थान, भारत, इडिया असे नावातही वैविध्य असणारा आपला देश खरोखरच विविधतेने नटलेला आहे. काश्मीरपासून कन्याकुमारीपर्यंत प्रत्येक राज्यात विविधता आढळते. ही विविधता संस्कृती, परंपरा, सण, उत्सव, भाषा, अन्न, पेहराव, तसेच भौगोलिकतेतही आढळते. असे असूनही एका धाग्याने आम्ही सारे बांधलेलो आहोत. तो धागा आहे \'भारतीयत्व.\' भारतभर वेगवेगळी संस्कृती आढळते. यामध्ये वेगवेगळ्या प्रकारचे कपडे परिधान करणारे लोक आढळतात. वेगवेगळ्या भाषा बोलल्या जातात. वेगळे नृत्यप्रकार, सण, उत्सव साजरे करण्याच्या वेगवेगळ्या परंपरा येथे प्रत्येक राज्यात पाळल्या जातात. प्रत्येक राज्यात वेगळी भाषा बोलली जाते; किंबहुना एकाच राज्यात अनेक भाषा देखील बोलल्या जातात. भारत हा एकमेव असा देश असू शकेल येथे जगभरातील विविध गोष्टी पाहायला मिळतात. भारतात समुद्रकिनारे, नद्या आहेत. वाळवंट आहेत. येथे बर्फ पडते. हिमालयासारख्या बर्फाच्या पर्वतरांगा आहेत. हिवाळा, पावसाळा, उन्हाळा हे तिन्ही ऋतू आपल्याला अनुभवता येतात. भारताच्या विविधतेचे आणखी एक वैशिष्ट्य म्हणजे इंग्रजी कॅलेंडरमधील एका वर्षांत विविधधर्मी अनेक भाषेचे लोक वेगवेगळ्या दिवशी नवीन वर्षाचे स्वागत करत असतात.','खालील उतारा वाचा. त्याचा तुम्हांला समजलेला अर्थ सारांश रूपाने पुन्हा लिहा.\n\n','','','भारत हा देश विविधतेने नटलेला आहे. येथे भाषा, खानपान, पोषाख, संस्कृती, सण, परंपरा यांमध्ये प्रत्येक राज्यांत विविधता आहे तरीही भारतीय म्हणून सगळे एक आहेत. भारतात भौगोलिक विविधता आढळते. भारत असा देश आहे, की ज्यामध्ये विविध धर्मानुसार नवीन वर्ष वेगवेगळ्या दिवशी साजरे केले जाते.','',0,0,0,NULL),(59947,1666,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','तो सूर्य पहा, त्याचे दर्शन म्हणजे परमात्म्याचे दर्शन. तो नाना प्रकारची चित्रे आकाशात रंगवीत असतो. चित्रकार महिनेच्या महिने कुंचले मारून सूर्योदयाची चित्रे रंगवितात. सकाळी उठून जरा पहा परमेश्वराची कला. त्या दिव्य कलेला, त्या अनंत सौंदर्याला उपमा तरी देता येईल कां ? पण पाहतो कोण ? तिकडे तो सुंदर भगवान उभा राहून म्हणतो, \"आळश्या तू निजू पाहशील, परंतु मी तुला उठवणार आहे.\" स्थावर जंगमाचा सूर्य हा आत्मा आहे. हा मित्र लोकांना हाका मारतो. त्यांना काम करायला लावतो. त्याने स्वर्गपृथ्वीचे रूप धारण केले आहे. खरोखरच तो सूर्य जीवनाचा आधार आहे. त्याच्या ठिकाणी परमात्मा पाहा.','खालील उतारा वाचून त्याचा सारांश लिहा व योग्य शीर्षक लिहा.\n\n','','','सूर्याचे दर्शन म्हणजे प्रत्यक्ष परमेश्वराचेच दर्शन. हा ईश्वर आकाशात विविध चित्रे काढीत असतांना, पृथ्वीवर ही चित्रकार सूर्योदयाची चित्रे अनेक महिने काढीत असतात. जी माणसे सकाळी खूप उशीरापर्यंत झोपून राहतात. अशा आळशी माणसांना भगवान सूर्य सांगतात की, \'हे आळश्या, तू झोपण्याचा प्रयत्न केला तरी मी तुला उठवणार आहे. सूर्य हा जगाचा आत्म आहे. जीवनाचा आधार आहे.\n<b>या उताऱ्यास योग्य शीर्षक</b> : \'जीवनाधार सूर्य\', किंवा \'महान कलाकार\' अथवा \'परमात्म्याचे दर्शन\' यापैकी एक\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59948,1666,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','आळस सोडावयाचा म्हणजे शरीर परिश्रम करावयाचे. आळस जिंकण्याचा हाच एक उपाय आहे. हा उपाय अमलात आणला नाही तर त्याची शिक्षा निसर्ग भोगावयास लावील. रोगाच्या किंवा अन्य कोणत्यातरी रूपाने शिक्षा भोगाणे सुटत नाही. शरीर ज्या अर्थी आम्हांस दिलेले आहे. त्या अर्थी श्रम हे करावेच लागणार. शरीर श्रमात गेलेला वेळ फुकट जात नाही. त्याचा मोबदला मिळतोच. उत्तम आरोग्य लाभते. बुद्धी सतेज, तीव्र व शुद्ध होते. पुष्कळ विचारवंतांच्या विचारातही त्यांच्या पोटदुखीचे व डोळेदुखीचे प्रतिबिंब उमटते. विचारवंत जर सृष्टीच्या सान्निध्यात विचार करील तर त्याचे विचारही तेजस्वी होतील. शारीरिक रोगाचा जसा मनावर परिणाम होतो. तसाच आरोग्याचाही होतो ही अनुभवाची गोष्ट आहे. पुढे जीवनात रोग जडल्यावर वैयाकडे जाऊन औषधोपचार घेण्यापेक्षा आजच जर बाहेर कुदळी घेऊन खणले, बागेला पाणी घातले, लाकडे फोडली तर काय वाईट?','पुढील गढ्य उताऱ्याचे सारांश लेखन आपल्या शब्दांत लिहा.\n','','','शरीर कष्टानेच आळसावर मात करता येते. शारीरिक श्रम केल्यानेच उत्तम आरोग्य, बुद्धी व सतेजता प्राप्त होते. सृष्टीच्या मोकळ्या हवेतील विचार व लेखनही दोष व द्वेष मुक्त असतात. रोगाप्रमाणेच आपल्या आरोग्याचाही शरीरावर व मनावर परिणाम होतो. रोग झाल्यावर आजारी पडून उपचार घेण्यापेक्षा रोग होऊच नये म्हणून आधीच परिश्रम केलेले केव्हाही चांगले आहे.','',0,0,0,NULL),(59949,1666,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','भारतात वन्यजीवांचा अतिशय गंभीर प्रश्न निर्माण झाला आहे. वन्य प्राण्यांच्या संरक्षणाची गरज भासत आहे. प्राण्यांचे विविध अवयव, कातडे, शिंगे, इत्यादी गोष्टी मिळवण्याकरिता भारतामध्ये वन्यजीवांची सर्रास हत्या केली जाते. सतत होत असणाऱ्या शिकारीमुळे काही प्राणी नष्ट होऊ लागले आहेत, तर काही प्राण्यांची संख्या अचानक कमी झाल्यामुळे जंगलातील अन्नसाखळीवर दुष्परिणाम झालेला आहे. या प्राण्यांची संख्या वाढावी यासाठी काही प्रकल्प शासकीय स्तरावर योजले गेले आहेत. कायद्याने प्राण्यांच्या शिकारीवर बंदी घालण्यात आली आहे. एखादया वन्य प्राण्याची शिकार करताना दिसल्यास शिकार करणाऱ्या व्यक्तीला तुरुंगवासाची शिक्षा होऊ शकते व दंड म्हणून काही हजारांपर्यंत पैसे भरण्याची शिक्षा केली जाते. शासनाच्या या प्रयत्नांमुळे वन्य प्राण्यांची शिकार कमी होऊन त्यांची संख्या वाढण्यास मदत झाली आहे. जंगलातील अन्नसाखळीतील सर्व प्राणी सुरक्षित राहून निसर्गाचेसंतुलन राखण्याच्या दृष्टीने आपण उचललेले हे पाऊल आहे, असे म्हणता येईल.','खालील उतारा वाचा. त्याचा तुम्हांला समजलेला अर्थ सारांश रूपाने पुन्हा लिहा.\n','','','भारतामध्ये विविध कारणांसाठी वन्य प्राण्यांच्या केल्या जाणाऱ्या हत्येमुळे त्यांच्या संरक्षणावावत फार मोठा प्रश्न निर्माण झाला आहे. प्राण्यांची संख्या दिवसेंदिवस कमी होत आहे, तर काही प्राणी नष्ट होत आहेत. यामुळे. निसर्गाचे संतुलन विघडत आहे. यावर उपाय म्हणून शासनाने विविध प्रकल्प सुरू केले आहेत, तसेच कायदयाने प्राण्यांच्या शिकारीवर बंदी घातली आहे. परिणामी, प्राण्यांची संख्या वाढून अन्नसाखळी सुरक्षित राखण्यात व निसर्गाच्या संतुलनात मदत होत आहे.','',0,0,0,NULL),(59951,1666,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','भारत हा सांस्कृतिकदृष्ट्या विविधता असलेला देश आहे. भारतातील प्रत्येक प्रदेशामध्ये विविध लोककलांची परंपरा आहे. यामध्ये लोकगीत, लोकवाक्य, लोकनृत्य आणि लोकनाट्य यांचा समावेश आहे. धार्मिक सण व सामाजिक जीवन यांचा एक महत्त्वाचा भाग म्हणून या लोककलांची परंपरा निर्माण होऊन त्या विकसित झाल्या. गुजरातमधील गरवा, पंजावमधील भांगडा यांसारखी इतर राज्यांमध्ये काही लोकनृत्ये आहेत. महाराष्ट्रातील लावणी, आसाममधील विहू, केरळमधील कथकली आणि राजस्थानमधील घुमर व भवाई हे वैशिष्ट्यपूर्ण नृत्यप्रकार आहेत. सर्व नृत्यप्रकार सादर करत असताना गायन, वादन यांच्या साथीची आवश्यकता असते. या नृत्यांमधून भारतीय संस्कृतीचे सादरीकरण केले जाते. लोकगीतांच्या माध्यमातून संस्कृतीवरोवरच इतिहासातील वैशिष्ट्यपूर्ण घटना गायनाद्वारे सादर केल्या जातात. उदा. पोवाड्यातून शौर्यकथा, तर भजन-कीर्तनातून संतांचे विचार मांडले जातात, म्हणूनच आपली संस्कृती व इतिहास पुढच्या पिढीलाही माहीत होण्यासाठी लोककलेची परंपरा जपणे आवश्यक आहे.','खालील उतारा वाचा. त्याचा तुम्हांला समजलेला अर्व सारांश रूपाने पुन्हा लिहा.\n','','','भारतामध्ये विविध स्वरूपाच्या लोककला प्रत्येक प्रदेशात तेथील सामाजिक जीवन व धार्मिक सण यांनुसार विकसित झाल्या आहेत. याव्यतिरिक्त, भारतातील विविध राज्यांचे वैशिष्ट्य सांगणारी व गायन वादनाच्या साथीने सादर केली जाणारी नृत्ये आढळतात. त्यातून भारतीय संस्कृती व इतिहास यांचे सादरीकरण केले जाते. म्हणूनच, पुढल्या पिढीकडे संस्कृती व इतिहासाचा हा वारसा सोपवण्याकरिता या परंपरा जपणे महत्त्वाचे आहे.\n\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59952,1666,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','कला हा माणसाच्या जीवनाचा अविभाज्य भाग आहे. नृत्य, नाट्य, गायन, वादन, लेखन, चित्रकला, शिल्पकला अशा विविध कला आपल्या मनाला सुखावणारा अनुभव देतात; किंबहुना कलेमुळेच आपण जीवनाचा परिपूर्ण अनुभव घेऊ शकतो. रोजच्या आयुष्यातील अनेक प्रकारच्या चिंता, ताणतणाव हलके करून क्षणभर विसावण्यासाठी कलेचा आस्वाद किंवा तिचे सादरीकरण यासारखा दुसरा विरंगुळा नाही. मानवी जीवन अनेक अडचणी, चिंता आणि विवंचनांनी भरलेले असते. कलाकाराकडे निसर्गाकडे पाहण्याची एक वेगळी सौंदर्यदृष्टी असते. निसर्गाच्या विविध रूपांमधून त्याला कलेच्या आविष्काराची ऊर्मी प्राप्त होते. ही ऊर्मी कलाकाराला स्वस्थ बसू देत नाही. त्यामुळेच, कोणत्याही अडचणीवर मात करून कलाकार आपली कला सादर करतो. प्रत्येक सच्चा कलाकार आपल्या कलेमध्ये अधिकाधिक प्रावीण्य मिळवण्यासाठी अखंडपणे झटत असतो. कलेच्या सादरीकरणातील परिपूर्णत्व हाच त्याचा ध्यास असतो; किंबहुना कला हाच त्याचा श्वास असतो, असे म्हटल्यास वावगे ठरणार नाही.','खालील उतारा वाचा. त्याचा तुम्हांला समजलेला अर्थ सारांश रूपाने पुन्हा लिहा.\n','','','विविध कलांमुळे आपण रोजच्या जीवनातील ताणतणावांतून बाहेर पडून जीवनाचा पूर्ण आनंद घेऊ शकतो. कलेचे सादरीकरण करणाऱ्या कलाकाराला निसर्गाकडे पाहण्याची अनोखी सौंदर्यदृष्टी लाभलेली असते. कलेच्या आविष्काराची ऊर्मी कलाकाराच्या मनात सतत उचंबळून येत असते. प्रत्येक सच्चा कलाकार आपल्या कलेमध्ये अधिकाधिक प्रावीण्य मिळवण्यासाठी सातत्याने प्रयत्नशील असतो. कलेतील परिपूर्णता हाच प्रत्येक कलाकाराचा ध्यास आणि श्वास असतो.','',0,0,0,NULL),(59957,1669,'descriptive','5b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','प्रत्येक व्यक्तीच्या आयुष्यात सुखदुःखाचे क्षण नेहमीच येत असतात. दुःखाच्या व अडचणीच्या प्रसंगाना जे खिलाडू वृत्तीने सामोरे जातात, जे जिकण्याच्या उर्मीने हाती घेतलेले काम पूर्ण करण्यासाठी स्वयंप्रेरणेने काम करतात, तेच आयुष्यात यश मिळवतात. कोणतीही वाईट परिस्थिती तुम्हांला अडवू किवा हरवू शकत नाही. वेळप्रसंगी तुम्हांला दोन पावले मागेही टाकावी लागतात; परंतु जर आपण मनानेच हरलो, तर पुढील कार्य पूर्ण करण्यासाठी आपण तयार होऊ शकत नाही. अशा परिस्थितीत कायम आपले आपल्या मनावर नियंत्रण असणे आवश्यक असते.\nनकारात्मक विचार करण्यापासून आपण स्वतःला थांबवणे आवश्यक आहे. त्याचबरोबर आपल्या मनाला चांगल्या सवयी लावणेही आवश्यक आहे. आपल्या मनाला चांगली सवय लावणे हे कठीण असले, तरी अशक्य मात्र नक्कीच नाही। आपल्या अगो असणाऱ्या चांगल्या सवयी, वाईट सवयींना जवळ येऊ देत नाहीत. मनाला चांगल्या विचारांची सवय लावली, तर ती सवय वाईट विचारांपासून तुम्हांला नक्कीच दूर ठेवील.यासाठी तुम्हाला काही गोष्टी लक्षात ठेवाव्या लागतील. उदा., चांगले वाचन, चांगल्या मित्रमैत्रिणीची संगत, घरातील ज्येष्ठ व्यक्तीशी असणारे जिव्हाळ्याचे व आपुलकीचे संबंध इत्यादी. जो दुसऱ्याच्या दुःखात नेहमी सहभागी होतो त्यालाच जीवनाचा खरा अर्थ कळतो. मानसिक आधार देऊन, विचारांच्या देवाणघेवाणीतून आपण एकमेकांचे दुःख सहज हलके करू शकतो.असे सुखदुःखाचे प्रसंग प्रत्येकाच्या आयुष्यात सतत येत असतात; मात्र या प्रसंगांना जो धीराने सामोरा जातो, तोच जीवनात यशस्वी होतो.\n','खालील उतारा वाचा व त्यास योग्य शीर्षक दया.\n','','','शीर्षक : यशाचा मूलमंत्र','',0,0,0,NULL),(59959,1669,'descriptive','5b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','माणसाच्या आयुष्यात अनेक नाती असतात. काही जन्मतः मिळतात, काही नाती रक्ताची नसतात तरीही माणसाच्या आयुष्यात ती अनमोल असतात. यातील एक नातं म्हणजे \'मैत्री\'. मैत्री हे असं एक नातं आहे ज्याची तुलना इतर कोणत्याही नात्याबरोबर होऊ शकत नाही. मित्र कसा असावा? हा प्रश्न नेहमीच विचारला जातो. मित्र सूर्यासारखा असावा असे म्हटले जाते. नेहमी प्रकाश देणारा; पण रात्रीच्या वेळी तो आपली साथ सोडतो. मित्र पुस्तकासारखा असावा असेही म्हटले जाते, पण सगळीच पुस्तके योग्य मार्ग दाखवतात असेही नाही. मित्र कृष्णासारखा असावा का? गरीब सुदामाला न मागता देणारा आणि प्रत्यक्ष युद्धात सहभागी न. होता पार्थाचे सारथ्य करून पांडवांना विजयी करणारा, की मित्र कर्णासारखा असावा? दुर्योधन चुकीचा आहे हे माहीत असूनही, समोर पराभव दिसत असतानाही मित्रप्रेमाखातर मरेपर्यंत साथ देणारा! मित्र हा आपल्या मनाचा आरसा असावा. आपण चुकलो, तर योग्य मार्ग दाखवणारा, आपण जिंकलो, तर \'विजयोत्सव\' साजरा करणारा आणि पराभूत झालो, तर \'पुन्हा प्रयत्न करू\' म्हणत साथ देणारा.','खालील उतारा वाचा व त्यास योग्य शीर्षक दया.\n','','','शीर्षक : मित्र कसा असावा?','',0,0,0,NULL),(59961,1669,'descriptive','5b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','माणूस इतर प्राण्यांपेक्षा वेगळा ठरला याचे कारण त्याने भाषा बोलायला सुरुवात केली. इतर प्राणी एकमेकाशी संवाद साधतात किंवा त्यांच्या भावना व्यक्त करतात; मात्र त्यांना त्या स्पष्टपणे मांडता येत नाहीत. कुत्र्याला भूक लागली, राग आला किंवा कंटाळा आला तरीही तो भुंकतो. त्याच्या भुंकण्याची पद्धत थोडीफार वेगळी असते. माणसाला आपल्या मनातील भावभावना व्यक्त करण्यासाठी भाषेचे माध्यम वापरता येते. जगभरात विविध भाषा बोलल्या आणि लिहिल्या जातात. वर्षानुवर्षे भाषेच्या स्वरूपात सातत्याने बदल झालेले दिसून येतात. चारशे-पाचशे वर्षांपूर्वी बोलली जाणारी मराठी भाषा आणि आजची मराठी भाषा यामध्ये खूप मोठे बदल झालेले आपल्याला पाहायला मिळतात. भाषेचे स्वरूप हे भौगोलिक वातावरण, संस्कृती, नवे शोध, परकीय आक्रमणे यांनुसार बदललेले पाहायला मिळते. कोणतीही भाषा ही केवळ संवाद साधण्याचे माध्यम नसते, तर ती एक सांस्कृतिक ठेवा असते. ज्यामध्ये माणसाच्या होणाऱ्या प्रगतीची पाळेमुळे असतात. भाषेच्या इतिहासामुळे मानवी इतिहास समजण्यास मदत होते. भाषा नसती, तर कदाचित माणसाची प्रगती खुंटली असती.\n','खालील उतारा वाचा व त्यास योग्य शीर्षक दया.\n','','','शीर्षक : भाषेचे मोल','',0,0,0,NULL),(59962,1669,'descriptive','5b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','\"स्वामी तिन्ही जगाचा आईविना भिकारी\" या ओळीमध्ये खूप मोठा अर्थ सामावलेला आहे. आई ही कोणाचीही असू दे, तिची थोरवी सगळीकडे सारखीच असते. पक्षी, प्राणी अथवा मानव-जन्मदात्री ही आपल्या बाळाची अगदी तशीच काळजी घेते. आपल्या पिल्लांवर लक्ष ठेवून आकाशात उडणारी घार असो किंवा पिल्लांसाठी शिकार घेऊन येणारी वाघीण प्रत्येकात \'आईपण\' ओथंबून भरलेले दिसते. एवढीशी कोंबडीदेखील आपल्या चिमुकल्या पिल्लांच्या रक्षणासाठी लढायला तयार होते. माणसाच्या आईची तर गोष्टच निराळी. ही माय माऊली अगदी कमरेत वाकली आणि तिची मुले साठीत पोहोचली तरीही तिला ती लहानच वाटतात. आई जशी वात्सल्यमूर्ती आहे तशीच ती आपली पहिली गुरु आहे. जिजामातेने स्वप्न पाहिले म्हणूनच शिवबा छत्रपती झाले. आईचे ऋण आपण या जन्मात फेडू शकत नाही हे खरं आहे. असं म्हटलं जातं, की देव प्रत्येकाच्या घरी जाऊ शकत नाही म्हणून त्याने आई निर्माण केली. त्या आईच्या प्रेमाची भुरळ देवालाही पडली.\n','खालील उतारा वाचा व त्यास योग्य शीर्षक दया.\n','','','शीर्षक : आईची महती','',0,0,0,NULL),(59964,1669,'descriptive','5b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','केवळ पृथ्वी हा असा ग्रह आहे, जेथे जीवसृष्टी अस्तित्वात आहे. आपल्या सूर्यमालेतील इतर कोणत्याही ग्रहावर जीवसृष्टीच्या अस्तित्वाचा पुरावा संशोधकांना सापडलेला नाही. पृथ्वीवरील जीवसृष्टी म्हणजेच सजीव. यामध्ये प्राणी, पक्षी, झाडे, कीटक, जीवजंतू आणि माणूस या साऱ्यांचा समावेश होतो. सजीव निर्मिती झाली ती पाण्यामध्ये, म्हणून पाण्याला जीवन असे म्हटले जाते. प्रत्येक सजीवाला जगण्यासाठी पाण्याची आवश्यकता असते. माणूस इतर जीवांसह या पृथ्वीवरचा रहिवासी आहे, मात्र आपल्या बुद्धीसामर्थ्याच्या जोरावर त्याने इतर साऱ्या जीवांना आपले अंकित केले आहे. कधी काळी जंगलात, गुहेमध्ये इतर हिस्र प्राण्यांपासून लपूनछपून राहणारा कमजोर माणूस आता त्याच बलशाली प्राण्यांना आपल्या इशाऱ्यावर नाचवताना दिसतो. ही पृथ्वी केवळ आपली जहागीर आहे, या तोऱ्यात माणसाने इतर सजीवांना संपवण्याचा सपाटा लावला आहे. यामुळेच, अनेक वृक्ष, वनस्पती, विविध प्राण्यांच्या जाती नामशेष झालेल्या दिसतात. माणूस जर स्वतःला सर्वश्रेष्ठ समजून इतरांना संपवत राहिला, तर पृथ्वीवरील जीवनचक्र संपुष्टात येईल आणि माणसाचादेखील हास होईल हे निश्चित!\n','खालील उतारा वाचा व त्यास योग्य शीर्षक दया.\n\n','','','शीर्षक : अविचारी मानव','',0,0,0,NULL),(59966,1669,'descriptive','5b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','आयुर्वेद शास्त्रामध्ये प्रत्येक ऋतूंमध्ये कोणता आहार घ्यावा, याचा खूप बारकाईने अभ्यास करण्यात आला आहे. देशाच्या विविध भागांत वर्षभर साजऱ्या केल्या जाणाऱ्या अनेक सणवारांच्या कालावधीत तेथील ऋतूनुसार साजेसे अन्नपदार्थ बनवले जातात. ऋतूनुसार आहारात आवश्यक बदलही केला जातो. उदा. थंडीच्या ऋतूत येणाऱ्या संक्रांत, दिवाळी या सणांच्या वेळी गूळपोळी, तिळगूळ, चकली, करंजी, लाडू असे उष्णता आणि स्निग्धता असलेले पदार्थ बनवले जातात. उन्हाळ्याच्या कालावधीत आहारामध्ये कैरीचे पन्हे, कोकम सरबत, सोलकढी असे थंडावा देणारे पदार्थ घेतले जातात. पावसाळ्याच्या काळात कुई, टाकळा, भारंगी अशा विविध औषधी रानभाज्या खाल्ल्या जातात. आपल्या परिसरात व हवामानात जे पिकते तेच आपल्या प्रकृतीला मानवते असे म्हटले जाते. देशातील ज्या भागात जे धान्य पिकते त्याचा समावेश तेथील लोकांच्या आहारात जास्त प्रमाणात केला जातो. उदा. उत्तर भारतामध्ये गहू जास्त प्रमाणात पिकतो. त्यामुळे, तेथील लोकांच्या आहारात गव्हापासून बनवलेले पदार्थ जास्त प्रमाणात असतात, तर दक्षिण भारतात तांदळाचे उत्पादन मोठ्या प्रमाणावर होत असल्याने तेथील लोक मुख्यतः तांदळापासून बनलेले पदार्थ खातात. तेथील हवामानात ते आरोग्यदायी ठरते.\nआहारामध्ये ऋतुनिहाय बदल करण्याचे हे ज्ञान एका पिढीकडून दुसऱ्या पिढीकडे संक्रमित झाले आहे.\nत्यामुळे, प्रत्येक कुटुंबातील ज्येष्ठ स्त्री ऋतुनिहाय विविध खाद्यपदार्थ तयार करून आपल्या कुटुंबाचे आरोग्य उत्तम राखण्यात पारंगत असते. आजच्या आधुनिक काळात जगातील विविध संस्कृतींचा आपल्याला खूप जवळून परिचय झाला आहे. त्यामुळे, परदेशातील पिझ्झा, बर्गर, पास्ता, विविध प्रकारचे नूडल्स, विविध चायनीज पदार्थ, शीतपेये आपल्या आहारात सहज समाविष्ट झाले आहेत. हे पदार्थ आपल्या ऋतुमानाला अनुरूप नाहीत आणि येथील हवामानात मानवणारेही नाहीत. हे पदार्थ सातत्याने\nखाल्ल्यास आरोग्याच्या विविध समस्या उद्भवू शकतात. थोडक्यात, ऋतूनुसार आपल्या देशात पिकणारे धान्य, फळे यांचा आहारात समावेश केल्यास आपले आरोग्य उत्तम राहण्यास मदत होते.\n','खालील उतारा वाचा व त्यास योग्य शीर्षक ट्या.\n','','','शीर्षक :  आहार परंपरा पाळा, अनारोग्य टाळा.','',0,0,0,NULL),(59967,1669,'descriptive','5b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','मानवाच्या उत्क्रांतीपासूनच निसर्ग आणि माणूस यांच्यामध्ये अतूट असे नाते निर्माण झाले आहे. सुरुवातीला निसर्गात घडणाऱ्या घटना जसे पाऊस, वारा, ऊन, ढगांचा गडगडाट इत्यादींविषयी कुतूहल वाटत होते. हळूहळू परिस्थितीशी जुळवून घेत निसर्गात आपले अस्तित्व टिकवण्याचा त्याने प्रयत्न केला. \'जो थांबला तो संपला\' असे म्हटले जाते. डार्विन या शास्त्रज्ञानेही असे म्हटले आहे, की प्रत्येकाला आपले अस्तित्व टिकवून ठेवण्यासाठी निसर्गाशी जुळवून घ्यावेच लागते. म्हणजेच, अनुकूलन साधावे लागते, म्हणूनच पृथ्वीवर विविध नैसर्गिक परिस्थितीनुसार वनस्पती, प्राणी, पक्षी व मानवी जीवन यांच्यामध्ये भिन्नता आढळते. उदा. उष्ण वाळवंटी प्रदेशातील वनस्पती या पावसाचे प्रमाण कमी असल्यामुळे खुरट्या व काटेरी असतात, तसेच, त्यांच्यात पाणी साठवून ठेवण्याची क्षमता असते. तर या भागात आढळणाऱ्या प्राण्यांपैकी उंटाची शरीररचना वैशिष्ट्यपूर्ण असते. चरबी व पाणी साठवण्यासाठी त्याच्या शरीराची वैशिष्ट्यपूर्ण रचना असते. तसेच, वाळूत चालता यावे यादृष्टीने पावलांची रचना असते. तेथील मानवही सुती कापडाचा वस्त्रासाठी उपयोग करतो, तर थंड वर्फाच्छादित प्रदेशामध्ये राहणाऱ्या रेनडियर, हिमकोल्हा यांसारख्या प्राण्यांच्या अंगावर दाट केस असतात. तेथील मानवदेखील प्राण्यांच्या कातड्यांपासून तयार केलेल्या वस्त्रांचा प्रामुख्याने वापर करतो. अशारीतीने, प्रत्येक सजीव अनुकूलन साधण्याचा म्हणजेच निसर्गाशी मिळतेजुळते घेण्याचा प्रयत्न करत असतो.\n','खालील उतारा वाचा व त्यास योग्य शीर्षक ट्या.\n','','','शीर्षक : अनुकूलन.','',0,0,0,NULL),(59969,1669,'descriptive','5b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','बहु असोत सुंदर संपन्न की महा। प्रिय अमुचा एक महाराष्ट्र देश हा ।। अशा या विस्तृत व सुंदर महाराष्ट्राला भौगोलिक संपन्नता लाभली आहे. पश्चिमेला अरबी समुद्राचा किनारा त्याला लागून चिंचोळा किनारी मैदानी प्रदेश, त्यालगत उत्तरदक्षिण दिशेने पसरलेल्या सह्याद्री पर्वताच्या रांगा आणि पूर्वेला दख्खनचे पठार, याशिवायगोदावरी, कृष्णा, भीमा, कोयना या नदया अशी महाराष्ट्राची भौगोलिक रचना आहे. सह्याद्री पर्वतरांगा या पश्चिम घाटाचाच महाराष्ट्रात असलेला भाग आहे. याच्या मुख्य पर्वतरांगेपासून पूर्वेकडे सातमाळा-अजिंठा, हरिश्चंद्रगड-बालाघाट व महादेव डोंगररांगा हे प्रमुख फाटे आहेत. सह्याद्रीचे महाराष्ट्राच्या हवामानामध्ये महत्त्वाचे स्थान आहे. अरबी समुद्रावरून वाहणारे व पाऊस घेऊन येणारे (वाष्पयुक्त) वारे सहयाद्री पर्वतांमुळे अडवले जातात व पश्चिम महाराष्ट्राला जून ते सप्टेंबर या काळात पाऊस मिळतो. ज्यामुळे धान्य पिकवू शकणारा बळीराजाही सुखावतो. सह्याद्री पर्वतरांगांमधील विविध घाटांमुळे कोकणातील व दख्खनच्या पठारावरील ठिकाणे जोडलेली आहेत. शिवाजी महाराजांच्या काळातही या घाटांचा ये-जा करण्याच्या दृष्टीने फार मोठा उपयोग झाला; किंबहुना सह्याद्रीच्या साथीनेच शिवरायांनी संख्येने कमी असलेल्या मावळ्यांसह हिंदवी स्वराज्याचे स्वप्न साकारले.\nगिर्यारोहणासारख्या साहसी खेळाची आवड असणाऱ्या गिर्यारोहकांना सह्याद्री नेहमीच खुणावत असतो. येथील कळसूबाई हे सर्वोच्च शिखर, हरिश्चंद्र, अलंग, मलंग, कुलंग यांसारखी अनेक शिखरे सर करण्यासाठी गिर्यारोहक उत्सुक असतात. सह्याद्री हा निसर्गसौंदर्याने नटलेला आहे. त्यामुळे, त्याचे सौंदर्य डोळ्यांत भरण्यासाठी अनेक पर्यटकदेखील भेट देतात. येथील जैवविविधतेमुळेच कास पठाराचा जागतिक वारसास्थळांच्या यादीत समावेश आहे.\n\n','खालील उतारा वाचा व त्यास योग्य शीर्षक ट्या.\n','','','शीर्षक : सहयाद्री - महाराष्ट्राची शान','',0,0,0,NULL),(59970,1669,'descriptive','5b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','अग्नी, पृथ्वी, वायू, जल आणि आकाश ही पंचमहाभूते या विश्वाचे कार्य अखंडितपणे चालू ठेवण्याचे काम करतात. या महाभूतांच्या विविध रूपांतून आपल्याला या सृष्टीची विविध रूपे अनुभवता येतात. या महाभूतांमधून सतत वाहणारी ऊर्जा पृथ्वीवरील जीवसृष्टीची निर्मिती, स्थैर्य आणि विनाश यांना कारणीभूत ठरते. सृष्टीतील प्रत्येक घटनेचा जाणीवपूर्वक अनुभव घेतल्यास \'ऊर्जा निर्माण करता येत नाही किंवा ती नष्टही करता येत नाही, तिचे एका ऊर्जेतून दुसऱ्या ऊर्जेत रूपांतर होते.\' या ऊर्जेविषयीच्या नियमाचा प्रत्यय येतो. प्राचीन काळापासून हे विश्व नेमके कशापासून बनले आहे, असा प्रश्न मानवाला सतावत आहे आणि अनेक\n तत्त्वचिंतकांनी यावर लेखनही केले आहे. महर्षी कणाद यांनी, \'हे विश्व अणूंचे बनलेले आहे\' असा सिद्धान्त मांडला. आजच्या आधुनिक विज्ञानानेदेखील अणू हा या विश्वातील लहानात लहान पदार्थ असून त्याच्या केंद्रकामध्ये प्रचंड ऊर्जा एकवटलेली असते, हे सिद्ध केले आहे. एकूणच, या सृष्टीच्या प्रत्येक कणामध्ये कोणत्या ना कोणत्या रूपात ऊर्जा सामावलेली आहे.\n','खालील उतारा वाचा व त्यास योग्य शीर्षक ट्या.\n','','','शीर्षक : ऊर्जा हाच विश्वाचा आधार.','',0,0,0,NULL),(59971,1668,'descriptive','5b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','तुमच्या शाळेत सांस्कृतिक कार्यक्रमाचे आयोजन करण्यात आले आहे. हा कार्यक्रम पाहण्यासाठी पालकांना आवाहन करणारा सूचनाफलक तयार करा.','','','<div style=\"border:3px solid black; padding: 20px; margin: 20px; border-radius: 10px\">•सूचना •\nदि. २४ फेब्रुवारी\nज्ञानसाधना विद्यालय, पंढरपूर\nसमस्त पालकवर्गाला सहर्ष कळवण्यात येते, की दरवर्षीप्रमाणे या वर्षीही आपल्या शाळेच्या सांस्कृतिक कार्यक्रमाचे आयोजन दि. २७ फेब्रुवारी रोजी नटराज नाट्यगृह येथे करण्यात आले आहे. या कार्यक्रमासाठी आवश्यक असणारी प्रवेशिका शाळेच्या कार्यालयात विनामूल्य उपलब्ध आहे. सदर कार्यक्रमास पालकांनी उपस्थित राहून मुलांना प्रोत्साहन द्यावे ही विनंती.\nमुख्याध्यापक ज्ञा\nनसाधना विद्यालय, पंढरपूर</div>\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59976,1668,'descriptive','5b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','गणेशोत्सवानिमित्त शाळेला देण्यात येणाऱ्या सुट्टीची माहिती देणारा सूचनाफलक तयार करा','','','<div style=\"border:3px solid black; padding: 20px; margin: 20px; border-radius: 10px\">•सूचना •सूचना •\nशारदा विद्यामंदिर, गोरेगाव\nदि. ९ सप्टेंबर\nसर्व विद्यार्थ्यांना सूचित करण्यात येत आहे, की दि. १० सप्टेंबर ते १४ सप्टेंबर या कालावधीत गणेशोत्सवानिमित्त शाळेला सुट्टी राहील. दि. १५ सप्टेंबरपासून शाळा नियमित वेळेत भरेल, याची सर्व विद्यार्थ्यांनी नोंद घ्यावी. </div\n\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59983,1668,'descriptive','5b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','खालील विषयावर सूचनाफलक तयार करा.\n\'शैक्षणिक सहलीसाठी नावनोंदणी.\'','','','<div style=\"border:3px solid black; padding: 20px; margin: 20px; border-radius: 10px\">\n• सूचना•\nदि. १२ नोव्हेंबर\nज्ञानभूषण विद्यालय, माणगाव\nदरवर्षीप्रमाणे यावर्षीदेखील एकदिवसीय शैक्षणिक सहलीचे आयोजन करण्यात आले आहे. सदर सहल दि. २५ नोव्हेंबर रोजी \'प्रतापगड किल्ला\' येथे जाणार आहे. याकरिता वर्गशिक्षकांकडे आपली नावनोंदणी करायची आहे. सहलीसाठी नावनोंदणी करताना पालकांचे परवानगी पत्र सादर करणे आवश्यक आहे. . </div\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59984,1668,'descriptive','5b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','इमारतीच्या प्रवेश‌द्वारासमोर वाहने उभी न करण्याविषयी सूचनाफलक तयार करा.','','','<div style=\"border:3px solid black; padding: 20px; margin: 20px; border-radius: 10px\">\n•सूचना •\nदि. २० जून\nसन्मान सहकारी सोसायटी, बदलापूर सोसायटीच्या प्रवेशद्वारासमोर कोणत्याही प्रकारची वाहने लावू नयेत. सदर रस्ता सोसायटीच्या रहदारीचा आहे. रस्त्यासमोर लावलेल्या वाहनांचे क्रमांक वाहतूक नियंत्रण विभागाला कळवून योग्य ती कारवाई केली जाईल. . </div\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59985,1668,'descriptive','5b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','खालील विषयावर सूचनाफलक तयार करा.\nरस्ते स्वच्छता.','','','<div style=\"border:3px solid black; padding: 20px; margin: 20px; border-radius: 10px\">\n•सूचना •\nदि. २५ मार्च\nग्रामपंचायत मारळ\nग्रामपंचायत मारळ विभागातील समस्त नागरिकांना कळवण्यात येते, की गेल्या काही दिवसांपासून आपल्या विभागातील रस्ते कचऱ्याने भरलेले आहेत. नागरिकांनी कचराकुंडीचा वापर कचरा टाकण्यासाठी करावा ही नम्र विनंती. कोणीही रस्त्यावर कचरा टाकताना आढळल्यास दंडात्मक कारवाई केली जाईल. . </div\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59987,1668,'descriptive','5b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','सूचनाफलक तयार करा : उद्या शहरात मुसळधार पावसाची शक्यता. नागरिकांनी खबरदारी घ्यावी -महानगरपालिका दक्षता विभाग.','','','<div style=\"border:3px solid black; padding: 20px; margin: 20px; border-radius: 10px\">\nमहानगरपालिका दक्षता विभाग\nदिनांक : ८ जून २०१८\nतमाम नागरिकांना,\nमहानगर पालिका, दक्षता विभाग, दादर, मुंबई तर्फे कळविण्यात येते की, उद्या दिनांक ९ जून २०१८ रोजी मुंबईत मुसळधार पावसाची शक्यता आहे. जनजीवन विस्कळीत होण्याची शक्यता आहे. तरी नागरिकांनी आवश्यक कारणाशिवाय घराबाहेर पडू नये.\nदक्षता घ्यावी. महानगरपालिका कर्मचारी मदतीसाठी सिद्ध आहेतच. परंतु तरीही नागरिकांनी खबरदीरी घ्यावी.\nयाची नागरिकांनी नोंद घ्यावी.\n- महानगरपालिका दक्षता विभाग</div\n\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59989,1668,'descriptive','5b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','खालील विषयावर सूचनाफलक तयार करा.\nरहदारी संबंधी खास सूचना.','','','<div style=\"border:3px solid black; padding: 20px; margin: 20px; border-radius: 10px\">\nमुंबई महानगरपालिका वाहतूक विभाग, कुर्ला\nदिनांक : १३ जून २०१८\nकुर्ला, एस वॉर्ड, विभागातील रस्त्यांची अवस्था खूपच खराब झाल्याने व पावसाळा तोंडावर आल्याने तातडीने या भागातील रस्ता दुरुस्तीचे काम हाती घेण्यात आले आहे. यासाठी या विभागातील वाहतूक एकेरी करण्यात आली आहे. नागरिकांनी या काळात पदपथाचाच वापर करावा. वाहनचालकांनी वेगमर्यादा पाळावी. रस्त्यात घोळक्याने उभे राहून रहदारीस अडथळा आणू नये. फुटपाथवरील विक्रेत्यास येथे व्यवसायास बंदी आहे.\nकृपया सर्व नगरिकांनी सूचनांचे पालन करून सहकार्य करावे. </div\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59991,1668,'descriptive','5b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','\'स्वच्छ मुंबई, सुंदर मुंबई\' योजनेत नागरिकांनी सहभाग घेण्यासाठी सूचनाफलक तयार करा.','','','<div style=\"border:3px solid black; padding: 20px; margin: 20px; border-radius: 10px\">\nमुंबई महानगरपालिका\nदिनांक : २६ जानेवारी २०१८\nमुंबई शहरात राहणाऱ्या तमाम नागरिक, दुकानदार, फेरीवाले, भाजी विक्रेते, व इतरही सर्वांस कळविण्यात येत आहे की, आपल्या माननीय पंतप्रधानांनी \'स्वच्छ भारत, रोगमुक्त भारत\' ही योजना जाहिर केली आहे. याच योजने अंतर्गत मुंबई महानगरपालिकेने ही मुंबई सार्वजनिक आरोग्यस्खात्यातर्फे \'स्वच्छ मुंबई, सुंदर मुंबई\' ही योजना राबविण्याचे ठरवले आहे.\nतमाम नागरिकांना कळविण्यात येत आहे की त्यांनी केरकचरा, घाण, विड्या सिगरेटची थोटके, कागदाचे बोळे कचरापेटीतच टाकावे. आपले शहर स्वच्छ ठेवण्यास आम्हांस सहकार्य करावे. आपली मुंबई स्वच्छ व सुंदर ठेवणे हे प्रत्येक नागरिकाचे कर्तव्य आहे. याची नोंद घ्यावी.\nमुंबई सार्वजनिक आरोग्य विभाग,\nमुंबई महानगरपालिका</div>\n\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59993,1668,'descriptive','5b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','\nसूचनाफलक तयार करा शाळेच्या सहलीबाबत माहिती व सूचना\n','','','<div style=\"border:3px solid black; padding: 20px; margin: 20px; border-radius: 10px\">\nसूचनाफलक\nसर्वोदय विद्यालय, कळवा\nदिनांक : १३ जून २०१८\nयावर्षी आपल्या शाळेची वर्षासहल \'गंगोत्री\' येथे नेण्याचे निश्चित करण्यात आले आहे. \'गंगोत्री\' हे पवित्र स्थळ असून \'शिवा\'ची भव्य मुर्ती तसेच अप्रतिम निसर्ग सौंदर्याने नटलेले आहे.\nसहल दिनांक २१ जुलै २०१८ ते २३ जुलै २०१८ या तीन दिवसांची आहे. सहलीची वर्गणी रुपये ७००/- (सातशे) फक्त ठेवण्यात आली आहे. विवार्थ्यांनी वरील रक्कम व पालकांचे संमतीपत्र पुढील दहा दिवसांत आपल्या वर्गशिक्षकांकडे जमा करून आपल्या नावाची नोंदणी करावयाची आहे.\nपुढील आठवड्यात दिनांक १९/७/१८ रोजी सकाळी ठीक दहा वाजता विद्यार्थी व पालकांची सभा शाळेच्या सभागृहात घेतली जाईल. या सभेत सहली संबंधीत सर्व माहिती दिली जाईल. तसेच पालकांच्या शंकांचे समाधानही करण्यात येईल.\nकृपया विद्यार्थ्यांनी त्वरा करावी. नाव नोंदणी मर्यादित आहे.\nमुख्याध्यापक, सर्वोदय विद्यालय </div>\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59996,1667,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','नदी व झाड या दोघांमधील संवादाची कल्पना करून संवादलेखन करा.\n\n','','','नदी : काय रे वृक्षराजा, असा उदास का आहेस?\nझाड : काय सागू सरिता ताई, दिवसेंदिवस तुझे पाणी कमी होत आहे आणि पावसाचा अजूनही काही पत्ता नाही. मला भविष्याची चिता वाटू लागली आहे.\nनदी : काही काळजी करू नकोस झाड दादा. मी वाहते आहे तोपर्यंत तुला पाण्याची चिंता करायची गरज नाही; पण या माणसांचा काही भरवसा नाही\nझाड : काग? काय झाले?\nनदी : काही दिवसापूर्वी मी ऐकले, की माझ्या मागच्या बाजूला बंधारा घालून मला अडवणार आहेत. मी विचार करत होते किती स्वार्थी आहे हा माणूस! मला तिथे अडवणार मग मी पुढे जे पाणी पोहोचवते त्याचे काय?\nझाड : हो तर! माझे काय? मला तर आता ऐकूनच घाम फुटला. तुझ्या प्रवाहात आनंदाने राहणाऱ्या जलचरांचे काय होणार? तुझ्या पाण्यावर अवलबून असणाऱ्या शेतकऱ्यांचंच काय?\nनदी : कोणी कितीही बांध बांधले तरी मी मुळीच थांबणार नाही. जोपर्यंत सागराला जाऊन भेटत नाही तोपर्यंत मला समाधान लाभणार नाही.\nझाड : तू खरी जीवनदायिनी आहेस. मनुष्य, पशू पक्षी, प्राणी, किडे, जलचर आणि आम्ही वृक्षवेली सारेजण तुझेच पाणी पिऊन तृप्त होतो.\nनदी : मी जीवनदायिनी आहे, तर तू परोपकारी मित्र आहेस साऱ्यांचा. माणसाला लाकूडफाटा पुरवतोस, तुझ्या सावलीमध्ये प्राणी, पक्षी, माणसे सुखावतात. तुझी फळे खाऊन तृप्त होतात. पक्षी तुझ्या फांट्यांवर घरटी बांधतात. प्राणी तुझ्या अंगाखांदयांवर बागडतात.\nझाड : आपण तर सगळ्यांना देतच असतो नेहमी. मनुष्य कधी शिकणार आपल्याकडून देव जाणे?\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(59999,1667,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','चिमणी आणि माणूस या दोघांमधील संवादाची कल्पना करून संवादलेखन करा.','','','चिमणी : किती हे ऊन ! अरे मानवा, आमच्यासाठी आडोसा देखील नाही ठेवलास.\nमाणूस : अगं, चिमणीताई हे बघ तुझ्यासाठी पाण्याचे भांडे ठेवले आहे. पाणी पिऊन घे.\nचिमणी : पाणी तर पिते; पण सावली कुठे शोधू? तुम्ही सारी झाडे तोडली आणि आमची घरे उद्ध्वस्त झाली.\nमाणूस : होय चिमणीताई आमची चूक झाली हे खरं आहे. आम्ही आमची घरे बांधण्यासाठी झाडे तोडली आणि नवी झाडे लावली नाहीत; पण मी तुझ्यासाठी गच्चीवर एक घरटे ठेवले आहे. तू खुशाल तिकडे राहा.\nचिमणी : तू घरटे ठेवलेस त्याबद्दल धन्यावाद, पण झाडांवर घरटी बांधायला आम्हांला आवडते. झाडे नाहीत, त्यामुळे उन्हाचा त्रास होतो. पाऊस पडत नाही, त्यामुळे पाण्याची टंचाई होते. तुमच्या या निष्काळजीपणामुळे एक दिवस सारेच जीव धोक्यात येतील\nमाणूस : तुझे म्हणणे मला पटते. माणसाने आपल्याबरोबरच इतरांचा विचार केला पाहिजे. मी आता माझ्या घराजवळ नक्कीच झाडे । लावेन\nचिमणी : आणि या मोबाइल टॉवरचे काय? त्यातून निघणाऱ्या लहरींमुळे आमचा जीव घाबराघुबरा होऊन जातो.\nमाणूस : खरं आहे तुझं चिमणीताई, आम्ही माणसांनी तंत्रज्ञानाच्या नादात तुम्हा भावंडांकडे दुर्लक्ष केले. तुमच्यासाठी काहीतरी करायलाच हवे, कारण आपण सारे या धरतीमातेची लेकरे आहोत.\nचिमणी : आता खूप बरं वाटलं. साऱ्यांनी असा विचार केला, तर आपण नक्कीच गुण्यागोविंदानं राहू. चल आता मी जाते अन्न गोळा करायला.३. पणती आणि विजेचा दिवा या दोघांमधील संवादाची कल्पना करून संवादलेखन करा.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(60001,1667,'descriptive','5a',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','पणती आणि  विजेचा दिवा या दोघांमधील संवादाची कल्पना करून संवादलेखन करा.','','','पणती : काय रे दिव्या अशी फडफड का करतो आहेस?\nविजेचा दिवा : काही नाही गं पणतीबाई. बहुतेक वीज जाणार बघ. विजेचा दाब कमी-जास्त होतोय म्हणून मी घाबराघुबरा झालोय.\nपणती : अच्छा! तरीच मला पेटवले आहे मालकांनी तू बंद झाल्यावर खोलीत प्रकाश देण्याची जबाबदारी माझ्यावरच येते.\nविजेचा दिवा : होय तर. तू आहेस त्यामुळे आमच्या बंद होण्यानंतरही मालकांना प्रकाश मिळतो. स्वतः जळून दुसऱ्याला प्रकाश देण्याची तुझी सवय तुला महान बनवते.\nपणती : हो रे; पण आता आमचे दिवस गेले. आमची आठवण तू बंद झाल्यावर किवा दिवाळीच्या सणालाच येते.\nविजेचा दिवा : वाईट वाटून घेऊ नको बाई. काळ बदलला. नवे शोध लागले; पण अनेक शतके सूर्य अस्ताला गेल्यावर तुम्ही भगिनीच। लोकांची घरे प्रकाशाने उजळत होतात.\nपणती : ते खरं आहे. तुमच्या येण्याने आमच्यावरचा भार कमी झाला; पण कधी कधी मालकांना आमचा विसरच पडतो आणि आम्हांला अडगळीच्या खोलीत टाकून दिले जाते.\nविजेचा दिवा : पणतीबाई एक गोष्ट नक्की आहे; तुमची गरज माणसाला नसली तरी तुमचे महत्त्व कमी झालेले नाही. देवाजवळ, धार्मिक सण-समारंभात तुमचे स्थान अढळ आहे. कार्यक्रमाची सुरुवातच तुमच्या प्रज्वलनाने होते.\nपणती : होय रे बाबा. आपण समाजसेवेचे कार्य स्वीकारले आहे. लोकांसाठी जळत राहणे हेच आपले जीवन. अरे बापरे! वीज गेली बहुतेक, तू तर बंद झालास. माझे काम सुरू झाले.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(60003,1667,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','सायकल आणि माणूस या दोघांमधील संवादाची कल्पना करून संवादलेखन करा.','','','सायकल : अरे मित्रा, निघालास कुठे? माझ्याकडे बघ मी अडगळीत पडलेय कधीपासून, मला घेऊन चल बाहेर\nमाणूस : आता मी घाईत आहे तुला घेऊन जाण्याएवढा वेळ माझ्याकडे नाही. मी मोटारसायकल घेऊन जातो.\nसायकल : तुम्ही खूप आळशी झाला आहात. तुम्हांला सगळे आरामदायी हवे असते; पण एक गोष्ट तुम्ही विसरता. यामध्ये तुमच्या शरीराचे नुकसान होते.\nमाणूस : हो पण आमचा वेळ वाचतो. वेळ महत्त्वाचा नाही का?\nसायकल : वेळ महत्त्वाचा आहे हे खरं असलं तरीही मला नाकारून तुम्ही शरीरात चरबीचे प्रमाण वाढवता आणि मग पैसे देऊन व्यायामशाळेतील सायकल चालवता. केवढा हा विरोधाभास आणि हो प्रदूषणाचे काय?\nमाणूस : प्रदूषणाचे काय आता? वाहने तर चालतच असतात रस्त्यावर. त्याशिवाय लोक प्रवास कसा करतील?\nसायकल : अरे बाबा, वाहने चालू देत; पण जेथे शक्य…\n माणूस : बरोबर आहे तुझ म्हणणं मला पटल मी नक्कीच स्वतःला बदलेन यापुढे तुझा जास्तीत जास्त वापर करेन ज्यामुळे मी स्वत तदुरुस्त राहीन आणि पर्यावरणाचेही रक्षण होईल.\nसायकल :  आता कस बोललास. चल तर मग बाहेर जाऊन येऊ खूप दिवसांत मी बाहेर नाही गेले. जरा फेरफटका मारू\nमाणूस : चल जाऊया\n\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(60005,1667,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','पुस्तक आणि मोबाइल या दोघांमधील संवादाची कल्पना करून संवादलेखन करा.','','','मोबाइल: काय पुस्तकदादा, कंटाळा नाही का आला या कोपऱ्यात पडून? कधीपासून तिकडेच आहात कोणी हातदेखील लावत नाही.\nपुस्तक : होय रे भाऊ. आमचा काळ संपला असे वाटते. कोणालाही माझी गरज उरली नाही. जो तो हातात तुलाच घेऊन असतो.\nमोबाइल : हे खर आहे पुस्तकदादा एकेकाळी लोक तुम्हांला घेऊन प्रवास करत असत. प्रवासात तुमचे वाचन करताना त्याचे मनोरंजन होई. त्यांना ज्ञान मिळे. रात्री झोपेपर्यंत पुस्तक वाचणारी मंडळीदेखील कमी नव्हती.\nपुस्तक : आता मात्र परिस्थिती बदलली आहे. आमच्यामध्ये केवळ एखादी कथा किवा ठरावीक पात्रे. तेदेखील लिखित माहितीच्या स्वरूपात लोकांना वेगळेपण पाहिजे.\nमोबाइल : होय त्यासाठी मी आहे ना ! खरं तर आमचा जन्म केवळ एकमेकांशी संवाद साधण्याचे साधन म्हणून झाला; पण आज आमचे रूप \'स्मार्ट\' झाले आहे. आम्ही सारे जग आमच्यात सामावून घेतले आहे.\n\nपुस्तक : लोकांना सतत काही ना काही नवे हवे असते. तुमच्याकडे ते मिळते. कधी गेम, व्हिडिओ, चित्रपट, बातम्या अगदी पुस्तकेदेखील तुमच्यामध्ये वाचता येतात. मग माझ्यासारख्याकडे कोण कशाला लक्ष देईल?\nमोबाइल : नाराज नको होऊ रे पुस्तकदादा. प्रत्येकाचा काळ असतो. एक काळ तुझा होता. आजही तुझे रूप लोकांना आवडते. तुमच्यासाठी जीव टाकणारे \'पुस्तकवेडे\' आजही आहेत.\nपुस्तक बरोबर बोललास \'ठेविले अनंते तैसेची रहावे\', हेच खरं आहे.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(60007,1667,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','बैल आणि शेतकरी या दोघांमधील संवादाची कल्पना करून संवादलेखन करा.','','','बैल : काय रे शेतकरी दादा मी ऐकलं ते खरं आहे का?\nशेतकरी : काय ऐकल आहेस तू? आणि तू नाराज का आहेस?\nबैल : मी ऐकलं आहे तू मला विकणार आहेस आणि शेतीच्या कामासाठी ट्रॅक्टर घेणार आहेस.\nशेतकरी : नाही रे मित्रा तू जे ऐकलं आहेस ते अर्धसत्य आहे. मी शेतीच्या कामासाठी ट्रॅक्टर घेणार आहे हे सत्य आहे; पण तुला विकणार नाही. तू माझ्या कुटुंबाचा भाग आहेस आणि आज मी जे काही आहे त्यात तुझ्याही मेहनतीचा वाटा आहे\nबैल  : अरे मग ट्रॅक्टर कशाला? मी करेन ना काम. तुझी शेती फुललेली पाहतो तेव्हा मलाही खूप आनंद होतो. तुला उदास, काळजी करताना बघतो तेव्हा मलाही दुःख होते.\nशेतकरी : तू काम करशील, अगदी इमानदारीने करशील, मला माहीत आहे; पण जसा मी थकलो आहे, तसे तुझेही वय झालेच की तुलादेखील आराम नको का मिळायला? म्हणून ट्रॅक्टर. माझी मुले शेतीत काम करतात. ते ट्रॅक्टर चालवतील. आपण दोघे त्यांना मार्गदर्शन करू\n\nबैल : बैलपोळ्याला मला सजवले जाते ना, तेव्हा माझ्या मनात नेहमी एक गोष्ट मी ठरवतो. आपण कायम आपल्या मालकाला साथ ट्यायची नुसते बसून खाणे मला पटणारे नाही.\nशेतकरी : अरे ठीक आहे. आपण दोघे मिळून शेतीतील छोटी-मोठी कामे करू, मग तर झाले. वाईट नको वाटून घेऊस चल कामाला लागूया\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(60009,1667,'descriptive','5a',0,2,'Out of Text Book','','प्लॅस्टिकची पिशवी आणि माणूस या दोघांतील  संवादलेखन करा.','','','प्लॅस्टिकची पिशवी  : काय मानवा, प्लॅस्टिकबंदीनंतर तरी सुखी झालास ना ? कसं वाटतंय तुला ?\nमाणूस  : प्लॅस्टिकबंदीमुळे फारच अडचण झालीए गं आमची. दरवेळी तुझी गरज आम्हांला लागतेच. बाजारातून दूध, मांस-मच्छी आणताना, पावसात सामान भिजू नये म्हणून, डबा सांडू नये म्हणून तुझी आठवण येतेय गं.\nप्लॅस्टिकची पिशवी :  मी आतापर्यंत तुमच्या जीवनाचा अविभाज्य भाग झालेच आहे. म्हणूनच माझ्या वापरावर पूर्णपणे बंदी आणताना तुम्हांला असा त्रास सहन करावा लागतोय.\nमाणूस  : अगं, १९७० सालचा जन्म तुझा. तुझ्या जन्मानंतर लगेचच तू आमचं जीवन व्यापून टाकलंस. आमच्या रोजच्या जगण्यात तुझं स्थान इतकं पक्क झालं, की तुला बाजूला काढणं कठीणच होऊन गेलं.\nप्लॅस्टिकची पिशवी : हो, मला तुम्हीच जन्म दिला आणि तुम्हीच माझा अतिवापर केला. मी विघटनशील नाही. त्यामुळे, माझा कचरा पर्यावरणात साचून राहू लागला. प्रदूषण वाढलं. पर्यावरणाचा हास झाला.\nमाणूस  : हो गं. त्यात तुझा काही दोष नाही म्हणा. पर्यावरणाचा हास थांबवणं अत्यंत गरजेचं झालं आहे. त्यामुळे, तुझा वापर पूर्णपणे बंद करण्याचा निर्धार आम्ही केला आहे.\nप्लॅस्टिकची पिशवी :  हो, हे फार चांगलं केलंय. माझ्या  मृत्यूची मला भीती नाही. रोग नष्ट करण्यासाठी रोगाचं मूळच नष्ट केलं पाहिजे. पर्यावरण सांभाळा, लेकांनो. तरच पुढच्या पिढ्या सुखाने या पृथ्वीतलावर नांदू शकतील. जाते मी.\nमाणूस  : हो, पर्यावरण संवर्धन हाच आमचा मूलमंत्र असेल यापुढे. चल, आम्हांला इथपर्यंत साथ दिल्याबद्दल धन्यवाद.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(60012,1667,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','पोटोबा बद्दलची तक्रार \'मेंदूराजे कडे करणाऱ्या इंद्रियांचा तक्राररूपी संवाद लिहा.\n\n','','',' स्थळ : आपल शरीर, काही इंद्रिये मेंदूराजाकडे पोटोबांची तक्रार घेऊन आले आहेत.\nमेंदूराजे कोण आहे रे तिकडे, काय हा गोंधळ चालला आहे ?\nजिव्हाताई : नमस्कार मेंदूराजे. आमच्यामुळे तुम्हांला त्रास झाला.\nमेंदूराजे : नमस्ते, नमस्ते. वर यायचे काही खास कारण.\nजिव्हाताई : मेंदूराजे, आम्ही सर्वजण पोटोबांची तक्रार घेऊन आलो आहोत.\nमेंदूराजे : पोटोबांची तक्रार. काय केले पोटोबांनी ?\nहस्तराज : फारच खादाड झाले आहेत. हल्ली मला सारख भरवाक लागत त्यांना.\nजिव्हाताई : मलाही पोटोबाच्या खादाडीची चीड यायला लागलीय.\nनासिका : पोटोबा नेहमी चांगल्या पदार्थांच्या वासावरच असतात. किती वास घेत बसायच. वेगवेगळ्या वासांनी हैराण झाले मी.\nनयनकुमार : जेव्हा पहाव तेव्हा पोटोबांसाठी खादयच पहाव लागत. दुसर काही पहायला आवडतच नाही या पोटोबाला.\nपदकुमार : हो, ना, कित्ती पळवतात मला पोटोबा. स्वयंपाक घर, शेजारी, हॉटेल, रस्त्यावरचे फेरीवाले. अगदी कंटाळलो मी, पोटोबांना.\nमेंदूराजे : काय पोटोबा, हा काय उच्छाद मांडला आहे? का त्रास देता आपल्या भावंडांना ? किती दिवस चालल आहे ? किती दिवस चालणार?\nपोटोबा : महाराजांचा विजय असो. महाराज आपण न्यायी व हुशार आहात. मलाही काही सांगायचे आहे. माझीपण एक तक्रार आहे.\nमेंदूराजे : बोला पोटोबा बोला ! करा पोट मोकळे, मनमोकळे\nपोटोबा : महाराज, हे सगळे लबाड आहेत. चूक स्वतः करतात नाव माझे घेतात.\nमेंदूराजे : हे कसे काय ? पोटोबा.\nपोटोबा :  महाराज, ऐका! हे नयनकुमार चांगले चांगले पदार्थ बघतात. पदकुमार पदार्थांकडे घेऊन जातात, नयनकुमार डोळे भरून बघतात. नासिकाताईंनी वास घ्यायला सांगणेच नको. त्यांच काम सुरू असतंच. जिव्हाताईच्या तोंडाला पाणी सुटल की त्या हस्तकुमारांना सांगून तो पदार्थ खातात. मला कोणी विचारत नाही. माझ्या आवडी-निवडीचा प्रश्नच नाही. उलट हे जे काही मला न विचारता खातात. ते मला पचवाव लागत. महाराज, मलाच यांच्यामुळे त्रास होतो व कामही कराव लागत. महाराज, न्याय करा, न्याय दया महाराज.\nमेंदूराजे  : हो, हो पोटोबाचे म्हणणे खरे आहे. पटले आम्हांला. पोटोबा निरपराध आहेत. सर्वांनी त्यांचाही विचार घ्यावा.\nसर्वजण  : होय महाराज, आम्हांला माफ करा. चुकलो आम्ही आता पुन्हा नाही तक्रार करणार. पोटोबा आम्हांला माफ करा. आपण सारे भाऊ-भाऊ, मिळून राहू.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(60016,1667,'descriptive','5a',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','शब्दकोश, नेहा व सायली यांच्यामध्ये सुरू असलेला संवाद लिहा.\nशाळेच्या ग्रंथालयात शब्दकोशावरून नेहा, सायली व स्वतः शब्दकोश यांच्यामध्ये हा संवाद सुरू आहे.','','','नेहा  :काय गं सायली \'दीन\' या शब्दाचा अर्थ दिवस असाच आहे ना ?\nसायली  : \'दीन\' या शब्दाचा अर्थ \'गरीब\' असा आहे. \'दिन\' म्हणजे दिवस. तू गडबड करतेस\nनेहा : तुला कोणी सांगितला हा फरक. तू फार शहाणी आहेस.\nशब्दकोश: मी सांगितला नेहा तिला. सायली नेहमी माझी मदत घेते.\nनेहा  :  शब्दकोश दादा, तू कसा उपयोगी पडतो, मदत करतो बरं.\nसायली : अग नेहा, आपल्याला जेव्हा शब्दांचा अर्थ कळत नाही ना ? तेव्हा शब्दकोश दादा मदतीला येतो. त्याच्या मदतीचा उपयोग केव्हा व कसा घ्यायचा ते मी तुला सांगते.\nशब्दकोश : मीच सांगतो ऐका, आधी माझी माहिती घ्या, कुठला शब्द, कुठे मिळेल, कसा शोधावा हे जाणून घ्या. एकदम सोप आहे.\nनेहा  : सायली तू समजवना चांगल. तुला कळल आहे नां ?\nसायली  :  अक्षर समूहास \'शब्द\' म्हणतात. शब्द संग्रहाला \'शब्दकोश\' म्हणतात.\nनेहा :  थोड अधिक सविस्तर सांग ना?\nसायली : भाषेतील बहुतेक सर्व शब्दांचा संग्रह, विशिष्ट रचना, अर्थ, उपयोग सविस्तरपणे ज्यात दिलेला असतो त्याला शब्दकोश म्हणतात.\nशब्दकोश : माझा उपयोग फार महत्त्वाचा आहे व सोपाही आहे. विचार सायलीला ती सांगेल तुला अर्थ कसा शोधायचा ते. मी तुमचा मित्रच आहे.\n\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(60022,1673,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','History gives us a chronological, scientific and a ----------- account of the past events.\nA) random B) systematic C) detailed\n','','','B) systematic ','',0,0,0,NULL),(60023,1673,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Forts have an important place among the --------- sources.\nA) material B) oral C) written\n','','','A) material ','',0,0,0,NULL),(60024,1673,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Inscriptions carved on sheets of copper are called as -------------\nA) metal plates B) wooden plates C) copper plates\n','','','C) copper plates','',0,0,0,NULL),(60025,1673,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','----------- is the Sanskrit biography of Shivaji Maharaj composed by the poet Paramanand.\nA) Shrishivbharat B) Yugavatar C) Shivcharitra\n','','','A) Shrishivbharat','',0,0,0,NULL),(60026,1673,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','------------ is a type of chronicle that originated in Maharashtra.\nA) Tavarikh B) Bakhar C) Shakavali\n','','','B) Bakhar ','',0,0,0,NULL),(60027,1673,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Royal edicts, verdicts, etc. are inscribed on ------------------\nA) copper plates B) rock shelters C) palm leaves\n','','','A) copper plates','',0,0,0,NULL),(60028,1673,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','-------------- is a type of chronicle that originated in Maharashtra.\nA) Shakavali B) Bakhar C) Rajatarangini\n','','','B) Bakhar','',0,0,0,NULL),(60029,1673,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The quality of sources of history can be determined with the help of ---------- standards.\nA) external B) physical C) internal\n','','','C) internal','',0,0,0,NULL),(60030,1674,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In the first war at Tarai, --------- defeated Muhammad Ghuri.\nA) Chandbibi B) Maharana Pratap C) Prithviraj Chauhan\n','','','C) Prithviraj Chauhan','',0,0,0,NULL),(60031,1674,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','During the reign of ------------ of the Rashtrakuta dynasty in Maharashtra, the Rashtrakut power spread from Kanauj up to Rameshwar.\nA) Govind III B) Rajendra I C) Rana Jaswantsingh\n','','','A) Govind III','',0,0,0,NULL),(60033,1674,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The capital of Bhillam V of the Yadava dynasty was at --------- near Aurangabad.\nA) Mewad B) Deogiri C) Ahmadnagar\n','','','B) Deogiri ','',0,0,0,NULL),(60034,1674,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','-------------- was the last Sultan.\nA) Babur B) Iltutmish C) Ibrahim Lodi\n','','','C) Ibrahim Lodi','',0,0,0,NULL),(60035,1674,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Krishnadevraya wrote ......, a Telugu compendium on polity.\nA) \'Amuktamalyada\' B) \'Guru Granth Sahib\' C) \'Aadigrantha\'\n','','','A) \'Amuktamalyada\'','',0,0,0,NULL),(60036,1674,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In Maharashtra, ----------- was established under the leadership of Shivaji Maharaj.\nA) Swadharma B) Swaraj C) Swakul\n','','','B) Swaraj','',0,0,0,NULL),(60037,1674,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','------------- was the most powerful king of the Mughal Empire.\nA) Akbar B) Humayun C) Jahangir\n','','','A) Akbar','',0,0,0,NULL),(60038,1674,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Sultan Mahmud of ------------ invaded India many times.\nA) Kabul B) Lahore C) Ghazni\n','','','C) Ghazni','',0,0,0,NULL),(60039,1674,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','---------------- was the first king of Vijaynagar.\nA) Bukka B) Harihar C) Krishnadevraya\n','','','B) Harihar ','',0,0,0,NULL),(60040,1674,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','---------------- was the Governor of Punjab under the Sultanate.\nA) Daulatkhan Lodi B) Sher Khan C) Taimur\n','','','A) Daulatkhan Lodi','',0,0,0,NULL),(60041,1675,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','--------- and brahmadnyan were greatly emphasized in the Indian religious life.\nA) Rituals B) Mantras C) Songs\n','','','A) Rituals','',0,0,0,NULL),(60042,1675,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','---------- was a renowned Vaishnawa Sant in Gujarat.\nA) Guru Nanak B) Narsi Mehta C) Manmath Swami\n','','','B) Narsi Mehta','',0,0,0,NULL),(60043,1675,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','-------------- is a composition by Manmath Swami which is very well-known.\nA) \'Ramcharita-Manasa\' B) \'Vachana\' C) \'Paramarahasya\'\n','','','C) \'Paramarahasya\'','',0,0,0,NULL),(60044,1675,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The followers of Guru Nanak are known as ----------------\nA) Sikhs B) Muslims C) Hindus\n','','','A) Sikhs','',0,0,0,NULL),(60045,1675,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','---------- music has made valuable contribution to Indian music.\nA) Carnatic B) Sufi C) Classical\n','','','B) Sufi','',0,0,0,NULL),(60046,1675,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','----------- strengthened the Bhakti movement in North India.\nA) Sant Ramanand B) Sant Namdev C) Sant Dnyaneshwar\n','','','A) Sant Ramanand ','',0,0,0,NULL),(60047,1675,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Chaitanya Mahaprabhu underlined the importance of Krishnabhakti in ----------\nA) Gujarat B) Orissa C) Bengal\n','','','C) Bengal','',0,0,0,NULL),(60048,1675,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','------------- was the Guru of Chakradhar Swami.\nA) Sant Tukaram B) Shri Govind Prabhu C) Namdev\n','','','B) Shri Govind Prabhu','',0,0,0,NULL),(60049,1675,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','A conversation between a Hindu and a Muslim written by ---------- is important from the viewpoint of religious harmony.\nA) Sant Eknath B) Guru Ramdas C) Swami Samarth\n','','','A) Sant Eknath','',0,0,0,NULL),(60050,1676,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The --------- of Ahmadnagar and ------------ of Bijapur ruled most of the territory in Maharashtra at the beginning of the seventeenth century CE.\nA) Nizamshah, Adilshah B) Adilshah, Qutubshah C) Nizamshah, Qutubshah\n','','','A) Nizamshah, Adilshah ','',0,0,0,NULL),(60051,1676,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The different people from Europe were called ------------ because of their customary headgear.\nA) Turbaned B) Foreigners C) Topkar\n','','','C) Topkar\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(60052,1676,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The ------------- in Maharashtra endeavoured to inspire the masses.\nA) Warriors B) Sants C) Farmers\n','','','B) Sants','',0,0,0,NULL),(60053,1676,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Sants gave the message of -------------- to people.\nA) Rituals B) Equality C) Wealth\n','','','B) Equality','',0,0,0,NULL),(60054,1676,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','A great famine occurred in Maharashtra in -------------- CE.\nA) 1615 B) 1620 C) 1630\n','','','C) 1630','',0,0,0,NULL),(60055,1676,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The Sants and pilgrims used to rejoice in their devotion on the banks of river ---------- at Pandharpur.\nA) Chandrabhaga B) Krishna C) Godavari\n','','','A) Chandrabhaga','',0,0,0,NULL),(60056,1676,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','---------- propagated the message of Bhagwat religion in all quarters.\nA) Sant Eknath B) Sant Namdeo C) Sant Tukaram\n','','','B) Sant Namdeo','',0,0,0,NULL),(60057,1676,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Dnyaneshwari is also known as --------------\nA) Jnanashatak B) Varkari Grantha C) Bhawartha–Deepika\n','','','C) Bhawartha–Deepika','',0,0,0,NULL),(60058,1676,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','------------- gave lessons in good conduct and practical education through his works.\nA) Ramdas Swami B) Sant Kabir C) Guru Nanak\n','','','A) Ramdas Swami','',0,0,0,NULL),(60059,1677,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Shivaji Maharaj was born on ------------\nA) 20th Feb 1630 B) 19th Mar 1630 C) 19th Feb 1630\n','','','C) 19th Feb 1630','',0,0,0,NULL),(60060,1677,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Adilshah gave Siddi Jauhar the title ----------\nA) Rustum-e-Jaman B) Salabatkhan C) Afzalkhan\n','','','B) Salabatkhan','',0,0,0,NULL),(60061,1677,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','During the siege laid by Siddi Jauhar to Panhalgad, ------ a brave youth, came forward and sacrificed himself to let Shivaji Maharaj escape safely from the siege.\nA) Shiva Kashid B) Baji Prabhu Deshpande C) Bandal Deshmukh\n','','','A) Shiva Kashid','',0,0,0,NULL),(60062,1677,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The objective of Shivaji Maharaj of establishing Swaraj is clearly expressed in his -------\nA) Sword B) Royal seal/Rajmudra C) Fortress\n','','','B) Royal seal/Rajmudra','',0,0,0,NULL),(60063,1677,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','A meeting of Shivaji Maharaj and Afzalkhan took place at the foot of Pratapgad near ----------\nA) Wai B) Satara C) Mahabaleshwar\n','','','A) Wai','',0,0,0,NULL),(60064,1677,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','