) JVP   C) Standing   D) Kelkar\n','','','A) Khilafat','',0,0,0,NULL),(62468,1944,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The non-co-operation movement spread from the tea planters in ------- to rail workers in Bengal.\nA) Assam   B) Punjab   C) Kerala   D) Delhi\n','','','A) Assam','',0,0,0,NULL),(62470,1944,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Gandhiji was arrested in March 1922 for writing three anti-national (anti-British) articles in\nA) Young India   B) Darpan   C) Kesari   D) Mahratta\n','','','A) Young India','',0,0,0,NULL),(62472,1944,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In December 1929, the Lahore session of the Indian National Congress was presided by\nA) Dadabhai Naoroji   B) Annie Besant   C) Gopal Krishna Gokhale   D) Pandit Nehru\n','','','D) Pandit Nehru','',0,0,0,NULL),(62473,1944,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The resolution of Poorna Swaraj was taken in the -------- session of the Indian National Congress.\nA) Gorakhpur   B) Lucknow   C) Lahore   D) Amritsar\n','','','C) Lahore','',0,0,0,NULL),(62474,1952,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Text Book','','Parliamentary System of government developed in\na) England   b) France   c) United States of America   d) Nepal\n','','','a) England','',0,0,0,NULL),(62475,1952,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Text Book','','In the Presidential System, ---------- is the executive head.\na) Prime Minister   b) Lok Sabha Speaker   c) President   d) Governor\n','','','c) President','',0,0,0,NULL),(62476,1952,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The interrelationship between the Legislature, Executive and Judiciary is decided by the\na) Government   b) Presidential System   c) Constitution   d) Parliament\n','','','c) Constitution','',0,0,0,NULL),(62477,1952,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The English Constitution is an ---------- Constitution where governance is based on conventions.\na) changeable   b) unchangeable   c) unwritten   d) written\n','','','c) unwritten','',0,0,0,NULL),(62478,1952,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Sometimes, when no party gets a clear majority, ---------- government is formed.\na) Presidential   b) Coalition   c) Military   d) Communist\n','','','b) Coalition','',0,0,0,NULL),(62479,1952,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The Constitution of ---------- is an unwritten one.\nA) India   B) England   C) United States of America   D) France\n','','','B) England','',0,0,0,NULL),(62480,1952,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The Prime Minister and the Council of Ministers chosen by the Prime Minister together forms the ---------- in a parliamentary system of government.\nA) Judiciary   B) Parliament   C) Executive   D) Legislature\n','','','C) Executive','',0,0,0,NULL),(62481,1952,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The Legislature of the Central government in India is known as the\nA) Speaker   B) Rajya Sabha   C) Parliament   D) Constitution\n','','','C) Parliament','',0,0,0,NULL),(62485,1953,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Text Book','','Candidates to the Lok Sabha are elected through\na) Territorial constituencies  b) Religious constituencies  c) Local bodies  d) Proportional Representation System\n','','','a) Territorial constituencies','',0,0,0,NULL),(62486,1953,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Text Book','','The ----------- of India is the ex-officio chairman of the Rajya Sabha.\na) President  b) Vice-President  c) Prime Minister  d) Chief Justice\n','','','b) Vice-President','',0,0,0,NULL),(62487,1953,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','---------- is the upper House of the Parliament.\na) Legislative Assembly  b) Lok Sabha  c) Rajya Sabha  d) Legislative Council\n','','','c) Rajya Sabha','',0,0,0,NULL),(62488,1953,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The ----------- of India has created the Parliament of India.\na) Legislature  b) Executive  c) Constitution  d) British Law\n','','','c) Constitution','',0,0,0,NULL),(62489,1953,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','1/3rd members of total membership of Rajya Sabha, who have completed their tenure of six years, retire after every ----------- years.\na) Two  b) Four  c) Five  d) Six\n','','','a) Two','',0,0,0,NULL),(62490,1953,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','If ---------- feels that the Parliament should make a law of the subject in the state list, it can pass a resolution to that effect.\na) Lok Sabha  b) Rajya Sabha  c) Executive  d) President\n','','','b) Rajya Sabha','',0,0,0,NULL),(62491,1953,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Every year in the month of February, ---------- presents the national budget to the Lok Sabha.\na) Prime Minister  b) President  c) Finance Minister  d) Speaker\n','','','c) Finance Minister','',0,0,0,NULL),(62492,1953,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The President appoints ----------- distinguished personalities to the Rajya Sabha.\na) Two  b) Eight  c) Fifteen  d) Twelve\n','','','d) Twelve','',0,0,0,NULL),(62493,1953,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','---------- does not participate in the discussions of either house of the Parliament.\na) Prime Minister  b) Council of Ministers  c) President  d) Members of Parliament\n','','','c) President','',0,0,0,NULL),(62495,1953,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','As per the Constitution there can be a maximum of --------- members in the Lok Sabha.\na) 550  b) 552  c) 252  d) 250\n','','','b) 552','',0,0,0,NULL),(62496,1953,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The members of the ----------- are indirectly elected.\na) Lok Sabha  b) First House  c) House of Representatives  d) Rajya Sabha\n','','','d) Rajya Sabha','',0,0,0,NULL),(62497,1953,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','----------- is elected in the very first meeting of the newly elected Lok Sabha.\na) Prime Minister  b) Speaker  c) President  d) Vice President\n','','','b) Speaker','',0,0,0,NULL),(62498,1954,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Text Book','','In India, the executive power is vested in the\na) President   b) Prime Minister   c) Speaker\n','','','a) President','',0,0,0,NULL),(62499,1954,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Text Book','','The tenure of the President is of ----------- years.\na) Three   b) Four   c) Five\n','','','c) Five','',0,0,0,NULL),(62500,1954,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Text Book','','The Council of Ministers is led by the -----------\na) Party Chief   b) Prime Minister   c) President\n','','','b) Prime Minister','',0,0,0,NULL),(62501,1954,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The --------- bears the responsibility of protecting the Constitution and ensuring that the government runs as per the Constitution.\na) Speaker   b) President   c) Vice-President\n','','','b) President','',0,0,0,NULL),(62502,1954,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The President can be removed if the impeachment resolution is passed by --------- majority in both the Houses of Parliament.\na) 1/3rd   b) 2/3rd   c) 3/4th\n','','','b) 2/3rd','',0,0,0,NULL),(62503,1954,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The ----------- is the Commander-in-Chief of the armed forces.\na) Prime Minister   b) Vice-President   c) President   d) Brigadier\n','','','c) President','',0,0,0,NULL),(62504,1954,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In case a minister is not the member of the Parliament, he/she has to get elected to the Parliament within ---------- months.\na) Three   b) Six   c) Nine   d) Two\n','','','b) Six','',0,0,0,NULL),(62505,1954,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','As per the amendment, the number of ministers in the council should not be more than .......% of the total number of members in Lok Sabha.\na) 10   b) 20   c) 15   d) 25\n','','','c) 15','',0,0,0,NULL),(62507,1954,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The Council of Ministers stays in power till it enjoys the support of majority in ---------\na) Legislative Assembly   b) Legislative Council   c) Rajya Sabha   d) Lok Sabha\n','','','d) Lok Sabha','',0,0,0,NULL),(62508,1954,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In the absence of the President, ---------- carries out his functions.\na) Vice-President   b) Prime Minister   c) Speaker of Lok Sabha   d) Chief Election Commissioner\n','','','a) Vice-President','',0,0,0,NULL),(62509,1954,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The Union government means the ------------ government.\na) Central   b) State   c) Regional\n','','','a) Central','',0,0,0,NULL),(62510,1954,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In a Parliamentary system of government the Executive is part of the -----------\na) Judiciary   b) Legislature   c) Finance\n','','','b) Legislature','',0,0,0,NULL),(62760,1938,'descriptive','2b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the chart : ','','','','',1,0,1,NULL),(62761,1938,'descriptive','2b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the chart : ','','','','',1,0,1,NULL),(62762,1938,'descriptive','2b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the chart : ','','','i) Material sources	ii) Oral sources		iii) Written sources','',1,0,0,NULL),(62763,1938,'descriptive','2b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the chart ','','','i. Audio sources	ii. Video sources	iii. Audio-visual sources','',1,0,0,NULL),(62764,1938,'descriptive','2b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the chart : ','','','i. Various bridges	ii. roads			iii. water supply systems\niv. government offices	v. residences of officers, leaders and revolutionaries\nvi. palaces of rulers of Princely States\nvii. forts		viii. prisons\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(62765,1938,'descriptive','2b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the chart ','','','i. Correspondence	ii. Foreign Accounts	iii. Newspapers\niv. Biographies		v. Periodicals		vi. Factory Records\nvii. Autobiographies	viii. Books\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(62766,1938,'descriptive','2b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the chart :','','','i. Inspirational songs		ii. Folk songs		iii. Powada\niv. Folk Tales			v. Narrations		vi. Interviews\nvii. Fairs, Jalsa, Art groups	viii. Rhythmic Prose (Owis)\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(62767,1939,'descriptive','2b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the chart : ','','','','',1,0,1,NULL),(62768,1939,'descriptive','2b',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the chart :  ','','','','',1,0,1,NULL),(62769,1939,