-\nA) 35⁰C  B) 36⁰C  C) 37⁰C  D) 38⁰C','','','C) 37⁰C','',0,0,0,NULL),(65531,138,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Earth’s heat is also called as ------\nA) Nuclear energy  B) Solar energy  C) Geothermal energy  D) Tidal energy','','','C) Geothermal energy','',0,0,0,NULL),(65532,138,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','If the average kinetic energy of atoms in two objects is equal then their ----- will also be equal.\nA) Heat  B) Mass  C) Temperature  D) Volume','','','C) Temperature','',0,0,0,NULL),(65533,138,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Heat always flows from a hotter object to ------.\nA) Warmer object  B) Colder object  C) Any direction  D) Object with more mass','','','B) Colder object\n\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(65534,138,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','The ---- of an object is the amount of heat required to increase the temperature of unit mass of that substance through one degree.\nA) Density  B) Specific heat  C) Thermal conductivity  D) Latent heat','','','B) Specific heat\n\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(65535,138,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','A thermometer is used to measure ------\nA) Pressure  B) Volume  C) Heat  D) Temperature','','','D) Temperature\n\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(65536,138,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','The apparatus to measure heat is the -----\nA) Voltmeter  B) Barometer  C) Calorimeter  D) Thermometer','','','C) Calorimeter\n\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(65537,138,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Temperature is the measure of the ---- kinetic energy of the atoms in a substance.\nA) Total  B) Average  C) Maximum  D) Minimum','','','B) Average\n\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(65538,138,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','The heat contained in a substance is the measure of the ----- kinetic energy of atoms in the substance.\nA) Average  B) Partial  C) Total  D) Specific','','','C) Total\n\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(65539,138,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Temperature of boiling water cannot be measured by a -----\nA) Digital thermometer  B) Lab