 ------\nA) cells B) atoms C) matter D) air','','','C) matter','',0,0,0,NULL),(66093,321,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','----- and ----- are two important properties of matter.\nA) length and width B) shape and color C) mass and volume D) taste and odor','','',' C) mass and volume','',0,0,0,NULL),(66094,321,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Matter made of only one constituent is called -----\nA) substance B) element C) mixture D) solution','','','A) substance','',0,0,0,NULL),(66095,321,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','A substance whose molecules are made of exactly alike atoms is called -----\nA) compound B) solution C) element D) alloy','','','C) element','',0,0,0,NULL),(66096,321,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Scientists have discovered ---- elements; of these, ---- elements occur in nature.\nA) 118, 92 B) 120, 90 C) 112, 89 D) 110, 100','','',' A) 118, 92','',0,0,0,NULL),(66097,321,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Brass, steel, twenty-two carat gold are a few examples of ------\nA) compounds B) elements C) mixtures D) alloys','','',' D) alloys','',0,0,0,NULL),(66098,321,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','------ is also used for purification of impure liquids.\nA) Sedimentation B) Filtration C) Distillation D) Decantation','','','C) Distillation','',0,0,0,NULL),(66099,322,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Salt dissolves in water. Hence, salt is -------- in water.\na) soluble         b) insoluble         c) immiscible       d) miscible','','','a) soluble \n','',0,0,0,NULL),(66100,322,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Ice, water and steam are three states of -----------\na) hydrogen          b) oxygen           c) water         d) vapour','','','c) water   \n','',0,0,0,NULL),(66101,322,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','The type of matter with fixed shape, size and mass is -------\na) solid            b) liquid             c) gas           d) all of these','','','a) solid      \n','',0,0,0,NULL),(66102,322,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out