तापमानावर अधातू स्थायू किंवा वायू अवस्थेत असतात. (अपवाद – ब्रोमिन द्रव)</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>६) सामान्यत: धातूंची घनता उच्च असते. उदा., सोने, चांदी, पारा</td>\n    <td>६) सर्वसाधारणपणे अधातूंची घनता कमी असते. उदा., ऑक्सिजन, हायड्रोजन</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>','',0,0,0,NULL),(81420,2191,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','मिश्रणे आणि संयुगे :','','','<table border=\"1\" style=\"width:100%; border-collapse: collapse\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n  <tr>\n    <th>मिश्रण</th>\n    <th>संयुगे</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>१) दोन किंवा अधिक पदार्थ कोणत्याही प्रमाणात मिसळले असता मिश्रण तयार होते.</td>\n    <td>१) दोन किंवा अधिक मूलद्रव्यांच्या वजनी प्रमाणात रासायनिक अभिक्रिया घडून संयुग तयार होते.</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>२) मिश्रणातील घटक साध्या भौतिक पद्धतीने वेगळे करता येतात.</td>\n    <td>२) संयुगातील घटक मूलद्रव्ये साध्या भौतिक पद्धतीने वेगळी करता येत नाहीत.</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>३) मिश्रणातील मूळ घटक पदार्थांचे गुणधर्म कायम राहतात. उदा., हवा, स्टील.</td>\n    <td>३) संयुगाचे गुणधर्म हे त्यातील घटक मूलद्रव्यांच्या गुणधर्मांपेक्षा पूर्णपणे वेगळे असतात. उदा., मीठ, साखर, पाणी.</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>','',0,0,0,NULL),(81422,2191,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','फरक स्पष्ट करा : अणू आणि रेणू ','','','<table border=\"1\" style=\"width:100%; border-collapse: collapse\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n  <tr>\n    <th>अणू</th>\n    <th>रेणू</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>१) मूलद्रव्याचा सर्वांत लहान कण ज्यात मूलद्रव्याचे सर्व गुणधर्म असतात, त्याला अणू असे म्हणतात.</td>\n    <td>१) रेणू हा दोन किंवा अधिक अणूंपासून बनतो. त्याला स्वतःचे गुणधर्म असतात.</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>२) अणूचे विभाजन सहज शक्य नसते. त्याचे विभाजन केल्यास मूलद्रव्याचे गुणधर्म नाहीसे होतात.</td>\n    <td>२) रेणू हा त्याच्या दोन किंवा अधिक अणूंपासून विभाजित करता येतो. उदा., पाण्याच्या रेणूपासून हायड्रोजन आणि ऑक्सिजनचे अणू तयार होतात.</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>३) अणू एकत्र आल्यास रेणू बनतो.</td>\n    <td>३) रेणू एकत्र आल्यास उत्पादन तयार होते.</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>','',0,0,0,NULL),(81424,2191,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','फरक स्पष्ट करा : विलगीकरण व ऊर्ध्वपातन ','','','<table border=\"1\" style=\"width:100%; border-collapse: collapse\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n  <tr>\n    <th>विलगीकरण</th>\n    <th>ऊध्र्वपातन</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>१) एकमेकांत न विरघळणाऱ्या दोन द्रवांचे मिश्रण एकमेकांपासून वेगळे करण्यासाठी विलगीकरण पद्धती वापरतात.</td>\n    <td>१) द्रावणातून द्राव्य आणि द्रावक वेगळे करण्यासाठी ऊध्र्वपातन पद्धती वापरली जाते.</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>२) या पद्धतीत उष्णता द्यावी लागत नाही.</td>\n    <td>२) या पद्धतीत उष्णता द्यावी लागते.</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>','',0,0,0,NULL),(81425,2191,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','साखर हा पदार्थ किती मूलद्रव्यांपासून बनला आहे ? ','','','साखर हा पदार्थ कार्बन, हायड्रोजन आणि ऑक्सिजन या मूलद्रव्यांपासून बनला आहे.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81427,2191,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','कार्बन डायऑक्साइड या नावावरून हा पदार्थ किती व कोणत्या मूलद्रव्यांपासून बनल्याचे लक्षात येते ? ','','','कार्बन डायऑक्साइडमध्ये कार्बन व ऑक्सिजन ही मूलद्रव्ये आहेत. कार्बनचा एक अणू आणि ऑक्सिजनचे दोन अणू यांनी कार्बन डायऑक्साइडचा रेणू बनला आहे.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81429,2191,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','पाणी, ऑक्सिजन, कार्बन डायऑक्साइड यांपैकी मूलद्रव्य व संयुग कोणते आहे ?','','','पाणी आणि कार्बन डायऑक्साइड ही संयुगे आहेत, तर ऑक्सिजन हे मूलद्रव्य आहे.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81431,2191,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','संयुगाच्या लहानांत लहान कणाला काय म्हणतात ? ','','','संयुगाच्या लहानांत लहान कणाला रेणू असे म्हणतात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81434,2191,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','विजेच्या बल्बमधील टंगस्टनची संज्ञा काय आहे ? ती कशावरून पडली ?','','','विजेच्या बल्बमधील टंगस्टनची संज्ञा W आहे. वुल्फ्रॅम (Wolfram) या त्याच्या जर्मन नावावरून ती घेतली आहे.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81436,2191,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','रेणुसूत्रे कशी लिहितात?','','','संयुग कोणत्या मूलद्रव्यांपासून बनलेले आहे आणि त्या मूलद्रव्यांचे अणू किती आहेत, यानुसार रेणुसूत्रे लिहितात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81438,2191,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','मूलद्रव्यांचे वर्गीकरण कसे करतात?','','','मूलद्रव्यांचे वर्गीकरण धातू आणि अधातू या दोन गटांत करतात.\n\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(81440,2191,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','ऑक्सिजनचा रेणू कसा तयार होतो?','','','ऑक्सिजनचे दोन अणू जोडले जाऊन ऑक्सिजनचा स्वतंत्र अस्तित्व असलेला रेणू तयार होतो.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81441,2191,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','मूलद्रव्यांच्या संज्ञा कशा तयार करतात ?','','','प्रत्येक मूलद्रव्याची स्वतंत्र संज्ञा असते. संज्ञा दाखवण्यासाठी मूलद्रव्याच्या इंग्रजी नावाच्या स्पेलिंग्जमधील पहिले अक्षर वापरतात. जसे Hydrogen साठी H, Nitrogen साठी N. जेव्हा दोन किंवा अधिक मूलद्रव्यांच्या नावांतील पहिले अक्षर सारखे असेल, तेव्हा संज्ञा लिहिण्यासाठी अक्षरांची जोडी वापरतात. जसे, C ही संज्ञा कार्बन (Carbon) दर्शवते, Cl ही संज्ञा क्लोरीन (Chlorine) व Ca ही संज्ञा कॅल्शिअम (Calcium) दर्शवते. यामध्ये पहिले अक्षर कपिटल (मोठ्या लिपीत) व दुसरे अक्षर दुसय्या (लहान) लिपीत लिहितात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81444,2191,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','मिश्रणातील विविध घटक साध्या पद्धतीने कसे वेगळे केले जातात ?\nगाळणे, चाळणे, वेचणे, निवडणे, पाखडणे, चुंबक फिरवणे तसेच संप्लवन या पद्धतींचा वापर केल्याने कोणकोणत्या मिश्रणातील कोणकोणते घटकपदार्थ वेगळे होतात?','','','मिश्रणातील घटक वेगळे करण्यासाठी निरनिराळ्या पद्धती आहेत. त्यांतील काही रोजच्या दैनंदिन जीवनांतल्या आहेत. उदा., निवडणे, वेचणे, पाखडणे, गाळणे, चाळणे, चुंबक फिरवणे इत्यादी.\n(1) गाळणे : द्रवातील अविद्राव्य पदार्थ वेगळे काढण्यासाठी गाळणे ही पद्धत उपयोगी आहे. (2) चाळणे : मिश्रणातून कमी-अधिक आकाराचे पदार्थ वेगळे करण्यासाठी चाळणे उपयोगी आहे. (3) वेचणे आणि निवडणे : या पद्धतीत मिश्रणातील नको/हवे असलेले पदार्थ उचलून बाहेर काढले जातात. (4) पाखडणे : वजनाने हलके आणि मिश्रणातून काढून टाकायचे पदार्थ पाखडून वेगळे करता येतात. शेतात धान्य स्वच्छ करण्याच्या कामात ही पद्धत प्रामुख्याने वापरतात. (5) चुंबक फिरवणे : मिश्रणात जर लोखंडी वस्तूची भेसळ झाली असेल तर चुंबक फिरवून ते कण वेगळे करता येतात. उदा., रव्यातील लोखंडी चुरा चुंबकाने वेगळा करता येतो. (6) संप्लवन करून घन पदार्थ थेट वायू रूपात अवस्थांतरित करता येतो. उदा., कापूर जर काही पदार्थांत मिसळला गेला असेल, तर तो संप्लवन करून निराळा करता येईल.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81447,2191,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','कोणती मूलद्रव्ये धातू, अधातू व धातुसदृश आहेत? ','','','अधातू : हायड्रोजन, कार्बन, नायट्रोजन, फॉस्फरस, ऑक्सिजन, सल्फर सर्व हॅलोजन्स आणि नोबल वायू.\nधातुसदृश : बोरॉन, सिलिकॉन, जर्मेनिअम, अर्सेनिक, ऑन्टिमनी, टेलेरीअम, पोलोनिअम, सेलेनिअम आणि अस्टाटाईन.\nधातू : लोह, तांबे, सोडिअम, पोटॅशिअम, अल्युमिनिअम, सोने, चांदी इत्यादी.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81450,2191,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','दैनंदिन व्यवहारात अपकेंद्री पद्धतीचा वापर कोठे व कशासाठी होतो ? (HOTS)','','','थेट अपकेंद्री पद्धतीचा वापर दैनंदिन व्यवहारात केला जात नाही. त्यासाठी आवश्यक असलेले उपकरण घरात नसते. अपकेंद्री पद्धतीचा वापर करून ठरावीक आकाराचे कण वेगळे केले जातात. या तत्त्वावर आधारित पद्धत म्हणजे ताक करणे. परंतु ताक करताना अपकेंद्री उपकरण वापरले जात नाही. रवीचा वापर केला जातो. रवीने ताकातील लोण्याचे कण एकत्र केले जातात. यात लोण्याचे कण केंद्र अपसारी बलाने वेगळे करून बाजूला जमा होतात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81452,2191,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','ऊर्ध्वपातन व विलगीकरण पद्धतींचा उपयोग कोठे होतो? का ?','','','<b>I. ऊर्ध्वपातन</b> : अशुद्ध द्रवपदार्थ शुद्ध करण्यासाठी ऊर्ध्वपातन पद्धती वापरली जाते. तसेच द्रावणामधून द्रावक आणि द्राव्य यांना वेगळे करण्यासाठी देखील ऊर्ध्वपातन करतात. या पद्धतीने समुद्राच्या पाण्यापासून पिण्यायोग्य पाणी तयार केले जाते.\n<b>II. विलगीकरण </b>: एकमेकांत न विरघळणान्या दोन द्रवांचे मिश्रण एकमेकांपासून वेगळे करण्यासाठी विलगीकरण पद्धती वापरतात. या पद्धतीने निरनिराळी रासायनिक द्रावणे वेगळी केली जातात. उदा., केरोसीन व पाणी यांचे मिश्रण विलग करता येईल.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81453,2191,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','ऊर्ध्वपातन व विलगीकरण पद्धत वापरताना तुम्ही कोणती काळजी घ्याल ?','','','ऊर्ध्वपातन पद्धतीत सर्व उपकरणे व्यवस्थित मांडली पाहिजेत. संघननी नलिका योग्य रितीने थंड राहिली पाहिजे. चंबूला उष्णता देताना ठरावीक तापमानाचे नियंत्रण केले पाहिजे.\nविलगीकरण पद्धतीमध्ये तोटी व्यवस्थित बंद ठेवली पाहिजे. बन्याच वेळा ही तोटी सैल झाल्यामुळे त्यातून द्रव खाली गळू लागतात. तसेच वेगळे झालेले द्रव तोटीतून बाहेर काढताना अतिशय काटेकोरपणे तोटी उघड-बंद करता आली पाहिजे.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81454,2191,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','रवा, मीठ व लोहकीस यांच्या एकत्र मिश्रणातील प्रत्येक घटक वेगळा कसा कराल?','','','प्रथम लोहकीस वेगळा करण्यासाठी त्यातून चुंबक फिरवण्यात येईल. रवा आणि मीठ या मिश्रणापैकी रवा पाण्यात अविद्राव्य आहे. मात्र मीठ पाण्यात विरघळते. त्यामुळे लोहकीस काढल्यावर उरलेले मिश्रण पाण्यात विरघळवले जाईल. हे मिश्रण गाळण्याने गाळून घेतले जाईल. गाळण्यावर रवा राहील आणि विरधळलेल्या मिठाचे पाणी गाळण्यातून खाली पडेल. हे मीठ-पाणी नंतर बाष्पीभवन किंवा उर्ध्वपातन करून त्यातून मीठ वेगळे केले जाईल.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81455,2191,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','पुढील पदार्थांचे गुणधर्मांनुसार वर्गीकरण करा : (पाठ्यपुस्तक पान क्र. 92)\n(पाणी, थर्मोकोल, माती, लोखंड, कोळसा, कागद, रबर, तांबे, ताग, प्लास्टिक.)\n','','','(1) पाणी : नैसर्गिक द्रव पदार्थ.\n(2) थर्मोकोल, रबर, प्लास्टिक, कागद : मानवनिर्मित संश्लेषित घन पदार्थ.\n(3) माती, ताग : नैसर्गिक घन पदार्थ.\n(4) कोळसा : अधातू.\n(5) लोखंड व तांबे : धातू.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81462,2191,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','सुबक व नामनिर्देशित आकृतीसह पुढील प्रश्नाचे उत्तर लिहा :\nसमुद्राच्या अशुद्ध पाणयापासून शुद्ध पाणी कसे मिळवतात?','','','समुद्राच्या अशुद्ध पाण्यापासून शुद्ध पाणी ऊर्ध्वपातन पद्धतीने मिळवतात. एका गोल चंबूमध्ये समुद्राचे अशुद्ध पाणी घ्या. चंबूला दोन छिद्रे असलेले बूच लावा. एका छिद्रातून तापमापी, तर दुसन्या छिद्रातून काचेची वाकडी नळी बसवा. रबरी नळी घेऊन तिचे एक टोक काचेच्या नळीला, तर दुसरे टोक संघननीच्या नळीला जोडा. संघननीच्या दुसन्या टोकाला पुन्हा रबरी नळी जोडा आणि ती चंचुपात्रात सोडा. आकृतीनुसार प्रयोगाची मांडणी करा. गोल चंबू लोखंडी जाळीवर ठेवून उष्णता देणे सुरू करा. थोड्या वेळात गोल चंबूतील समुद्राच्या पाण्याची 100^∘ सेला वाफ होते. ही वाफ संघननीतून जाताना भोवतालच्या पाण्याने थंड होऊन द्रवरूपात चंचुपात्रात येते. अशा प्रकारे चंचुपात्रात पडणारे थेंब हे गोल चंबूतील समुद्राच्या पाण्याचे असतात. चंबूतील सगळ्या पाण्याची वाफ झाल्यावर चंचुपात्रात ऊर्ध्वपातित शुद्ध पाणी, तर चंबूत मीठ शिल्लक राहते.','',0,0,1,NULL),(81464,2191,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','लोणी काढणयासाठी ताक घुसळले जाते.','','','घुसळणे ही एक पदार्थ वेगळे करण्याची पद्धत आहे. ताकात लोण्याचे कण विखुरलेले असतात. घुसळण केल्याने केंद्र अपसारी बलाने ते एकत्र येऊन त्याचा एकच गोळा बनतो. लोणी ताकापासून वेगळे करण्यासाठी ताक घुसळले जाते.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81466,2191,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','शास्त्रीय कारणे लिहा : लोणी काढणयासाठी ताक घुसळले जाते.\n','','घुसळणे ही एक पदार्थ वेगळे करण्याची पद्धत आहे. ताकात लोण्याचे कण विखुरलेले असतात. घुसळण केल्याने केंद्र अपसारी बलाने ते एकत्र येऊन त्याचा एकच गोळा बनतो. लोणी ताकापासून वेगळे करण्यासाठी ताक घुसळले जाते.','','',0,0,0,NULL),(81468,2191,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','शास्त्रीय कारणे लिहा : रंजकद्रव्य पृथक्करण पद्धतीत पाणी कागदाच्या टोकापर्यत चढते, तेव्हा मिश्रणातील घटकपदार्थ कमी उंचीपर्यतच चढलेले असतात. ','','','पदार्थाची वर चढणाऱ्या  द्रावकातील विद्राव्यता आणि स्थिर असलेल्या गाळण कागदाला चिकटून राहायाची त्याची क्षमता या दोन गुणधर्माचा वापर रंजकद्रव्य पृथक्करण पद्धतीत केला जातो. पाणी हे द्रावक असल्याने ते जलद वेगाने वर चढते. प्राण्यातील मिश्रणाचे घटकपदार्थ तितक्या वेगाने वर चढणार नाहीत कारण ते गाळण कागदाला चिकटून राहतीले, पाणी मात्र तसे करणार नाही, म्हणून रंजकद्रव्य पृथक्करण पद्धतीत पाणी कागदाच्या टोकापर्यत चढते, तेन्ह्रा मिश्रणातील घटकपदार्थ कमी उंचीपर्यतच चढलेले असतात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81469,2191,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','शास्त्रीय कारणे लिहा : उन्हाळ्यात पाणी साठवण्याच्या भांड्याला बाहेरून ओले कापड गुंडाळले जाते.','','','पाणी साठवण्याच्या भांड्याला बाहेरून गुंडाळलेल्या ओल्या कापडातले पाणी उष्णतेने बाष्पात रूपांतरित होते. या बाष्पीभवनाच्या वेळी ते भांड्यातील उष्णता खेचून घेते. त्यामुळे भांड्यातील पाणी गार राहते. म्हणून उन्हाळ्यात पाणी साठवण्याच्या भांड्याला बाहेरून ओले कापड गुंडाळले जाते.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81470,2191,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','आपण सभोवताली तसेच दैनंदिन जीवनामध्ये अनेक वस्तू पाहतो, आपण त्यांना स्पर्श करतो, त्यांचे गुणधर्म अभ्यासतो. या सर्व वस्तूंची निर्मिती एकाच प्रकारच्या द्रव्यापासून झालेली असते की एकापेक्षा अधिक द्रव्यांपासून ? ','','','निरनिराळ्या वस्तूंची निर्मिती अनेक प्रकारच्या द्रव्यांपासून झालेली असते. काहींमध्ये एकाच प्रकारचे द्रव्य असते. काहींमध्ये अनेक द्रव्ये असतात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81472,2191,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','पाणी, सरबत, लोखंड, पोलाद, कोळसा, हवा, मीठ, तांबे, पितळ, माती यांमधील मिश्रणे कोणती?','','','सरबत, पोलाद, हवा, पितळ आणि माती ही मिश्रणे आहेत.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81473,2191,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','हवेमध्ये असणारी मूलद्रव्ये कोणती?','','','ऑक्सिजन, नायट्रोजन, हायड्रोजन, अर्गोन, क्रिप्टॉन, झेनॉन इत्यादी मूलद्रव्ये हवेमध्ये आहेत.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81475,2191,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','कार्बन डायऑक्साइड हे मूलद्रव्य आहे का ? ','','','नाही. कार्बन डायऑक्साइड हे संयुग आहे. कार्बनचा एक आणि ऑक्सिजनचे दोन रेणू यांनी कार्बन डायऑक्साइडचा रेणू तयार होतो.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81476,2191,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','मूलद्रव्यास त्यांचे गुणधर्म कशामुळे प्राप्त होतात ? ','','','मूलद्रव्ये अणूंनी बनलेली असतात. त्याच्या अणूंच्या रचनेनुसार मूलद्रव्यास त्यांचे गुणधर्म प्राप्त होतात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81480,2191,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','विविध मूलद्रव्यांचे अणू एकसारखे असतात की वेगवेगळे? ','','','विविध मूलद्रव्यांचे अणू वेगवेगळे असतात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81481,2191,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','ढगातून पडणारे पाणी निसर्गतः शुद्ध असते का?','','','ढगातून पडणारे पाणी निसर्गतःच शुद्ध असते. परंतु ते जसजसे पृथ्वीवर पोहोचते तसे त्यात विषारी वायू विरघळून ते अशुद्ध होऊ शकते.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81482,2191,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','ऊर्ध्वपातनाने शुद्ध केलेल्या पाणयाचा उपयोग कोठे करतात ? ','','','ऊर्ध्वपातनाने शुद्ध केलेले पाणी रासायनिक प्रयोगात वापरले जाते. तसेच मोटरगाड्यांच्या बॅटरीमध्ये वापरतात. काही देशांत समुद्राच्या पाण्याचे ऊर्ध्वपातन करून त्यापासून पिण्याचे पाणी बनवले जाते.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81483,2191,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','ऊर्ध्वपातन पद्धतीत द्रवाचे कोणकोणते गुणधर्म दिसून येतात? ','','','द्रव ठरावीक तापमानाला उत्कलन दाखवतो. तसेच त्याचे संघनन देखील होते.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81484,2191,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','आपण दैनंदिन वापरात कोणकोणती मूलद्रव्ये (धातू व अधातू), संयुगे, मिश्रणे वापरतो?','','','मूलद्रव्ये-धातू : लोह, सोने, चांदी, तांबे. अधातू : कार्बन, ऑक्सिजन, हायड्रोजन, नायट्रोजन.\nसंयुगे : साखर, मीठ, तेल. मिश्रणे : साबण, संमिश्र (स्टील, पोलाद, दागिन्यातील सोने).','',0,0,0,NULL),(81485,2191,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','दैनंदिन जीवनात वापरली जाणारी मिश्रणे कोणती आहेत?','','','चहा, कॉफी, फालुदा, भेळ, स्वयंपाकगृहात तयार केलेली भाजी, आमटी यांसारखे पदार्थ. निरनिराळ्या धातूचे मिश्रण असलेले संमिश्र जसे स्टेनलेस स्टील, पितळ, पोलाद, सोन्याचे दागिने हे देखील दैनदिन जीवनात वापरली जाणारी मिश्रणे आहेत.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81486,2191,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','सर्वच मिश्रणे आपल्याला उपयुक्त असतात का? ','','','काही मिश्रणे हानिकारक देखील असतात. उदा., अन्नभेसळ करताना अन्नात इतर विषारी अपायकारक पदार्थ घातले जातात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81488,2192,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','आज आपण दात स्वच्छ करण्यासाठी कशाचा वापर करतो ?','','','आता आपण दात स्वच्छ करण्यासाठी टूथपेस्ट आणि दंतमंजन वापरतो.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81489,2192,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','दात स्वच्छ करण्यासाठी पूर्वी कोणकोणत्या पदार्थांचा वापर केला जात असे ?','','','दात स्वच्छ करण्यासाठी पूर्वी बाभळीची साल, कडुनिंबाची काडी, कोळशाची पूड, राख, मंजन, मीठ, डाळिंबाची साल असे अनेक पर्याय वापरले जात असत.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81490,2192,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','टूथपेस्ट व टूथपावडरमधील फ्लोराइड कोठून मिळते ?','','','पाण्याच्या सर्व स्रोतांत फ्लोराइड असते. मॅग्नेशिअम फ्लोराइडच्या स्वरूपात टूथपेस्ट व टूथपावडरमध्ये फ्लोराइड घातले जाते. ते दातांच्या आवरणात शोषले जाते.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81491,2192,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','बांधकामासाठी वापरले जाणारे पदार्थ कोणते ?','','','रेती, चुना, सिमेंट, माती, विटा असे निरनिराळे पदार्थ बांधकामासाठी वापरले जातात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81494,2192,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Text Book','','पदार्थाच्या पृष्ठभागावरील मळ काढून टाकण्यासाठी पाण्याला साहाय्य करणाऱ्या पदार्थास _______ म्हणतात।\na) साबण                     b) अपमार्जक                 c) पोर्टलंड\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(81495,2192,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Text Book','','_______ रोखण्यासाठी टूथपेस्टमध्ये फ्लोराइड वापरले जाते।\na) हाडांची झीज                 b) दंतक्षय              c) तेलाम्ल\n','','','b) दंतक्षय','',0,0,0,NULL),(81497,2192,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Text Book','','साबण हा _______ व सोडिअम हायड्रॉक्साइडचा क्षार आहे।\na) तेलाम्ल                 b) मृदू                c) कठीण\n','','','a) तेलाम्ल','',0,0,0,NULL),(81498,2192,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Text Book','','संश्लिष्ट अपमार्जके ही _______ पाण्यातही वापरता येतात।\na) कठीण                   b) मृदू                  c) पोर्टलंड\n','','','a) कठीण','',0,0,0,NULL),(81500,2192,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Text Book','','बांधकामासाठी प्रामुख्याने _______ सिमेंट वापरला जातो।\na) पांढरे सिमेंट                b) पोर्टलंड                c) साबण\n','','','b) पोर्टलंड','',0,0,0,NULL),(81503,2192,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','पुढील विधाने चूक की बरोबर ते लिहा :\nफार पूर्वी हाडे, शिंपले यांचा चुरा मिसळून टूथपेस्ट तयार करीत असत.','','','बरोबर','',0,0,0,NULL),(81505,2192,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','पुढील विधाने चूक की बरोबर ते लिहा :\nअपमार्जकाचे रेणू तोकडे असतात.','','','चूक. (अपमार्जकाचे रेणू जास्त लांबीचे असतात.)','',0,0,0,NULL),(81506,2192,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','पुढील विधाने चूक की बरोबर ते लिहा :\nपृष्ठसक्रियतेचा एक परिणाम म्हणजे फेस न येणे.','','','चूक. (पृष्ठसक्रियतेचा एक परिणाम म्हणजे फेस येणे.) ','',0,0,0,NULL),(81507,2192,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','पुढील विधाने चूक की बरोबर ते लिहा :\nसुमारे 2000 वर्षापूर्वी प्राण्यांची चरबी आणि लाकडाची राख वापरून साबण तयार केला जात होता.','','','बरोबर','',0,0,0,NULL),(81508,2192,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','पुढील विधाने चूक की बरोबर ते लिहा :\n1756 मध्ये रोमन लोकांनी जलीय सिमेंट बनवण्याची पद्धत शोधून काढली.','','','चूक. (1756 मध्ये ब्रिटिश अभियंते जॉन स्मीटन यांनी जलीय सिमेंट बनवण्याची पद्धत शोधून काढली.)','',0,0,0,NULL),(81513,2192,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','आमच्यातील सारखेपणा व फरक काय आहे?\nनैसर्गिक अपमार्जके व मानवनिर्मित अपमार्जक :','','','सारखेणणा : दोन्ही स्वच्छतेसाठी वापरतात.\n<table border=\"1\" style=\"width:100%; border-collapse: collapse\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n  <tr>\n    <th>नैसर्गिक अपमार्जक</th>\n    <th>मानवनिर्मित अपमार्जके</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>१) नैसर्गिक अपमार्जके हे निसर्गात आढळणारे पदार्थ असतात।</td>\n    <td>१) मानवनिर्मित अपमार्जके हे मानवाने बनवलेले पदार्थ आहेत।</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>२) या अपमार्जकांमध्ये सॅपोनिन हा नैसर्गिक रासायनिक पदार्थ असतो।</td>\n    <td>२) या अपमार्जकांमध्ये सुगंधी द्रव्ये, रंगद्रव्ये, जंतुनाशके, अल्कोहोल, फेननाशक, कोरडेपणा टाळणारे पदार्थ, रेती इत्यादी पूरक घटक घातले जातात।</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>३) नैसर्गिक अपमार्जकांचा कपड्यांवर अनिष्ट परिणाम होत नाही।</td>\n    <td>३) विविध रसायनांमुळे मानवनिर्मित अपमार्जके कपड्यांची हानी करू शकतात।</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>४) यांनी जलाशयांचे प्रदूषण होत नाही. उदा., रिठा आणि शिकेकाई।</td>\n    <td>४) यांनी जलाशयांचे प्रदूषण होते. उदा., निरनिराळी संश्लिष्ट अपमार्जके।</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>','',0,0,0,NULL),(81517,2192,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','आमच्यातील सारखेपणा व फरक काय आहे? \nसाबण व संश्लिष्ट अपमार्जक','','','<table border=\"1\" style=\"width:100%; border-collapse: collapse\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n  <tr>\n    <th>साबण</th>\n    <th>संश्लिष्ट अपमार्जक</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>१) साबण बनवताना सोडिअम हायड्रॉक्साइड किंवा पोटॅशिअम हायड्रॉक्साइड, खोबरेल तेल, मीठ इत्यादी घटक वापरले जातात।</td>\n    <td>१) संश्लिष्ट अपमार्जके बनवताना स्निध पदार्थ किंवा केरोसीन वापरले जाते।</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>२) कठीण पाण्यात साबणाला फेस येत नाही।</td>\n    <td>२) कठीण पाण्यातही संश्लिष्ट अपमार्जकाला फेस येऊ शकतो।</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>३) कपड्याच्या स्वच्छतेसाठी साबणाचा परिणाम खूप प्रभावशाली नसतो।</td>\n    <td>३) कपड्याच्या स्वच्छतेसाठी अपमार्जकाचा परिणाम खूप प्रभावशाली असतो।</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>४) साबणाचा त्वचेवर वाईट परिणाम होत नाही।</td>\n    <td>४) संश्लिष्ट अपमार्जकाचा त्वचेवर वाईट परिणाम होतो।</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>','',0,0,0,NULL),(81518,2192,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','आमच्यातील सारखेपणा व फरक काय आहे? \nअंगाचा साबण व कपडे धुण्याचा साबण :','','','सारखेपणा : दोन्हीत तेलाम्ले असतात व दोन्ही स्वच्छतेसाठी वापरतात.\n<table border=\"1\" style=\"width:100%; border-collapse: collapse\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n  <tr>\n    <th>अंगाचा साबण</th>\n    <th>कपडे धुण्याचा साबण</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>१) अंगाचा साबण वैयक्तिक स्वच्छतेसाठी वापरला जातो।</td>\n    <td>१) कपडे धुण्याचा साबण कपड्यांच्या स्वच्छतेसाठी वापरला जातो।</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>२) हा मृदू साबण असतो।</td>\n    <td>२) हा कठीण साबण असतो।</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>३) हा तेलाम्लांचा पोटॅशिअम क्षार असतो।</td>\n    <td>३) हा तेलाम्लांचा सोडिअम क्षार असतो।</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>','',0,0,0,NULL),(81519,2192,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','आमच्यातील सारखेपणा व फरक काय आहे?\nआधुनिक सिमेंट व प्राचीन सिमेंट ','','','सारखेणणा : दोन्ही बांधकामासाठी वापरतात.\n<table border=\"1\" style=\"width:100%; border-collapse: collapse\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n  <tr>\n    <th>आधुनिक सिमेंट</th>\n    <th>प्राचीन सिमेंट</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>आधुनिक सिमेंट हे सिलिका (वाळू), अल्युमिना (ऑल्युमिनिअम ऑक्साइड), चुना, आयर्न ऑक्साइड व मॅग्नेशिया (मॅग्नेशिअम ऑक्साइड) यांच्यापासून तयार करतात।</td>\n    <td>भिजवलेल्या चुन्यात ज्वालामुखीची राख घालून प्राचीन काळात जलीय सिमेंट बनवले जात असे।</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>','',0,0,0,NULL),(81556,2192,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','उंची वस्त्रांसाठी वापरली जाणारी अपमार्जके कशी असावीत?','','','रिठा आणि शिकेकाईसारखी निसर्गनिर्मित अपमार्जके उंची वस्त्रांसाठी वापरावीत. कारण या अपमार्जकांचा रेशमी व लोकरी धाग्यांवर आणि कपड्यांवर अनिष्ट परिणाम होत नाही.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81557,2192,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','पाणी कठीण आहे का, हे तुम्ही साबण चुन्याच्या साहाय्याने कसे तपासाल?','','','कठीण पाण्यात साबणाला फेस येत नाही. कारण त्यात जे क्षार विरघळलेले असतात, त्यामुळे साबणाची प्रक्रिया होऊ शकत नाही. म्हणून साबण चुरा वापरून पाणी कठीण आहे का हे समजते.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81558,2192,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','टूथपेस्टचे महत्त्वाचे घटक कोणते व त्यांचे कार्य काय?','','','टूधपेस्टचे महत्त्वाचे घटक कॅल्शिअम कार्बोनेट, कॅल्शिअम हायड्रोजन फॉस्फेट हे आहेत. यांच्यामुळे दातांवरील घाण साफ होते. शिवाय हे घटक दातांना पॉलिश करण्याचे काम करतात. टूर्थपेस्टमध्ये असणाऱ्या ठरावीक प्रमाणातील फ्लोराइडमुळे दंतक्षय रोखला जातो. फ्लोराइडमुळे दातांवरील आवरण बळकट होते.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81559,2192,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','अपमार्जक वापरल्याने मळकट कपडे कसे स्वच्छ होतात? (HOTS)','','','कपड्यावरचा मळ, तेलाचे डाग इत्यादी कछण्यासाठी अपमर्जके वापरली जातात. याचे रेणू जास्त लांबीचे असून त्याच्या दोन्ही टोकांचे गुणधर्म भिन्न असतंत.  ^\"हा \"  अपमार्जक रेणू त्याच्या एका टोकाशी पाण्याचा रेणू आणि दुसय्या टोकाशी तेलाचा रेणू पकडून ठेवतो. त्यामुळे तेलाचे रेणू पाण्यात मिसळतात व तेल आणि मळ बाहेर पडून कपडे स्वच्छ होतात. 、','',0,0,0,NULL),(81560,2192,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','पृष्ठसक्रियता म्हणजे काय? विविध अपमार्जकांच्या पृष्ठसक्रियतेला कारणीभूत ठरणान्या तीन रसायनांची नावे लिहा.','','','पृष्ठभागावर सहजरीत्या पसरण्याच्या गुणधर्माला पृष्ठसक्रियता म्हणतात. अपमार्जके पृष्ठसक्रिय असल्यामुळे त्यांना फेस येतो.,पेट्रोलियम, मेद, सल्फर ट्रायऑक्साइड, अल्कोहोल अशा पदार्थांमुले विविध अपमार्जकांत पृष्ठसक्रियता येते.,','',0,0,0,NULL),(81561,2192,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','सिमेंटमधील घटक कोणते ?','','','साध्या सिमेंटमध्ये सिलिका (वाळू), ऑल्युमिना (ऑल्युमिनिअम ऑक्साइड), चुना, आयर्न ऑक्साइड ब मॅग्नेशिया (मॅग्नेशिअम ऑक्साइड) यांचे मिश्रण असते, तर पोर्टलंड सिमेंटमध्ये 60% चूना (कॅल्शिअम ऑक्साईड), 125% सिलिका (सिलिकॉन डायऑक्साइड), 5% ऑल्युमिना व उरलेला भाग आयनॅ ऑक्साइड व मनेशिया ने बनलेला असतो.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81563,2192,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','काँक्रीट बनवताना सिमेंट वापरले नाही तर काय होईल ?','','','काँक्रीटमध्ये सिमेंट, पाणी, वाळू व खडी मिसळली जाते. हे घटक मिसळले नाहीत तर इमारतीची स्लैब भक्कम होणार नाही. पाण्याची गळती होईल. सिमेंटमुले गळती रोखली जाते. बांधकामाच्या सुरक्षिततेसाठी काँक्रीट बनवताना सिमेंट वापरले जाते. जर सिमेंट वापरले नाही, तर इमारत कोसळून जाईल.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81564,2192,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','अलीकडच्या काळात रस्ते काँकीटचे का तयार करतात? (HOTS)','','','रस्त्यावर मोठया प्रमाणात जड वाहनांची रहदारी असते. त्यामुळे रस्ते भक्कम असणे आवश्यक आहे. म्हणून जलद दळणवळण साधण्यासाठी अलीकडच्या काळात काँक्रीटचे रस्ते तयार करतात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81565,2192,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','पाण्याला कठीणपणा कशामुळे येतो? (HOTS) ','','','पाण्यात जर कॅल्शिअमचे आणि मॅग्नेशिअमचे बायकार्बोनेटस्, क्लोराइडस् आणि सल्फेटस् विरघळलेले असतील, तर पाण्याला कठीणपणा येतो.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81566,2192,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','कारणे लिहा :  कठीण पाणयात साबणाचा उपयोग होत नाही.','','','कठीण पाण्यात निरनिराले क्षार असतात. त्यामुळे साबणाचा फेस न होता साका तयार होतो. या साक्यामुळे अपमार्जन करण्याचा साबणाचा गुणधर्म नष्ट होतो. म्हणून कठीण पाण्यात साबणाचा उपयोग होत नाही.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81567,2192,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','कारणे लिहा :  तेल पाणयात मिसकत नाही; परंतु पुरेसा अपमार्जक वापरला की, तेल व पाणी एकजीव होते.','','','दोन्ही टोकांचे गुणधर्म भिन्न असणान्या अपमार्जकाचे रेणू जास्त लांबीचे असतात. हे रेणू त्यांच्या एका टोकाशी पाण्याचा रेणू आणि दुसन्या टोकाशी तेलाचा रेणू पकडून ठेवतात) त्यामुळे तेलाचे रेणू पाण्यात मिसळतात. एरव्ही तेल आणि पाणी मिसळत नाहीत परंतु अपमार्जक वापरला, की ते अशा रितीने एकजीव होतात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81569,2192,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','कारणे लिहा :  संश्लिष्ट अपमार्जके ही साबणापेक्षा सरस आहेत.','','',':(संश्लिष्ट अपमार्जके कठीण पाण्यात वापरता येतात. या अपमार्जकांची निर्मिती वापराच्या गरजेनुसार वेगवेगळ्या पद्धती अवलंबून करतात) त्यांच्यामध्ये सुगंधी द्रव्ये, रंगद्रव्ये, जंतुनाशके, अल्कोहोल, फेननाशक, कोरडेपणा टाळणारे पदार्थ, रेती इत्यादी पूरक घटक मिसळले जातात. त्यामुळे संश्लिष्ट अपमार्जकांना उपयुक्त गुणधर्म मिळतात आणि ती साबणापेक्षा सरस ठरतात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81573,2192,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','कारणे लिहा :  बऱ्याच वेळा कपडे धुताना कपड्यांवर रंगीत डाग निर्माण होतात.','','','साबणातील अशुद्धी कधी कधी कपङ्यांवर उतरू शकते. हळदीसारखे डाग कपड्यांवर पडले असतील, तर ते साबणाच्या रासायनिक क्रियेने लाल होतात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81574,2192,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','दात स्वच्छ करणयासाठी तंबाखूची मशेरी वापरू नये.','','','(तंबाखू हा आरोग्याला हानिकारक पदार्थ आहे. त्याच्या वापरण्याने अनेक प्रकारचे कॅन्सर होऊ शकतात. मशेरीत तंबाखू असल्यास या तंबाखूचा परिणाम दात आणि हिरड्या यांच्यावर होतीै. म्हणून दात स्वच्छ करण्यासाठी तंबाखूची मशेरी वापरू नये.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81577,2192,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','नैसर्गिक व मानवनिर्मित पदार्थ म्हणजे काय ? ','','','निसर्गातून उपलब्ध होणारे पदार्थ म्हणजे नैसर्गिक पदार्थ होत. उपलब्ध पदार्थांवर विविध रासायनिक प्रक्रिया करून मानवाने तयार केलेले पदार्थ म्हणजे मानवनिर्मित पदार्थ होत.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81691,2484,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In the contour line method the height of the land is measured from the --------\na) mountain peak b) sea level c) river bed\n','','','b) sea level','',0,0,0,NULL),(81692,2484,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The contour line method is useful to understand the -------- of the land and the -------- of different places.\na) slope, height b) length, depth c) area, width\n','','','a) slope, height','',0,0,0,NULL),(81693,2484,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In the -------- method, the spaces between the contour lines are filled with colour.\na) layer tinting b) contour shading c) hill diagram\n','','','a) layer tinting ','',0,0,0,NULL),(81694,2484,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Generally -------- are coloured blue in the layer tinting method.\na) mountains b) water bodies c) plateaus\n','','','b) water bodies','',0,0,0,NULL),(81695,2484,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In the digital elevation method the information obtained through man-made -------- is presented with the help of computers.\na) satellites b) balloons c) towers\n','','','a) satellites','',0,0,0,NULL),(81696,2484,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Previously, relief was shown on a map using the -------- technique.\na) block diagram b) hill shading c) contour marking\n','','','b) hill shading','',0,0,0,NULL),(81697,2484,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The most modern method of drawing maps is -----\n(A) Digital elevation model (B) Hill shading (C) Layer tinting (D) Contour line\n','','','A) Digital elevation model','',0,0,0,NULL),(81698,2484,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Layer tinting method of drawing maps gives information of the ----- of a region.\n(A) height (B) relief (C) slope (D) all of these\n','','','B) relief','',0,0,0,NULL),(81699,2484,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The land adjoining water bodies is generally coloured ----- in the layer tinting method.\n(A) blue (B) yellow (C) dark green (D) black\n','','','C) dark green','',0,0,0,NULL),(81700,2484,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Contour lines on a map are drawn to show -----\n(A) temperature (B) height (C) rainfall (D) population\n','','','B) height','',0,0,0,NULL),(81701,2484,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The method in which shades are used to show slopes is called -----\n(A) Contour line (B) Hill shading (C) Digital elevation model (D) Layer tinting\n','','','B) Hill shading','',0,0,0,NULL),(81702,2484,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The contour interval means the ----- between two contour lines.\n(A) vertical distance (B) horizontal distance (C) diagonal distance (D) slope angle\n','','','A) vertical distance','',0,0,0,NULL),(81703,2484,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following is not a traditional method of map drawing?\n(A) Contour line (B) Hill shading (C) Digital elevation model (D) Layer tinting\n','','','C) Digital elevation model','',0,0,0,NULL),(81704,2484,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In contour maps, close spacing of contour lines indicates -----\n(A) gentle slope (B) steep slope (C) flat surface (D) plain region\n','','','B) steep slope','',0,0,0,NULL),(81705,2484,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Underline the correct word. : Less distance between two adjacent contour lines means steep/ gentle slope.','','','Less distance between two adjacent contour lines means <u>steep</u> slope.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81706,2484,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Underline the correct word. : Conventional signs/ symbols are miniature drawings of objects shown on a map as per convention.','','','Conventional <u>symbols</u> are miniature drawings of objects shown on a map as per convention.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81707,2484,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give some examples of different landforms.','','','Mountains, valleys, plateaus, plains and islands are some examples of different landforms.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81708,2484,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is a contour line?','','','The line joining the places of equal height on a map is called a contour line.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81709,2484,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','How do we determine the form of slope from the contour line method?','','','In the contour line method, if the distance between the contour lines is less the slope of the landform is steep, whereas if the distance is more the slope is gentle.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81710,2484,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What indicates different heights in the layer tinting method?','','','In the layer tinting method, different colours indicate the different heights.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81711,2484,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is used to indicate the signs and symbols given in the map?','','','A key shown besides the map is used to indicate the signs and symbols given in the map.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81712,2484,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','In the following sentences, underline the words that represent landforms and prepare signs or symbols for them.\n(i) Sonali lives just beyond Mount Takmak.\n(ii) Nilesh has gone on a trip to Gharapuri Island.\n','','','The words that represent landforms are underlined in the sentences as given below.\n(i) Sonali lives just beyond <u>Mount</u> Takmak.\nHere the word \'Mount\' represents the landform mountain. It can be represented by the symbol △\n(ii) Nilesh has gone on a trip to Gharapuri <u>Island.</u>\nHere the word \'Island\' represents a landform. It can be represented by the symbol ------\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(81713,2484,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','Prepare signs and symbols for the following components:\nHouse, hospital, factory, park, playground, road, hill, river.\n','','','The signs and symbols for the given components are given in the table below.','',0,0,1,NULL),(81714,2484,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','The given map shows height through the use of colours. However, one colour representation is wrong. Write which colour would be correct in its place.','','','In the given map, the <u>blue colour is incorrectly used</u> to show height of low lying areas. This is because, blue colour is generally used for representing water bodies. The low areas should have been represented by <u>dark green colour.</u>','',1,0,0,NULL),(81715,2484,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Why were maps used in the times of war?','','','Maps were used in the times of war, so as to have a detailed knowledge of the terrain used for fighting the battle. Maps were also useful in working out strategies of defeating the enemy.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81716,2484,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Explain the process of preparing maps using the contour line method. \n                       OR \nWrite short notes on contour line method.','','','i) The contour line method is used to show the unevenness of land on a map.\n(ii) In this method, the height of the land is measured from sea-level.\n(iii) The points of same heights are identified and their positions are accurately marked on the map.\n(iv) The locations with same height are then joined with a line, known as contour line.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(81717,2484,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write about the layer tinting method.','','','i) The layer tinting method is based on the contour line method.\n(ii) Here the spaces between the contour lines are filled with different colours.\n(iii) Each colour indicates a specific height.\n(iv) Thus, if the water bodies are shown in blue colour, the land adjoining it can be shown by dark green colour. Land higher than that can be shown by light green, next higher by yellow and so on.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(81718,2484,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Explain the digital elevation model.','','','i) The digital elevation model is the most modern method used to prepare maps.\n(ii) In this method information about the various landforms is obtained through manmade satellites.\n(iii) This information is then presented using computers.\n(iv) The differences in the height of the landforms can be easily observed in maps prepared using this method. Also the height of each point can be found from these maps using computers.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(81719,2484,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','How are the physical maps useful to us?','','','i) The physical maps help us to understand the physical set-up of a region.\n(ii) They give us an idea of the region\'s height, relief and slope.\n(iii) We can also find the height of each point from the maps made with the use of computers.\n(iv) Physical maps can be used in military operations, tourism, drawing up mountaineering routes, in making regional development plans, etc.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(81720,2484,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Why are standard signs and symbols necessary in a map?','','','i) If the several components shown on a map are represented in different form in different maps, it will be difficult for people to understand them.\n(ii) To avoid this confusion, standard signs and symbols are used to make maps.\n(iii) These signs and symbols are universally accepted and hence are easy for everyone to understand.\nHence, standard signs and symbols are necessary in a map.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(81721,2484,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write in short about the Survey of India.','','','i) The Survey of India is the foremost mapmaking institute in India, established in 1767.\n(ii) Its headquarters are located in Dehradun in Uttarakhand.\n(iii) This institute makes large number of topographic maps of the Indian subcontinent on various scales by conducting field surveys.\n(iv) Its maps are known worldwide for their accuracy.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(81722,2484,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','In map A, how has the height of the land been shown?','','','In map A, each continuous line (contour line) shows the height in metres indicated by the number written besides that line. The tallest peak is shown with the help of small triangle indicating 500 m height.','',1,0,0,NULL),(81723,2484,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Why have colours been used in map B ?','','','In map B, the colours filled between two adjacent lines represent the change of height between these two lines. The part with green colour represents height less than 200 m , the part with yellow colour represents height ranging from 200 to 300 m , and so on.','',1,0,0,NULL),(81724,2484,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','How is map C different from the other two maps?','','','In map C, the change in height can be seen by visual observation without the help of lines. This map is an image taken from a man-made satellite and presented using computer.','',1,0,0,NULL),(81725,2484,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','Answer the following questions :\ni) In which direction is the highest point in maps A, B and C ?\nii) In which map can the landforms be seen most clearly?\n','','','i) In maps A, B and C the highest point is in the lower half towards the right side. Thus the highest point is towards the south-east direction in all the maps.\nii) The landforms can be seen clearly in map C due to its computerized representation.\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(81726,2484,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','different heights are shown in the box given. Find and join the dots that show places of the same height. What method of showing the landforms on a map have you used here? Write the answer.','','','The Contour Line method of showing the landforms has been used in this map.','',1,0,1,NULL),(81727,2484,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','Identify the signs and symbols given table and write their names.','','','','',1,0,1,NULL),(81728,2484,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','Jasbir and Manjeet are reading a map. They do not understand the following signs and symbols.\ni) Will you help them by writing the meanings of each sign and symbol?\nii) Sign or symbol? Write in the brackets.\n','','','','',1,0,1,NULL),(81729,2484,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the method by which maps are made using information obtained through manmade satellites.','','','Digital elevation model','',0,0,0,NULL),(81730,2484,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which objects are generally represented by conventional symbols in maps?','','','Objects such as temples, mosques, forts, etc., are generally represented by conventional symbols in maps.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81731,2484,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','What are conventional signs?','','','Conventional signs are signs used to show various things on a map as per convention in the form of letter or geometrical shapes.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81732,2484,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which is the foremost mapmaking institute of India?','','','The \'Survey of India\' is the foremost mapmaking institute of India.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81733,2484,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Right or Wrong? If Wrong, write the correct sentence. : It is difficult to show the length and width of a landform on a piece of paper.','','','Wrong\nIt is easy to show the length and width of a landform on a piece of paper.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81734,2484,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Right or Wrong? If Wrong, write the correct sentence. : We can find height of each point on a digital map using computers.','','','Right','',0,0,0,NULL),(81735,2484,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Right or Wrong? If Wrong, write the correct sentence. : Conventional signs are miniature drawings of the object represented by it.','','','Wrong\nConventional symbols are miniature drawings of the object represented by it.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(81736,2484,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Right or Wrong? If Wrong, write the correct sentence. :  The digital elevation model is the method which is based on the contour line method and uses colours to represent height.','','','Wrong\nThe layer tinting method is based on the contour line method and uses colours to represent height.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(81737,2484,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is the main purpose of using the contour line method?','','','The contour line method is mainly used to show the unevenness of landforms on a map.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81738,2484,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','How is information obtained and presented in the digital elevation model?','','','In the digital elevation model, the information is obtained through man-made satellites and is presented with the help of computers.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81739,2484,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','What difficulties are faced while showing different landforms on a map? List the different methods used for the showing the different landforms?','','','The length and width of a landform can be shown easily on a piece of paper or a map. However it is difficult to show its depth and height. To overcome this issue and to show correct representation of the landforms the following three methods are used.\n(a) Contour line method\n(b) Layer tinting method\n(c) Digital elevation model\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(81740,2484,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','How is the relief of the land shown in the contour line method?','','','a) In the contour line method, the places of same height are located on map.\n(b) These places are then joined with contour line.\n(c) The distance between two contour lines helps us to understand the relief of the land.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(81901,1907,'descriptive','1a',6,2,'Out of Text Book','','येथे चित्रांचा वापर करून एक गोष्ट दिलेली आहे. येथे काही ठिकाणी शब्दांऐवजी चित्रे दिलेली आहेत. चित्रांऐवजी शब्द वापरून गोष्ट वाचा.','','','(जंगलात, सिंह, जंगलाचा, जंगलात, सिंह, जंगलात, प्राणी व पक्षी, सिंह, बेडकांचा, बेडकाने, सिंहाला, सिंहाला, सिंहाने, बेडूक, सिंहाने, सिंह, बेडकाच्या, बेडूक, सिंहाने.)','',1,0,0,NULL),(81902,1907,'descriptive','1a',6,2,'Out of Text Book','एका ------ एक ------- राहायचा. त्याला त्या --------- कंटाळा आला आणि तो नव्या ------- राहायला गेला. एकदा -------- मोठ्याने गरजला. त्या --------- अनेक -------- तसेच काही बेडूकही राहत होते. त्यांनी यापूर्वी --------- पाहिला नव्हता. ------- पुढारी म्हणाला, \"कोणीतरी मोठा आवाज काढत आहे. आता मीही मोठा आवाज काढतो.\" -------- मोठा आवाज काढला. ------- हा आवाज नवीन होता. ----------- वाटले, \'कोणीतरी आपल्याला आव्हान देत आहे, आपण सावध राहिले पाहिजे.\' ------- आपली गर्जना थांबवली. तो शांत उभा राहिला. --------- मोठमोठ्याने ओरडत पुढे-पुढे सरकू लागला. --------- त्याला पाहिले व त्याचा आवाज ऐकला. --------- वेगाने पुढे सरकला. ------ डोक्यावर पाय दिला. --------- गयावया करू लागला. -------- त्याला सोडून दिले.','पुढील चौकटीतील गोष्टीत गाळलेल्या जागी कंसातील योग्य शब्द भरून गोष्ट तयार करा व वाचा :\n(Complete the story by filling the blanks using the words given below. Read the story again :) (जंगलात, सिंह, जंगलाचा, जंगलात, सिंह, जंगलात, प्राणी व पक्षी, सिंह, बेडकांचा, बेडकाने, सिंहाला, सिंहाला, सिंहाने, बेडूक, सिंहाने, सिंह, बेडकाच्या, बेडूक, सिंहाने.)\n','','','एका <u>जंगलात</u> एक <u> सिंह</u> राहायचा. त्याला त्या <u> जंगलाचा</u> कंटाळा आला आणि तो नव्या <u> जंगलात</u> राहायला गेला. एकदा <u>सिंह</u> मोठ्याने गरजला. त्या <u> जंगलात</u> अनेक <u> प्राणी व पक्षी</u> तसेच काही बेडूकही राहत होते. त्यांनी यापूर्वी <u>सिंह</u> पाहिला नव्हता. <u> बेडकांचा</u> पुढारी म्हणाला, \"कोणीतरी मोठा आवाज काढत आहे. आता मीही मोठा आवाज काढतो.\" <u> बेडकाने</u> मोठा आवाज काढला. <u>सिंहाला</u> हा आवाज नवीन होता. <u>सिंहाला</u> वाटले, \'कोणीतरी आपल्याला आव्हान देत आहे, आपण सावध राहिले पाहिजे.\' <u>सिंहाने</u> आपली गर्जना थांबवली. तो शांत उभा राहिला. <u>बेडूक</u> मोठमोठ्याने ओरडत पुढे-पुढे सरकू लागला. <u>सिंहाने</u> त्याला पाहिले व त्याचा आवाज ऐकला. <u>सिंह</u> वेगाने पुढे सरकला. <u>बेडकाच्या</u> डोक्यावर पाय दिला. <u>बेडूक</u> गयावया करू लागला. <u> सिंहाने</u>  त्याला सोडून दिले.','',0,0,0,NULL),(81903,1907,'descriptive','1a',6,2,'Out of Text Book','एका जंगलात एक  सिंह राहायचा. त्याला त्या  जंगलाचा कंटाळा आला आणि तो नव्या  जंगलात राहायला गेला. एकदा सिंह मोठ्याने गरजला. त्या  जंगलात अनेक  प्राणी व पक्षी तसेच काही बेडूकही राहत होते. त्यांनी यापूर्वी सिंह पाहिला नव्हता.  बेडकांचा पुढारी म्हणाला, \"कोणीतरी मोठा आवाज काढत आहे. आता मीही मोठा आवाज काढतो.\"  बेडकाने मोठा आवाज काढला. सिंहाला हा आवाज नवीन होता. सिंहाला वाटले, \'कोणीतरी आपल्याला आव्हान देत आहे, आपण सावध राहिले पाहिजे.\' सिंहाने आपली गर्जना थांबवली. तो शांत उभा राहिला. बेडूक मोठमोठ्याने ओरडत पुढे-पुढे सरकू लागला. सिंहाने त्याला पाहिले व त्याचा आवाज ऐकला. सिंह वेगाने पुढे सरकला. बेडकाच्या डोक्यावर पाय दिला. बेडूक गयावया करू लागला.  सिंहाने  त्याला सोडून दिले.','खालील प्रश्नांची उत्तरे लिहा : ','प्रश्न १. या गोष्टीतील प्राण्यांची नावे सांगा व लिहा.\n प्रश्न २. सिंह व बेडूक यांमध्ये हुशार कोण, ते सांगा.\nप्रश्न ३. या गोष्टीतील सिंह व बेडूक यांचे स्वभाव सांगा. ','','१) १) सिंह         २) बेडूक\n२) सिंह हुशार आहे; कारण त्याला आपल्या शक्तीची जाणीव आहे. बेडूक मात्र गर्विष्ठ आहे.\n३) सिंह हुशार आहे. बेडूक गर्विष्ठ आहे.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82531,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Correct the following statements and rewrite them : There are coffee plantations in Himachal Pradesh.','','','There are coffee plantations in Kerala and Karnataka.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82532,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Correct the following statements and rewrite them : Konkan lies in the eastern part of India.','','','Konkan lies in the western part of India.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82533,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Correct the following statements and rewrite them : Tripura is the smallest state in India.','','','Goa is the smallest state in India.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82534,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Correct the following statements and rewrite them : The Sabarmati River flows through Madhya Pradesh.','','','The Sabarmati River flows through Gujarat.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82535,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Correct the following statements and rewrite them : The Sahyadri Mountains are located in Andhra Pradesh.','','','The Sahyadri Mountains are located in Maharashtra.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82536,2485,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In India, the primary crop in the south and along the coast is ____\na) Wheat  b) Rice  c) Maize  d) Barley','','','b) Rice','',0,0,0,NULL),(82537,2485,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','India is a ____ republic.\na) Socialist  b) Democratic  c) Communist  d) Monarchical','','','b) Democratic','',0,0,0,NULL),(82538,2485,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Considering the area, ____ is the largest state in India.\na) Maharashtra  b) Uttar Pradesh  c) Rajasthan  d) Madhya Pradesh','','','c) Rajasthan','',0,0,0,NULL),(82539,2485,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The lofty ____ mountain ranges form the northern boundary of the Indian subcontinent.\n(A) Sahyadri  (B) Himalayan  (C) Vindhya  (D) Aravali\n','','','B) Himalayan','',0,0,0,NULL),(82540,2485,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The Indian peninsula has the ____ sea to its west.\n(A) Arabian  (B) Pacific  (C) Atlantic  (D) Bay of Bengal\n','','','A) Arabian','',0,0,0,NULL),(82541,2485,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','____ is the area wise smallest state.\n(A) Maharashtra  (B) Rajasthan  (C) Goa  (D) Madhya Pradesh\n','','','C) Goa','',0,0,0,NULL),(82542,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Underline the correct word : The capital of the Maharashtra state is Panaji/Mumbai.','','','The capital of the Maharashtra state is <u>Mumbai.</u>','',0,0,0,NULL),(82543,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Underline the correct word : The Coromandel Coast is along the southwestern/southeastern coast of India.','','','The Coromandel Coast is along the <u>southeastern</u> coast of India.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82544,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Underline the correct word : Jowar/Rice is produced on large scale in central India.','','','<u>Jowar</u> is produced on large scale in central India.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82545,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following : The primary crop in north India.','','','Wheat','',0,0,0,NULL),(82546,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following :  The islands in the Bay of Bengal which are a part of the Indian territory.','','','Andaman and Nicobar islands','',0,0,0,NULL),(82547,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following : The capital of India.','','','New Delhi','',0,0,0,NULL),(82548,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following : Area-wise the second largest state in India.','','','Madhya Pradesh','',0,0,0,NULL),(82549,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which part of the Indian subcontinent is called the Indian peninsula?','','','The part of the Indian subcontinent which is surrounded by water on its three sides and tapers towards the south is called the Indian peninsula.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82550,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What gets affected due to the diversity in India?','','','The diversity affects the lifestyle, customs, traditions and culture of the people in India.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82551,2485,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','Make a chart of the states and the rivers flowing through/in them.','','','<table border=\"1\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width:fit-content;\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n  <tr>\n    <th>River</th>\n    <th>Rivers flowing through/in States</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(1) Ganga</td>\n    <td>Uttarakhand, Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, Jharkhand and West Bengal.</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(2) Beas</td>\n    <td>Himachal Pradesh and Punjab.</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(3) Narmada</td>\n    <td>Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra and Gujarat.</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(4) Godavari</td>\n    <td>Maharashtra, Telangana, Chhattisgarh and Andhra Pradesh.</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(5) Krishna</td>\n    <td>Maharashtra and Karnataka.</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(6) Kaveri</td>\n    <td>Karnataka and Tamil Nadu.</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(7) Brahmaputra</td>\n    <td>Assam and Arunachal Pradesh.</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(8) Sabarmati</td>\n    <td>Rajasthan and Gujarat.</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>','',0,0,0,NULL),(82552,2485,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','In which things do we find diversity in different regions of India?','','','i) In India we find diversity in the climate, plants, animals, birds and the crops cultivated.\n(ii) Also people of different castes, tribes and religions speaking different languages live in our country.\n(iii) We also see differences in food, clothing and festivals and their celebrations in different regions of India.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82553,2485,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Apart from the Indian mainland which are the islands that form a part of the Indian Territory?','','','Apart from the Indian mainland the islands which form a part of the Indian Territory are given below,\n(i) The Lakshadweep islands in the Arabian Sea.\n(ii) The Andaman and Nicobar Islands in the Bay of Bengal.\n(iii) The coastal islands near the Indian mainland.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82554,2485,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Explain the importance of islands along the coast of Maharashtra.','','','i) Islands have strategic locations and thus are important from defence point of view.\n(ii) The historical sea forts on the islands, along the coast of Maharashtra were built to safeguard the coasts.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82555,2485,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reasons : There are variety of plants, animals and birds in India.','','','i) The expanse of India is very large.\n(ii) The height, measured above sea-level varies from place to place due to which weather conditions change from region to region.\n(iii) These varying weather conditions gives rise to a wide variety of plants, animals and birds in India.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82556,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Which is the state next to us which was formed in 2014?','','','The state of Telangana next to Maharashtra was formed in 2014.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82557,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','How many states are there in India?','','','There are in all 29 states in India.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82558,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','In which state is the Great India Desert mainly located?','','','The Great India Desert is mainly located in Rajasthan.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82559,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What forms the northern border of Indian subcontinent?','','','The Himalaya ranges form the northern border of the Indian subcontinent.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82560,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','How many states and union territories are present in India?','','','29 states and 7 union territories are present in India.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82561,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name some of the famous rivers in India.','','','Ganga, Yamuna, Narmada, Godavari, Krishna, and Kaveri.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82562,2485,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Match the name of the city / state in Group \' A \' with its importance mentioned in Group \'B\'.\n<table border=\"1\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width:fit-content;\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n  <tr>\n    <th>Group \'A\'</th>\n    <th>Group \'B\'</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(i) Rajasthan</td>\n    <td>(a) Area wise smallest state</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(ii) Goa</td>\n    <td>(b) Area wise third largest state</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(iii) Maharashtra</td>\n    <td>(c) Area wise largest state</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>','','','(i) - (c), (ii) - (a), (iii) - (b)','',0,0,0,NULL),(82563,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following : The states which are famous for their coffee plantations.','','','Kerala, Karnataka','',0,0,0,NULL),(82564,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following : The desert located in Rajasthan.','','','The Great Indian Desert','',0,0,0,NULL),(82565,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following : The state adjacent to Maharashtra formed in 2014.','','','Telangana','',0,0,0,NULL),(82566,2485,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Write about the diversity in the crops cultivated in different regions of India.','','','a) Different crops are cultivated in different parts of India.\n(b) The primary crop in the north is wheat.\n(c) In south India and along the coastal regions the primary crop is rice.\n(d) Jowar is produced on large scale in central India.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82567,2485,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','What lies along the borders of the Indian subcontinent?','','','a) The Indian subcontinent has the lofty Himalaya ranges along its northern border.\n(b) The lower part of the subcontinent is surrounded on three sides by water. This part is known as the Indian peninsula.\n(c) It has the Arabian Sea to its west, the Indian Ocean to its south and the Bay of Bengal to its east.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82568,2485,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reason : India has great diversity.','','','i) India has a vast area. The weather conditions are different in different regions of the country. This leads to wide variety of plants, animals, birds as well as the cultivated crops.\n(ii) Also people of different castes, tribes and religions live in India. There are differences in their food, clothing, festivals, lifestyle, customs, traditions, culture and the languages spoken by them.\nDue to all these reasons, India is said to have great diversity.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82569,2485,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Areawise, ____ is the largest state of India.\na) Maharashtra  b) Madhya Pradesh  c) Rajasthan','','','c) Rajasthan','',0,0,0,NULL),(82570,2485,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Areawise, Maharashtra is the ____ largest state of India.\na) second  b) third  c) fifth','','','b) third','',0,0,0,NULL),(82571,2485,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','____ state is in the western part of India.\na) West Bengal  b) Meghalaya  c) Gujarat','','','c) Gujarat','',0,0,0,NULL),(82572,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Correct the following statements and rewrite them : The Nilgiri Mountains are located in the northern part of India.','','','The Nilgiri Mountains are located in the southern part of India.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82573,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Correct the following statements and rewrite them : There are many plateaus in the far-east states of India.','','','There are many hills in the far-east states of India.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82574,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following : The capital of India ','','','New Delhi.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82575,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following : Any three hills located in the far-east states of India','','','Naga, Patkai, Lushai.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82576,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following : Any five rivers in India ','','','Ganga, Yamuna, Sabarmati, Narmada, Krishna','',0,0,0,NULL),(82577,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following : Any five states in India ','','','Karnataka, Odisha, Himachal Pradesh, Arunachal Pradesh and Bihar.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82578,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following : The highest peak in the Sahyadri Mountains in Maharashtra ','','','Kalsubai','',0,0,0,NULL),(82579,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following : World-famous lake in Maharashtra ','','','Lonar lake.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82580,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following : A place / district famous for orange production in Maharashtra ','','','Nagpur','',0,0,0,NULL),(82581,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following : A place / district famous for onion production in Maharashtra ','','','Nashik','',0,0,0,NULL),(82582,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which mountain has defined the northern boundary of India?','','','Himalaya Ranges has defined the northern boundary of India.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82583,2485,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which part of India is called the Indian Peninsula?','','','The Indian subcontinent that is surrounded by water on the three sides and tapers towards the south is called the \'Indian Peninsula\'.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82584,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which strait is to the south of India?','','','Palk Strait is to the south of India.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82585,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In which water body are the Lakshadweep Islands located?','','','The Lakshadweep Islands are located in the Arabian Sea.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82586,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In which water body are the Andaman and Nicobar Islands located?','','','The Andaman and Nicobar Islands are located in the Bay of Bengal.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82587,2485,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','In which region of India is a camel found?','','','A camel is found in the desert region of India.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82588,2485,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','India has diversity in which aspects?','','','We find diversity in physical set-up, climate, plants, animals, birds, crops, food, clothing, festivals, languages, customs, traditions and culture in India.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82589,2491,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Substances that have got mixed with the water are ----- for living things.\na) Beneficial b) Neutral c) Essential d) Harmful','','','d) Harmful\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82590,2491,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Waste water contains many ------.\na) Vitamins b) Nutrients c) Impurities d) Minerals','','','c) Impurities\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82591,2491,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Sewage water can carry many ----- that cause disease.\na) Chemicals b) Micro-organisms c) Metals d) Salts','','','b) Micro-organisms\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82592,2491,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Before water is supplied to a town or city, it is -------\na) Boiled b) Frozen c) Purified d) Colored','','','c) Purified\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82593,2491,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','It is ----- for a factory owner to treat water before letting it out.\na) Optional b) Compulsory c) Unnecessary d) Difficult','','','b) Compulsory\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82594,2491,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','There is a threat to the ----- living things if the proportion of oxygen in water is reduced.\na) Domestic b) Aquatic c) Terrestrial d) Wild\n','','','b) Aquatic\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82595,2491,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','A famine is a ---- disaster.\na) Natural b) Man-made c) Technological d) Financial','','','a) Natural\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82596,2491,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','------ are set up to take care of domestic animals.\na) Fodder camps b) Animal shelters c) Pet clinics d) Farms','','','a) Fodder camps\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82597,2491,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','----- are present in sewage water that spread disease.\na) Plastics b) Micro-organisms c) Minerals d) Gases','','','b) Micro-organisms\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82598,2491,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','The proportion of ------ dissolved in the water is reduced.\na) Carbon dioxide b) Nitrogen c) Oxygen d) Hydrogen','','','c) Oxygen\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82599,2491,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','---- is mixed in the water to kill the germs in it.\na) Mercury b) Iodine c) Chlorine d) Fluoride','','','c) Chlorine\n\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82600,2485,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','Study the map showing the major rivers of India and answer the questions only in words :','1) Name the rivers that are mentioned in patriotic songs.\n2) Write the names of the places that you know in the map.\n3) Which mountain is located in the western part of Maharashtra?\n4) Which mountain is located in the northern part of Maharashtra?\n','','1) Yamuna, Ganga, Godavari, etc.\n2) Sahyadri, Konkan, River Krishna, Deccan Plateau, Himalaya, etc.\n3) Sahyadri mountain is located in the western part of Maharashtra.\n4) Satpuda mountain is located in the northern part of Maharashtra.\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(82601,2485,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','Study the physical map of India given below and answer the questions only in words/one sentence:','1) Find the mountains and name them.\n2) Name the hills shown on the map.\n3) Find the plateaus in the map and name them.\n4) Write the names of the rivers which originate in the Himalayas and join the Indus. Consider the height and write the direction of their flow.\n','','1) Himalaya, Ladakh, Aravali, Sahyadri, Satpura, Nilgiri, Vindhya, Girnar, etc.\n2) Ajanta, Mahadeo, Satmala, Balaghat, Maikala, Nallamala, etc.\n3) Mewad, Malwa, Chota Nagpur, Maharashtra, Telangana, Karnataka, etc.\n4) The rivers which originate in the Himalayas and join the Indus are Jhelum, Chenab, Ravi, Beas, Satluj, etc. They all flow from the east to the west.\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(82602,2485,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','Study the physical map of India given below and answer the questions only in words/one sentence:','1) Write the names of the major rivers which flow into the Coromandel Coast.\n2) Study the course of the Ganga, Narmada, Vainganga, Godavari and Kaveri rivers. Note the slope of the land in each basin and write the direction of the slope.\n3) Find the lakes on the map and name them.\n','','1) Kaveri, Krishna and Godavari.\n2) i) The direction of the slope of the land in Narmada River Basin : From the east to the west. \nii) The direction of the slope of the land in Wainganga River Basin : From the north to the south. \niii) The direction of the slope of the land in Ganga, Godavari and Kaveri River Basins : From the west to the east.\n3) Wular, Sambhar, Lonar, Vembanad, Pulicat, Chilika, Koleru, etc.\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(82603,2485,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','Study the physical map of India given below and answer the questions only in words/one sentence:','1) Find and name the gulfs and the direction in which they are located with respect to India.\n2) Study the water bodies on the three sides of India. Find their names and write the direction in which they are located.\n3) Find the Lakshadweep, Andaman and Nicobar Island groups and write the names of some of the islands.\n4) Which river basin is located in the northern plain of India?\n','','1) Names of gulfs : Gulf of Kachchh, Gulf of Khambhat, Gulf of Mannar. Gulf of Kachchh and Gulf of Khambhat are to the west of India and Gulf of Mannar is to the south of India.\n2) Names of water bodies on the three sides of India : Arabian Sea, Bay of Bengal and Indian Ocean. Arabian Sea is to the west, Bay of Bengal is to the east and Indian Ocean is to the south of India.\n3) The names of some of the islands in Lakshadweep Island group : Minicoy, Kavaratti, Chettlatt, Kilttan, Amindivi, etc. The names of some of the islands in Andaman and Nicobar Island group : Narcondam, Barren, Car Nicobar, Port Blair, Great Nicobar, etc.\n4) Ganga river basin is located in the northern plain of India.\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(82604,2485,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','Study the political map of India given below and answer the questions only in words/one sentence:','1) Find our state and write the name of its capital.\n2) Which is the northernmost state?\n3) Which is the southernmost state?\n4) Write the name of the largest state and write the name of its capital.\n','','1) Our State: Maharashtra. Capital: Mumbai.\n2) The northernmost state is Jammu and Kashmir/Ladakh.\n3) The southernmost state is Tamil Nadu/Kerala.\n4) The largest state: Rajasthan. The name of its capital: Jaipur.\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(82605,2485,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','Study the map of India given below and answer the questions only in words/one sentence:\n(1) From where will we obtain saffron?\n2) In which states is tea grown?\n3) Name the states in which apples are grown.\n4) How will you send onions from Maharashtra to Arunachal Pradesh?\n','','','1) We will obtain saffron from Jammu and Kashmir.\n2) Tea is grown in the states of Assam and West Bengal.\n3) Apples are grown in Jammu and Kashmir and Himachal Pradesh.\n4) We will send onions from Maharashtra to Arunachal Pradesh by the following National Highway routes : From Nashik to Nagpur, From Nagpur to Kolkata, from Kolkata to the state of Assam and from the state of Assam to the state of Arunachal Pradesh.\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(82606,2486,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','People build houses using the ------- that are available in a region.\na) tools  b) machines  c) natural resources  d) bricks','','','c) natural resources','',0,0,0,NULL),(82607,2486,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','A section of our society being homeless is a --------- problem.\na) economic  b) social  c) political  d) cultural','','','b) social','',0,0,0,NULL),(82608,2486,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','-------- is produced using natural fuels like coal, natural gas or mineral oil.\na) Water  b) Energy  c) Food  d) Plastic','','','b) Energy','',0,0,0,NULL),(82609,2486,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','When there is shortage of agricultural land, -------- land is used for agriculture.\na) barren  b) forest  c) desert  d) rocky','','','b) forest','',0,0,0,NULL),(82610,2486,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Glass is prepared from ____\n(A) sand  (B) limestone  (C) cement  (D) coal\n','','','A) sand','',0,0,0,NULL),(82611,2486,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following is an exhaustible source of energy?\n(A) Biogas  (B) Wind energy  (C) Natural gas  (D) Solar energy\n','','','C) Natural gas','',0,0,0,NULL),(82612,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Underline the correct word : Flat-roofed houses and boathouses are found in mountainous/marshy regions.','','','Flat-roofed houses and boathouses are found in <u>mountainous</u> regions.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82613,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Underline the correct word : Limestone/Coal is used as a natural fuel to produce energy.','','','<u>Coal</u> is used as a natural fuel to produce energy.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82614,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Underline the correct word : The city of Mumbai comprises of six/ seven islands.','','','The city of Mumbai comprises of <u>seven</u> islands.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82615,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What are the basic needs of every human being?','','','The basic needs of every human being are water, food, clothing and shelter.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82616,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is the right of every human being?','','','Every human being has the right to clean potable water, sufficient food, a safe shelter and education.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82617,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give examples where energy is used to produce construction materials?','','','Energy is used in large scale to prepare construction materials like bricks from soil, cement from limestone, glass from sand, etc.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82618,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What are known as non-exhaustible sources of energy?','','','The sources of energy like solar energy and wind energy which are available in plenty are known as non-exhaustible sources of energy.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82619,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Which type of houses shown below would be suitable in a mountainous region? Give reasons for selecting that house.','','','The selected house would be appropriate for a mountainous region due to the following reasons:\n Its sloping roof does not allow the accumulation of rainwater or snowfall.\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(82620,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Which type of houses shown below would be suitable in a mountainous region? Give reasons for selecting that house.','','','The selected house would be appropriate for a mountainous region due to the following reasons: Due to lack of flat land, houses with multiple storey are built to accommodate more number of people.','',1,0,0,NULL),(82621,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Which type of houses shown below would be suitable in a mountainous region? Give reasons for selecting that house. ','','','The selected house would be appropriate for a mountainous region due to the following reasons: Mud and stones available in mountainous regions are used to build the house.','',1,0,0,NULL),(82622,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Which type of houses shown below would be suitable in a mountainous region? Give reasons for selecting that house.','','','The selected house would be appropriate for a mountainous region due to the following reasons: The house is strong enough to withstand mountainous winds.','',1,0,0,NULL),(82623,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','What materials will you mainly use for building a multi-storeyed house? Choose the correct option.\na) Mortar / coal / cement / bricks       b) Cement / bricks / cotton / iron      c) Iron / cement / mortar / bricks\n','','','c) Iron / cement / mortar / bricks','',0,0,0,NULL),(82624,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','Arrange the following considerations from the most to least important in housebuilding.\ni) Luxury         ii) Structure       iii) Climate\n','','','In the process of house-building the most to least important considerations are as follows.\ni) Climate       ii) Structure           iii) Luxury\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82625,2486,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','List the eco-friendly things in your house. ','','','We can use the following eco-friendly things in our house;\na) Solar cooker       b) Solar heater\nc) Hand-held fans which not only help in saving electricity, but are also made using eco-friendly and easily available materials.\n(d) Bicycles which can be used instead of vehicles.\n(e) Induction cook-tops which save cooking gas.\n(f) Energy efficient appliances like CFLs (Compact Fluorescent Lamp).\n(g) Energy efficient cookware which helps in faster cooking and thus saves energy. (Students are expected to make a list of eco-friendly things in their house)\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82626,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','Which of the gadgets in the house can be run on solar energy?','','','In our house we can use gadgets like solar cooker and solar heater which run on solar energy. Also we can install solar panels in our house / building and use the solar energy thus generated for running several appliances like refrigerator, etc.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82627,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','What are the types of pollution that can be observed at a construction site?','','','The dust generated causes air pollution, different chemicals can cause soil and water pollution and loud noise of machines cause sound pollution at a construction site.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82628,2486,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Board Paper','','Why do we need a house?','','','We need a house for the following reasons:\n(i) A house is used as a shelter.\n(ii) It is a resting place.\n(iii) It protects us from the sun, wind, cold, rains and wild animals.\n(iv) Our house also keeps us safe from the anti-social elements.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82629,2486,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','What happens when humans\' basic need of shelter is not fulfilled?','','','When humans basic need of shelter is not fulfilled, such people take shelter at the roadside or on footpaths, under bridges, in tumbledown buildings, in railway or bus stations and even on open grounds. Several people are also left homeless due to insufficient or no means of livelihood.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82630,2486,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','How does the government try to solve the problem of homelessness?','','','The government implements several schemes to provide homes to the homeless. Also in some cities, the government provides night shelters to the homeless people.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82631,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reasons : We should bring into use other sources of energy like the solar energy and wind energy.','','','i) Natural fuels like coal, natural gas and mineral oil can be used only once. They get consumed as and when we use them.\n(ii) These fuels take lakhs of years to get replenished.\n(iii) Also, burning of these fuels causes air pollution.\n(iv) Sources of energy like solar and wind energy are available in plenty and do not cause pollution.\nTherefore, we should bring into use other sources of energy like the solar energy and wind energy.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82632,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Give reasons : Growing urbanization leads to reduction in forests.','','','i) Growing urbanization leads to the use of agricultural land for building roads and to raise settlements. Due to this, agricultural land gets reduced.\n(ii) To fulfill the shortage of agricultural land, forest land is cleared by felling trees. Thus, the growing urbanization leads to reduction in forests.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82633,2486,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','For what purpose do birds use their nests?','','','Birds use their nests for the following reasons.\n(i) Laying eggs and giving birth to their young ones.\n(ii) Protecting themselves and their young ones from sun, rains, wind, etc.\n(iii) Protecting their eggs and young ones from predator birds and animals.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82634,2486,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','What can we do to build houses without harming the environment? Discuss your solutions in the class.','','','Some of the points to be considered while building an eco-friendly house are as follows:\n(i) Minimal use of natural resources.\n(ii) Make rooms with large windows facing the sun so as to make maximum use of sunlight and also to allow air to flow.\n(iii) Avoid usage of artificial materials and colours.\n(iv) Avoid excessive lighting in the house.\n(v) Recycle water\n(vi) Have proper tap and pipe fittings so as to avoid wastage of water.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82635,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Mention any one provision implemented by the government for homeless people in some cities.','','','In some cities, the government makes \'night shelters\' available for homeless people.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82636,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name some non-exhaustible sources of energy.','','','Solar energy, wind energy and biogas','',0,0,0,NULL),(82637,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which construction material in produced from limestone?','','','Cement is produced from limestone.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82638,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','What are underwater shelters?','','','Underwater shelters are a part of water tourism from which tourists get a direct view of the sea-hed and the morino life','',0,0,0,NULL),(82639,2486,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','Complete the chart.','','','i) Unemployment          ii) Physical and mental disorders          iii) Natural disasters\niv) Poverty                     v) Lack of affordable housing\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(82640,2486,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','People build houses to suit the ____ of their region.\n(A) soil (B) climate (C) population (D) language','','','B) climate','',0,0,0,NULL),(82641,2486,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','The government makes night shelters available to the ____.\n(A) farmers (B) homeless (C) teachers (D) students','','','B) homeless','',0,0,0,NULL),(82642,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What does the burning of natural fuels lead to?','','','The burning of natural fuels leads to air pollution.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82643,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What type of houses should we build to reduce the harm caused to environment?','','','We must build eco-friendly houses so as to reduce the harm caused to environment','',0,0,0,NULL),(82644,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','What gives rise to different types of houses?','','','People build houses to suit the climate of their region. They use the natural resources available to them in that region. Hence, the differences in the construction and building materials give rise to the different types of houses.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82645,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Why is the land of Mumbai called as \'reclaimed\' land?','','','The city of Mumbai comprises of seven islands. The portion of water bodies between these islands was filled with stone and earth. Due to this, the land of Mumbai is called as \'reclaimed\' land.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82646,2486,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Houses made up of material like ____ are mainly seen in cities.\n(A) clay  (B) wood  (C) cement\n','','','C) cement','',0,0,0,NULL),(82647,2486,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Homelessness is a ____ problem.\n(A) personal  (B) political  (C) social\n','','','C) social','',0,0,0,NULL),(82648,2486,'mcq','1a',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','____ is a non-exhaustible source of energy.\n(A) Coal  (B) Mineral oil  (C) Solar energy\n','','','C) Solar energy','',0,0,0,NULL),(82649,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following are the exhaustible sources of energy?\n(a) Solar energy, Coal, Mineral oil, Wind energy\n(b) Wind energy, Solar energy, Natural gas, Coal\n(c) Coal, Natural gas, Petrol, Diesel\n','','','The following are the exhaustible sources of energy : Coal, Natural gas, Petrol, Diesel.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82650,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following are causes of homelessness?\n(a) Poverty, Unemployment, Physical disorder, Natural disasters\n(b) Mental disorder, Richness, Physical disorder, Inadequate income\n(c) Adequate income, Employment, Poverty, Lack of affordable housing\n','','','The following are the causes of homelessness : Poverty, Unemployment, Physical disorder, Natural disasters.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82651,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Correct the statements and rewrite them : Flat-roofed houses are seen in the regions of heavy rainfall.','','','Slanted-roofed houses are seen in the regions of heavy rainfall.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82652,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Correct the statements and rewrite them : Wind energy is exhaustible source of energy.','','','Wind energy is non-exhaustible source of energy.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82653,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Correct the statements and rewrite them : Heavy-weight houses are seen in the marshy region.','','','Light-weight houses are seen in the marshy region.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82654,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following : Materials used for building houses ','','','Bricks, cement, iron, wood, water, rubble, glass, floor tiles, sand, roof tiles, tin sheets, etc.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82655,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following : The basic needs of man ','','','Air, water, food, clothing, shelter and education.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82656,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following :  Social problems ','','','Poverty, unemployment, homelessness, population explosion, etc.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82657,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following :  Types of pollution ','','','Air pollution, water pollution, soil pollution and noise pollution.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82658,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Name the following :  Non-exhaustible sources of energy ','','','Solar energy, wind energy, etc.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82659,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Match the Groups :\n<table border=\"1\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width:fit-content;\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n  <tr>\n    <th>\'A\' (Building Material)</th>\n    <th>\'B\' (Original Source)</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(1) Bricks</td>\n    <td>(a) Water</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(2) Cement</td>\n    <td>(b) Sand</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>(3) Glass</td>\n    <td>(c) Soil</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td></td>\n    <td>(d) Limestone</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>','','','(1) Bricks - Soil\n(2) Cement - Limestone\n(3) Glass - Sand\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82660,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What is \'energy\'?','','','\'Energy\' is defined as the ability or capacity to do work.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82661,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What are the exhaustible sources of energy?','','','The resources that are susceptible to depletion by overuse are the \'exhaustible sources of energy\'.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82662,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','What are the non-exhaustible sources of energy?','','','The resources that can be naturally replaced even after depletion are the non-exhaustible sources of energy.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82663,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What type of pollution does the burning of fuels lead to?','','','The burning of fuels leads to air pollution.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82664,2486,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','What type of houses should be built by man?','','','Permanent houses that are eco-friendly should be built by man.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82665,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Why do we find differences in houses built by man?','','','We find differences in houses built by man because of the regional differences in weather conditions and natural resources.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82666,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','Where do the homeless people seek shelter?','','','The homeless people seek shelter at the roadside, on footpaths, under bridges, in tumbledown buildings, in railway or bus stations and even on open grounds.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82667,2486,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','What facilities are provided by the government to the homeless?','','','Government implements many schemes to provide homes to the homeless and also provides \'night shelters\' in some of the cities.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82668,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Write down the conversation between Tara, Bittu, Paddy and Kuku.\n','','','Tara : Hi Bittu! \n         Hi Paddy!\n         Hi Kuku!\n         I\'m so excited about starting studies again.\nBittu : Oh, no!\n          Holidays are over!\nKuku : More play on the school ground.\nPaddy : Hi Tara!\n             I\'m excited too!\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82669,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Write down the conversation between doggy, cat and parrot.\n','','','Doggie : I\'m sad without Paddy\nCat       : We are lucky!\n               We don\'t have school.\nParrot : Mia, you will never learn!\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82670,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Answer the following questions : Why is Tara excited?\n','','','Tara is excited about starting studies again.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82671,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Why did Bittu become nervous?\n','','','Bittu became nervous because holidays were over.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82672,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Why did Cat think that they are lucky?\n','','','The cat thought that they were lucky because they didn\'t have school.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82673,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Why is Kuku happy?\n','','','Kuku is happy because now she can play more on the school ground.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82674,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','What did Parrot say to the cat?\n','','','Parrot said to the Cat that it would never learn.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82675,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Write one meaningful question each beginning with the following words : Who ------?\n','','','Who is that boy?\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82676,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Write one meaningful question each beginning with the following words : What ------?\n','','','What are you doning?\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82677,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Write one meaningful question each beginning with the following words : Where ------?\n','','','Where do you live?\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82678,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Write one meaningful question each beginning with the following words : Where ------?\n','','','Where do you live?\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82679,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Write one meaningful question each beginning with the following words : \ni) When ------?        ii) Why ------?','','','i) When is English period?\nii) Why are you laughing?\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82680,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Write one meaningful question each beginning with the following words : \ni) Don\'t you ------?        ii) Doesn\'t she -----?','','','i) Don\'t you have any money?\nii) Doesn\'t she like to play?\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82681,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Write one meaningful question each beginning with the following words : \ni) Can\'t we ------?      ii) Won\'t you ----------?','','','i) Can\'t we swim today?\nii) Won\'t you play?','',0,0,0,NULL),(82682,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Write one meaningful question each beginning with the following words :\ni) May ------?           ii) Could ----------?\n','','','i) May I come in?\nii) Could you please send me your mobile number?\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82683,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Correct the following sentence : i) You is a boy      ii) We was running fast.','','','i) You are a boy.           ii) We were running fast.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82684,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Correct the following sentences : i) She don\'t know it.    ii) It doesn\'t rain yesterday\n','','','i) She doesn\'t know it.\nii) It didn\'t rain yesterday.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82685,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Correct the following sentence : i) He have done well          ii) Seeta like flowers\n','','','i) He has done well.\nii) Seeta likes flowers.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82686,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Correct the following sentence : i) One of the mangoes are ripe.\nii) He will be here within a hour.','','','i) One of the mangoes is ripe\nii) He will be here within an hour.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82687,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Correct the following sentence : i) I have a lot of moneys.\nii) An earth moves round the sun.','','','i) I have a lot of money.\nii) The earth moves round the sun.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82688,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Classify the following words into parts of speech :\nunder, beautiful, river, Alas!, play, and, fast, day, of, or, he, slowly, nice, they, oh!, eat\n\nAns. : i) Noun : --------------------            ii) Verb : -------------\n         iii) Pronoun : ------------------          iv) Adjectives : ----------------\n         v) Adverb : ----------------              vi) Preposition : --------------\n         vii) Conjunction : ---------------       viii) Interjection : -------------- ','','','         i) Noun : river, day                          ii) Verb : play, eat\n         iii) Pronoun : he, they                       iv) Adjectives : beautiful, nice\n         iv) Adverb : fast slowly                     v) Preposition : under, of\n         vi) Conjunction : and, or                 vii) Interjection : Alas!, oh ','',0,0,0,NULL),(82689,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Write any five words that end with (s/es).\n','','','notebooks, trees, boys, houses, shoes\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82690,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Write any five words that end with \'-ing\'.\n','','','beginning, caring, loving, joking, riding \n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82691,563,'descriptive','1',2,0,'Out of Text Book','','Write any five words that end with \'-ed\'.\n','','','walked, stopped, talked, offered, helped.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82692,563,'descriptive','2',10,0,'Out of Text Book','','a) Write one meaningful question each beginning with the following with the following words : ---------------------- 5M\ni) Who ----------?                                             ii) What -------------? \nii) Where -------?                                            iv) When ----------? \nv) Why ---------?                                               vi) How ------------?\nb) Write one meaningful question each beginning with the following with the following words : ----------------------- 5M\n i) Are ----------?                                       ii) Is -------------?\n ii) Have -------?                                        iv) Has ----------? \nv) Do ---------?                                            v) Does ------------?','','','a) i) Who is that boy?                     ii) What are you doing? \n          iii) Where do you live?               iv) When is English period? \n          v) Why are you laughing?           vi) How do you go to school? \nb) i) Are you ready?                              ii) Is she is good girl?\n     iii) Have you finished your work?     iv) Has she finished her lunch? \n      v) Do you like cold drink?                  vi) Does she know everything? ','',0,0,0,NULL),(82693,563,'descriptive','2',10,0,'Out of Text Book','','a) Write one meaningful question each beginning with the following with the following words : ------------------------------ 5M\n i) Aren\'t they ----------?                             ii) Isn\'t he -------------? \nii) Don\'t you -------?                                    iv) Doesn\'t she ----------? \nv) Can\'t we ---------?                                    vi) Won\'t you ------------?\nb) Write one meaningful question each beginning with the following with the following words : ------------------------------ 5M\n i) Can ----------?                                 ii) Will ---------------?\n iii) May ---------?                                iv) Could --------------?\n  v) Did ----------?\n','','','a) i) Aren\'t they coming?                        ii) Isn\'t he precious?\n         iii) Don\'t you have any money?         iv) Doesn\'t she like to play? \n         v) Can\'t we swim today?                      vi) Won\'t you play? \n     b) i) Can you sing?                ii) Will you stand up, please?\n          iii) May I come in?       iv) Could you please send me your mobile number?  \n          v) Did they go home?\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82694,563,'descriptive','2',10,0,'Out of Text Book','','Write the following conversation using this titles (any two) : ---------- 10M\n i) Asking a friend to lend you her notebook.\n ii) Inviting a friend to your birthday party.\n iii) Saying sorry to someone for trodding on his/her foot. \niv) Offering a glass of water to a guest.','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(82695,563,'descriptive','2',10,0,'Out of Text Book','','a) Adding \'s\' to verbs. -------------- 5M\ni) I like -----------                    ii) We like ---------- \niii) You like -------                 iv) He likes ---------- \nv) She likes ----------\nb) Use of \'do\' : ---------------- 5M\ni) I do/don’t ---------                     ii) You do/don’t ------------\niii) We do/don’t ----------            iv) We did/didn’t ------------\nv) You did/didn’t ------------        vi) They did/didn’t ----------------','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(82698,563,'descriptive','2',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','Observe the following table and answer the questions: ------------ 10M\n1) Write down three letter words from the given table.\n2) Write down the words which begin with ‘a’\n3) Write down the words which end with ‘t’.\n4) Write down four letter words.','','','1) the, and, for, not, you, but, his, her, she, one, all, out, who, can\n2) and, as, at, an, all, about\n3) that, it, not, at, but, what, out, about\n4) that, have, with, this, from, they, will, what, when','',1,0,0,NULL),(82699,564,'descriptive','2',10,2,'Out of Text Book','It was an early Easter. In the yards lay snow, and rills ran down the village. A large puddle had run down from a manure pile into a lane between two farms. And at this puddle two girls, one older than the other, had met. Both of them had been dressed by their mothers in new clothes. The little girl had a blue dress, and the elder a yellow one with a design. Both had their heads wrapped in red kerchiefs.\nAfter prayers in the Church, the two girls went to the puddle, where they showed their new garments to each other, and began to play. They wanted to plash in the water. The little girl started to go into the puddle with her shoes on, but the older girl said to her: \n\"Don\'t go, Malasha, your mother will scold you. I will take off my shoes, and you do the same.”','Read the following passage and complete the activities : \n1) i) Name the following :   \na) Name of the festival : -------\n b) Place of worship for the christians : ------------ \nii) Complete the following sentences :\na) The two girls went to the puddle (time) ----------\nb) The large puddle ran into (place) --------','2) Complete the following : Two girls  ----------- 1M\nAge : -----------------\nDress : ---------------\n3) Write the following words in appropriate Coloumn : Snow, village, water, farms \ni) Countable noun : \nii) Uncountable noun : \n4) Write the past tense of given verbs :\ni) grasp -              ii) pick -               iii) gather -               iv) laugh ','','1) i) a) Easter     b) Church\n               ii) a) After prayers in the church\n                    b) a lane between two farms\n        2) Age : elder, younger\n            Dress : yellow, blue\n3) i) Countable Noun : Village, farms\n    ii) Uncountable noun : Snow, water \n4) i) grasped                 ii) picked                 iii) gathered              iv) laughed ','',0,0,0,NULL),(82700,564,'descriptive','2',10,2,'Out of Text Book','One word brought back another, and the women began to quarrel. The men, too, ran out, and a big crowd gathered in the street. All were crying, and nobody could hear his neighbour. They scolded and cursed each other; one man gave another man a push, and a fight had begun, when Akulka\'s grandmother came out. She stepped in the midst of the peasants, and began to talk to them:\n\"What are you doing, dear ones? Consider the holiday. This is a time for rejoicing. And see what sin you are doing!\"\nThey paid no attention to the old woman, and almost knocked her off her feet. She would never have stopped them, if it had not been for Akulka and Malasha.\nWhile the women exchanged words, Akulka wiped off her dress, and went back to the puddle in the lane. She picked up a pebble and began to scratch the ground so as to let the water off into the street. While she was scratching, Malasha came up and began to help her. She picked up a chip and widened the rill.','Read the following passage and do the activities : ','1) How did the quarrel start?\n2) Did the people stop fighting?\n3) What did Akulka do?\n4) What did Malasha do?\n5) Change the words in the boxes to make other meaningful sentences :\n     i) I’ll take off may shoes and you do the same.\n     ii) This is a time for rejoicing.','','1) Malasha bespattered Alkuka’s new dress, her nose and eyes. Akulka told her mother that Malasha had purposely did it. So Akulka’s mother grasped Malasha and gave her a knock. Malasha began to howl and her mother ran out of the house. When Malasha’s mother saw that she began to scold her neighbor and the quarrel began.\n2) People didn\'t stop their fighting eventhough the old woman was telling them to stop.\n3) Akulka wiped off her dress and went back to the puddle in the lane. She picked up a pebble and began to scratch the ground to let the water off into the street.\n4) While Akulka was scratching, Malasha came up and began to help her. She picked up a chip and widened the rill.\n5) i) I’ll put on my new dress and you do the same.\nii) This is a time for studying.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82701,564,'descriptive','3a',10,2,'Out of Text Book','After prayers in the Church, the two girls went to the puddle, where they showed their new garments to each other, and began to play. They wanted to plash in the water. The little girl started to go into the puddle with her shoes on, but the older girl said to her:\n\"Don\'t go, Malasha, your mother will scold you. I will take off my shoes, and you do the same.\"\nThe girls took off their shoes, raised their skirts, and walked through the puddle toward each other. Malasha stepped in up to her ankles, and said:\n\"It is deep, Akulka, I am afraid.\"\n\"Never mind,\" she replied, \"it will not be any deeper. Come straight toward me!\"\nThey came closer to each other. Akulka said: \"Malasha, look out, and do not splash it up, but walk softly.\"\nShe had barely said that when Malasha plumped her foot into the water and bespattered Akulka\'s new dress, and not only her dress, but also her nose and eyes. When Akulka saw the spots on her dress, she grew angry at Malasha, and scolded her, and ran after her, and wanted to strike her. Malasha was frightened and, seeing what trouble she had caused, jumped out of the puddle and ran home.\nAkulka\'s mother passed by; she saw her daughter\'s dress bespattered and soiled.\n\"Where, accursed one, did you get yourself so dirty?\"\n\"Malasha has purposely splashed it on me.\"\nAkulka\'s mother grasped Malasha and gave her a knock on the nape of her neck. Malasha began to howl, and her mother ran out of the house.','Read the following passage and do the activities :','Q.1) a) Where did the two girls go after prayers in the church?\n        b) Which mistakes did Malasha commit?\n2) a) Why did Akulka want to strike Malasha?\n    b) Why did Malasha run home?\n3) What did Akulka tell her mother?\n4) How did-Akulka\'s mother react at that time?\n5) Spot the names of body parts from the story. Add three other names of your own.\n','','1) a) After prayers in the church, the two girls went to the puddle.\nb) Malasha plumped her foot into the water and bespattered Akulka’s new dress.\n2) a) Malasha bespattered Akulka\'s new dress, her nose and eyes. That\'s why Akulka grew angry with Malasha and wanted to strike her.\nb) Akulka grew angry with Malasha after seeing the spots on her new dress. She scolded Malasha and ran after her. Malasha was frightened by this and ran home.\n3) Akulka told her mother that Malasha had purposely splashed the spots on her dress.\n4) Akulka\'s mother grasped Malasha and gave her a knock on the nape of her neck.\n5) head, foot, eyes, nose, neck, back, legs, hands, ears, shoulders, mouth.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82702,564,'descriptive','3a',10,2,'Out of Text Book','The peasants had begun to fight, just as the water went down the rill toward the place where the old woman was trying to separate the men. The girls ran, one from one side of the rill, the other from the other side.\n\"Look out, Malasha, look out!\" shouted Akulka.\nMalasha wanted to say something herself, but could not speak for laughter. The girls were running and laughing at a chip which was bobbing up and down the rill. They ran straight into the crowd of the peasants. The old woman saw them and said to the peasants:\n\"Shame on you before God, men! You have started fighting on account of these two girls, and they have long ago forgotten it: the dear children have been playing nicely together. They are wiser than you.\"\nThe men looked at the girls, and they felt ashamed. Then they laughed at themselves, and scattered to their farms.','Read the following passage and do the activities ','1) What was the old woman trying to do?\n2) Did the girls forget their quarrel?\n3) How can we say that?\n4) Why did the men feel ashamed?\n5) List the characters in the story and write their approximate ages.\n\n','','1) The old woman was trying to stop the fighting among the peasants. She was trying to tell them that it was Easter, time for rejoicing and not for making sin.\n2) Yes, the girls forgot their quarrel after some time.\n3) After sometime when the men were fighting, Akulka and Malasha began to talk and play with each other.\n4) When the old woman told peasants that they had started fighting on account of those two girls and they had long ago forgotton it and they had started playing nicely together. At that time the men looked at the girls and they felt ashamed.\n5) i) Akulka – 10, Malasha – 8, Akulaka’s Mother – 35, Malasha’s Mother – 32, Akulaka’s Grand-mother – 60','',0,0,0,NULL),(82703,565,'descriptive','2',10,2,'Out of Text Book','This particular journey that we are going to read about was actually a journey from China to our own country! It was made by the famous seventh century travellers Yuan Chwang.\nIn those days, travelling from China to India was not an easy rask – one had to travel thousands of miles on foot or horseback, crossing deserts, crossing snow-clad mountains, crossing strange, unfamiliar regions, using roads where bandits and robbers roamed – who would do it? But Yuan Chwang had a dream. He wanted to take Buddhist scriptures from India to his homeland in China. It was like a pilgrimage to him.','Read the following passage and complete the activity :','1) Complete the following sentences\ni) Yuan Chwang was ----------------------\nii) Yuan Chwang travelled from ------------- to --------\niii) Yoan Chewang’s dream was to ------------ to --------\n2) i) What was Yuan Chwang\'s dream?\nii) What is the novel about?\n3) Complete the following web : \nTravelling from China to India was difficult because \n      ↓                                 ↓                                 ↓\n\n----------              -------------------               -------------------\n4) i) From the passage find the opposite of : \na) difficult × --------------            b) familiar × -------------\nii) Find out the words that mean.\na) really             b) thieves ','','1) i) The famous seventh century traveller.\nii) China to India.\niii) To take Buddhist scriptures from India to China.\n2) i) Yuan Chwang wanted to take Buddhist Scriptures from India to his homeland in China.\n ii) The novel is about the famous pilgrimage undertaken by Yuan Chwang.\n3) i) One had to travel thousands of miles on foot or horseback.\nii) One had to cross deserts, snow-clad mountains and unfamiliar regions.\niii) One had to use roads where robbers roamed.\n4) i) a) easy        b) unfamiliar\nii) a) actually           b) robbers ','',0,0,0,NULL),(82704,565,'descriptive','2',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','Answer the following questions : \nA] Say whether the following sentences are right or wrong : \n1) The novel \'Journey to the West\' is about a journey to western countries like England and America.\n2) In the days of Yuan Chwang travelling from China to India was not an easy task.\n3) Yuan Chwang travelled to many parts of India.\n4) Yuan Chwang\'s way back home was relatively easy\n5) Gods and supernatural powers had helped Yuan Chwang in his quest.\n6) The three disciples were three saints.\n7) The three disciples have supernatural powers.\nB] List all the persons and characters mentioned in the story. Which of them are real? Which are imaginary?\n','','','A] 1) wrong           2) right             3) right             4) wrong            5) right       6) wrong             7) right\nB] Characters in the story : i) Yuan Chwan	 ii) Guanyin deity       iii) Monkey King         iv) Zu Bajji          v) Sha Wujing\nAmong these characters only Yuan Chwang is real character and remaining all are imaginary.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82705,565,'descriptive','2a',10,2,'Out of Text Book','This particular journey that we are going to read about was actually a journey from China to our own country! It was made by the famous seventh century traveller Yuan Chwang.\nIn those days, travelling from China to India was not an easy task - one had to travel thousands of miles on foot or horseback, crossing deserts, crossing snow-clad mountains, crossing strange, unfamiliar regions, using roads where bandits and robbers roamed - who would do it? But Yuan Chwang had a dream. He wanted to take Buddhist scriptures from India to his homeland in China. It was like a pilgrimage to him.','1) Complete the following sentences.\n     i. Yuan Chwang was ------------------\n     ii. Yuan Chwang travelled from --------- to ---------------\n     iii. Yoạn Chwang\'s dream was to -----------------------','2) Complete the following web :','3) From the passage find the opposites of :\n     a) difficult                 b) easy','1) i) The famous seventh century traveller.\n    ii) China to India.\n    iii) to take Buddhist scriptures from India to China.\n2) i) One had to travel thousands of miles on foot or horseback ii) One had to cross deserts, snow-clad mountains and unfamiliar regions. iii) One had to use roads where robbers roamed.\n3) a) easy              b) unfamiliar ','',0,1,0,NULL),(82706,565,'descriptive','2b',10,2,'Out of Text Book','The most powerful among the three disciples is Sun Wukong. Everything about him is extra- ordinary. He was born when winds blew over a huge stone egg on the Flower Fruit Mountain. He is able to transform himself in 72 different ways. Not only that but he can also transform each of his hair strands into any living or non-living thing of his choice. His \'As-you-wish-gold-banded cudgel\' is also magical. It can grow as big as a pillar supporting the sky, but at other times, it becomes as tiny as a needle. Then the Monkey King just tucks it away behind his ear. Sun Wukong can travel thousands of kilometres in just one somersault. He can walk through fire, travel under water and fly to any place at will. His body is as hard as a diamond. So no one and nothing can injure him. His \'golden-gaze-fiery eyes\' have x-ray vision. No one can deceive him.','1) Say whether the following sentences are true or false.\n     i. Sun Wukong was most powerful.\n    ii. Sun Wukong was born on the Flower Fruit Mountain.','2) Complete the following web :\n','3) Write the past tense forms of :\n     a) blow                b) grow','1) i) True             ii) True\n 2) i) Sun Wukong can transform himself in 72 different ways.\n     ii) He can walk through fire. \n     iii) He can travel under water\n     iv) His body was as hard as a diamond.\n3) a) blew                 b) grew\n','',0,1,0,NULL),(82707,565,'descriptive','3a',10,2,'Out of Text Book','The most powerful among the three disciples is Sun Wukong. Everything about him is extra- ordinary. He was born when winds blew over a huge stone egg on the Flower Fruit Mountain. He is able to transform himself in 72 different ways. Not only that but he can also transform each of his hair strands into any living or non-living thing of his choice. His \'As-you-wish-gold-banded cudgel\' is also magical. It can grow as big as a pillar supporting the sky, but at other times, it becomes as tiny as a needle. Then the Monkey King just tucks it away behind his ear. Sun Wukong can travel thousands of kilometres in just one somersault. He can walk through fire, travel under water and fly to any place at will. His body is as hard as a diamond. So no one and nothing can injure him. His \'golden-gaze-fiery eyes\' have x-ray vision. No one can deceive him.','Read the following passage and complete the activity : \nQ.1) Say whether the following sentences are true or false.\ni) Sun Wukong was most powerful.\nii) Sun Wukong was born on the Flower Fruit Mountain.\n','Q.2) i) Who’s the most powerful among the three disciples?\nii) Write any five features of Sun Wukong’s character that you like best.\n3) Complete the following web :\n','Q.4) Write the past tense forms of : \ni) blow             ii) grow             iii) choose           iv) fly','1) i) True           ii) False\n2) i) The most powerful among the three disciples was Sun Wukong.\nii) can walk through fire, can travel under water, can fly to any place at will, can grow as big as a pillar, can become as tiny as needle. \n3) i) Sun Wukong can transform himself in 72 different ways.\nii) He can walk through fire\niii)  He can travel under water \niv) His body was as hard as a diamond\n4) i) blew         ii) grew          iii) chose          iv) flew ','',0,1,0,NULL),(82708,565,'descriptive','3a',10,2,'Out of Text Book','','Answer the following questions : \nA] Read the statements on the chit and think on it. Say whether each one is historical or fictional :\n1) Indian merchants used to travel across the seas many centuries ago.\n2) Sindbad, the sailor completed seven voyages.\n3) Neil Armstrong landed on the moon in the 20th century.\n4) Alladdin could fly on his magic carpet.\n5) Alexander the great conquered a number of counties before he came to India.\n6) Gulliver met very tiny people in Lilliput and giants in the country of Brobdingnag.\n7) There\'s a man in the moon who watches what\'s going on the earth.\n8) Emperor Ashoka\'s Empire stretched from the modern day Afghanistan to Bangladesh.\nB] i) Can you think of other words starting with \'folk\'?\n    ii) Write the opposites of the following :\n        a) Unsafe × --------                     b) Unimportant × --------------\n','','','i) Fictional               ii) Historical    \nAns. : A] 1) Historical         2) Fictional               3) Historical             4) Fictional      5) Historical             6) Fictional             7) Fictional               8) Historical    \nB] i) folksong, folkdance, folklore, folkliterature.\n     ii) a) safe              b) important\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(82709,567,'descriptive','2',10,2,'Out of Text Book','The Sun, after hos morning dip in the river\nDressed up in his golden muslin turban\nWaits and smiles on one side of the road,\nFor children are going to school.\nThrough the green-topped branches,\nBreezes sing their songs of blessings.\nFragrant Flowers awaken the sleepy roads\nWith their melodies.\nAt the corner of the lane,\nThe Peepal in his lush deep foliage \nWaves his hands','A] Read the following extract and complete the activity : -------------- 5M\n1) Complete the following sentences.\ni) The sun is dressed up in ----------------\nii) The children are -------------------\niii) The trees have ---------------\niv) The peepal tree is at --------------\n','2) Match the following parts to make meaningful sentences\n              A                                                B\ni) The Sun                                 a) waits and smiles \nii) The breezes                        b) sing their songs\niii) Fragrant flowers               c) waves his hands\niv) The Peepal                         d) awaken the sleepy roads\n3) From the extract find the words that rhyme with.\ni) code             ii) pool             iii) power               iv) cart\nB] Answer the following questions : ------------------ 5M\n     1) Find at least two phrases from the poem that indicate the following : \n         i) It is an early morning \n        ii) The atmosphere is pleasant.','','A] 1) i) ---------- his golden muslin turban.\nii) ------------- going to school\niii) ------------ green topped branches\niv) ------------ at the corner of the lane.\n2) i – a, ii – b, iii – d, iv – c \n3) i) road           ii) school            iii) hour            iv) heart \nB] i) a) Morning light spreads over the earth.\nb) The sun, after his morning dip in the river dressed up in his golden muslin turban.\n ii) a) Breezes sing their songs of blessings.\n      b) Fragrant flowers awaken the sleepy roads with their melodies.','',0,0,0,NULL),(82710,567,'descriptive','2a',5,2,'Out of Text Book','The Sun, after his morning dip in the river \ndressed up in his golden muslin turban \nwaits and smiles on one side of the road, \nFor children are going to school.\nThrough the green-topped branches, \nBreezes sing their songs of blessings.\nFragrant Flowers awaken the sleepy roads \nwith their melodies. \nAt the corner of the lane, the Peepal in his lush deep foliage \nwaves his hands','1) Complete the following sentences.\n     i. The sun is dressed up in ------------------------------------\n     ii. The children are -----------------------------------------------','2) Match the following parts to make meaningful sentences.\n<table border=\"1\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width:fit-content;\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n  <tr>\n    <th>A</th>\n    <th>B</th>\n  </