n of 5 nouns : surgery →','','','surgery → youth → happiness → strength → health','',0,0,0,NULL),(94644,2968,'descriptive','1',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Pick out the antonyms of the following words from those given in bracket : simple, increased\n[successful, complicated, reduced, invasive, separate]\n','','','simple × complicated\nincreased × reduced\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(94645,2968,'descriptive','1',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Arrange the following words in alphabetical order\ndramatically, mortality, disorders, magnified.\n','','','disorders, dramatically, magnified, mortality.','',0,0,0,NULL),(94646,2968,'descriptive','1',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Find out four hidden words from the word \'technology\': (Each word should have at least 4 letters.)','','','technology: loot, tool, note, hole','',0,0,0,NULL),(94647,2968,'descriptive','1',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Use \'through\' and its homophone in a single sentence.','','','The little boy <u>threw</u> the ball <u>through</u> the window.','',0,0,0,NULL),(94648,2968,'descriptive','1',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Rewrite sentence: as an affirmative\nThe doctors had to cut open the part of the body that was not healthy.\n','','','The doctors had to cut open the part of the body that was unhealthy.','',0,0,0,NULL),(94649,2968,'descriptive','1',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Pick out the verb from the given sentence and state its tense and aspect :\nThese have made such operations successful.\n','','','verb - have made; tense - present; aspect – perfect','',0,0,0,NULL),(94650,2968,'descriptive','1',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Rewrite the sentence using the modal auxiliary \'can\':\nOur surgeons are able to perform a growing number of complex surgical procedures.','','','Our surgeons <u>can</u> perform a growing number of complex surgical procedures.','',0,0,0,NULL),(94651,2968,'descriptive','1',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','Pick out the nouns from the sentence:\nPatients can recover from cardiac surgery faster than they did before