्ट करा : प्रकाशवर्ष ','','','एक प्रकाशवर्ष म्हणजे प्रकाशाने एका वर्षात पार केलेले अंतर होय.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95509,2217,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','संज्ञा स्पष्ट करा : तांबडा राक्षसी तारा ','','','ताऱ्यांच्या उत्क्रांती दरम्यान त्याचे मोठ्या प्रमाणात प्रसरण होते व त्यांचा आकार १०० ते २०० पटीने वाढतो. ह्या अवस्थेला तांबडा राक्षसी तारा म्हणतात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95510,2217,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','संज्ञा स्पष्ट करा : कृष्ण विवर ','','','जेव्हा ताऱ्यातून प्रकाशसुद्धा बाहेर पडू शकत नाही. तान्यावर पडलेला प्रकाश शोषला जातो.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95511,2217,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','आकाशगंगेला तिच्या केंद्रातून जाणाऱ्या अक्षावर परिवलन करणयास किती वर्षे लागतात ?','','','2 × 10<sup>8</sup> वर्षे लागतात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95512,2217,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','M<sub>sun</sub>  म्हणजे काय ?','','','ताऱ्यांचे वस्तुमान मोजताना ते सूर्याच्या सापेक्ष मोजले जाते. म्हणजे सूर्याचे वस्तुमान हे एकक घेतले जाते.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95513,2217,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','अल्फा सेंटॉरीस या ताग्यापासून प्रकाशा आपल्यापर्यंत येण्यास किती वर्षे लागतात ?','','','4.2 वर्षे लागतात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95514,2217,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','वायुगोल आकुंचित झाल्यास वायूचे तापमान का वाढते ?','','','गुरुत्व स्थितिज ऊर्जेचे उष्णतेत रूपांतर होते.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95515,2217,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','सूर्य बिंदूरूप केव्हा होईल ?','','','सूर्यात वायूचा दाब नसेल तर गुरुत्वीय बलामुळे १ ते २ तासात संपूर्णपणे आकुंचित होऊन बिंदुरूप होईल.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95516,2217,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','ताऱ्यांची निर्मिती कशी होते ?','','','आंतरतारकीय मेघ आकुंचित होऊन ताऱ्यांची निर्मिती होते.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95517,2217,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','ताऱ्यांची उत्क्रांती कशामुळे होते ?','','','ताऱ्यांची उत्क्रांती म्हणजे त्याचे वेगवेगळ्या अवस्थेत रूपांतर होण्याची प्रक्रिया.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95518,2217,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','ताऱ्यांच्या तीन अंतिम अवस्था कोणत्या ?','','','i) श्वेत बटू            (ii) न्युट्रॉन तारा            (iii) कृष्णविवर ह्या तीन अंतिम अवस्था आहेत.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95519,2217,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','कृष्णविवर हे नाव कशामुळे पडते ?','','','ताऱ्यांवर प्रकाश पडल्यानंतर तो शोषला जातो त्यामुळे एक अतिसूक्ष्म काळे छिद्र दिसते, त्याला कृष्णविवर म्हणतात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95520,2217,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','न्युट्रॉन तारा ही कोणत्या प्रकारच्या ताऱ्यांची अंतिम स्थिती असते ?','','','महाराक्षसी ताऱ्यांची महाविस्फोटानंतरची अंतिम स्थिती म्हणजे न्युट्रॉन तारा होय.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95521,2217,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','टीपा लिहा : ताऱ्यांची निर्मिती ','','','दीर्घिकातील ताऱ्यांच्यामध्ये असलेल्या रिक्त जागात वाळू व धुळीचे प्रचंड मेघ सापडतात, त्यांना आंतरतारकीय मेघ म्हणतात. मोठी अंतरे मोजण्यासाठी शास्त्रज्ञ प्रकाशवर्ष हे एकक वापरतात. आंतरतारकीय मेघांचा आकार काही प्रकाशवर्षे इतका असतो. म्हणजे प्रकाशाला या मेघांच्या एका टोकापासून दुसऱ्यापर्यंत जाण्यास काही वर्षे लागतात. एखाद्या विक्षोभामुळे हे आंतरतारकीय मेघ आकुंचित होऊ लागतात. या आकुंचनामुळे त्यांची घनता वाढत जाते, तसेच तापमानही वाढते. त्यातून एक तप्त वायूचा गोल निर्माण होतो. तापमान व घनता पुरेसे वाढल्यानंतर अणुऊर्जा निर्मिती सुरू होते. या ऊर्जानिर्मितीमुळे हा वायूचा गोल स्वयंप्रकाशित होतो. म्हणजे ह्या प्रक्रियेतून एक तारा निर्माण होतो किंवा ताऱ्यांचा जन्म होतो. एका विशाल आंतरतारकीय मेघाच्या आकुंचनातून एकाच वेळेस अनेक तारे निर्माण होतात.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95522,2217,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','टीपा लिहा : ताऱ्यांची उत्क्रांती','','','ताऱ्यांची उत्क्रांती म्हणजे काळ्राप्रमाणे तान्याच्या गुणधर्मात बदल होऊन त्याचे वेगवेगळ्या अवस्थात रूपांतर होण्याची प्रक्रिया होय. ताऱ्यांच्या जीवनात उत्क्रांती अतिशय संथ गतीने होते. तारे सातत्याने ऊर्जा देत असल्याने त्यातील ऊर्जा घटत असते. तान्याचे स्थैर्य राहण्यासाठी वायूचा दाब व गुरुत्वीय बदल यांचा समतोल राहण्यासाठी तान्याचे तापमान स्थिर राहणे आवश्यक असते. ताऱ्यांच्या उत्क्रांतीचे कारण त्याच्या केंद्रातील इंधन जळणे व त्याचे परिणाम कमी होणे. केंद्रातील इंधन संपुष्टात आल्यावर ऊर्जानिर्मितीही संपुष्टात येते. ताय्याचे तापमान कमी होते. त्यामुळे दाब कमी होऊन गुरुत्वबलाशी संतुलन रहात नाही. गुरुत्वीय बदल वायूच्या दाबापेक्षा अधिक होते. व तारा आकुंचित होतो. यामुळे केंद्रातील इंधने वापरली जातात. ही इंधने वापरणे ताऱ्यांच्या वस्तुमानावर अवलंबून असते. सर्व इंधने संपल्यावर ऊर्जानिर्मिती संपते. तसेच ताऱ्यांचे तापमान कमी होत जाते.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95523,2217,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','टीपा लिहा : ताऱ्यांचे स्थैर्य ','','','ताऱ्यांचे स्थैर्य कायम राहणे म्हणजे वायूचा दाब व गुरुत्वीय बल यांत समतोल राहण्यासाठी ताऱ्यांचे तापमान स्थिर असणे आवश्यक आहे. तापमान स्थिर राहण्यासाठी ताऱ्यांत ऊर्जानिर्मिती होणे आवश्याक आहे. ही ऊर्जानिर्मिती ताय्यांच्या केंद्रातील इंधन जळण्याने होते. ताऱ्यांची उत्क्रांती केंद्रातील इंधन जळणे व त्याचे परिणाम कमी होणे हे आहे. केंद्रातील इंधन संपुष्टात आल्यावर ऊर्जानिर्मिती संपुष्टात येते. ताऱ्यांचे तापमान कमी होते. वायूचा दाब कमी होतो व तो गुरुत्वीय बलाशी संतुलन राखू शकत नाही. गुरुत्वीय बल वायूच्या दाबापेक्षा अधिक असल्याने तारा आकुंचित होतो. यामुळे दुसरे इंधन वापरात येते व ऊर्जानिर्मिती पुन्हा सुरू होते. इंधन संपूर्ण संपल्यानंतर ऊर्जानिर्मिती संपते. उत्क्रांती थांबून अंतिम अवस्था येते. कारण तापमान कमी होत गेल्यावरही हे दाब स्थिर राहतात, त्यामुळे तान्याचे स्थैर्य कायम राहू शकते.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95524,2217,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','ताऱ्यांची अंतिम अवस्था दाखविणारा तक्ता तयार करा.','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(95526,2217,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','सूर्याच्या वायू गुणधर्माचा तक्ता पूर्ण करा.','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(95527,2217,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','सूर्याचा आकार व तापमानाचा तक्ता तयार करा.\nपर्याय - 4.5, 1.5 × 10⁷ K, 5800 K, 695700 km, 2 × 10³⁰ kg, 5920 K','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(95528,2217,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','तक्ता पूर्ण करा.\n<table border=\"1\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width:fit-content; text-align:left;\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n\n  <tr style=\"background-color:#e6f3ff; text-align:center;\">\n    <th>ताऱ्यांचे मूळ वस्तुमान</th>\n    <th>ताऱ्यांची अंतिम अवस्था</th>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td>(i) &lt; 8M<sub>sun</sub></td>\n    <td>..............</td>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td>(ii) 8 ते 25M<sub>sun</sub></td>\n    <td>................</td>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td>(iii) &gt; 25M<sub>sun</sub></td>\n    <td>..................</td>\n  </tr>\n\n</table>','','','<table border=\"1\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width:fit-content; text-align:left;\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n\n  <tr style=\"background-color:#e6f3ff; text-align:center;\">\n    <th>ताऱ्यांचे मूळ वस्तुमान</th>\n    <th>ताऱ्यांची अंतिम अवस्था</th>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td>(i) &lt; 8M<sub>sun</sub></td>\n    <td>श्वेत बटू</td>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td>(ii) 8 ते 25M<sub>sun</sub></td>\n    <td>न्युट्रॉन तारा</td>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td>(iii) &gt; 25M<sub>sun</sub></td>\n    <td>कृष्ण विवर</td>\n  </tr>\n\n</table>','',0,0,0,NULL),(95529,2217,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','फरक स्पष्ट करा : Mₛₜₐᵣ < 8Mₛᵤₙ व  8Mₛᵤₙ < Mₛₜₐᵣ < 25Mₛᵤₙ','','','<table border=\"1\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width:fit-content; text-align:left;\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n\n  <tr style=\"background-color:#e6f3ff; text-align:center;\">\n    <th>M<sub>star</sub> &lt; 8M<sub>sun</sub></th>\n    <th>8M<sub>sun</sub> &lt; M<sub>star</sub> &lt; 25M<sub>sun</sub></th>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td>(i) ताऱ्यांचे मोठ्या प्रमाणात प्रसरण होते.</td>\n    <td>(i) हा तारा महाराक्षसी ह्या अवस्थेतून जातो.</td>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td>(ii) आकार १०० ते २०० पटीने वाढतो.</td>\n    <td>(ii) आकार १००० पटीने वाढतो.</td>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td>(iii) उत्क्रांतीच्या शेवटी ह्या ताऱ्याचा विस्फोट होतो.</td>\n    <td>(iii) महाविस्फोट होतो. खूप शक्तिशाली असतो त्यामुळे दिवसा दिसू शकतो.</td>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td>(iv) आवरण बाहेर फेकल्याने आकुंचन पावतो.</td>\n    <td>(iv) केंद्रातील भाग आकुंचित होऊन 10 km च्या जवळपास येतो.</td>\n  </tr>\n\n</table>','',0,0,0,NULL),(95531,2217,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Text Book','','तुम्ही जर सूर्य असाल तर तुमचे गुणधर्म स्वतःच्या शब्दात लिहा.','','','(i) मी एक सामान्य तारा आहे.\n(ii) मी तप्त वायूचा गोल आहे.\n(iii) माझ्या केंद्रात 72% हायड्रोजन, 26% हेलियम, 2% इतर मूलद्रव्ये अणूच्या रूपात आहेत.\n(iv) माझे वस्तुमान 2 × 10³⁰ kg.\n(v) त्रिज्या 695700 km आहे.\n(vi) माझे तापमान 1.5 × 10⁷ K आहे.\n(vii) माझे वय 4.5 अब्ज वर्षे आहे.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95532,2217,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','ताऱ्यांचे गुणधर्म लिहा.','','','(i) रात्री आकाशात आपण तारे डोळ्यांनी पाहू शकतो.\n(ii) सूर्य हा एक सामान्य तारा आहे.\n(iii) तारे हे तप्त वायूचे प्रचंड गोल आहेत.\n(iv) सूर्यापेक्षा कमीअधिक प्रमाणात वस्तुमान व तापमान असेलेले अब्जावधी तारे आकाशात आहेत.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(95533,2217,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','शास्त्रीय कारणे लिहा : ग्रह व ताऱ्यांव्यतिरिक्त इतर घटक दुर्बिणीतून दिसतात','','','(i) अनेक दुर्बिणी पृथ्वीच्या पृष्ठभागावर ठेवलेल्या असतात.\n(ii) पृथ्वीच्या वायुमंडलावर असल्याने प्रभावीपणे खगोलीय वस्तूंचे निरीक्षण करता येते. म्हणून ग्रह व ताऱ्या व्यतिरिक्त इतर घटक दुर्बिणीतून दिसतात.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(95534,2217,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','शास्त्रीय कारणे लिहा : सूर्याच्या वस्तुमानाच्या ८ पटीहून कमी वस्तुमान असलेल्या Mₛₜₐᵣ < 8Mₛᵤₙ ताऱ्याला तांबडा राक्षसी तारा म्हणतात.','','','(i) ताऱ्यांचे उत्क्रांतीदरम्यान त्यांचे प्रसरण होऊन त्यांचा आकार १०० ते २०० पटीने वाढतो.\n(ii) तसेच त्यांचे तापमान कमी झाल्याने तो लालसर दिसू लागतो.\n(iii) त्यांच्या मोठ्या आकारामुळे व लालसर दिसत असल्याने Mₛₜₐᵣ < 8Mₛᵤₙ ताऱ्याला तांबडा राक्षसी तारा म्हणतात.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(95535,2217,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','श्वेत बटूबद्दल माहिती लिहा.','','','तांबङ्या राक्षसी ताऱ्यांच्या उत्क्रांतीच्या शेवटी या ताऱ्यांचा विस्फोट होतो. ताऱ्यांचे बाहेरील आवरण दूर फेकले जाते. आतील भाग आकुंचित होतो. या आतील भागाचा आकार साधारणपणे पृथ्वीच्या आकाराइतका होतो. पृथ्वीपेक्षा वस्तुमान अधिक व आकार पृथ्वीइतका म्हणून ताऱ्यांची घनता वाढते.\nत्यामुळे इलेक्ट्रॉनमुळे निर्माण झालेला दाब तापमानावर अवलंबून असत नाही व तो ताऱ्यांच्या गुरुत्वीय बलास अनंतकाळापर्यंत संतुलित करण्यास पुरेसा असतो. या अवस्थेत तारे श्वेत दिसतात व त्यांच्या लहान आकारामुळे ते श्वेत बटू म्हणून ओळखले जातात. त्यानंतर तापमान कमी होत जाते. परंतु आकार व वस्तुमान अनंतकाळपर्यंत स्थिर राहतात म्हणून ही बटू अवस्था अंतिम अवस्था असते. श्वेत बटूची घनता जास्त असते. त्यातील एक चमचा पदार्थाचे वजन सुमारे काही टन असेल.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(95536,2217,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Text Book','','ताऱ्यांच्या मूळ वस्तुमानाप्रमाणे त्यांच्या उत्क्रांतीचे तीन मार्ग आहेत, हे स्पष्ट करा.','','','ताऱ्यांची उत्क्रांती म्हणजे काळाप्रमाणे ताऱ्यांच्या गुणधर्मात बदल होऊन त्यांच्या वेगवेगळ्या अवस्थांत रूपांतर होण्याची प्रक्रिया. यानुसार आपण ताऱ्यांना तीन गटात विभागतो. एका गटातील सर्व ताऱ्यांचा उत्क्रांतीचा मार्ग व त्यांची अंतिम स्थिती एकसमान असते. \n(i) सूर्याच्या वस्तुमानाच्या ८ पटीहून कमी मूळ वस्तुमान असलेल्या ताऱ्यांची अंतिम अवस्था (Mₛₜₐᵣ < 8Mₛᵤₙ)\n(ii) सूर्याच्या वस्तुमानाच्या ८ ते २५ पट वस्तुमान असलेल्या ताऱ्यांची अंतिम अवस्था (8Mₛᵤₙ < Mₛₜₐᵣ < 25Mₛᵤₙ)\n(iii) सूर्याच्या वस्तुमानाच्या २५ पटीहून अधिक वस्तुमान असलेल्या ताऱ्यांची (Mₛₜₐᵣ > 25Mₛᵤₙ) अंतिम अवस्था होय.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(95537,2217,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Out of Text Book','','नामनिर्देशित आकृती काढा : विविध ताऱ्यांच्या आकाराची तुलना','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(95538,2217,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','नामनिर्देशित आकृती काढा : वस्तुमानाप्रमाणे ताऱ्यांची उत्क्रांती व त्यांच्या अंतिम अवस्था','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(95539,2217,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','ताऱ्यांचे स्थैर्य कायम राहण्यासाठी म्हणजे वायूचा .........  व गुरुत्वीय ........... यात समतोल राखण्यासाठी ताऱ्यांचे ........... स्थिर राहणे आवश्यक असते. ह्यासाठी ............ निर्मिती होणे आवश्यक असते. ताऱ्यांच्या उत्क्रांतीचे कारण त्या केंद्रातील ............. व त्याचे परिमाण ............. होणे.','परिच्छेद पूर्ण करून पुन्हा लिहा.\n(कमी, इंधन जळणे, ऊर्जा, तापमान, बल, दाब, आकुंचित होणे, हायड्रोजन)\n','','','ताऱ्यांचे स्थैर्य कायम राहण्यासाठी म्हणजे वायूचा दाब व गुरुत्वीय बल यात समतोल राखण्यासाठी ताऱ्यांचे तापमान स्थिर राहणे आवश्यक असते. ह्यासाठी ऊर्जा निर्मिती होणे आवश्यक असते. ताऱ्यांच्या उत्क्रांतीचे कारण त्या केंद्रातील इंधन जळणे व त्याचे परिमाण कमी होणे.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95540,2217,'descriptive','3',3,2,'Out of Text Book','','दिलेल्या आकृतीवरून दीर्घिकेबद्दल माहिती लिहा.','','','खालील आकृती चक्राकार दीर्घिकेची आहे. आपली सूर्यमाला ही एका दीर्घिकेत म्हणजेच आकाशगंगेत सामावलेली आहे. दीर्घिका हा अब्जावधी तारे, त्यांच्या ग्रहमालिका व ताऱ्यांमधील रिकाम्या जागेत आढळणाऱ्या आंतरतारकीय मेघांचा समूह असतो. आपण दीर्घिका तीन प्रकारात विभागू शकतो. (i) चक्राकार (ii) लंबगोलाकार व (iii) अनियमित आकाराच्या दीर्घिका. आपल्या आकाशगंगेत सुमारे 10¹¹ तारे आहेत.','',1,0,0,NULL),(95541,2217,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','खालील आकृती वरून प्रश्नांची उत्तरे लिहा.','(१) वरील आकृती कोणती आहे ?\n(२) ह्या मेघाचे नाव लिहा.\n(३) ह्या मेघातून तप्त वायूचा गोल कसा तयार होतो ?\n(४) हा गोल स्वयंप्रकाशीत कसा होतो ?\n(५) सूर्यामध्ये ही क्रिया कशी घडते ?\n','','१) हबल दुर्बिणीने टिपलेले अशा मेघांचे एक प्रकाशचित्र दाखविले आहे.\n२) ह्या मेघाचे नाव आंतरतारकीय मेघ आहे.\n३) एखाद्या विक्षोभामुळे हे आंतरतारकीय मेघ आकुंचित होऊ लागतात. या आकुंचनामुळे त्याची घनता वाढत जाते व तसेच त्याचे तापमानही वाढत जाते व त्यामधून तप्त वायूचा गोल तयार होतो.\n४) ह्या गोलाच्या केंद्रातील तापमान व घनता पुरेसे वाढल्यावर तेथे अणुऊर्जा निर्मिती सुरु होते. या ऊर्जानिर्मितीमुळे हा वायूचा गोल स्वयंप्रकाशित होतो.\n५) सूर्यात ही ऊर्जा हायड्रोजनच्या केंद्रकांचे एकत्रीकरण होऊन हेलिअमचे केंद्रक तयार होणे या प्रक्रियेतून उत्पन्न होते. म्हणजे सूर्याच्या केंद्रभागातील हायड्रोजन हा इंधनाचे कार्य करतो.\n','',1,0,0,NULL),(95542,2217,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','ताऱ्यांची अंतिम स्थिती याचे सविस्तर वर्णन करा.','','','ताऱ्यांचे वस्तुमान जितके अधिक तितक्या जलद गतीने त्याची उत्क्रांती होते. तान्यांच्या उत्क्रांतीत टप्याटप्याने येणाऱ्या अवस्था म्हणजे ताऱ्यांच्या उत्क्रांतीचा मार्ग हा देखील ताऱ्यांच्या वस्तुमानावर अवलंबून असतो.\nताऱ्यांमधून होणारी ऊर्जानिर्मिती बंद झाल्यावर तापमान कमी होते. वायूचा दाब कमी होतो व तारा आकुंचित होऊन त्याची घनता वाढत जाते. ह्याच वेळेला असे दाब निर्माण होतात जे तापमानावर अवलंबून असत नाही त्यामुळे तापमान कमी झाले तरी ते स्थिर राहतात. त्यामुळे ताऱ्यांचे स्थैर्य राहते व हीच ताऱ्यांची अंतिम अवस्था ठरते. ताऱ्याच्या मूळ वस्तुमानाप्रमाणे त्यांच्या उत्क्रांतीचे तीन मार्ग आहेत. त्यानुसार आपण ताऱ्यांची विभागणी तीन गटात करू शकतो. \n(i) सूर्याच्या वस्तुमानाच्या 8 पटीहून कमी मूळ वस्तुमान असलेल्या ताऱ्यांची (Mₛₜₐᵣ < 8Mₛᵤₙ) अंतिम अवस्था\n(ii) सूर्याच्या वस्तुमानाच्या 8 ते 25 पट वस्तुमान (8Mₛᵤₙ < Mₛₜₐᵣ < 25Mₛᵤₙ) असलेल्या ताऱ्यांची अंतिम अवस्था\n(iii) सूर्याच्या वस्तुमानाच्या 25 पटीहून अधिक वस्तुमान असलेल्या ताऱ्यांची (Mₛₜₐᵣ > 25Mₛᵤₙ) अंतिम अवस्था.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(95543,2217,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','ताऱ्यांच्या मूळ वस्तुमानाप्रमाणे त्यांच्या उत्क्रांतीचे तीन मार्ग स्पष्ट करा.','','','(i) Mₛₜₐᵣ < 8Mₛᵤₙ : या ताऱ्यांच्या उत्क्रांतीदरम्यान प्रसरण पावल्याने त्यांचा आकार 100 ते 200 पटीने वाढतो. या अवस्थेत त्यांना तांबडे राक्षसी तारे म्हणतात. उत्क्रांतीच्या शेवटी या ताऱ्यांचा विस्फोट होतो व त्यातून श्वेत बटू ह्या ताऱ्यांची निर्मिती होते. आकार व वस्तुमान अनंत काळपर्यंत स्थिर राहतात म्हणून ही बटू अवस्था या ताऱ्यांची अंतिम अवस्था असते.\n\n(ii) 8Mₛᵤₙ < Mₛₜₐᵣ < 25Mₛᵤₙ : हे तारे तांबडा राक्षसी तारा व नंतर महाराक्षसी तारा या अवस्थांमधून जातात. त्यांचा आकार 1000 पटीपर्यंत वाढतो. महाविस्फोट झाल्यावर केंद्रातील भाग आकुंचित होऊन त्याचा आकार 10 km च्या जवळपास येतो. या अवस्थेत ते पूर्णपणे न्युट्रॉनचे बनलेले असतात. न्यूट्रॉनमुळे निर्माण झालेला दाब तापमानावर अवलंबून नसतो. तो अनंत कालापर्यंत गुरुत्वीय बलाला संतुलित करण्यात सक्षम असतो. न्युट्रॉन तारे ही या ताऱ्यांची अंतिम अवस्था असते.\n\n(iii) Mₛₜₐᵣ > 25Mₛᵤₙ : महाविस्फोटानंतर कोणताही दाब त्याच्या प्रचंड गुरुत्वीय बलाशी समतोल राहू शकत नाही. तो सतत आकुंचित होत राहतो. त्याची घनता व गुरुत्वीय बल खूप अधिक वाढते. त्यामुळे ताऱ्याच्या जवळील सर्व वस्तू आकर्षित होतात. ताऱ्यातून काहीच बाहेर पडू शकत नाही. अगदी प्रकाश देखील बाहेर पडू शकत नाही. ताऱ्यावर पडलेला प्रकाश शोषला जातो. तो परावर्तित होत नाही. त्यामुळे ह्या ताऱ्याच्या स्थानावर एक काळे छिद्र दिसू शकते. त्याला कृष्णविवर म्हणतात. ही त्याची अंतिम अवस्था असते.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95544,2217,'descriptive','4',4,2,'Out of Text Book','','ताऱ्यांची जीवनयात्रा यावर संकल्पना चित्र तयार करा.','','','','',0,0,1,NULL),(95545,2217,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','दीर्घिका म्हणजे काय ?','','','दीर्घिका अब्जावधी तारे, ग्रहमालिका, आंतरतारकीय मेघांचा समूहु असतो.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95546,2217,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','आपाल्या सूर्यमालेत कोणकोणते घटक आहेत ?','','','आपल्या सूर्यमालेत तारे, ग्रह.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95547,2217,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','तारे व ग्रह यातील प्रमुख फरक कोणता ?','','','तारे स्वयंप्रकाशी आहेत व ग्रहांना स्वतःचा प्रकाश नसतो.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95548,2217,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Text Book','','उपग्रह म्हणजे काय ?','','','एखाद्या ग्रहाभोवती परिभ्रमण करणारी वस्तू किंवा ग्रह म्हणजे उपग्रह. उपग्रह दोन प्रकारचे असू शकतात. (i) नैसर्गिक (ii) कृत्रिम','',0,0,0,NULL),(95549,2217,'descriptive','1b',1,2,'Out of Text Book','','आपल्याला सर्वात जवळ असलेला तारा कोणता ?','','','आपल्या सर्वात जवळचा असलेला तारा म्हणजे सूर्य ','',0,0,0,NULL),(95550,2217,'descriptive','2',2,2,'Text Book','','संतुलित व असंतुलित बले म्हणजे काय?','','','संतुलित बल : वस्तूवर जेन्हा गुरुत्वाकर्षणीय बल व जमिनीकडून होणारी प्रतिक्रिया ही दोन्ही बले कार्यान्वित असून ती वस्तूला संतुलित करतात त्या बलाला संतुलित बल म्हणतात.\nअसंतुलित बल : वस्तूच्या गतीच्या दिशेने एकच बल कार्यरत असते त्यास असंतुलित बल असे म्हणतात.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(95666,712,'descriptive','5a',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','(A1 or A2) Do any one of the following activities :\n1) You are Sunit/Sunanina Patil, residing at 20, Cosmos Towers, J. B. Road, Airoli (West), Navi Mumbai – 400 700. Write any one letter as per the instructions given below.\n','','','A1. 20, Cosmos Towers\n      J. B. Road Airoli (West)\n      Navi Mumbai – 400 700\n     18th January, 2020\nDear Radhika, \nI hope you are doing well. Ever since you moved to Akola to pursue your MBBS, we haven\'t seen each other much. I hope that you have been able to adjust well to the new hostel life.\nI wish to share with you that I have recently got an offer to work as a Telemarketing Executive with Royalsity Corporation, Kharghar. Although this is a part-time position, it will help me to launch my career. My professional goal is to become a property salesperson in next five years and I look at this job as my professional baby-step. It will also help me to earn the much-needed pocket money while I complete my post-graduation. I shall be joining the company from 1st February.\nLet\'s meet when you come home for Deepavali, and let me treat you to a pizza lunch with my first salary. Take care.\nYours lovingly,\nSunaina \n                                                     OR\nA2.  20, Cosmos Towers\n        J. B. Road, Airoli (West)\n        Mumbai – 400 700\n        8th January, 2020\n       To \n       The Manager\n       Royalsity Corporation\n       Kharghar\n      Navi Mumbai – 410 715\nRef : Advertisement in ‘Darpan’ newspaper dated 7th January, 2020\nSubject : Application for the post of Telemarketing Executive at ‘Royalsity Corporation’\nRespected Sir,\nWith reference to the advertisement published in \'Darpan\' newspaper dated 7th January, 2020, I wish to apply for the post of a Telemarketing Executive in your renowned organisation.\nI am a 21 year old Commerce graduate from the University of Mumbai. I possess good fluency in Marathi, Hindi and English. I am enthusiastic and outgoing by nature. My multi-tasking abilities and problem-solving skills add to the communication skills that I possess. These personality traits can assist me in helping the customers of this organisation understand how to use the products made by it in a trouble-free manner. I also possess good listening skills and am familiar with various computer applications to further support me in my role in this organisation.\nI have attached my bio-data herewith for your kind perusal. Given the opportunity, I assure you that I will give my best to the organisation.\nYours faithfully, \nMs. Sunaina Patil\nEnclosed:\ni. Copy of B.Com Mark sheet and Passing certificate\nii. Copy of Bio-data ','',1,0,0,NULL),(95667,712,'descriptive','5a',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','(A1 or A2) Do any one of the following activities :\n8th March is celebrated as International Women’s Day. As Ronak Jain, write any one of the following letters based on the given instructions.\n','','','A1. \n103 – A Sunrise Society\nR. J. Road, Dadar (W)\nMumbai – 400 000\n12th March, 2019\n Dear Pranita,\n I hope this letter finds you in cheerful mood after your North India trip. I loved the scenic postcards that you sent me from Gulmarg!\nFor the past week, I was busy preparing for the Women\'s Day celebration at our school. It was a wonderful event, with Ms. Anuradha Desai, Senior Editor at \'Women\'s World\', speaking about the urgent need for ensuring women\'s safety in the today\'s world and Ms. Romila Khanna, an eminent historian, calling upon the society to strive and restore the high status given to women in ancient India. Thereafter, all of us at the school pledged to always respect the women in our lives.\nWe also had our share of fun! The cultural programme was a hit, as everyone enjoyed the skits and performances put up by the students. The school presented awards to five women from different fields, for their exceptional work. It was an exciting day indeed! I am keen to share more of this with you when we meet next. \nYours lovingly,\nRonak\n                                                                OR\nA2. Paramount Vidyalaya\n       15, Cross lane\n       E. F. Road, Dadar (W)\n       Mumbai – 400 000\n       20th February, 2019\n       To\n       The Director\n       Stree Foundation\n       Malabar Road, Bandra (W)\n       Mumbai – 400 007\n      Subject : Invitation to preside as the Chief Guest for the women’s Day celebration at Paramount Vidyalaya\nRespected Ma’am,\nI, Ronak Jain, the student representative of Paramount Vidyalaya, am writing this letter to you on behalf of my school.\nOur school celebrates and respects diversity in all its forms. And the women of all the different ethnicities from our country ought to be celebrated for their vibrant personalities. In keeping with this philosophy, each year, our school celebrates Women\'s Day on a large scale, by involving the local community. On this day, the women who have silently worked to uplift the society are awarded for their achievements. As someone who has done so much in the legal field for ensuring women\'s rights, it would be a pleasure to have you grace this occasion as the Chief Guest.\nThe function will be held on Friday, 8th March between 9:30 a.m. to 12:00 p.m. in our school auditorium. It would comprise of a prayer, speeches on the contribution of women in various fields, the prize distribution ceremony and a short cultural programme. We warmly invite you to grace this occasion and sincerely hope that you would take this invitation into consideration.\nYours sincerely,  \nRonak Jain   ','',1,0,0,NULL),(95669,712,'descriptive','5a',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','(A1 or A2) Do any one of the following activities :\nImagine you are Sanjay/Sanjana Bhosale from Room No. B/10, Sai Nagar, Purva Colony, Amravati. Now, attempt any one of the following letters after reading the advertisement.\n','','','A1. \nSanjana Bhosale\nRoom No. B/10, \nSai Nagar\nPurva Colony\nAmravati\n22nd July, 2021\nDear Rahul,\nHow are you? I hope you have completed the admission formalities at your college and settled comfortably in your hostel room. I would have written to you sooner but I, too, was busy with my own exams and submissions.\nRahul, I know that mom and dad have finally bought you the car of your dreams. I also know that you must be excited to drive it and looking for any reason to do so. While I am happy for you, I need to share a few things with you that you should always keep in mind.\nRemember that the only way to reach anywhere on time is to leave on time. You may feel that you can compensate for the time you have lost by over speeding or overtaking others but doing these things will only get you into even more trouble. Always wear your seatbelt, no matter how uncomfortable you find it, and never drink and drive. Always follow the \'you first\' rule and never use your mobile phone while driving. Lastly, always follow the traffic rules. Trust me, they have been made to make your life easier and not harder.\nI hope that you will remember everything I have mentioned and drive your car safely. Please take care of yourself and I\'ll visit during the Diwali vacations.\nYour loving sister, \nSanjana\n                                                OR\nSanjay Bhosale\nRoom No. B/10\nSai Nagar, Purva Colony\nAmravati\n22nd July, 2021\nTo\nThe Chief Traffic Controller\nTraffic Police Headquarters\nAmravati\nSubject : Thank you letter for poster regarding ‘Road Safety Week’.\nRespected Sir,\nI am writing this letter to thank you for the informative and appealing poster regarding \'Road Safety Week\' that has been put up on Rajiv Chowk. \nSir, first of all, allow me to congratulate you with respect to the content of the poster. All the points that have been mentioned are absolutely applicable and should be kept in mind by all road users. Secondly, the placement of the poster at Rajiv Chowk is also ideal as it is impossible to not notice the poster at this location. I would also like to inform you that the poster is proving to be truly useful to the citizens of Amravati since it serves as a regular reminder of the conduct that should be followed on the roads. In fact, quite a few people have told me that the first point in the poster, about leaving early, has helped them avoid last-minute troubles.\nI am now sure that under your leadership we will get to see even more such initiatives and I can assure you that citizens like me will make our apprecition known to you.\nThanking you.\nYours faithfully, \nSanjay Bhosale','',1,0,0,NULL),(95670,712,'descriptive','5a',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','(A1 or A2) Do any one of the following activities :\nImagine you are Sanjay/Sanjana Bhosale from Room No. B/10, Sai Nagar, Purva Colony, Amravati. Now, attempt any one of the following letters after reading the advertisement.\n','','','A1. \nSanjana Bhosale\nRoom No. B/10, \nSai Nagar\nPurva Colony\nAmravati\n22nd July, 2021\nDear Rahul,\nHow are you? I hope you have completed the admission formalities at your college and settled comfortably in your hostel room. I would have written to you sooner but I, too, was busy with my own exams and submissions.\nRahul, I know that mom and dad have finally bought you the car of your dreams. I also know that you must be excited to drive it and looking for any reason to do so. While I am happy for you, I need to share a few things with you that you should always keep in mind.\nRemember that the only way to reach anywhere on time is to leave on time. You may feel that you can compensate for the time you have lost by over speeding or overtaking others but doing these things will only get you into even more trouble. Always wear your seatbelt, no matter how uncomfortable you find it, and never drink and drive. Always follow the \'you first\' rule and never use your mobile phone while driving. Lastly, always follow the traffic rules. Trust me, they have been made to make your life easier and not harder.\nI hope that you will remember everything I have mentioned and drive your car safely. Please take care of yourself and I\'ll visit during the Diwali vacations.\nYour loving sister, \nSanjana\n                                                OR\nSanjay Bhosale\nRoom No. B/10\nSai Nagar, Purva Colony\nAmravati\n22nd July, 2021\nTo\nThe Chief Traffic Controller\nTraffic Police Headquarters\nAmravati\nSubject : Thank you letter for poster regarding ‘Road Safety Week’.\nRespected Sir,\nI am writing this letter to thank you for the informative and appealing poster regarding \'Road Safety Week\' that has been put up on Rajiv Chowk. \nSir, first of all, allow me to congratulate you with respect to the content of the poster. All the points that have been mentioned are absolutely applicable and should be kept in mind by all road users. Secondly, the placement of the poster at Rajiv Chowk is also ideal as it is impossible to not notice the poster at this location. I would also like to inform you that the poster is proving to be truly useful to the citizens of Amravati since it serves as a regular reminder of the conduct that should be followed on the roads. In fact, quite a few people have told me that the first point in the poster, about leaving early, has helped them avoid last-minute troubles.\nI am now sure that under your leadership we will get to see even more such initiatives and I can assure you that citizens like me will make our apprecition known to you.\nThanking you.\nYours faithfully, \nSanjay Bhosale','',1,0,0,NULL),(95671,713,'descriptive','5b',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','Dialogue writing/Drafting a speech :\nB1 or B2. Do any one of the following :\nB1. Dialogue writing :\ni. Put the sentences in the proper order to prepare a meaningful dialogue.\n    a) My favourite pastime is gardening.\n    b) Which book are you engrossed in?\n    c) I am engrossed in reading \'The Shadow of the Wind\'.\n    d) What is your favourite pastime?\nii. Complete the following dialogue :\n    Kanika : Are there any situations when you get afraid?\n    Varun : _______________________________\n    Kanika : How would you react if you had to travel alone?\n    Varun : _____________________________\niii. Write a dialogue of minimum three meaningful exchanges between Arijit, a college student, and a career counsellor, Ms. Ritika, about the additional skills required these days to start a career.\n                                              OR\nB2. Speech Writing :\n       You are going to participate in an Inter-school Elocution Competition arranged by your school. Write a speech on ‘Books are our Real Friends’ with the help of the following points :\n• Real friends\n• Treasures of knowledge\n• Personality development \n• Increase delivering speech ability and confidence\n• Leadership','','','B1.  i. d) What is your favourite pastime?\n           a) My favourite pastime is gardening.\n           b) Which book are you engrossed in?\n            c) I am engrossed in reading \'The Shadow of the Wind\'.\nii. Kanika : Are there any situations when you get afraid?\n    Varun : Yes, Kanika, I am afraid of seeing ghosts when I am al alone in the dark.\n    Kanika : How would you react if you had to travel alone?\n    Varun : Oh, it would be a delight to travel alone, as long as it’s not dark.\niii. Arijit : Hello, Ritika. Can you please guide on how I can start a career immediately after finishing my college?\nRitika : Sure, Arijit. I appreciate that you are keen on starting a career at the earliest. You will need certain skills apart from the learning obtained from your college course.\nArijit : Oh, I see! Which are those skills?\nRitika : Firstly, you need to know how to use a computer. You must learn MS Office and should know how to use the internet. You should also have a good command over spoken and written English communication.\nArijit : I already know the basics of MS Office and email correspondence and I have been good with communicating in English since childhood.\nRitika : That\'s great! Keep sharpening your skills and you can soon expect to get a job of your choice.\nB2.        Speech on ‘Books are our real friends’\nGood morning, respected judges, teachers and my dear friends! Today, I am here to speak on the topic \'Books are our real friends\'. This is true indeed, because books are a world in themselves. They are like friends you never want to leave. They are always there to comfort you in your hour of need. There is no better company than that of a good book. Books are a source of knowledge.\nThe ideas, concepts, adventures and experiences expressed in a book help expand our knowledge base. They are a world of priceless treasures. \nJust like the search for knowledge is endless, the number of books in the world is also innumerable. Books also help to build character. They help a person gain confidence and give them the courage to speak. They improve our language skills. Books develop our personality by helping us to form our own ideas, opinions and perspectives. They make us a better person with their rich and ethical content. \nThey encourage us to be a better version of ourselves. They help us build a new environment in which we can stay focused and lead a successful life. In conclusion, books can be our friends, philosophers and our truest guides. Thank you!','',0,0,0,NULL),(95672,713,'descriptive','5b',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','Dialogue writing/Drafting a speech :\nB1 or B2. Do any one of the following :\nB1. Dialogue writing :\ni. Prepare a dialogue from the jumbled sentences:\n   a) Have you watched today\'s Match?\n   b) Rohit Sharma hits the century.\n   c) Who scored century today?\n   d) Yes, I have.\nii. Complete the dialogue :\n    RIYA : Do you like singing?\n    PRIYA : ______________________\n    RIYA : Who is your favourite singer?\n    PRIYA : ___________________________ \niii. Write a dialogue between a headmaster and a student who has lost his/her bicycle from school campus. Write minimum three meaningful exchanges.\n                                            OR\nB2. Imagine that you are the general secretary of your school cultural committee. Write a speech on ‘The trees are our best friends’ with the help of the following points :\n• Trees gives us flowers, fruits, wood, shade and oxygen/\n• Trees maintain the balance of nature.\n• It is everyone’s responsibility to save trees.\n• Plant more trees, save more lives.\n• Add your own points.','','','B1. i. a) Have you watched today\'s Match?\n          d) Yes, I have.\n         c) Who scored century today?\n        b) Rohit Sharma hits the century.\nii. RIYA : Do you like singing?\n    PRIYA : Yes, I do like singing.\n    RIYA : Who is your favourite singer?\n    PRIYA : Lucky Ali is my favourite singer.\niii. Headmaster : Akhil, why do look so upset?\n     Akhil : Sir, I’m upset because I lost my bicycle from the school campus.\n     Headmaster : Oh, that’s sad! Do you remember where you had parked it when you came to school in the morning?\n     Akhil : Yes, sir. I had parked it in the bicycle stand at the back gate.\n      Headmaster : Okay. You don\'t worry. The back gate is always locked. There is no chance of someone stealing the bicycle from the school campus. I\'m sure we\'ll be able to find it. I\'ll send someone with you to help you find your bicycle.\n      Akhil : Thank you so much, Sir!\n                                             OR\nB2.               The Trees Are Our Best Friends\nGood morning, respected principal, teachers and my dear friends. I, Vijay Singh, general secretary of the cultural committee, am honoured to be here today to speak about the importance of trees. Trees are our best friends. They give us beautiful flowers, tasty fruits, useful wood, cool shade and invaluable oxygen. And, just like best friends, they expect nothing from us in return. Trees also maintain the balance of nature by improving the quality of air, saving water, saving soil and supporting wildlife. \nBut, how do we repay them for their kindness? We repay them by clearing entire forests of trees in a matter of days because we need more land. Friends, we need to understand that it is everyone\'s the rich and the powerful can solve this responsibility to save trees. We need to stop thinking that only problem. Because, repeatedly, we have seen the efforts of a single person make a huge difference. Perhaps, right now, we cannot see the harmful effects of not saving trees so we think that this would not affect us. But the truth is that, around 11,000 years ago, the Sahara Desert used to be a forest. It turned into a desert because we, humans, allowed our cattle to overgraze it. Thus, if we do not save trees, even the most fertile land will turn infertile and we would not be able to survive for a long time. So let us get into action, while we can, and save trees as well as ourselves. \nLet us all pledge to plant atleast one tree and build a better future. \nThank you.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95673,3070,'descriptive','6a',0,0,'Out of Text Book','','Information Transfer : (A1 or A2). Do any one of the following :\nA1. Non-verbal to Verbal\n      You have visited a tourist place. you liked it very much. use the points given in the table and write a paragraph.','A2. Verbal to Non – Verbal\nPrepare a tree diagram by using given information about vitamins :\nThere are in all four types of Vitamins: Vitamin A, B, C and D. You get vitamin A from milk, butter and eggs. Vitamin B is derived from meat and eggs. Fruits and vegetables will provide you with Vitamin C. Vitamin D can be obtained from fish oil and sunlight. A lack of any of the above vitamins may cause certain diseases and ailments. Lack of vitamin A may result in blindness. Insufficiency of Vitamin B gives rise to disorders of the nervous system. Insufficient supply of Vitamin C can cause skin diseases. Bone diseases are likely to occur in the absence of Vitamin D.\n','','A1.  Kolhapur – A traveller’s Paradise\nKolhapur is an important, historic city that can be reached by bus or train from all important places in Maharashtra. There are many dharmashalas and hotels in Kolhapur, where one can stay. Rajwada, Rankala Lake, Mahalakshmi Temple are some of the places of tourist interest. Panhala and Jyotiba are some other places located close by that can be visited. Kolhapuri chappals and ornaments are a must-buy when one visits Kolhapur. The best time to visit Kolhapur is November and December, when the climate is cool and pleasant.\nA2. ','',1,0,1,NULL),(95674,3070,'descriptive','6a',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','Information Transfer : (A1 or A2). Do any one of the following :\nA1. Non-verbal to Verbal\nRead the information given in the following table. Write two short paragraphs based on it. give a suitable title to it.\nNos.       Electrical Vehicles                            Non – Electric Vehicles\ni. 	Run on electric energy		         Run on fuels \nii.	Cause no pollution			         Cause air pollution\niii. 	Low maintenance/high mileage        High maintenance, low mileage\niv. 	Need good roads			          Can run on rough roads\nv.	Can run low speed			         Can run high speed\n                                       OR\nA2. Verbal to Non-verbal \nRead the following information and present it in the tree diagram given below. Give a suitable title to it :\nRocks are not all the same! The three main types, or classes of rocks they are sedimentary, metamorphic and igneous. Sedimentary rocks are formed from particles of sand, shells, pebbles and other fragments of material. Generally, sedimentary rock is fairly soft and may break apart or crumble easily. It is usually the only type that contains fossils. Examples of this rock type include conglomerate and limestone.\nMetamorphic rocks are formed under the surface of the earth from the change that occurs due to intense heat and pressure. The rocks that result from these processes often have ribbon like layers and may have shiny crystals, formed by minerals growing slowly over time, on their surface. Examples of this rock type include gneiss and marble.\nIgneous rocks are formed when magma cools and hardens. Sometimes the magma cools inside the earth, and other times it erupts onto the surface from volcanoes. When lava cools very quickly, no crystals form and the rock looks shiny and glasslike. Sometimes gas bubbles are trapped in the rock during the cooling process, leaving tiny holes and spaces in the rock. Examples of this rock type include basalt and obsidian.','','','A1. Difference between Electric and Non-Electric Vehicles\nVehicles are generally of two types - electric and non-electric. Electric vehicles run on electric energy and therefore, cause no pollution. These vehicles are low maintenance and give high mileage. However, electric vehicles need good roads to run properly and they tend to run at low speeds.\nNon-electric vehicles run on fuels, and are thus a major cause of air pollution. These vehicles give low mileage, but have a high maintenance cost. Such vehicles can easily run on rough roads and can even run at high speeds.  \nA2.  ','',1,0,1,NULL),(95675,3070,'descriptive','6a',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','Information Transfer : (A1 or A2). Do any one of the following :\nA1. Non-verbal to Verbal\n      The following diagram shows important factors to be considered while choosing a career. Write paragraph based on it. Give a suitable title to it : \n','A2. Verbal to Non-verbal\nRead the following statements and prepare a chart of \'Dos\' and \'Don\'ts\'. Suggest a suitable title for it.\nNature is abode for all of us. It provides us with all our basic needs. However, we must take care of the following things so that our mother nature is not harmed.\n• We must plant more trees.\n• We should not cut trees.\n• We must keep our area neat and clean.\n• We should never discharge garbage without proper management.\n• We should not pollute air and water.\n• We should not use plastic bags.\n• We should not hunt birds or animals.\n• We should use more of public transport.\n• We should spread awareness about the importance of maintaining balance in nature.','','A1. Choosing a Career\nThere are a number of factors that need to be considered while choosing a career. Firstly, a person must be skilled at the career they choose. For example, a person must be skilled at painting if they choose to be a painter. Secondly, a person must have the required abilities. For example, to paint, a person must have the ability to distinguish among the different shades of a colour, the ability to keep their hand steady etc.\nThirdly, they must have an interest in the career. For example, even if a person has the skills and abilities needed, he would not do well as a painter if he has no interest in painting. Also, personality traits need to be considered. For example, every painter is expected to exhibit their work at exhibitions and talk about it, mostly in front of complete strangers. And, if they do not have a confident personality they would not be able to do so. Next, financial gains need to be considered. If a person is not able to make money, sooner or later, they would have to change careers. Demand and future prospects are also equally important. For example, these days painters are learning to paint digitally because digital art is in demand and has better future prospects compared to traditional art. Lastly, a person\'s family\'s profession also influences their career as children often mimic their parents and follow their example.\nA2.  Guarding Nature','',1,0,1,NULL),(95676,3071,'descriptive','6b',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','Expand the theme : (B1 or B2). Do any one of the following :\nB1. 20 people suffered due to food poising in your locality last evening when they consumed sweets from a local sweetmeat vendor during a social gathering. Write a report describing the details of the incident based on the following headlines :','Include the following in your news report :\n• Headline 	                                 • Dateline\n• Introduction			• Short continuing paragraph\n                                     OR\nB2. Write a story based on the following beginning. Suggest a suitable title for it.\n      ‘Once a fishman went to the sea -----\'','','B1.                         Sweet Poison!\n                                                                  - Nehal Mishra, Student Reporter\nNavi Mumbai, January 29, 2020\n         20 people, including 7 children, 5 women and 8 men, fell ill on Tuesday, at a social gathering in Navi Mumbai, after consuming the free sweets distributed there. \nThe sweets were apparently bought from a local sweetmeat vendor, who had sold them at a very low price, to the organisers of the event. The affected people complained about severe dizziness and vomiting, immediately after they had consumed the sweets. Meanwhile, one of the organisers, who requested not to be named, apologised for the incident and assured that all medical expenses due to the incident would be borne by the organising committee of the event.\nThe affected people were taken to the nearby Manaswi Clinic to be treated. \"Food poisoning due stale and low quality mava to used in making sweetmeats seems to be the reason for the unfortunate incident,\" said Dr. Tiwari, who was treating the patients at the clinic.\nB2.  The Fisherman and The Mermaid\n        Once upon a time, a fisherman was at the sea, catching fish. Due to the bad weather, he was worried that the catch would be poor. While he was lost in thought, he felt something pulling at the fishing line.\nWhen he drew the line towards himself and saw a mermaid stuck to the hook of the fishing rod. She requested the fisherman to release her back into the sea in return for a reward. The fisherman carefully released the mermaid, without even asking what the reward was.\nThe mermaid swam back into water, surfaced back with a giant pearl, and handed it over to the fisherman. She told him he need not fish anymore, as he could live the rest of his life in luxury. He must, however, continue to do good all his life. The fisherman promised her that he would continue his good deeds.','',1,0,0,NULL),(95677,3071,'descriptive','6b',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','Expand the theme : (B1 or B2). Do any one of the following :\nRead the following headline and prepare a news report with the help of the given points :','Include the following in your news report :\n• Headline 	                                 • Dateline\n• Introduction			• Short continuing paragraph\n                                       OR\nB2. Develop a story with the help of the following beginning. Suggest a suitable title.\nOnce there was a poor farmer. He had three sons. They were --------','','B1.    Heavy rainfall disturbs the normal life in Marathwada\n                          - Miss Radhika Mehant, Student Reporter\nChatrapati SambhajiNagar, August 24, 2020\n           For the first time in the last 15 years, the entire region of Marathwada came to a halt. For the past two days, heavy rainfall in the region has made life difficult for its residents.\nCases of severe water-logging have been reported in several parts of the region. All outstation trains have been cancelled, which has created difficulties for the public. People have been advised to remain in their houses and only go outdoors in case of emergencies. No loss of life has been reported. However, the power cut, water-logging and traffic jams have caused many problems. During such times of crisis, both, government officials and the people have come forward to help one another. People welcomed others stuck in the rains, into their homes. Police stations around the region were kept open, so women and children could easily take shelter. \nRam Saxena, one of the many people stuck due to the rains, commented, \"Even in the middle of a crisis, our spirit is not lost.\"\nB2. Unity is Strength\n        Once there was a poor farmer. He had three sons. They were always fighting. So, one day, the farmer decided to teach them an important lesson about unity.\nHe called all three of his sons and gave them one stick each. He asked them to break the sticks. All three of them could easily break the sticks. Then, the farmer gave them a bundle of sticks to break. All three of them tried their best, but could not break the bundle of sticks. When they finally gave up, the farmer explained to them that they are just like the bundle of sticks; if they are separated then anyone can break them, but if they are together, then no one can tear them apart. There is strength in unity. \nThe three boys understood the lesson that their father tried to impart and they never fought again.','',1,0,0,NULL),(95678,3071,'descriptive','6b',0,0,'Out of Text Book','','Expand the theme : (B1 or B2). Do any one of the following :\nB1. Read the following headline and prepare a news report with the help of given points :','Make use the following guidelines :\n• Headline			• Dateline\n• Lead line			• Body of the report\n                                   OR\nB2. Develop a story using the following beginning. Give a suitable title.\n     Once upon a time, there lived a woodcutter in a small village. One day he went to the forest \n      ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n      -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------','','B1. 21 – Year – Old Mayur wins World Chess Championship\n                                  - By a staff Reporter \nMumbai, March 22, 2022\n          The name of Mayur More was recorded in the history books on Friday, the 18th of March, when the 21-year-old won the World Chess Championship held at Rhodes Island in Greece. \nThe young man made the nation proud by defeating his challenger, Sergey Karjakin of Russia, in a record time of 35 minutes, and a record 14 moves. Talking about his win, Mayur said that it was an incredible experience to play with the top players from across the globe. \"The only thing I kept telling myself was that I needed to trust my training and not make any silly mistakes. The rest would take care of itself,\" he said. \nMayur admitted that juggling chess and his college work took effort but added that, in the end, he could not have expected a better outcome. When asked what was next for the World Champion, Mayur said that he could not wait to go home and dive into his pile of unread fantasy novels.\nB2. The Honest Woodcutter\n       Once upon a time, there lived a woodcutter in a small village. One day he went to the forest to cut trees. All of a sudden, while he was cutting a tree, his axe slipped out of his hand and fell into the river. Since he had only one axe and without it, he would not be able to earn money, the poor woodcutter began to cry.\nUpon hearing him cry, the God of the river appeared before him and asked him what had happened. The woodcutter explained the problem and the God offered to look for his axe. He dived into the water and after a while, came out of the river with an axe made of gold. But the woodcutter told him that the axe was not his. So, the God dived into the river again and came out of the water with an axe made of silver. Once again, the woodcutter told him that the axe was not his. The God now dived into the river for the third time and came out with an axe made of iron with a handle made of wood. Upon seeing this axe, the woodcutter immediately exclaimed that the axe was his and thanked the God for bringing his axe back to him. Impressed with the woodcutter\'s honesty, the God gifted all three axes to him.','',1,0,0,NULL),(95679,3072,'descriptive','7',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','Translation :\ni. Translate the following words into your medium of instruction (any four)  ----  2M\n    a) responsibility             b) challenges                      c) international\n    d) professional		e) education			e) butterfly\nii. Translate the following sentences into your medium of instruction (any two) ---- 2M\n     a) He was no longer afraid. \n     b) He was near the sea now.\n     c) I don\'t know what\'s happening to Pipalnagar.\n     d) I hear they have stopped paying employees.\niii. Translate the following idioms/proverbs into your medium of instruction (any one) : ---------- 1M\n      a) Listen to advice, but follow your heart.\n       b) You fail only when you stop trying. ','','','i. a) जबाबदारी 	b) आव्हाने 		c) आंतरराष्ट्रीय \n    d) व्यावसायिक	e)  शिक्षण 		f) फुलपाखरू\nii. a) तो आता अजिबात घाबरत नव्हता.        \n     b) तो आता समुद्राजवळ आला होता.\n     c) पिपलनगरला काय झालं आहे ते मला खरंच माहीत नाही.\n      d) मी असं ऐकलं आहे, की त्यांनी कर्मचाऱ्यांना पगार देणे बंद केले आहे.\niii. a) ऐकावे जनाचे, करावे मनाचे.\n     b) तुम्ही तेव्हाच अपयशी होता जेव्हा तुम्ही प्रयत्न करणे थांबवता.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95680,3072,'descriptive','7',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','Translation :\ni. Translate the following words into your medium of instruction (any four)  ----  2M\n    a) neighbour		b) parrot		c) temple\n    d) conversation 		e) envious		f) greedy\nii. Translate the following sentences into your medium of instruction (any two) ---- 2M\n     a) I try and lead as normal a life as possible.\n   b) Dr Hawking firmly believes that in the next millennium, science will discover the core secrets of the universe.\n  c) \'Swami and Friends\' is a good read for children of all ages.\n  d) The initial plan for the dam\'s construction would have flooded the valley containing the Abu Simbel Temples.\niii. Translate the following idioms/proverbs into your medium of instruction (any one) : ---------- 1M\n      a) Hate cannot drive out hate; only love can do that.\n     b) Anyone who has never made a mistake has never tried anything new. ','','','i. a) शेजारी 		b) पोपट		c)  मंदिर \n    d) संभाषण	e)  मत्सरी 		f) हावरट\nii. a) मी जमेल तितके सामान्य जीवन जगण्याचा प्रयत्न करतो.\n     b) पुढील सहस्रकात विज्ञान विश्वातील मुख्य रहस्ये उलगडेल, यावर डॉ. हॉकिंग यांचा ठाम विश्वास आहे.\n    c) सर्वप्रकारच्या वयाच्या मुलांकरता \'Swami and Friends\' हे उत्तम वाचन आहे.\n    d) धरणाच्या बांधणीकरता तयार करण्यात आलेल्या मूळ योजनेमुळे दरी व त्यामधील मंदिरेही वाहून गेली असती.\niii. a) द्वेष द्वेषाला संपवू शकत नाही, ते फक्त प्रेमच करू शकते.\n     b) ज्यांनी कधीच चूक केली नाही त्यांनी कधीच काही नवीन करण्याचा प्रयत्न केला नाही.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95681,3072,'descriptive','7',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','Translation :\ni. Translate the following words into your medium of instruction (any four)  ----  2M\n    a) coward 			b) grief 		c) satisfaction \n    d) artist 			e) awareness	f) salt\nii. Translate the following sentences into your medium of instruction (any two) ---- 2M\n     a) Meena was transferred to Bombay and soon we all forgot about her. \n      b) I felt ashamed of myself.\n      c) That day, I decided to change my attitude towards life.\n       d) I find happiness in every small thing, in every situation and in every person. \niii. Translate the following idioms/proverbs into your medium of instruction (any one) : ---------- 1M\n      a) Save water, save earth.\n      b) Service to man is service to God.','','','i. a) मित्रास		b)  दुःख		c)  समाधान\n   d) कलाकार 	e) जागरूकता	f)  मीठ\nii. a) मीनाची मुंबईला बदली करण्यात आली आणि लवकरच आम्ही सगळे तिच्याबद्दल विसरलो.\n     b) मला स्वतःचीच लाज वाटली.\n     c) त्यादिवशी मी जीवनाबद्दलचा माझा दृष्टिकोन बदलायचा ठरवले.\n     d)  मी प्रत्येक लहान गोष्टीत, प्रत्येक परिस्थितीमध्ये आणि प्रत्येक व्यक्तीमध्ये आनंद शोधतो.\niii. a) पाणी वाचवा, वसुंधरा वाचवा\n     b) मानवसेवा हीच ईश्वरसेवा','',0,0,0,NULL),(95682,3072,'descriptive','7',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','Translation :\ni. Translate the following words into your medium of instruction (any four)  ----  2M\n    a) success 		b) happily 		c) habit\n    d) confidence 		e) universal		f) customer \nii. Translate the following sentences into your medium of instruction (any two) ---- 2M\n     a) The book was full of nice pictures.\n    b) But I will teach them all to fight for France.\n    c) The Curies now began to work with greater enthusiasm.\n   d) Overwork seriously affected Madame Curie\'s health.\niii. Translate the following idioms/proverbs into your medium of instruction (any one) : ---------- 1M\n      a) All that glitters is not gold.\n      b) No pain, no gain.','','','i. a) यश 		b) आनंदाने 		c) सवय \n   d) विश्वास 		e) सार्वत्रिक		f)  ग्राहक\nii. a) पुस्तक छान चित्रांनी भरलेले होते.\n     b) पण, मी त्या सगळ्यांना फ्रान्ससाठी लढायला शिकवेन.\n     c) क्यूरीजनी आता प्रचंड उत्साहाने काम करायला सुरुवात केली.\n     d) जादाच्या कामाने खरोखरंच मॅडम क्यूरीजच्या तब्येतीवर परिणाम झाला.\niii. a) चकाकते ते सारे सोने नसते.          b) कष्टाशिवाय फळ नाही','',0,0,0,NULL),(95683,3072,'descriptive','7',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','Translation :\ni. Translate the following words into your medium of instruction (any four)  ----  2M\n    a) picnic 			b) favourite 			c) important \n    d) success			e) parents 			f) route\nii. Translate the following sentences into your medium of instruction (any two) ---- 2M\n     a) Always speak respectfully with others.\n    b) Take advices from your parents from time to time.\n    c) Give respect to elders.\n    d) Parents and grandparents are the pillars of our family.  \niii. Translate the following idioms/proverbs into your medium of instruction (any one) : ---------- 1M\n      a) Service to man is service to God.\n      b) As you sow, so shall you reap. ','','','i. a) सहल 		b) आवडते 		c) महत्त्वपूर्ण \n   d) यश		e)  पालक		f)  मार्ग\nii. a) इतरांशी नेहमी आदरपूर्वक बोला.\n     b) तुमच्या पालकांकडून वेळोवेळी सल्ले घ्या.\n     c) मोठ्यांचा आदर करा.\n     d) आईबाबा आणि आजी-आजोबा हे आपल्या कुटुंबाचे आधारस्तंभ असतात.\niii. a) जनसेवा हीच ईश्वरसेवा.\n     b)  पेरावे तसे उगवते.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95684,3072,'descriptive','7',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','a) Translate the following words into Marathi.\n     i) disaster                        ii) imposter\nb) Translate the following sentences in Marathi. \n     i) India is a secular country.\n     ii) It takes two to make a quarrel.\nc) Translate the following sentences into good English.\n     i) आरोग्य हीच संपत्ती.\n     ii) डॉ. स्टीफन हॉकींग हे एक महान विश्वउत्पत्तीशास्त्रज्ञ होते.','','','a)  i) संकट              ii) भोंदू\nb) i) भारत हे एक धर्मनिरपेक्ष राष्ट्र आहे          ii) एका हाताने टाळी वाजत नाही.\nc) i) Health is wealth.        ii) Dr. Stephen Hawking was a great cosmologist.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95685,3072,'descriptive','7',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','a) Translate the following words into Marathi.\n     i) passivity              ii) illiteracy\nb) Translate the following sentences into Marathi.\n      i) He began studying the concept of \'Black Holes\'.\n     ii) Honesty is the best policy.\nc) Translate the following sentences into English.\n     i) पर्यटकांनी निसर्गरम्य वातावरणाचा आस्वाद घ्यावा.\n     ii) उपचारापेक्षा प्रतिबंध बरा.','','','a) i) निष्क्रियता                  ii) निरक्षरता\nb) i) त्याने\' कृष्णविवर\' या संकल्पनेच्या अभ्यासास सुरुवात केली.\n     ii) प्रामाणिकपणा हाच सद्गुण.\nc) i) The tourists should enjoy natural atmosphere. \n    ii) Prevention is better than cure.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95686,3072,'descriptive','7',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','a) Translate the following words into Marathi.\n     i) sacrifice                ii) innocence\nb) Translate the following sentences into Marathi. \n      i) Pen is mightier than sword.\n      ii) Keep away from vices such as smoking and drinking. \nc) Translate the following sentences into English.\n     i) मानवसेवा हीच खरी ईश्वरसेवा.\n     ii) स्वच्छता देवपूजेपेक्षा श्रेष्ठ असते.','','','a) i) बलिदान            ii) निष्पापपणा\nb) i) तलवारीपेक्षा लेखणी श्रेष्ठ.\n     ii) धूम्रपान व मद्यपान यांसारख्या व्यसनांपासून दूर राहा.\nc) i) Service to man is service to God.\n    ii) Cleanliness is next to godliness.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(95687,3072,'descriptive','7',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','a) Translate the following words into Marathi.\n     i) voyage            ii) mournful\nb) Translate the following sentences into Marathi.\n      i) Sound mind lives in a sound body.\n      ii) Save water as well as fuel.\nc) Translate the following sentences into English.\n     i) कष्टाविना फळ नाही. \n     ii) उत्कृष्ट संवाद साधणारी व्यक्ती दुसऱ्यांवर छाप टाकू शकते.\n','','','a) i) समुद्रप्रवास                ii) खिन्न\nb) i) निरोगी शरीरात निकोप मन राहते.\n     ii) पाण्याप्रमाणेच इंधनाचीही बचत करा.\nc) i) No pains, no gains.\n    ii) A person who makes effective communication impresses others.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95688,3072,'descriptive','7',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','a) Translate the following words into Marathi.\n     i) sponsor           ii) trafficking\nb) Translate the following sentences into Marathi.\n      i) Time and tide wait for nobody.\n      ii) I still fondly remember that encounter.\nc) Translate the following sentences into English.\n     i) परिश्रम हीच पूजा.\n     ii) यश म्हणजे अंधारातून केलेली वाटचाल होय.\n','','','a) i) प्रायोजक               ii) तस्करी\nb) i) काळ आणि वेळ कोणासाठीही थांबत नाहीत.\n     ii) आजसुद्धा मला ती चकमक आठवते.\nc) i) Work is worship.\n    ii) Success is a walk in the dark.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(95689,3072,'descriptive','7',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','a) Translate the following words into Marathi.\n      i) resemblance              ii) drought\nb) Translate the following sentences into Marathi.\n      i) Well begun is half done.\n      ii) We all have natural talents.\nc) Translate the following sentences into English.\n     i) ज्याचा शेवट गोड ते सारेच गोड.\n     ii) सर्व महान धर्म आपल्या मुलांची काळजी घेण्यास शिकवतात.\n','','','a) i) सारखेपणा                   ii) दुष्काळ\nb) i) चांगली सुरुवात म्हणजे अर्धे काम झालेच समजा.\n     ii) आपणा सर्वांमध्ये उपजत कौशल्य असते.\nc) i) All is well that ends well.\n    ii) All the great religions teach us to care for our children.\n','',0,0,0,NULL),(95690,711,'descriptive','4a',10,0,'Out of Text Book','One of the most vocal amongst the \'low-caste\' leaders was Jyotirao Phule. Born in 1827, he studied in schools set up by Christian missionaries. On growing up he developed his own ideas about the injustices of caste society. He set out to attack the Brahmans\' claim that they were superior to others, since they were Aryans. Phule argued that the Aryans were foreigners who came from outside the subcontinent, and defeated and subjugated the true children of the country - those who had lived here from before the coming of the Aryans. As the Aryans established their dominance, they began looking at the defeated population as inferior, as low-caste people. According to Phule, the \'upper\' castes had no right to their land and power: in reality, the land belonged to indigenous people, the so-called \'low\' castes.\nPhule claimed that before Aryan rule there existed a golden age when warrior-peasants tilled the land and ruled the Maratha countryside in just and fair ways. He proposed that Shudras (labouring castes) and Ati Shudras (untouchables) should unite to challenge caste discrimination. The Satyashodhak Samaj, an association Phule founded, propagated caste equality.\nIn 1873, Phule wrote a book named Gulamgiri, meaning slavery. Some ten years before this, the American Civil War had been fought, leading to the end of slavery in America. Phule dedicated his book to all those Americans who had fought to free slaves, thus establishing a link between the conditions of the \'lower\' castes in India and the black slaves in America. As this example shows, Phule extended his criticism of the caste system to argue against all forms of inequality. He was concerned about the plight of \'upper\'-caste women, the miseries of the labourer, and the humiliation of the \'low\' castes. This movement for caste reform was continued in the twentieth century by other great dalit leaders like Dr. B. R. Ambedkar in western India and E.V. Ramaswamy Naicker in the south.',' <b>A1] Simple Factual Question </b>\n       Choose the correct alternative\n        i. Mahatma Phule learnt in schools set up by --------------\n           a) Government                             b) British         \n           c) Christian missionaries            d) Brahmins\n      ii. Mahatma Phule established the ------------- Samaj.\n           a) The Aryans        b) Satyashodhak         c) Upper          d) Brahmin\n      iii. Mahatma Phule asserted that ---------- were foreigners.\n            a) The Aryans             b) British        c) The Greeks          d) The Indians\n       iv. ----------- was a great dalit leader in western India. \n           a) E.V. Ramaswamy              b) Mahatma Phule          \n            c) Mahatma Buddha           d) Dr. B. R. Ambedkar\n',' <b>A2] Complex Factual Question </b>\n        Complete the following :\n        Write Mahatma Phule works in 4 – 5 sentences.\n <b>A3] Vocabulary  </b>\n       Find out the root words from the following words.\n       i. dedication          ii. association          iii. missionaries         iv. inequality\n <b>A4] Grammar  </b>\n        i. Shudras should unite to challenge caste discrimination. \n            (Identify the non-finite verbs) \n        ii. In 1873, Phule wrote a book named Gulamgiri. \n             (Rewrite the sentence beginning with \'object\')\n <b>A5] Personal response question </b>\n        Name any social worker you know. Write 3-4 sentences about him/her.\n <b>Q.4 (B)  </b>Write a summary of the passage in Q. no. 4 (A). Suggest a suitable title.           [05 Marks]','','A1] i) c) Christian missionaries               ii) b) Satyashodhak\n      iii) a) The Aryans                                iv) d) Dr. B. R. Ambedkar \nA2] i) Set up the Satyashodhak Samaj to eradicate caste system.\n       ii) Wrote a book called Gulamgiri.\n       iii) Tried to make equality among all.\n       iv) Showed sympathy on the miseries of the labourers.\nA3] i) dedicate                    ii) associate              iii) mission           iv) equal\nA4] i) should, to challenge\n       ii) A book named Gulamgiri was written by Phule in 1873.\nA5] Personal response question. Mother Teresa was a social worker. She founded the Charity mission in 1950. In 1956, she set up the Nimral Hriday, a home for the dying destitute in Calcutta. She was rightly called \'mother\' because she took care of orphans. She was awarded the Nobel Prize for peace. She devoted her entire life for the welfare of deprived people.\nB]              <b>AN IDEAL PERSONALITY: MAHATMA PHULE </b>\nMahatma Jyotirao Phule was born in 1827. He pursued education in schools run by Christian missionaries. When he grew up, he saw the sense of inequality among people based upon caste system. Then upper class people would do injustice with lower class people. He proposed that the Aryans were foreigners and they discriminated people in India. He always thought that Shudras (untouchables) should come together and eradicate caste system. He founded the Satyashodhak Samaj to make caste equality. He wrote a book Gulamgiri and dedicated his book to American who fought for the abolition of slavery. He focussed on the problems of labourers too. Mahatma Phule was, is and will be an ideal personality for all.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95691,711,'descriptive','4a',10,0,'Out of Text Book','Our forests are important sources of natural wealth, covering one-fifth of the country\'s land area. They are a source of wood for railways, buildings and furniture making. They also supply fuel for cooking and bamboo for papermaking. Medicinal herbs also come from the forests.\nIn the olden days, our wise men and philosophers had their ashrams in the forests. These ashrams were centres of knowledge and learning. Those sages had done an excellent job of maintaining our forests. This is why we had wonderful forests in the past.\nUnfortunately, forests were ruthlessly cut down in the past few years. While the forests areas are reducing, the demand for wood is growing. We must, therefore, protect and develop our forests. Vanamahotsav is an important step in this direction. It is observed for a week in July every year. During this week, lakhs of saplings are planted throughout the country. This is being done to restore our forests that are disappearing fast.\nEven then, deforestation poses a serious threat to forests on the earth. Deforestation results in soil erosion, sudden floods and global warming.','<b>A1] Simple Factual Question</b>\n       Complete the following sentences by choosing the correct alternatives.\n     i) Forests cover -------- of the country’s land area.\n         a) 1/7                  b) 1/15          c) 1/5                  d) 1/2\n     ii) Forests supply wood for ---------------.\n          a) railways         b) space-crafts        c) aeroplanes        d) cars\n     iii) In the olden days, our wise men and philosophers had their ------ in the forests.\n          a) bungalows         b) cottages         c) offices              d) ashrams \n    iv) Vanmahostav is celebrated for a week in --------------\n          a) June               b) July               c) August            d) September','','<b>A2] Complex Factual</b>\n       Read the passage and complete the table :\n<table border=\"1\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width:fit-content; text-align: left;\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n  <tr style=\"background-color: #e6f3ff; text-align: center;\">\n    <th></th>\n    <th>Topic</th>\n    <th>Details</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>i.</td>\n    <td>Uses of forests</td>\n    <td>------</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>ii.</td>\n    <td>Effects of deforestation</td>\n    <td>--------</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n<b>A3] Vocabulary </b>\n       Find the words from the passage which mean the following :\n         i) not artificial             ii) stop being visible        \n        iii) cruelly                     iv) danger\n<b>A4] Grammar</b>\n        Do as directed :\n        i) Lakhs of saplings are planted. \n            (Rewrite by beginning the sentence with ‘They’)\n        ii) We ------- protect and develop our forests.\n          (Fill in a modal auxiliary showing necessity)\n<b>A5] Open/ended/Personal response</b>\n       Forests are an important resource of India. State your opinion.\n<b>Q.4) B] </b>Read the passage given Q.4) A) and write a summary of it. Suggest a suitable title to the summary. -------------- 5M ','Q.4) A)\nA1] i) C          ii) A            iii) D                  iv) B\nA2] i) Uses of forests : a) We get wood, bamboo, fuel\n            b) Used for medicinal herbs, paper making, fuel for cooking, provide us  \n                 with wood for railways, buildings, and furniture’s making\n      ii) Effects of deforestation : a) Results in erosion, sudden floods\n          b) Leads to global warming.\nA3] i) natural            ii) disappear            iii) ruthlessly           iv) threat \nA4] i) They plant lakhs of saplings.\n       ii) We must protect and develop our forests.\nA5] Forests are definitely an important resource of India. They provide us with important raw materials for many industries and products. Valuable forest products are exported, which results in a good amount of foreign exchange. Many villagers survive by selling forest products. I also think that forests are important because they provide shelter to animals, prevent soil erosion and promote rainfall.\n\nQ.4) B)            <b>Saving the Forests</b>\nOur forests are important sources of natural wealth such as wood, fuel, bamboo and medicinal herbs. The sages and philosophers of the past spread their knowledge from their ashrams located in the forests, and maintained them in a good state. Unfortunately, the forests are ruthlessly being destroyed nowadays due to the growing demand for wood. As forest areas are reducing, it becomes necessary for us to save them. In Vanamahotsav, lakhs of saplings are planted throughout the country, in an effort to restore our fast-disappearing forests. De','',0,0,0,NULL),(95692,711,'descriptive','4a',10,0,'Out of Text Book','The elephant\'s trunk is a very important organ, without which it cannot exist. It may be called as the lifeline of an elephant. It is as essential for the elephant as our hands are for us. It is an extension of the nose and upper lip. For an elephant, it performs the functions of hands, nose and lips. They also have a heavy head which cannot be carried on a long neck, so the elephants need a long trunk to reach their food. The trunk has about 40,000 muscles. Because of so many muscles, it is flexible and strong. It can lift huge wooden poles with its trunk. The tip of the trunk is just like a finger and is so sensitive that it can even lift a needle. Elephants carry their food to the mouth with the trunk. They also drink water with its help.\nTo take a bath, an elephant fills water in the trunk, curls it up and pours that over its back. Thus, we can see how the trunk is very useful for the elephant.','<b>A1] Simple Factual Question</b>\n       Complete the following table based on the passage :\n<table border=\"1\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width:fit-content; text-align: left;\" class=\"table table-bordered table-striped\">\n  <tr style=\"background-color: #e6f3ff; text-align: center;\">\n    <th></th>\n    <th>Question</th>\n    <th>Answer</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>i.</td>\n    <td>Lifeline of an elephant is its</td>\n    <td>-----------</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>ii.</td>\n    <td>The tip of the trunk is</td>\n    <td>-----------</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>iii.</td>\n    <td>The trunk is flexible and strong because</td>\n    <td>------------</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>iv.</td>\n    <td>A trunk acts like</td>\n    <td>------------</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>','<b>A2] Complex Factual</b>\n       Complete the following sentences with the help of the extract:\n    i) An elephant needs a long trunk because ------------.\n     ii) The trunk can even lift a needle because -----------.\n     iii) The trunk is a very important organ as --------------.\n      iv) An elephant fills its trunk with water as -----------.\n<b>A3] Vocabulary </b>\n         Use the following words/phrases in sentences of your own :\n            i) exist                  ii) lifeline\n<b>A4] Grammar </b>\n       1. Choose the correct exclamatory sentence from the alternatives for the following : The trunk is very useful.\n    i) How useful the trunk is!           ii) What useful the trunk is!\n   iii) How very useful the trunk is!      iv) The trunk is how useful!\n2. Choose the correct alternative from the following that the underlined verb suggests. An elephant can lift huge wooden poles with its trunks.\n     i) It is necessary for elephant to lift very huge wooden poles with its trunk.\n     ii) It is an elephant\'s ability of lifting very huge wooden poles with its trunk.\n     iii) An elephant should lift very huge wooden poles with its trunk.\n     iv) It is possible for an elephant to lift very huge wooden poles with its trunk.\n<b>A5] Open ended/Personal Response </b>\n       State the measures to be taken by the government for the protection of elephants.\n\n<b>Q.4) B) </b>Read the passage given Q.4) A) and write a summary of it. Suggest a suitable title to the summary. -------------- 5M ','','Q.4) A)\nA1] i) trunk without which it cannot exist.\n      ii) just like a finger and is so sensitive that it can even lift a needle\n     iii) it has about 40,000 muscles.\n      iv) hands, nose and lips.\nA2] i) it has a heavy head which cannot be carried on a long neck, so the elephant needs a long trunk to reach its food\nii) the tip of the trunk is just like a finger and is very sensitive\niii) it performs the functions of hands, nose and lips for the elephant\niv) it drinks water with it and also takes a bath with it\nA3] i) There is a possibility that life could exist on planets other than Earth.\n      ii) The local trains are known as Mumbai’s lifeline.\nA4] 1) i) How useful the trunk is!\n       2) iv) It is possible for an elephant to lift huge wooden poles with its trunk.\nA5] Elephants live in forest, which is their natural habitat. Hence, the government of India should protect the forest areas in order to save them. Elephants are also killed for their ivory tusks (long teeth) and their skin. The use of ivory in our country should be banned to save the lives of elephants.\n\nQ.4) B)            The Elephant’s Trunk\nThe trunk of an elephant is its lifeline, as the animal can\'t exist without it. An extension of the nose and upper lip, it performs the functions of hands, nose and lips. An elephant has a heavy head that cannot be carried on a long neck and the animal therefore needs a long trunk to reach its food. Owing to its 40,000 muscles, the trunk is flexible and so strong that it can lift huge wooden poles. The finger-like tip of the trunk is sensitive enough to lift a needle. An elephant carries its food and water to its mouth and also bathes with the help of its trunk. This explains how crucial the trunk is to the elephant.','',0,0,0,NULL),(95702,2294,'descriptive','1b',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','कविता “बसंत गीत” में “सजी आयो रे, ऋतु बसंत सजी आयो।” — यह किसने किससे कहा?','','','यह कवि ने सब लोगों से कहा।','',0,0,0,NULL),(95703,2294,'descriptive','1b',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','कविता “बसंत गीत” में “अजी गाओ रे, ऋतु बसंत सजी आयो।” — यह किसने किससे कहा?','','','यह कवि ने सब लोगों से कहा।','',0,0,0,NULL),(95704,2294,'descriptive','1b',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','कविता “बसंत गीत” में “कलि-कलि करत कलोल कुसुम मन, मंद-मंद मुस्कायो।” — यह किसने किससे कहा?','','','यह कवि ने फूलों के बारे में कहा।','',0,0,0,NULL),(95705,2294,'descriptive','1b',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','कविता “बसंत गीत” में “मधु मकरंद चुरायो।” — यह किसने किससे कहा?','','','यह कवि ने भँवरे के बारे में कहा।','',0,0,0,NULL),(95706,2294,'descriptive','1b',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','कविता “बसंत गीत” में “वन-वन, बाग-बाग, बगिया में युतिहि सुगंध उड़ाओ।” — यह किसने किससे कहा?','','','यह फूलों ने हवा से कहा।','',0,0,0,NULL),(95707,2294,'descriptive','1b',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','कविता “बसंत गीत” में “गीत कोयलिया गाये।” — यह किसने किससे कहा?','','','यह कवि ने कोयल के बारे में कहा।','',0,0,0,NULL),(95708,2294,'descriptive','1b',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','कविता “बसंत गीत” में “पीली-पीली सरसों फूली।” — यह किसने किससे कहा?','','','यह कवि ने सरसों के फूलों के बारे में कहा।','',0,0,0,NULL),(95709,2294,'descriptive','1b',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','कविता “बसंत गीत” में “हरी-हरी मटर बिछी है।” — यह किसने किससे कहा?','','','यह कवि ने मटर के पौधों के बारे में कहा।','',0,0,0,NULL),(95710,2294,'descriptive','1b',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','कविता “बसंत गीत” में “अमित रंग बरसायो।” — यह किसने किससे कहा?','','','यह कवि ने बसंत ऋतु के बारे में कहा।','',0,0,0,NULL),(95711,2295,'descriptive','1b',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','पाठ “चंदा मामा की जय” में “ये रोने वाले बच्चे हैं, विशेषकर यह अतुल।” — यह किसने किससे कहा?','','','निंदिया ने रात्रानी से कहा।','',0,0,0,NULL),(95712,2295,'descriptive','1b',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','पाठ “चंदा मामा की जय” में “तुम क्यों रोते हो?” — यह किसने किससे कहा?','','','रात्रानी ने अतुल से कहा।','',0,0,0,NULL),(95713,2295,'descriptive','1b',1,0,'Out of Text Book','',' पाठ “चंदा मामा की जय” में “जवाब दो।” — यह किसने किससे कहा?','','','रात्रानी ने सुनील से कहा।','',0,0,0,NULL),(95714,2295,'descriptive','1b',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','पाठ “चंदा मामा की जय” में “अच्छे बच्चे बड़ों को जवाब नहीं देते।” — यह किसने किससे कहा?','','','सुनील ने रात्रानी से कहा।','',0,0,0,NULL),(95715,2295,'descriptive','1b',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','पाठ “चंदा मामा की जय” में “तुम बड़ों का मजाक उड़ाते हो।” — यह किसने किससे कहा?','','','रात्रानी ने सुनील से कहा।','',0,0,0,NULL),(95716,2295,'descriptive','1b',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','पाठ “चंदा मामा की जय” में “सुनील भैया को कड़ी सजा मत दो।” — यह किसने किससे कहा?','','','अतुल ने रात्रानी से कहा।','',0,0,0,NULL),(95717,2295,'descriptive','1b',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','पाठ “चंदा मामा की जय” में “तुम रो क्यों रहे हो?” — यह किसने किससे कहा?','','','रात्रानी ने अतुल से कहा।','',0,0,0,NULL),(95738,3078,'descriptive','2',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','A) Matter      B) Atomicity     C) Metalloid     D) Homogeneous Mixture     E) Heterogeneous Mixture    F) Crystallisation    G) Chemistry','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95739,3078,'descriptive','3',6,0,'Out of Text Book','','What is elements? Give it\'s characteristics and explain the type of elements on the basis of atomicity with Examples. ','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95740,3078,'descriptive','3',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','Explain the differences between Metal and Non-metal','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95741,3078,'descriptive','3',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','Define Compound and give it\'s Characteristics. ','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95742,3078,'descriptive','3',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','What is Mixture? Explain differences between mixtures and Compounds','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95743,3078,'descriptive','3',5,0,'Out of Text Book','',' What is mean by Solution, Solvent and Solute. Give the types of Solution on the basis of particle size and their Visibility. ','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95744,3078,'descriptive','3',5,0,'Out of Text Book','','What\'s are the different characteristics of mixture? and enlisted various methods of separation of the constituent of mixture.','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95770,2622,'descriptive','4',2,0,'Out of Text Book','कलि-कलि करत कलोल कुसुम मन, मंद-मंद मुस्कायो\nगुन-गुन-गुन-गुन गूंॅजे मधुप गन मधु मकरंद चुरायो','','','','कलियाँ क्रीडा कर रही हैं। फूल ऐसे लग रहे हैं, मानो वे मन में मंद-मंद मुसकुरा रहे हों। भौर गुन-गुन गुंजार कर रहे हैं और इधर से उधर उड़कर फूलों का रस पी रहे हैं।','',0,0,0,NULL),(95771,2622,'descriptive','4',2,0,'Out of Text Book','जो वीरत्व-विवेक समर में हम सैनिक दिखलाऍंगे,\nउसकी गाथाएँ भारत के गॉंव, नगर, घर गाऍंगे,\nअनगिन कंठों में गूँजेंगे बोल हमारे गान के । ','','','','हम भारतीय सैनिक युद्ध-भूमि में जिस विवेक और वीरता का प्रदर्शन करेंगे, गाँव-गाँव, नगर-नगर, घर-घर में उनकी गाथाएँ गाई जाएँगी। अनगिनत कंठों से हमारी वीरता और हमारे बलिदान के गीत गाए जाएँगे।','',0,0,0,NULL),(95835,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following is a heterogeneous mixture?\nA) Air\nB) Brass\nC) Milk\nD) Vinegar','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95836,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Which property is NOT suitable for separating iron filings from sand?\nA) Density\nB) Magnetism\nC) Solubility\nD) Sublimation\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95837,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following is a compound?\nA) Sea water\nB) Sugar\nC) Air\nD) Brass\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95838,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','The formula of aluminium oxide is:\nA) AlO\nB) Al₂O₃\nC) Al₃O₂\nD) AlO₂\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95839,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following contains polyatomic ions?\nA) NaCl\nB) H₂O\nC) NH₄Cl\nD) O₂\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95840,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','A mixture of alcohol and water can be separated by:\nA) Filtration\nB) Fractional distillation\nC) Sublimation\nD) Chromatography\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95841,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following is not an element?\nA) Sulphur\nB) Diamond\nC) Carbon dioxide\nD) Copper\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95842,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','The valency of phosphate radical is:\nA) 1\nB) 2\nC) 3\nD) 4\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95843,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Which pair shows variable valency?\nA) Na, K\nB) Cu, Fe\nC) Mg, Ca\nD) O, S\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95844,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Which method is used to obtain pure crystals from impure copper sulphate solution?\nA) Distillation\nB) Crystallisation\nC) Sublimation\nD) Sedimentation\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95845,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following is not true for compounds?\nA) Fixed composition\nB) Definite melting point\nC) Can be separated physically\nD) New properties\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95846,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','The formula of calcium phosphate is:\nA) CaPO₄\nB) Ca₃PO₄\nC) Ca₃(PO₄)₂\nD) Ca₂PO₄\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95847,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Which is a colloidal solution?\nA) Salt in water\nB) Chalk in water\nC) Milk\nD) Sugar in water\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95848,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','A substance that directly changes from solid to gas is separated by:\nA) Distillation\nB) Filtration\nC) Sublimation\nD) Chromatography\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95849,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Which ion has +3 charge?\nA) Fe²⁺\nB) Al³⁺\nC) Zn²⁺\nD) Pb²⁺\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95850,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','The formula of zinc oxide is:\nA) ZnO₂\nB) Zn₂O\nC) ZnO\nD) Zn₂O₃','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95851,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Which one is a non-metal conductor?\nA) Sulphur\nB) Carbon (graphite)\nC) Bromine\nD) Phosphorus\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95852,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following is incorrectly matched?\nA) Sulphate – SO₄²⁻\nB) Nitrate – NO₃⁻\nC) Carbonate – CO₃⁻\nD) Hydroxide – OH⁻\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95853,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','A pure substance formed by chemical combination is:\nA) Mixture\nB) Compound\nC) Solution\nD) Colloid\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95854,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','The symbol Fe comes from:\nA) Ferrum\nB) Ferrous\nC) Iron\nD) Ferric\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95855,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Which has the highest boiling point?\nA) Oxygen\nB) Water\nC) Hydrogen\nD) Nitrogen\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95856,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Which mixture can be separated by separating funnel?\nA) Sugar + water\nB) Oil + water\nC) Salt + water\nD) Alcohol + water\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95857,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Which of the following is not a cation?\nA) NH₄⁺\nB) Al³⁺\nC) OH⁻\nD) Cu²⁺\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95858,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','The valency of sulphur in SO₂ is:\nA) 2\nB) 4\nC) 6\nD) 8\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95859,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','Which one is a metalloid?\nA) Iron\nB) Germanium\nC) Sulphur\nD) Oxygen\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL),(95860,3078,'mcq','1a',1,0,'Out of Text Book','','The formula of ammonium sulphate is:\nA) NH₄SO₄\nB) (NH₄)₂SO₄\nC) NH₄(SO₄)₂\nD) NH₄₂SO₄\n','','','','',0,0,0,NULL)