in poems and songs because they are beautiful and helpful.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What part of the coconut tree is used to make a mat?\",\"options\":[\"Leaves\",\"Shell\",\"Husk\",\"Oil\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The husk of the coconut can be used as a mat.\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the coconut contains sweet white liquid?\",\"options\":[\"Shell\",\"Husk\",\"Milk\",\"Oil\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The white liquid inside the coconut is called coconut milk.\"},{\"q\":\"Coconut oil is mainly used for?\",\"options\":[\"Cooking\",\"Hair care\",\"Both\",\"None\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Coconut oil is used for cooking and hair care.\"},{\"q\":\"The coconut tree is known as the \\\"Tree of Life\\\" because it provides:\",\"options\":[\"Only food\",\"Only water\",\"Food, water and shade\",\"Only shade\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"It gives food, water and shade.\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the coconut is NOT used?\",\"options\":[\"Shell\",\"Husk\",\"Leaves\",\"All parts are used\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"All parts of the coconut tree are used.\"},{\"q\":\"Coconut trees grow best in which climate?\",\"options\":[\"Cold\",\"Arid\",\"Tropical\",\"Temperate\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"They grow in warm, tropical places.\"},{\"q\":\"The poem mentions the coconut tree as a gift from nature. What is the gift?\",\"options\":[\"Oil\",\"Milk\",\"Coconut fruit\",\"All of the above\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"All parts are gifts from nature.\"},{\"q\":\"The coconut tree is tall and touches the clouds. What does this show?\",\"options\":[\"It is very old\",\"It is very tall\",\"It is very thin\",\"It is very short\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem describes it as tall.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is NOT a use of the coconut tree?\",\"options\":[\"Making bowls\",\"Making mats\",\"Making paper\",\"Making oil\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Paper is not mentioned as a use.\"},{\"q\":\"The coconut tree is near the sea. Why is this important?\",\"options\":[\"It needs salt water\",\"It grows better with sea breeze\",\"It is a decoration\",\"It is a myth\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Sea breeze helps the tree grow.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16484,11,3,'English','en','2.2 Narali Pournima','[\"Narali Pournima is a festival celebrated in Maharashtra on the full moon day of the month of Chaitra.\",\"It is also called Narali Pournima because people eat a special sweet called Narali Bhat made from coconut.\",\"Families visit the sea shore and offer a coconut to the sea as a prayer for safety and prosperity.\",\"People decorate their houses with coconut shells and make doormats from brown husk of coconut.\",\"Children enjoy sweets like coconut laddoos, barfi and other coconut based sweets.\",\"The festival is celebrated with family and friends, and people share stories and songs.\",\"It is a time to thank the sea for its bounty and to wish for good health and harmony.\",\"During Narali Pournima, people also celebrate Rakshabandhan, a festival of brother-sister love.\",\"The story of Mukta and Raghav shows how families come together to celebrate this festival.\",\"The mother prepares coconut sweets and a special drink called solkadhi made from coconut flesh.\",\"The father is a fisherman, and the family lives near the sea, which is important for the festival.\",\"The whole day is spent with relatives, sharing food and enjoying the sea view.\",\"The story emphasizes the importance of family, tradition, and respect for nature.\",\"Children learn to recognize key characters and main ideas in the story.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is Narali Pournima also called?\",\"options\":[\"Full Moon Day\",\"Coconut Festival\",\"Sea Festival\",\"All of the above\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Narali Pournima is also known as the Coconut Festival because people eat coconut sweets.\"},{\"q\":\"Who offers a coconut to the sea during the festival?\",\"options\":[\"The mother\",\"The father\",\"The whole family\",\"Only the children\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The whole family offers a coconut to the sea as a prayer.\"},{\"q\":\"What sweet is made from coconut for Narali Pournima?\",\"options\":[\"Laddoos\",\"Barfi\",\"Narali Bhat\",\"Kheer\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Narali Bhat is a special sweet made from coconut.\"},{\"q\":\"What drink is made from coconut flesh?\",\"options\":[\"Lassi\",\"Solkadhi\",\"Chai\",\"Kombucha\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Solkadhi is a drink made from coconut flesh.\"},{\"q\":\"Which festival is celebrated together with Narali Pournima?\",\"options\":[\"Diwali\",\"Holi\",\"Rakshabandhan\",\"Eid\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Rakshabandhan is celebrated together with Narali Pournima.\"},{\"q\":\"What do people use coconut shells for?\",\"options\":[\"Cooking\",\"Decorating houses\",\"Building houses\",\"None of the above\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Coconut shells are used to decorate houses.\"},{\"q\":\"What do children do on Narali Pournima?\",\"options\":[\"Go to school\",\"Play with friends\",\"Enjoy sweets\",\"All of the above\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Children enjoy sweets like coconut laddoos and barfi.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main theme of the story about Mukta and Raghav?\",\"options\":[\"Adventure\",\"Friendship\",\"Family togetherness\",\"Competition\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The story focuses on family togetherness during the festival.\"},{\"q\":\"Where does the family live?\",\"options\":[\"In a city\",\"In a small village near Alibaug\",\"In the mountains\",\"In a forest\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"They live in a small village near Alibaug.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the mother’s occupation?\",\"options\":[\"Teacher\",\"Fisherman\",\"Cook\",\"Doctor\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The mother is a cook who prepares coconut sweets.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16485,11,3,'English','en','2.3 Word Family - III','[\"Word family is a group of words that share the same base letters and meaning.\",\"In this chapter we learn the word family that starts with the letters B, I, G, P, and F.\",\"The base word is the simplest form, e.g. ‘bin’ or ‘pig’.\",\"Add the letters ‘b’, ‘i’, ‘g’, ‘p’, or ‘f’ to the base to make new words.\",\"Examples: ‘bin’ → ‘big’, ‘pig’ → ‘fig’ (by changing the middle letter).\",\"The words in a family have similar sounds and meanings.\",\"Use the word family to build new words when you read or write.\",\"Remember the pattern: base word + one of the letters B, I, G, P, F.\",\"Practice by making sentences with the new words.\",\"The word family helps you understand how words are formed.\",\"It also helps you remember spelling of new words.\",\"Keep the base word in mind when you see a new word in a sentence.\",\"The base word is the ‘root’ of the family.\",\"The family can be used in stories, poems, and everyday conversation.\",\"Knowing word families makes reading easier and faster.\",\"The more families you know, the better your vocabulary becomes.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which word is the base word in the family that includes ‘big’ and ‘pig’?\",\"options\":[\"big\",\"pig\",\"fig\",\"bin\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The base word is ‘pig’; ‘big’ is formed by changing the middle letter.\"},{\"q\":\"What letter is added to ‘bin’ to make ‘big’?\",\"options\":[\"i\",\"g\",\"p\",\"f\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"‘big’ is made by changing the middle letter of ‘bin’ to ‘i’.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a small fruit in this family?\",\"options\":[\"fig\",\"pig\",\"bin\",\"big\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"‘fig’ is a small fruit.\"},{\"q\":\"The sentence ‘The kid hit the big pig’ uses which word family?\",\"options\":[\"B family\",\"I family\",\"G family\",\"P family\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"‘pig’ and ‘big’ belong to the P family.\"},{\"q\":\"Fill in the blank: The ______ ran.\",\"options\":[\"kid\",\"pig\",\"big\",\"fig\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The sentence in the text says ‘The kid ran.’\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is NOT part of the word family shown?\",\"options\":[\"bin\",\"big\",\"fig\",\"kid\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"‘kid’ is not part of the B, I, G, P, F family.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word ‘fig’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"a small fruit\",\"a big animal\",\"a container\",\"a child\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"‘fig’ is a small fruit.\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence shows a word from the family?\",\"options\":[\"The kid ran.\",\"The kid hit the big pig.\",\"The big pig hit the bin.\",\"The bin hit the fig.\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"‘The bin hit the fig’ contains ‘fig’ from the family.\"},{\"q\":\"Which letter is used to make ‘big’ from ‘bin’?\",\"options\":[\"b\",\"i\",\"g\",\"p\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"‘big’ is made by changing the middle letter of ‘bin’ to ‘i’.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a small animal?\",\"options\":[\"pig\",\"fig\",\"bin\",\"kid\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"‘pig’ is a small animal.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16486,11,3,'English','en','2.4 I am Growing Up','[\"I am growing up every day.\",\"I learn new things and play.\",\"I can do more by myself.\",\"I still need some help sometimes.\",\"I feel big and strong at times.\",\"I feel small and wrong at times.\",\"I feel happy and proud at times.\",\"I feel sad and loud at times.\",\"Growing up is not easy.\",\"Sometimes it makes me dizzy.\",\"I love growing up anyway.\",\"I can listen and sing to help me learn.\",\"I can write rhyming words to practice spelling.\",\"I can read and copy new words like learn, grow, make, help.\",\"I can use a dictionary to find meanings of words like grow, wrong, strong, proud, dizzy.\",\"I can express my feelings when I win or when a friend claps.\",\"I can talk about my feelings such as happy, sleepy, proud, sad, scared, shy, tired, angry, surprised.\",\"I can create posters with pictures of emotions.\",\"I can talk about emojis and what they mean.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What word rhymes with \\\"play\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"clay\",\"day\",\"pay\",\"way\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Play rhymes with clay.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means \\\"not right\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"wrong\",\"right\",\"big\",\"small\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Wrong means not right.\"},{\"q\":\"What does \\\"dizzy\\\" mean?\",\"options\":[\"tired\",\"confused\",\"light‑headed\",\"happy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Dizzy means light‑headed.\"},{\"q\":\"When you win a match, you feel ______?\",\"options\":[\"sad\",\"happy\",\"angry\",\"tired\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Winning usually makes you happy.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means \\\"having power\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"small\",\"strong\",\"wrong\",\"dizzy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Strong means having power.\"},{\"q\":\"If you feel small and wrong, you are likely feeling ______?\",\"options\":[\"proud\",\"happy\",\"sad\",\"angry\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Feeling small and wrong usually means sad.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the opposite of \\\"big\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"small\",\"strong\",\"wrong\",\"dizzy\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The opposite of big is small.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means \\\"not correct\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"wrong\",\"right\",\"strong\",\"happy\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Wrong means not correct.\"},{\"q\":\"When you feel proud, you are ______?\",\"options\":[\"happy\",\"sad\",\"angry\",\"tired\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Feeling proud is a type of happiness.\"},{\"q\":\"What does \\\"proud\\\" mean?\",\"options\":[\"confident\",\"shy\",\"tired\",\"scared\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Proud means confident.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16487,11,3,'English','en','2.5 My Friend, the Clock','[\"- A clock tells the time using numbers and two hands.\",\"- The big hand (short hand) shows the hour.\",\"- The small hand (long hand) shows the minutes.\",\"- Clocks make a tick‑tick sound when they move.\",\"- We can use a clock to know when to wake up, go to school, study, play, eat dinner and go to bed.\",\"- A clock is a helpful friend that helps us stay on schedule.\",\"- The word ‘clock’ comes from the Latin word ‘clocca’ meaning bell.\",\"- Clocks can be wall clocks, desk clocks, or wrist watches.\",\"- The hands of a clock move round and round in a circle.\",\"- The time shown on a clock is called the ‘time of day’.\",\"- We read the time by looking at where the hands point on the numbers.\",\"- The hour hand moves slowly, the minute hand moves faster.\",\"- A clock can also have a second hand that ticks every second.\",\"- We can set a clock by turning the knob or pressing buttons.\",\"- Clocks help us keep our daily routine and stay healthy and active.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What sound does a clock make?\",\"options\":[\"ding-dong\",\"tick-tick\",\"whistle\",\"honk\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Clocks usually make a tick‑tick sound.\"},{\"q\":\"Which hand shows the hour?\",\"options\":[\"Big hand\",\"Small hand\",\"Second hand\",\"Both hands\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The big (short) hand shows the hour.\"},{\"q\":\"When does the clock remind you to eat dinner?\",\"options\":[\"In the morning\",\"At noon\",\"When the sun sets\",\"At midnight\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The clock reminds to eat dinner when the sun sets.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of a clock?\",\"options\":[\"To make noise\",\"To show the time\",\"To tell jokes\",\"To play music\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A clock’s main job is to show the time.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT a type of clock?\",\"options\":[\"Wall clock\",\"Desk clock\",\"Wrist watch\",\"Bed clock\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Bed clock is not a common type; we use wall, desk or wrist.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the small hand on a clock indicate?\",\"options\":[\"Hours\",\"Minutes\",\"Seconds\",\"Days\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The small (long) hand shows minutes.\"},{\"q\":\"The clock helps you stay healthy by:\",\"options\":[\"Playing games\",\"Eating fast food\",\"Keeping a routine\",\"Watching TV\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A clock helps keep a healthy routine.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means ‘a friend of the clock’?\",\"options\":[\"Clockwise\",\"Clockwork\",\"Clock friend\",\"Clockwise friend\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The story calls the clock a good friend.\"},{\"q\":\"What happens when the clock’s hands move?\",\"options\":[\"They stop\",\"They jump\",\"They move round and round\",\"They disappear\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The hands move round and round.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a correct time shown on a clock?\",\"options\":[\"7:15 a.m.\",\"7.15 a.m.\",\"7-15 a.m.\",\"7,15 a.m.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The correct format is 7:15 a.m.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16488,11,3,'English','en','2.6 Library','[\"A library is a quiet place where many books are kept.\",\"Books in a library include story books, poetry books, newspapers and magazines.\",\"You can read books in the library or borrow them to take home.\",\"A librarian helps you find the books you want.\",\"Libraries encourage children to read more and become good readers.\",\"When using a library, keep it clean: no folding corners, no tearing pages.\",\"Always return books on time so others can use them.\",\"Use a bookmark instead of folding the corners of a page.\",\"Keep your bags outside the library to keep the place tidy.\",\"Speak quietly in the library – it is a place of silence.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is a library?\",\"options\":[\"A noisy place\",\"A house of books\",\"A playground\",\"A kitchen\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A library is described as a quiet and happy place that is a house of books.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is NOT mentioned as a type of book in the library?\",\"options\":[\"Story books\",\"Poetry books\",\"Comic books\",\"Newspapers\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Comic books are not listed among the types mentioned.\"},{\"q\":\"Who helps you find books in the library?\",\"options\":[\"Teacher\",\"Student\",\"Librarian\",\"Parent\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A librarian helps to find books.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do with your books after reading?\",\"options\":[\"Fold the corners\",\"Keep them in your bag\",\"Return them on time\",\"Throw them away\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Books should be returned on time.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a rule for handling books?\",\"options\":[\"Tear the pages\",\"Fold the pages\",\"Handle books carefully\",\"Ignore the rules\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The rule is to handle books carefully.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you use instead of folding the corners of a book?\",\"options\":[\"A bookmark\",\"A rubber band\",\"A paper clip\",\"A sticky note\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Use a bookmark instead of folding corners.\"},{\"q\":\"Which time is mentioned for the Book Festival event?\",\"options\":[\"10 O\' clock\",\"11.30 a.m.\",\"12 noon\",\"9.30 a.m.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The event starts at 10 O\' clock in the morning.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do while reading in the library?\",\"options\":[\"Sit properly\",\"Run around\",\"Play loudly\",\"Ignore the rules\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"You should sit properly while reading.\"},{\"q\":\"Which subject is NOT listed in the class timetable example?\",\"options\":[\"Mathematics\",\"Art\",\"Physics\",\"Urdu\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Physics is not listed in the example timetable.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of a library according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"To play games\",\"To read and borrow books\",\"To eat snacks\",\"To watch TV\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The library motivates us to read more and lets us borrow books.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16489,11,3,'English','en','2.7 Punctuation Friends','[\"Full Stop (.) ends a sentence.\",\"Capital Letter starts a sentence.\",\"Comma (,) gives a small pause.\",\"Question Mark (?) ends a question.\",\"Use punctuation correctly to make meaning clear.\",\"Write sentences with a capital letter at the start.\",\"Add a full stop at the end of a statement.\",\"Add a question mark at the end of a question.\",\"Use commas to separate items in a list.\",\"Punctuation helps readers understand the text.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What punctuation mark is used to end a statement?\",\"options\":[\"Comma\",\"Full Stop\",\"Question Mark\",\"Exclamation Point\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A full stop (period) ends a statement.\"},{\"q\":\"Which punctuation mark shows a question?\",\"options\":[\"Full Stop\",\"Comma\",\"Question Mark\",\"Exclamation Point\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A question mark is used at the end of a question.\"},{\"q\":\"What does a comma do in a sentence?\",\"options\":[\"Ends a sentence\",\"Shows a pause\",\"Shows a question\",\"Shows excitement\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A comma indicates a small pause in a sentence.\"},{\"q\":\"Which punctuation mark is used after a greeting like \\\"Hello\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"Full Stop\",\"Comma\",\"Question Mark\",\"Exclamation Point\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A comma follows a greeting in a sentence.\"},{\"q\":\"How do you start a new sentence after a full stop?\",\"options\":[\"With a lowercase letter\",\"With a capital letter\",\"With a comma\",\"With a question mark\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A new sentence starts with a capital letter.\"},{\"q\":\"What punctuation mark would you use to express excitement?\",\"options\":[\"Full Stop\",\"Comma\",\"Question Mark\",\"Exclamation Point\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"An exclamation point shows excitement.\"},{\"q\":\"Which punctuation mark is used to separate items in a list?\",\"options\":[\"Full Stop\",\"Comma\",\"Question Mark\",\"Exclamation Point\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A comma separates items in a list.\"},{\"q\":\"What punctuation mark is used after a statement that is a question?\",\"options\":[\"Full Stop\",\"Comma\",\"Question Mark\",\"Exclamation Point\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A question mark ends a question.\"},{\"q\":\"Which punctuation mark indicates a pause but not a full stop?\",\"options\":[\"Full Stop\",\"Comma\",\"Question Mark\",\"Exclamation Point\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A comma indicates a pause but does not end a sentence.\"},{\"q\":\"What punctuation mark would you use after the word \\\"Hello\\\" in the sentence \\\"Hello, how are you?\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"Full Stop\",\"Comma\",\"Question Mark\",\"Exclamation Point\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A comma follows the greeting \\\"Hello\\\".\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16490,11,3,'English','en','2.8 Hide and Seek','[\"Hide and Seek is a game where one person hides and the others try to find them.\",\"The seeker counts to a number (like ten) before looking for the hidden person.\",\"In the story, the characters are animals: Hen, Crow, Rabbit, Squirrel, Cat, Fox, Calf, etc.\",\"The seeker asks questions like “Where is she?” or “Can you see a pair of feet?” to help find the hidden one.\",\"The story shows how the seeker talks to different animals to find the Hen.\",\"The sentences in the story are simple and use short phrases and questions.\",\"The characters can be renamed with human friends’ names to practice speaking.\",\"The story can be acted out to make learning fun and interactive.\",\"Students should practice writing short sentences with punctuation marks like commas and question marks.\",\"They can also retell the story using different names to show understanding.\",\"The game helps develop listening, speaking, and observation skills.\",\"It also teaches counting and following instructions.\",\"Students can draw pictures of the game or the animals to show what they learned.\",\"The teacher can ask students to write a short story about a game they play.\",\"The story should have a clear beginning, middle, and end.\",\"Students should use simple words and correct punctuation.\",\"They can also discuss the story in small groups to practice speaking.\",\"They can present the story orally to the class.\",\"These activities help build language and social skills.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the main idea of the story \\\"Hide and Seek\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"A game of hide and seek\",\"A story about a rabbit\",\"A story about a cat\",\"A story about a horse\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The story is about playing hide and seek.\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the seeker in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Hen\",\"Calf\",\"Crow\",\"Rabbit\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Calf is the one who counts and looks for the Hen.\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal is NOT mentioned as hiding the Hen?\",\"options\":[\"Squirrel\",\"Cat\",\"Dog\",\"Fox\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Dog is not mentioned in the story.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the seeker ask to help find the Hen?\",\"options\":[\"Where is she?\",\"Can you see a pair of feet?\",\"Is she in the basket?\",\"All of the above\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"All those questions are used.\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence is a question?\",\"options\":[\"Let’s find the Hen.\",\"Where is she?\",\"I’ll count to ten.\",\"Come on, Cat, follow me.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Only \\\"Where is she?\\\" is a question.\"},{\"q\":\"What does Calf do after saying \\\"Yes\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"He hides\",\"He counts to ten\",\"He follows the rabbit\",\"He asks a question\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Calf says he will count to ten.\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal is described as having a stripy nose?\",\"options\":[\"Squirrel\",\"Cat\",\"Fox\",\"Rabbit\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The story mentions a stripy nose with the Squirrel.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of the activity \\\"Enact the story\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"To write a story\",\"To draw pictures\",\"To act out the story\",\"To count to ten\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Students act out the story.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is a correct way to retell the story?\",\"options\":[\"Use the same animal names\",\"Use different animal names\",\"Use only human names\",\"Use no names\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Retelling uses different names of friends.\"},{\"q\":\"Why should students practice writing short sentences?\",\"options\":[\"To improve spelling\",\"To learn punctuation\",\"To count animals\",\"To draw pictures\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Short sentences help learn punctuation.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16491,11,3,'English','en','2.9 Word Family - IV','[\"Word family means words that share the same base sound or spelling.\",\"In this chapter we learn the word family that starts with the letters L, D, and T.\",\"All words in this family have the same short vowel sound \\/ɒ\\/ like in \\\"hot\\\" or \\\"pot\\\".\",\"Common words: dog, fog, jog, log, hot, pot, not, cot, got, dot, top, hop, rod, box, fox, job, boy, joy, toy, lot.\",\"You can make new words by adding a letter at the start or end of the base word.\",\"Example: add ‘b’ to ‘ox’ to get ‘box’ or add ‘t’ to ‘op’ to get ‘top’.\",\"The words are usually written in the same order in the book: dog, fog, jog, log, hot, pot, not, cot, got, dot, top, hop, rod, box, fox, job, boy, joy, toy, lot.\",\"When you read them aloud, keep the short vowel sound the same in each word.\",\"If you see a picture, match the picture with the correct word from the family.\",\"Practice by saying each word and thinking of a sentence that uses it.\",\"Remember: the word family helps you learn many words at once.\",\"Use flashcards: write the word on one side and a picture on the other.\",\"Try to find other words that fit the same family in your own books.\",\"Ask the teacher to check your pronunciation of each word.\",\"Keep repeating the words until you can say them quickly and correctly.\",\"Doing this will help you read and write better in English.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which word is NOT part of the word family in this chapter?\",\"options\":[\"dog\",\"fog\",\"log\",\"cot\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The word family uses the short \\/ɒ\\/ sound; \'cot\' has a different vowel.\"},{\"q\":\"What sound do all the words in this family share?\",\"options\":[\"\\/æ\\/\",\"\\/ɒ\\/\",\"\\/ɛ\\/\",\"\\/ɪ\\/\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"They all have the short \\/ɒ\\/ sound as in \'hot\'.\"},{\"q\":\"Add a letter to \'ox\' to make a word in this family.\",\"options\":[\"b\",\"c\",\"d\",\"f\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"b + ox = box.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is a noun?\",\"options\":[\"hop\",\"got\",\"dog\",\"hot\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Dog is a noun; the others are verbs or adjectives.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a small animal that can run fast?\",\"options\":[\"dog\",\"fox\",\"job\",\"boy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A fox is a small animal that can run fast.\"},{\"q\":\"What word means a small piece of furniture you lie on?\",\"options\":[\"cot\",\"pot\",\"box\",\"lot\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A cot is a small bed.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is a verb that means to move quickly?\",\"options\":[\"hop\",\"hot\",\"lot\",\"job\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Hop means to jump quickly.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a small container for food?\",\"options\":[\"pot\",\"box\",\"dog\",\"fox\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A pot is a container for cooking.\"},{\"q\":\"What word means a small toy?\",\"options\":[\"toy\",\"job\",\"lot\",\"cot\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Toy is a small plaything.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a small amount of something?\",\"options\":[\"lot\",\"hot\",\"dog\",\"fox\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Lot can mean a large amount, but in this family it is a word; the question is tricky – the best answer is \'lot\' as it appears in the list.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16492,11,3,'English','en','2.10 Diwali, the Festival of Lights','[\"Diwali is called the Festival of Lights.\",\"It celebrates the victory of good over evil.\",\"People light lamps (diya) and candles to brighten streets.\",\"Children play with sparklers and watch fireworks.\",\"Elders exchange gifts and sweets to greet each other.\",\"Families decorate homes with rangoli (colorful designs).\",\"Common Diwali foods include sweets like laddoos and kheer.\",\"People also make paper lanterns and clay forts for fun.\",\"Health care during Diwali: eat balanced food, stay hydrated, avoid too much sugar.\",\"Diwali brings happiness and removes sorrow.\",\"Sparklers, candles, lights, gifts, sweets, fireworks, streets, victory, delight are key words.\",\"Rangoli can be made with English letters or colors.\",\"Children can create their own greeting cards for friends.\",\"Diwali is a time for sharing love and joy.\",\"Remember to keep homes clean and safe during celebrations.\",\"Diwali lights symbolize hope and new beginnings.\",\"Families often pray for health and prosperity.\",\"Diwali is celebrated with music, dance, and family gatherings.\",\"The festival lasts for five days in many places.\",\"Diwali marks the end of the harvest season in some regions.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What does Diwali celebrate?\",\"options\":[\"The end of winter\",\"The victory of good over evil\",\"The start of school\",\"A new year\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Diwali marks the triumph of good over evil.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT a typical Diwali activity?\",\"options\":[\"Lighting candles\",\"Eating sweets\",\"Playing chess\",\"Watching fireworks\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Playing chess is not a common Diwali activity.\"},{\"q\":\"What is a \'diya\'?\",\"options\":[\"A type of sweet\",\"A small lamp\",\"A festival song\",\"A dance move\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A diya is a small oil lamp used in Diwali.\"},{\"q\":\"Who usually exchanges gifts during Diwali?\",\"options\":[\"Teachers\",\"Elders\",\"Teachers and elders\",\"Teachers, elders and students\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"All of them exchange gifts.\"},{\"q\":\"What do children use to make a rangoli?\",\"options\":[\"Painted stones\",\"English letters\",\"Stickers\",\"None of the above\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Children can use English letters to design rangoli.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is opposite to \'happiness\'?\",\"options\":[\"Sorrow\",\"Delight\",\"Victory\",\"Sparklers\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Sorrow is the opposite of happiness.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do to keep healthy during Diwali?\",\"options\":[\"Eat only sweets\",\"Drink lots of water\",\"Skip meals\",\"None of the above\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Staying hydrated helps health during celebrations.\"},{\"q\":\"What is a common material for making a clay fort?\",\"options\":[\"Clay\",\"Paper\",\"Wood\",\"Stone\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Clay is used to build a fort.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a Diwali greeting card activity?\",\"options\":[\"Drawing a paper lantern\",\"Writing a poem\",\"Reading a story\",\"All of the above\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"All are activities related to Diwali.\"},{\"q\":\"What does \'sparklers\' refer to?\",\"options\":[\"A type of food\",\"A decorative lamp\",\"A small firework\",\"A song\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Sparklers are small fireworks that sparkle.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16493,11,3,'English','en','3.1 Tiranga','[\"- The Tiranga is the flag of India.\",\"- It has three colours: saffron, white and green.\",\"- Saffron stands for courage, bravery and sacrifice.\",\"- White represents peace, truth and honesty.\",\"- Green symbolizes growth, nature and hope.\",\"- In the centre of the flag is the Ashoka Chakra (a blue wheel with 24 spokes).\",\"- The flag is called the National Flag of India.\",\"- We salute the flag every day to show respect and love for our country.\",\"- The national anthem is sung every day with pride.\",\"- The flag is flown high in the sky, showing our unity.\",\"- The flag’s colours are bright and beautiful.\",\"- The flag is a symbol of our freedom and independence.\",\"- Children learn to sing the anthem and salute the flag.\",\"- The flag is made of cotton or polyester fabric.\",\"- The flag should be kept clean and not damaged.\",\"- The flag is hung on flag poles during national holidays.\",\"- The flag is a source of pride for every Indian child.\",\"- The flag is a reminder of our duty to protect the nation.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What colour on the Tiranga represents courage?\",\"options\":[\"Saffron\",\"White\",\"Green\",\"Blue\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Saffron stands for courage and sacrifice.\"},{\"q\":\"Which colour on the flag stands for peace?\",\"options\":[\"Saffron\",\"White\",\"Green\",\"Red\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"White symbolizes peace and truth.\"},{\"q\":\"What is in the centre of the Tiranga?\",\"options\":[\"Ashoka Chakra\",\"Red star\",\"Moon\",\"Sun\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The Ashoka Chakra is a blue wheel with 24 spokes.\"},{\"q\":\"How many spokes does the Ashoka Chakra have?\",\"options\":[\"12\",\"18\",\"24\",\"30\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Chakra has 24 spokes.\"},{\"q\":\"When do we salute the flag?\",\"options\":[\"Only on Independence Day\",\"Every day\",\"Only during festivals\",\"Only at school\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"We salute the flag every day.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the national anthem of India called?\",\"options\":[\"Jana Gana Mana\",\"Vande Mataram\",\"Saare Jahan Se Acha\",\"Rang De Basanti\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The national anthem is Jana Gana Mana.\"},{\"q\":\"Which colour represents growth on the flag?\",\"options\":[\"Saffron\",\"White\",\"Green\",\"Blue\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Green symbolizes growth and nature.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main message of the national anthem?\",\"options\":[\"Love for the flag\",\"Unity and freedom\",\"Respect for elders\",\"Patience and kindness\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The anthem calls for unity and freedom.\"},{\"q\":\"The flag is also called what?\",\"options\":[\"National Flag\",\"State Flag\",\"Regional Flag\",\"Local Flag\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"It is the National Flag of India.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT a colour of the Tiranga?\",\"options\":[\"Saffron\",\"White\",\"Green\",\"Blue\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Blue is not a colour of the flag.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16494,11,3,'English','en','3.2 Word Family - V','[\"Word family V words have the same ending sound ‘‑un’ or ‘‑up’ or ‘‑ut’ etc.\",\"The words in this chapter are: bus, but, bug, bun, cut, cup, fun, gun, gum, mud, hut, tub, nut, pup, run, rub, rug, jug, sun, sum.\",\"All these words rhyme because they end with the same vowel and consonant sound.\",\"Students can practice by saying the words aloud and noticing the common sound.\",\"They can also write sentences using these words to see how they fit in context.\",\"The chapter shows how changing the first letter can give a new word with the same ending sound.\",\"For example: run – bun – sun – fun – gun – cup – cut – etc.\",\"The picture activity asks students to complete the missing first letter of each word.\",\"The invitation card activity encourages writing sentences using the words from the word family.\",\"Students should read the sentences carefully and identify the word family words.\",\"They can underline the word family words in the text.\",\"They can also create their own sentences with these words.\",\"The chapter helps build phonics awareness and spelling skills.\",\"It also introduces simple sentence structure with subject, verb and object.\",\"Students should practice writing and reading aloud to improve fluency.\",\"They can use flashcards to quiz each other on the word family.\",\"Repetition of the words helps memory retention.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the word that means a small cup used for drinking?\",\"options\":[\"cup\",\"cut\",\"cup\",\"cud\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The word \'cup\' refers to a small container for liquids.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a small round food item that can be eaten?\",\"options\":[\"bun\",\"but\",\"bug\",\"bub\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A \'bun\' is a small, round bread.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means to move quickly on foot?\",\"options\":[\"run\",\"rub\",\"rug\",\"rut\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"To \'run\' is to move fast on foot.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means to cut something with a sharp tool?\",\"options\":[\"cut\",\"cud\",\"cud\",\"cud\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"To \'cut\' means to divide with a blade.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a small container for holding liquids?\",\"options\":[\"cup\",\"cut\",\"cud\",\"cud\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A \'cup\' holds liquids.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a small round piece of bread that can be sweet or savory?\",\"options\":[\"bun\",\"but\",\"bug\",\"bub\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A \'bun\' is a small bread.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a small, round, sweet treat often eaten as dessert?\",\"options\":[\"bun\",\"but\",\"bug\",\"bub\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A \'bun\' can also be sweet.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a small container for holding food or drink?\",\"options\":[\"cup\",\"cut\",\"cud\",\"cud\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A \'cup\' holds food or drink.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a small, round, sweet or savory bread item?\",\"options\":[\"bun\",\"but\",\"bug\",\"bub\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A \'bun\' is a small bread.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a small, round, sweet or savory bread item that can be eaten with butter?\",\"options\":[\"bun\",\"but\",\"bug\",\"bub\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A \'bun\' can be eaten with butter.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16495,11,3,'English','en','3.3 Kind Radha','[\"Radha is a kind girl who helps others.\",\"She sees a blind man struggling to cross the road.\",\"She helps him by holding his hand and guiding him.\",\"The blind man thanks her and feels happy.\",\"Radha’s headmistress sees this and is proud of her.\",\"She rewards Radha with a story book.\",\"The story teaches that helping people is good.\",\"A blind person is called a ‘Divyang’ person in the story.\",\"The main idea is that kindness and help are important.\",\"The story shows how a small act can make a big difference.\",\"Radha’s action shows courage and empathy.\",\"The headmistress praises Radha for being helpful.\",\"The reward is a story book, a symbol of learning.\",\"The story encourages students to help others too.\",\"It also shows that kindness is appreciated by teachers and friends.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What did Radha see on her way to school?\",\"options\":[\"A blind man\",\"A dog\",\"A teacher\",\"A bus\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Radha saw a blind man struggling to cross the road.\"},{\"q\":\"How did Radha help the blind man?\",\"options\":[\"By giving him money\",\"By holding his hand\",\"By calling a taxi\",\"By ignoring him\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"She held his hand and guided him across the road.\"},{\"q\":\"What did the headmistress give Radha as a reward?\",\"options\":[\"A pencil\",\"A story book\",\"A sticker\",\"A candy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"She gave Radha a story book.\"},{\"q\":\"What is another word used for a blind person in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Divyang\",\"Smart\",\"Fast\",\"Tall\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The story calls the blind man a ‘Divyang’ person.\"},{\"q\":\"Why did the headmistress feel proud of Radha?\",\"options\":[\"Because she was late\",\"Because she helped a person\",\"Because she ate lunch\",\"Because she sang a song\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"She was proud because Radha helped a blind man.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT mentioned in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Radha’s friends praised her\",\"Radha was given a book\",\"Radha was late for school\",\"Radha helped a blind man\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The story does not say Radha was late.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word ‘Divyang’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"Blind\",\"Smart\",\"Fast\",\"Tall\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"‘Divyang’ refers to a person with a disability, here a blind man.\"},{\"q\":\"What did the blind man say after Radha helped him?\",\"options\":[\"Thank you\",\"Goodbye\",\"Sorry\",\"Please\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"He thanked Radha.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a key theme of the story?\",\"options\":[\"Competition\",\"Helping others\",\"Winning prizes\",\"Being selfish\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The story’s theme is helping others.\"},{\"q\":\"What did Radha’s teachers and friends do after the incident?\",\"options\":[\"They ignored her\",\"They praised her\",\"They scolded her\",\"They left school\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"They praised her for her kindness.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16496,11,3,'English','en','3.4 Butterfly','[\"Butterfly is a colourful insect with two pairs of wings.\",\"Its wings are covered with tiny scales that give it bright colours.\",\"Butterfly starts life as a caterpillar (larva).\",\"The caterpillar eats leaves and grows larger.\",\"When ready, it forms a chrysalis (pupa) and changes into a butterfly.\",\"Butterfly has a long, thin body and two antennae on its head.\",\"It flies by beating its wings fast.\",\"Butterfly feeds on nectar from flowers using a long tongue called a proboscis.\",\"Butterfly can be found in gardens, parks and fields.\",\"It likes warm sunny places.\",\"Butterfly has a short life, usually a few weeks.\",\"The song in the lesson is a simple rhyme about a butterfly visiting a garden.\",\"Students can sing the rhyme to remember the words “butterfly”, “garden”, “blossom”, “scene”.\",\"The activity makes a paper butterfly by folding, cutting, rolling and decorating.\",\"The paper butterfly has a body and two wings that can be stuck on a wall.\",\"The word “fly” is repeated to show the action of a butterfly.\",\"The lesson encourages listening, repeating, looking, writing, and making.\",\"The butterfly’s colours in the picture are red, blue, yellow, pink, orange, green.\",\"The butterfly is positioned in different places: above, near, under, between, behind.\",\"The activity helps students learn vocabulary and fine‑motor skills.\",\"The lesson is suitable for Standard 3 English learners.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the main colour of the butterfly shown in the picture?\",\"options\":[\"Red\",\"Blue\",\"Yellow\",\"Green\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The picture shows a red butterfly.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is NOT mentioned in the rhyme?\",\"options\":[\"garden\",\"scene\",\"rain\",\"flower\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The rhyme mentions garden, scene, flower but not rain.\"},{\"q\":\"What do butterflies eat?\",\"options\":[\"Leaves\",\"Nectar\",\"Seeds\",\"Water\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Butterflies feed on nectar from flowers.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first step in making a paper butterfly?\",\"options\":[\"Cut a curve\",\"Fold a square paper\",\"Roll a strip\",\"Decorate\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The first step is to fold a square paper in half.\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the butterfly positioned in the picture?\",\"options\":[\"Above\",\"Near\",\"Under\",\"Between\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The picture shows the butterfly above the ground.\"},{\"q\":\"What word is repeated to show the butterfly’s action?\",\"options\":[\"Fly\",\"Run\",\"Jump\",\"Swim\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The word “fly” is repeated.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT a colour of the butterfly?\",\"options\":[\"Pink\",\"Orange\",\"Purple\",\"Green\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The butterfly colours are pink, orange, green, but not purple.\"},{\"q\":\"What do you do after making the paper butterfly?\",\"options\":[\"Stick it on the wall\",\"Throw it away\",\"Put it in a jar\",\"Give it to a friend\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The instruction is to stick it on the wall.\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the butterfly is made by rolling a strip?\",\"options\":[\"Wings\",\"Body\",\"Head\",\"Antennae\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The body is made by rolling a small strip.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of the lesson?\",\"options\":[\"To learn a song\",\"To learn about insects\",\"To practice writing\",\"All of the above\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The lesson covers singing, listening, looking, writing, and making.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16497,11,3,'English','en','3.5 The Ant and the Grasshopper','[\"The ant is a small, hardworking insect that carries food.\",\"The grasshopper is a fun-loving insect that likes to sing and jump.\",\"In summer the sun is hot and bright.\",\"The ant collects food in summer to prepare for the rainy season.\",\"The grasshopper does not collect food and only plays in summer.\",\"When the rainy season comes, the ground becomes wet and the grasshopper feels cold and hungry.\",\"The ant has enough food stored for the rainy days.\",\"The ant shares its food with the grasshopper when the grasshopper is hungry.\",\"The moral: work when it is time to work and play when it is time to play.\",\"The ant is right because it prepares for the future.\",\"The grasshopper learns to work after the rainy season.\",\"The story shows the importance of planning ahead.\",\"The ant is a good example of a careful worker.\",\"The grasshopper shows that playing is also important.\",\"The lesson is that both work and play have their places.\",\"The ant’s food is carried in a small bag or on its back.\",\"The grasshopper’s wings get wet when it rains.\",\"The ant’s house is a safe place during rain.\",\"The story uses simple language for young readers.\",\"The characters are clear and easy to remember.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the ant carrying in the story?\",\"options\":[\"A bag of mangoes\",\"A grain of rice\",\"A leaf\",\"A flower\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The ant carries a grain of rice.\"},{\"q\":\"Which season does the ant prepare for?\",\"options\":[\"Winter\",\"Summer\",\"Rainy season\",\"Spring\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The ant prepares for the rainy season.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the grasshopper do in summer?\",\"options\":[\"Collect food\",\"Sing and play\",\"Build a house\",\"Sleep\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The grasshopper sings and plays.\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the ant keep working?\",\"options\":[\"Because it likes to play\",\"Because it wants to be a singer\",\"Because it needs food for rain\",\"Because it is bored\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The ant needs food for the rainy days.\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the grasshopper when it rains?\",\"options\":[\"It flies away\",\"It gets wet and hungry\",\"It sings louder\",\"It builds a house\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The grasshopper gets wet and hungry.\"},{\"q\":\"Who shares food with the grasshopper?\",\"options\":[\"The ant\",\"The grasshopper\",\"Both\",\"No one\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The ant shares its food.\"},{\"q\":\"What lesson does the story teach?\",\"options\":[\"Always play\",\"Always work\",\"Work when it is time to work and play when it is time to play\",\"Never share\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The moral is to work when it is time to work and play when it is time to play.\"},{\"q\":\"Which season is the sun hot?\",\"options\":[\"Winter\",\"Rainy\",\"Summer\",\"Spring\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The sun is hot in summer.\"},{\"q\":\"What did the grasshopper do in summer?\",\"options\":[\"Collected food\",\"Sang and jumped\",\"Built a house\",\"Slept\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The grasshopper sang and jumped.\"},{\"q\":\"Who is right in the story?\",\"options\":[\"The ant\",\"The grasshopper\",\"Both\",\"Neither\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The ant is right because it prepared for the future.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16498,11,3,'English','en','3.6 Word Family - VI','[\"Word family means words that share the same root or base word.\",\"In this chapter we learn words that start with the letters **b**, **c**, **h**, **l**, **m**, **p**, **t**, **w** and end with **oo** or **ook**.\",\"Examples: book, cook, hook, look, took, wood, wool, good, tool, foot, shook, stood.\",\"The root word is the part that stays the same in all words of the family.\",\"Changing the first letter or adding a few letters gives new words but the meaning stays related.\",\"The words in this chapter help you read and write better because they look similar.\",\"Practice by reading the sentences and repeating the words aloud.\",\"Remember: all words in a family have the same sound in the middle, like **oo** in *book* and *look*.\",\"Use the pictures to match the words with their meanings.\",\"When you see a new word, try to find its family word to remember it easier.\",\"Keep a list of word families in your notebook and add new words as you learn them.\",\"Ask your teacher to show you more pictures of the same family.\",\"Try to make your own sentences using the new words.\",\"Listen carefully when the teacher reads the words aloud.\",\"Repeat after the teacher to improve pronunciation.\",\"Write the words in bold to see the common part clearly.\",\"Review the word families every week to keep them fresh in your mind.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which word is NOT part of the word family that starts with \'b\' and ends with \'ook\'?\",\"options\":[\"book\",\"cook\",\"hook\",\"look\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Look does not start with \'b\'.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the common part in the words book, cook, hook, and look?\",\"options\":[\"boo\",\"ook\",\"ook\",\"ook\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The middle sound is \'ook\'.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a place where many books are kept?\",\"options\":[\"library\",\"computer\",\"banana\",\"camera\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A library is a place with many books.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a device used to take pictures?\",\"options\":[\"camera\",\"computer\",\"holiday\",\"book\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A camera takes pictures.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a long period of rest?\",\"options\":[\"holiday\",\"computer\",\"library\",\"banana\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Holiday is a rest period.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a large animal with a long trunk?\",\"options\":[\"elephant\",\"computer\",\"holiday\",\"banana\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"An elephant has a long trunk.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a sweet fruit that is yellow?\",\"options\":[\"banana\",\"camera\",\"library\",\"elephant\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A banana is a yellow fruit.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a piece of wood used for building?\",\"options\":[\"wood\",\"tool\",\"foot\",\"shook\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Wood is a piece of timber.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a piece of fabric made from sheep?\",\"options\":[\"wool\",\"wood\",\"look\",\"took\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Wool is made from sheep.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a small piece of metal used to hold things together?\",\"options\":[\"tool\",\"good\",\"hook\",\"foot\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A tool can hold or fix things.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16499,11,3,'English','en','3.7 Technology Around Us','[\"Technology is a tool that helps us in many ways.\",\"A tablet is a small computer that you can hold in your hands.\",\"An app is a small software program that runs on a tablet or phone.\",\"A robot is a machine that can do tasks for us, like cleaning or helping doctors.\",\"A keyboard has keys but no doors – it lets us type on a computer.\",\"A calculator helps us add numbers like 1 + 1.\",\"A camera takes pictures with one click and keeps memories.\",\"A book‑like device with keys is a computer – it shows pictures and words and lets us write.\",\"A drone flies high and takes photos from the sky.\",\"A storage device keeps files, pictures, games and more.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is a tablet used for?\",\"options\":[\"Playing games only\",\"Watching videos and reading apps\",\"Cooking food\",\"Cleaning rooms\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A tablet can run apps to watch videos, read, and play games.\"},{\"q\":\"Which device helps doctors perform surgeries?\",\"options\":[\"A phone\",\"A robot\",\"A calculator\",\"A drone\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Robots can assist doctors in performing precise surgeries.\"},{\"q\":\"What does a keyboard have?\",\"options\":[\"Doors\",\"Keys\",\"Buttons\",\"Lights\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A keyboard has keys that let us type.\"},{\"q\":\"Which device takes pictures with one click?\",\"options\":[\"A phone\",\"A camera\",\"A robot\",\"A drone\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A camera captures images instantly with one click.\"},{\"q\":\"Which device shows pictures and words and helps you write?\",\"options\":[\"A drone\",\"A computer\",\"A robot\",\"A phone\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A computer displays pictures and words and lets you write.\"},{\"q\":\"What flies high without a crew and takes photos from the sky?\",\"options\":[\"A robot\",\"A drone\",\"A tablet\",\"A camera\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A drone is a small aircraft that can fly and take photos.\"},{\"q\":\"Which device keeps your files, pictures, and games?\",\"options\":[\"A phone\",\"A computer\",\"A storage device\",\"A robot\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A storage device (like a hard drive) stores files, pictures, and games.\"},{\"q\":\"What helps you count 1 + 1?\",\"options\":[\"A drone\",\"A calculator\",\"A robot\",\"A tablet\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A calculator is used to add numbers.\"},{\"q\":\"Which device is described as having keys but no doors?\",\"options\":[\"A robot\",\"A keyboard\",\"A drone\",\"A camera\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A keyboard has keys but no doors.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main benefit of technology mentioned in the conversation?\",\"options\":[\"It makes us lazy\",\"It helps us learn and enjoy\",\"It replaces teachers\",\"It is expensive\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Technology helps us learn and enjoy at the same time.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16500,11,3,'English','en','3.8 Sant Gora Kumbhar','[\"Sant Gora Kumbhar was a saint from Maharashtra.\",\"He lived in the village ‘Ter’ in Dharashiv district.\",\"He was a potter by occupation.\",\"He made pots with his hands and moulded clay.\",\"He believed in hard work and honesty.\",\"He taught people to work sincerely and be kind.\",\"He sang Abhangas and performed Kirtanas.\",\"He was respected by people and called ‘Kaka’.\",\"He also described other occupations like goldsmith, blacksmith, carpenter.\",\"He encouraged people to be good to others.\",\"He was a contemporary of Sant Namdev and Dnyaneshwar.\",\"He worked with clay, gold, hammer, wood and other tools.\",\"He made pots, jewellery, tools, tables and chairs.\",\"He was known for his honesty and hard work.\",\"He was a role model for honest and sincere work.\",\"He was a saint who used his occupation to teach moral values.\",\"He lived long ago and his life is remembered in Maharashtra.\",\"He was a potter who used his craft to spread good teachings.\",\"He sang Abhangas to inspire people.\",\"He performed Kirtanas to spread good deeds.\",\"He was respected by people for his honesty.\",\"He was called ‘Kaka’ by people.\",\"He was a saint who taught through his work.\",\"He was a saint who lived in the same time as Sant Namdev and Dnyaneshwar.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What was Sant Gora Kumbhar’s main occupation?\",\"options\":[\"Potter\",\"Goldsmith\",\"Blacksmith\",\"Carpenter\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"He was a potter.\"},{\"q\":\"Which village did Sant Gora Kumbhar live in?\",\"options\":[\"Ter\",\"Pune\",\"Mumbai\",\"Nagpur\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"He lived in the village ‘Ter’.\"},{\"q\":\"What did Sant Gora Kumbhar believe in?\",\"options\":[\"Hard work and honesty\",\"Wealth and power\",\"Magic and spells\",\"Traveling the world\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"He believed in hard work and honesty.\"},{\"q\":\"What did Sant Gora Kumbhar sing to inspire people?\",\"options\":[\"Abhangas\",\"Songs of love\",\"Songs of war\",\"Songs of nature\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"He sang Abhangas.\"},{\"q\":\"What was the nickname given to Sant Gora Kumbhar by people?\",\"options\":[\"Kaka\",\"Guru\",\"Baba\",\"Maharshi\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"People called him ‘Kaka’.\"},{\"q\":\"Which saint lived at the same time as Sant Gora Kumbhar?\",\"options\":[\"Sant Namdev\",\"Shivaji\",\"Maharaja Pratap\",\"Raja Bhimrao\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"He lived in the same time as Sant Namdev.\"},{\"q\":\"What moral did Sant Gora Kumbhar teach people?\",\"options\":[\"Be honest and kind\",\"Be rich and powerful\",\"Be brave and strong\",\"Be quiet and silent\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"He taught people to be honest and kind.\"},{\"q\":\"What other occupations did Sant Gora Kumbhar describe?\",\"options\":[\"Goldsmith, blacksmith, carpenter\",\"Teacher, farmer, soldier\",\"Doctor, lawyer, engineer\",\"Singer, dancer, painter\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"He described goldsmith, blacksmith, carpenter.\"},{\"q\":\"What did Sant Gora Kumbhar use to make pots?\",\"options\":[\"Clay\",\"Gold\",\"Wood\",\"Stone\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"He moulded clay to make pots.\"},{\"q\":\"What type of performances did Sant Gora Kumbhar do?\",\"options\":[\"Kirtanas\",\"Dances\",\"Poetry recitations\",\"Drama plays\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"He performed Kirtanas.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16501,11,3,'English','en','3.9 Sh... sh... sh...','[\"- The chapter is about the sound ‘sh’ and words that start with ‘sh’.\",\"- ‘sh’ is a consonant sound made by putting the tongue close to the roof of the mouth and blowing air.\",\"- Words that start with ‘sh’ include: shop, shoe, sheep, ship, shush, shiver, shadow, shell, she, sheaf, shoo, shush, shiver, shiver, shiver.\",\"- In the book, you will see many sentences with the word ‘sh’ repeated to help you hear the sound.\",\"- The book also teaches how to write words that start with ‘br’ (e.g., bread, brush, brother, brown).\",\"- Alphabetical order: words are arranged from A to Z. For example, shoe, shop, sheep, ship.\",\"- To make a sentence, put the words in the right order and add punctuation marks like commas and periods.\",\"- When you write a sentence, start with a capital letter and end with a period, question mark or exclamation mark.\",\"- Practice makes you better: write the words that start with ‘br’, ‘sh’, ‘sc’, ‘tr’ etc. in a word bank.\",\"- The chapter also has fill‑in‑the‑blank and rearrange‑the‑words activities to help you use the new words.\",\"- Remember to read the sentences aloud to hear the ‘sh’ sound clearly.\",\"- The ‘sh’ sound is often used in words that mean something small or quiet, like ‘shush’ or ‘shiver’.\",\"- In the book, you will find a list of words that start with ‘sh’ and you can try to use them in your own sentences.\",\"- The teacher’s notes suggest making a word register – a list of new words you learn each week.\",\"- When you see a word that starts with ‘sh’, try to think of other words that also start with ‘sh’ to build your vocabulary.\",\"- The chapter ends with a short quiz to test your understanding of the ‘sh’ sound and the words you learned.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which word starts with the sound ‘sh’?\",\"options\":[\"shark\",\"tiger\",\"apple\",\"lion\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"‘shark’ begins with the ‘sh’ sound.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct alphabetical order of the words: shoe, shop, sheep, ship?\",\"options\":[\"shoe, shop, sheep, ship\",\"shoe, sheep, shop, ship\",\"sheep, shoe, shop, ship\",\"shop, shoe, sheep, ship\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Alphabetical order places ‘shoe’ before ‘shop’, ‘sheep’, and ‘ship’.\"},{\"q\":\"Fill in the blank: I will ______ my teeth after breakfast.\",\"options\":[\"brush\",\"wash\",\"eat\",\"play\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The correct word is ‘brush’.\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence uses the word ‘sh’ correctly?\",\"options\":[\"She sells sea shells by the sea shore.\",\"She sells sea shells by the sea shore.\",\"She sells sea shells by the sea shore.\",\"She sells sea shells by the sea shore.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"All options are the same; the correct sentence is the one that repeats the ‘sh’ sound.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word ‘sheep’?\",\"options\":[\"A type of fruit\",\"A type of animal\",\"A type of vehicle\",\"A type of plant\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Sheep is a type of animal.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is NOT a correct ‘sh’ word from the list?\",\"options\":[\"shush\",\"shiver\",\"shark\",\"shampoo\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"‘shark’ does not start with the ‘sh’ sound in this context.\"},{\"q\":\"Choose the correct sentence with punctuation: ______ the blue blanket the.\",\"options\":[\"Warn is\",\"Warn is\",\"Warn is\",\"Warn is\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The correct sentence is ‘Warn is blue blanket the.’\"},{\"q\":\"Which word starts with ‘br’?\",\"options\":[\"bread\",\"shark\",\"apple\",\"fish\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"‘bread’ starts with ‘br’.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct order of the words: chair, chalk, chase, chess?\",\"options\":[\"chalk, chair, chase, chess\",\"chair, chalk, chase, chess\",\"chair, chase, chalk, chess\",\"chess, chair, chalk, chase\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Alphabetical order: chair, chalk, chase, chess.\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence is correctly punctuated?\",\"options\":[\"The table the on is spoon the\",\"The table the on is spoon the\",\"The table the on is spoon the\",\"The table the on is spoon the\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The correct sentence is ‘The table the on is spoon the.’\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16502,11,3,'English','en','3.10 Tarabai Modak','[\"Tarabai Modak was born on 19 April 1892 in Maharashtra.\",\"She loved children and wanted every child to go to school.\",\"In the early 1900s many children in villages did not attend school.\",\"She started the first balwadi (pre‑school) in Bordi village, Thane.\",\"A balwadi is a small school where children learn through play, songs and games.\",\"She used toys, songs and games to make learning fun and easy.\",\"She trained children to become teachers who teach in fun ways.\",\"She worked especially for tribal children in Maharashtra.\",\"She received the Padma Bhushan award for her social work.\",\"She passed away on 31 August 1973.\",\"She is called the Mother of Pre‑school Education in India.\",\"Her work shows that children learn best by playing.\",\"She believed that learning should be enjoyable and interactive.\",\"She encouraged teachers to use games and songs in lessons.\",\"Her life teaches us to help others and make learning fun.\"]','[{\"q\":\"When was Tarabai Modak born?\",\"options\":[\"19 April 1892\",\"1 January 1900\",\"15 August 1890\",\"31 August 1973\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Her birth date is 19 April 1892.\"},{\"q\":\"What did Tarabai Modak start in Bordi village?\",\"options\":[\"A university\",\"A hospital\",\"A balwadi\",\"A library\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"She started the first balwadi (pre‑school).\"},{\"q\":\"Which award did she receive?\",\"options\":[\"Nobel Prize\",\"Padma Shri\",\"Padma Bhushan\",\"Sangeet Natak Akademi Award\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"She received the Padma Bhushan.\"},{\"q\":\"What is a balwadi?\",\"options\":[\"A type of toy\",\"A small school for children\",\"A dance form\",\"A cooking class\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A balwadi is a small pre‑school where children learn by play.\"},{\"q\":\"Tarabai Modak believed children learn best by?\",\"options\":[\"Reading books\",\"Playing\",\"Listening to lectures\",\"Watching TV\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"She believed learning is best through play.\"},{\"q\":\"She worked especially for children from which group?\",\"options\":[\"Urban children\",\"Tribal children\",\"School teachers\",\"Farmers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"She worked for tribal children in Maharashtra.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the term \'Mother of Pre‑school Education\' refer to?\",\"options\":[\"A famous mother in a story\",\"The first woman teacher in India\",\"Tarabai Modak\",\"A type of school\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"It refers to Tarabai Modak.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT a method she used in teaching?\",\"options\":[\"Toys\",\"Songs\",\"Games\",\"Strict exams\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"She used toys, songs and games, not strict exams.\"},{\"q\":\"Tarabai Modak died in which year?\",\"options\":[\"1973\",\"1980\",\"1965\",\"1990\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"She died on 31 August 1973.\"},{\"q\":\"Which state is Tarabai Modak associated with?\",\"options\":[\"Karnataka\",\"Maharashtra\",\"Tamil Nadu\",\"Kerala\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"She was from Maharashtra.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16503,11,3,'English','en','4.1 Colour Song','[\"Red is the colour of an apple, cherries and strawberries.\",\"Blue is the colour of the sky, baby things and my sister’s eyes.\",\"Yellow is the colour of the sun, lemonade and a baby chick.\",\"Green is the colour of leaves, green peas and a watermelon.\",\"Orange is the colour of oranges, carrots and a pumpkin.\",\"Purple is the colour of grapes, grape juice and a brinjal (eggplant).\",\"The rainbow has seven colours: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo (purple) and violet (purple).\",\"A rainbow appears after rain and looks like a bow.\",\"Colours are used to describe objects in our world.\",\"The song helps children remember which colour goes with which object.\",\"Rearranging letters can help find colour names.\",\"Matching colours with objects helps learning vocabulary.\",\"Rhyming words make learning fun and memorable.\",\"The poem encourages children to sing about colours.\",\"Teachers can ask students to create picture dictionaries for new words.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which colour is mentioned for an apple in the song?\",\"options\":[\"Red\",\"Blue\",\"Green\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The song says \\\"Red is the colour for an apple to eat.\\\"\"},{\"q\":\"What colour is used for the big blue sky?\",\"options\":[\"Red\",\"Blue\",\"Green\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The song states \\\"Blue is the colour for the big blue sky.\\\"\"},{\"q\":\"Which colour is used for a baby chick?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"Yellow\",\"Red\",\"Green\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The song says \\\"Yellow is the colour of a baby chick.\\\"\"},{\"q\":\"Which colour is used for a pumpkin?\",\"options\":[\"Orange\",\"Purple\",\"Blue\",\"Green\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The song says \\\"Orange is the colour of a pumpkin.\\\"\"},{\"q\":\"Which colour is used for a bunch of grapes?\",\"options\":[\"Purple\",\"Orange\",\"Red\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The song says \\\"Purple is the colour for a bunch of grapes.\\\"\"},{\"q\":\"What colour is used for the leaves on trees?\",\"options\":[\"Red\",\"Blue\",\"Green\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The song says \\\"Green is the colour for the leaves on the trees.\\\"\"},{\"q\":\"Which colour is used for a watermelon?\",\"options\":[\"Red\",\"Green\",\"Blue\",\"Orange\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The song says \\\"Green is the colour of a watermelon.\\\"\"},{\"q\":\"Which colour is used for a brinjal?\",\"options\":[\"Purple\",\"Orange\",\"Red\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The song says \\\"Purple is the colour for a brinjal.\\\"\"},{\"q\":\"Which colour is used for a big blue sky?\",\"options\":[\"Green\",\"Red\",\"Blue\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The song repeats that blue is the colour for the big blue sky.\"},{\"q\":\"Which colour is used for a baby chick?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"Red\",\"Yellow\",\"Green\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The song repeats that yellow is the colour of a baby chick.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16504,11,3,'English','en','4.2 Source of Energy','[\"Solar energy is produced by the Sun and is clean and renewable.\",\"Solar panels are special devices that change sunlight into electricity.\",\"They work even when the main electricity supply is off.\",\"Solar power does not create pollution or smoke.\",\"Wind can also produce electricity, but the text says it cannot, which is incorrect; however, for this class we focus on solar energy.\",\"Food gives us energy for our bodies, not electricity for lights.\",\"Solar panels give light, warmth and electricity to homes.\",\"Using solar panels helps save money and keeps Earth green.\",\"The Sun is the main source of power for our planet.\",\"Solar panels are placed on roofs to capture sunlight.\",\"When the Sun is high, panels produce more electricity.\",\"Solar energy is safe for the environment.\",\"Solar panels help reduce dependence on fossil fuels.\",\"Solar power can be used for lights, fans, and TVs.\",\"Solar energy is a clean source of power for homes and schools.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What do solar panels do?\",\"options\":[\"They produce heat\",\"They convert sunlight into electricity\",\"They store water\",\"They make noise\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Solar panels change sunlight into electricity.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a benefit of solar energy?\",\"options\":[\"It creates pollution\",\"It saves money\",\"It uses fossil fuels\",\"It produces smoke\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Solar energy saves money and is pollution-free.\"},{\"q\":\"True or False: Solar panels work only when the main electricity is on.\",\"options\":[\"True\",\"False\",\"Maybe\",\"Not sure\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"They work even when the main electricity is off.\"},{\"q\":\"Which source gives us light, warmth and electricity?\",\"options\":[\"Wind\",\"Water\",\"Sun\",\"Moon\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The Sun is the source of light, warmth and electricity.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main message of the conversation between Manu and Anil?\",\"options\":[\"Solar panels are useless\",\"Solar panels are harmful\",\"Solar panels are good for Earth\",\"Solar panels are expensive\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"They emphasize solar panels are good for Earth.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT mentioned as a benefit of solar panels?\",\"options\":[\"Reduces pollution\",\"Saves money\",\"Produces smoke\",\"Keeps Earth green\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Solar panels do not produce smoke.\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity is suggested for students?\",\"options\":[\"Draw a picture\",\"Write a poem\",\"Make a short oral presentation\",\"Sing a song\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Students are encouraged to make short oral presentations.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main source of energy for our bodies?\",\"options\":[\"Sunlight\",\"Food\",\"Electricity\",\"Wind\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"We get energy from food.\"},{\"q\":\"Which statement is FALSE according to the text?\",\"options\":[\"Solar panels convert sunlight into electricity\",\"Wind can not produce electricity\",\"Solar energy pollutes the Earth\",\"We get energy from food\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The text incorrectly says solar energy pollutes Earth.\"},{\"q\":\"What should students observe about the Sun?\",\"options\":[\"Its color\",\"Its position at different times\",\"Its size\",\"Its sound\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Students should observe the Sun\'s position in morning, noon, evening.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16505,11,3,'English','en','4.3 Word Family - VII','[\"• Words with the sound ‘ee’ are called a word family.\",\"• In this family the letters ‘ee’ stay the same in all words.\",\"• Examples: bee, see, jeep, keep, meet, deep, feet, peel, knee, fee, need, peep, week, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep, jeep, bee, see, deep, feet, knee, keep\",\"• When you read a word, listen for the ‘ee’ sound like in ‘see’ or ‘deep’.\",\"• You can make new words by adding a prefix or suffix to a word in this family, e.g., ‘kept’, ‘keeps’, ‘keening’.\",\"• Practice by writing sentences with words that have ‘ee’.\",\"• The teacher can ask students to name objects around the school that have ‘ee’ in their name.\",\"• Repetition and singing the words helps memory.\",\"• Use flashcards with pictures to show the words.\",\"• Encourage students to read aloud to hear the ‘ee’ sound.\",\"• Ask students to find other words that have ‘ee’ but are not in the list.\",\"• Write the words in a notebook and colour them to remember.\",\"• The word family helps build spelling and vocabulary skills.\",\"• Keep practicing by adding new words to the list each week.\",\"• Review the list regularly to reinforce learning.\",\"• Use the words in simple sentences like “The bee is in the tree.”\",\"• The ‘ee’ sound is short, like in ‘see’ and ‘deep’.\",\"• The ‘ee’ sound is long, like in ‘bee’ and ‘meet’.\",\"• Both short and long ‘ee’ sounds belong to the same word family.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which word has the long ‘ee’ sound?\",\"options\":[\"bee\",\"jam\",\"cat\",\"bus\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"‘bee’ has the long ‘ee’ sound.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the word for a vehicle that can carry many people?\",\"options\":[\"jeep\",\"bus\",\"bike\",\"train\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A jeep is a large vehicle.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means to keep something safe?\",\"options\":[\"keep\",\"meet\",\"deep\",\"pee\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"‘keep’ means to hold or store.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is a body part that touches the ground?\",\"options\":[\"feet\",\"bee\",\"tree\",\"jam\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"‘feet’ are the body parts that touch the ground.\"},{\"q\":\"What word means to gather or come together?\",\"options\":[\"meet\",\"deep\",\"bee\",\"jam\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"‘meet’ means to gather.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is a fruit that is red?\",\"options\":[\"red\",\"tree\",\"bee\",\"jam\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"‘red’ is a colour, not a fruit.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a small, sweet fruit?\",\"options\":[\"jam\",\"tree\",\"bee\",\"deep\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"‘jam’ is a sweet fruit spread.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is a small insect that makes honey?\",\"options\":[\"bee\",\"jam\",\"tree\",\"deep\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"‘bee’ makes honey.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means to look at something?\",\"options\":[\"see\",\"deep\",\"bee\",\"meet\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"‘see’ means to look.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a long, narrow piece of wood?\",\"options\":[\"tee\",\"tree\",\"deep\",\"bee\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"‘tree’ is a long, narrow piece of wood.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16506,11,3,'English','en','4.4 A Trip to the Moon','[\"- The moon is a natural satellite of Earth.\",\"- It is round and appears bright at night.\",\"- A full moon is when the whole face of the moon is lit.\",\"- The moon has less gravity than Earth, so things can jump higher.\",\"- Astronauts wear special suits to stay safe in space.\",\"- The moon is a place where we can dream of exploring.\",\"- Gravity is the force that pulls objects toward the center of the Earth.\",\"- An astronaut is a person who travels in space.\",\"- On the moon, you can bounce like a ball because of low gravity.\",\"- The moon is waiting for future explorers.\",\"- We can make a paper rocket to learn about space travel.\",\"- We can write sentences using words like moon, bounce, dream, safe, less.\",\"- The moon is a big, beautiful object in the sky.\",\"- Space travel requires learning and dreaming.\",\"- The moon is a place for adventure and learning.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the moon?\",\"options\":[\"A satellite of Earth\",\"A planet\",\"A star\",\"A comet\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The moon orbits Earth.\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to your jump on the moon?\",\"options\":[\"You jump lower\",\"You jump higher\",\"You cannot jump\",\"You jump the same\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Less gravity lets you jump higher.\"},{\"q\":\"What do astronauts wear?\",\"options\":[\"Shoes\",\"Suits\",\"Hats\",\"Gloves\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Special suits keep them safe.\"},{\"q\":\"What is gravity?\",\"options\":[\"A force that pulls objects\",\"A force that pushes objects\",\"A type of light\",\"A type of sound\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Gravity pulls objects toward Earth.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a person who travels in space?\",\"options\":[\"Astronaut\",\"Teacher\",\"Student\",\"Doctor\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Astronaut travels in space.\"},{\"q\":\"What can you do on the moon because of less gravity?\",\"options\":[\"Run fast\",\"Jump high\",\"Sit still\",\"Sleep\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"You can jump higher.\"},{\"q\":\"What is a full moon?\",\"options\":[\"Moon is dark\",\"Moon is bright\",\"Moon is small\",\"Moon is invisible\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Full moon is fully lit.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a dream?\",\"options\":[\"Bounce\",\"Safe\",\"Dream\",\"Less\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Dream is a hope or wish.\"},{\"q\":\"What can you make to learn about space?\",\"options\":[\"Paper rocket\",\"Paper boat\",\"Paper house\",\"Paper plane\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Paper rocket simulates space travel.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the moon invite?\",\"options\":[\"Dreams\",\"Food\",\"Games\",\"Music\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The moon invites dreams of exploration.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16507,11,3,'English','en','4.5 Cloud','[\"Clouds are fluffy white things that float in the sky.\",\"They are made of tiny water droplets or ice crystals.\",\"Clouds can bring rain, snow, or sunshine.\",\"When it rains, clouds release water as drops.\",\"Snow comes from clouds when it is very cold.\",\"A rainbow appears when sunlight shines through rain droplets.\",\"Clouds can be seen when the sky is blue or grey.\",\"Clouds move with the wind.\",\"Clouds are important for the water cycle.\",\"They help keep the Earth cool by reflecting sunlight.\",\"Clouds can be described as cotton, smoke, or clouds of milk.\",\"Clouds can be high, low, or middle in the sky.\",\"Clouds can be thick (stormy) or thin (clear).\",\"Clouds are part of the atmosphere.\",\"Clouds help plants grow by providing water.\",\"Clouds can be seen in many shapes and sizes.\",\"Clouds can be white, gray, or sometimes colorful.\",\"Clouds are made of water vapor that condenses.\",\"Clouds can be seen in pictures and poems.\",\"Clouds are a natural part of weather.\",\"Clouds can be fun to watch and to learn about.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What colour is the sky on a clear day?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"Red\",\"Green\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The sky appears blue because of scattering of sunlight.\"},{\"q\":\"What do clouds bring when it rains?\",\"options\":[\"Sunshine\",\"Wind\",\"Water drops\",\"Snowflakes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Clouds release water droplets as rain.\"},{\"q\":\"Which natural phenomenon appears when sunlight passes through rain?\",\"options\":[\"Moon\",\"Sun\",\"Rainbow\",\"Star\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A rainbow forms when light refracts in raindrops.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main component of a cloud?\",\"options\":[\"Dust\",\"Water droplets\",\"Sand\",\"Fire\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Clouds are made of tiny water droplets or ice crystals.\"},{\"q\":\"When clouds are very cold, what do they produce?\",\"options\":[\"Rain\",\"Snow\",\"Wind\",\"Heat\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Cold clouds produce snow.\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity helps you feel the movement of a cloud?\",\"options\":[\"Reading a book\",\"Listening to music\",\"Wiggling fingers upward\",\"Drawing a picture\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Wiggling fingers upward mimics cloud movement.\"},{\"q\":\"What colour is the sky when it is cloudy?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"Gray\",\"Green\",\"Pink\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Cloudy skies often appear gray.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT a type of cloud?\",\"options\":[\"Cumulus\",\"Stratus\",\"Nimbus\",\"Sunflower\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Sunflower is not a cloud type.\"},{\"q\":\"What happens when clouds are thick and heavy?\",\"options\":[\"They float higher\",\"They bring sunshine\",\"They bring storms\",\"They disappear\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Thick clouds often bring storms.\"},{\"q\":\"What does a rainbow show?\",\"options\":[\"Cloud shape\",\"Sun position\",\"Colorful arc\",\"Wind direction\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A rainbow is a colorful arc seen after rain.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16508,11,3,'English','en','4.6 Tej, The Tiger','[\"Tej is a tiger, a wild animal.\",\"Tigers have orange bodies with black stripes.\",\"Their eyes are bright and teeth are sharp.\",\"Tigers have strong legs and can run fast.\",\"They live in forests with tall trees, rivers and grass.\",\"Their home is called a den where they rest during the day.\",\"They hunt deer and other animals by stalking quietly.\",\"A stalking walk is called a stalk.\",\"Tigers can roar loudly to communicate with other tigers.\",\"A tiger’s roar can be heard far away.\",\"Tigers are meat‑eaters and hunt when hungry.\",\"A baby tiger is called a cub.\",\"Tigers can swim well to cross rivers.\",\"India’s national animal is the tiger.\",\"Protecting tigers helps keep the jungle healthy.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What colour is a tiger’s body?\",\"options\":[\"Red\",\"Orange\",\"Blue\",\"Green\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Tigers have orange bodies.\"},{\"q\":\"What is a baby tiger called?\",\"options\":[\"Pup\",\"Cub\",\"Kitten\",\"Calf\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A baby tiger is called a cub.\"},{\"q\":\"Where does a tiger live?\",\"options\":[\"Den\",\"House\",\"Tree\",\"Cave\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A tiger’s home is a den.\"},{\"q\":\"What does a tiger use to hunt quietly?\",\"options\":[\"Roar\",\"Stalk\",\"Run\",\"Jump\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A quiet walk to hunt is called a stalk.\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal is a tiger’s main food?\",\"options\":[\"Fish\",\"Deer\",\"Bird\",\"Insect\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Tigers hunt deer and other animals.\"},{\"q\":\"How do tigers communicate with each other?\",\"options\":[\"Dance\",\"Roar\",\"Sing\",\"Whistle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"They use a loud roar to communicate.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the national animal of India?\",\"options\":[\"Elephant\",\"Tiger\",\"Peacock\",\"Lion\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"India’s national animal is the tiger.\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of a tiger’s body is sharp?\",\"options\":[\"Eyes\",\"Teeth\",\"Legs\",\"Tail\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Tigers have sharp teeth.\"},{\"q\":\"What does a tiger do when it feels hungry?\",\"options\":[\"Sleep\",\"Roar\",\"Hunt\",\"Play\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"They hunt when hungry.\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity helps a tiger cross a river?\",\"options\":[\"Climb\",\"Jump\",\"Swim\",\"Run\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Tigers can swim well to cross rivers.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16509,11,3,'English','en','4.7 My Profile','[\"- A profile is a short description about yourself.\",\"- It usually includes your name, age, family members, school, hobbies and favourite things.\",\"- Write in simple sentences: \\\"I am ___ years old.\\\"\",\"- Mention where you live and what you like to do.\",\"- Include your favourite colour, food, animal, fruit and subject.\",\"- End with a wish: \\\"I wish to be ___ when I grow up.\\\"\",\"- Use capital letters at the start of each sentence.\",\"- Keep sentences short and clear for Standard‑3 students.\",\"- Practice writing your own profile to improve writing skills.\",\"- Check spelling of common words like mother, father, colour, favourite, animal, fruit, subject.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the first thing you should write in a profile?\",\"options\":[\"Your favourite colour\",\"Your name\",\"Your age\",\"Your school\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A profile starts with your name.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is spelled correctly?\",\"options\":[\"Favourit\",\"Favourite\",\"Favourite\",\"Favourite\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The correct spelling is \\\"favourite\\\".\"},{\"q\":\"I am nine years old. What is my age?\",\"options\":[\"Nine\",\"Nine years\",\"Nine years old\",\"Nine years old and one month\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The age is expressed as \\\"nine years old\\\".\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence shows where you live?\",\"options\":[\"I like to draw.\",\"I live in Shahapur.\",\"I study in grade three.\",\"I am a girl.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The sentence about living place is \\\"I live in Shahapur.\\\"\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct way to end a profile?\",\"options\":[\"I wish to be an artist when I grow up.\",\"I like to draw.\",\"I am nine years old.\",\"I live in Shahapur.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Profiles often end with a wish or future dream.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a favourite food mentioned?\",\"options\":[\"Puranpoli\",\"Chakli\",\"Mango\",\"Cat\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Puranpoli is listed as a favourite food.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct spelling of the animal?\",\"options\":[\"Cat\",\"Cat\",\"Cat\",\"Cat\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The animal is \\\"cat\\\".\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence is NOT part of a profile?\",\"options\":[\"I am a girl.\",\"I wish to be an artist when I grow up.\",\"My favourite subject is English.\",\"Your Photo\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"\\\"Your Photo\\\" is not part of the written profile.\"},{\"q\":\"How many words are in the sentence \\\"I study in grade three.\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"3\",\"4\",\"5\",\"6\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The sentence has five words.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the best way to write a profile?\",\"options\":[\"Use long complex sentences\",\"Use short simple sentences\",\"Write in bullet points\",\"Write in a poem\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Short simple sentences are easiest for Standard‑3.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16510,11,3,'English','en','4.8 Money cannot Buy Everything','[\"Money means money but it cannot buy everything.\",\"Aman is 8 years old.\",\"His father earns about Rs.500 per hour.\",\"Aman has saved about Rs.1,500 in his piggy bank.\",\"Aman wants his father to spend time with him, play and have dinner together.\",\"The story shows that time and love are more valuable than money.\",\"The moral: Money cannot buy love and time.\",\"Aman’s father is busy and forgets to spend time with his son.\",\"Aman asks how much his father earns to understand the value of money.\",\"Aman’s father is surprised by his son’s question.\",\"The father embraces his son after learning his wish.\",\"The story encourages children to ask questions and value relationships.\",\"Teachers can ask students to visit a shop and note prices.\",\"Teachers can ask students to read stories and identify characters.\",\"Teachers can ask students to find simple sentences and questions in a story.\",\"The story is about a child who wants to spend time with his father.\",\"The father’s earnings are about Rs.500 per hour, not per day.\",\"The piggy bank holds Rs.1,500, which is 3 times the hourly wage.\",\"The story teaches that money cannot buy time, love or happiness.\",\"The father’s love is priceless and cannot be bought with money.\",\"The story is suitable for Standard‑3 students to learn values.\"]','[{\"q\":\"How old is Aman?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"6\",\"7\",\"8\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The text says Aman was eight years old.\"},{\"q\":\"What does Aman want to do with his father?\",\"options\":[\"Go to school\",\"Play and have dinner\",\"Buy a toy\",\"Watch TV\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Aman wants his father to play with him and have dinner together.\"},{\"q\":\"How much does Aman’s father earn in an hour?\",\"options\":[\"Rs.200\",\"Rs.300\",\"Rs.400\",\"Rs.500\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The father says he earns around Rs.500 per hour.\"},{\"q\":\"How much money does Aman have in his piggy bank?\",\"options\":[\"Rs.500\",\"Rs.1,000\",\"Rs.1,500\",\"Rs.2,000\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Aman says he has saved about Rs.1,500.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main lesson of the story?\",\"options\":[\"Money is everything\",\"Time and love are priceless\",\"Money can buy happiness\",\"We should save money\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The moral is that money cannot buy everything, especially time and love.\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity can a teacher suggest to help students understand prices?\",\"options\":[\"Read a story\",\"Visit a store\",\"Draw a picture\",\"Sing a song\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Teachers can encourage students to visit a store and note prices.\"},{\"q\":\"What does Aman’s father do when he hears his son’s wish?\",\"options\":[\"Laugh\",\"Get angry\",\"Embrace him\",\"Ignore him\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The father embraces his son after learning his wish.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT mentioned in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Aman’s father is busy\",\"Aman has a piggy bank\",\"Aman wants to play\",\"Aman wants to buy a car\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Buying a car is not mentioned.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the story encourage children to do?\",\"options\":[\"Ask questions\",\"Avoid money\",\"Ignore parents\",\"Play alone\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The story encourages children to ask questions and value relationships.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is a moral of the story?\",\"options\":[\"Money can buy everything\",\"Time is more valuable than money\",\"We should never ask questions\",\"We should always save money\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The moral is that time is more valuable than money.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16511,11,3,'English','en','4.9 Stay Calm and Smile','[\"Stay calm and smile means to keep your cool when you feel angry.\",\"Anger is a normal feeling but it must be controlled so it does not hurt others.\",\"You can control anger by talking to someone you trust, like parents or friends.\",\"Sharing your feelings helps you feel better.\",\"Doing something you enjoy, like playing, drawing, or listening to music, can calm you.\",\"Taking deep breaths and counting from 100 to 1 helps you relax.\",\"Walking or running in a park can also reduce anger.\",\"When you feel angry, try to stay quiet for a moment before reacting.\",\"Smile and think of something happy to change your mood.\",\"If you feel angry, ask a teacher or a friend to help you calm down.\",\"It is okay to feel angry, but it is important to manage it.\",\"You can use simple techniques like breathing, counting, or talking to control anger.\",\"Being calm and smiling shows you are in control of your feelings.\",\"Practice these techniques so you can stay calm in any situation.\",\"Remember: Anger is natural, but calmness is powerful.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is a good way to calm down when you feel angry?\",\"options\":[\"Ignore the feeling\",\"Talk to someone you trust\",\"Yell loudly\",\"Throw a tantrum\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Talking to a trusted person helps you share feelings and calm down.\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity can help you feel better when angry?\",\"options\":[\"Playing a game\",\"Drawing\",\"Listening to music\",\"All of the above\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"All listed activities help reduce anger.\"},{\"q\":\"What does counting from 100 to 1 do?\",\"options\":[\"Makes you more angry\",\"Helps you relax\",\"Makes you sleepy\",\"Makes you hungry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Counting slowly helps you take deep breaths and calm.\"},{\"q\":\"If you feel angry, what should you do first?\",\"options\":[\"Yell at the person\",\"Stay quiet for a while\",\"Run away\",\"Ignore the situation\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Staying quiet gives you time to calm before reacting.\"},{\"q\":\"Why is it okay to feel angry?\",\"options\":[\"Because it shows you are strong\",\"Because it is a natural feeling\",\"Because it helps you win arguments\",\"Because it is a sign of intelligence\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Anger is a natural emotion that everyone experiences.\"},{\"q\":\"What can you do if your friend is teasing you?\",\"options\":[\"Talk to them calmly\",\"Yell back\",\"Ignore them\",\"Throw a tantrum\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Talking calmly helps resolve the situation.\"},{\"q\":\"What is a sign of being calm?\",\"options\":[\"Smiling\",\"Frowning\",\"Angry face\",\"Screaming\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Smiling shows you are calm.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT a technique to control anger?\",\"options\":[\"Talking to parents\",\"Drawing\",\"Yelling at the teacher\",\"Listening to music\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Yelling at the teacher increases anger.\"},{\"q\":\"When should you take a walk to calm down?\",\"options\":[\"After a fight with a friend\",\"When you are happy\",\"When you are bored\",\"When you are tired\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A walk after a fight helps reduce anger.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the phrase \\\"stay calm and smile\\\" mean?\",\"options\":[\"Keep your face still\",\"Keep your anger hidden\",\"Keep your emotions in control\",\"Keep your mouth closed\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"It means to control emotions and remain peaceful.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16512,11,3,'English','en','4.10 Word Family - VIII','[\"Word family means a group of words that share the same root word, like bake, baker, baking.\",\"In a word family, you can change the ending to make new words: bake → baker, baking, baked.\",\"The book shows words that have the same ending, such as -ate, -ate, -ate, etc.\",\"You can find many words that start with the same letters, for example: bake, baker, baking, baked.\",\"The word family helps you learn new words faster because you already know the base word.\",\"A word family can have many words: bake, baker, baking, baked, bakery, etc.\",\"When you read a new word, try to see if it belongs to a word family you already know.\",\"The book lists words that have ‘tr’ in them, like ‘control’ or ‘rocket’ – these are special groups to remember.\",\"Words that end with ‘ing’ are action words, like ‘running’, ‘jumping’ – they show an action is happening.\",\"The longest word in the list is ‘immediately’ – it has 11 letters.\",\"Words related to space include ‘astronaut’, ‘rocket’, ‘space’, ‘gravity’ and ‘sunlight’.\",\"Words related to the forest are ‘forest’, ‘wild’, ‘cub’ and ‘hunting’ – they describe nature.\",\"Opposites of some words: spend ↔ earn, pet ↔ let, downward ↔ upward, ugly ↔ beautiful.\",\"Words that end with ‘y’ in the list: ‘beautiful’, ‘colour’, ‘energy’, ‘different’, ‘learning’, ‘protect’, ‘suit’.\",\"The book also shows words that have nine letters, like ‘question’, ‘puzzle’, ‘colour’ and ‘future’.\",\"Use flash cards or word games to practice these word families and remember them better.\",\"Remember to read each word carefully and find its meaning and use in a sentence.\",\"When you see a new word, try to guess its meaning from the root word and the ending.\",\"Practice writing the words in sentences to improve your vocabulary.\",\"Keep a small notebook of new words and their families to review every week.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which word is part of the same family as \\\"bake\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"baker\",\"bakey\",\"baking\",\"baked\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"All words share the root \\\"bake\\\" and differ by ending.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the longest word in the list?\",\"options\":[\"immediately\",\"astronaut\",\"question\",\"puzzle\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\\\"immediately\\\" has 11 letters, the most in the list.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is an action word ending in \\\"-ing\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"baking\",\"baker\",\"baked\",\"bake\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\\\"baking\\\" ends in -ing and shows an action.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is related to space?\",\"options\":[\"forest\",\"rocket\",\"wild\",\"cub\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\\\"rocket\\\" is a space vehicle.\"},{\"q\":\"Opposite of \\\"downward\\\" is?\",\"options\":[\"upward\",\"downward\",\"leftward\",\"rightward\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\\\"upward\\\" is the opposite direction.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word ends with the letter \\\"y\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"beautiful\",\"color\",\"energy\",\"different\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\\\"beautiful\\\" ends with the letter y.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word has nine letters?\",\"options\":[\"question\",\"puzzle\",\"future\",\"control\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\\\"question\\\" has nine letters.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is related to the forest?\",\"options\":[\"space\",\"forest\",\"rocket\",\"gravity\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"\\\"forest\\\" describes a wooded area.\"},{\"q\":\"Opposite of \\\"spend\\\" is?\",\"options\":[\"earn\",\"save\",\"spend\",\"use\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"To spend is to use money; to earn is to receive money.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means \\\"to be helpful\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"helpful\",\"hunting\",\"hunger\",\"hobby\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"\\\"helpful\\\" means giving help.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16513,12,3,'Marathi','mr','रानवेडी (कविता) तुकाराम धांडे','[\"रानवेडी ही तुकाराम धांडे यांनी लिहिलेली एक सुंदर निसर्ग कविता आहे.\",\"या कवितेत एका लहान मुलीचे निसर्गावर असलेले प्रेम व्यक्त झाले आहे.\",\"रानवेडी म्हणजे रानात रमणारी किंवा रानाचे वेड लागलेली मुलगी.\",\"कवितेतील मुलगी रानात फिरताना खूप आनंदी असते.\",\"तिला रानातील फुले, फळे आणि पक्षी खूप आवडतात.\",\"तिला रानातील प्रत्येक गोष्ट आपलीशी वाटते.\",\"तिला रानातून पळसाची फुले सापडली आहेत.\",\"तिने रानातून वेचलेली फुले आपल्या पदरात जपून ठेवली आहेत.\",\"तिला रानातील वाटेवर चालताना खूप मजा येते.\",\"तिला रानातील झाडे, वेली आणि डोंगर आपलेसे वाटतात.\",\"तिला रानातील शांतता आणि निसर्गाचे सौंदर्य भावते.\",\"तिचे मन रानाच्या प्रेमात पूर्णपणे गुंतलेले आहे.\",\"कवितेतून निसर्ग संवर्धनाचा संदेश मिळतो.\",\"निसर्गाच्या सानिध्यात राहिल्याने मन प्रसन्न होते.\",\"ही कविता निसर्गाशी मैत्री करायला शिकवते.\"]','[{\"q\":\"रानवेडी ही कविता कोणी लिहिली आहे?\",\"options\":[\"कुसुमाग्रज\",\"तुकाराम धांडे\",\"शांता शेळके\",\"मंगेश पाडगावकर\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"रानवेडी ही कविता तुकाराम धांडे यांनी लिहिली आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील मुलगी कोठे रमली आहे?\",\"options\":[\"शाळेत\",\"घरात\",\"रानात\",\"बाजारात\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"कवितेतील मुलगी रानात रमली आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"मुलीला रानातून काय सापडले आहे?\",\"options\":[\"पळसाची फुले\",\"आंबे\",\"पेरू\",\"सफरचंद\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"मुलीला रानातून पळसाची फुले सापडली आहेत.\"},{\"q\":\"रानवेडी म्हणजे काय?\",\"options\":[\"रानात हरवलेली\",\"रानात काम करणारी\",\"रानात रमणारी\",\"रानात राहणारी\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"रानवेडी म्हणजे ज्या मुलीला रानाचे वेड लागले आहे अशी मुलगी.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील मुलीला निसर्ग कसा वाटतो?\",\"options\":[\"भीतीदायक\",\"आपलासा\",\"दूरचा\",\"कंटाळवाणा\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"मुलीला रानातील निसर्ग आपलासा वाटतो.\"},{\"q\":\"मुलीने फुले कोठे जपून ठेवली आहेत?\",\"options\":[\"पिशवीत\",\"पेटीत\",\"पदरात\",\"हातात\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"मुलीने रानातून वेचलेली फुले आपल्या पदरात जपून ठेवली आहेत.\"},{\"q\":\"निसर्गाच्या सानिध्यात राहिल्याने काय होते?\",\"options\":[\"मन प्रसन्न होते\",\"राग येतो\",\"भूक लागते\",\"झोप येते\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"निसर्गाच्या सानिध्यात राहिल्याने मन प्रसन्न होते.\"},{\"q\":\"ही कविता कोणत्या विषयावर आधारित आहे?\",\"options\":[\"शहरातील जीवन\",\"निसर्ग प्रेम\",\"शाळा\",\"खेळ\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"ही कविता निसर्ग प्रेमावर आधारित आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेत कोणाचे वर्णन केले आहे?\",\"options\":[\"एका मुलाचे\",\"एका मुलीचे\",\"प्राण्याचे\",\"पक्षाचे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"कवितेत एका रानात रमणाऱ्या मुलीचे वर्णन केले आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील मुलगी रानात काय करत आहे?\",\"options\":[\"अभ्यास\",\"खेळत आणि फिरत आहे\",\"झोपली आहे\",\"जेवत आहे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"मुलीला रानात फिरण्याचे आणि निसर्गाचा आनंद घेण्याचे वेड लागले आहे.\"}]','gemini-3.1-flash-lite','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16514,12,3,'Marathi','mr','वासाची किंमत (चित्रकथा) 1','[\"वास म्हणजे गंध, वासाची किंमत म्हणजे वासाला पैसे देणे\",\"मिठाईचा वास घेऊन त्याची किंमत विचारणे\",\"पडघम म्हणजे चर्मवाद्य\",\"टिपरी वाजवणे म्हणजे आवाज करणे\",\"पडघमवर टिपरी पडणे म्हणजे वाजवणे\",\"ध्वनी शब्द: तडतड, गडगड, कोसळ\",\"धान्य दळण्यासाठी गहू, ज्वारी, बाजरी वापरतात\",\"पाककृतीत मसाला वाटण्यासाठी वाटी, चहा गाळण्यासाठी छलनी\",\"पडणे म्हणजे घडणे, होणे\",\"वाक्यांतील \'पडले\' शब्दाचा अर्थ \'घडले\'\",\"पाऊस पडणे म्हणजे पाणी जमिनीवर येणे\",\"पावसात भिजल्यावर ताजेतवाने वाटते\",\"काव्यांमध्ये नादमय शब्दांनी गाणे ऐकवतात\",\"वासाची किंमत विचारणे हे विनोदाचे उदाहरण\",\"शिवानीने मिठाईच्या दुकानात वासाची किंमत विचारली\",\"शाळा, घर, शेतातील मुलांना वास आवडतो\",\"वस्तूंची किंमत वासाने मोजणे हे कल्पनाशील विचार\"]','[{\"q\":\"वासाची किंमत या गोष्टीत मिठाईच्या दुकानात काय घडले?\",\"options\":[\"मिठाईची किंमत विचारली\",\"मिठाई विकत घेतली\",\"मिठाईची वास घेतला\",\"मिठाईची पिशवी दिली\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"शिवानीने मिठाईच्या दुकानात वास घेऊन किंमत विचारली.\"},{\"q\":\"शिवानीने मिठाईच्या दुकानात काय मागितले?\",\"options\":[\"पैसे\",\"वाट\",\"पिशवी\",\"भाजी\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"ती पिशवीत पैसे घेऊन आली.\"},{\"q\":\"पडघम म्हणजे काय?\",\"options\":[\"चर्मवाद्य\",\"पाणी\",\"भाजी\",\"भांडे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"पडघम म्हणजे चर्मवाद्य.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेत \'टिपरी पडली\' याचा अर्थ काय?\",\"options\":[\"टिपरी वाजवली\",\"टिपरी पडली\",\"टिपरी गातली\",\"टिपरी नाचली\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"कवीने टिपरी वाजवण्याऐवजी पडली असे म्हटले.\"},{\"q\":\"पडघमवर टिपरी वाजवणारा कोण?\",\"options\":[\"शिवानी\",\"मिठाई विक्रेता\",\"शाळेचा शिक्षक\",\"कौटुंबिक सदस्य\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"पडघमवर टिपरी वाजवणारा शिवानी.\"},{\"q\":\"मिठाईच्या दुकानात लोक काय ऐकले?\",\"options\":[\"पैशांचा आवाज\",\"भाजीची किंमत\",\"वाटाचा आवाज\",\"पडघमचा आवाज\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"गर्दीत पैशांचा आवाज ऐकला.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील \'धरणी\' म्हणजे काय?\",\"options\":[\"जमीन\",\"पाणी\",\"भाजी\",\"भांडे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"धरणी म्हणजे जमीन.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेत \'धरणीचे रंश्रा\' म्हणजे काय?\",\"options\":[\"मातीचे बारीक कण\",\"पाण्याचे थेंब\",\"भाजीचे दाणे\",\"भांडे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"रंश्रा म्हणजे मातीचे बारीक कण.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेत \'तडतड\' या शब्दाचा अर्थ काय?\",\"options\":[\"ध्वनी\",\"पाऊस\",\"भाजी\",\"भांडे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"तडतड म्हणजे ध्वनी.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेत \'पडघमवर टिपरी पडली\' मध्ये \'पडली\' या शब्दाचा अर्थ काय?\",\"options\":[\"वाजवली\",\"पडली\",\"गातली\",\"नाचली\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"पडली म्हणजे पडली.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16515,12,3,'Marathi','mr','आम्ही बातमी वाचतो','[\"बातमी म्हणजे घडलेल्या किंवा घडणाऱ्या गोष्टींची माहिती\",\"बातमी वाचताना प्रथम शीर्षक वाचतो\",\"शीर्षकातून बातमीची मुख्य कल्पना समजते\",\"बातमीतील महत्त्वाचे शब्द जोडाक्षर असू शकतात\",\"बातमीतील ठिकाण आणि वेळ ओळखण्यासाठी वाक्ये शोधतो\",\"बातमीतील पाणी साचलेल्या भागांची नोंद करतो\",\"बातमीतील हवामानाची माहिती लक्षात ठेवतो\",\"बातमीतील शब्दांची अर्थ आणि पर्यायी शब्द ओळखतो\",\"बातमी वाचताना शब्दांचे उच्चार आणि अर्थ लक्षात ठेवतो\",\"बातमीतील शब्दांमध्ये जोडाक्षर ओळखण्यासाठी अधोरेखित करतो\",\"बातमीतील शब्दांमध्ये अक्षरांची जोडणी पाहतो\",\"बातमी वाचताना शब्दांची योग्य वर्तनी लक्षात ठेवतो\",\"बातमीतील शब्दांचे अर्थ लहान वाक्यांत लिहून ठेवतो\",\"बातमी वाचताना शब्दांचे उच्चार आणि अर्थ एकत्र लक्षात ठेवतो\",\"बातमीतील शब्दांचे अर्थ आणि वापर समजून घेण्यासाठी उदाहरणे लिहून ठेवतो\"]','[{\"q\":\"बातमी म्हणजे काय?\",\"options\":[\"घडलेल्या गोष्टींची माहिती\",\"कविता\",\"गाणे\",\"चित्र\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"बातमी म्हणजे घडलेल्या किंवा घडणाऱ्या गोष्टींची माहिती.\"},{\"q\":\"बातमी वाचताना प्रथम काय वाचतो?\",\"options\":[\"मजकूर\",\"शीर्षक\",\"चित्र\",\"सारांश\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"प्रथम शीर्षक वाचून बातमीची मुख्य कल्पना समजते.\"},{\"q\":\"बातमीतील शब्दांमध्ये काय शोधायला हवे?\",\"options\":[\"जोडाक्षर\",\"रंग\",\"आकार\",\"आवाज\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"बातमीतील शब्दांमध्ये जोडाक्षर असू शकतात.\"},{\"q\":\"बातमीतील पाणी साचलेल्या भागांची नोंद कशी करावी?\",\"options\":[\"चित्र काढून\",\"शब्द लिहून\",\"दोन्ही\",\"काहीही नाही\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"पाणी साचलेल्या भागांची नोंद शब्दांनी करावी.\"},{\"q\":\"बातमीतील ठिकाण आणि वेळ ओळखण्यासाठी काय शोधावे?\",\"options\":[\"वाक्ये\",\"चित्रे\",\"आवाज\",\"रंग\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"ठिकाण आणि वेळ ओळखण्यासाठी वाक्ये शोधावीत.\"},{\"q\":\"बातमीतील शब्दांचे पर्यायी शब्द शोधणे का महत्त्वाचे?\",\"options\":[\"शब्दसंग्रह वाढतो\",\"वाचन सोपे होते\",\"काही नाही\",\"फक्त मजा\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"पर्यायी शब्द शोधल्याने शब्दसंग्रह वाढतो.\"},{\"q\":\"बातमीतील शब्दांचे अर्थ लहान वाक्यांत लिहिणे कसे मदत करते?\",\"options\":[\"समज वाढते\",\"काही नाही\",\"फक्त वेळ वाया जातो\",\"काहीही नाही\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"लहान वाक्यांत लिहिल्याने समज वाढते.\"},{\"q\":\"बातमीतील शब्दांचे उच्चार लक्षात ठेवण्यासाठी काय करावे?\",\"options\":[\"शब्द पुन्हा पुन्हा वाचणे\",\"चित्र काढणे\",\"आवाज ऐकणे\",\"दोन्ही\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"उच्चार लक्षात ठेवण्यासाठी शब्द पुन्हा वाचणे आणि ऐकणे दोन्ही उपयुक्त.\"},{\"q\":\"बातमीतील शब्दांचे अर्थ आणि वापर समजण्यासाठी काय करावे?\",\"options\":[\"उदाहरणे लिहून ठेवणे\",\"फक्त वाचणे\",\"काहीही नाही\",\"चित्र काढणे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"उदाहरणे लिहून ठेवल्याने वापर समजतो.\"},{\"q\":\"बातमीतील शब्दांचे अर्थ आणि वापर समजण्यासाठी कोणती पद्धत सर्वात चांगली?\",\"options\":[\"उदाहरणे लिहून ठेवणे\",\"फक्त वाचणे\",\"काहीही नाही\",\"चित्र काढणे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"उदाहरणे लिहून ठेवणे सर्वात चांगली पद्धत आहे.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16516,12,3,'Marathi','mr','ss पाणी किती खोल ?','[\"पाणी म्हणजे द्रव पदार्थ जो आपल्याला पिण्यासाठी, स्वच्छतेसाठी आणि निसर्गात विविध जीवांना आधार देतो.\",\"पाण्याची खोली म्हणजे पाण्याच्या तळापासून वरच्या पृष्ठभागापर्यंतचे अंतर.\",\"पाण्याची खोली मोजण्यासाठी आपण पाण्याच्या पातळीपासून आपले पाय किंवा वस्तू किती खाली जातात ते पाहतो.\",\"नदीतील पाणी उंच-नीच असते; काही ठिकाणी गुडघ्याइतकं, काही ठिकाणी पोटापर्यंत पोहोचतं.\",\"बैलाच्या गुडघ्याइतकं पाणी असताना बैल सहज चालू शकतो.\",\"गाढवाच्या पोटापर्यंत पाणी असताना गाढवाला थोडं अडचण येऊ शकते.\",\"रेडकूला वाटलं की पाणी खूप खोल आहे, पण प्रत्यक्षात ते गुडघ्याच्या थोडं वर होतं.\",\"कडबा म्हणजे धान्याचे तुकडे, कडबाकुट्टी म्हणजे कडब्याचे बारीक तुकडे करणारे यंत्र.\",\"चघळणे म्हणजे अन्न तोंडात घोळवणे.\",\"कथा सांगताना प्राण्यांचे आवाज काढून सांगणे मजेदार असतं.\",\"नदीचे पाणी डोंगरातून सुरू होतं आणि प्रवाहाने खाली येतं.\",\"नदीचे पाणी वाढतं जेव्हा पाऊस पडतो किंवा डोंगरातून अधिक पाणी वाहतं.\",\"पानांच्या शिरा नदीच्या प्रवाहासारख्या असतात, त्या लहान ओढ्यांसारख्या असतात.\",\"नदीबद्दल बोलताना आपण तिच्या आकार, प्रवाह आणि पाण्याच्या खोलीबद्दल बोलू शकतो.\",\"कथा वाचताना आणि प्रश्नांची उत्तरे देताना शब्दांची योग्य स्पेलिंग आणि अर्थ लक्षात ठेवणे महत्त्वाचे आहे.\",\"पाणी आणि निसर्गाबद्दल शिकताना आपण निरीक्षण, प्रश्न विचारणे आणि चर्चा करणे हे शिकवणुकीचे महत्त्वाचे भाग आहेत.\",\"शाळेत नदीबद्दल चर्चा करताना आपण चित्र काढून किंवा पानांच्या शिरा दाखवून समजावू शकतो.\",\"पाण्याच्या खोलीबद्दल बोलताना आपण आपल्या पायांच्या किंवा वस्तूंच्या पाण्याच्या पातळीशी तुलना करू शकतो.\",\"पाणी आणि निसर्गाबद्दल शिकताना आपण प्राणी, वनस्पती आणि मानवी क्रिया यांचा संबंध समजून घेऊ शकतो.\",\"पाणी हे जीवनाचे मूलभूत स्रोत आहे, त्यामुळे त्याची काळजी घेणे आणि स्वच्छ ठेवणे आवश्यक आहे.\",\"पाण्याबद्दल शिकताना आपण नद्यांचे, तळ्यांचे आणि पाण्याच्या प्रवाहाचे निरीक्षण करू शकतो.\",\"पाणी आणि निसर्गाबद्दल शिकताना आपण आपल्या दैनंदिन जीवनात पाण्याचा कसा वापर करतो हे लक्षात ठेवू शकतो\"]','[{\"q\":\"पाण्याची खोली मोजण्यासाठी काय वापरले जाते?\",\"options\":[\"पाण्याची उंची\",\"पाण्याची खोली\",\"पाण्याची पातळी\",\"पाण्याची गती\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"पाण्याची खोली म्हणजे पाण्याच्या तळापासून पृष्ठभागापर्यंतचे अंतर.\"},{\"q\":\"बैलाच्या गुडघ्याइतकं पाणी असताना बैल काय करू शकतो?\",\"options\":[\"बुडतो\",\"सहज चालतो\",\"पळतो\",\"उडतो\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"गुडघ्याइतकं पाणी असताना बैल सहज चालू शकतो.\"},{\"q\":\"रेडकूला पाणी किती खोल वाटलं?\",\"options\":[\"गुडघ्याच्या थोडं वर\",\"गुडघ्याइतकं\",\"पोटापर्यंत\",\"पाण्याच्या तळापर्यंत\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"रेडकूला वाटलं की पाणी गुडघ्याच्या थोडं वर आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"कडब्याचे बारीक तुकडे करणारे यंत्र काय म्हणतात?\",\"options\":[\"कडबाकुट्टी\",\"कडबयंत्र\",\"कडब्याचे यंत्र\",\"कडब्याची कात\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"कडबाकुट्टी म्हणजे कडब्याचे बारीक तुकडे करणारे यंत्र.\"},{\"q\":\"नदीचे पाणी डोंगरातून सुरू होते आणि कोणत्या दिशेने जाते?\",\"options\":[\"उजवीकडे\",\"डावीकडे\",\"खाली\",\"वर\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"नदीचे पाणी डोंगरातून सुरू होऊन खाली वाहते.\"},{\"q\":\"पानांच्या शिरा नदीच्या प्रवाहासारख्या असतात. हे कोणत्या शब्दाने दर्शविले जाते?\",\"options\":[\"उंचउंच\",\"तरंगत तरंगत\",\"पुढेपुढे\",\"गारगार\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"पुढेपुढे हे नदीच्या प्रवाहासारखे असते.\"},{\"q\":\"गाढवाच्या पोटापर्यंत पाणी असताना गाढवाला काय वाटते?\",\"options\":[\"सुखी\",\"अडचण\",\"उदास\",\"उत्साही\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"पोटापर्यंत पाणी असताना गाढवाला थोडी अडचण येऊ शकते.\"},{\"q\":\"कथा सांगताना प्राण्यांचे आवाज काढणे का महत्त्वाचे आहे?\",\"options\":[\"मजेदार बनवण्यासाठी\",\"शिक्षकाला आवडण्यासाठी\",\"परीक्षेत गुण वाढवण्यासाठी\",\"काही कारण नाही\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"प्राण्यांचे आवाज काढल्याने कथा अधिक जिवंत आणि मजेदार होते.\"},{\"q\":\"पाण्याच्या खोलीबद्दल बोलताना आपण काय तुलना करतो?\",\"options\":[\"पाण्याची रंग\",\"पाण्याची गंध\",\"पायांची पातळी\",\"पाण्याची गती\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"पाण्याची खोली पायांच्या पातळीशी तुलना करतो.\"},{\"q\":\"नदीबद्दल चर्चा करताना आपण काय काढू शकतो?\",\"options\":[\"झाडाचे चित्र\",\"पाण्याचे चित्र\",\"पानांचे चित्र\",\"सर्व वरील\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"नदीबद्दल चर्चा करताना आपण पाण्याचे चित्र, पानांचे शिरा इत्यादी काढू शकतो.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16517,12,3,'Marathi','mr','हिक्के होक्के मरांग उरस्काट (कविता) ७००२०२००२०','[\"हिक्के होक्के मरांग उरस्काट ही एक बालकविता आहे ज्यात गोंडीतून मराठी शब्दांची जोड दिली आहे.\",\"कवितेत \'हिक्के\' आणि \'होक्‍्के\' हे शब्द एकमेकांशी जोडलेले आहेत.\",\"कवितेतील शब्दांची पुनरावृत्ती लयबद्धता आणि लक्षात ठेवण्यास मदत करते.\",\"कवितेतील \'उरस्काट\' म्हणजे \'उरु\' म्हणजे \'उरु\' आणि \'स्काट\' म्हणजे \'सकट\' असा अर्थ होतो.\",\"कवितेतील \'पिसीहकाट\' म्हणजे \'पिसी\' म्हणजे \'पिसी\' आणि \'हकाट\' म्हणजे \'हकाट\' असा अर्थ होतो.\",\"कवितेतील \'पुंगार\' म्हणजे \'पुंगार\' आणि \'पुंगारे\' म्हणजे \'पुंगारे\' असा अर्थ होतो.\",\"कवितेतील \'कायांग\' म्हणजे \'कायांग\' आणि \'कायांगे\' म्हणजे \'कायांगे\' असा अर्थ होतो.\",\"कवितेतील \'उरस्तांग\' म्हणजे \'उरस्तांग\' आणि \'पिसीहकाट\' म्हणजे \'पिसीहकाट\' असा अर्थ होतो.\",\"कवितेतील \'मरांगना\' म्हणजे \'मरांगना\' आणि \'गेळा\' म्हणजे \'गेळा\' असा अर्थ होतो.\",\"कवितेतील \'कियाकाट\' म्हणजे \'कियाकाट\' असा अर्थ होतो.\",\"कवितेतील \'इकडे\', \'तिकडे\', \'जिकडे\' हे शब्द स्थान दर्शवतात.\",\"कवितेतील \'झाडेच झाडे\', \'फुलेच फुले\', \'फळेच फळे\' हे शब्द पुनरावृत्तीने लयबद्धता वाढवतात.\",\"कवितेतील \'झाडी\', \'जंगल\' हे शब्द निसर्गाचे वर्णन करतात.\",\"कवितेतील \'लावूया\', \'वाढवूया\', \'मिळवूया\' हे शब्द कृती दर्शवतात.\",\"कवितेतील \'कख्या\' म्हणजे \'कख्या\' असा अर्थ होतो.\",\"कवितेतील \'उरस्काट\' आणि \'उरस्तांग\' हे शब्द गोंडीतून मराठी शब्दांमध्ये रूपांतरित केले आहेत.\",\"कवितेतील \'उरस्काट\' आणि \'उरस्तांग\' हे शब्द गोंडीतून मराठी शब्दांमध्ये रूपांतरित केले आहेत.\",\"कवितेतील \'उरस्काट\' आणि \'उरस्तांग\' हे शब्द गोंडीतून मराठी शब्दांमध्ये रूपांतरित केले आहेत.\",\"कवितेतील \'उरस्काट\' आणि \'उरस्तांग\' हे शब्द गोंडीतून मराठी शब्दांमध्ये रूपांतरित केले आहेत.\"]','[{\"q\":\"हिक्के होक्के मरांग उरस्काट या कवितेत कोणते शब्द पुनरावृत्तीने वापरले आहेत?\",\"options\":[\"हिक्के\",\"होके\",\"मरांग\",\"वरील सर्व\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"सर्व शब्दांची पुनरावृत्ती लयबद्धता वाढवते.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील \'उरस्काट\' या शब्दाचा अर्थ काय?\",\"options\":[\"उरु + स्काट\",\"उरु + कात\",\"उरु + सकट\",\"उरु + कात\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"उरु + सकट असा अर्थ होतो.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील \'पुंगार\' शब्दाचा अर्थ काय?\",\"options\":[\"पुंगार\",\"पुंगारे\",\"पुंगार\",\"पुंगारे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"पुंगार हा शब्द पुनरावृत्तीने वापरला आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील \'कायांग\' शब्दाचा अर्थ काय?\",\"options\":[\"कायांग\",\"कायांगे\",\"कायांग\",\"कायांगे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"कायांग हा शब्द पुनरावृत्तीने वापरला आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील \'उरस्तांग\' शब्दाचा अर्थ काय?\",\"options\":[\"उरु + तांग\",\"उरु + सांक\",\"उरु + तांग\",\"उरु + सांक\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"उरु + तांग असा अर्थ होतो.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील \'मग\' शब्दाचा अर्थ काय?\",\"options\":[\"मग\",\"मग\",\"मग\",\"मग\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"मग हा शब्द पुनरावृत्तीने वापरला आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील \'क्या\' शब्दाचा अर्थ काय?\",\"options\":[\"क्या\",\"क्या\",\"क्या\",\"क्या\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"क्या हा शब्द पुनरावृत्तीने वापरला आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील \'उरस्काट\' आणि \'उरस्तांग\' हे शब्द कोणत्या भाषेतून आले आहेत?\",\"options\":[\"गोंडी\",\"मराठी\",\"हिंदी\",\"इंग्रजी\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"गोंडी भाषेतील शब्द आहेत.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील \'उरस्काट\' आणि \'उरस्तांग\' या शब्दांमध्ये काय फरक आहे?\",\"options\":[\"उरस्काट म्हणजे उरु + स्काट\",\"उरस्तांग म्हणजे उरु + तांग\",\"दोन्ही समान आहेत\",\"दोन्ही भिन्न आहेत\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"दोन्ही शब्द भिन्न आहेत.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील \'उरस्काट\' आणि \'उरस्तांग\' हे शब्द गोंडीतून मराठी शब्दांमध्ये कसे रूपांतरित केले आहेत?\",\"options\":[\"उरु + स्काट\",\"उरु + तांग\",\"उरु + सकट\",\"उरु + तांग\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"उरु + स्काट असा रूपांतरित केले आहे.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16518,12,3,'Marathi','mr','आम्ही कविता करतो स','[\"कविता म्हणजे लयबद्ध शब्दांची रचना\",\"कवितेत शब्दांची लय आणि ताल महत्त्वाची असते\",\"कवितेतील शेवटचे अक्षर एकसारखे असलेले शब्दांना \'समानाक्षरी\' म्हणतात\",\"समानाक्षरी शब्दांमुळे कविता सुंदर वाटते\",\"कविता लिहिताना शब्दांची निवड आणि लय याकडे लक्ष द्या\",\"कवितेतील ओळींची लांबी समान असणे चांगले\",\"कविता वाचताना आवाजात थोडी चढ-उतार असावी\",\"कविता लिहिताना आपल्या भावना व्यक्त करायला हव्यात\",\"कवितेतील शब्दांची पुनरावृत्ती केल्याने प्रभाव वाढतो\",\"कविता वाचताना श्वास घेणे महत्त्वाचे\",\"कवितेतील चित्रण जिवंत असावे\",\"कवितेतील शब्दांची लय आणि ताल एकत्र असायला हवे\",\"कविता लिहिताना विषय स्पष्ट असावा\",\"कवितेतील शब्दांची निवड साधी आणि स्पष्ट असावी\",\"कविता वाचताना आवाजात थोडी लयबद्धता असावी\"]','[{\"q\":\"कवितेतील शेवटचे अक्षर एकसारखे असलेल्या शब्दांना काय म्हणतात?\",\"options\":[\"समानाक्षरी\",\"समानध्वनी\",\"समानरचना\",\"समानवर्ण\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"अशा शब्दांना समानाक्षरी म्हणतात.\"},{\"q\":\"कविता लिहिताना शब्दांची लय आणि ताल महत्त्वाचे का असते?\",\"options\":[\"कारण ते वाचकाला आनंद देतात\",\"कारण ते शब्दांची संख्या कमी करतात\",\"कारण ते कवितेची लांबी वाढवतात\",\"कारण ते शब्दांची किंमत कमी करतात\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"लय आणि तालामुळे कविता सुंदर वाटते.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील ओळींची लांबी समान असणे का चांगले?\",\"options\":[\"यामुळे कविता लहान होते\",\"यामुळे वाचणे सोपे होते\",\"यामुळे शब्दांची संख्या वाढते\",\"यामुळे शब्दांची किंमत कमी होते\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"समान लांबीमुळे वाचणे सोपे होते.\"},{\"q\":\"कविता वाचताना आवाजात काय असायला हवे?\",\"options\":[\"थांबणे\",\"चढ-उतार\",\"समान आवाज\",\"उच्च आवाज\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"आवाजात चढ-उतार असावा.\"},{\"q\":\"कविता लिहिताना आपल्या भावना कशा व्यक्त कराव्यात?\",\"options\":[\"साध्या शब्दांत\",\"जटिल शब्दांत\",\"गूढ भाषेत\",\"काहीही न सांगता\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"साध्या शब्दांत भावना व्यक्त कराव्यात.\"},{\"q\":\"समानाक्षरी शब्द शोधण्यासाठी काय पाहावे?\",\"options\":[\"शब्दाची सुरुवात\",\"शब्दाची लांबी\",\"शब्दाचा शेवट\",\"शब्दाचा अर्थ\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"शब्दाच्या शेवटच्या अक्षरावर लक्ष द्या.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील शब्दांची पुनरावृत्ती केल्याने काय होते?\",\"options\":[\"कविता लांब होते\",\"कविता सुंदर होते\",\"कविता गोंधळात पडते\",\"कविता लहान होते\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"पुनरावृत्तीने प्रभाव वाढतो.\"},{\"q\":\"कविता लिहिताना विषय कसा असावा?\",\"options\":[\"अस्पष्ट\",\"स्पष्ट\",\"गूढ\",\"अव्यवस्थित\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"विषय स्पष्ट असावा.\"},{\"q\":\"कविता वाचताना श्वास कसा घ्यावा?\",\"options\":[\"जास्त\",\"कमी\",\"नियमित\",\"कधीही न घ्या\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"नियमित श्वास घेणे महत्त्वाचे.\"},{\"q\":\"कविता लिहिताना शब्दांची निवड कशी असावी?\",\"options\":[\"साधी\",\"जटिल\",\"अस्पष्ट\",\"गूढ\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"साधी आणि स्पष्ट शब्द निवडा.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16519,12,3,'Marathi','mr','मुग्धा लिहू लागली निर्मला मठपती','[\"मुग्धा ही एक शाळेतील मुलगी आहे ज्याने चित्रकला, रांगोळी आणि कथाकथन स्पर्धेत भाग घेतला.\",\"शाळेत बक्षीस समारंभ झाला ज्यात प्रमुख पाहुणे आले.\",\"मुग्धा आणि तिचे आईबाबा शाळेत आले आणि बक्षिसे घेतली.\",\"पाहुणे लेखक होते ज्यांनी आपला अनुभव सांगितला.\",\"लेखकाने लिहिण्याचा छंद कसा लागला आणि तो कसा वाढला हे स्पष्ट केले.\",\"लेखनाने त्याची निरीक्षणशक्ती, स्मरणशक्ती आणि शब्दसंपत्ती वाढली.\",\"मुग्धाने नवीन वर्षात डायरी (रोजनिशी) घेऊन रोज लिहायला सुरुवात केली.\",\"दैनंदिन लेखनाने तिला बोलणे आणि लिहिणे या दोन्ही गोष्टींमध्ये आत्मविश्वास आला.\",\"मुग्धाने आपला संकल्प केला की रोज काहीतरी लिहायचे.\",\"शाळेतील वाचन आणि लेखनाने तिला साहित्यिक होण्याची प्रेरणा दिली.\",\"शब्दार्थ: नित्य‑रोज, अभिनय‑हावभाव, दैनिक‑रोज प्रसिद्ध होणारे, मासिक‑दर महिन्याला प्रसिद्ध होणारे, घुम्या‑कमी बोलणारा, अबोल‑कमी बोलणारा, परिवर्तन‑बदल, संकल्प‑निर्धार, सुसंवाद‑चांगली चर्चा.\",\"मुग्धाच्या कथा वाचून आपणही रोज लिहिण्याचा प्रयत्न करू शकतो.\",\"लेखनामुळे आपली कल्पनाशक्ती आणि संवाद कौशल्य वाढते.\",\"शाळेतील स्पर्धा आणि बक्षिसे मुलांना प्रोत्साहित करतात.\",\"लेखकाच्या भाषणाने मुलांना लिहिण्याची प्रेरणा दिली.\",\"मुग्धा आणि तिचे कुटुंब एकमेकांशी चांगला संवाद साधू लागले.\",\"मुग्धाने डायरी लिहून आपले अनुभव नोंदवले.\",\"डायरी लिहिणे हे आत्मचिंतन आणि आत्मविकासाचे साधन आहे.\",\"लेखनामुळे आपल्याला आपले विचार स्पष्टपणे मांडता येतात.\",\"मुग्धाच्या अनुभवातून आपण शिकतो की लेखनाने आपले जीवन बदलू शकते.\"]','[{\"q\":\"मुग्धाच्या शाळेत कोणती स्पर्धा झाली?\",\"options\":[\"चित्रकला\",\"रांगोळी\",\"कथाकथन\",\"वरील सर्व\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"शाळेत चित्रकला, रांगोळी आणि कथाकथन स्पर्धा झाल्या.\"},{\"q\":\"पाहुणे लेखक होते, त्यांनी काय सांगितले?\",\"options\":[\"त्यांचा छंद\",\"त्यांचा प्रवास\",\"त्यांचा अनुभव\",\"त्यांचा आवडता खेळ\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"लेखकाने लिहिण्याचा छंद आणि अनुभव सांगितला.\"},{\"q\":\"मुग्धाने नवीन वर्षात काय दिले?\",\"options\":[\"डायरी\",\"पेन\",\"कागद\",\"काहीही नाही\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"बाबांनी तिला नवीन वर्षाची डायरी दिली.\"},{\"q\":\"मुग्धाने रोज काय लिहायला सुरुवात केली?\",\"options\":[\"कथा\",\"कविता\",\"डायरी\",\"पुस्तक\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"तिने रोज डायरी लिहायला सुरुवात केली.\"},{\"q\":\"लेखनाने लेखकाची कोणती क्षमता वाढली?\",\"options\":[\"दृष्टी\",\"स्मरणशक्ती\",\"श्रवणशक्ती\",\"स्मरणशक्ती व शब्दसंपत्ती\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"लेखनाने स्मरणशक्ती आणि शब्दसंपत्ती वाढली.\"},{\"q\":\"मुग्धा कोणत्या संकल्पाने प्रेरित झाली?\",\"options\":[\"संकल्प\",\"सुसंवाद\",\"स्मरणशक्ती\",\"साहित्यिक होणे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"तिने रोज लिहिण्याचा संकल्प केला.\"},{\"q\":\"मुग्धाच्या डायरीत काय लिहिले जाते?\",\"options\":[\"भाऊशी भांडण\",\"आजीचे वर्णन\",\"मैत्रिणीचा वाढदिवस\",\"वरील सर्व\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"डायरीत विविध विषय लिहिले जातात.\"},{\"q\":\"लेखकाने लिहिण्याचा छंद कसा लागला?\",\"options\":[\"बोलून\",\"पाहून\",\"वाचून\",\"लिहून\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"लेखकाने रोज वहीत लिहून छंद लागला.\"},{\"q\":\"मुग्धाने काय केले ज्यामुळे ती बोलू लागली?\",\"options\":[\"डायरी लिहिली\",\"कविता लिहिली\",\"कथा लिहिली\",\"काहीही नाही\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"डायरी लिहिल्यामुळे ती बोलू लागली.\"},{\"q\":\"मुग्धाच्या अनुभवातून काय शिकायला मिळते?\",\"options\":[\"लेखन महत्त्वाचे नाही\",\"लेखनाने जीवन बदलते\",\"परीक्षा महत्त्वाची आहे\",\"काहीही नाही\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"लेखनाने जीवनात बदल घडतो.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16520,12,3,'Marathi','mr','कोण बोलतं ते आम्ही शोधतो','[\"कोण बोलतं ते आम्ही शोधतो या अध्यायात आपण शब्दांच्या अर्थावर लक्ष देतो.\",\"वाक्यातील कण आणि शब्दांची ओळख करून घेऊन वाक्याचा अर्थ समजतो.\",\"वाक्ये लहान आणि साधी असतात, ज्यात ‘मी’, ‘तू’, ‘तो’ इत्यादी सर्वनाम वापरलेले असतात.\",\"वाक्यांमध्ये ‘आहे’, ‘आहेत’ या क्रियापदांचा वापर वाक्य पूर्ण करते.\",\"‘कोण’, ‘कोणता’, ‘काय’ अशा प्रश्नार्थक शब्दांनी वाक्य सुरू होते.\",\"वाक्याच्या शेवटी ‘आहे’ किंवा ‘आहेत’ हे कण वाक्याला पूर्णत्व देतात.\",\"वाक्याचे मुख्य भाग ‘कर्म’ आणि ‘कर्मकारक’ यांमध्ये विभागले जातात.\",\"वाक्याचे अर्थ समजण्यासाठी ‘कण’ आणि ‘सर्वनाम’ यांची ओळख आवश्यक आहे.\",\"वाक्याचे ‘साधे’ आणि ‘जटिल’ प्रकार असतात, साधे वाक्य एकच क्रिया दर्शवते.\",\"वाक्यांमध्ये ‘कण’ म्हणजे ‘आहे’, ‘आहेत’ हे शब्द वाक्याला जोडतात.\",\"वाक्याचे ‘विषय’ आणि ‘कर्म’ ओळखून वाक्याचा अर्थ स्पष्ट होतो.\",\"वाक्यांमध्ये ‘कण’ व ‘सर्वनाम’ यांचा योग्य वापर केल्यास वाक्य स्पष्ट होते.\",\"वाक्याचे ‘अर्थ’ समजण्यासाठी शब्दांची क्रमवारी महत्त्वाची असते.\",\"वाक्याचे ‘उदाहरण’ म्हणून ‘मी गोड खाल्लं’ हे वाक्य घेऊ शकतो.\",\"वाक्याचे ‘अभ्यास’ करताना ‘कण’ व ‘सर्वनाम’ यांची जोडणी तपासावी.\",\"वाक्याचे ‘सोपे’ वाक्य ‘मी शाळेत जातो’ असे असते.\",\"वाक्याचे ‘जटिल’ वाक्य ‘मी शाळेत जाऊन पुस्तक वाचतो’ असे असते.\",\"वाक्याचे ‘अभ्यास’ करताना ‘कण’ व ‘सर्वनाम’ यांची ओळख करून घेणे आवश्यक आहे.\",\"वाक्याचे ‘संदर्भ’ समजण्यासाठी ‘कण’ व ‘सर्वनाम’ यांचा वापर महत्त्वाचा आहे.\",\"वाक्याचे ‘उदाहरण’ ‘तो गाडी चालवतो’ हे वाक्य आहे.\",\"वाक्याचे ‘अभ्यास’ करताना ‘कण’ व ‘सर्वनाम’ यांची जोडणी तपासावी.\",\"वाक्याचे ‘अर्थ’ समजण्यासाठी ‘कण’ व ‘सर्वनाम’ यांची ओळख आवश्यक आहे.\"]','[{\"q\":\"कोण बोलतंय हे शोधण्यासाठी कोणती पद्धत वापरली जाते?\",\"options\":[\"वाचन\",\"ऐकणे\",\"सर्वेक्षण\",\"सर्वोत्तम\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"पाठ वाचून बोलणारा कोण आहे हे शोधता येते.\"},{\"q\":\"मयूरने डब्यात काय आणले?\",\"options\":[\"गुळाची पोळी\",\"अंड्याची पोळी\",\"चपाती\",\"फोडणीचा भात\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"मयूरने गुळाची पोळी आणल्याचं सांगितलं.\"},{\"q\":\"जया ने काय म्हटलं?\",\"options\":[\"माझा डबा विसरलाय\",\"मी डब्यात गुळाची पोळी आणली\",\"मी अंड्याची पोळी आणली\",\"मी फोडणीचा भात आणला\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"जया ने डबा विसरलाय असं सांगितलं.\"},{\"q\":\"अभिजीतची चिंता काय होती?\",\"options\":[\"डबा विसरला\",\"उपाशी राहायचं\",\"शाळेत पोचायचं\",\"स्पर्धा जिंकायची\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"अभिजीत उपाशी राहण्याबद्दल चिंतित होता.\"},{\"q\":\"सायना ने काय म्हटलं?\",\"options\":[\"माझा डबा विसरलाय\",\"मी डब्यात गुळाची पोळी आणली\",\"मी अंड्याची पोळी आणली\",\"मी फोडणीचा भात आणला\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"सायना ने डबा विसरलाय असं सांगितलं.\"},{\"q\":\"केंद्रशाळेत पोचण्यासाठी काय करावं?\",\"options\":[\"लवकर धावावं\",\"वाचन करावं\",\"परिपाठाच्या आधी वाचावं\",\"स्पर्धा जिंकाव्या\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"परिपाठाच्या आधी वाचून पोचायचं.\"},{\"q\":\"केंद्रशाळेच्या दारात कोण आले?\",\"options\":[\"मुलं\",\"बाई\",\"मायूर\",\"सर्वेक्षण\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"मुलं केंद्रशाळेच्या दारात आले.\"},{\"q\":\"फोडणीची भाकरी कोण आणतो?\",\"options\":[\"मयूर\",\"जया\",\"सायना\",\"अभिजीत\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"मयूरने फोडणीची भाकरी आणल्याचं सांगितलं.\"},{\"q\":\"केंद्रशाळेत स्पर्धा कधी सुरू होतात?\",\"options\":[\"लवकर\",\"सुरू होतात\",\"नंतर\",\"कधीही नाही\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"स्पर्धा लगेच सुरू होतात.\"},{\"q\":\"कोण बोलतंय हे शोधण्यासाठी काय मदत करते