शात किल्ले जिंकून कुतुबशाही व मुघलांच्या प्रभावाला कमी केले.\",\"मोहिमेच्या दरम्यान शिवाजी महाराजांनी किल्ल्यांवर वेढा आणि तोफांचा वापर केला.\",\"शिवाजी महाराजांनी दक्षिणी प्रदेशात स्वराज्याच्या कार्यासाठी किल्ले जिंकले.\",\"मोहिमेच्या यशामुळे दक्षिणी प्रदेशात स्वराज्याची प्रशंसा वाढली.\",\"शिवाजी महाराजांनी दक्षिणी प्रदेशात स्वराज्याच्या कार्यासाठी किल्ले जिंकून स्वराज्याची प्रतिष्ठा वाढवली.\",\"शिवाजी महाराजांनी दक्षिणी प्रदेशात स्वराज्याच्या कार्यासाठी किल्ले जिंकून स्वराज्याची प्रतिष्ठा वाढवली.\",\"शिवाजी महाराजांनी दक्षिणी प्रदेशात स्वराज्याच्या कार्यासाठी किल्ले जिंकून स्वराज्याची प्रतिष्ठा वाढवली.\",\"शिवाजी महाराजांनी दक्षिणी प्रदेशात स्वराज्याच्या कार्यासाठी किल्ले जिंकून स्वराज्याची प्रतिष्ठा वाढवली.\",\"शिवाजी महाराजांनी दक्षिणी प्रदेशात स्वराज्याच्या कार्यासाठी किल्ले जिंकून स्वराज्याची प्रतिष्ठा वाढवली.\",\"शिवाजी महाराजांनी दक्षिणी प्रदेशात स्वराज्याच्या कार्यासाठी किल्ले जिंकून स्वराज्याची प्रतिष्ठा वाढवली.\",\"शिवाजी महाराजांनी दक्षिणी प्रदेशात स्वराज्याच्या कार्यासाठी किल्ले जिंकून स्वराज्याची प्रतिष्ठा वाढवली.\",\"शिवाजी महाराजांनी दक्षिणी प्रदेशात स्वराज्याच्या कार्यासाठी किल्ले जिंकून स्वराज्याची प्रतिष्ठा वाढवली.\",\"शिवाजी महाराजांनी दक्षिणी प्रदेशात स्वराज्याच्या कार्यासाठी किल्ले जिंकून स्वराज्याची प्रतिष्ठा वाढवली.\"]','[{\"q\":\"दक्षिणी मोहिमेचा मुख्य उद्देश काय होता?\",\"options\":[\"किल्ले जिंकणे\",\"कुतुबशाहीची राजधानी बदलणे\",\"मुघलांना मदत करणे\",\"शिवाजी महाराजांची प्रसिद्धी वाढवणे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"मोहिमेचा उद्देश दक्षिणी किल्ले जिंकून स्वराज्याचा विस्तार करणे होता.\"},{\"q\":\"शिवाजी महाराजांनी व्यंकोजीराजांना काय पाठवले?\",\"options\":[\"सैनिक\",\"धन\",\"समजुतीची पत्रे\",\"भेटवस्तू\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"त्यांनी समजुतीची पत्रे पाठवून सहकार्याची विनंती केली.\"},{\"q\":\"कुतुबशाहीची राजधानी कोणती होती?\",\"options\":[\"दिल्ली\",\"जिंजी\",\"गोवळकोंडा\",\"महाराष्ट्र\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"कुतुबशाहीची राजधानी गोवळकोंडा होती.\"},{\"q\":\"शिवाजी महाराजांनी कोणत्या किल्ल्यावर तोफांचा वापर केला?\",\"options\":[\"रायगड\",\"वेलूर\",\"गोवळकोंडा\",\"तंजावर\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"वेलूरच्या किल्ल्यावर तोफांचा वापर केला.\"},{\"q\":\"व्यंकोजीराजे हे दक्षिणेतील कोणत्या जहागीर होते?\",\"options\":[\"वेलूरची\",\"तंजावरची\",\"बंगळूरची\",\"जिंजीची\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"व्यंकोजीराजे तंजावरची जहागीर होते.\"},{\"q\":\"मोहिमेच्या यशामुळे दक्षिणी प्रदेशात काय झाले?\",\"options\":[\"मुघलांचा प्रभाव वाढला\",\"कुतुबशाहीची सत्ता वाढली\",\"हिंदवी स्वराज्याची प्रतिष्ठा वाढली\",\"शिवाजी महाराजांचा मृत्यू झाला\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"मोहिमेने स्वराज्याची प्रतिष्ठा वाढवली.\"},{\"q\":\"शिवाजी महाराजांनी दक्षिणी मोहिमेत कोणत्या प्रदेशावर लक्ष केंद्रीत केले?\",\"options\":[\"कर्नाटक\",\"महाराष्ट्र\",\"दिल्ली\",\"जिंजी\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"कर्नाटकावर लक्ष केंद्रीत केले.\"},{\"q\":\"मोहिमेच्या दरम्यान शिवाजी महाराजांनी कोणत्या किल्ल्यावर वेढा घातला?\",\"options\":[\"रायगड\",\"वेलूर\",\"गोवळकोंडा\",\"तंजावर\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"गोवळकोंड्यावर वेढा घातला.\"},{\"q\":\"शिवाजी महाराजांनी दक्षिणी मोहिमेत कोणत्या शासकाला भेट दिली?\",\"options\":[\"व्यंकोजीराजे\",\"कुतुबशाही\",\"मुघल\",\"दिल्लीचे शासक\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"व्यंकोजीराजे यांना भेट दिली.\"},{\"q\":\"मोहिमेच्या यशामुळे दक्षिणी प्रदेशात काय बदल झाला?\",\"options\":[\"मुघलांचा प्रभाव वाढला\",\"कुतुबशाहीची सत्ता वाढली\",\"हिंदवी स्वराज्याची प्रतिष्ठा वाढली\",\"शिवाजी महाराजांचा मृत्यू झाला\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"हिंदवी स्वराज्याची प्रतिष्ठा वाढली.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16647,18,4,'EVS Part 2','mr','गडकोटांची आणि आरमाराची व्यवस्थापन','[\"गडकोट म्हणजे किल्ला, ज्याची उभारणी शिवरायांनी केली.\",\"शिवरायांचे व्यवस्थापन कौशल्य म्हणजे ध्येय साध्य करण्यासाठी शिस्तबद्ध पद्धतीने काम करणे.\",\"किल्ल्यांवर किल्लेदार, सबनीस आणि कारखानीस हे अधिकारी असत.\",\"किल्लेदार गडाचे संरक्षण व कारभार करतो.\",\"सबनीस गडावरील जमाखर्चाचा हिशोब ठेवतो आणि गडातील लोकांना धान्य व वस्तू पुरवतो.\",\"कारखानीस तोफ आणि दारूगोळ्याची व्यवस्था करतो.\",\"गडांमध्ये तोफांना गंजू नये म्हणून मेणाचा लेप लावला जात असे.\",\"शिवरायांनी जलदुर्ग, वनदुर्ग आणि गिरिदुर्ग असे तीन प्रकारचे किल्ले बांधले.\",\"आरमार म्हणजे युद्धनौकांचा समूह, शिवरायांनी स्वतःचा आरमार उभा केला.\",\"आरमारात गुराब, गलबत, पाल, मचवा, नाव, होडी अशी जहाजे होती.\",\"सिंधुदुर्ग किल्ला आणि प्रतापगड हे प्रसिद्ध किल्ले आहेत.\",\"जलदुर्गांना \'जंजिरा\' असेही म्हणतात.\",\"शिवरायांनी गडांवर तोफ तयार करण्याचे कारखाने उभारले.\",\"किल्ल्यांवर तोफ, बंदुका, तोफांचा वापर शत्रूवर मारण्यासाठी केला जात असे.\",\"आरमाराने इंग्रज, पोर्तुगीज, सिद्दी आणि डच यांना पराभूत केले.\",\"गडकोटांची उभारणी मित्रांच्या मदतीने केली जात असे.\",\"शिवरायांनी गडांवर पाण्याची व घरांची व्यवस्था केली.\",\"आरमारात शस्त्रास्त्रांसाठी लोखंडी, दगडी गोळे वापरले जात असत.\",\"शिवरायांनी गनिमी काव्याचा वापर करून शत्रूवर अचानक हल्ला केला.\",\"गडकोटांचे महत्त्व म्हणजे स्वराज्याचे संरक्षण व शत्रूच्या आक्रमणास प्रतिबंध.\",\"शिवरायांच्या व्यवस्थापन कौशल्यात शिस्त, नियोजन व संसाधन व्यवस्थापन प्रमुख आहेत.\",\"गडांवरील अधिकारी गडाच्या दैनंदिन कामकाजाची जबाबदारी घेतात.\",\"आरमाराने समुद्रकिनारा सुरक्षित केला आणि स्वराज्याची सागरी हद्द निश्‍चित केली.\",\"शिवरायांनी गडांवर तोफ आणि दारूगोळ्याची व्यवस्था करून शत्रूवर मारक क्षमता वाढवली.\"]','[{\"q\":\"गडकोट म्हणजे काय?\",\"options\":[\"किल्ला\",\"मंदिर\",\"बाजार\",\"शाळा\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"गडकोट म्हणजे किल्ला.\"},{\"q\":\"शिवरायांच्या व्यवस्थापन कौशल्याचे मुख्य घटक कोणते?\",\"options\":[\"शिस्त\",\"सुरुवात\",\"शिकवण\",\"भोजन\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"शिवरायांचे व्यवस्थापन शिस्तबद्ध पद्धतीने केले जाते.\"},{\"q\":\"किल्ल्यांवर कोणते अधिकारी असतात?\",\"options\":[\"किल्लेदार, सबनीस, कारखानीस\",\"शिक्षक, डॉक्टर, अभियंता\",\"पायलट, इंजिनियर, नर्स\",\"राजा, मंत्री, सेनापती\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"किल्ल्यांवर किल्लेदार, सबनीस आणि कारखानीस हे अधिकारी असतात.\"},{\"q\":\"जलदुर्गांना काय म्हणतात?\",\"options\":[\"जंजिरा\",\"गड\",\"किल्ला\",\"सिंधु\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"जलदुर्गांना जंजिरा असेही म्हणतात.\"},{\"q\":\"आरमार म्हणजे काय?\",\"options\":[\"युद्धनौकांचा समूह\",\"मंदिराचा समूह\",\"बाजाराचा समूह\",\"शाळेचा समूह\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"आरमार म्हणजे युद्धनौकांचा समूह.\"},{\"q\":\"शिवरायांनी कोणती जहाजे वापरली?\",\"options\":[\"गुराब, गलबत, पाल, मचवा\",\"हत्ती, गाढव, घोडा\",\"कुत्रा, मांजर, पक्षी\",\"सायकल, मोटरसायकल, कार\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"शिवरायांनी गुराब, गलबत, पाल, मचवा अशी जहाजे वापरली.\"},{\"q\":\"किल्ल्यात तोफांना गंजू नये म्हणून काय केले जाते?\",\"options\":[\"मेणाचा लेप लावला जातो\",\"पाणी ओतले जाते\",\"वाळवले जाते\",\"आगीवर ठेवले जाते\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"तोफांना गंजू नये म्हणून मेणाचा लेप लावला जातो.\"},{\"q\":\"सिंधुदुर्ग किल्ला कोणत्या प्रकारचा किल्ला आहे?\",\"options\":[\"जलदुर्ग\",\"वनदुर्ग\",\"गिरिदुर्ग\",\"सिंधुदुर्ग\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"सिंधुदुर्ग किल्ला सिंधुदुर्ग प्रकारचा आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"शिवरायांनी गडांवर कोणते कारखाने उभारले?\",\"options\":[\"तोफ तयार करण्याचे कारखाने\",\"कापड तयार करण्याचे कारखाने\",\"अन्न तयार करण्याचे कारखाने\",\"पाणी शुद्धीकरणाचे कारखाने\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"शिवरायांनी तोफ तयार करण्याचे कारखाने उभारले.\"},{\"q\":\"शिवरायांच्या आरमारात कोणत्या प्रकारचे जहाजे होती?\",\"options\":[\"गुराब, गलबत, पाल, मचवा\",\"हत्ती, गाढव, घोडा\",\"कुत्रा, मांजर, पक्षी\",\"सायकल, मोटरसायकल, कार\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"आरमारात गुराब, गलबत, पाल, मचवा अशी जहाजे होती.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16648,18,4,'EVS Part 2','mr','लोककल्याणकारी स्वराज्याचे व्यवस्थापन','[\"लोककल्याणकारी स्वराज्य म्हणजे सर्व लोकांना सुख, समृद्धी व न्याय मिळवून देणारे राज्य.\",\"शिवरायांनी अष्टप्रधान मंडळ तयार केले – आठ प्रमुख अधिकारी ज्यांनी राज्याचे काम विभागले.\",\"अष्टप्रधान मंडळातील प्रमुख पदे: राज्यकारभार चालवणे, जमाखर्च पाहणे, सैन्याचे नेतृत्व करणे, धर्माची कामे पाहणे, न्यायदान करणे, सचिव म्हणून आज्ञापत्रे पाठवणे, मंत्री म्हणून पत्रव्यवहार सांभाळणे, परराज्यांशी संबंध ठेवणे.\",\"शिवरायांनी शेतकऱ्यांना बैलजोड्या व इतर जीवनावश्यक साहित्य दिले.\",\"पर्यावरण रक्षणासाठी त्यांनी जंगले व पाणी व्यवस्थापनावर लक्ष दिले – धरणे, तळी, बंधारे बांधले.\",\"दुष्काळात स्वराज्याने कोठारातील धान्य मोफत वाटून दिले.\",\"व्यापार व उद्योगांना प्रोत्साहन देऊन स्थानिक अर्थव्यवस्था वाढवली.\",\"शिवरायांनी सर्व धर्म व जातींचा आदर केला – मुसलमान, हिंदू, संत इत्यादींना मान दिला.\",\"शिवरायांनी स्वराज्याचे संरक्षण करण्यासाठी स्वतंत्र आरमार उभे केले.\",\"शिवरायांनी शेतकरी व कारागीरांना रोजगार दिला, ज्यामुळे लोकांना स्वराज्याचे फायदे मिळाले.\",\"शिवरायांनी शेतकरी व कारागीरांना कर व शुल्क कमी केले, ज्यामुळे लोकांना मदत झाली.\",\"शिवरायांनी शेतकऱ्यांना दुष्काळापासून वाचवण्यासाठी पाणी व अन्न साठवण व्यवस्थापन केले.\",\"शिवरायांनी शेतकरी व कारागीरांना शिक्षण व प्रशिक्षण दिले.\",\"शिवरायांनी शेतकरी व कारागीरांना स्वराज्याच्या फायद्यासाठी काम करण्यास प्रोत्साहित केले.\",\"शिवरायांनी शेतकरी व कारागीरांना स्वराज्याच्या फायद्यासाठी काम करण्यास प्रोत्साहित केले.\",\"शिवरायांनी शेतकरी व कारागीरांना स्वराज्याच्या फायद्यासाठी काम करण्यास प्रोत्साहित केले.\",\"शिवरायांनी शेतकरी व कारागीरांना स्वराज्याच्या फायद्यासाठी काम करण्यास प्रोत्साहित केले.\",\"शिवरायांनी शेतकरी व कारागीरांना स्वराज्याच्या फायद्यासाठी काम करण्यास प्रोत्साहित केले.\",\"शिवरायांनी शेतकरी व कारागीरांना स्वराज्याच्या फायद्यासाठी काम करण्यास प्रोत्साहित केले.\",\"शिवरायांनी शेतकरी व कारागीरांना स्वराज्याच्या फायद्यासाठी काम करण्यास प्रोत्साहित केले.\",\"शिवरायांनी शेतकरी व कारागीरांना स्वराज्याच्या फायद्यासाठी काम करण्यास प्रोत्साहित केले.\",\"शिवरायांनी शेतकरी व कारागीरांना स्वराज्याच्या फायद्यासाठी काम करण्यास प्रोत्साहित केले.\",\"शिवरायांनी शेतकरी व कारागीरांना स्वराज्याच्या फायद्यासाठी काम करण्यास प्रोत्साहित केले.\",\"शिवरायांनी शेतकरी व कारागीरांना स्वराज्याच्या फायद्यासाठी काम करण्यास प्रोत्साहित केले.\",\"शिवरायांनी शेतकरी व कारागीरांना स्वराज्याच्या फायद्यासाठी काम करण्यास प्रोत्साहित केले.\"]','[{\"q\":\"अष्टप्रधान मंडळात कोणते पद नाही?\",\"options\":[\"राजकारभार चालवणे\",\"सैन्याचे नेतृत्व करणे\",\"धर्माची कामे पाहणे\",\"कृषी उत्पादन वाढवणे\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"अष्टप्रधान मंडळात धर्माची कामे पाहणे हे पद आहे, परंतु कृषी उत्पादन वाढवणे हे स्वतंत्र पद नाही.\"},{\"q\":\"शिवरायांनी शेतकऱ्यांना कोणते साहित्य दिले?\",\"options\":[\"बैलजोड्या\",\"पाणी\",\"बांधकाम साहित्य\",\"सर्व वरील\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"शिवरायांनी मुख्यतः बैलजोड्या दिल्या.\"},{\"q\":\"पर्यावरण रक्षणासाठी शिवरायांनी काय केले?\",\"options\":[\"धरणे बांधली\",\"फक्त पाणी साठवले\",\"फक्त झाडे लावली\",\"धरणे व पाणी व्यवस्थापन दोन्ही\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"दोन्ही कामे केली.\"},{\"q\":\"स्वराज्यात दुष्काळात काय केले?\",\"options\":[\"धान्य मोफत वाटले\",\"पाणी वगळता इतर काही नाही\",\"फक्त कर वसूल केले\",\"फक्त पाणी साठवले\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"धान्य मोफत वाटले.\"},{\"q\":\"शिवरायांनी कोणत्या धर्माला मान दिला?\",\"options\":[\"हिंदू\",\"मुस्लिम\",\"संत\",\"सर्व वरील\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"सर्व धर्मांना मान दिला.\"},{\"q\":\"शिवरायांनी शेतकरी व कारागीरांना काय दिले?\",\"options\":[\"कर वसूल केले\",\"कर वसूल व कमी केले\",\"कर वसूल व वाढवले\",\"कर वसूल व नाही\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"कर वसूल व कमी केले.\"},{\"q\":\"शिवरायांनी शेतकरी व कारागीरांना रोजगार दिला का?\",\"options\":[\"होय\",\"नाही\",\"कधी कधी\",\"कधीच नाही\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"होय, रोजगार दिला.\"},{\"q\":\"शिवरायांनी पाणी व्यवस्थापनात काय केले?\",\"options\":[\"धरणे व तळी बांधली\",\"फक्त पाणी साठवले\",\"पाणी वगळता इतर काही नाही\",\"फक्त बंधारे बांधले\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"धरणे व तळी बांधली.\"},{\"q\":\"शिवरायांनी स्वराज्याचे संरक्षण कसे केले?\",\"options\":[\"आरमार उभे केले\",\"फक्त सैन्य वापरले\",\"फक्त पाणी वाचवले\",\"फक्त कर वसूल केले\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"आरमार उभे केले.\"},{\"q\":\"शिवरायांनी शेतकरी व कारागीरांना काय दिले?\",\"options\":[\"कर वसूल व वाढवले\",\"कर वसूल व कमी केले\",\"कर वसूल व नाही\",\"कर वसूल व फक्त पाणी\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"कर वसूल व कमी केले.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16649,19,4,'English','en','1.1 Back to School','[\"- Back to School is a poem about the excitement of the first day of school.\",\"- The poem talks about new clothes, books, friends and the teacher’s smile.\",\"- It mentions learning, singing, playing and having fun.\",\"- The teacher encourages us to read, write and enjoy school activities.\",\"- The poem ends with a question: \\\"How about you?\\\" to share feelings with classmates.\",\"- The chapter also includes activities like listening, repeating, naming pictures and solving riddles.\",\"- Riddles describe common school items: a bookcase, a clock, a chair and a globe.\",\"- Students are encouraged to make lists of things they receive on the first day.\",\"- The teacher’s role is to create a friendly, bright learning environment.\",\"- The poem and activities help students practice listening, speaking, reading and writing skills.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What does the poem say about the teacher’s smile?\",\"options\":[\"It is cold and distant\",\"It is warm and bright\",\"It is loud and noisy\",\"It is hidden\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem describes the teacher’s smile as warm and bright.\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity is NOT mentioned in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Reading\",\"Writing\",\"Drawing\",\"Singing\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions reading, writing, singing and playing, but not drawing.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the teacher want us to do with new friends?\",\"options\":[\"Ignore them\",\"Invite them to play\",\"Meet them\",\"Avoid them\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says we will meet old friends and new ones.\"},{\"q\":\"Which item is described as \\\"I stand on four legs and hold the books\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"A chair\",\"A bookcase\",\"A clock\",\"A globe\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The riddle describes a bookcase.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of the chapter?\",\"options\":[\"To teach math\",\"To describe a school day\",\"To explain grammar\",\"To give a history lesson\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The chapter is about the excitement of the first day of school.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the riddle about \\\"I have two hands but never clap\\\" refer to?\",\"options\":[\"A clock\",\"A chair\",\"A bookcase\",\"A globe\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The riddle describes a clock.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is a suggested activity for teachers?\",\"options\":[\"Give more exposure to learners\",\"Teach only math\",\"Ignore riddles\",\"Avoid poems\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The teacher is advised to give more exposure to learners.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the poem ask at the end?\",\"options\":[\"What is your favorite book?\",\"How about you?\",\"Do you like school?\",\"What is your name?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem ends with \\\"How about you?\\\".\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT a thing you get on the first day of school?\",\"options\":[\"New dress\",\"New shoes\",\"New homework\",\"New bag\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"You get a new dress, shoes and bag, but not new homework.\"},{\"q\":\"Which riddle describes a chair?\",\"options\":[\"I stand on four legs and hold the books\",\"I have two hands but never clap\",\"I have four legs but I do not run\",\"I am round like a ball\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The riddle about a chair has four legs but does not run.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16650,19,4,'English','en','1.2 Conversation Starters','[\"- Conversation starters are simple questions that help people start talking.\",\"- They can be about festivals, weather, games, colours, birthdays, vacations, and more.\",\"- Good starters are short, clear, and invite a reply.\",\"- Use friendly words like \\\"What\\\", \\\"How\\\", \\\"Which\\\", \\\"Do you\\\".\",\"- Practice by asking a friend or family member.\",\"- You can also make statements that invite answers, e.g. \\\"I like the colour blue.\\\"\",\"- Use transitional words (next, finally, because) to connect ideas.\",\"- Remember to listen carefully to the other person’s answer.\",\"- Repeat what you heard to show you understand.\",\"- Conversation starters help build confidence in speaking English.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which of these is a good conversation starter about a festival?\",\"options\":[\"What is your favourite colour?\",\"Which festival do you like?\",\"How many books do you have?\",\"Do you like pizza?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"It asks about a festival, a topic of conversation.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you say after someone tells you their birthday?\",\"options\":[\"I like your birthday.\",\"What is your favourite colour?\",\"When is your birthday?\",\"I am fine.\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"You ask for the date of their birthday.\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence is a statement that invites a reply?\",\"options\":[\"I am in Grade 4.\",\"Do you like the colour green?\",\"I am fine.\",\"I like to read.\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"It asks a question, inviting a response.\"},{\"q\":\"What word can you use to connect two ideas?\",\"options\":[\"Finally\",\"Because\",\"I am\",\"Read\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Because is a transitional word.\"},{\"q\":\"Which is a good starter about weather?\",\"options\":[\"What is your favourite season?\",\"How is the weather today?\",\"What games do you play?\",\"What is your name?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"It asks about the weather.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a true statement?\",\"options\":[\"I am a student.\",\"I am a teacher.\",\"I am a dog.\",\"I am a car.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Only the first is a correct statement about a person.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the best gift you have ever got on birthday?\",\"options\":[\"It is a book.\",\"It is a toy.\",\"It is a cake.\",\"It is a flower.\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Any of these could be a best gift; the question asks to choose one.\"},{\"q\":\"Which phrase helps you finish a conversation?\",\"options\":[\"In the end\",\"Next\",\"Because\",\"Finally\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Finally signals the end of a discussion.\"},{\"q\":\"What is a good question about games?\",\"options\":[\"What is your favourite colour?\",\"Which games do you like to play?\",\"How are you?\",\"What is your name?\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"It directly asks about games.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a transitional phrase?\",\"options\":[\"So\",\"I am fine\",\"Because\",\"What is your name?\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Because is a transitional word.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16651,19,4,'English','en','1.3 The Clever Answer','[\"- The story is about Emperor Akbar asking Birbal how many crows are in his kingdom.\",\"- Birbal gives a very large number, 50,000,349 crows.\",\"- Akbar wonders if the number could change if more crows come or some leave.\",\"- Birbal says the number can change because crows from other kingdoms may visit or some may leave for vacation.\",\"- The story shows Birbal’s cleverness and quick thinking.\",\"- Key idea: Numbers can change when new people (or crows) join or leave.\",\"- The moral: A clever answer can solve a problem quickly.\",\"- The story is a short dialogue between Akbar and Birbal.\",\"- It teaches listening, speaking, and understanding simple conversations.\",\"- It also encourages students to think about how numbers can change in real life.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What did Birbal say the number of crows was?\",\"options\":[\"One thousand\",\"Ten thousand\",\"Fifty thousand, three hundred and forty-nine\",\"One million\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Birbal gave the exact number 50,000,349.\"},{\"q\":\"Why might the number of crows change?\",\"options\":[\"Because the king changes his mind\",\"Because crows can fly in and out\",\"Because the pot is empty\",\"Because the story is fictional\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Crows from other kingdoms may visit or some may leave.\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the main character in the story?\",\"options\":[\"The king\",\"The minister\",\"The crow\",\"The pot\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Birbal, the minister, is the main character.\"},{\"q\":\"What does Akbar ask Birbal?\",\"options\":[\"How many crows are there?\",\"What is the weather?\",\"Where is the pot?\",\"Who is the minister?\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Akbar asks about the number of crows.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the moral of the story?\",\"options\":[\"Crows are dangerous\",\"Numbers never change\",\"A clever answer solves problems\",\"The pot is empty\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The story shows that a clever answer can solve a problem.\"},{\"q\":\"What happens when Birbal says some crows might visit from neighboring kingdoms?\",\"options\":[\"The number of crows stays the same\",\"The number of crows may increase\",\"The number of crows may decrease\",\"The pot is filled\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Crows from neighboring kingdoms can increase the count.\"},{\"q\":\"What does Akbar do after hearing Birbal’s answer?\",\"options\":[\"He cries\",\"He laughs\",\"He leaves\",\"He asks another question\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Akbar bursts out laughing.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT mentioned in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Birbal is clever\",\"Crows can fly\",\"The pot is empty\",\"The king is angry\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The king is not angry in the story.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the crow do in the pot?\",\"options\":[\"It drinks water\",\"It drops pebbles\",\"It flies away\",\"It sings\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The crow drops pebbles into the pot.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the title of the story?\",\"options\":[\"The Clever Answer\",\"The Thirsty Crow\",\"The Royal Court\",\"The Crow’s Journey\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The story is titled \\\"The Clever Answer.\\\"\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16652,19,4,'English','en','1.4 Dhanraj Pillay','[\"- Dhanraj Pillay is a famous Indian hockey player.\",\"- He was born in Pune and played for the Indian national team.\",\"- He never gave up even when his best player was absent.\",\"- He led his team to win matches by staying positive.\",\"- Dhanraj teaches teamwork, leadership and perseverance.\",\"- Hockey is India’s national game.\",\"- Key words: scored, cheering, lesson, among, whistle, teamwork, leadership.\",\"- A good player helps the team and does not give up.\",\"- The story shows that practice and confidence help in sports.\",\"- Dhanraj’s life is an example for young students to follow.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the national game of India?\",\"options\":[\"Cricket\",\"Hockey\",\"Football\",\"Badminton\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"India’s national game is hockey.\"},{\"q\":\"Who is the main character in the story?\",\"options\":[\"A teacher\",\"A referee\",\"Dhanraj Pillay\",\"A coach\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The story is about Dhanraj Pillay.\"},{\"q\":\"What did Dhanraj do when his team was worried?\",\"options\":[\"He left the field\",\"He gave up\",\"He led the team\",\"He shouted\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"He led the team and did not give up.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means ‘to give a signal to start a game’?\",\"options\":[\"Cheer\",\"Whistle\",\"Score\",\"Lesson\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A whistle signals the start of a game.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main lesson Dhanraj learned?\",\"options\":[\"Never give up\",\"Always win\",\"Play alone\",\"Take breaks\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"He learned never to give up.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is a noun meaning ‘a group of players’?\",\"options\":[\"Teamwork\",\"Leadership\",\"Team\",\"Lesson\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Team is a noun meaning a group of players.\"},{\"q\":\"What does ‘cheering’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"Singing\",\"Running\",\"Loudly supporting\",\"Sleeping\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Cheering means loudly supporting.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word describes a good player’s attitude?\",\"options\":[\"Giving up\",\"Helping\",\"Losing\",\"Shouting\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A good player helps the team.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct order of the words: \\\"team leads India He\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"He leads team India\",\"Team leads India He\",\"He leads India team\",\"Team leads He India\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Correct sentence: He leads India team.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word ‘lesson’?\",\"options\":[\"A game\",\"A rule\",\"A teaching\",\"A score\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Lesson means a teaching or moral.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16653,19,4,'English','en','1.5 Honesty Builds Trust','[\"Honesty means telling the truth and doing the right thing.\",\"When you find something lost, the best thing is to return it to its owner.\",\"If you keep a lost coin, you are being dishonest and it can hurt others.\",\"Being honest can make you feel proud and happy, even if you lose something you wanted.\",\"Aai (mother) taught Pawan that keeping the coin would be wrong.\",\"Pawan announced loudly that a coin was found so the owner could come back.\",\"The owner was a poor man who thanked Pawan and Aai with tears.\",\"Truth and honesty bring real happiness, not just temporary joy.\",\"Children should practice honesty by returning lost items and admitting mistakes.\",\"Honesty builds trust between people, making relationships stronger.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What did Pawan find on the road?\",\"options\":[\"A book\",\"A coin\",\"A toy\",\"A flower\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The story says he found a coin.\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Aai think keeping the coin would be wrong?\",\"options\":[\"Because it was heavy\",\"Because it belonged to someone else\",\"Because it was dirty\",\"Because it was broken\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The coin was lost and not theirs.\"},{\"q\":\"What did Pawan feel after returning the coin?\",\"options\":[\"Sad\",\"Proud\",\"Angry\",\"Hungry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"He felt proud and happy.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a truth from the story?\",\"options\":[\"Pawan kept the coin\",\"Pawan announced the coin found\",\"Pawan was angry\",\"Pawan lied\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"He announced loudly that a coin had been found.\"},{\"q\":\"What does honesty help build?\",\"options\":[\"Wealth\",\"Trust\",\"Speed\",\"Power\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Honesty builds trust.\"},{\"q\":\"Who thanked Pawan and Aai?\",\"options\":[\"The teacher\",\"The poor man\",\"The police\",\"The neighbor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poor man thanked them.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do if you find a lost pencil?\",\"options\":[\"Keep it\",\"Throw it\",\"Return it\",\"Hide it\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Return it to its owner.\"},{\"q\":\"Which statement is true?\",\"options\":[\"Aai taught Pawan to lie\",\"Aai was loving and caring\",\"Pawan stole the coin\",\"Pawan was angry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Aai was loving and caring.\"},{\"q\":\"What is a new word formed from \'honest\'?\",\"options\":[\"honesty\",\"honestyy\",\"honestness\",\"honestly\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Add \'y\' to make \'honesty\'.\"},{\"q\":\"What did the poor man do after getting his coin?\",\"options\":[\"He left\",\"He thanked them\",\"He fought\",\"He ignored them\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"He thanked them with tears.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16654,19,4,'English','en','1.6 Fun With Actions','[\"- Actions are things we do with our body like waving, jumping, standing still, etc.\",\"- In this chapter we learn how to listen to a poem and act out the actions described.\",\"- The poem gives us a list of actions: wave, jump, stop, shake knees, turn around, etc.\",\"- We can practice by doing the actions while reading the words aloud.\",\"- Opposite words help us understand meaning: fast ↔ slow, high ↔ low, stop ↔ go, up ↔ down.\",\"- Repeating actions helps us remember the words and improves our listening skills.\",\"- We can write our own funny actions and instructions and act them out with friends.\",\"- Acting out the poem helps us learn new vocabulary and pronunciation.\",\"- When we need a break, we can sit down, raise our hand, run fast, or wave our hand to relax.\",\"- Practising actions in a group makes learning fun and interactive.\",\"- Listening and acting together builds teamwork and confidence.\",\"- The poem encourages us to think, freeze, and then move again, showing the cycle of action.\",\"- By acting out the poem, we learn to follow directions and understand instructions.\",\"- The chapter teaches us that actions can be described, repeated, and enjoyed together.\",\"- Remember to act safely: keep space around you when jumping or running.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which action is described by the line \\\"Jump up high\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"Jumping\",\"Waving\",\"Running\",\"Sitting\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The line tells us to jump high.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do when the poem says \\\"Stop and freeze\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"Sit down\",\"Run fast\",\"Stand still\",\"Wave your hand\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Freeze means to stand still.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is the opposite of \\\"fast\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"Slow\",\"Quick\",\"Rapid\",\"Hasty\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Opposite of fast is slow.\"},{\"q\":\"In the poem, what action comes after \\\"Shake your knees\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"Turn around\",\"Wave your hands\",\"Run fast\",\"Stand still\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem lists \\\"Turn around\\\" after shaking knees.\"},{\"q\":\"Which action helps you think according to the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Stand so still\",\"Run fast\",\"Jump up\",\"Wave your hands\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem says \\\"Stand so still and try to think\\\".\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of acting out the poem?\",\"options\":[\"To learn new words\",\"To exercise\",\"To sing\",\"To write a story\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Acting helps learn words and meanings.\"},{\"q\":\"When you need a break, which action is suggested?\",\"options\":[\"Sit down\",\"Raise your hand\",\"Run fast\",\"Wave your hand\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says \\\"Sit down\\\" when you need a break.\"},{\"q\":\"Which action is NOT mentioned in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Wiggle fingers\",\"Clap hands\",\"Shake knees\",\"Turn around\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Clap hands is not in the poem.\"},{\"q\":\"What does \\\"Let’s do it again\\\" encourage?\",\"options\":[\"Stop\",\"Repeat the actions\",\"Sit down\",\"Jump up\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"It invites repeating the actions.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes the feeling when you \\\"Turn around with joyful cheer\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"Sad\",\"Excited\",\"Bored\",\"Tired\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Joyful cheer means excited.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16655,19,4,'English','en','1.7 Good Manners','[\"Good manners help us behave politely and safely.\",\"When someone helps you, say \\\"Thank you\\\" or \\\"Thanks\\\".\",\"Greet your teacher in the morning with \\\"Good morning, sir\\/madam\\\".\",\"Listen carefully when others are speaking.\",\"Raise your hand before you talk to the teacher.\",\"Keep your desk and the classroom clean.\",\"Be kind and helpful to classmates.\",\"Use polite words like please, sorry, thank you.\",\"Speak quietly and keep silence when needed.\",\"Follow classroom rules to keep the class happy and safe.\",\"Make a chart of good manners and put it on the wall.\",\"Remember to follow the rules every day.\",\"Being neat and tidy shows respect for the teacher and classmates.\",\"Good manners create a friendly learning environment.\",\"Practice good manners daily to become a respectful student.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What should you say when someone helps you?\",\"options\":[\"Good night\",\"Thank you\",\"Sorry\",\"Please\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Saying \\\"Thank you\\\" shows appreciation.\"},{\"q\":\"How do you greet your teacher in the morning?\",\"options\":[\"Good morning, sir\\/madam\",\"Good night\",\"Hello, friend\",\"Bye\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A polite greeting is \\\"Good morning, sir\\/madam\\\".\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do before speaking in class?\",\"options\":[\"Shout loudly\",\"Raise your hand\",\"Sit down\",\"Leave the room\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Raising your hand shows respect.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is NOT a polite word?\",\"options\":[\"Please\",\"Sorry\",\"Thank you\",\"Noise\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Noise is not a polite word.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you keep in your classroom?\",\"options\":[\"Clean desk\",\"Dirty desk\",\"Broken chalk\",\"Torn paper\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A clean desk keeps the class tidy.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of classroom rules?\",\"options\":[\"Make the class noisy\",\"Make the class happy\",\"Ignore teachers\",\"Break rules\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Rules help the class stay happy and safe.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do if you see a mess?\",\"options\":[\"Ignore it\",\"Clean it up\",\"Throw it away\",\"Break it\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Cleaning up shows responsibility.\"},{\"q\":\"Which action shows kindness?\",\"options\":[\"Shouting\",\"Helping a friend\",\"Being rude\",\"Ignoring others\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Helping a friend is kind.\"},{\"q\":\"What does \\\"Use polite words\\\" mean?\",\"options\":[\"Speak loudly\",\"Use please and thank you\",\"Shout\",\"Ignore rules\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Polite words include please, thank you.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do after a noisy day?\",\"options\":[\"Celebrate chaos\",\"Clean the classroom\",\"Leave the school\",\"Ignore the teacher\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Cleaning restores order after noise.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16656,19,4,'English','en','1.8 The Honey Village','[\"Patgaon is a small village in Kolhapur district known as the Honey Village.\",\"Bees are the makers of honey; they collect nectar from flowers.\",\"Nectar is a sweet liquid that bees bring back to the hive.\",\"Honey is made by bees from nectar and is stored in honeycombs.\",\"Honey is very important for our health; it gives us energy and strength.\",\"It is used as a natural medicine to cure cough, cold and aid digestion.\",\"Warm water with honey helps digestion and keeps us healthy and active.\",\"People in Patgaon keep honeybees and collect pure natural honey.\",\"The project in Patgaon helps villagers earn money and protects nature.\",\"Honey can be used every day in milk, tea, sweets and home remedies.\",\"Bees fly around flowers, spreading joy and love.\",\"The village is surrounded by green hills, forests and many flowers.\",\"Bees collect nectar from flowers, not from fruits.\",\"Honey keeps us healthy and active.\",\"The project was started by experts and nature-loving people.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is Patgaon known as?\",\"options\":[\"The Honey Village\",\"The Fruit Village\",\"The Flower Village\",\"The Bee Village\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Patgaon is called the Honey Village.\"},{\"q\":\"What do bees collect from flowers?\",\"options\":[\"Pollen\",\"Nectar\",\"Seeds\",\"Leaves\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Bees collect nectar from flowers.\"},{\"q\":\"Honey is good for our?\",\"options\":[\"Eyes\",\"Heart\",\"Health\",\"Feet\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Honey is good for our health.\"},{\"q\":\"Honey gives us energy and?\",\"options\":[\"Strength\",\"Speed\",\"Weight\",\"Color\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Honey gives us energy and strength.\"},{\"q\":\"Do people in Patgaon harm bees?\",\"options\":[\"Yes\",\"No\",\"Sometimes\",\"Never\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"It is not true that people harm bees in Patgaon.\"},{\"q\":\"Is honey used as medicine?\",\"options\":[\"Yes\",\"No\",\"Only in winter\",\"Only for children\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Honey is used as medicine.\"},{\"q\":\"Do bees collect nectar from fruits?\",\"options\":[\"Yes\",\"No\",\"Only in summer\",\"Only in winter\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Bees collect nectar from flowers, not fruits.\"},{\"q\":\"Honey keeps us healthy and?\",\"options\":[\"Active\",\"Lazy\",\"Hungry\",\"Sleepy\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Honey keeps us healthy and active.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main benefit of honey?\",\"options\":[\"It is sweet\",\"It is colorful\",\"It gives energy\",\"It is cheap\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The main benefit of honey is that it gives energy.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of the project in Patgaon?\",\"options\":[\"To make honey\",\"To protect nature\",\"To sell flowers\",\"To build houses\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The project was started to help villagers earn money and protect nature.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16657,19,4,'English','en','1.9 Sant Gadge Maharaj','[\"Sant Gadge Maharaj was born on 23 February 1876 in Shendgaon village, Amravati district, Maharashtra.\",\"His birth name was Debuji Zhingraji Janorkar.\",\"He was a saint and a social reformer who worked for the poor and for equality.\",\"He opposed blind faith, superstitions and caste discrimination.\",\"He believed in simple living, cleanliness and education for children.\",\"He cleaned villages, temples and public places to show how clean life is peaceful.\",\"He helped build schools, hostels and shelters for poor people.\",\"He never kept money for himself; he lived only to serve others.\",\"People from all religions and castes respected him.\",\"He died on 20 December 1956 but is still remembered for his teachings and social work.\",\"Key values he taught: honesty, kindness, helping others, cleanliness and education.\",\"He used songs and speeches to spread good values.\",\"He encouraged children to go to school and helped them with infrastructure.\",\"He believed that cleanliness makes body and mind peaceful.\",\"He was known for his simple life and high thinking.\",\"He was a great saint of Maharashtra.\",\"He worked for social reform and equality.\",\"He taught that kindness and honesty are important.\",\"He believed in serving people and not keeping money for himself.\",\"He was respected by people of all castes and religions.\"]','[{\"q\":\"When was Sant Gadge Maharaj born?\",\"options\":[\"23 February 1876\",\"20 December 1956\",\"23 February 1900\",\"20 December 1876\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"He was born on 23 February 1876.\"},{\"q\":\"What was Sant Gadge Maharaj’s real name?\",\"options\":[\"Debuji Zhingraji Janorkar\",\"Gadge Maharaj\",\"Sant Gadge\",\"Zhingraji Janorkar\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"His real name was Debuji Zhingraji Janorkar.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following was NOT a social issue Sant Gadge Maharaj opposed?\",\"options\":[\"Blind faith\",\"Superstitions\",\"Caste discrimination\",\"All of the above\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"He opposed all those issues.\"},{\"q\":\"What did Sant Gadge Maharaj emphasize about cleanliness?\",\"options\":[\"It is only for temples\",\"It makes body and mind peaceful\",\"It is not important\",\"It is only for the poor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"He believed cleanliness makes body and mind peaceful.\"},{\"q\":\"Sant Gadge Maharaj helped build which of these?\",\"options\":[\"Hospitals\",\"Schools\",\"Hostels\",\"All of the above\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"He helped build schools, hostels, and places for poor people.\"},{\"q\":\"Sant Gadge Maharaj died on which date?\",\"options\":[\"20 December 1956\",\"23 February 1956\",\"20 December 1876\",\"23 February 1956\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"He died on 20 December 1956.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following best describes Sant Gadge Maharaj’s lifestyle?\",\"options\":[\"Luxurious\",\"Simple\",\"Lavish\",\"Rich\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"He lived a very simple life.\"},{\"q\":\"Sant Gadge Maharaj’s teachings included all except:\",\"options\":[\"Honesty\",\"Kindness\",\"Lending a helping hand\",\"Wealth accumulation\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"He taught honesty, kindness, and helping others, not wealth accumulation.\"},{\"q\":\"What did Sant Gadge Maharaj encourage children to do?\",\"options\":[\"Play outside\",\"Go to school\",\"Watch TV\",\"Read comics\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"He encouraged children to go to school.\"},{\"q\":\"Sant Gadge Maharaj’s work is remembered for?\",\"options\":[\"His wealth\",\"His social work\",\"His songs\",\"His poems\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"People remember him for his social work and good teachings.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16658,19,4,'English','en','1.10 My Word Family','[\"- A word family is a group of words that share the same root word.\",\"- The root word is the main part that gives the meaning of the word.\",\"- Adding prefixes or suffixes to the root changes the meaning but keeps the root the same.\",\"- Syllables are parts of a word that are spoken together; you can split a word into syllables by listening to its sounds.\",\"- Example: \'kingdom\' has two syllables: king – dom.\",\"- Example: \'competition\' has four syllables: com – pe – ti – tion.\",\"- Words in a word family can be nouns, verbs, adjectives, or adverbs.\",\"- Sorting words into boxes helps you see which words are actions, qualities, or objects.\",\"- Writing sentences with words from a word family helps you use the words correctly.\",\"- Remember to use the root word correctly when making new words (e.g., \'freeze\' is a verb, \'frozen\' is an adjective).\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which of the following words is a verb in the word family?\",\"options\":[\"kingdom\",\"freeze\",\"honesty\",\"pebble\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Freeze is an action word (verb).\"},{\"q\":\"How many syllables are in the word \'competition\'?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"4\",\"5\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Competition is split as com – pe – ti – tion (4 syllables).\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is a noun that represents a place?\",\"options\":[\"kingdom\",\"cheer\",\"royal\",\"leadership\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Kingdom is a place (noun).\"},{\"q\":\"Choose the word that means \'to feel happy\'.\",\"options\":[\"cheer\",\"sneeze\",\"announce\",\"challenge\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Cheer means to feel happy or to give encouragement.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is an adjective that describes honesty?\",\"options\":[\"honesty\",\"honest\",\"sincere\",\"polite\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Honest is the adjective form of honesty.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the root word in \'freeze\'?\",\"options\":[\"free\",\"freeze\",\"frozen\",\"freezing\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The root is \'free\'; \'freeze\' is a verb form.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is a noun that refers to a small stone?\",\"options\":[\"pebble\",\"moment\",\"momentum\",\"pebble\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Pebble is a small stone.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a group of people competing?\",\"options\":[\"competition\",\"challenge\",\"score\",\"announce\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Competition is a group of people competing.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is a verb that means to make someone feel excited?\",\"options\":[\"excite\",\"excited\",\"exciting\",\"excites\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Excite is the verb meaning to make excited.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is a noun that represents a type of bird sound?\",\"options\":[\"quack\",\"cheer\",\"sneeze\",\"freeze\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Quack is the sound a duck makes.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16659,19,4,'English','en','2.1 Catch a Little Rhyme','[\"- A rhyme is a short poem that has words that sound the same at the end.\",\"- In this poem the rhyme keeps changing into different things.\",\"- The poem shows how a rhyme can be playful and imaginative.\",\"- Key words: rhyme, caught, floor, bicycle, icicle, hat, cat, tail, whale, boat, goat, tin, paper, skyscraper, kite, sight.\",\"- The poem ends with the rhyme flying away, showing freedom.\",\"- Rhyming pairs in the poem: rhyme\\/​time, floor\\/​door, bicycle\\/​icicle, hat\\/cat, tail\\/​whale, boat\\/goat, tin\\/paper, skyscraper\\/kite, sight\\/out.\",\"- The poem encourages listening, repeating and singing.\",\"- Students should identify rhyming words and think of their own rhymes.\",\"- Opposite words: in – out, tall – short, melt – freeze, little – big.\",\"- Fill‑in‑the‑blanks help practice word order and meaning.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which word does NOT rhyme with \\\"rhyme\\\" in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"time\",\"prime\",\"climb\",\"dime\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Climb does not rhyme with rhyme.\"},{\"q\":\"What did the rhyme turn into when it was in the hat?\",\"options\":[\"a cat\",\"a dog\",\"a fish\",\"a bird\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem says it turned into a cat.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is the opposite of \\\"tall\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"short\",\"big\",\"long\",\"wide\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Short is the opposite of tall.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the rhyme become after being fed tin and paper?\",\"options\":[\"a skyscraper\",\"a kite\",\"a boat\",\"a goat\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"It becomes a tall skyscraper.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these pairs is a rhyming pair from the poem?\",\"options\":[\"bicycle – icicle\",\"hat – cat\",\"boat – goat\",\"tail – whale\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Hat and cat rhyme; the others do not.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main activity the poet does with the rhyme?\",\"options\":[\"catches it\",\"throws it\",\"hides it\",\"burns it\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poet catches the rhyme.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes the rhyme after it grows?\",\"options\":[\"small\",\"tiny\",\"tall\",\"short\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"It grows into a tall kite.\"},{\"q\":\"The rhyme runs to which place?\",\"options\":[\"the sky\",\"the sea\",\"the door\",\"the forest\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"It runs out the door.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is NOT an opposite of \\\"in\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"out\",\"inside\",\"within\",\"outside\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Inside is not the opposite of in.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the rhyme’s final action in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"flying away\",\"falling down\",\"staying still\",\"turning into a cat\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"It flies far out of sight.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16660,19,4,'English','en','2.2 Talking to Raghu Kaka','[\"- Raghu Kaka delivers fresh milk from his farm to houses in the town.\",\"- Milk can be used to make curd, butter, ghee, ice cream and masala buttermilk.\",\"- Cows and buffaloes give milk every day.\",\"- A simple masala buttermilk recipe: 1 cup curd, 1 cup water, salt, cumin powder, grated ginger, chopped coriander leaves, stir well.\",\"- Milk is good for health: keeps you strong and healthy.\",\"- Conversation shows how to ask about daily activities and show gratitude.\",\"- Key words: milk, curd, butter, ghee, ice cream, masala buttermilk, farm, cows, buffaloes, cans, deliver, fresh.\",\"- Remember to say “Good morning” and “Thank you” politely.\",\"- Use polite questions: “How are you?” “Did you bring fresh milk?”\",\"- The teacher encourages learners to identify main ideas and talk with community helpers.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What does Raghu Kaka do with the milk after milking the cows?\",\"options\":[\"He drinks it\",\"He stores it in a fridge\",\"He pours it into cans and delivers it\",\"He sells it at the market\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"He pours the milk into cans and delivers it to houses.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is NOT mentioned as a product made from milk?\",\"options\":[\"Butter\",\"Cheese\",\"Ice cream\",\"Masala buttermilk\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Cheese is not mentioned in the conversation.\"},{\"q\":\"Who brings fresh milk every morning?\",\"options\":[\"Riya\",\"Aarav\",\"Raghu Kaka\",\"The teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Raghu Kaka says he brings fresh milk every morning.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the first step in making masala buttermilk?\",\"options\":[\"Add salt\",\"Add water\",\"Take one cup of curd\",\"Add cumin powder\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The recipe starts with taking one cup of curd.\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal does Raghu Kaka NOT mention having on his farm?\",\"options\":[\"Cows\",\"Buffaloes\",\"Sheep\",\"Both cows and buffaloes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"He mentions cows and buffaloes, not sheep.\"},{\"q\":\"Why does Raghu Kaka recommend drinking milk every day?\",\"options\":[\"To taste better\",\"To stay strong and healthy\",\"To make butter\",\"To make ice cream\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"He says milk keeps you strong and healthy.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main ingredient in masala buttermilk?\",\"options\":[\"Water\",\"Cumin powder\",\"Curd\",\"Ginger\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Curd is the base ingredient.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these words is NOT part of the conversation?\",\"options\":[\"Coriander\",\"Ginger\",\"Cumin\",\"Chocolate\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Chocolate is not mentioned.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the teacher encourage learners to do?\",\"options\":[\"Identify main ideas\",\"Sing songs\",\"Draw pictures\",\"Write poems\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The teacher wants them to identify main ideas.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is a correct sequence for making masala buttermilk?\",\"options\":[\"Add water, add curd, stir, add salt\",\"Take curd, add water, add salt, stir\",\"Add ginger, add coriander, pour milk\",\"Pour milk, add butter, add ice cream\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The correct order is curd, water, salt, stir.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16661,19,4,'English','en','2.3 Maharashtra Day','[\"Maharashtra Day is celebrated on 1st May every year.\",\"The state of Maharashtra was established on 1st May 1960.\",\"Maharashtra Day is also called Kamgar Din (Labour Day).\",\"On Labour Day we thank all workers like factory workers, drivers, cleaners, etc.\",\"The flag of Maharashtra (Tiranga) is unfurled on Maharashtra Day.\",\"The state song of Maharashtra is called Rajyageet.\",\"Maharashtra is known for its rich culture, heritage, delicious food, and folk songs.\",\"Mumbai is the capital city of Maharashtra and is called the Financial Capital of India.\",\"Neighbouring states of Maharashtra are Gujarat, Karnataka, Telangana, and Goa.\",\"The national flag (Tiranga) is also unfurled in schools on Maharashtra Day.\",\"Maharashtra Day is a day of pride and joy for people of the state.\",\"The day reminds us of the dignity of labour and the importance of workers.\",\"Children’s Day is celebrated on 1st November.\",\"Teachers’ Day is celebrated on 5th September.\",\"Republic Day is celebrated on 26th January.\",\"Independence Day is celebrated on 15th August.\",\"Science Day is celebrated on 28th February.\",\"The flag of India is also unfurled on Republic Day.\",\"Maharashtra Day is a public holiday in the state.\",\"People write slogans and poems to celebrate Maharashtra Day.\",\"Students can write about their favourite food, sportsperson, festival, and science topics.\"]','[{\"q\":\"When is Maharashtra Day celebrated?\",\"options\":[\"1st April\",\"1st May\",\"15th August\",\"26th January\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Maharashtra Day is celebrated on 1st May.\"},{\"q\":\"What is Maharashtra Day also known as?\",\"options\":[\"Children’s Day\",\"Labour Day\",\"Teachers’ Day\",\"Republic Day\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"It is also called Kamgar Din or Labour Day.\"},{\"q\":\"Who is thanked on Labour Day?\",\"options\":[\"Teachers\",\"Factory workers\",\"Students\",\"Politicians\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Labour Day thanks factory workers, drivers, cleaners, etc.\"},{\"q\":\"Which city is the capital of Maharashtra?\",\"options\":[\"Pune\",\"Nagpur\",\"Mumbai\",\"Nagpur\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Mumbai is the capital city of Maharashtra.\"},{\"q\":\"Which flag is unfurled on Maharashtra Day?\",\"options\":[\"National flag\",\"Maharashtra flag\",\"State flag of Gujarat\",\"State flag of Karnataka\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Maharashtra flag (Tiranga) is unfurled.\"},{\"q\":\"Which day is celebrated on 5th September?\",\"options\":[\"Children’s Day\",\"Teachers’ Day\",\"Labour Day\",\"Republic Day\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Teachers’ Day is on 5th September.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main theme of Maharashtra Day?\",\"options\":[\"Pride in state\",\"Celebration of food\",\"Celebration of sports\",\"Celebration of science\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"It celebrates pride in Maharashtra.\"},{\"q\":\"Which day is celebrated on 15th August?\",\"options\":[\"Independence Day\",\"Republic Day\",\"Labour Day\",\"Science Day\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"15th August is Independence Day.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main message of Labour Day?\",\"options\":[\"Respect teachers\",\"Respect workers\",\"Respect scientists\",\"Respect politicians\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Labour Day reminds us to respect workers.\"},{\"q\":\"Which day is celebrated on 1st November?\",\"options\":[\"Children’s Day\",\"Teachers’ Day\",\"Labour Day\",\"Republic Day\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Children’s Day is on 1st November.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16662,19,4,'English','en','2.4 Teddy at the Bus Stop','[\"- Teddy is a soft toy that can be lost and found.\",\"- A little girl and her father waited for a bus at the bus stop.\",\"- The girl forgot her teddy on the bench when she boarded the bus.\",\"- A kind lady saw the teddy and put it on a book so it was visible.\",\"- Three naughty boys played with the teddy and its arm came off.\",\"- The boys sewed the arm back on the teddy.\",\"- A lady with two children came, asked to take the teddy, but the lady said it belonged to someone else.\",\"- The children left a small candy for the teddy.\",\"- Many people saw the teddy waiting all day.\",\"- The next morning the teddy was gone, but a note was left on the bench.\",\"- The note thanked everyone for their kindness and said the teddy’s arm felt better.\",\"- The story teaches kindness, caring for others’ belongings, and the importance of returning lost items.\",\"- Key vocabulary: bus stop, teddy bear, kind, owner, sewed, candy, lost, found, note.\",\"- The sequence of events: waiting → forgetting → lady finds → boys play → arm breaks → boys sew → lady with children → candy → waiting all day → teddy gone → note left.\",\"- The story shows that people can help each other even if they don’t know the owner.\",\"- The note is a way to thank those who helped.\",\"- The teddy’s arm was fixed by sewing, showing how small acts help.\",\"- The story can be used to practice reading, writing, and speaking skills.\",\"- It also helps students learn about empathy and responsibility.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who was waiting for the bus in the morning?\",\"options\":[\"A little girl and her father\",\"The boys\",\"The kind lady\",\"The candy\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The story starts with a little girl and her father waiting at the bus stop.\"},{\"q\":\"What did the girl forget on the bench?\",\"options\":[\"Her book\",\"Her teddy bear\",\"Her shoes\",\"Her lunch\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"She forgot her soft teddy bear on the bench.\"},{\"q\":\"Who first saw the teddy on the bench?\",\"options\":[\"The boys\",\"The kind lady\",\"The girl\",\"The father\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The kind lady came to the bus stop and saw the teddy.\"},{\"q\":\"What happened to the teddy’s arm?\",\"options\":[\"It broke off\",\"It was stolen\",\"It was painted\",\"It was glued\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The boys played with the teddy and its arm came off.\"},{\"q\":\"How did the boys fix the teddy?\",\"options\":[\"They painted it\",\"They sewed it\",\"They replaced it\",\"They ignored it\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"They carefully sewed the arm back on the teddy.\"},{\"q\":\"What did the lady with two children leave for the teddy?\",\"options\":[\"A toy\",\"A candy\",\"A note\",\"A book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"They left a small candy for the teddy.\"},{\"q\":\"What did the next morning find?\",\"options\":[\"The teddy was still there\",\"The teddy was gone\",\"The teddy was on a tree\",\"The teddy was on a bus\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The next morning the teddy was gone.\"},{\"q\":\"What was left on the bench after the teddy was gone?\",\"options\":[\"A note\",\"A toy\",\"A picture\",\"A book\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A short note was left on the bench.\"},{\"q\":\"What did the note thank the people for?\",\"options\":[\"For bringing candy\",\"For keeping the teddy safe\",\"For buying a new teddy\",\"For playing with the teddy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The note thanked them for keeping the teddy safe.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the story teach about kindness?\",\"options\":[\"It is not important\",\"It is only for adults\",\"It helps others\",\"It is the same as sharing\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The story shows that being kind helps others.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16663,19,4,'English','en','2.5 From the Sugarcane to Sweet Gold','[\"- Sugarcane is a tall plant grown in fields.\",\"- Farmers cut sugarcane when it is ready for harvest.\",\"- The cut cane is taken to a jaggery‑making place called Gurhal.\",\"- In Gurhal a big machine crushes the cane to get sweet juice.\",\"- The juice is poured into a big iron pan and heated over fire.\",\"- While heating, the juice thickens and turns brown, becoming jaggery.\",\"- Workers stir the juice to help it cook evenly.\",\"- The thickened jaggery is poured into small moulds to set.\",\"- After cooling, jaggery blocks are ready for use.\",\"- Jaggery is a natural sweetener used in many Indian dishes.\",\"- The process shows how a plant becomes a sweet food.\",\"- The story of Rajveer shows how children learn by watching.\",\"- Jaggery is famous in Maharashtra and is used in tea and sweets.\",\"- The process involves crushing, heating, stirring, and moulding.\",\"- Understanding the steps helps students see science in everyday life.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the first step after sugarcane is ready for harvest?\",\"options\":[\"Cutting the cane\",\"Crushing the cane\",\"Heating the juice\",\"Poured into moulds\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Farmers cut the cane when it is ready.\"},{\"q\":\"Where is the jaggery‑making place called?\",\"options\":[\"Gurhal\",\"Bakery\",\"Dairy\",\"Factory\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The place is called Gurhal.\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the juice when it is heated?\",\"options\":[\"It evaporates\",\"It thickens and turns brown\",\"It becomes cold\",\"It turns into water\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Heating makes the juice thick and brown.\"},{\"q\":\"What is poured into moulds after the juice thickens?\",\"options\":[\"Water\",\"Sugarcane stalks\",\"Jaggery\",\"Milk\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The thickened juice becomes jaggery and is poured into moulds.\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal is mentioned as helping to carry sugarcane?\",\"options\":[\"Horse\",\"Bullock\",\"Dog\",\"Cat\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Bullock-cart is used to carry cane.\"},{\"q\":\"What does Rajveer call the jaggery?\",\"options\":[\"Candy\",\"Magic\",\"Sweetness\",\"Gold\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"He says it is a magic.\"},{\"q\":\"Who uses jaggery in tea?\",\"options\":[\"Rajveer\",\"His grandmother\",\"His father\",\"His uncle\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"His grandmother uses jaggery in tea.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT part of the jaggery process?\",\"options\":[\"Crushing\",\"Stirring\",\"Boiling water\",\"Moulding\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Boiling water is not mentioned.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main ingredient of jaggery?\",\"options\":[\"Sugarcane juice\",\"Milk\",\"Flour\",\"Rice\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Jaggery comes from sugarcane juice.\"},{\"q\":\"Why does the teacher suggest visiting a Gurhal?\",\"options\":[\"To see jaggery making\",\"To buy jaggery\",\"To learn cooking\",\"To play games\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"To see how jaggery is made.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16664,19,4,'English','en','2.6 We Say, Thank You','[\"• ‘Thank you’ is said when someone gives or helps you.\",\"• ‘Please’ is used when you want something politely.\",\"• ‘Excuse me’ is said before you interrupt or when you sneeze.\",\"• ‘Sorry’ is said when you hurt someone or make a mistake.\",\"• Saying these words shows good manners and kindness.\",\"• We use ‘Thank you’ after receiving help or a gift.\",\"• We use ‘Please’ before asking for something.\",\"• ‘Excuse me’ can mean ‘Sorry’ or ‘Pardon me’ when we bump into someone.\",\"• ‘Sorry’ is used when we do something wrong.\",\"• Good manners make friends and keep peace.\",\"• When you help a friend tie shoelaces, you show kindness.\",\"• A small help can make someone’s day better.\",\"• Listening kindly and speaking politely keeps relationships strong.\",\"• Polite words are called ‘magic words’ because they make people happy.\",\"• We can pair a word with a picture to remember its meaning.\",\"• We can create short poems or posters to practice polite words.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which word is used when you want something politely?\",\"options\":[\"Thank you\",\"Please\",\"Sorry\",\"Excuse me\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Please is used before asking for something.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you say when you sneeze?\",\"options\":[\"Thank you\",\"Please\",\"Excuse me\",\"Sorry\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Excuse me is used before or after a sneeze.\"},{\"q\":\"If you accidentally bump into someone, what do you say?\",\"options\":[\"Thank you\",\"Sorry\",\"Please\",\"Excuse me\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Sorry is used when you hurt someone.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is a synonym for ‘kind’?\",\"options\":[\"Rude\",\"Effort\",\"Helpful\",\"Sadness\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Helpful is a synonym for kind.\"},{\"q\":\"What do you do when you see a friend struggling to tie shoelaces?\",\"options\":[\"Ignore them\",\"Tell them to wait\",\"Help them\",\"Ask them to leave\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Helping shows kindness.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means ‘to give a small gift’?\",\"options\":[\"Thank you\",\"Please\",\"Sorry\",\"Excuse me\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Thank you is said after receiving a gift.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the opposite of ‘big’?\",\"options\":[\"Tiny\",\"Small\",\"Little\",\"None of the above\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Small is the opposite of big.\"},{\"q\":\"When you want to borrow a toy, which phrase do you use?\",\"options\":[\"May I go out?\",\"May I help you?\",\"May I borrow your toy?\",\"May I drink water?\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The phrase asks for borrowing a toy.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means ‘to make someone happy’?\",\"options\":[\"Happiness\",\"Sadness\",\"Effort\",\"Rude\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Happiness is the feeling of being happy.\"},{\"q\":\"If you forget to bring a book to class, what should you do?\",\"options\":[\"Tell the teacher you forgot\",\"Ask a friend for the book\",\"Ignore the situation\",\"None of the above\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Asking a friend for the book is polite.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16665,19,4,'English','en','2.7 The Giant Panda','[\"The giant panda is a very rare animal found only in the mountains of Western China and Tibet.\",\"It lives in bamboo forests at high altitudes.\",\"Its favourite food is bamboo – about 99 % of its diet.\",\"A panda can eat 12–38 kilograms of bamboo each day.\",\"Pandas have strong jaws and teeth to crush bamboo stalks.\",\"Adult pandas weigh 70–100 kilograms, sometimes more.\",\"A baby panda is called a cub and weighs about 100 grams at birth.\",\"Pandas are slow‑moving, peaceful and friendly animals.\",\"They are a symbol of peace and friendship in China.\",\"Pandas spend most of their day eating and resting.\",\"Only a few pandas remain in the world, so we must protect forests for them and other animals.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where do giant pandas live?\",\"options\":[\"In deserts\",\"In bamboo forests\",\"In oceans\",\"In cities\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"They live in bamboo forests in the mountains.\"},{\"q\":\"What makes up 99% of a panda’s diet?\",\"options\":[\"Leaves\",\"Bamboo\",\"Fish\",\"Insects\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Bamboo is the main food of pandas.\"},{\"q\":\"How much bamboo can a panda eat in one day?\",\"options\":[\"5–10 kg\",\"12–38 kg\",\"40–50 kg\",\"60–70 kg\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The range given is 12–38 kilograms.\"},{\"q\":\"What is a baby panda called?\",\"options\":[\"Cub\",\"Pup\",\"Kitten\",\"Calf\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A baby panda is called a cub.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following best describes pandas?\",\"options\":[\"Fast and aggressive\",\"Slow and peaceful\",\"Nocturnal and shy\",\"Aquatic and social\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Pandas are slow‑moving and peaceful.\"},{\"q\":\"Pandas are symbols of what?\",\"options\":[\"Power and strength\",\"Peace and friendship\",\"Speed and agility\",\"Wealth and luck\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"They symbolize peace and friendship.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the typical adult weight of a panda?\",\"options\":[\"30–50 kg\",\"70–100 kg\",\"120–150 kg\",\"200–250 kg\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Adults usually weigh 70–100 kg.\"},{\"q\":\"Pandas spend most of their day doing which two activities?\",\"options\":[\"Running and hunting\",\"Eating and resting\",\"Swimming and playing\",\"Sleeping and singing\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"They mainly eat and rest.\"},{\"q\":\"Which mountain ranges are home to pandas?\",\"options\":[\"Himalayas and Alps\",\"Rockies and Andes\",\"Western China and Tibet\",\"Sahara and Gobi\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Pandas are found in Western China and Tibet.\"},{\"q\":\"Why should we protect forests for pandas?\",\"options\":[\"To build houses\",\"To keep them safe\",\"To mine resources\",\"To grow crops\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Protecting forests helps pandas and other animals survive.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16666,19,4,'English','en','2.8 True Friends','[\"True friends are people who help each other without asking for anything in return.\",\"A best friend is someone you trust, share secrets with, and spend time together.\",\"Honesty means telling the truth and being fair to others.\",\"Friendship is shown by sharing, caring, and being honest.\",\"In the story, Gopi and Krishna were good friends and neighbours.\",\"Krishna’s crops were ruined by heavy rains, showing how nature can hurt farmers.\",\"Gopi lent land to Krishna so he could grow crops, showing kindness.\",\"Krishna found a golden statue while tilling the land.\",\"The king listened to the friends and decided to buy the statue.\",\"Tenali Raman suggested using the money to help poor farmers.\",\"A monument can remember a good friendship for everyone.\",\"The moral of the story is that honesty and friendship are very important.\",\"When friends face problems, they should help each other and be honest.\",\"A good friend is always ready to share his land, time, or money if needed.\",\"True friends respect each other’s property and do not keep it for themselves.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What did Gopi and Krishna do for each other in the story?\",\"options\":[\"They were enemies\",\"They were friends and neighbours\",\"They were rivals\",\"They were strangers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The story says Gopi and Krishna were friends as well as neighbours.\"},{\"q\":\"Why did Krishna’s crops get ruined?\",\"options\":[\"Heavy rains\",\"Drought\",\"Pest attack\",\"Fertilizer misuse\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text mentions Krishna’s crops were ruined by heavy rains.\"},{\"q\":\"What did Krishna find in the field?\",\"options\":[\"A silver coin\",\"A golden statue\",\"A wooden chest\",\"A silver statue\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Krishna found a precious golden statue.\"},{\"q\":\"Who suggested buying the statue at a fair price?\",\"options\":[\"Krishna\",\"Gopi\",\"Raja Krishnadevaraya\",\"Tenali Raman\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Tenali Raman suggested buying it at a worthy price.\"},{\"q\":\"What did the king decide to do with the money from the statue?\",\"options\":[\"Keep it for himself\",\"Donate to a temple\",\"Use it to help peasants\",\"Send it to the king’s treasury\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The king used the money to help peasants like Krishna.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the moral of the story?\",\"options\":[\"Honesty and friendship\",\"Hard work pays off\",\"We should avoid gold\",\"We should ignore problems\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The story teaches about honesty and friendship.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is NOT true about the story?\",\"options\":[\"Gopi kept the statue for himself\",\"Krishna wanted to give the statue to Gopi\",\"The king ignored the farmers\' problem\",\"Tenali Raman gave a wise suggestion\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Gopi did not keep the statue; he offered it to the king.\"},{\"q\":\"What did Tenali Raman propose to do with the statue?\",\"options\":[\"Throw it away\",\"Give it back to Gopi\",\"Buy it at a fair price\",\"Hide it in the palace\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Tenali Raman suggested buying it at a fair price.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes the relationship between Gopi and Krishna?\",\"options\":[\"Enemies\",\"Neighbors\",\"Friends\",\"Rivals\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"They were friends as well as neighbours.\"},{\"q\":\"What did the king do with the statue after buying it?\",\"options\":[\"He kept it in his palace\",\"He erected a pillar in its honor\",\"He sold it to a foreign king\",\"He buried it in the ground\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The king erected a pillar as a timeless monument for their friendship.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16667,19,4,'English','en','2.9 Eat Healthy, Stay Better !','[\"- Eating healthy food keeps the body strong and happy.\",\"- Fruits and vegetables are full of vitamins that help you grow and stay fit.\",\"- Milk is good for bones and teeth and gives energy for play.\",\"- Eating too many sweets can upset the stomach and make you feel tired.\",\"- Water is essential; drink enough every day to stay active.\",\"- Resting well helps the body recover and keeps the mind sharp.\",\"- Healthy foods include carrots, tomatoes, apples, bananas, sprouts, lentils, rice, roti, eggs, fish, and milk.\",\"- A balanced meal should have at least two servings of grains and vegetables.\",\"- Avoid eating too many chocolates or sugary snacks.\",\"- If you feel a tummyache, ask a parent or a doctor for help.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What can happen if you eat too many sweets?\",\"options\":[\"You feel energetic\",\"You get a tummyache\",\"You grow taller\",\"You sleep less\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Too many sweets upset the stomach and cause a tummyache.\"},{\"q\":\"Which food is mentioned as being rich with vitamins?\",\"options\":[\"Carrot\",\"Tomato\",\"Chocolate\",\"Milk\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says tomato is rich with vitamins.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do if you have a stomachache?\",\"options\":[\"Eat more sweets\",\"Take a nap\",\"Ask a doctor\",\"Drink coffee\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The doctor is the right person to consult.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT a healthy food mentioned?\",\"options\":[\"Egg\",\"Fish\",\"Chocolate\",\"Milk\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Chocolate is not listed as healthy in the chart.\"},{\"q\":\"How many times a day should you eat grains like rice or roti?\",\"options\":[\"Once\",\"Twice\",\"Three times\",\"Four times\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The chart says at least twice a day.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the benefit of drinking milk before work or play?\",\"options\":[\"Makes you sleepy\",\"Makes you run better\",\"Makes you hungry\",\"Makes you sad\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says milk helps you run better.\"},{\"q\":\"Which food is described as \\\"long, yellow and soft\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"Carrot\",\"Banana\",\"Apple\",\"Orange\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Carrot fits that description.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do to stay active?\",\"options\":[\"Eat more chocolate\",\"Skip water\",\"Rest enough\",\"Skip breakfast\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Resting enough keeps the body active.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a fruit that is red and juicy?\",\"options\":[\"Orange\",\"Apple\",\"Banana\",\"Carrot\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Apple is red and juicy.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main message of the chapter?\",\"options\":[\"Eat more sweets\",\"Drink less water\",\"Eat healthy and stay better\",\"Skip meals\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The chapter encourages eating healthy foods.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16668,19,4,'English','en','2.10 My Word Family','[\"- A word family is a group of words that share the same root or base word.\",\"- Words in a word family can be nouns, verbs, adjectives, etc.\",\"- Example: the root word \\\"giant\\\" can lead to \\\"giant\\\" (noun), \\\"gigantic\\\" (adj).\",\"- Some words in the list are action words (verbs) like chase, stretch, melt, deliver, hug, pour, sew, crush.\",\"- Some words describe nature: sugarcane, ginger, jaggery, mountain.\",\"- One-syllable words are short and easy to remember: chase, stretch, melt, hug, pour, sew, crush, giant, rare, jaw, peace, symbol, capital, pride, brave, celebrate, vitamin.\",\"- Opposites help you understand meaning: brave ↔ fearful, giant ↔ tiny, rare ↔ common, peace ↔ war, excite ↔ calm.\",\"- Practice by making lists, finding odd ones out, and circling one-syllable words.\",\"- Remember: a word family helps you learn many words from one root.\",\"- Use the word family to improve reading, writing, and speaking skills.\",\"- Keep a notebook of new word families and review them regularly.\",\"- Try to use new words in sentences to remember them better.\",\"- The word \\\"sugarcane\\\" is a plant, \\\"ginger\\\" is a spice, \\\"jaggery\\\" is a sweetener.\",\"- \\\"Mould\\\" and \\\"mold\\\" are the same word spelled differently in UK and US.\",\"- \\\"Specimen\\\" is a sample, \\\"extinct\\\" means no longer existing.\",\"- \\\"Capital\\\" can mean a city or money, but here it means city.\",\"- \\\"Symbol\\\" represents an idea, like a peace sign.\",\"- \\\"Vitamin\\\" is a nutrient that keeps you healthy.\",\"- \\\"Celebrate\\\" means to honor or enjoy a special day.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which word is NOT an action word?\",\"options\":[\"chase\",\"stretch\",\"melt\",\"giant\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Giant is a noun, not an action.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the opposite of \\\"rare\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"common\",\"unique\",\"scarce\",\"unusual\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Common means many, opposite of rare.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means \\\"very big\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"giant\",\"tiny\",\"small\",\"little\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Giant means very big.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is a plant?\",\"options\":[\"ginger\",\"sugarcane\",\"jaggery\",\"crush\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Sugarcane is a plant.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is a spice?\",\"options\":[\"ginger\",\"sugarcane\",\"jaggery\",\"crush\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Ginger is a spice.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means \\\"to move quickly\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"chase\",\"stretch\",\"melt\",\"deliver\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Chase means to run after.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is a sweetener?\",\"options\":[\"ginger\",\"sugarcane\",\"jaggery\",\"crush\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Jaggery is a sweetener.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is a mountain?\",\"options\":[\"giant\",\"mountain\",\"rare\",\"peace\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Mountain is a large hill.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means \\\"to make a shape\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"sew\",\"crush\",\"pour\",\"stretch\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Sew means to stitch or make a shape.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means \\\"to make a liquid spread\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"pour\",\"stretch\",\"melt\",\"hug\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Pour means to let liquid flow.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16669,19,4,'English','en','3.1 Wheat Jowar and Bajra Grow','[\"Wheat, jowar and bajra are crops grown on farms.\",\"Seeds are sown in long, narrow rows.\",\"Farmers water the seeds and pull out weeds.\",\"They protect the crops from birds by standing all day.\",\"When the crops are ready, the farmer cuts them and blows a horn.\",\"The poem describes the whole process of growing these crops.\",\"Chapati is made from wheat flour, while jowar roti is made from jowar flour.\",\"Both roti types are cooked on a hot griddle.\",\"Farmers use simple tools like a foot stamp and a hand clap to show their work.\",\"The poem mentions the farmer’s pride in his land.\",\"Harvest time is a festive occasion for many people.\",\"Farming involves planting, watering, weeding, protecting, and harvesting.\",\"The farmer’s work is celebrated in songs and poems.\",\"Learning about farming helps us understand food production.\",\"Being a farmer requires hard work, patience, and care for the land.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is the first step a farmer takes when growing wheat, jowar, or bajra?\",\"options\":[\"Planting the seeds\",\"Harvesting the crops\",\"Weeding the field\",\"Cutting the corn\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The farmer first sows the seeds.\"},{\"q\":\"Which tool does the farmer use to show his work in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"A hammer\",\"A foot stamp\",\"A watering can\",\"A scarecrow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions the farmer stamping his foot.\"},{\"q\":\"What happens when the crops are ready?\",\"options\":[\"The farmer waters them\",\"The farmer pulls out weeds\",\"The farmer cuts the corn and blows a horn\",\"The farmer sings a song\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem says the farmer cuts the corn and blows a horn.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is NOT mentioned in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"The farmer protects crops from birds\",\"The farmer pulls out weeds\",\"The farmer uses a tractor\",\"The farmer stamps his foot\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A tractor is not mentioned.\"},{\"q\":\"What is a common use of wheat?\",\"options\":[\"Making jowar roti\",\"Making chapati\",\"Making rice\",\"Making sugar\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Wheat is used to make chapati.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the farmer do to scare birds away?\",\"options\":[\"He sings loudly\",\"He uses a horn\",\"He stands all day\",\"He throws stones\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The farmer stands all day to scare birds.\"},{\"q\":\"Which festival is mentioned as a time of merrymaking in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Diwali\",\"Holi\",\"Harvest festival\",\"Christmas\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem refers to merrymaking during harvest.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of pulling out weeds?\",\"options\":[\"To make the field look tidy\",\"To give the crops more sunlight\",\"To keep the farmer busy\",\"To collect seeds\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Weeds compete with crops for light.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main ingredient in jowar roti?\",\"options\":[\"Wheat flour\",\"Rice flour\",\"Jowar flour\",\"Corn flour\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Jowar roti is made from jowar flour.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a task farmers do during harvest?\",\"options\":[\"Planting seeds\",\"Weeding\",\"Cutting the corn\",\"Watering the fields\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Cutting the corn happens during harvest.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16670,19,4,'English','en','3.2 Our Flying Friends','[\"- Birds have three kinds of feathers: down (warmth), body (cover), flight (help flying).\",\"- All birds are warm‑blooded and have two feet.\",\"- Birds have wings; most can fly, but penguins and ostriches cannot.\",\"- A bird’s body is light and shaped like an aeroplane, with strong muscles and light bones.\",\"- Beaks are used to cut, open, tear, and crush food; they have no teeth.\",\"- Birds have three toes forward and one toe backward, used for walking, holding, balancing, climbing, swimming, and wading.\",\"- Birds build nests in trees, walls, or on the ground; the female sits on eggs to keep them warm.\",\"- After hatching, baby birds are blind and featherless; parents feed and care for them.\",\"- Migration is the yearly journey to warmer places to find food and then return to build nests.\",\"- Penguins live in cold places, swim well, and walk\\/slide on ice.\",\"- Ostriches live in hot places, are the heaviest and largest birds, and run fast on land.\",\"- Claws are used for different purposes: ducks swim, eagles catch prey, cranes walk in water, hens scratch ground, woodpeckers climb trees.\",\"- An Arctic Tern can travel about 35,000 km in a year, almost around the Earth.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which bird cannot fly?\",\"options\":[\"Crow\",\"Sparrow\",\"Penguin\",\"Ostrich\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Penguins are flightless birds.\"},{\"q\":\"Penguins live in ______.\",\"options\":[\"hot places\",\"dry places\",\"cold places\",\"tropical places\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Penguins live in cold regions like Antarctica.\"},{\"q\":\"Beaks help birds to ______.\",\"options\":[\"chew food\",\"tear or crush food\",\"talk\",\"fly\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Beaks are used for cutting, tearing or crushing food.\"},{\"q\":\"Birds have ______ bones.\",\"options\":[\"heavy\",\"light\",\"solid\",\"dense\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Birds have lightweight bones to aid flight.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a flight feather?\",\"options\":[\"Down feather\",\"Body feather\",\"Flight feather\",\"Featherless\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Flight feathers are specialized for flying.\"},{\"q\":\"What keeps a bird warm?\",\"options\":[\"Down feathers\",\"Flight feathers\",\"Body feathers\",\"Wings\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Down feathers provide insulation.\"},{\"q\":\"Which bird is the heaviest and largest?\",\"options\":[\"Penguin\",\"Ostrich\",\"Eagle\",\"Swan\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The ostrich is the largest bird.\"},{\"q\":\"Which bird is known for swimming?\",\"options\":[\"Penguin\",\"Ostrich\",\"Eagle\",\"Swan\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Penguins are excellent swimmers.\"},{\"q\":\"Birds have how many toes in front?\",\"options\":[\"Two\",\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Most birds have three toes forward and one back.\"},{\"q\":\"Which bird is the fastest running bird on land?\",\"options\":[\"Penguin\",\"Ostrich\",\"Eagle\",\"Swan\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The ostrich runs fastest among birds.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16671,19,4,'English','en','3.3 I am Indian First','[\"- India is a country in South Asia.\",\"- It is called the land of sages and has a rich culture.\",\"- The poem talks about snowy peaks and the sea at its feet.\",\"- India invented the number zero, a very important idea.\",\"- Soldiers protect the country and are called heroes.\",\"- The poem celebrates being Indian first, not Hindu or Muslim.\",\"- Republic Day is celebrated on 26th January to honor the Constitution.\",\"- Students can make posters and poems about India.\",\"- Maps help us see where each state is located.\",\"- The word ‘crowned’ means having a crown or being the best.\",\"- ‘Prostrate’ means lying down or showing respect.\",\"- ‘Heights’ refers to high places like mountains.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What does the poem say about India’s culture?\",\"options\":[\"It is modern and new\",\"It is rich and old\",\"It is only about food\",\"It is about sports\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions a land of sages and a culture rich from ages.\"},{\"q\":\"Which mountain range is described as snowy?\",\"options\":[\"Himalayas\",\"Andes\",\"Rockies\",\"Alps\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Snowy peaks are part of the Himalayas in India.\"},{\"q\":\"Who protects India according to the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Teachers\",\"Soldiers\",\"Farmers\",\"Artists\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem says soldiers are heroes.\"},{\"q\":\"What important number did India invent?\",\"options\":[\"One\",\"Zero\",\"Ten\",\"Five\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions India knows the value of Zero.\"},{\"q\":\"What day is celebrated to honor the Constitution?\",\"options\":[\"Independence Day\",\"Republic Day\",\"Victory Day\",\"New Year\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Republic Day is on 26th January.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT mentioned in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Sages\",\"Soldiers\",\"Mountains\",\"Space\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Space is not mentioned.\"},{\"q\":\"The poem says India is first to what?\",\"options\":[\"Be rich\",\"Be Indian\",\"Be Hindu\",\"Be Muslim\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"It says \'I am Indian first\'.\"},{\"q\":\"What should students create for Republic Day?\",\"options\":[\"A song\",\"A poster\",\"A dance\",\"A story\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The activity asks to create a poster.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means having a crown?\",\"options\":[\"Crowned\",\"Prostrate\",\"Snowy\",\"Heights\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Crowned means having a crown.\"},{\"q\":\"What does \'prostrate\' mean?\",\"options\":[\"Standing tall\",\"Lying down\",\"Flying\",\"Singing\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Prostrate means lying down or showing respect.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16672,19,4,'English','en','3.4 The Smart Traveller','[\"- The story is about a smart traveller named Ramdas and a thief named Hari.\",\"- Ramdas is a merchant who travels to Royal Parks.\",\"- Hari joins him on the journey and pretends to be a merchant.\",\"- While Ramdas sleeps at an inn, Hari searches for money but finds none.\",\"- Ramdas hides his money in Hari’s own bag for safekeeping.\",\"- Hari discovers the trick and admits he was outsmarted.\",\"- Key words: traveller, merchant, inn, belongings, profession, identity, outsmarted.\",\"- Important ideas: honesty, cleverness, safety of money, travel etiquette.\",\"- Remember: a traveller should keep money in a safe place, like a bag that is hard to find.\",\"- The story shows that being clever can protect you from thieves.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Who is the main traveller in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Ramdas\",\"Hari\",\"A merchant\",\"A thief\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Ramdas is the traveller and merchant.\"},{\"q\":\"Where was Ramdas travelling to?\",\"options\":[\"Royal Parks\",\"Mumbai\",\"Delhi\",\"Chennai\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says he was on a journey to Royal Parks.\"},{\"q\":\"What did Hari do while Ramdas slept?\",\"options\":[\"He slept too\",\"He searched for money\",\"He ate food\",\"He left the inn\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Hari searched Ramdas’s belongings for money.\"},{\"q\":\"Why was Hari disappointed?\",\"options\":[\"He lost his bag\",\"He found no money\",\"He was hungry\",\"He was tired\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"He found no money in the belongings.\"},{\"q\":\"Where did Ramdas hide his money?\",\"options\":[\"In a chest\",\"In a safe\",\"In Hari’s bag\",\"In a tree\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"He hid it in Hari’s own bag.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes Ramdas?\",\"options\":[\"Smart\",\"Strong\",\"Fast\",\"Tall\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Ramdas is described as smart.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main lesson of the story?\",\"options\":[\"Travel is fun\",\"Keep money safe\",\"Be honest\",\"Be hungry\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The story teaches to keep money in a safe place.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a person who travels for business?\",\"options\":[\"Traveller\",\"Merchant\",\"Businessman\",\"Thief\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A businessman travels for business.\"},{\"q\":\"What did Hari reveal about himself?\",\"options\":[\"He is a merchant\",\"He is a thief\",\"He is a teacher\",\"He is a student\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Hari admitted he was a thief.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means to beat someone at something?\",\"options\":[\"Outsmarted\",\"Lost\",\"Found\",\"Hidden\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Outsmarted means to beat someone at something.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16673,19,4,'English','en','3.5 Yoga','[\"Yoga is a set of exercises that keeps the body fit and the mind calm.\",\"Doing yoga every day helps you stay active and happy.\",\"Yoga helps you develop healthy habits like regular breathing and stretching.\",\"It improves flexibility, balance and concentration.\",\"Yoga can be practiced at home or in school after playtime.\",\"You can make a chart of healthy habits and paste it at home to remember them.\",\"Yoga is good for all ages and can be done in a quiet space.\",\"It encourages a calm and peaceful mind.\",\"Doing yoga regularly can help you sleep better and feel energetic.\",\"Yoga is a simple way to stay healthy and happy every day.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What does daily yoga help you keep?\",\"options\":[\"Your hair\",\"Your body fit and mind calm\",\"Your toys\",\"Your homework\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Daily yoga keeps the body fit and the mind calm.\"},{\"q\":\"Who said that play time is required at school?\",\"options\":[\"Sunny\",\"Papa\",\"Teacher\",\"Friend\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Papa said play time is required at school.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do after play time at school?\",\"options\":[\"Go home\",\"Do yoga\",\"Eat lunch\",\"Read a book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"After playtime, you should do yoga.\"},{\"q\":\"What can you make to remember healthy habits?\",\"options\":[\"A poem\",\"A chart\",\"A song\",\"A picture\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"You can make a chart of healthy habits.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main benefit of yoga mentioned in the conversation?\",\"options\":[\"It makes you taller\",\"It keeps the body fit and mind calm\",\"It gives you more friends\",\"It helps you learn maths\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Yoga keeps the body fit and mind calm.\"},{\"q\":\"Who says, \\\"I will do yoga every day\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"Sunny\",\"Papa\",\"Teacher\",\"Friend\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Sunny says he will do yoga every day.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do after listening to the teacher?\",\"options\":[\"Sleep\",\"Play\",\"Enact\",\"Read\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The teacher says to listen, repeat and enact.\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity is suggested for the teacher?\",\"options\":[\"Write sentences on given topics\",\"Sing a song\",\"Draw a picture\",\"Play a game\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The teacher is encouraged to write sentences on given topics.\"},{\"q\":\"What can you collect to label?\",\"options\":[\"Pictures of Yogasana\",\"Pictures of animals\",\"Pictures of cars\",\"Pictures of books\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Collect pictures of Yogasana and label them.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you prepare for Yoga Day?\",\"options\":[\"Invitation card\",\"Birthday card\",\"Thank you card\",\"Shopping list\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Prepare an invitation card for ‘Yoga Day.’\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16674,19,4,'English','en','3.6 Let’s Fly in an Aeroplane','[\"Let’s Fly in an Aeroplane is about a trip from Mumbai to Goa by plane.\",\"The story starts at the airport where we check in, show tickets and ID, and get boarding passes.\",\"At the security check, bags go on a conveyor belt and pass through a machine that makes a whir‑whir sound.\",\"We walk through a gate that beeps and then wait at the gate for our turn to board.\",\"The flight number 302 to Goa is announced and we board through a long tunnel called the aerobridge.\",\"The air hostess greets us at the door and we find our seats and fasten seat belts with a click sound.\",\"The plane starts to move slowly, then faster, and the wings stretch wide while the engines roar and the plane takes off.\",\"During flight we see tiny houses, moving cars, twisting roads, fluffy clouds, green trees and an endless blue sky.\",\"The pilot speaks from the speaker, saying the weather is clear and sunny and that we are flying high above the clouds.\",\"When we reach Goa the pilot announces we are ready to land, the plane slows down, touches the ground and we land safely.\",\"The whole experience is full of sounds like whir‑whir, beep‑beep, vroom‑vroom, whoosh, and sights like cotton candy clouds and a green carpet of trees.\",\"The story teaches us about airport procedures, safety, and what we can see from a plane’s window.\",\"It also includes activities such as matching dialogues, arranging events in order, and making a paper aeroplane.\",\"The chapter encourages listening, repeating, and describing what we see and feel.\",\"It introduces simple transitional words like “first”, “then”, “after that”, “finally”.\",\"It helps students practice vocabulary related to travel, such as aeroplane, airport, ticket, boarding, seat belt, engine, pilot, passengers, and flight.\",\"The exercises involve fill‑in‑the‑blank, matching, true\\/false, and descriptive questions.\",\"Students can also create new words from given letters and match sound words to actions.\",\"The chapter ends with a hands‑on activity to fold a paper aeroplane.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What do we show to the officer at the check‑in counter?\",\"options\":[\"Passport\",\"Tickets and ID cards\",\"Baggage\",\"Food\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The officer asks for tickets and ID cards.\"},{\"q\":\"Which sound does the machine that checks our bags make?\",\"options\":[\"Beep‑beep\",\"Whir‑whir\",\"Vroom‑vroom\",\"Whoosh\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The conveyor belt machine makes a whir‑whir sound.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the name of the long tunnel we walk through to board the plane?\",\"options\":[\"Aero‑bridge\",\"Airport\",\"Check‑in\",\"Security\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"It is called the aerobridge.\"},{\"q\":\"What do we fasten before the plane takes off?\",\"options\":[\"Seat belt\",\"Seat cushion\",\"Window\",\"Baggage\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"We fasten the seat belt.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT seen from the window?\",\"options\":[\"Tiny houses\",\"Moving cars\",\"Ribbons of roads\",\"Mountains\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Mountains are not mentioned.\"},{\"q\":\"Which sound is made when the plane lands?\",\"options\":[\"Vroom‑vroom\",\"Whir‑whir\",\"Thud\",\"Whoosh\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The landing makes a thud sound.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the pilot say about the weather?\",\"options\":[\"Rainy\",\"Cloudy\",\"Clear and sunny\",\"Windy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The pilot says the weather is clear and sunny.\"},{\"q\":\"What activity is included at the end of the chapter?\",\"options\":[\"Drawing a picture\",\"Making a paper aeroplane\",\"Reading a story\",\"Listening to music\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Students fold a paper aeroplane.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes the clouds?\",\"options\":[\"Hard\",\"Fluffy\",\"Sharp\",\"Cold\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The clouds are described as fluffy.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of the aerobridge?\",\"options\":[\"To carry luggage\",\"To connect the gate and the plane\",\"To check passengers\",\"To serve food\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The aerobridge connects the gate to the plane.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16675,19,4,'English','en','3.7 The Warli Art and Culture','[\"Warli people live in Maharashtra, near green forests and hills of Palghar and Thane.\",\"They are one of the oldest tribes in India.\",\"They live in small mud houses with thatched roofs.\",\"They decorate their houses with beautiful white Warli art.\",\"Warli painting is a special kind of art made by the Warli people.\",\"It is done on mud walls using white paint made from rice flour paste.\",\"They use simple shapes like circles, triangles, and squares in their paintings.\",\"Shapes represent people, animals, trees, huts and the sun.\",\"Warli paintings tell stories about farming, hunting, dancing, fishing and celebrations.\",\"Every picture shows how they love and respect nature.\",\"Tarpa dance is a famous Warli dance where men and women hold hands and move in a circle.\",\"A Tarpa is a musical instrument made from bamboo and a dried gourd.\",\"Warli art is not just decoration; it is a way to share life, joy and love for nature.\",\"The art helps the Warli people express their daily life and feelings.\",\"Warli artists use bright white paint on dark mud walls.\",\"They often paint scenes of their village life and nature.\",\"The art style is simple but powerful and symbolic.\",\"Warli art has gained national and international recognition.\",\"Warli people value community, nature and harmony.\",\"They celebrate festivals with dances and music.\",\"Their art is passed down from generation to generation.\",\"Warli culture is an important part of Maharashtra’s heritage.\",\"Warli art is a living tradition that continues to thrive today.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where do the Warli people live?\",\"options\":[\"In the deserts of Rajasthan\",\"In the green forests of Palghar and Thane\",\"In the mountains of Himachal Pradesh\",\"In the plains of Punjab\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The Warli people live in Maharashtra, near the green forests and hills of Palghar and Thane.\"},{\"q\":\"What material is used to make the white paint for Warli paintings?\",\"options\":[\"Oil and charcoal\",\"Rice flour paste\",\"Cement and water\",\"Grape juice\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"White paint is made from rice flour paste.\"},{\"q\":\"Which shapes are commonly used in Warli art?\",\"options\":[\"Circles, triangles, squares\",\"Stars, moons, spirals\",\"Ovals, rectangles, diamonds\",\"Hexagons, pentagons, octagons\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Simple shapes like circles, triangles, and squares are used.\"},{\"q\":\"What does a Warli painting usually depict?\",\"options\":[\"Modern city life\",\"Space exploration\",\"People, animals, trees, huts and the sun\",\"Underwater scenes\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"They depict people, animals, trees, huts and the sun.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the Tarpa dance?\",\"options\":[\"A dance where people jump on rooftops\",\"A dance where men and women hold hands and move in a circle\",\"A dance performed only by men\",\"A dance that uses fire sticks\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Tarpa dance involves men and women holding hands and moving in a circle.\"},{\"q\":\"What is a Tarpa?\",\"options\":[\"A type of drum\",\"A musical instrument made from bamboo and a dried gourd\",\"A wooden flute\",\"A stringed instrument\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Tarpa is a musical instrument made from bamboo and a dried gourd.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main purpose of Warli art?\",\"options\":[\"To decorate houses only\",\"To share life, joy and love for nature\",\"To create modern abstract art\",\"To make money for the tribe\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Warli art is a way to share life, joy and love for nature.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is NOT mentioned as a subject in Warli paintings?\",\"options\":[\"Farming\",\"Fishing\",\"Space travel\",\"Hunting\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Space travel is not mentioned.\"},{\"q\":\"How do Warli people show respect for nature in their art?\",\"options\":[\"By painting only animals\",\"By painting only people\",\"By painting scenes of nature and life\",\"By painting only the sky\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Their paintings show love and respect for nature.\"},{\"q\":\"What is a common feature of Warli houses?\",\"options\":[\"Glass windows\",\"Thatched roofs\",\"Stone walls\",\"Metal roofs\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Warli houses have thatched roofs.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16676,19,4,'English','en','3.8 The Kite','[\"- A kite is a light toy that flies in the wind.\",\"- Kites are usually made of paper, cloth or plastic on a lightweight frame.\",\"- The string is tied to the kite and pulled to keep it aloft.\",\"- Kites fly because the wind pushes against their wings, giving lift.\",\"- Colours of kites are bright and many people choose their favourite colour.\",\"- In Maharashtra, people celebrate Makar Sankranti by flying kites and eating Tilgul.\",\"- To make a paper kite, you need paper, a stick, string, and glue.\",\"- The kite’s shape is like a triangle or diamond to catch the wind.\",\"- Opposites: up ↔ down, light ↔ heavy, small ↔ big, above ↔ below, wild ↔ tame, town ↔ forest.\",\"- Kites are fun because they let us see the sky from a new height.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What gives a kite lift in the wind?\",\"options\":[\"Its weight\",\"Its colour\",\"The wind pushing against its wings\",\"The string length\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The wind pushes against the kite’s wings, creating lift.\"},{\"q\":\"Which festival in Maharashtra is famous for kite flying?\",\"options\":[\"Diwali\",\"Makar Sankranti\",\"Holi\",\"Ganesh Chaturthi\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Makar Sankranti is celebrated with kite flying.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main material used for a paper kite?\",\"options\":[\"Wood\",\"Paper\",\"Plastic\",\"Metal\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Paper is the light material used for paper kites.\"},{\"q\":\"Opposite of \\\"light\\\" is:\",\"options\":[\"Heavy\",\"Fast\",\"Small\",\"Tall\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Heavy is the opposite of light.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is NOT a kite part?\",\"options\":[\"String\",\"Wings\",\"Stick\",\"Fireworks\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Fireworks are not part of a kite.\"},{\"q\":\"What do we eat during Makar Sankranti?\",\"options\":[\"Samosa\",\"Tilgul\",\"Pav Bhaji\",\"Biryani\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Tilgul is a sweet eaten during Makar Sankranti.\"},{\"q\":\"The shape of a kite that looks like a triangle is called:\",\"options\":[\"Square\",\"Rectangle\",\"Triangle\",\"Circle\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A kite often has a triangular shape.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a synonym for \\\"wild\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"Tame\",\"Calm\",\"Quiet\",\"Soft\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Wild means untamed or not domesticated.\"},{\"q\":\"The opposite of \\\"above\\\" is:\",\"options\":[\"Below\",\"Near\",\"Far\",\"Above\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Below is the opposite of above.\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the sky do kites fly in?\",\"options\":[\"Ground\",\"Sea\",\"Air\",\"Water\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Kites fly in the air.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16677,19,4,'English','en','3.9 A Windy Discovery','[\"- Windmills or wind turbines use the wind to make electricity.\",\"- When wind blows, it pushes the long blades of a windmill, making them spin.\",\"- The spinning blades turn a rod that is connected to a generator.\",\"- A generator is a machine that turns the movement of the wind wheel into electrical power.\",\"- Wind energy is renewable, meaning it never runs out and it does not produce dirty smoke like factories.\",\"- Windmills are clean, green and smart helpers for our homes.\",\"- A simple model of a windmill can be made with paper, a pin and a straw or pencil.\",\"- The model has 7 coloured sections that spin when blown or moved by wind.\",\"- The windmill’s blades are like a giant fan that turns electricity.\",\"- Wind energy is a type of renewable energy that helps keep the earth clean.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What does a windmill use to produce electricity?\",\"options\":[\"Sunlight\",\"Water\",\"Wind\",\"Heat\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Windmills use the wind to spin their blades.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the machine that turns the wind’s movement into power called?\",\"options\":[\"Motor\",\"Generator\",\"Pump\",\"Engine\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The generator converts motion into electrical power.\"},{\"q\":\"Wind energy is considered renewable because:\",\"options\":[\"It is expensive\",\"It never runs out\",\"It is made of metal\",\"It is loud\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Renewable means it can be used again and again.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is NOT a word from the lesson about wind?\",\"options\":[\"superhero\",\"factories\",\"turbines\",\"rainbow\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Rainbow is not listed in the lesson words.\"},{\"q\":\"What happens to the windmill’s blades when the wind stops?\",\"options\":[\"They keep spinning\",\"They stop spinning\",\"They turn into a fan\",\"They become a generator\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The blades stop when there is no wind.\"},{\"q\":\"The model windmill described in the chapter has how many coloured sections?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"6\",\"7\",\"8\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The model uses 7 sections like pizza slices.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of the pin in the windmill model?\",\"options\":[\"To hold the paper together\",\"To stop the wind\",\"To light a bulb\",\"To measure wind speed\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The pin holds the twisted tips at the centre.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes wind energy?\",\"options\":[\"Dirty\",\"Polluting\",\"Renewable\",\"Expensive\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Wind energy is clean and renewable.\"},{\"q\":\"What do the windmill blades do when the wind blows?\",\"options\":[\"They vibrate\",\"They spin\",\"They fall\",\"They grow\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Blades spin when pushed by wind.\"},{\"q\":\"The windmill model should be placed where?\",\"options\":[\"Inside a closed room\",\"In a windy area\",\"Under a tree\",\"In a dark room\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"It should be taken outdoors or in a windy place.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16678,19,4,'English','en','3.10 My Word Family','[\"- A word family is a group of words that share the same root or meaning.\",\"- Opposite words are called antonyms. Example: essential – unnecessary.\",\"- Hidden words are smaller words inside a longer word. Example: downtrodden contains down, odd, den.\",\"- Double letters appear when a letter is repeated, e.g., “cluck” has double ‘c’ sound but only one letter; a better example is “fluffy” with double ‘f’ sound.\",\"- Words ending with the letter ‘e’ are called e‑words. Example: essential, equality, justice.\",\"- Alphabetical order means arranging words from A to Z.\",\"- Syllables are the beats in a word. Example: hu-ma-ni-ty has three syllables.\",\"- A poem can use many words from the word family to make it interesting.\",\"- Dictionaries give the meaning of words and help you learn new ones.\",\"- Practice makes you better at spotting hidden words, antonyms, and syllables.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which of these pairs are opposite words?\",\"options\":[\"essential – unnecessary\",\"tunnel – tunnel\",\"garbage – clean\",\"citizen – citizen\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Essential means needed, its opposite is unnecessary.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word contains the hidden word ‘den’?\",\"options\":[\"downtrodden\",\"garbage\",\"humanity\",\"cluck\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"downtrodden hides the word den.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word has double letters?\",\"options\":[\"cluck\",\"equality\",\"justice\",\"garbage\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"cluck has a double ‘c’ sound (two c’s in pronunciation).\"},{\"q\":\"Which word ends with the letter ‘e’?\",\"options\":[\"justice\",\"evils\",\"cluck\",\"garbage\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"justice ends with e.\"},{\"q\":\"Arrange these words alphabetically: outward, reporter, narrow, evils, cluck.\",\"options\":[\"cluck, evils, narrow, outward, reporter\",\"cluck, evils, outward, narrow, reporter\",\"cluck, evils, reporter, narrow, outward\",\"cluck, evils, reporter, outward, narrow\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Alphabetical order from A to Z.\"},{\"q\":\"How many syllables are in the word ‘humanity’?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"3\",\"4\",\"5\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"hu-ma-ni-ty has three syllables.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is NOT a hidden word in ‘downtrodden’?\",\"options\":[\"down\",\"odd\",\"den\",\"trod\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"trod is not part of downtrodden.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is an antonym of ‘essential’?\",\"options\":[\"necessary\",\"important\",\"unnecessary\",\"critical\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Unnecessary is the opposite of essential.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is a poem word from the family?\",\"options\":[\"justice\",\"evils\",\"cluck\",\"equality\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Evils can be used in a poem about good and bad.\"},{\"q\":\"Identify the syllable count for ‘simplicity’.\",\"options\":[\"4\",\"5\",\"6\",\"7\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"sim-pli-ci-ty has four syllables.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16679,19,4,'English','en','4.1 Our Smart Village','[\"Solar energy is light from the Sun that can be used to make electricity or heat.\",\"Solar lights are small lamps that work all day and night by using solar panels.\",\"E‑library is a digital library where we can read books on a computer or phone.\",\"Maps help us find places and directions like North, South, East and West.\",\"Farmers can use phones to check weather and learn how to grow crops better.\",\"In a smart village, technology like solar power and e‑libraries make life easier.\",\"Solar panels absorb sunlight and convert it into electricity for lights and gadgets.\",\"Reading books in an e‑library is free and can be done anywhere in the village.\",\"Maps are useful for planning routes, finding schools, markets and farms.\",\"Using solar energy reduces the need for electricity from the grid.\",\"E‑libraries help children learn new words and stories without travelling.\",\"Smart villages use technology to improve health, education and farming.\",\"Solar lights keep streets bright after sunset, making it safer to walk.\",\"E‑libraries and maps are examples of digital tools that help villagers.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is solar energy?\",\"options\":[\"Energy from the Sun\",\"Energy from the moon\",\"Energy from wind\",\"Energy from water\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Solar energy comes from sunlight.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT a use of solar energy mentioned in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Lighting streets\",\"Charging phones\",\"Growing crops\",\"Powering lights\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The poem talks about lights and phones, not growing crops with solar energy.\"},{\"q\":\"Which direction is NOT mentioned in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"North\",\"East\",\"South\",\"Northeast\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The poem lists North, South, East and West.\"},{\"q\":\"True or False: Solar lights only work during the day.\",\"options\":[\"True\",\"False\",\"Maybe\",\"Not sure\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Solar lights work all day and night.\"},{\"q\":\"What is an e‑library?\",\"options\":[\"A place with solar panels\",\"A digital library\",\"A type of street light\",\"A farm tool\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"An e‑library is a digital library of books.\"},{\"q\":\"Which tool helps farmers check the weather?\",\"options\":[\"Phone\",\"Solar panel\",\"E‑library\",\"Map\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem says farmers use a phone to grow grain.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main benefit of using solar lights on streets?\",\"options\":[\"They are cheap\",\"They make streets bright after sunset\",\"They are colorful\",\"They are loud\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Solar lights keep streets bright after sunset.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a direction mentioned in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"North\",\"Southwest\",\"Northeast\",\"Northwest\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions North, South, East and West.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the poem suggest about reading maps?\",\"options\":[\"It is boring\",\"It is useful\",\"It is hard\",\"It is fun\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem says reading maps is just the best, but the extracted item says it is boring. The poem implies it is useful.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a suggested activity in the chapter?\",\"options\":[\"Drawing a picture of a village item\",\"Playing a game\",\"Reading a story\",\"Writing a poem\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The chapter asks students to draw and label a village item.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16680,19,4,'English','en','4.2 The Giant Radish','[\"- A radish is a root vegetable that grows underground.\",\"- Ramu Kaka planted radish seeds in his garden.\",\"- He dug holes, sowed seeds, covered them with soil, watered and pulled weeds.\",\"- Most radishes grew small, but one grew very big – a giant radish.\",\"- Ramu Kaka, his wife, daughter, son, dog, cat, and hen all tried to pull the giant radish.\",\"- The hen helped by scratching the soil around the radish, loosening it.\",\"- After the soil was loose, the radish came out easily.\",\"- The story shows teamwork and that even a small hen can help a big task.\",\"- Key words: radish, soil, leaves, giant, curry, pull, heave‑ho, scratch, peck, loose, easier, harder.\",\"- The story also teaches listening to sounds and matching them with actions.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What did Ramu Kaka plant in his garden?\",\"options\":[\"carrot\",\"radish\",\"potato\",\"tomato\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Ramu planted radish seeds.\"},{\"q\":\"Who finally helped pull the giant radish out?\",\"options\":[\"Ramu alone\",\"Ramu and his wife\",\"Ramu and the hen\",\"Ramu and the cat\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The hen loosened the soil, making it easy to pull.\"},{\"q\":\"What sound did the hen make while scratching the soil?\",\"options\":[\"heave‑ho\",\"scratch\",\"peck\",\"woof\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The hen scratched the soil.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best describes the radish at the end?\",\"options\":[\"small\",\"big\",\"giant\",\"tiny\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"It was a giant radish.\"},{\"q\":\"What did Ramu Kaka say to the hen?\",\"options\":[\"Thank you\",\"Good job\",\"You are small\",\"You are big\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"He thanked the hen.\"},{\"q\":\"How did the radish come out?\",\"options\":[\"By pulling hard\",\"By digging with a shovel\",\"By loosening the soil\",\"By watering it\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The soil was loosened by the hen.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main lesson of the story?\",\"options\":[\"Hard work alone is enough\",\"Teamwork helps\",\"Eating curry is good\",\"Dogs are helpful\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Everyone worked together.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT a character in the story?\",\"options\":[\"Ramu Kaka\",\"Renu\",\"Raju\",\"Sita\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Sita is not mentioned.\"},{\"q\":\"What did the hen do after scratching the soil?\",\"options\":[\"Clucked\",\"Pecked\",\"Both\",\"None\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"She scratched and pecked.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means \'very big\'?\",\"options\":[\"small\",\"short\",\"big\",\"tiny\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Big means very big.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16681,19,4,'English','en','4.3 Animal Fair','[\"- An animal fair is a place where many animals are sold.\",\"- Raju and his father went to the fair to buy animals for their farm.\",\"- They bought five cows and twenty hens.\",\"- The farm already had a horse, a bullock and two dogs.\",\"- Cows give milk, which can be used to make butter and cheese.\",\"- Hens give eggs, which can be used to make cakes and other foods.\",\"- Animals need a clean home: a shed for cows, a coop for hens, a stable for the horse, kennels for dogs.\",\"- If animals get sick, a veterinary doctor gives them medicine.\",\"- Animals make different sounds: cows moo, ducks quack, hens squawk, dogs bark, goats bleat, donkeys bray, snakes hiss.\",\"- Children should learn to care for animals and keep them healthy.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Where did Raju and his father go to buy animals?\",\"options\":[\"The zoo\",\"The market\",\"The animal fair\",\"The farm\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"They went to the animal fair.\"},{\"q\":\"How many cows did Raju buy?\",\"options\":[\"Three\",\"Four\",\"Five\",\"Six\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Raju bought five cows.\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal gives milk?\",\"options\":[\"Hens\",\"Cows\",\"Dogs\",\"Horses\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Cows give milk.\"},{\"q\":\"What sound does a duck make?\",\"options\":[\"Moo\",\"Quack\",\"Bark\",\"Squeak\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Ducks quack.\"},{\"q\":\"What is a place where hens live?\",\"options\":[\"Stable\",\"Kennel\",\"Coop\",\"Shed\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Hens live in a coop.\"},{\"q\":\"Who gives medicine to sick animals?\",\"options\":[\"Farmer\",\"Veterinary doctor\",\"Teacher\",\"Mother\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"A veterinary doctor gives medicine.\"},{\"q\":\"Which animal is a bird?\",\"options\":[\"Cow\",\"Dog\",\"Hen\",\"Bullock\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Hen is a bird.\"},{\"q\":\"What do cows give that can be made into cheese?\",\"options\":[\"Eggs\",\"Milk\",\"Butter\",\"Bread\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Milk is used to make cheese.\"},{\"q\":\"Which sound does a goat make?\",\"options\":[\"Bleat\",\"Bark\",\"Moo\",\"Quack\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Goats bleat.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main job of a veterinary doctor?\",\"options\":[\"Feed animals\",\"Build houses\",\"Give medicine\",\"Paint fences\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"They give medicine to animals.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16682,19,4,'English','en','4.4 Mindset','[\"- A mindset is a way of thinking that helps you do your best.\",\"- Saying \\\"I will try my best\\\" means you will keep working even if it is hard.\",\"- Learning from mistakes means you look at what went wrong and try to do better next time.\",\"- Giving up is not good; you should keep trying until you succeed.\",\"- Being positive means you think good thoughts and feel hopeful.\",\"- Practice makes things easier; the more you try, the better you get.\",\"- Trying different ways helps you find the best way to solve a problem.\",\"- Sharing thoughts with friends can give you new ideas.\",\"- Determination means you are firm in doing something.\",\"- Training your brain by learning new things keeps it strong.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What does it mean to learn from mistakes?\",\"options\":[\"You ignore them\",\"You copy them\",\"You try to do better next time\",\"You blame others\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Learning from mistakes means you use them to improve.\"},{\"q\":\"Which sentence shows a positive mindset?\",\"options\":[\"I will give up\",\"I will try my best\",\"I am sad\",\"I will not try\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Saying \\\"I will try my best\\\" shows positivity.\"},{\"q\":\"If you keep practicing, what happens?\",\"options\":[\"You get tired\",\"You get better\",\"You forget the task\",\"You stop learning\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Practice makes things easier and improves skill.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do if you see a friend crying?\",\"options\":[\"Ignore them\",\"Tell a teacher\",\"Ask how they feel\",\"Leave the room\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"You should ask how they feel to help.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT a part of the \\\"I can\\\" statements?\",\"options\":[\"I can learn from mistakes\",\"I can give up\",\"I can try different ways\",\"I can improve by working hard\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The statements encourage trying, not giving up.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the purpose of asking \\\"How often do you see him\\/her?\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"To find a friend\",\"To know the friend’s schedule\",\"To learn about the friend’s habits\",\"To ask about a teacher\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"It helps you learn about the friend’s habits.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word best completes \\\"I will not give ________\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"up\",\"away\",\"away\",\"up\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The phrase is \\\"I will not give up.\\\"\"},{\"q\":\"What does \\\"I will listen, speak, read and ______\\\" mean?\",\"options\":[\"write\",\"play\",\"dance\",\"sleep\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The missing word is \\\"write\\\" to complete the list of skills.\"},{\"q\":\"Which activity is suggested for a poster?\",\"options\":[\"Draw a picture\",\"Write your own ideas\",\"Read a poem\",\"Sing a song\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The text says \\\"Prepare a poster by using your own ideas.\\\"\"},{\"q\":\"Why do we ask \\\"Why do you like it?\\\" about a dish?\",\"options\":[\"To find the recipe\",\"To know the taste\",\"To understand the preference\",\"To ask for a picture\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The question seeks the reason for liking the dish.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16683,19,4,'English','en','4.5 We are One - The Rainbow Story','[\"A rainbow is a beautiful arc of colours seen after rain when sunlight passes through water droplets.\",\"The rainbow has seven colours: Red, Orange, Yellow, Green, Blue, Indigo, Violet.\",\"Red is the colour of fire and bravery.\",\"Orange is full of energy and joy.\",\"Yellow makes everyone smile and is bright like the sun.\",\"Green gives life to plants and trees.\",\"Blue is calm like the sky and deep like the sea.\",\"Indigo is magical and mysterious.\",\"Violet is royal and graceful.\",\"All colours together make a rainbow and they are all friends.\",\"White light is made of all the rainbow colours mixed together.\",\"When white light passes through a prism, it splits into the seven rainbow colours.\",\"Unity in diversity means that even though colours are different, they are all part of one whole.\",\"The story teaches that fighting is wrong and cooperation makes the world bright.\",\"The main lesson is that we should respect differences and work together.\",\"The colours in the story were fighting because each thought it was the greatest.\",\"White colour explained that they all come from white light and become white again when together.\",\"If two colours disappear, the rainbow will be incomplete and less bright.\",\"The rainbow appears in the sky after rain when sunlight shines through water droplets.\",\"The story encourages children to be kind, respectful and to celebrate differences.\",\"The rainbow is a natural phenomenon that shows the spectrum of visible light.\",\"The colours of the rainbow are always in the same order: Red, Orange, Yellow, Green, Blue, Indigo, Violet.\"]','[{\"q\":\"How many colours are there in a rainbow?\",\"options\":[\"5\",\"6\",\"7\",\"8\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"A rainbow has seven colours: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, violet.\"},{\"q\":\"Which colour is described as the colour of fire and bravery?\",\"options\":[\"Red\",\"Orange\",\"Yellow\",\"Blue\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Red is the colour of fire and bravery.\"},{\"q\":\"What happens when light passes through a prism?\",\"options\":[\"It becomes a rainbow\",\"It disappears\",\"It turns into white\",\"It turns into black\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A prism splits light into the seven rainbow colours.\"},{\"q\":\"What message does the white colour give to the other colours?\",\"options\":[\"They should fight harder\",\"They are all born from white\",\"They should stay separate\",\"They should ignore each other\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"White says all colours come from it and together they become white again.\"},{\"q\":\"Which colour is described as calm like the sky and deep like the sea?\",\"options\":[\"Blue\",\"Green\",\"Indigo\",\"Violet\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Blue is calm like the sky and deep like the sea.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main lesson of the story?\",\"options\":[\"Fight to win\",\"Be the strongest\",\"Unity in diversity\",\"Ignore differences\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"The story teaches that unity in diversity makes the world bright.\"},{\"q\":\"Which colour is described as magical and mysterious?\",\"options\":[\"Indigo\",\"Violet\",\"Orange\",\"Red\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Indigo is described as magical and mysterious.\"},{\"q\":\"What happens if two colours from the rainbow disappear?\",\"options\":[\"The rainbow becomes brighter\",\"The rainbow becomes dull\",\"The rainbow stops existing\",\"The rainbow turns into a single colour\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"If two colours disappear, the rainbow cannot exist.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the white colour say about the colours when they come together?\",\"options\":[\"They become black\",\"They become white again\",\"They become invisible\",\"They become red\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"When all colours come together, they become white again.\"},{\"q\":\"Which colour is described as royal and graceful?\",\"options\":[\"Violet\",\"Indigo\",\"Blue\",\"Green\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Violet is described as royal and graceful.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16684,19,4,'English','en','4.6 The Encyclopaedia','[\"An encyclopaedia is a large book that contains information about many subjects like animals, planets, famous people and volcanoes.\",\"It used to be a big book kept in libraries, but now it is available online on computers and phones.\",\"You can learn about Science, Technology, Geography and Space with just a few clicks.\",\"An encyclopaedia is like a friend that helps us find answers and learn more about the world.\",\"It is a useful reference book that contains facts, definitions and explanations.\",\"You can read an encyclopaedia to learn new words and ideas.\",\"Encyclopaedias are organized in alphabetical order so you can find information quickly.\",\"They are written by many experts who research and write about different topics.\",\"You can use an encyclopaedia to study for school, do homework or satisfy curiosity.\",\"The book is a collection of articles, each about a specific topic.\",\"It is a reliable source of information because it is checked by experts.\",\"Encyclopaedias are available in many languages.\",\"You can use online encyclopaedias like Wikipedia or Britannica.\",\"Reading an encyclopaedia helps improve vocabulary and reading skills.\",\"Encyclopaedias can be used for research, writing reports and learning new facts.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What is an encyclopaedia?\",\"options\":[\"A small diary\",\"A big magic book\",\"A comic book\",\"A science textbook\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"An encyclopaedia is described as a big magic book that contains information about many topics.\"},{\"q\":\"Where did people read encyclopaedias in the past?\",\"options\":[\"On phones\",\"In libraries\",\"On the internet\",\"In schools\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Earlier encyclopaedias were large books kept in libraries.\"},{\"q\":\"How can we access encyclopaedias today?\",\"options\":[\"Only in libraries\",\"Through online platforms\",\"Only on paper\",\"By listening to radio\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Today encyclopaedias are available through online platforms like computers and mobile phones.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is NOT mentioned as a subject in encyclopaedias?\",\"options\":[\"Science\",\"Technology\",\"Cooking\",\"Space\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Cooking is not listed; subjects mentioned are Science, Technology, Geography, Space.\"},{\"q\":\"What role does an encyclopaedia play for us?\",\"options\":[\"It is a friend\",\"It is a toy\",\"It is a game\",\"It is a diary\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The text says an encyclopaedia is like a friend for all of us.\"},{\"q\":\"What activity is suggested for the classroom?\",\"options\":[\"Encyclopaedia Detective Game\",\"Reading circles\",\"Writing essays\",\"Drawing maps\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The teacher is advised to arrange an \'Encyclopaedia Detective Game\'.\"},{\"q\":\"In the detective game, who asks questions?\",\"options\":[\"The detective\",\"Other learners\",\"The teacher\",\"The book\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Other learners will ask questions to the Encyclopaedia Detective.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a suggested topic for the detective game?\",\"options\":[\"Volcano\",\"Library\",\"Animal\",\"All of the above\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The example lists volcano, library, animal, planet as topics.\"},{\"q\":\"What should students fill after reading a book?\",\"options\":[\"Title and writer\",\"Title only\",\"Writer only\",\"None of the above\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Students are asked to fill in Title and Name of the Writer after reading.\"},{\"q\":\"What is one of the rating symbols used for book rating?\",\"options\":[\"😑\",\"😎\",\"🤔\",\"🤗\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The rating uses the symbol 😑 among others.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16685,19,4,'English','en','4.7 Civic Sense','[\"Civic sense is the habit of being a good citizen by following rules and keeping the surroundings clean.\",\"It means not littering and putting garbage in the bin.\",\"It includes respecting public property like benches and walls.\",\"Waiting for your turn in a line shows respect for others.\",\"Helping friends cross the street safely is a civic act.\",\"Small actions together make the city safer and happier.\",\"Civic sense is taught by Parry the Civic sense parrot in the story.\",\"The story shows how children can practice civic sense in a park.\",\"Civic sense is about responsibility and caring for the community.\",\"When you throw garbage in a bin, you are following civic sense.\",\"Public property should never be damaged or defaced.\",\"Civic sense helps keep the city clean, safe and pleasant.\",\"Children can promise to practice civic sense every day.\",\"Civic sense is a promise to follow rules and respect others.\",\"Civic sense is a way to keep our city beautiful and friendly.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What does civic sense mean?\",\"options\":[\"Following rules and keeping clean\",\"Playing games\",\"Eating snacks\",\"Sleeping early\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Civic sense is about following rules and keeping surroundings clean.\"},{\"q\":\"Where should you throw garbage?\",\"options\":[\"In the bin\",\"On the ground\",\"In a bag\",\"On a tree\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Garbage should be thrown in the bin.\"},{\"q\":\"Which action shows respect for others?\",\"options\":[\"Running on the road\",\"Waiting for your turn in line\",\"Throwing litter\",\"Damaging benches\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Waiting for your turn shows respect.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you not do with public property?\",\"options\":[\"Paint it\",\"Clean it\",\"Damage it\",\"Use it\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Public property should not be damaged.\"},{\"q\":\"Who teaches the children about civic sense?\",\"options\":[\"A teacher\",\"Parry the parrot\",\"A dog\",\"A cat\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Parry the parrot teaches civic sense.\"},{\"q\":\"Which is a civic action?\",\"options\":[\"Helping friends cross the street safely\",\"Running on the road\",\"Throwing garbage on the ground\",\"Damaging benches\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Helping friends cross the street safely is civic.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main theme of the conversation?\",\"options\":[\"Littering\",\"Civic sense\",\"Playing games\",\"Eating food\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The theme is civic sense.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do with garbage?\",\"options\":[\"Throw it in the bin\",\"Throw it on the ground\",\"Keep it in your pocket\",\"Throw it in a bag\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Garbage should be thrown in the bin.\"},{\"q\":\"Which is a synonym for \\\"clean\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"Dirty\",\"Messy\",\"Neat\",\"Unclean\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Neat is a synonym for clean.\"},{\"q\":\"What does civic sense help create?\",\"options\":[\"A dirty city\",\"A safe and happy city\",\"A noisy city\",\"A crowded city\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Civic sense creates a safe and happy city.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16686,19,4,'English','en','4.8 Rose','[\"Roses are beautiful flowers with many colours like pink, white, red.\",\"They have soft petals that feel like velvet.\",\"The centre of a rose is called the heart and it is sweet and fragrant.\",\"Roses grow on bushes or hedges and can be seen in gardens or parks.\",\"The word ‘rose’ can mean both the flower and the colour red.\",\"Roses are often used in poems and songs because of their beauty and smell.\",\"The petals of a rose are arranged in layers around the heart.\",\"Roses can be described as ‘dainty’, ‘shy’, or ‘beautiful’ depending on how they look.\",\"Roses have a strong fragrance that can be felt from a distance.\",\"The word ‘rose’ is also used as a verb meaning to become red or pink.\",\"Roses are often given as gifts on special occasions like birthdays and anniversaries.\",\"The stem of a rose is long and can be used to hold the flower in a vase.\",\"Roses can be used to make perfumes, jams, and teas.\",\"The word ‘rose’ can also mean a past tense of ‘rise’ in English.\",\"Roses are a symbol of love, friendship, and respect in many cultures.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What colour is a rose that is described as ‘rosepink’ in the poem?\",\"options\":[\"Pink\",\"Red\",\"Blue\",\"Yellow\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions ‘Rosepink’ which indicates a pink coloured rose.\"},{\"q\":\"Which part of the rose is described as sweet and fragrant?\",\"options\":[\"Petals\",\"Leaves\",\"Stem\",\"Heart\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"The poem says the heart of the rose is sweet and fragrant.\"},{\"q\":\"Roses are often found growing on what type of plant?\",\"options\":[\"Trees\",\"Hedges\",\"Bamboo\",\"Cactus\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The poem mentions roses clambering on a hazel hedge.\"},{\"q\":\"The word ‘rose’ can also mean what in English?\",\"options\":[\"A colour\",\"A verb meaning to become red\",\"A type of bird\",\"A musical instrument\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"In English, ‘rose’ is the past tense of ‘rise’.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of the following is NOT a colour of roses mentioned?\",\"options\":[\"Pink\",\"White\",\"Red\",\"Blue\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"Pink, white, and red are mentioned; blue is not.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the opposite of ‘shy’?\",\"options\":[\"Bold\",\"Quiet\",\"Soft\",\"Happy\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Opposite of shy is bold.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the opposite of ‘sweet’?\",\"options\":[\"Sour\",\"Bitter\",\"Salty\",\"Spicy\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Opposite of sweet is sour.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the opposite of ‘close’?\",\"options\":[\"Near\",\"Open\",\"Far\",\"Hidden\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Opposite of close is open.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the opposite of ‘beautiful’?\",\"options\":[\"Ugly\",\"Pretty\",\"Gorgeous\",\"Lovely\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Opposite of beautiful is ugly.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the opposite of ‘white’?\",\"options\":[\"Black\",\"Red\",\"Blue\",\"Green\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Opposite of white is black.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16687,19,4,'English','en','4.9 Saying ‘No’ to Strangers','[\"- A stranger is someone you do not know.\",\"- Children should never talk to strangers.\",\"- If a stranger offers gifts, say ‘NO’ loudly.\",\"- Stay together with parents or teachers.\",\"- Call for help if you feel unsafe.\",\"- Saying ‘NO’ is a safe action.\",\"- Do not accept chocolates or toys from strangers.\",\"- Keep your distance from unknown people.\",\"- Always stay in a group when outside school.\",\"- Report any suspicious person to a teacher or adult.\"]','[{\"q\":\"What should you do if a stranger offers you a gift?\",\"options\":[\"Accept it\",\"Ask for a price\",\"Say ‘NO’ loudly\",\"Ignore it\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Saying ‘NO’ loudly keeps you safe.\"},{\"q\":\"Who should you stay with after school?\",\"options\":[\"Your friends\",\"Your parents or teachers\",\"A stranger\",\"No one\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Staying with parents or teachers is safest.\"},{\"q\":\"What does the word ‘unsafe’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"Very safe\",\"Uncertain\",\"Dangerous\",\"Happy\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Unsafe means dangerous.\"},{\"q\":\"If you feel worried, what should you do?\",\"options\":[\"Run away\",\"Call your teacher\",\"Sit still\",\"Talk to the stranger\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Call a teacher for help.\"},{\"q\":\"Which of these is a transitional word?\",\"options\":[\"Fast\",\"Soon\",\"Good\",\"Happy\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Soon is a transitional word.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the main idea of the conversation?\",\"options\":[\"Children play together\",\"Children say ‘NO’ to strangers\",\"Children eat chocolate\",\"Children go home early\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"The conversation shows children saying ‘NO’.\"},{\"q\":\"What should you do if a stranger says ‘I am in a hurry’?\",\"options\":[\"Follow him\",\"Stay with your group\",\"Ask for a gift\",\"Ignore him\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Stay with your group for safety.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is the opposite of ‘together’?\",\"options\":[\"Alone\",\"Near\",\"Fast\",\"Safe\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Alone is the opposite of together.\"},{\"q\":\"What does ‘hurry’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"Stop\",\"Wait\",\"Move quickly\",\"Sit down\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"Hurry means to move quickly.\"},{\"q\":\"Why should you not talk to strangers?\",\"options\":[\"They are friendly\",\"They might be dangerous\",\"They are your friends\",\"They are teachers\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Strangers can be dangerous.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16688,19,4,'English','en','4.10 My Word Family','[\"- A word family is a group of words that share the same root or base word.\",\"- Words in a family are connected by meaning or sound.\",\"- In this chapter we learn words like *grassland*, *desert*, *turbine* and *elephant*.\",\"- A word chain is a sequence where each word is linked to the next by a common theme.\",\"- Riddles help us think about words in a fun way.\",\"- Anagrams are words made by rearranging letters of another word.\",\"- Dictionary is a useful tool to find meanings of new words.\",\"- *Windmills* are machines that turn with the wind to make electricity.\",\"- *Volcano* is a mountain that erupts lava and ash.\",\"- *Planet* is a large body that orbits a star.\",\"- *Adult* means a grown-up person.\",\"- *Tear* can mean a drop of liquid from the eye or a rip in paper.\",\"- *Nectar* is sweet liquid from flowers that bees collect.\",\"- *Exact* means precise or correct.\",\"- *Turbine* is a device that turns when air or water flows through it.\",\"- *Journey* is a long travel from one place to another.\",\"- *Knowledge* is information and understanding you have.\",\"- *Muscles* are body parts that help you move.\",\"- *Migration* is the movement of animals from one place to another.\",\"- *Discovery* is finding something new.\",\"- *Flour* (likely *flesh* in OCR) is the body part of animals.\",\"- *Bones* are the hard parts inside the body.\",\"- *Warmer* can mean a device that makes heat.\",\"- *Windmills* and *turbines* both use wind to produce power.\",\"- Understanding word families helps improve reading and writing skills.\"]','[{\"q\":\"Which word is a part of the word family that means a place where many plants grow?\",\"options\":[\"Desert\",\"Grassland\",\"Turbine\",\"Windmill\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Grassland is a large area covered with grasses.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the meaning of the word *tear*?\",\"options\":[\"A sweet liquid\",\"A drop of liquid from the eye\",\"A machine that makes electricity\",\"A long journey\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"Tear is a drop of liquid from the eye.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is an anagram of \\\"u-j-o-e-y-r-n-\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"Journey\",\"Journeyer\",\"Jounery\",\"Joruney\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Rearranging the letters gives \\\"journey\\\".\"},{\"q\":\"What does *windmill* do?\",\"options\":[\"It makes electricity\",\"It is a type of animal\",\"It is a sweet liquid\",\"It is a mountain\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Windmills use wind to generate electricity.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a large body that orbits a star?\",\"options\":[\"Planet\",\"Volcano\",\"Turbine\",\"Desert\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A planet is a large body that orbits a star.\"},{\"q\":\"What is the correct meaning of *exact*?\",\"options\":[\"Precise\",\"Wrong\",\"Fast\",\"Soft\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Exact means precise or correct.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is related to a machine that turns with the wind?\",\"options\":[\"Turbine\",\"Desert\",\"Knowledge\",\"Adult\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"A turbine turns with the wind to produce power.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word means a long travel from one place to another?\",\"options\":[\"Journey\",\"Turbine\",\"Windmill\",\"Desert\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Journey is a long travel.\"},{\"q\":\"Which word is a sweet liquid collected by bees?\",\"options\":[\"Nectar\",\"Tear\",\"Flesh\",\"Knowledge\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Nectar is the sweet liquid from flowers.\"},{\"q\":\"What is *migration*?\",\"options\":[\"Movement of animals\",\"A type of plant\",\"A machine\",\"A type of mountain\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"Migration is the movement of animals.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16689,20,4,'Marathi','mr','धरतीची आम्ही लेकरं (कविता) द. ना. गव्हाणकर','[\"धरतीची आम्ही लेकरं ही कविता द. ना. गव्हाणकर यांनी लिहिली आहे.\",\"कवितेत पृथ्वीवरील जीवनाचे सौंदर्य आणि मेहनतीचे महत्त्व सांगितले आहे.\",\"शेतावर जाऊन गाणे गाणे, मेहनत करणे आणि फळ मिळणे यावर भर दिला आहे.\",\"कवितेत ‘धरतीची आम्ही लेकरं’ या ओळीने पृथ्वीवरील सर्व जीवांना एकत्रितपणे दर्शविले आहे.\",\"कवितेतील ‘भाग्यवान’ या शब्दाने आपल्याला निसर्गाचे आशीर्वाद लक्षात येते.\",\"शेतात मेहनत केल्याने फळ मिळते, हे जीवनाचे एक नियम आहे.\",\"कवितेत ‘रानपाखरं’ आणि ‘रानीवनी’ यांचा उल्लेख करून निसर्गाची विविधता दाखविली आहे.\",\"कवितेत ‘पोलादी ऐक्यता’ या शब्दाने सर्व जीवांमध्ये समानता आणि एकता दर्शविली आहे.\",\"कवितेतील ‘मोत्यांची सालभरी’ या ओळीने निसर्गातील विविध गोष्टींची तुलना केली आहे.\",\"कवितेतील ‘शाळु, जुंधळा मोती’ या ओळीने निसर्गातील सौंदर्याचे वर्णन केले आहे.\",\"कविता वाचताना तालासुरात वाचणे महत्त्वाचे आहे.\",\"कवितेतील ‘ध्रु.’ आणि ‘शिवार’ या शब्दांनी काव्यरचनेत गती आणली आहे.\",\"कवितेतील ‘म्हणा’ आणि ‘वाचा’ या शब्दांनी वाचकाला सक्रिय करण्यास प्रवृत्त केले आहे.\",\"कवितेतील ‘संगाती गाऊया’ या ओळीने एकत्रित गाण्याचे महत्त्व दाखविले आहे.\",\"कवितेतील ‘आज आलं फळ’ या ओळीने मेहनतीचे फळ त्वरित मिळते हे दाखविले आहे.\",\"कवितेतील ‘सामानता’ आणि ‘समानता’ या शब्दांनी सर्व जीवांमध्ये समानतेची कल्पना दिली आहे.\",\"कवितेतील ‘पोलादी’ या शब्दाने धातूच्या ताकदीची तुलना केली आहे.\",\"कवितेतील ‘चाकर’ या शब्दाने निसर्गातील सर्व गोष्टींची एकता दर्शविली आहे.\",\"कवितेतील ‘डुले’ या शब्दाने फळाचे सौंदर्य दर्शविले आहे.\",\"कवितेतील ‘सालभरी’ या शब्दाने निसर्गातील विविध गोष्टींची तुलना केली आहे.\",\"कवितेतील ‘म्हणा’ आणि ‘वाचा’ या शब्दांनी वाचकाला सक्रिय करण्यास प्रवृत्त केले आहे.\",\"कवितेतील ‘ध्रु.’ आणि ‘शिवार’ या शब्दांनी काव्यरचनेत गती आणली आहे.\",\"कवितेतील ‘संगाती गाऊया’ या ओळीने एकत्रित गाण्याचे महत्त्व दाखविले आहे.\",\"कवितेतील ‘आज आलं फळ’ या ओळीने मेहनतीचे फळ त्वरित मिळते हे दाखविले आहे.\",\"कवितेतील ‘सामानता’ आणि ‘समानता’ या शब्दांनी सर्व जीवांमध्ये समानतेची कल्पना दिली आहे.\"]','[{\"q\":\"धरतीची आम्ही लेकरं ही कविता कोणी लिहिली?\",\"options\":[\"द. ना. गव्हाणकर\",\"द. ना. पाटील\",\"द. ना. शिंदे\",\"द. ना. वाघ\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"कविता द. ना. गव्हाणकर यांनी लिहिली आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेत ‘भाग्यवान’ या शब्दाचा अर्थ काय?\",\"options\":[\"सुदैवी\",\"कष्टकरी\",\"साधारण\",\"निराश\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"भाग्यवान म्हणजे सुदैवी.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील ‘रानपाखरं’ कोणत्या गोष्टीचे प्रतीक आहे?\",\"options\":[\"निसर्गाची विविधता\",\"शेतातील पिके\",\"मानव समाज\",\"पोलादी धातू\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"रानपाखरं निसर्गाची विविधता दर्शविते.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेत ‘ध्रु.’ आणि ‘शिवार’ या शब्दांनी काय साधले?\",\"options\":[\"काव्याला गती दिली\",\"शेतात पाणी साठवले\",\"पोलादी धातूची ताकद दाखविली\",\"म्हणा आणि वाचा यांना जोडले\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"हे शब्द काव्याला गती देतात.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील ‘समानता’ आणि ‘समानता’ या शब्दांनी काय दर्शविले?\",\"options\":[\"सर्व जीव समान आहेत\",\"फक्त मानवी समाज समान आहे\",\"पोलादी धातू समान आहे\",\"फक्त शेतातील पिके समान आहेत\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"समानता सर्व जीवांमध्ये समानतेची कल्पना देते.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील ‘मोत्यांची सालभरी’ या ओळीचा अर्थ काय?\",\"options\":[\"निसर्गातील विविध गोष्टींची तुलना\",\"पोलादी धातूची ताकद\",\"शेतातील पिके\",\"कवितेतील गती\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"मोत्यांची सालभरी म्हणजे निसर्गातील विविध गोष्टींची तुलना.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील ‘शाळु, जुंधळा मोती’ या ओळीने काय दर्शविले?\",\"options\":[\"निसर्गातील सौंदर्य\",\"पोलादी धातू\",\"मानवी समाज\",\"शेतातील पिके\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"शाळु, जुंधळा मोती निसर्गातील सौंदर्य दर्शविते.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील ‘धनी’ या शब्दाचा अर्थ काय?\",\"options\":[\"संपन्न\",\"कमी\",\"मध्यम\",\"निराश\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"धनी म्हणजे संपन्न.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील ‘पोलादी ऐक्यता’ या ओळीने काय दाखविले?\",\"options\":[\"सर्व जीवांमध्ये एकता\",\"पोलादी धातूची ताकद\",\"शेतातील पिके एकत्र\",\"निसर्गातील विविधता\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"पोलादी ऐक्यता सर्व जीवांमध्ये एकता दर्शविते.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील ‘म्हणा’ आणि ‘वाचा’ या शब्दांचा उद्देश काय?\",\"options\":[\"वाचकाला सक्रिय करणे\",\"शेतात पाणी साठवणे\",\"पोलादी धातूची ताकद दाखवणे\",\"कवितेतील गती वाढवणे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"म्हणा व वाचा वाचकाला सक्रिय करण्यास प्रवृत्त करतात.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16690,20,4,'Marathi','mr','बोलणारी नदी —','[\"बोलणारी नदी म्हणजे अशी नदी जी बोलू शकते आणि आपल्याशी संवाद साधते.\",\"लीला नावाची एक खोडकर मुलगी होती जी नदीकडे जाऊन बोलायची.\",\"लीला नदीला बोलायला शिकली आणि तिला नदीची परवानगी मिळाली.\",\"नदीबाई (नदी) ताई, आई, माईपेक्षा मोठी आहे.\",\"लीला बर्फाचा गोळा, शाळा बुडवणे, पेढे यासारख्या गोष्टींमध्ये नदीची मदत घेते.\",\"नदी बोलण्यासाठी लीला स्वतःला नदीबाई म्हणते आणि नदीला आदेश देते.\",\"नदीबाईला बोलताना लीला \'नदी गं नदी\' असे म्हणते.\",\"नदीबाईने लीला सांगितले की तिला बर्फाचा गोळा खायचा आहे आणि शाळा बुडवायची नाही.\",\"नदीबाईने लीला पेढे घेऊन जाण्यास सांगितले आणि तिला आठ पेढे द्यायला सांगितले.\",\"नदीबाईचे बोलणे ताई, आई, माईच्या बोलण्यासारखेच असते.\",\"वावर म्हणजे शेत किंवा वर्दळ अशी दोन अर्थे असतात.\",\"बिनधास्त म्हणजे बेफिकीर, काळजी न करता.\",\"शिंकाळे म्हणजे छताला टांगलेले दोरीचे जाळे ज्यात दही, दुधाची भांडी ठेवतात.\",\"बुट्टी म्हणजे बांबूची टोपली.\",\"परस म्हणजे घरामागची मोकळी जागा.\",\"लीला आणि नीला यांनी नदीबाईला पेढे दिले आणि खेळायला गेले.\",\"नदीबाईने लीला सांगितले की तिला बर्फाचा गोळा खायचा आहे.\",\"लीला ने नदीबाईला बोलायला शिकले आणि ती नदीबाईला आदेश देते.\",\"नदीबाईने लीला सांगितले की तिला बर्फाचा गोळा खायचा आहे.\",\"नदीबाईने लीला सांगितले की तिला शाळा बुडवायची नाही.\",\"नदीबाईने लीला सांगितले की तिला पेढे घेऊन जायचे आहे.\",\"नदीबाईने लीला सांगितले की तिला बर्फाचा गोळा खायचा आहे.\",\"नदीबाईने लीला सांगितले की तिला शाळा बुडवायची नाही.\",\"नदीबाईने लीला सांगितले की तिला पेढे घेऊन जायचे आहे.\",\"नदीबाईने लीला सांगितले की तिला बर्फाचा गोळा खायचा आहे.\"]','[{\"q\":\"लीला कोणती गोष्ट खायला आवडते?\",\"options\":[\"बर्फाचा गोळा\",\"पेढे\",\"शाळा\",\"नदी\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"लीला बर्फाचा गोळा खायला आवडते.\"},{\"q\":\"नदीबाई कोणापेक्षा मोठी आहे?\",\"options\":[\"ताई\",\"आई\",\"माई\",\"सगळे\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"नदीबाई ताई, आई, माईपेक्षा मोठी आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"लीला नदीला काय सांगते?\",\"options\":[\"शाळा बुडवायची\",\"पेढे द्यायचे\",\"बर्फाचा गोळा खायचा\",\"सगळे\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"लीला नदीला बर्फाचा गोळा खायचा, शाळा बुडवायची नाही, पेढे द्यायचे असे सांगते.\"},{\"q\":\"वावर या शब्दाचे दोन अर्थ काय आहेत?\",\"options\":[\"शेत आणि वर्दळ\",\"घर आणि शाळा\",\"बर्फ आणि पेढे\",\"नदी आणि तळे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"वावर म्हणजे शेत आणि वर्दळ.\"},{\"q\":\"लीला नदीबाईला कोणते नाव देते?\",\"options\":[\"नदी\",\"नदीबाई\",\"लीला\",\"बर्फ\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"लीला नदीबाईला \'नदीबाई\' असे म्हणते.\"},{\"q\":\"नदीबाईने लीला पेढे किती दिले?\",\"options\":[\"सात\",\"आठ\",\"दहा\",\"बारा\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"नदीबाईने लीला आठ पेढे दिले.\"},{\"q\":\"लीला शाळा बुडवण्याचा प्रयत्न का करते?\",\"options\":[\"कंटाळा वाटतो\",\"नदीची मदत हवी\",\"पेढे हवे\",\"सगळे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"लीला कंटाळा वाटल्यामुळे शाळा बुडवायची इच्छा करते.\"},{\"q\":\"नदीबाईला बोलताना लीला काय म्हणते?\",\"options\":[\"नदी गं नदी\",\"नदी बर्फ\",\"नदी शाळा\",\"नदी पेढे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"लीला नदीला \'नदी गं नदी\' असे म्हणते.\"},{\"q\":\"लीला पेढे कुठे शोधते?\",\"options\":[\"शिंकाळे\",\"बुट्टी\",\"परस\",\"सगळे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"लीला पेढे शिंकाळ्यात शोधते.\"},{\"q\":\"लीला नदीबाईला काय बोलायला शिकते?\",\"options\":[\"बर्फाचा गोळा खायचा\",\"शाळा बुडवायची नाही\",\"पेढे द्यायचे\",\"सगळे\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"लीला नदीबाईला बर्फाचा गोळा खायचा, शाळा बुडवायची नाही, पेढे द्यायचे असे बोलायला शिकते.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16691,20,4,'Marathi','mr','आम्ही संबाद करतो','[\"- संवाद म्हणजे बोलणे आणि ऐकणे.\",\"- संवादात बोलणारा आणि ऐकणारा दोघेही असतात.\",\"- संवादात शब्द, आवाज, हावभाव आणि चेहऱ्याचे भाव वापरले जातात.\",\"- पक्षी आणि प्राणी आपापसात बोलतात, पण आपण त्यांना समजू शकतो.\",\"- संवाद लिहिताना बोलणाऱ्याचे नाव आणि काय बोलले ते लिहावे.\",\"- संवादात \'म्हणून\', \'म्हणून\', \'म्हणून\' या शब्दांचा वापर होतो.\",\"- संवादात प्रश्न विचारणे आणि उत्तर देणे दोन्ही असू शकतात.\",\"- संवाद लिहिताना वाक्य सुरू करताना बोलणाऱ्याचे नाव आणि नंतर कोलन वापरावे.\",\"- संवादात \'होय\', \'नाही\', \'कदाचित\' असे शब्द वापरता येतात.\",\"- संवादात भावना व्यक्त करण्यासाठी \'आनंद\', \'दुःख\', \'राग\' असे शब्द वापरता येतात.\",\"- संवाद लिहिताना वाक्ये स्पष्ट आणि सोपी ठेवावी.\",\"- संवादात बोलणाऱ्याचे नाव आणि बोललेले वाक्य स्पष्टपणे लिहावे.\",\"- संवाद लिहिताना विषयावर लक्ष द्यावे.\",\"- संवाद लिहिताना शब्दांची योग्य वर्तनी वापरावी.\",\"- संवाद लिहिताना विरामचिन्हे योग्यरित्या वापरावी.\"]','[{\"q\":\"संवाद म्हणजे काय?\",\"options\":[\"बोलणे आणि ऐकणे\",\"फक्त बोलणे\",\"फक्त ऐकणे\",\"काहीही नाही\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"संवादात बोलणे आणि ऐकणे दोन्ही असतात.\"},{\"q\":\"संवादात कोणते घटक असतात?\",\"options\":[\"फक्त शब्द\",\"फक्त आवाज\",\"शब्द आणि आवाज\",\"फक्त हावभाव\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"शब्द आणि आवाज दोन्ही संवादाचे भाग आहेत.\"},{\"q\":\"पक्षी आणि प्राणी संवाद करताना काय वापरतात?\",\"options\":[\"फक्त आवाज\",\"फक्त हावभाव\",\"शब्द, आवाज आणि हावभाव\",\"काहीही नाही\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"ते आवाज आणि हावभाव वापरतात.\"},{\"q\":\"संवाद लिहिताना बोलणाऱ्याचे नाव कसे लिहावे?\",\"options\":[\"नाव नंतर कोलन\",\"नाव नंतर कॉमा\",\"नाव नंतर डॅश\",\"नाव नंतर सेमीकोलन\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"बोलणाऱ्याचे नाव नंतर कोलन वापरतात.\"},{\"q\":\"संवादात भावना व्यक्त करण्यासाठी कोणते शब्द वापरता येतात?\",\"options\":[\"आनंद, दुःख, राग\",\"फक्त आनंद\",\"फक्त दुःख\",\"फक्त राग\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"आनंद, दुःख, राग हे भावना दर्शवतात.\"},{\"q\":\"संवाद लिहिताना कोणते विरामचिन्ह वापरतात?\",\"options\":[\"फक्त पूर्णविराम\",\"फक्त अल्पविराम\",\"पूर्णविराम आणि अल्पविराम\",\"काहीही नाही\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"विरामचिन्हे स्पष्टतेसाठी आवश्यक आहेत.\"},{\"q\":\"संवादात प्रश्न विचारण्यासाठी कोणता शब्द वापरतात?\",\"options\":[\"होय\",\"नाही\",\"कदाचित\",\"काय\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"प्रश्न विचारण्यासाठी \'काय\' वापरतात.\"},{\"q\":\"संवाद लिहिताना वाक्ये कशी असावीत?\",\"options\":[\"जटिल\",\"स्पष्ट आणि सोपी\",\"लांब\",\"कमी\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"स्पष्ट आणि सोपी वाक्ये चांगली असतात.\"},{\"q\":\"संवादात बोलणाऱ्याचे नाव आणि बोललेले वाक्य कसे लिहावे?\",\"options\":[\"नाव आणि वाक्य एकत्र\",\"नाव नंतर कोलन आणि वाक्य\",\"नाव नंतर कॉमा आणि वाक्य\",\"नाव आणि वाक्य वेगळे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"नाव नंतर कोलन वापरतात.\"},{\"q\":\"संवाद लिहिताना विषयावर लक्ष कसे द्यावे?\",\"options\":[\"विषय दुर्लक्षित करणे\",\"विषयावर लक्ष न देणे\",\"विषयावर लक्ष देणे\",\"काहीही नाही\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"विषयावर लक्ष देणे महत्त्वाचे आहे.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16692,20,4,'Marathi','mr','आम्हांलाही हबाय मोबाईल ! (नाट्यछटा) सूर्यकांत सराफ','[\"- मोबाईल म्हणजे एक छोटा फोन ज्याने आपण बोलू शकतो आणि मजकूर पाठवू शकतो.\",\"- मोबाईल वापरल्याने मित्रांना आणि कुटुंबाला लवकर पोहोचता येते.\",\"- मोबाईलने शाळेतील कामे सोपी होतात, जसे की सुट्टीची माहिती घेणे.\",\"- मोबाईलचा वापर करताना वेळेची काळजी घ्यावी, जास्त वेळ बोलू नये.\",\"- मोबाईल वापरताना इतरांना त्रास होऊ नये म्हणून शांत ठिकाणी वापरावा.\",\"- मोबाईलवर गेम्स खेळणे मजेदार असते, पण अभ्यासात अडथळा होऊ नये.\",\"- मोबाईलने आपल्याला नवीन गोष्टी शिकायला मदत होते, जसे की व्हिडिओ ट्यूटोरियल्स.\",\"- मोबाईल वापरताना सुरक्षिततेची काळजी घ्यावी, जसे की अज्ञात नंबरवर कॉल न करणे.\",\"- मोबाईल वापरताना शाळेच्या नियमांचे पालन करावे, जसे की वर्गात फोन बंद ठेवणे.\",\"- मोबाईलने आपल्याला आपले विचार आणि भावना व्यक्त करण्यास मदत होते.\",\"- मोबाईलने आपल्याला जगभरातील लोकांशी संपर्क साधता येतो.\",\"- मोबाईल वापरताना आपले आरोग्य लक्षात ठेवावे, जसे की डोळ्यांना आराम द्यावा.\",\"- मोबाईलने आपल्याला आपले वेळापत्रक व्यवस्थापित करण्यास मदत होते.\",\"- मोबाईल वापरताना इतरांच्या गोपनीयतेचा आदर करावा.\",\"- मोबाईलने आपल्याला आपले स्वप्न पूर्ण करण्यास मदत होते.\",\"- मोबाईल वापरताना आपल्याला आपले कुटुंब आणि मित्रांना वेळ द्यावा.\",\"- मोबाईलने आपल्याला आपले ज्ञान वाढविण्यास मदत होते.\",\"- मोबाईल वापरताना आपल्याला आपले लक्ष केंद्रीत ठेवावे.\",\"- मोबाईलने आपल्याला आपले काम वेळेवर पूर्ण करण्यास मदत होते.\",\"- मोबाईल वापरताना आपल्याला आपले शारीरिक आरोग्य लक्षात ठेवावे.\",\"- मोबाईलने आपल्याला आपले सामाजिक कौशल्य वाढविण्यास मदत होते.\",\"- मोबाईल वापरताना आपल्याला आपले मानसिक आरोग्य लक्षात ठेवावे.\",\"- मोबाईलने आपल्याला आपले जीवन अधिक सोपे आणि आनंदी बनविण्यास मदत होते.\"]','[{\"q\":\"मोबाईलचा मुख्य उपयोग काय आहे?\",\"options\":[\"बोलणे आणि मजकूर पाठवणे\",\"फक्त गेम खेळणे\",\"फक्त व्हिडिओ पाहणे\",\"फक्त संगीत ऐकणे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"मोबाईलने आपण बोलू शकतो आणि मजकूर पाठवू शकतो.\"},{\"q\":\"मोबाईल वापरताना कोणत्या गोष्टीची काळजी घ्यावी?\",\"options\":[\"फक्त गेम खेळणे\",\"इतरांना त्रास होऊ नये\",\"फक्त संगीत ऐकणे\",\"फक्त व्हिडिओ पाहणे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"इतरांना त्रास होऊ नये म्हणून शांत ठिकाणी वापरावे.\"},{\"q\":\"शाळेत मोबाईल कधी बंद ठेवावा?\",\"options\":[\"वर्गात\",\"सुट्टीच्या वेळी\",\"सकाळी\",\"संध्याकाळी\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"वर्गात मोबाईल बंद ठेवणे शाळेचे नियम आहेत.\"},{\"q\":\"मोबाईलने आपल्याला काय शिकायला मदत होते?\",\"options\":[\"फक्त गेम्स\",\"फक्त व्हिडिओ\",\"फक्त संगीत\",\"नवीन गोष्टी\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"मोबाईलवर व्हिडिओ ट्यूटोरियल्स आणि अॅप्सने नवीन गोष्टी शिकता येतात.\"},{\"q\":\"मोबाईल वापरताना आरोग्याची काळजी कशी घ्यावी?\",\"options\":[\"डोळ्यांना आराम द्या\",\"फक्त गेम खेळा\",\"फक्त संगीत ऐका\",\"फक्त व्हिडिओ पाहा\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"डोळ्यांना आराम देणे महत्त्वाचे आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"मोबाईलने मित्रांशी कसा संपर्क साधता येतो?\",\"options\":[\"फोन करून\",\"मजकूर पाठवून\",\"दोन्ही\",\"काहीही नाही\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"दोन्ही मार्गांनी संपर्क साधता येतो.\"},{\"q\":\"मोबाईल वापरताना कोणत्या गोष्टीचा आदर करावा?\",\"options\":[\"इतरांच्या गोपनीयतेचा\",\"फक्त आपल्या गोपनीयतेचा\",\"दोन्ही नाहीत\",\"काहीही नाही\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"इतरांच्या गोपनीयतेचा आदर करणे आवश्यक आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"मोबाईलने आपले वेळापत्रक कसे व्यवस्थापित करता येते?\",\"options\":[\"कॅलेंडर अॅप वापरून\",\"फक्त फोन कॉल करून\",\"फक्त गेम खेळून\",\"काहीही नाही\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"कॅलेंडर अॅपने वेळापत्रक व्यवस्थापित करता येते.\"},{\"q\":\"मोबाईल वापरताना कोणते नियम पाळावेत?\",\"options\":[\"फक्त गेम खेळणे\",\"फक्त संगीत ऐकणे\",\"शाळेचे नियम\",\"काहीही नाही\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"शाळेचे नियम पाळणे आवश्यक आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"मोबाईलने आपले जीवन कसे सोपे बनवते?\",\"options\":[\"फक्त मजा करते\",\"फक्त गेम खेळते\",\"संपर्क आणि माहिती देते\",\"फक्त संगीत ऐकते\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"संपर्क आणि माहिती देऊन जीवन सोपे होते.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16693,20,4,'Marathi','mr','शॅ. या भारतात______ (कविता) राष्ट्रसंत तुकडोजीमहाराज','[\"भारतात बंधुभाव म्हणजे सर्व लोक एकमेकांना मदत करतात.\",\"जातिभाव विसरून सर्वजण एक होतात.\",\"अस्पृश्यता म्हणजे कोणालाही अपवित्र समजणे, ती नष्ट करायची आहे.\",\"सर्व पंथ आणि संप्रदाय एकसारखे असावेत.\",\"सत्य आणि न्याय सर्वत्र पसरवायचे आहेत.\",\"सुख आणि समृद्धी सर्वांना मिळावी.\",\"गरीब आणि अमीर एकत्र येऊन आनंदी असावेत.\",\"सौंदर्य सर्व घरात असावे.\",\"हिंदू, ख्रिश्चन, मुस्लिम सर्वजण एकत्र राहावेत.\",\"भीती आणि विपत्ती दूर व्हाव्यात.\",\"स्वातंत्र्य आणि सुख सर्वांना मिळावे.\",\"सर्वांना एकत्र काम करायला हवे.\",\"मानवता आणि राष्ट्रभावना सर्वत्र पसरवायची आहे.\",\"कवितेतील संदेश तालासुरात गाऊन लक्षात ठेवावा.\",\"शिक्षकांनी विद्यार्थ्यांना हे शिकवावे.\",\"कवितेतील शब्दांचा अर्थ समजून घ्यावा.\",\"सर्वजण एकमेकांना मदत करतात हे लक्षात ठेवावे.\",\"सर्व पंथांना समान वागणूक द्यावी.\",\"सत्य आणि न्याय सर्वत्र पसरवावेत.\",\"सुख आणि समृद्धी सर्वांना मिळावी.\",\"सर्वजण एकत्र काम करायला हवे.\",\"मानवता आणि राष्ट्रभावना सर्वत्र पसरवायची आहे.\",\"कवितेतील संदेश लक्षात ठेवावा.\"]','[{\"q\":\"कवितेतील मुख्य विषय काय आहे?\",\"options\":[\"राष्ट्रभावना\",\"सामाजिक समरसता\",\"धर्मभेद\",\"सर्वोच्च सत्ता\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"कवितेत राष्ट्रभावना आणि सामाजिक समरसतेवर भर दिला आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील लेखक कोण आहे?\",\"options\":[\"तुकडोजी महाराज\",\"राष्ट्रसंत तुकडोजी\",\"संत तुकडोजी\",\"तुकडोजी महाराज\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"लेखकाचे नाव \'राष्ट्रसंत तुकडोजी\' असे दिले आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील \'बंधुभाव\' म्हणजे काय?\",\"options\":[\"भाऊ-बहिणीचा प्रेम\",\"सर्व लोकांमधील एकात्मता\",\"सामाजिक वर्गभेद\",\"धर्मभेद\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"बंधुभाव म्हणजे सर्व लोकांमध्ये एकात्मता.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील \'अस्पृश्यता\' कशी नष्ट होईल?\",\"options\":[\"शिक्षणाने\",\"धर्मभेदाने\",\"सामाजिक समरसतेने\",\"राष्ट्रभावनेने\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"कवितेत अस्पृश्यता नष्ट करण्यासाठी सामाजिक समरसता आणि राष्ट्रभावना महत्त्वाची आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील \'सर्वोच्च सत्ता\' कोणाला म्हणतात?\",\"options\":[\"देव\",\"राजा\",\"सर्व लोक\",\"सर्वोच्च सत्ता\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"कवितेत सर्व लोकांना सर्वोच्च सत्ता मानले आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील \'सुख\' कोणाला दिले जाते?\",\"options\":[\"सर्व लोकांना\",\"फक्त श्रीमंतांना\",\"फक्त गरीबांना\",\"फक्त धार्मिकांना\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"कवितेत सर्व लोकांना सुख दिले जाईल असे म्हटले आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील \'सर्वोच्च सत्ता\' कोणाला दिली जाते?\",\"options\":[\"सर्व लोकांना\",\"फक्त श्रीमंतांना\",\"फक्त गरीबांना\",\"फक्त धार्मिकांना\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"कवितेत सर्व लोकांना सर्वोच्च सत्ता दिली जाईल असे म्हटले आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील \'सर्वोच्च सत्ता\' कोणाला दिली जाते?\",\"options\":[\"सर्व लोकांना\",\"फक्त श्रीमंतांना\",\"फक्त गरीबांना\",\"फक्त धार्मिकांना\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"कवितेत सर्व लोकांना सर्वोच्च सत्ता दिली जाईल असे म्हटले आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील \'सर्वोच्च सत्ता\' कोणाला दिली जाते?\",\"options\":[\"सर्व लोकांना\",\"फक्त श्रीमंतांना\",\"फक्त गरीबांना\",\"फक्त धार्मिकांना\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"कवितेत सर्व लोकांना सर्वोच्च सत्ता दिली जाईल असे म्हटले आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"कवितेतील \'सर्वोच्च सत्ता\' कोणाला दिली जाते?\",\"options\":[\"सर्व लोकांना\",\"फक्त श्रीमंतांना\",\"फक्त गरीबांना\",\"फक्त धार्मिकांना\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"कवितेत सर्व लोकांना सर्वोच्च सत्ता दिली जाईल असे म्हटले आहे.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16694,20,4,'Marathi','mr','ष्‌. मला शिकायचंय ! आबा गोविंदा महाजन','[\"स्नेहा ही चौथीपर्यंत शिक्षण घेतलेली मुलगी आहे.\",\"तिचे कुटुंब गरीब आहे, त्यामुळे तिला परगावी शिक्षण घेता येत नाही.\",\"स्नेहाला पाचवी इयत्तेत जाण्याची इच्छा आहे.\",\"सखाराम आणि सुलभा हे तिचे पालक आहेत.\",\"स्नेहाची मैत्रीण बबली पाचवी इयत्तेत प्रवेश घेतलेली आहे.\",\"बबली गावच्या सरपंचांची मुलगी आहे.\",\"सरपंचांनी स्नेहाला पाचवी इयत्तेत प्रवेश दिला.\",\"सखारामला शाळेचा खर्च परवडत नाही, पण तो प्रयत्न करतो.\",\"स्नेहाला शाळेत जाण्यासाठी शिष्यवृत्तीची गरज आहे.\",\"सखारामने मुख्याध्यापकांना विनंती केली.\",\"मुख्याध्यापकांनी शिष्यवृत्ती परीक्षेची माहिती दिली.\",\"स्नेहाला शिष्यवृत्ती मिळाली तर ती स्वावलंबी होऊ शकेल.\",\"स्नेहाला पाचवी इयत्तेत जाण्याने तिचे भविष्य उज्ज्वल होईल.\",\"स्नेहाला शिक्षण घेण्यासाठी कुटुंबाची मदत आवश्यक आहे.\",\"स्नेहाच्या कुटुंबातील सर्वजण शिक्षणाला महत्त्व देतात.\",\"स्नेहाला शिक्षण घेण्यासाठी परगावी जाणे आवश्यक आहे.\",\"स्नेहाला पाचवी इयत्तेत जाण्याने तिला अधिक संधी मिळतील.\",\"स्नेहाला शिष्यवृत्ती मिळाली तर तिला परगावी शिक्षण घेता येईल.\",\"स्नेहाला पाचवी इयत्तेत जाण्यासाठी पालकांची सहमती आवश्यक आहे.\",\"स्नेहाला शिक्षण घेण्यासाठी समाजाची मदत हवी.\",\"स्नेहाला शिक्षण घेण्यासाठी शाळेची सुविधा आवश्यक आहे.\",\"स्नेहाला पाचवी इयत्तेत जाण्याने तिची बुद्धिमत्ता वाढेल.\",\"स्नेहाला शिक्षण घेण्यासाठी कुटुंबाची आर्थिक मदत आवश्यक आहे.\",\"स्नेहाला शिक्षण घेण्यासाठी समाजाची प्रेरणा आवश्यक आहे.\"]','[{\"q\":\"स्नेहाला कोणत्या वर्गापर्यंत शिक्षण झाले होते?\",\"options\":[\"पहिला\",\"दुसरा\",\"तिसरा\",\"चौथा\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"स्नेहाचे शिक्षण चौथीपर्यंत पूर्ण झाले होते.\"},{\"q\":\"स्नेहाची मैत्रीण बबली कोणत्या इयत्तेत प्रवेश घेतली?\",\"options\":[\"पहिली\",\"दुसरी\",\"तिसरी\",\"पाचवी\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"बबली पाचव्या इयत्तेत प्रवेश घेतली.\"},{\"q\":\"सखारामची पत्नी कोण आहे?\",\"options\":[\"सुलभा\",\"स्नेहा\",\"पिंटू\",\"बबली\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"सखारामची पत्नी सुलभा आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"सखारामच्या गावात चौथीच्या पुढे कोणते वर्ग होते?\",\"options\":[\"पाचवी\",\"सहावी\",\"सातवी\",\"आठवी\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"गावात चौथीच्या पुढे पाचवी इयत्ता नव्हती.\"},{\"q\":\"सखारामने स्नेहाला पुढे शिक्षण का द्यायला नकार दिला?\",\"options\":[\"आर्थिक कारण\",\"स्नेहाला आवड नाही\",\"स्नेहाला शाळेत जाणे अवघड\",\"स्नेहाला शारीरिक समस्या\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"गरिबीमुळे सखारामला स्नेहाला परगावी पाठवणे अवघड वाटले.\"},{\"q\":\"स्नेहाला पुढे शिकवण्यासाठी कोणाने मदत केली?\",\"options\":[\"सुलभा\",\"बबली\",\"सरपंच\",\"मुख्याध्यापक\"],\"answer\":3,\"explain\":\"मुख्याध्यापकांनी स्नेहाला पुढे शिकवण्यासाठी मदत करण्यास सांगितले.\"},{\"q\":\"स्नेहाला पाचव्या इयत्तेत प्रवेश घेण्यासाठी कोणत्या व्यक्तीने मदत केली?\",\"options\":[\"सखाराम\",\"सुलभा\",\"सरपंच\",\"बबली\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"सरपंचांनी स्नेहाला पाचव्या इयत्तेत प्रवेश दिला.\"},{\"q\":\"स्नेहाच्या वर्गात बबली कोणती भूमिका बजावते?\",\"options\":[\"शिक्षक\",\"मुलगी\",\"पालक\",\"सहपाठी\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"बबली स्नेहाची सहपाठी आहे.\"},{\"q\":\"स्नेहाला पाचव्या इयत्तेत प्रवेश घेण्यासाठी कोणती अडचण होती?\",\"options\":[\"आर्थिक\",\"भौगोलिक\",\"भाषिक\",\"सामाजिक\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"आर्थिक अडचणीमुळे स्नेहाला पाचव्या इयत्तेत प्रवेश घेणे कठीण होते.\"},{\"q\":\"स्नेहाला पुढे शिकवण्यासाठी मुख्याध्यापकांनी काय सुचवले?\",\"options\":[\"शिष्यवृत्ती परीक्षा\",\"शाळा बदलणे\",\"कौटुंबिक मदत\",\"शिक्षण शुल्क माफ करणे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"मुख्याध्यापकांनी शिष्यवृत्ती परीक्षेचा सल्ला दिला.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16695,20,4,'Marathi','mr','आम्ही कथा लिहितो-१ -','[\"स्नेहा रडत होती कारण तिला आपल्या आईची काळजी वाटत होती.\",\"सरपंच आणि मुख्याध्यापक सखारामच्या घरी आले कारण स्नेहाला मदत करायची होती.\",\"स्नेहाला आनंद झाला कारण तिला कुटुंबाची साथ मिळाली.\",\"स्नेहाची आई चिंतेत पडली कारण स्नेह रडत होती.\",\"मुख्याध्यापकाने पोटतिडकीने सांगितले की स्नेहाला शाळेत जाणे आवश्यक आहे.\",\"सरपंचाने समजुतीच्या स्वरात सखारामला सांगितले की शिक्षण महत्त्वाचे आहे.\",\"सखारामने निर्णय घेतला की स्नेहाला शाळेत पाठवायचे.\",\"चिंतेत पडणे म्हणजे मनात अस्वस्थता वाटणे.\",\"अचंबा वाटणे म्हणजे आश्चर्य वाटणे.\",\"गहिवरून येणे म्हणजे घाबरून येणे.\",\"पोटतिडकीने बोलणे म्हणजे अचानक बोलणे.\",\"डोळे पाणावणे म्हणजे डोळ्यातून पाणी येणे.\",\"रक्ताचे पाणी करणे म्हणजे रक्त पातळ करणे.\",\"खूप पुस्तके पाहून आपल्याला ज्ञान मिळते.\",\"बाजारात फिरताना आपण विविध गोष्टी पाहतो.\",\"आजारी व्यक्तीला पाहून आपण काळजी करतो.\",\"झोपेत असताना कोणी हाका मारल्यास आपण जागे होतो.\",\"ओ माय, माले पुढे शिकायला ये…\",\"स्नेहा, तुले चबथीलोंग शिकाड…\",\"अरे सखा, तुन्ही पोरगी एवढीच मन्ही बबली…\",\"मंग पोरगीना बाबतमाच असा भेद कसाले…\",\"आपुरं शिक्शन नको. दिनरात कष्ट करसू…\"]','[{\"q\":\"स्नेहा का रडत होती?\",\"options\":[\"ती घरी जाऊ शकत नव्हती\",\"तिच्या आईने तिला रडायला सांगितले\",\"ती वडिलांना भेटायला इच्छित होती\",\"ती रडत नव्हती\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"स्नेहा तिच्या आईच्या चिंतेमुळे रडत होती.\"},{\"q\":\"सरपंचांनी बबलीला कोणत्या इयत्तेत प्रवेश घेतला होता?\",\"options\":[\"पहिली इयत्ता\",\"दुसरी इयत्ता\",\"तिसरी इयत्ता\",\"चौथी इयत्ता\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"सरपंचांनी बबलीला दुसऱ्या इयत्तेत प्रवेश घेतला.\"},{\"q\":\"मुख्याध्यापक आणि सरपंच सखारामच्या घरी का गेले?\",\"options\":[\"स्नेहाला भेटायला\",\"स्नेहाच्या रडण्याबद्दल बोलायला\",\"स्नेहाला मदत करण्यासाठी\",\"स्नेहाला शाळेत पाठवायला\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"ते स्नेहाला मदत करण्यासाठी गेले.\"},{\"q\":\"स्नेहाला अतिशय आनंद का झाला?\",\"options\":[\"स्नेहाला शाळेत प्रवेश मिळाला\",\"स्नेहाला नवीन मित्र मिळाले\",\"स्नेहाला मदत मिळाली\",\"स्नेहाला पुस्तक दिले गेले\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"स्नेहाला मदत मिळाल्याने ती आनंदी झाली.\"},{\"q\":\"स्नेहाची आई चिंतेत का पडली?\",\"options\":[\"स्नेहाला शाळेत जाण्याची भीती\",\"स्नेहाला रडताना पाहून\",\"स्नेहाला शाळेत न जाण्याची चिंता\",\"स्नेहाला शाळेत प्रवेश न मिळाल्याने\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"स्नेहाला रडताना पाहून आई चिंतेत पडली.\"},{\"q\":\"मुख्याध्यापक सखारामला पोटतिडकीने काय सांगू लागले?\",\"options\":[\"सखारामला शाळेत जावे\",\"सखारामला अभ्यास करावा\",\"सखारामला कष्ट करावेत\",\"सखारामला शाळा सोडावी\"],\"answer\":2,\"explain\":\"मुख्याध्यापकाने पोटतिडकीने कष्ट करण्यास सांगितले.\"},{\"q\":\"सरपंच समजुतीच्या स्वरात सखारामला काय म्हणाले?\",\"options\":[\"सखाराम, तू शाळेत जाऊ शकतोस\",\"सखाराम, तुझी मदत करूया\",\"सखाराम, तुझी शाळा बंद कर\",\"सखाराम, तुझी शाळा चालू ठेव\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"सरपंचाने समजुतीने मदत करण्यास सांगितले.\"},{\"q\":\"सखारामने शेवटी कोणता निर्णय घेतला?\",\"options\":[\"शाळा सोडणे\",\"शाळेत जाणे सुरू ठेवणे\",\"शाळेत न जाणे\",\"शाळेत जाणे थांबवणे\"],\"answer\":1,\"explain\":\"सखारामने शाळेत जाणे सुरू ठेवण्याचा निर्णय घेतला.\"},{\"q\":\"खालील शब्दसमूहांचा अर्थ काय आहे? \\\"गहिवरून येणे\\\"?\",\"options\":[\"अचानक येणे\",\"हळूहळू येणे\",\"काळजीपूर्वक येणे\",\"सावधपणे येणे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"गहिवरून येणे म्हणजे अचानक येणे.\"},{\"q\":\"\\\"पोटतिडकीने बोलणे\\\" म्हणजे काय?\",\"options\":[\"मंद आवाजात बोलणे\",\"उच्च आवाजात बोलणे\",\"शांतपणे बोलणे\",\"कठोर आवाजात बोलणे\"],\"answer\":0,\"explain\":\"पोटतिडकीने बोलणे म्हणजे मंद आवाजात बोलणे.\"}]','nvidia/openai/gpt-oss-20b','2026-09-22 06:10:05'),(16696,20,4,'Marathi','mr','मायेची पाखर पां. चिं. पाटील','[\"कर्मवीर भाऊराव पाटील हे महाराष्ट्रातील शिक्षण क्षेत्रातील एक महत्त्वाचे व्यक्तिमत्त्व आहेत.\",\"त्यांनी रयत शिक्षण संस्था चालवून महाराष्ट्रभर शाळा व महाविद्यालये सुरू केली.\",\"त्यांची माया सर्व मुलांवर पसरली, विशेषतः वडील-मातेविना असलेल्या मुलांवर.\",\"भाऊराव पाटील यांना सर्वजण ‘कर्मबीर’ म्हणतात.\",\"त्यांनी मुलांना अंथरुण, अन्न व उब दिली.\",\"भाऊराव पाटील यांनी ‘मायेची पाखर’ या उपमेद्वारे मुलांना पंखाखाली घेतले.\",\"पोटात कावळे ओरडणे = खूप भूक लागणे.\",\"अधाशी = हावरा, खादाड.\",\"रुचकर = चवदार.\",\"बिछाना = अंथरूण.\",\"थंडीने कुडकुडणे = खूप थंडी वाजणे.\",\"पोटाशी धरणे = मायेने जबळ घेणे.\",\"उदंड = खूप, पुष्कळ.\",\"मायेचा वर्षाव करणे = खूप प्रेम करणे.\",\"भाऊराव पाटील यांनी वसतिगृहातील मुलांना स्वयंपाकघरातील शिल्लक अन्न दिले.\",\"भाऊराव पाटील यांनी मुलांना झोपवताना त्यांच्या पोटाशी धरले.\",\"भाऊराव पाटील यांनी मुलांना ‘मायेची पाखर’ म्हणून पाहिले.\",\"भाऊराव पाटील यांनी शिक्षणासाठी झटत राहिले.\",\"भाऊराव पाटील यांनी शाळा व महाविद्यालये सुरू केली.\",\"भाऊराव पाटील यांची माया सर्व मुलांवर पसरली.\",\"भाऊराव पाटील यांनी मुलांना उब दिली.\",\"भाऊराव पाटील यांनी मुलांना अन्न व अंथरुण दिले.\",\"भाऊराव पाटील यांनी मुलांना प्रेमाने वागवले.\",\"भाऊराव पाटील यांनी मुलांना ‘मायेची पाखर’ म्हणून घेतले.\",\"भाऊराव पाटील यांनी मुलांना ‘म